    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_162254.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's like asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:21.200\nThink about it like this: a chef tastes a soup to test if it needs more salt.\nOr, a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:35.200\nIn school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned.\nSo, whether it's a taste test, a medical test, or a school exam, the core idea is the same: we're using a test to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:43.800\nTests are a fundamental part of learning and understanding the world around us.\nIn short, a test is a tool we use to find answers!\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:47.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ea8246fc-55d3-4f40-b213-625d1bed9b74": {
    "id": "ea8246fc-55d3-4f40-b213-625d1bed9b74",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:10:20.837271",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T16:24:22.382515",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_162422.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_162422.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:11.100\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:20.500\nIt's like a little experiment to see what happens. For example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick test.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:27.600\nYou poke the cake with a toothpick, and if it comes out clean, the cake is done. That's a test!\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:33.700\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken. You turn it on.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:38.600\nIf it lights up, it passes the test. If it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:46.500\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is a simple procedure to determine if something meets a certain requirement.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:54.400\nIt could be anything from checking if your shoelaces are tied to making sure a bridge can hold a certain amount of weight.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:02.600\nTesting is all about making sure things work the way they're supposed to. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
