    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:10:21.743402",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T16:25:14.797329",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_162514.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_162514.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:09.500\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:20.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand more.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it this way: a spelling test helps your teacher see how well you know your words.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:29.700\nOr, a taste test lets you decide which cookie is the yummiest!\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:34.300\nSee?\nTests aren't scary, they just give us information.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:44.600\nFor example, you might take a test in school to see what you've learned about plants. Or, a scientist might test water to see if it's clean.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:48.600\nThe results tell us something important.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:58.100\nSo, tests are tools we use to learn, to check, and to understand things better. They come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to give us answers.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:02.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
