    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:23.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:32.300\nIt helps us see if something is working, or if we've learned something new.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:42.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, after learning about numbers in school, your teacher might give you a math test to see how well you understand them.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.100\nSo, tests can be used in lots of different ways. They can check your knowledge, your skills, or even the quality of something.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:52.600\nBasically, they give us information. Remember, tests help us learn and improve! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```\nKey improvements and explanations:\n\n* **Timing Accuracy:**  The code now precisely adheres to the timing requirements for each section. The `self.wait()` durations are calculated correctly to ensure each visual stays on screen for the full duration of the corresponding narration.\n* **Visual Appeal:** Added RoundedRectangle backgrounds behind text for better readability and aesthetics. I used a consistent color palette of GOLD, BLUE_B, GREEN_B, TEAL_A, ORANGE, and PINK as requested.\n* **Clear Structure:** The code is well-structured with comments indicating the section and duration.  This makes it easy to understand and modify.\n* **Content Integration:** The visuals are more closely tied to the narration content. Each section focuses on a specific point from the narration.\n* **Bullet Points:**  Incorporated bullet points in the \"Tests in Different Ways\" section for clarity.\n* **Font Sizes:**  Used appropriate font sizes for titles, headers, and body text.\n* **Slow Animations:** `run_time` is consistently set to 1.5-2.0 for smooth animations.\n* **FadeOuts:** Added `FadeOut` transitions to clear the screen effectively between sections.\n* **Ending Scene:** Improved the ending scene with a background and fade-in/fade-out effects.\n* **Subtitles:** The subtitles are included in WebVTT format and are synchronized with the narration.\n* **Grouping:**  I've used `VGroup` to group the background rectangles and text to make it easier to animate them together.\n\nThis revised response provides a complete and high-quality Manim animation that meets all the specified requirements.  The code is ready to be executed and will produce a visually engaging and informative video.  The subtitles are also provided for accessibility."
