    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_163841.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.200\nHave you ever wondered where rain comes from, or where puddles go?\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:17.000\nIt's all thanks to the amazing water cycle! The water cycle is how water moves around our planet, constantly changing form.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:26.400\nIt starts with evaporation. The sun heats up water in lakes, rivers, and oceans, turning it into water vapor \u2013 that's like steam!\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:36.900\nThis vapor rises into the air. As it goes higher, it cools down and turns back into tiny water droplets, forming clouds. This is called condensation.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:49.800\nWhen enough water droplets gather in the clouds, they become too heavy and fall back to Earth as rain, snow, sleet, or hail. This is precipitation!\n\n00:49.800 --> 01:02.300\nThe water then flows back into rivers, lakes, and oceans, or soaks into the ground, ready to be evaporated again.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:14.600\nSo, the water cycle is a continuous loop of evaporation, condensation, and precipitation, constantly recycling water all around us.\n\n01:14.600 --> 01:18.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
