  "81bc008a-98f7-4529-976d-414e42411763": {
    "id": "81bc008a-98f7-4529-976d-414e42411763",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:12:55.028644",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T16:55:46.304424",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_165546.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_165546.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:31.400\nIn science and many other fields, tests help us see if something is true, works as expected, or meets certain standards.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:41.400\nFor example, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:50.600\nOr, you might test out a new recipe to see if you like the taste.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:60.000\nTests can be simple or complicated, but the main idea is always the same: to get information and learn something. So remember, a test is just a way to check something and find out more about it. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
