    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:12:55.900287",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T16:57:28.332556",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_165728.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_165728.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:13.400\nIn general, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:22.900\nIt could be about anything! Think of it like an experiment or a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:31.200\nWe use tests all the time. For example, when you bake a cake, you might test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:38.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, maybe you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:45.200\nYou test your balance by trying to stay upright. You might fall, but that's part of the testing process!\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:51.500\nAnother example is when you go to the doctor. They might run some tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:51.500 --> 01:04.700\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new. Essentially, it helps us understand if something is working as expected or if we need to make a change.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:16.900\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to learn something, like checking if a cake is baked, learning to balance on a bike, or checking your health.\n\n01:16.900 --> 01:20.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1b998b24-4669-4a9c-82dc-d687c30e58a7": {
    "id": "1b998b24-4669-4a9c-82dc-d687c30e58a7",
