    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_165815.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:13.400\nNow, you've probably taken tests in school, but in general, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:24.700\nIt's a method used to determine the characteristics or capabilities of something or someone.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:30.300\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:36.400\nOr a chef might taste their soup to see if it needs more salt. Those are tests!\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:44.600\nThey're checking something specific. Another example could be trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:55.500\nThe \"test\" is whether you like how it tastes and if it turns out well. It's all about gathering information. So, a test is simply a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:59.100\nIt helps us understand, diagnose, or confirm something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
