    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_171038.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:06.700\nAt its most basic, a test is just a way to see how well you know something \nor how well something works.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:09.800\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb is good by screwing it in.\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:12.300\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don\u2019t realize it.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:16.300\nFor example, a spelling test at school checks if you understand how to spell words.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:20.900\nOr when you try a new recipe, you're testing if you can follow the instructions \nand make something delicious.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:22.500\nAnother example?\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:26.700\nLet's say you want to buy a used car. A mechanic might test the engine to make sure it\u2019s running smoothly.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:33.200\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method for evaluating knowledge, skills, or performance.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:37.900\nIt helps us understand where we're at and what we need to work on.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:40.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
