  "474ff27b-b6f4-4353-97cb-e394d9f89108": {
    "id": "474ff27b-b6f4-4353-97cb-e394d9f89108",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:03.802059",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T17:11:15.148216",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_171115.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_171115.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:18.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process we use to gather information and see how well something performs, or how much someone knows.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a physical exam \u2013 that's a test to see how healthy you are.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:37.300\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar. Businesses test new products before selling them to make sure they work properly.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:50.500\nEven your school quizzes are tests, designed to see how well you've understood the material. So, testing is all about gathering information and making sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:57.500\nIn short, a test is a way of learning more. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "33f1f509-74cb-4842-8c3b-00b87a0a8bc9": {
    "id": "33f1f509-74cb-4842-8c3b-00b87a0a8bc9",
