  "bbde1461-7529-4c63-873b-6837d6ef1499": {
    "id": "bbde1461-7529-4c63-873b-6837d6ef1499",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:09.294198",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T17:21:43.849482",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_172143.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_172143.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.500\nToday we're talking about tests!\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:27.400\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:40.000\nThink of it like this: a test is a simple question we ask to get a yes or no answer.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:45.500\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:48.800\nYou poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you \"yes,\" it's ready!\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:52.100\nIf it's gooey, the test says \"no,\" bake it longer.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:55.400\nAnother example could be testing if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:55.400 --> 00:58.700\nYou flip the switch. Does it light up?\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:01.700\nYes, it works! No? Then it's probably broken.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:08.400\nSo, a test is just a quick way to see if something meets a specific condition.\n\n01:08.400 --> 01:11.900\nIt's a fundamental part of figuring things out.\n\n01:11.900 --> 01:15.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
