    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: you use a test to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:35.500\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might use a toothpick test to see if it's done. You poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, then the cake has passed the test!\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:44.600\nOr, think about taking a quiz in school. That's a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:56.400\nTests are used everywhere, from checking your eyesight to making sure a bridge is safe. They help us understand things better and make sure everything is working as it should.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:00.000\nSo, a test is just a way to get information and see if something meets a certain standard. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
