    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:30.800\nOr, maybe you want to see if your flashlight works, you flip the switch. Another test!\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:40.800\nTests can be big and complicated, like a medical exam, or small and simple, like checking if a lightbulb is burned out.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:58.000\nThe main idea is to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation. Whether it's baking a cake, using a flashlight, or even learning a new skill, tests help us understand what's going on and make sure things are on the right track.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:07.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It can be anything from a quick look to a detailed examination.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:11.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
