    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer that tells you if something is working correctly, or if it's good enough.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:28.800\nFor example, you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:36.200\nOr, a doctor might test your vision to see how well you can see. It's all about gathering information.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:46.500\nWe perform tests all the time, even without realizing it. Another example: you're testing if your shoes are tied tightly enough by tugging on the laces.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:57.500\nIf they stay tied, the test passes! If they come undone, the test fails. So, in short, a test is a check, a way to see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:04.700\nWe use tests to make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
