    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:20.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to the answer, you're looking at how someone performs or something behaves to get the answer.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:30.000\nBasically, a test helps us measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:38.900\nFor example, a spelling test measures your spelling skills.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:47.500\nOr, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:56.100\nSee, tests come in all shapes and sizes! Your doctor might run blood tests, or you might take a quiz in class.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:00.100\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:03.900\nSo, remember, a test is a method for gathering information and evaluating something.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:08.000\nWe use tests to learn and improve all the time.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:11.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
