    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_174052.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:16.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\nA test is simply a way to check something, to see if it works or if it's true.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: you test a new toy to see if it's fun, right?\nOr a chef tests the soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:30.000\nIn science and math, tests are super important.\nWe use them to check if our ideas are right.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:36.100\nLet's say you think all apples are red.\nA test would be to go out and find apples.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:41.900\nIf you find a green apple, your test shows your idea wasn't quite right!\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:47.700\nAnother example is a spelling test.\nIt checks if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:53.600\nIf you spell them correctly, you pass the test!\nSo, a test is just a way of checking to see if something is correct, works, or is true.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:00.300\nIt helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
