  "4a9e73ca-c3c2-4fe9-92c0-0defdbf71adc": {
    "id": "4a9e73ca-c3c2-4fe9-92c0-0defdbf71adc",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:21.113603",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T17:45:17.268383",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_174517.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_174517.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.000\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in the world of technology, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you taste it to see if it's good. That's a test!\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:35.600\nSimilarly, when someone builds a website or an app, they need to test it to make sure all the buttons work, the pictures show up correctly, and that it doesn't crash.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:43.000\nAnother example is testing a light bulb; you screw it in to see if it lights up. That's a test too!\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:53.800\nSo, remember, a test is a way to verify something. It helps us find problems and fix them, making things better for everyone.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "476d67c3-3e55-44f3-84f9-98386a29ae2f": {
    "id": "476d67c3-3e55-44f3-84f9-98386a29ae2f",
