    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_175231.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let\u2019s talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you might test if a light bulb works by flipping the switch. The light turning on is the answer!\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:31.400\nOr, a doctor might test your temperature to see if you have a fever. The temperature reading is the answer to their question about your health.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:39.600\nTests aren't just for light bulbs and doctors, though. You take tests in school to see how well you've learned something.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:46.100\nChefs taste their food to test the flavor. Anyone can use a test for literally anything.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:54.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information. It\u2019s a way to check something and get an answer.\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:57.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
