  "6a398cea-1949-4972-8c57-dfeac3c1f019": {
    "id": "6a398cea-1949-4972-8c57-dfeac3c1f019",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:24.861152",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T17:53:25.971329",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_175325.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_175325.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:24.400\nIt's a process designed to evaluate your knowledge, skill, or ability in a particular area.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:36.900\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your spelling skills. A taste test helps you decide which flavor of ice cream you like best.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:46.700\nEven a simple experiment, like seeing if a plant grows faster in sunlight or shade, is a type of test.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:58.200\nTests can be formal, like the exams you take in school, or informal, like trying a new recipe to see if you like it. The important thing is that a test helps you gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:06.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for learning and evaluating. It helps you understand where you are and what you need to work on. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "48177d5e-0744-40e1-9723-1c287ab2b5e0": {
    "id": "48177d5e-0744-40e1-9723-1c287ab2b5e0",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:25.302237",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T17:54:15.402433",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_175415.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_175415.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:04.400\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:17.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something, to see if it works, or if it's true. Think of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's good.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:27.900\nOr, a doctor might test your temperature to see if you have a fever. In school, we often take tests to see how much we've learned about a subject.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:39.600\nThese tests can be quizzes, exams, or even projects. The important thing is they help us understand what we know well, and what we need to work on.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:47.300\nFor example, if you\u2019re learning about animals, a test might ask you to name different types of birds.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:55.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:58.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9f7d5523-8798-46cc-a991-32bed7f17c60": {
