    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_175501.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like an experiment, but usually with a specific question in mind.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:32.700\nEssentially, you're trying to see if something is true or false, good or bad, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:38.900\nFor example, a taste test tells you if you like a food.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:45.100\nA spelling test shows how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:58.900\nAnd a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. So, a test helps us learn. It gives us information that we can then use to make decisions or understand something better.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:00.600\nWhether it's knowing what flavor ice cream you prefer, or if your car is safe to drive, tests are everywhere. They're a fundamental part of how we learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
