    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_180810.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:18.900\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:27.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready. You do a test!\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test \u2013 it's done!\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:33.500\nOr imagine you're trying to guess what's in a box.\nYou might shake it \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:39.900\nThe sound you hear gives you a clue.\nTests can be used to check if something is working, to see what you know, or even just to try something new.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:55.500\nThey help us learn and understand the world around us.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information and find answers.\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:58.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1f837201-69b4-4e8f-af41-eada26779d55": {
    "id": "1f837201-69b4-4e8f-af41-eada26779d55",
