    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_181036.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.200\nHey there, welcome to this quick introduction to tests!\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:20.100\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:27.300\nWe use them all the time, even if you don't realize it.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:37.200\nThink of it as a question, or a series of questions, designed to give you an answer.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:42.500\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done, you can stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:47.800\nThat's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:53.100\nOr, if you're not sure if you have a fever, you take your temperature.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:57.800\nThat's another test! It gives you a number that tells you if you're running hot.\n```"
