  "7dca66d1-2d87-4f2b-9f50-c034505d873c": {
    "id": "7dca66d1-2d87-4f2b-9f50-c034505d873c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:35.176733",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:12:42.858043",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_181242.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_181242.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.300\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like an experiment, but designed to give you some information or a result.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:34.300\nThe basic idea is that you perform an action, or observe something, and then you measure or record what happens.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:43.900\nThat measurement or observation is your test result.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:51.500\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, tasting it is a test! You're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:58.800\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works, you screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passes! So, tests are all about finding things out and getting results. They help us learn and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0b586faf-5ba2-40ad-80e9-9fd8574a31e4": {
    "id": "0b586faf-5ba2-40ad-80e9-9fd8574a31e4",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:35.591092",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:13:35.527941",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_181335.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_181335.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:18.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like checking if something is true or false, or seeing how well something works.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:25.900\nWe use tests all the time! For example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:40.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done. Or, if you're trying to figure out which light switch turns on the lamp, you're running a little test each time you flip one.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:51.800\nTests can be formal, like the ones you take in school to show what you've learned. Or they can be informal, like checking the weather to see if you need a jacket.\n\n00:51.800 --> 01:06.200\nThe key thing is, they help us gather information and make decisions. So, a test is simply a process to gather information and see if something is true or works the way we expect.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:09.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "25c0515d-8326-4808-a4bb-20b0ba40a993": {
    "id": "25c0515d-8326-4808-a4bb-20b0ba40a993",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:36.017624",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:14:18.608331",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_181418.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_181418.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.500\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:11.900\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:18.900\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer. The answer helps us understand something better.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:23.400\nThink of it this way: a cookie baking test! You try a cookie to see if it needs more sugar. That's a test.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:27.900\nOr, a spelling test at school. It shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:33.900\nEven checking if a light bulb works is a test! You're testing if it's broken or not.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:44.200\nSo, a test is simply a way to gather information and learn something new. It helps us make decisions and understand the world around us a little bit better.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:49.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9c666639-6d4f-4c88-8655-1e50f145a152": {
    "id": "9c666639-6d4f-4c88-8655-1e50f145a152",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
