    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_181509.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, welcome!\nToday we're tackling the concept of a test.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something or someone to see how well they perform or what they know.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might taste it \u2013 that's a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:29.000\nOr, when you learn new words, a quiz is a test to see how many you remember.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:43.500\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:54.200\nThey help us understand what we've learned, identify areas where we need more practice, or simply confirm if something is working as expected.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:55.700\nSo, a test is basically a check-up, a way to evaluate and learn.\n```"
  },
