    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_181604.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:09.800\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:19.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt helps us check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\nOr, a doctor might run a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:35.800\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\nSome are super simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:44.900\nOthers are more complicated, like a school exam.\nBut the basic idea is always the same: to get information.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:52.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to help us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:54.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
