    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:07.700\nToday, we're going to explore something really fundamental: the test.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:11.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:18.000\nIt's a question, a task, or a procedure designed to reveal information.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it like this: a spelling test helps your teacher see how well you know your words.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:27.100\nOr, a taste test tells you which cookie you like best!\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:34.600\nTests aren't always about grades, though. A simple test could be trying a new recipe to see if it tastes good, or even checking if your flashlight works by pressing the on button.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:36.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:41.500\nSo, tests help us learn, discover, and confirm things.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:48.300\nThey can be formal, like exams, or informal, like trying something new.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:51.800\nThe key is that it helps us gather information and draw a conclusion.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:53.900\nThat's the basics of what a test is all about.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:55.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
