    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_182008.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.900\nA test is simply a way to find out something.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it this way: a scientist might test if a plant grows better in sunlight or in shade.\nThey put one plant in the sun and another in the shade and see which one grows taller.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:29.900\nOr, imagine you're baking cookies.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:39.300\nYou might test if adding more chocolate chips makes them taste better.\nYou bake one batch with the regular amount and another with extra chocolate chips.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:42.500\nThen you taste them!\nThat's also a test.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:50.100\nTests are used everywhere to learn and improve things.\nThey help us figure out what works and what doesn't.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:59.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding something out.\nIt's all about asking questions and observing the answers.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
