    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_182539.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:13.200\nYou've probably taken a test before, maybe in school.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:21.300\nBut what is a test, really? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:29.500\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:36.300\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:43.000\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:49.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:53.800\nOr, imagine you want to know if it's raining outside.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:01.000\nYou can test it by looking out the window. If you see raindrops, you know it's raining.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:08.700\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information and making a decision based on that information.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:18.800\nIt can be big or small, simple or complex, but the basic idea is always the same: find out something by doing something.\n\n01:18.800 --> 01:21.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
