    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:28:49.846851",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_182849.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_182849.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.100\nWhat are they, and why do we take them? Simply put, a test is a way to check your knowledge on a specific topic.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like a quick quiz to see what you've learned. Tests can come in many forms, like multiple-choice questions, true or false, or even fill-in-the-blanks.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:36.300\nFor example, a teacher might give you a test after a lesson on dinosaurs to see if you remember their names and what they ate.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:49.700\nOr, a driving test makes sure you know the rules of the road. Essentially, tests help you and your teachers understand what you already know and what you might need to study a little more.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:55.200\nSo, don't be afraid of tests! They're just a helpful tool for learning.\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:58.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
