    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_183137.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:13.000\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:25.700\nIt could be finding out if you know your alphabet, if a cake is ready, or even if a medicine works.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:36.500\nBasically, you do something, and then you see what happens. Think about it like this: your mom might test if the oven is hot enough by putting her hand near it.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:45.800\nOr, a teacher might test your knowledge with a quiz. Another example is checking if your bicycle tire has enough air by squeezing it.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:53.800\nIf it's squishy, it probably needs more air. So, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new or check if something is working like it should.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:58.800\nIt involves doing something and then observing the result.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
