    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like an experiment, but often with a specific question in mind.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:36.500\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:45.500\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:53.400\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:01.700\nThat's a test to see if it fixes the problem!\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:09.600\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if the water is hot enough for a shower.\n\n01:09.600 --> 01:17.500\nThe main idea is that you're trying something out to get information or confirm something you already suspected.\n\n01:17.500 --> 01:23.600\nSo, a test is just a method to learn or verify something.\n\n01:23.600 --> 01:25.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
