    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_184140.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:12.400\nWhat is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:21.600\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer. For example, a math test helps us understand how well you know your numbers.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:29.200\nA taste test helps us decide which cookie is the yummiest. A medical test can tell us if we're healthy.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:39.600\nSo, tests aren't just about school! They're everywhere, helping us learn, decide, and understand the world around us.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:47.600\nThey give us information. To recap, a test is a method of gathering information to learn about something.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:58.800\nWhether it\u2019s about your knowledge, your preferences, or your health, tests are valuable tools. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e13cbcf9-3f09-4a95-86d7-12c929f520ad": {
    "id": "e13cbcf9-3f09-4a95-86d7-12c929f520ad",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:50.638319",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:42:34.675338",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_184234.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_184234.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:16.100\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information or check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold. Or, maybe you take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:33.300\nIn both cases, the test is giving us valuable information.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:39.000\nAnother example? Imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:44.700\nYou might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:56.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that means the cake is ready! So, to recap, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:05.800\nIt helps us learn, diagnose, and ensure things are working as they should. That's the basics of tests in a nutshell.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b939824f-10cf-4204-a4bd-310bd249d146": {
    "id": "b939824f-10cf-4204-a4bd-310bd249d146",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:51.068408",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:43:36.072530",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_184335.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_184335.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests!\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in general, a test is just a way to check if something is working properly or to see if something is true.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: you might test a lightbulb to see if it still works by plugging it in. Or, you might test a recipe by making a small batch before you make a huge cake.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:37.000\nIn science, tests are called experiments. Scientists use them to see if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:46.200\nFor example, you could test if plants grow better in sunlight by putting one plant in the sun and another in the shade.\n\n00:46.200 --> 01:00.700\nThe plant in the sun is the test, and the shady plant is there for comparison. So, remember, a test is simply a way to find out if something is right, works, or is true.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:06.600\nIt's all about checking things out! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
