  "e82c722e-c3e4-4c38-b11a-9cc9c0259669": {
    "id": "e82c722e-c3e4-4c38-b11a-9cc9c0259669",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:54.329167",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:50:33.404232",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_185033.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_185033.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:18.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:30.100\nThink about it like this: a doctor gives you a physical exam \u2013 that's a test to check your health. Or when you bake a cake, you might taste it to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:34.800\nThat\u2019s a test too! Tests aren't just about grades in school.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:46.900\nThey help us understand where we're at and what we might need to work on. They can be formal, like a quiz, or informal, like checking if your shoelaces are tied.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:60.600\nThey're all about gathering information. So, remember, a test is a method for evaluation, used in all sorts of situations to learn something new.\n\n00:60.600 --> 00:63.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "88d78ebc-f387-43d2-a811-957ee473eb37": {
    "id": "88d78ebc-f387-43d2-a811-957ee473eb37",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:13:54.768551",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T18:51:21.899757",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_185121.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_185121.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHello and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is, in the simplest way possible.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:18.500\nA test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like an experiment, but instead of chemicals, we're usually testing skills or knowledge.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:29.300\nSo, what does that mean?\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:36.900\nWell, imagine you want to know if your plant needs more water. You might stick your finger in the soil.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:48.200\nThat's a test! Or, if you're learning your alphabet, a quiz where you have to write down the letters is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:57.700\nTests can be written, spoken, or even a physical activity. The important thing is they help us see what we know, or what something can do.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:03.700\nIn short, a test helps us to measure something, whether it's how well you know your ABCs, or how thirsty your plant is. It helps us learn and improve!\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:09.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
