    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_185402.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE\nGenerated subtitles. May contain errors.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:15.400\nThink of a test as a way to check your knowledge or skills on a certain topic.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:20.000\nIt helps you, and sometimes others, understand what you know and what you might need to work on.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:25.300\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\nYou might have a multiple-choice test, where you pick the best answer from a list.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:29.400\nOr maybe a true or false test, where you decide if a statement is correct.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:32.700\nSometimes, you might even have to write out your answers in a short essay!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:39.100\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem like \u201c2 + 2 = ?\u201d.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:45.000\nA reading test might ask you questions about a story you just read.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.700\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a tool to measure what you've learned.\nIt helps identify strengths and areas for improvement.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:56.700\nDon't be afraid of them!\nThey're a great way to learn.\n\n00:56.700 --> 00:59.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
