    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_185508.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.300\nIt's a set of questions or tasks designed to measure your knowledge, skill, or performance.\nThink about it like this: a spelling test shows how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:34.500\nOr, a taste test helps you decide which cookie is the tastiest!\nTests aren't always about getting a grade, though.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:45.600\nSometimes, a test helps you learn something new about yourself or the world around you.\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:55.600\nA scientist might run tests to see if a new invention works.\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to gather information.\n\n00:55.600 --> 01:05.600\nIt can be used in lots of different ways!\nTo recap, a test is a way to measure or find something out.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:15.000\nIt can be a quiz, an experiment, or even just a simple question.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
