    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:17.000\nNow, a test is basically a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb is good before you put it in a lamp. Tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:38.400\nFor example, a spelling test shows how good you are at spelling words. Or, a taste test can help you decide which cookie tastes the best.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:47.800\nTests can be as simple as asking a friend a question, or as complicated as a big exam at school.\n\n00:47.800 --> 01:01.500\nThe important thing is that they give us information. They tell us what we know, what we don't know, and what we need to learn.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:05.800\nSo, to recap, a test helps us learn something about knowledge or function.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.200\nThey come in all shapes and sizes,\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:12.000\nand are a really useful tool for understanding the world around us.\n\n01:12.000 --> 01:15.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
