    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_185957.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.800\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you understand a topic.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:26.500\nIt's like a simple question we ask to get an answer. The main idea behind a test is to compare what we expect to happen with what actually happens.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:31.300\nIf they match, great! The test passes. If they don't, then something might be wrong.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:38.000\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake. You test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:43.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:48.400\nOr, think about checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passes.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:54.800\nSo, a test is simply a way to verify something. We use tests all the time without even realizing it.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:01.200\nThey help us make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
