    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:20.200\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to see if something works, or to check its quality.\nThink of it like this: you want to bake a cake, but you're not sure if your oven is hot enough.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:26.700\nYou can do a little test!\nMaybe put a small piece of bread in there to see if it toasts quickly.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:31.100\nThat's the basic idea.\nTests are used everywhere!\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:38.700\nFrom checking if your phone app works correctly, to making sure a bridge can hold a certain amount of weight.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:48.000\nFor example, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:59.600\nThese tests help us understand something better or make sure something is working as it should.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:05.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to evaluate something.\nIt helps us confirm its functionality or quality.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:11.200\nRemember the oven and the bread?\nThat's testing in action!\n\n01:11.200 --> 01:16.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
