    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:11.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:19.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:28.700\nYou do a simple test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you the cake is ready!\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:35.500\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. Each time you try, you're testing your balance.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:42.000\nIf you stay upright, the test shows you're improving! Tests aren't just for cakes and bikes.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:48.500\nThey're used to check if something works, understand how well you've learned something, or even to see what your favorite color is!\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:57.700\nSo, a test is really just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:57.700 --> 00:59.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "7a1b2963-511e-4954-b2be-48824a189bdb": {
    "id": "7a1b2963-511e-4954-b2be-48824a189bdb",
