    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_190622.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_190622.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like an experiment or a check-up.\nWe use tests to see if something is true, or to measure how well something works.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:33.800\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling.\nOr, a taste test helps you decide which cookie is the yummiest!\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:46.700\nIn science, tests help prove or disprove ideas.\nScientists might test if a new fertilizer helps plants grow bigger.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:55.700\nSo, tests are a tool we use to learn, to improve, and to make decisions based on evidence.\nThey can be used for anything from learning new things to making everyday choices.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
