    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_190852.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about something super important: Tests.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:14.400\nThink of a test as just a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:23.000\nIt's like when you bake a cake. You might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:32.500\nIn science, a test might involve setting up an experiment to see if a certain idea, called a hypothesis, is correct.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:46.000\nFor example, let's say you think plants grow faster with more sunlight. You could test this by putting one plant in a sunny spot and another in a shady spot, and then see which one grows taller. That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:55.900\nSo, in short, a test is simply a way to find out if something is true or works the way we expect it to.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:05.400\nThis helps us learn and understand the world around us better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
