    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:03.900\nWhat exactly is a test, anyway?\n\n00:04.100 --> 00:07.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:10.300\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:14.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:15.800\nThink about it.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:19.700\nWhen you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:20.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.400\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken, you might try turning it on.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:26.600\nAgain, that's a test!\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:30.700\nTests can be more formal too, like the ones you take in school.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:34.200\nBut they all have the same basic idea: to gather information.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:38.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for finding something out, whether it's about cake,\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:41.500\nlightbulbs, or anything else!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:44.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
