    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like a little experiment. We use tests all the time!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:33.900\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:40.800\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:52.600\nYou put it in a lamp and turn it on. If it lights up, it passes the test \u2013 it\u2019s working! If it doesn't, well, it failed the test.\n\n00:52.600 --> 01:01.200\nSo, to recap, a test is just a process to see if something meets a certain requirement or expectation. It helps us understand how things work and if they're doing what they're supposed to.\n```"
