    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:08.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:11.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:15.400\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.800\nThe main idea behind any test is to check if something is working correctly, if something is true, or to see how well someone understands something.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:28.400\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:31.100\nThat's a test to see if the cake is done!\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:33.800\nOr, when you try to turn on a light switch,\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:37.200\nthat's a test to see if the light bulb works.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:41.900\nIn school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:47.400\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and figuring things out.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:53.200\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:56.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
