    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:04.700 --> 00:05.100\nToday we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.300\nNow, in the world of technology, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:16.200\nThink of it like a doctor checking your heartbeat to make sure your heart is healthy.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:24.200\nFor example, if you build a simple calculator, you\u2019d want to test if \"2 + 2\" really equals \"4\".\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:29.100\nOr, if you create a website, you\u2019d test if all the buttons work and the pages load properly.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:37.300\nThese tests can be done manually, where you click around and check things yourself, or automatically, where a computer runs the tests for you.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:42.500\nThe goal is always the same: to make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.800\nSo, tests are important because they help us find and fix problems early on, making everything more reliable.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:53.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
