    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, so you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:25.500\nBasically, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:31.700\nIt could be anything. For example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:42.500\nOr, your teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:50.200\nEven checking if your car starts when you turn the key is a type of test.\n\n00:50.200 --> 01:01.900\nThe goal is always to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:05.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:08.700\nIt helps us understand if things are working as they should, or if we need to make some adjustments.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:12.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
