    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to see\nhow much you know about something.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:09.500\nThink of it like checking if a\nlightbulb works.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:13.000\nYou turn it on, and if it lights up,\nit passes the test!\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:17.000\nIn school, tests help your\nteachers understand what you've learned in class.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:20.500\nThey can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:26.000\nThe goal isn't to trick you, but to see if you\nunderstand the main ideas.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:31.500\nFor example, a math test might ask you\nto solve a simple problem like 2 + 2.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:35.500\nA reading test might ask you to\nsummarize a short story.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:38.000\nThese examples help show what you've learned.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:45.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to measure\nyour understanding.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.000\nIt's a chance to show what you know and\na way for teachers to see where you might\nneed some extra help.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:56.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
