    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:14:21.073906",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T19:43:15.510284",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_194315.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_194315.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.800\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:24.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if we understand something.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:32.700\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:42.300\nA taste test checks if you like a certain flavor. Even checking if a light bulb turns on is a kind of test!\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:51.900\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you\u2019re healthy, or a teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:06.200\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. So, to recap, a test is just a way of checking something, whether it's your knowledge, your health, or even if a simple light bulb works.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:12.400\nIt helps us learn and improve. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
