    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_194405.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:24.400\nIt helps us see if something works, if it's true, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.400\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:36.500\nThat's a test! You're testing if the cake is done.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:44.600\nOr, imagine you get a new toy. You'll probably play with it to test if it's fun and if it works the way it should.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:56.000\nTests are used all the time, in all sorts of things. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, and engineers test bridges to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:57.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something out.\n```"
