    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_194708.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:17.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening, we're also observing or measuring something.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:31.900\nTests can be used for all sorts of things! For example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.700\nOr, a teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:41.900\nAnother example? Baking a cake! You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:46.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake's ready. That's a test!\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:59.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to gather information, it involves observing or measuring something, and it helps us understand things better.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:01.700\nTests help us make decisions and learn new things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
