    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_194919.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You plug it in \u2013 that's the test \u2013 and if it lights up, you know it's good!\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:36.700\nTests help us understand if things are working correctly, or if they meet certain standards.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:43.500\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:50.300\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:52.900\nAnother example is baking a cake.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:56.500\nThe taste test is a test to see if the cake is delicious! See?\n\n00:56.500 --> 00:58.900\nTests are everywhere! So, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n```"
  },
