    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_195047.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:24.000\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if we understand something.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:31.900\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:43.400\nOr, when you're learning something new in school, you might take a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:52.800\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test showing the cake is done!\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:02.200\nOr, if you're learning your ABCs, your teacher might ask you to recite them. That's a test to see if you know your letters.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:05.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:11.900\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:11.900 --> 01:15.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
