  "380522a9-2016-45bf-b838-48a1caaa90bb": {
    "id": "380522a9-2016-45bf-b838-48a1caaa90bb",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:14:27.604014",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T19:55:06.062737",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_195505.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_195505.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:15.600\nYou've probably taken them at school, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:34.600\nThink of it like this: imagine you're learning to ride a bike. The first time you try, you might wobble a lot.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:41.500\nA test would be seeing how far you can ride without falling.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:48.400\nOr, if you're learning new words, a test could be matching those words to their definitions.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:56.800\nTests aren't just for school, either. A chef might taste a soup to test if it has enough salt. A doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:00.400\nSo, tests help us measure things and see where we can improve.\n```"
  },
