    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_195826.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.200\nThink of a test as a way to check something. It's how we find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:21.000\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake. You might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:33.400\nYou stick it in, and if it comes out clean, the test shows the cake is ready. Or, if you're playing a game, a test might be a question you have to answer.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:41.200\nAnother example is a water test. You might test the water in a swimming pool to see if it\u2019s safe to swim in.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:51.000\nThe test tells you about the water quality. So, to recap, a test is simply a way to examine or evaluate something.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:58.200\nIt helps us understand more about the thing we're testing. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a5b1bcb6-c7c5-4ba8-9805-8d990a1e7529": {
    "id": "a5b1bcb6-c7c5-4ba8-9805-8d990a1e7529",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:14:29.713639",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T19:59:14.864625",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_195914.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_195914.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and then seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:23.300\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. Think about it: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:31.800\nOr, you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good. In school, tests help show what you've learned.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:40.100\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:48.800\nA spelling test might ask you to spell words correctly. These tests help measure your skills and knowledge.\n\n00:48.800 --> 01:01.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information. It helps us understand something better by giving us a way to check and measure.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:05.500\nTests can be simple, or they can be complex, but they all have the same goal: to give us answers!\n01:05.500 --> 01:08.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9a1fb754-dbf4-4da7-b2c2-c99e08bf8bb7": {
    "id": "9a1fb754-dbf4-4da7-b2c2-c99e08bf8bb7",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:14:30.193287",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T20:00:01.245575",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_200001.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_200001.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.300\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like an experiment, but not always in a science lab! Basically, you're trying to answer a question.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:36.900\nYou perform the test, observe the results, and then draw a conclusion.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:44.000\nFor example, you might test if a new plant food helps your flowers grow bigger.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:51.100\nYou'd use the plant food on some flowers and not on others, then compare their growth. That's a test!\n\n00:51.100 --> 01:03.300\nOr, you could test if a new recipe tastes good by having your friends try it. Their opinions are your results.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:11.300\nSo, remember: a test is about asking a question, doing something to find the answer, and then seeing what happens.\n\n01:11.300 --> 01:19.300\nIt's a simple process we use all the time to learn new things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
