    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.900\nNow, a test is basically a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:28.300\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it to see if it's done baking. Or, a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:37.100\nThe main idea behind a test is to get information. It helps us understand things better.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:50.500\nFor instance, a teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a lesson. That information helps them know what to teach next.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:59.600\nSo, tests can be simple like checking the weather outside to see if you need a coat, or more complex like a science experiment.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:08.700\nThe important thing is that they give us data to make decisions.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:16.100\nThey help us confirm, deny, or learn something new.\n\n01:16.100 --> 01:20.700\nIn short, tests are just ways of gathering information to see if something is true or working correctly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
