    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_200135.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.800\nWell, simply put, a test is just a way to find something out. It's a method we use to gather information and see how something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if an apple is ripe.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:33.300\nYou might squeeze it gently, smell it, or even take a small bite.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:39.500\nThose are all little tests! They help you decide if the apple is ready to eat.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:45.700\nOr imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:55.300\nEvery time you try to balance, that's a test. You're testing your ability to stay upright. So, a test is simply a way to learn by trying something out and seeing what happens.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:58.700\nIt's all about gathering information. That's the basic idea of what a test is. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
