    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.100\nHey there, welcome! Today we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:03.100 --> 00:07.700\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:10.300\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:10.300 --> 00:16.000\nThe main idea is to check if something works, or if it's good, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:21.500\nFor example, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:26.600\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it has enough salt.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:31.700\nAnother example could be testing a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids to play with.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:38.700\nBasically, we test things to learn more about them and make sure they are doing what they are supposed to do.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:45.800\nSo, remember, a test is a way to learn about something by checking it or trying it out.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:47.600\nSimple as that!\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:58.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
