    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_201343.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.799\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:06.799 --> 00:16.799\nNow, a test, in the simplest terms, is a way to check something. It\u2019s like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:16.799 --> 00:27.399\nThink of it like this: you might test if a cake is done by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the test says it\u2019s ready!\n\n00:27.399 --> 00:35.699\nOr, maybe you test if a light bulb works by flipping the switch. If it lights up, the test is positive!\n\n00:35.699 --> 00:51.399\nTests aren't just for baking or electronics though. Doctors use tests to check your health, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even you test things every day, like testing the temperature of your bath water.\n\n00:51.399 --> 01:03.799\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out if something is working, true, or ready. They help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n01:03.799 --> 01:07.399\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
