    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_201758.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.800\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:28.900\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it! Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:37.400\nThe question could be anything. Like, \"Does this cake taste good?\"\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:45.900\nYou bake the cake, someone tastes it, and their reaction is the answer, or the test result.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:54.600\nOr, \"Can this bridge hold weight?\" Engineers will actually load the bridge with increasing weight until they get their answer.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:04.300\nAnother simple example is a spelling test at school. The teacher asks you to spell words, and your written answers show what you know.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.900\nSo, tests help us learn, prove, or understand something.\n\n01:07.900 --> 01:19.700\nBasically, a test is a question or process designed to give us information.\n\n01:19.700 --> 01:23.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
