  "bc808ed6-82e7-4d9b-9a1a-e80261f4ccbe": {
    "id": "bc808ed6-82e7-4d9b-9a1a-e80261f4ccbe",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:14:41.245114",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T20:19:22.788599",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_201922.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_201922.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:23.400\nIt's like an experiment or a question you ask to see what happens or what the answer is.\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:32.100\nOr, a taste test lets you decide which cookie tastes the best.\nThese tests all help us learn or make a decision.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:45.800\nFor example, you might test if a toy car goes faster on a smooth surface or a carpet.\nOr, you could test different types of plant food to see which one helps a plant grow the tallest.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:53.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new by trying something out and observing the result.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:00.700\nIt's all about exploring and finding answers!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d68b623b-a940-4a70-bd39-e899ee41cb89": {
    "id": "d68b623b-a940-4a70-bd39-e899ee41cb89",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:14:41.691040",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T20:20:13.793697",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_202013.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_202013.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\nThink of it like an investigation.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:24.700\nWe want to learn about something, so we ask questions or perform actions to get answers.\nThe main idea is to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:34.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\nOr, a taste test checks which food you like better.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.900\nLet's say you're baking a cake.\nYou might do a \"toothpick test\" \u2013 poking the cake with a toothpick.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:46.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\nThat's a test!\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:51.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information and making sure things are as they should be.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:57.300\nIt helps us learn and improve.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b4e2ec5f-8276-4cc7-b3d3-1efd82f8eb07": {
    "id": "b4e2ec5f-8276-4cc7-b3d3-1efd82f8eb07",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:14:42.129276",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T20:21:02.272774",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_202102.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_202102.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.500\nWhat are they, and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:24.400\nThink about it like this: Your teacher gives you a quiz. That's a test to see how much you learned in class.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:36.300\nOr, a doctor might run a test on your blood to see if you're healthy. Companies even test new products, like phones, to make sure they don't break easily.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:41.400\nSo, tests help us measure things. They give us information.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:49.600\nAnd that information helps us make decisions, like what to study next, or what kind of medicine you need.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:57.400\nIn short, a test is a tool for learning and improvement. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
