    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_202958.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:59.4\n1\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n2\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n3\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.900\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works. Think about it like this: if you want to know if your cookies are done baking, you do a test \u2013 you poke them with a toothpick.\n\n4\n00:25.900 --> 00:38.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies pass the test! Or, if you're learning your ABCs, your teacher might give you a test to see how many letters you know.\n\n5\n00:38.200 --> 00:44.000\nTests aren't scary; they're just tools.\n\n6\n00:44.000 --> 00:55.900\nThey help us learn and improve. They let us know what we're doing well and where we might need some extra practice. So next time you hear the word \"test\", remember it's just a way to learn more about something.\n\n7\n00:55.900 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
