    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_203749.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process we use to gather information and see how well something works or how someone performs.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might do a simple test \u2013 stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:29.500\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:33.900\nOr, if you want to see how well you know your ABCs, someone might ask you to recite them.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:42.600\nThat's a test too! Tests aren't just about grades in school. They're used everywhere, from checking if a new toy is safe to making sure a car engine runs smoothly.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:56.200\nBasically, a test helps us understand something better. So, remember, a test is a process for gathering information to understand something or evaluate its performance.\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:00.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
