    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_204120.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:27.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:37.500\nIn general, a test helps us figure out if something is working the way it's supposed to, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:47.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a teacher might give you a quiz to see if you understand the material.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:59.000\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same basic purpose: to give us information about something. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.600\nEssentially, a test is a simple way to find out if something passes or fails. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
