    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_204437.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.200\nWhat are they and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it. The toothpick is a little test!\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:34.000\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned in class. They can be multiple choice, true or false, or even asking you to solve a problem.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:43.900\nFor example, a math test might ask you what two plus two equals. Or a reading test might ask you to explain what a story was about.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:49.200\nTests aren\u2019t meant to trick you. They're just a way to check your understanding.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:59.800\nSo, remember, a test is a tool for learning and growing. It helps you and your teacher see what you know and what you might need a little more help with.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
