    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.300\nNow, you might be thinking about school, but a test is really just a way to find out if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:21.200\nIt's like checking! Think of it this way: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:27.100\nThe test is screwing it into a lamp. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:33.000\nAnother example: you bake a cake. The test is tasting it.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.900\nIf it tastes good, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:49.200\nSo, a test is simply a procedure to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:59.700\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. We test recipes, we test our shoelaces to see if they're tied, we even test the weather by looking out the window.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:06.900\nIt's all about checking to make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:14.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
