  "1c671290-bce5-433c-8d82-aa021f08cd2f": {
    "id": "1c671290-bce5-433c-8d82-aa021f08cd2f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:15:08.255488",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:05:44.539390",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_210544.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_210544.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.999\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find out if something works as it should.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: If you bake a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the center. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:33.500\nOr, if you're checking if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:45.600\nEssentially, a test is any procedure designed to check the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:55.300\nWhether it's a cake, a lightbulb, or even a computer program, tests help us make sure things are working the way they're supposed to.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:58.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking!\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:03.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
