  "38e9eef8-f4db-486b-8253-6204ce10c8f9": {
    "id": "38e9eef8-f4db-486b-8253-6204ce10c8f9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:15:14.394321",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:15:59.682411",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_211559.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_211559.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:25.400\nIt's a process we use to gather information or measure something. Think of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you can test it by sticking a toothpick in the center.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:30.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:39.300\nOr, if you want to know how well you understand a new topic, you might take a quiz. That quiz is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:50.300\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if your car is working properly to seeing how well you remember what you learned in school.\n\n00:50.300 --> 01:00.600\nThey help us understand where we are and what we might need to work on. So, remember, a test is just a method for finding something out.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:08.600\nIt can be a simple check or a more formal evaluation. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "85afb58b-e810-4a1f-94bb-2d14f72defd7": {
    "id": "85afb58b-e810-4a1f-94bb-2d14f72defd7",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:15:14.882119",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:16:43.828727",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_211643.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_211643.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNo need to worry, it\u2019s not THAT kind of test! In this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:21.400\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and then you taste it. That's a test!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:26.800\nYou're checking if it tastes good. Or, imagine you buy a new toy car.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:32.200\nYou roll it across the floor to see if the wheels turn. That's another test!\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:42.500\nTests help us find problems early, before they become bigger issues. For example, a doctor might run blood tests to check your health.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:54.100\nCar manufacturers test their cars before they sell them to make sure they are safe. So, a test is just a way to verify something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:62.800\nRemember, testing is all about checking things work as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
