  "4634653f-7326-41ff-b45d-7eb7305d3a06": {
    "id": "4634653f-7326-41ff-b45d-7eb7305d3a06",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:15:15.872814",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:18:19.560798",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_211819.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_211819.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school exams. A test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might taste a little piece to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:32.200\nOr, if you're building a birdhouse, you might put it outside and see if the birds actually use it. That's a test!\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:45.800\nIn computers, we also use tests to make sure our programs are working correctly. We might test if a button does what it's supposed to, or if a calculation is giving us the right answer.\n\n00:45.800 --> 01:02.100\nTesting helps us find problems and fix them before they cause bigger issues. So, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected, whether it's a cake, a birdhouse, or a computer program.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:09.300\nIt's all about making sure things are doing what they should! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "78fad342-0b42-43ff-b0ec-2d1f13548c42": {
    "id": "78fad342-0b42-43ff-b0ec-2d1f13548c42",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:15:16.409673",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:19:09.739120",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_211909.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_211909.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:25.000\nIt's a process designed to give us information about a person, object, or situation.\nThink of it like this: a taste test tells you if food is delicious.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:33.700\nA doctor might run blood tests to see if you're healthy.\nOr, a student takes a test at school to show what they've learned.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:49.800\nSo, tests help us measure things, check for problems, or demonstrate knowledge.\nThey can be simple, like checking if a light bulb works, or complex, like a scientific experiment.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:56.800\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\nIn short, a test is a way to get answers.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
