    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:20:45.556273",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_212045.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_212045.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:18.000\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:23.600\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:33.400\nWe use tests all the time! A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:43.900\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:49.600\nEven tasting a new food is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing to see if you like it!\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:55.300\nFor example, a simple test could be: \"Does this light bulb work?\"\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:00.700\nYou plug it in. If it lights up, the test passes. If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:06.100\nAnother example: a spelling test. You're asked to spell words correctly.\n\n01:06.100 --> 01:14.700\nThat's a test of your spelling knowledge. So, remember, a test is simply a method for gathering information or checking if something works as expected.\n\n01:14.700 --> 01:21.000\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
