    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_212256.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.900\nNow, you've probably heard that word a lot, but what does it really mean?\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:26.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:30.100\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, or seeing how well you know your ABCs.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:33.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is ready.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:43.600\nYou insert a toothpick. That's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test and is done.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:52.100\nIf it's gooey, well, it needs more time.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:58.400\nAnother example: Your doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:04.700\nThey check your temperature and look in your throat. Those are both little tests!\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:12.600\nSo, a test is just a way of gathering information. It helps us understand things better and make decisions.\n\n01:12.600 --> 01:17.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
