    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_212756.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:07.400 --> 00:19.100\nToday we're going to explore something really important: tests. Now, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:29.000\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:38.600\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:47.000\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:55.400\nThe whole point is to get information. For example, you could test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in and turning it on.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:09.200\nIf it lights up, it passes the test! Or, you could test if a cookie is done by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cookie is ready.\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:16.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to find out if something is working as expected, or to gather information.\n\n01:16.000 --> 01:22.800\nIt helps us understand the world around us.\n\n01:22.800 --> 01:27.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
