    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_213151.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:22.900\nIt could be a physical test, like checking if your car's brakes work. Or, it could be an exam in school to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:35.900\nThe main idea is to get some information about a person, object, or situation. For example, a doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel sick.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:48.900\nOr, a food company might test a new recipe to make sure it tastes good. Think of it like this: you test the water temperature before jumping in the pool to make sure it's not too cold.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:59.600\nYou're using a mini-test to gather information before you take a bigger step. So, a test is just a process of checking something to learn more about it.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:09.300\nIn short, tests help us understand things better, whether it's our health, our knowledge, or even our swimming pool!\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:12.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
