    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nNow, you might be thinking about school, but a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your flashlight is working.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:24.900\nThe test? Turning it on!\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:29.900\nIf it shines, great, it passes the test. If not, well, it fails.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:34.900\nOr imagine baking a cake.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:39.800\nYou test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:43.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:44.900\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:53.200\nBasically, a test is just a simple procedure to see if something meets a certain standard or works correctly.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:57.800\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:03.400\nSo, remember, tests are just ways to check things.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:07.500\nThey help us make sure everything is working as it should.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:11.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
