    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_214052.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.200\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. Tests help us see if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:30.900\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:37.500\nOr, think about baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it\u2019s sweet enough.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:44.100\nAnother example? When you take a quiz at school, that\u2019s a test to see how much you\u2019ve learned.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:53.300\nSo, tests are all about checking things. They help us understand the world around us a little bit better. Basically, a test helps us find out what we need to know. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "14e7b77f-58b6-4dc1-a61f-e8ae3490b8ee": {
    "id": "14e7b77f-58b6-4dc1-a61f-e8ae3490b8ee",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:15:29.327900",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:41:51.228787",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_214151.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_214151.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:10.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school,\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:15.200\nbut in programming, a test is a way to check if your code is working correctly.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:20.000\nThink of it like a mini-experiment for your software.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:26.000\nBasically, you give your code some input, and then you check if the output is what you expect.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:31.000\nFor example, let's say you have a function that adds two numbers.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:36.000\nA test would be to give it 2 and 3, and then check if the answer is 5.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:39.000\nIf it is, the test passes!\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:41.800\nIf it's not, then something's wrong with your code.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:48.000\nTests help you find bugs early and make sure your code keeps working as you add more features.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:54.000\nSo, tests are about verifying and maintaining the quality of your code.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:57.100\nThey ensure things function as expected.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "29f9263b-18df-4f2c-a6d8-4b9cd4065671": {
    "id": "29f9263b-18df-4f2c-a6d8-4b9cd4065671",
    "topic": "Test",
