    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_214241.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This VTT file was generated by an AI.  It may contain errors. Please review and correct as needed.\n\n00:00.173 --> 00:05.773\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're diving into the basics of a test.\n\n00:05.773 --> 00:13.733\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:13.733 --> 00:25.903\nIt helps us measure your understanding or skill.\nThink of it like this: if you're learning to bake a cake, a taste test is a way to see if you followed the recipe correctly.\n\n00:25.903 --> 00:36.903\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, your ability to stay upright shows you're passing the \"balance test.\"\n\n00:36.903 --> 00:47.633\nTests aren't just for school, either.\nDoctors use tests to check your health, and scientists use tests to prove or disprove their ideas.\n\n00:47.633 --> 00:59.673\nThey're really just a tool to gather information.\nSo, a test is a way to measure knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:59.673 --> 01:03.153\nHopefully, this gives you a clearer idea of what a test is all about.\n\n01:03.153 --> 01:06.783\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
