    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_214552.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really fundamental: tests.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:16.100\nThink of a test as a way to find out something specific. It's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:24.000\nFor example, a simple test could be tasting a new fruit to see if you like it. You're testing your preference!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:30.600\nOr, think about a doctor giving you a check-up. They're running tests to see how healthy you are.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:38.000\nThey might check your temperature or listen to your heartbeat. Another example is a test you might take in school.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:49.800\nIt helps your teacher see how well you understand the material. So, tests help us learn things, confirm things, and understand things better.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:59.000\nThey are a tool for gathering information. In short, a test is just a way of gathering information in a systematic way.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:06.500\nIt helps us answer questions and learn new things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
