    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_214807.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way of finding out if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:30.700\nBasically, a test is a procedure designed to check the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:39.300\nIt could be testing if a toy still works with fresh batteries, or even testing if your cookies taste good after you bake them.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:49.300\nYou're trying to confirm something. So, if you're building a tower of blocks, testing it would be gently pushing it to see if it's stable.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:56.800\nIf it falls over, you know you need to adjust it. Tests help us learn and improve things all the time.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:05.800\nRemember, a test is just a way to see if something works as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
