    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:06.000\nToday we're going to explore something fundamental: what is a test?\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:11.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.000\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.000\nThink about it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you do a simple test.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:24.000\nYou stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:30.000\nOr, if you want to know if you understand a new concept, you might take a practice quiz.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:33.000\nThat quiz is a test, helping you see what you've learned.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:40.000\nTests can be used to check all sorts of things, from the safety of a new car to your understanding of, well, pretty much anything!\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:45.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:48.000\nIt helps us understand something better.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
