    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_215035.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_215035.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.200\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand something better.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes a soup to test if it needs more salt. Or a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:27.300\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:35.800\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. It helps you and your teacher know if you've learned how to spell certain words.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:46.000\nOr maybe you test a new recipe to see if your family likes it. So, to recap, a test is a method for gathering information.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:53.000\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make better decisions. It's all about finding things out!\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e41415a0-8084-437c-bfc5-269e0699a0a1": {
    "id": "e41415a0-8084-437c-bfc5-269e0699a0a1",
