    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:51:25.603025",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_215125.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_215125.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! \nToday we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:19.100\nNow, a test is basically a way to see how well you know something or how well something works. \nThink of it like checking if you understand a lesson, or making sure a toy does what it's supposed to.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:28.800\nSo, how does it work? \nWell, you get some questions or tasks, and you try your best to answer them or complete them.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:41.800\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. \nOr, if you're testing a new toy car, you'd see if it can drive straight and doesn't fall apart.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:51.900\nThe results of a test show you what you're good at and what you might need to work on. \nThat's why tests are so helpful \u2013 they give you information to improve!\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:00.200\nRemember, tests aren't scary, they're just tools for learning. \nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6fb04a7f-6a50-449c-a669-5cdf2f746dd4": {
    "id": "6fb04a7f-6a50-449c-a669-5cdf2f746dd4",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:15:35.573183",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T21:52:15.234664",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_215215.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_215215.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:18.800\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find something out. It's a method or procedure used to determine something about a person, object, or even an idea.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you can stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:36.800\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready. Or, if you want to know if you understand a new concept, you might take a quiz.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:47.800\nThe quiz is the test that shows you how well you learned. Tests can come in many forms, from simple observations to complex experiments.\n\n00:47.800 --> 01:01.500\nThey help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions. So, next time you hear the word \"test\", remember it's just a tool to help us understand something better.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:05.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
