    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_220543.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_220543.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something, or someone!\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it as a way to gather information. Tests can come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:28.000\nYour doctor might run a blood test to check your health. A teacher might give you a quiz to see what you've learned.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:39.500\nOr even a chef might taste a soup to see if it needs more salt \u2013 that's a test too! For example, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:45.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a simple test.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:55.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool for learning or checking something. It helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:02.200\nIn short, tests are all about gathering information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
