    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_221336.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_221336.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:23.800\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to. Think of it like this: you have an idea, you build something based on that idea, and then you test it to see if it actually works.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:30.100\nFor example, if you bake a cake, you test it by tasting it! Does it taste good? Is it cooked all the way through?\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:40.200\nOr, if you build a birdhouse, you test it by putting it outside and seeing if birds actually use it. Does it stay up in the wind? Does it keep the birds safe?\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:44.600\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to see if something is doing what you expect it to do.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:54.300\nIt's how we learn and improve!\n\n00:54.300 --> 00:57.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
