    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_222447.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of a test.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:16.300\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:26.400\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:35.400\nIt could be a school test, like a quiz to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:44.400\nOr it could be testing a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:54.700\nMaybe you're testing a toy to see if it's strong enough. The point is, you're trying to learn something by putting something to the test.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:07.400\nFor example, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works. Or a builder might test materials to make sure a building is safe.\n\n01:07.400 --> 01:14.500\nSo, a test is just a method to gather information and draw a conclusion.\n\n01:14.500 --> 01:27.200\nTo sum it up, a test helps us learn, improve, and make informed decisions. It's all about asking questions and finding the answers.\n\n01:27.200 --> 01:32.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
