    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_223316.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nWhat are they, and why are they important?\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:26.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It's how we find out if something works, if something is true, or if something is the right answer.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:32.300\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:38.500\nThat's a test to see if the cake is done!\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:44.700\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. Each time you try, you're testing your balance.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:51.200\nYou're seeing if you can stay upright. Doctors use tests to check if you're healthy. Teachers give tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:55.200\nSo, tests help us understand things better and make sure everything is working as it should.\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:58.000\nThey are a key part of learning and problem-solving.\n\n00:58.000 --> 00:58.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
