    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_223405.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.800\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we usually mean a way to check something.\nLike, how well you understand a topic, or how well something works.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: a test is just a set of questions or tasks designed to give you information.\nFor example, a quiz in school is a test to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:42.100\nOr, if you're trying out a new recipe, tasting it is a test to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:51.600\nTests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb turns on.\nOr, they can be more complex, like a science experiment.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:55.800\nThe important thing is that they help us learn and improve.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:01.000\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and seeing where we stand.\n01:01.000 --> 01:01.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
