    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer, or trying something out to see if it works.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:26.000\nBasically, a test helps us figure things out. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:34.500\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar. You're checking to see if it's right!\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:45.100\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on, or more complicated, like a doctor running tests to see what's making you sick.\n\n00:45.100 --> 01:00.900\nIn every case, a test is about finding information or confirming something. So, to recap, a test is a way of checking something to see if it's correct, working, or meeting a certain standard.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:07.200\nIt helps us learn and understand. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
