    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_224333.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.200\nNow, a test is basically just a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:25.700\nIn general, a test helps you figure out if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:36.200\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to check your understanding of a subject.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:42.800\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:49.600\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\nIf not, well, it probably needs replacing.\n\n00:49.600 --> 01:01.900\nSo, tests are all about checking things to see if they meet certain requirements.\nThey help us learn, diagnose, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:05.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
