    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:16:08.030615",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T22:49:59.183466",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_224959.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_224959.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests,\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:04.900\nand no, not the kind you cram for.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:07.400\nA test, in a general sense, is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:11.300\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:14.700\nFor example, a taste test tells you which food tastes better.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:20.200\nOr, a simple on/off switch is a test to see if your lightbulb is working.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:23.200\nIf the light turns on, the test passed!\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:26.700\nIf it doesn't, well, you probably need a new bulb.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:29.500\nTests help us understand things.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:34.200\nThey confirm if something works as expected, or if something needs to be fixed.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:38.700\nSo, a test is just a method, big or small, to see if something is true.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:41.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3204bcc6-652c-4476-9e9a-eac399d5a4ed": {
    "id": "3204bcc6-652c-4476-9e9a-eac399d5a4ed",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:16:08.482186",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T22:51:03.938092",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_225103.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_225103.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.200\nNow, a test is just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:22.200\nThe main idea behind a test is to see if something is true or not.\nWe do this by looking at evidence, or data.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:31.400\nWe then compare that data to what we expect to see.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:39.900\nFor example, a taste test helps us find out which cookie tastes better.\nA spelling test helps us find out which words someone knows how to spell.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:48.400\nAnd a medical test can help find out if you're healthy.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:56.900\nSo, in short, a test is a process where we gather information to learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:02.200\nWhether it's about cookies, spelling, or your health, tests help us understand the world a little better.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f3b79ba9-dca8-47ec-94ce-5c073e9bbdf2": {
    "id": "f3b79ba9-dca8-47ec-94ce-5c073e9bbdf2",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
