    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_225149.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_225149.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:17.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:25.200\nYou stick a toothpick in it. That's a test! The result of the test, whether the toothpick comes out clean or not, tells you something about the cake.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:31.600\nTests aren't just for baking, of course. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:41.300\nOr your teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:50.100\nSo, a test helps us understand something better by giving us information.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:53.600\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. Remember, a test is just a way to check and learn! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "77b31771-3d67-4ce0-a16c-307fa909da2b": {
    "id": "77b31771-3d67-4ce0-a16c-307fa909da2b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
