    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_225238.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:17.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process that helps us gather information or see how well something works.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks your knowledge of words. Or, a taste test helps you decide which cookie you like best.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:31.600\nSee? Different goals, but both are tests!\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:41.700\nAnother example is a doctor running tests to figure out what\u2019s making you feel unwell. They might check your temperature, or take a blood sample.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:51.800\nAll these things give them information. So, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new or measure something specific.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:58.900\nIt helps us understand things better, whether it's our spelling skills or the best flavor of ice cream.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
