    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_225644.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:28.600\nThat's a test! In school, you take tests to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:42.500\nIn science, scientists run experiments that are actually tests to see if their ideas are right. If you're buying a used car, you might take it for a test drive to make sure it runs smoothly.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:45.100\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:54.800\nThey help us learn, improve, and make better decisions. So, remember, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:06.500\nWhether it's a cake, a car, or your own knowledge, tests help us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2424cdbd-a81d-4cd4-9254-16910c32a364": {
    "id": "2424cdbd-a81d-4cd4-9254-16910c32a364",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:16:11.883556",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-31T22:57:31.704238",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20251231_225731.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_225731.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test actually is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:19.200\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to find something out. It's a procedure designed to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, a product's quality, or even how well a new medicine works.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:28.400\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your spelling skills. A taste test helps decide which cookie tastes better.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:38.300\nAnd a medical test helps doctors understand what's going on inside your body. Tests often involve asking questions or performing tasks.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:51.600\nThen, the answers or results are compared to a standard or benchmark. So, if you get 8 out of 10 correct on a quiz, that shows you understood 80% of the material.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:59.900\nBasically, a test gives us information to help us make decisions. It's a tool for learning and improvement.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
