    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_231312.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.900\nToday we're tackling something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:25.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:37.200\nIt's a process designed to measure your knowledge, ability, or even the quality of something.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:47.200\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:57.200\nThat's a test! Or, if your doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:07.200\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n01:07.200 --> 01:14.900\nThey can be multiple choice, true or false, or even essays.\n\n01:14.900 --> 01:22.800\nSo, tests are all about gathering information.\n\n01:22.800 --> 01:30.700\nThey help us understand where we stand and what we need to work on.\n\n01:30.700 --> 01:37.300\nThey're valuable tools for learning and improvement.\n\n01:37.300 --> 01:40.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
