    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_231613.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. Tests help us understand if things are working correctly, or if something needs to be checked.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:35.000\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:39.600\nOr, a doctor might run tests to check your health and make sure you're feeling your best.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:49.600\nAnother example is testing a lightbulb. You plug it in to see if it lights up. That's a simple test! It tells you if the bulb is good or if it needs replacing.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:59.900\nSo, tests are all about finding information and understanding something better. In short, a test is a way to gather information and check if something is working as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
