    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_232105.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:32.200\nThink of it like a check-up for your brain! It helps you and your teachers see what you've learned and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:44.200\nTests can come in different forms, like multiple choice where you pick the best answer, or true or false where you decide if a statement is correct.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:55.900\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem like \"2 + 2.\" Or a reading test might ask you questions about a story you just read.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:03.900\nThe important thing is to try your best and show what you know. So, in a nutshell, a test is just a tool to measure your knowledge and help you learn even better.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:08.500\nRemember to relax, read carefully, and answer honestly.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:09.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
