    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_232603.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.700\nHey there, welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:15.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:19.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, right?\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:23.300\nSo, you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:26.500\nThat's a test!\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:29.700\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:30.800\nGreat, the cake is ready.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:32.700\nIt comes out gooey?\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:34.500\nNot so ready.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:37.700\nSee, the toothpick is the test, and the cake is what we're testing.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:44.800\nAnother example? A doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature or listening to your heart.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:50.700\nOr, a teacher gives you a quiz to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:56.100\nSo, a test is just a process or tool used to get information.\n\n00:56.100 --> 00:59.200\nIt helps us understand, evaluate, or check something.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:00.100\nPretty useful, huh?\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:02.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
