    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_233013.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:05.000\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:10.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you do a test.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:11.600\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:15.200\nThe toothpick coming out clean? That's a positive test!\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:16.700\nIt means your cake is ready.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:18.500\nA gooey toothpick?\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:20.000\nNegative test!\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:21.700\nNeeds more baking.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:27.300\nSimilarly, a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:31.900\nOr a teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.500\nTests help us learn about things and make decisions based on the results.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:39.400\nBasically, it's just a way to get information.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:45.100\nSo, test means check something and see the result.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:51.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
