    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:19.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:30.500\nThat's a test! You're checking if the lightbulb performs its function.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:36.100\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:41.700\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:47.300\nThat's a test to check the cake's readiness.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:55.300\nOr maybe you're learning a new language. A quiz is a test to see how well you understand the vocabulary and grammar.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:03.400\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method for evaluating something and seeing if it meets a certain standard or expectation. We use tests every day, often without even realizing it!\n\n```"
