    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_234107.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:10.200\nnot the kind you dread taking in school, but tests in the broader sense.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:11.600\nA test is simply a way\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:13.200\nto find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:16.700\nThink of it as an experiment or an examination.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:20.500\nIt helps us check if something works, if something is true,\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:23.400\nor if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:27.100\nFor example, you might \"test\" if a lightbulb works by screwing it in.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:29.800\nOr a chef might \"test\" the soup\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:32.200\nto see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.000\nEven a doctor asking you questions about your health is performing a test\nto figure out what's going on.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.200\nSo, a test is all about gathering information and drawing conclusions.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:46.600\nIt's a fundamental way we learn and improve things all around us.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:49.700\nRemember, a test helps us understand something better.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:52.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
