    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_234154.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:21.000\nIt's a procedure we use to gather information.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:29.400\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:37.800\nThat's a test! The toothpick tells you if it's still gooey inside.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:46.200\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you're learning.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:59.400\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's making you sick. Even trying on clothes is a kind of test to see if they fit!\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:08.100\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all share the same goal: to give us answers.\n\n01:08.100 --> 01:16.800\nTo recap, a test is a process for gathering information.\n\n01:16.800 --> 01:20.400\nIt can be as simple as poking a cake or as complex as a medical exam.\n\n01:20.400 --> 01:23.500\nIt all comes down to finding something out.\n\n01:23.500 --> 01:27.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
