    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20251231_234335.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:26.700\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:34.900\nThink of it as a way to check if something is working, is true, or is good enough.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:46.300\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nA taste test checks if you like the flavor of something.\nAnd a stress test on a bridge checks if it's strong enough to handle heavy traffic.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:58.100\nTests help us make decisions.\nIf your spelling test shows you missed a lot of words, you know you need to study more.\nIf the taste test is a thumbs-down, the chef might change the recipe.\nAnd if the bridge passes the stress test, we know it's safe to drive on.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:01.700\nSo, a test is just a structured way to get information and make informed choices.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
