    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:16:49.012979",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:02:01.660664",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_000201.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_000201.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test is really just a way to see how well you know something. It could be about anything, from your knowledge of colors to how good you are at math.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:28.000\nBasically, a test presents you with questions or problems, and you try to answer them correctly. The more right answers you get, the better you've done on the test!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:36.900\nThink about it like this: your teacher might give you a test on the alphabet. The test would ask you to identify different letters.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:47.800\nOr, a doctor might give you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:53.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool for checking your understanding. It helps you and others see what you know and where you might need to learn more.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:56.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b11e2ee5-d0b8-40b3-be52-6daaad39f26a": {
    "id": "b11e2ee5-d0b8-40b3-be52-6daaad39f26a",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:16:49.422788",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:02:50.740529",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_000250.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_000250.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.500\nA test is simply a way to find out something, whether it's how well you know a subject, or if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like a question that needs an answer. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:34.300\nOr, when you\u2019re baking, you might test the cake with a toothpick to see if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:44.700\nSo, a test is just a method of checking something. It helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:53.500\nTests are everywhere, from school to science and even in the kitchen! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
