    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_000433.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:06.900 --> 00:13.200\nToday, we're diving into something super important: tests! \n\n00:13.200 --> 00:17.800\nA test, at its core, is just a way to find out information.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if the cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:24.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:29.400\nIn school, tests help us see what we\u2019ve learned.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:34.700\nThey can be multiple choice, where you pick the best answer, or maybe you have to write out the answer yourself.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:40.100\nFor example, a math test might ask you what 2 plus 2 equals.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:45.200\nOr, a spelling test could ask you how to spell the word \"apple.\"\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:46.900\nSee? It\u2019s just a way to check your knowledge.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:53.400\nSo, remember, tests are simply tools to help us learn and grow.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:56.800\nThey show us what we know and what we still need to work on.\n\n00:56.800 --> 00:59.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
