    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_000832.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:13.700\nThink of a test as a way to see how much you know about something.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:20.200\nIt's like a little game where you answer questions to show what you've learned.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:30.400\nTests can come in many forms. Sometimes they're written, like when you fill in bubbles on a sheet. Other times they might be practical, like showing you can ride a bike or bake a cake.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:38.800\nThe important thing is they help measure your understanding.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:50.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your words. A math test sees if you can solve problems. Even a taste test can be a test, seeing which foods you like best!\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:59.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check your knowledge or skills. It helps you and others see what you've learned and what you might need to practice more. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "8e9ff26e-53a7-4ba1-bf89-ff34d6203940": {
    "id": "8e9ff26e-53a7-4ba1-bf89-ff34d6203940",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:16:52.857273",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:09:26.112421",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_000926.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_000926.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:11.900\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working like it should.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:20.200\nIt's like a detective looking for clues! The main idea behind a test is to give something a specific input, and then see if the output matches what you expect.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:23.800\nIf it does, great! The test passes.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:32.200\nIf it doesn't, something's wrong and the test fails. For example, imagine you're testing a light bulb.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:38.600\nYour input is turning the switch on. The expected output is that the bulb lights up.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:44.500\nIf it doesn't light up, the light bulb has failed the test!\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:50.700\nAnother example? Checking if 2 + 2 equals 4.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:01.400\nThe input is the math problem. The expected output is 4. If the answer is anything else, the test fails!\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:06.900\nSo, remember: tests are all about checking if things are working as expected.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:16.900\nThey use inputs and expected outputs to find problems. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1f57e871-af6b-471c-b202-dfa5613c2651": {
    "id": "1f57e871-af6b-471c-b202-dfa5613c2651",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:16:53.308352",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:10:12.501941",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_001012.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_001012.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:24.400\nIt could be checking if a light bulb works, or if you understand a new topic. Think of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:33.000\nThat's a test! Or, if your phone isn't turning on, you might try plugging it in to test if the battery is dead.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:44.300\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if we need to make some changes. So, a test is just a check to see if something is right.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:47.900\nPretty simple, huh?\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:49.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ecf0a9a8-e19e-4095-a9ba-1ea0578a8c3f": {
