    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_001057.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.000 --> 00:02.000\nToday we're tackling something super important: tests!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.000\nIt helps us learn if something is true, correct, or working as expected.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:14.000\nYou do a test!\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:16.000\nYou poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:18.000\nIf it comes out clean, the test tells you they're ready.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:21.000\nTests aren't just for baking, though.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:23.000\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.000\nTeachers use tests to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:29.000\nEven scientists use tests to prove their ideas.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:37.000\nSo, whether it's a school exam, a medical check-up, or a baking experiment, a test is a tool that gives us information.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.000\nIt helps us understand the world around us a little bit better.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:43.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
