    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_001542.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:24.900\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true. Think about it like this: If you want to know if a light bulb works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:31.900\nOr, if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you stick a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:37.800\nTests are used everywhere! From checking if your spelling is correct,\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:46.800\nto making sure a bridge is safe to cross. They help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:57.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it works or is correct. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
