    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_001624.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:07.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:12.500\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case,\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:16.800\nwe're talking about something a little broader.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:22.300\nA test is basically a way to find out if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb is working.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:31.400\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:31.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:35.900\nOr, maybe you're trying a new recipe.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:39.000\nTasting it is a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:41.600\nTests help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:44.600\nThey tell us if we're on the right track.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:53.200\nSo, whether it's a light bulb, a recipe, or even a new app on your phone, tests are important for making sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:56.900\nThey help us find problems and fix them.\n\n00:56.900 --> 00:58.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
