    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_002007.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to see how much you know or understand about something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:25.300\nIt helps you, and sometimes others, measure your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:32.900\nThink of it like this: imagine you\u2019ve been learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:40.500\nA test could be seeing if you can ride around the block without falling.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:48.100\nOr maybe you\u2019ve been practicing your spelling words.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:57.800\nA test would be writing them down correctly from memory. Tests come in all shapes and sizes, from short quizzes to big exams.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:04.700\nThey can be written, spoken, or even hands-on activities. So, remember, a test is just a tool to help you understand how well you're learning. It's a chance to show what you know and identify areas where you might need a little extra practice. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
