    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.300\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests. Now, you might be thinking of school tests, but a test in general is really just a way to find out if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:27.100\nYour test? You flip the switch!\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:32.500\nIf the light turns on, the test passes. The lightbulb works!\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:41.300\nIf it doesn't, well, the test fails. Another example: you want to know if an apple is ripe.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:49.700\nYou might smell it, feel it, or even take a bite! Those are all different tests to see if the apple is ready to eat.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:57.100\nSo, a test is simply a procedure we use to check something. It helps us make sure things are the way we expect them to be.\n\n00:57.100 --> 00:58.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
