    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_002617.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\nIt could be checking if you understand something, like a quiz at school.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:25.700\nOr it could be checking if something works, like testing a new toy to make sure it's safe.\nSo, think of it like this: you bake a cake, right?\nYou don't just assume it's done.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:30.100\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\nThat toothpick is your test!\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:35.600\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready.\nAnother example: a doctor gives you a check-up.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:42.000\nThey're running tests to see if you're healthy.\nThey might check your heart rate or take your temperature.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:48.400\nAll of these are tests!\nBasically, a test helps us understand something better or see if something is working correctly.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:54.800\nIt's a way to gather information.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:00.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
