    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_002915.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHello everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:03.300\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:05.200\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:09.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:11.500\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:16.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:20.300\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:21.800\nThose are both tests!\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:27.200\nAnother example: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:29.500\nThe toothpick is performing a test!\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:32.600\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:35.000\nIf it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:43.100\nSo, tests are all about gathering information to help us make decisions or understand something better.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:47.600\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the basic idea is always the same:\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:49.500\nto learn something new.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
