    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_004200.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:15.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:26.000\nThink of it like gathering information. It's a process where we ask a question or present a challenge, and then observe the response.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:35.300\nThe response, or the result, gives us data. This data helps us understand whatever it is we're testing.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:44.400\nFor example, a simple spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling. A taste test lets you decide which flavor you prefer.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:55.900\nEven pressing a button on your phone to see if it turns on is a kind of test! So, a test is just a process to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:01.200\nWe ask a question, observe the answer, and draw a conclusion. That's the core idea! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
