    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. We want to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like asking a question and looking for the answer.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:32.200\nFor example, you might test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:38.500\nYou flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:44.900\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You test it with a toothpick.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:51.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that means the cake is done. That's another test!\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:55.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:59.300\nIt helps us know if things are working correctly, or if we've achieved the result we're looking for.\n```"
