    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_004809.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and then getting an answer.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:20.100\nIn everyday life, we use tests all the time. A taste test to see if you like a new food.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:29.600\nA spelling test at school to check your vocabulary. Even trying to turn on a light switch is a mini-test \u2013 does the light go on?\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:31.200\nYes? Great!\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:33.600\nNo? Then something's wrong.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:48.500\nTests help us understand things, identify problems, and learn new information. They can be formal, like a big exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:57.400\nThe important thing is they give us feedback. So, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:01.000\nIt's a question, followed by an answer.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:04.000\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is!\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
