    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_004933.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:12.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:25.200\nIt's a process or procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:32.300\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:38.200\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to show your teacher what you've learned.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:49.500\nHere's another example. Imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste the batter to test if it has enough sugar. That's a test too!\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:57.500\nSo, tests come in many forms but they all share a common goal: to gather information and help us understand something better.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.000\nThey help us see where we are, and what we need to work on. In short, a test helps us check something!\n```"
  },
