    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_010029.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.600\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something. It's like an experiment or a checkup to see if something is working correctly, or to learn more about it.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:25.500\nThink about it this way: a spelling test at school helps your teacher see how well you know your words.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:36.400\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar. Even a doctor uses tests to check your health and make sure you're feeling good.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:43.600\nSo, a test is really just a process. A way of gathering information or proving something.\n\n00:43.600 --> 01:00.500\nWhether it's in school, in the kitchen, or at the doctor's office, tests help us learn and improve. To recap, a test is a procedure used to determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:08.900\nIt's a fundamental part of learning and understanding the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "01a9074f-2945-45bf-920f-b05a7ba4e118": {
    "id": "01a9074f-2945-45bf-920f-b05a7ba4e118",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:17:23.191657",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T01:01:17.070590",
