    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_010116.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in this case, a test is really just a way to find out if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb is good. So, you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:28.900\nThat's a test! If it lights up, the test passes.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:33.200\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:36.700\nAnother example? Baking a cake!\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:40.300\nYou're testing your recipe.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:43.900\nDoes it taste good?\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:47.000\nIs it cooked all the way through?\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:50.500\nYou\u2019re checking to see if your cake meets your expectations.\n\n00:50.500 --> 01:06.700\nSo, basically, a test is just a simple way of checking if something is working correctly, whether it's a lightbulb, a recipe, or anything else! It's all about making sure things do what they're meant to do.\n\n01:06.700 --> 01:14.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
