    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:07.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:18.500\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out something, or to check if something works.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:29.900\nThink of it like an experiment to see what happens. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:39.800\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:46.600\nOr, if your toy car isn't working, you might try changing the batteries. That's a test to see if the old batteries were the problem.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:49.900\nSo, a test involves doing something specific and then observing the result.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:56.900\nDid it work? Did it pass? Did you learn something new? That result tells you something valuable.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.400\nRemember, tests help us learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
