    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.210 --> 00:03.070\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.070 --> 00:06.330\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:06.330 --> 00:12.130\nIt could be about you, like a quiz in school, or it could be about a thing, like checking if your phone still works after you drop it.\n\n00:12.130 --> 00:15.560\nBasically, you do something and then see what happens.\n\n00:15.560 --> 00:19.420\nIf you study hard and take a test, you're testing your knowledge.\n\n00:19.420 --> 00:23.070\nIf you bake a cake and taste it, you're testing the recipe.\n\n00:23.070 --> 00:26.910\nThe result tells you if you passed, if the phone is broken, or if the cake is delicious.\n\n00:26.910 --> 00:28.860\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n00:28.860 --> 00:32.180\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're sick.\n\n00:32.180 --> 00:35.340\nA chef tastes their soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:35.340 --> 00:37.530\nEverything is a test of some kind.\n\n00:37.530 --> 00:42.500\nSo remember, a test is just a way to learn more by doing something and observing the outcome.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:46.370\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
