    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_011329.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, in the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:26.000\nIt helps us answer a question or see if something is working correctly.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:38.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:44.200\nOr maybe you test a lightbulb to see if it still works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:48.300\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:59.400\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit. The important thing is that a test gives you information.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.000\nIt helps you make a decision or understand something better.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:07.400\nSo, a test is simply a way to gather information and answer a question.\n\n01:07.400 --> 01:10.300\nIt's all about finding out something!\n\n01:10.300 --> 01:13.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
