    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_011452.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nOkay, so you're hearing the word \"test\" a lot, right?\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:11.700\nBut what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:18.500\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see what we can learn.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: You want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:28.100\nYou stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:32.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:36.500\nAnother example? A doctor checks your temperature.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:39.600\nThat's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:43.100\nOr even just trying a new food!\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:45.900\nYou're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:52.200\nSo, a test is just a way to check something, gather information, and learn more.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:57.300\nIt can be simple, like tasting a cake, or more complex, like a science experiment.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:00.600\nEither way, it helps us understand the world around us better.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
