    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_011628.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:22.100\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. Think about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz to test what you've learned in class.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:28.200\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:32.600\nSee? Different kinds of tests!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:37.000\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.400\nYou plug it in. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:45.800\nIf it doesn't, the lightbulb has failed the test.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:53.600\nSo, remember, a test is a method to find something out. It can be a quiz, tasting something, or simply checking if something works.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:54.900\nThat's the basic idea.\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:58.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
