    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_012528.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests! In simple terms, a test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:17.700\nWe use tests all the time without even thinking about it. It's about finding out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:25.200\nThink about it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:33.200\nOr, you might test a recipe by following the instructions and tasting the result. Those are both tests!\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:40.200\nAnother example is taking a quiz in school. That's a test to see if you understand the material.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:49.000\nSo, a test can be anything from checking if a toy needs new batteries to figuring out if a car is safe to drive.\n\n00:49.000 --> 01:05.400\nBasically, it's a process to gather information and see if something meets certain standards. So remember, tests are all about checking things, finding out if they work, and making sure they meet our expectations.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:09.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
