    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_012655.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:26.100\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:33.700\nThink of it like this: you have an idea, you build something based on that idea, and then you test it to see if it actually does what you wanted it to do.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:41.300\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, the testing part might be tasting it to make sure it's sweet enough.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:53.400\nOr, if you're building a toy car, you test it by letting it roll to see if the wheels work properly.\nSo, a test is a fundamental part of learning and building.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:56.300\nIt helps us improve our ideas and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:56.300 --> 00:57.900\nIt\u2019s all about trying something out and seeing what happens!\n\n00:57.900 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
