    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:24.100\nThink of it like a question, or a series of questions, designed to give you information.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:34.800\nIt could be a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:48.600\nOr maybe a recipe test, where you try a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.200\nEven using a thermometer to check your temperature is a type of test!\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:55.900\nYou're testing to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:02.200\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to learn something new or confirm something you already suspect.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:05.800\nRemember, tests aren't always about being right or wrong, they're about gathering information.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:08.800\nTests help us learn and improve.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:12.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
