    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like this: you test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:30.400\nAnother example is a battery test. You use a device to check if the battery has enough power.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:35.800\nIf it does, great! If not, you know it needs to be replaced.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:44.900\nTests are used everywhere, from checking your spelling with a spell checker, to making sure a bridge can hold a certain weight.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:57.800\nBasically, a test helps us learn something or make sure things are as they should be. So, remember, a test is all about checking to see if something works or is true.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
