    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.600\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" before, right?\n\n00:01.600 --> 00:05.500\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:08.300\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:08.300 --> 00:11.500\nThink of it like this: you might test a new toy to see if it needs batteries.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:15.500\nOr, a chef might test a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:18.500\nTests aren't just for school! We use them all the time in everyday life.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:22.800\nFor example, you might test if your phone is charged by trying to turn it on.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:24.200\nSee?\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:25.800\nIt's a way of gathering information.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:32.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a process we use to get information or confirm something.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:36.300\nIt's a question we ask, and then we look for the answer.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:38.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
