    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_014428.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.999\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:21.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:31.500\nWe use tests all the time to see if things work, if we understand something, or even just to see what happens.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:40.900\nFor example, a simple test could be seeing if a light bulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:50.200\nOr, if you're learning to bake, you might taste your cake batter. That's a test to see if it tastes good before you bake the whole thing.\n\n00:50.200 --> 01:00.000\nAnother example is, when you take a multiple choice quiz in school, that's a test to see how much you know about a certain subject.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:05.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information and learn something new.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:10.600\nTests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:10.600 --> 01:14.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
