    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_014558.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. In everyday life, you take tests all the time, even if you don\u2019t realize it.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:27.700\nFor example, if you touch a hot stove, you're testing if it's hot.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:40.900\nThe result? Ouch! Or, if you try a new ice cream flavor, you're testing if you like it. The answer is hopefully, \"Yum!\"\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:51.300\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned. They can be written, like a quiz, or hands-on, like a science experiment.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:59.600\nThe key is, tests give us information. They help us understand something better.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.200\nSo remember, a test is just a way to ask a question and get an answer.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:06.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f4c80b79-b29f-49ef-bfb0-36332be5f609": {
