    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_014719.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:07.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 and no, not the kind you take in school!\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.100\nWe're talking about tests as a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.400\nThat's a test! You're testing the lightbulb.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:31.300\nOr, maybe you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done. You stick a toothpick in the middle; if it comes out clean, that's a test!\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:33.800\nYou're testing if the cake is cooked through.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:40.100\nBasically, a test is just a way to find out if something passes or fails.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:45.300\nIt helps us know if things are working properly, or if they need to be fixed.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:52.200\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:56.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
