    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_015015.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:13.000\nA test is simply a way to find out if something is true or correct.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:18.700\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:23.600\nYou wouldn't just guess, right? You'd put it in a lamp and see if it lights up. That's a test!\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:32.900\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Maybe you want to test a new recipe to see if it tastes good. Or maybe a scientist wants to test a new medicine to see if it helps people.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:47.800\nThe main idea is to gather evidence and see what happens. For example, if you\u2019re testing if a plant needs sunlight, you could put one plant in the sun and another in a dark room and see which one grows better.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:57.600\nThat's comparing the results of your test. So, remember, a test is a process to check if something is true, using evidence.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
