    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:24.700\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we've learned something new.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:37.400\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a test in school to show your teacher what you've learned.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:48.700\nTests can be anything from answering questions on paper, to running a machine to check its performance.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:51.700\nFor example, a car mechanic might test your car's battery to see if it needs replacing.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:54.700\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:57.700\nSee? Tests are all around us!\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:10.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard. It helps us make informed decisions and understand the world a little better.\n\n01:10.600 --> 01:14.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
