    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_015934.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:17.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:26.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking. You use a toothpick \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:36.300\nYou stick it in, and if it comes out clean, the cookies pass the test.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:48.100\nIn general, tests help us find out if something is working correctly, if it meets certain requirements, or if it's good enough.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:55.300\nFor example, a teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject. Or, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and reliable.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:58.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us learn and improve. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
