    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_020127.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:13.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:18.500\nThink of it like asking questions to see what you already know or can do.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:21.000\nIt's a measurement tool.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:23.700\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:36.200\nYou might take a written test in school, where you answer questions on paper.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:40.800\nOr, imagine a simple taste test, where you try different foods and say which one you like best.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:41.800\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:53.400\nAnother example is a medical test. A doctor might order blood tests to check your health.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:00.600\nAll these tests, from school exams to food tastings to medical checks, help us learn something new.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:04.600\nSo, a test is just a structured way to collect information.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:07.500\nAbout knowledge, abilities, or even preferences.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:09.000\nIt helps us understand something better.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:12.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
