    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:18:00.286241",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T02:06:29.709712",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_020629.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_020629.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:18.800\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:26.200\nIt's a process of asking a question and then trying to answer it.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:31.200\nThink about it like this: If you want to know if a lightbulb works, you can test it by plugging it in.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:35.700\nIf it lights up, the test is positive, the lightbulb works!\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:41.700\nOr, maybe you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:45.200\nYou can test them by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:47.800\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:51.800\nTests are everywhere, helping us understand the world around us.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:56.300\nThey help us confirm things, learn new things, and make decisions.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:01.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:02.400\nThis video was created by\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:03.400\nApilage AI.\n```"
  },
