    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:25.700\nTests can be used to check anything from how well you know your ABCs to how strong a bridge is.\nBasically, you're trying to measure or understand something better.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:37.200\nFor example, a spelling test shows how well you know how to spell words.\nOr, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:53.800\nEven trying out a new recipe is a kind of test to see if you like how it tastes!\nSo, in short, a test is a way of getting information by asking a question, performing an action, or making an observation.\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:59.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a9fdc2ba-cb54-42cf-be19-374c156480ae": {
    "id": "a9fdc2ba-cb54-42cf-be19-374c156480ae",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:18:06.493804",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T02:17:13.519288",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_021713.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_021713.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:21.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:33.000\nIn everyday life, we're constantly testing things. You might test the temperature of your shower water to make sure it's not too hot or too cold. Or, maybe you test a new recipe to see if you like how it tastes.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:40.000\nTests can also be more formal, like a quiz at school. The quiz is testing what you've learned.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:49.200\nThe key is that a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:52.800\nSo, a test is just a method for checking something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6f73ab9d-768e-4a8a-8cf2-d9201f1f2a40": {
    "id": "6f73ab9d-768e-4a8a-8cf2-d9201f1f2a40",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:18:06.949609",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T02:18:14.650226",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_021814.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_021814.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we\u2019re diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:16.400\nNow, don't worry, it's not the kind you cram for!\nIn computing, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and then you test it by pushing it to see if it rolls.\nThe same idea applies to software.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:30.300\nWe write little bits of code to test our bigger pieces of code.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:44.000\nFor example, if we're building a calculator, a test might be to input 2 + 2 and make sure the calculator shows 4.\nIf it does, great! The test passes.\nIf not, there\u2019s a bug we need to fix.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:47.600\nSo, tests help us catch mistakes early on,\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:59.600\nmaking sure our programs are reliable and do what they're supposed to.\nIn short, tests are crucial for building quality software.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:04.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
