    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:28.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\nThe main idea is to give something a specific input, and then see what output you get.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:45.000\nIf the output is what you expect, then the test passes!\nIt means everything's working correctly.\nFor example, if you're testing a calculator, you might input \"2 + 2\" and expect the output \"4.\"\nIf it shows \"4,\" the test passes!\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.200\nOr imagine testing a toy car; you wind it up and expect it to move forward.\nIf it moves, the test is successful.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:05.700\nSo, to recap, a test is all about checking if something works as expected by giving it an input and seeing if the output matches what you planned.\nPretty simple, right?\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:11.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
