    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.800\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:27.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something. It could be your knowledge, your skills, or even how well something works.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:34.900\nThink of it like this: a spelling test measures how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:42.000\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough. That taste is your test!\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:49.100\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in. You're testing to see if it'll light up.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:52.800\nSo, tests help us understand where we're at, and what needs improvement.\n```"
