    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_023913.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.900\nNow, you might be thinking of school exams, but a test is really just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:22.000\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:30.500\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:37.100\nOr, imagine you want to know if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:45.500\nIf it lights up, it passes the test. So, a test is simply a procedure designed to reveal something specific.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:54.900\nIt helps us make decisions based on the results. Whether it's baking a cake or checking a lightbulb, tests are all around us.\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:59.300\nIn short, a test helps us learn something new.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:02.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
