    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_024219.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\nIt\u2019s a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:34.900\nA teacher uses a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:47.100\nAnd a baker might taste their cake batter as a test to see if it needs more sugar.\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:58.900\nThey can be written, like a quiz; physical, like an eye exam; or even just an observation, like watching how well a plant grows in sunlight.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:05.300\nBasically, if you're trying to gather information to make a judgment, you're using a test. So, remember, a test is a tool for learning and evaluating. It helps us understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "bcc601bd-f628-47b9-a7b7-9a42251249e9": {
    "id": "bcc601bd-f628-47b9-a7b7-9a42251249e9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:18:22.540935",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T02:43:35.441367",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_024335.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_024335.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something works or if something is true.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.500\nThink of it like checking a lightbulb. You flip the switch, and if the light turns on, the test passes!\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:32.800\nBasically, a test compares what you expect to happen with what actually happens.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:44.000\nLet's say you're baking a cake. The recipe is like your expectation. If the cake comes out fluffy and delicious, the test, baking the cake, was a success!\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:51.400\nBut if it's flat and burnt, the test failed. Another example?\n\n00:51.400 --> 01:04.300\nIf you're learning to ride a bike, the test is whether you can ride without falling. Tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:13.300\nSo, remember, a test is simply checking if something is working as expected.\n\n01:13.300 --> 01:22.300\nIt\u2019s all about comparison and seeing if our expectations match reality.\n\n01:22.300 --> 01:23.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
