    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_030308.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there, and welcome!\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:11.800\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:18.700\nWhat is a test? Simply put, it's a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:27.100\nThat test measures your knowledge.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:31.300\nAnother example? A doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:37.600\nThe blood test is measuring things in your blood to give the doctor information.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:44.000\nTests can be written, spoken, physical, or even just observing something.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:49.100\nThe key is that they help us understand something better.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:50.600\nSo, a test is an action we take to learn more about something.\n```"
