    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_030419.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well something is performing.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a new lightbulb to make sure it turns on.\nOr, a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:41.600\nTests can be as simple as that lightbulb example, or they can be a bit more complex.\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or a car manufacturer might test a car's brakes to ensure they are safe.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:52.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\nIt helps us know if things are working as they should and allows us to find problems.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:55.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
