    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_030632.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:22.500\nIt's a process of asking a question or performing an action to see what happens.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:34.700\nYour test? You stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the test tells you the cake is ready!\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:40.500\nOr, maybe you want to know if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:46.300\nIf it lights up, the test is positive. Tests help us understand things and make decisions.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:55.800\nThey can be as simple as checking the weather before you go outside, or as complex as a doctor running blood work.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:01.600\nUltimately, a test is just a way to gather information.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.200\nSo remember, a test is a process to learn something new.\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:08.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
