    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:12.200\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:19.900\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:31.000\nSimply put, it's a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:38.500\nWe use tests all the time to check if things are working correctly or to see how well we understand something.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:46.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:53.500\nOr, maybe you take a quiz in school; that's a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:53.500 --> 01:01.100\nEven checking if a light bulb works is a type of test!\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:08.600\nSo, tests help us gather information.\n\n01:08.600 --> 01:17.400\nThey can be simple, like pressing a button to see if it works, or more complex, like taking a big exam.\n\n01:17.400 --> 01:26.900\nThe main idea is that a test gives us data or results that we can then use to make decisions or understand a situation better.\n\n01:26.900 --> 01:34.400\nBasically, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n01:34.400 --> 01:39.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
