    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_031212.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.500\nYou've probably taken a bunch of them in school, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:09.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:14.000\nIt's like a measuring tool for your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:17.500\nThink of it like this: a spelling test shows how well you can spell words.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:21.500\nA fitness test shows how strong or fast you are.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:22.500\nSee?\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.000\nIt's all about measuring something specific.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:30.500\nFor example, a multiple-choice quiz in history helps your teacher understand how much you remember about historical events.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:34.500\nOr, a cooking test might see if you can follow a recipe correctly.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:40.500\nSo, a test is just a way to check your understanding or ability in a particular area.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:47.000\nIt helps you and others see what you've learned and where you might need a little more practice.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:49.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
