    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_031337.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:24.200\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:36.100\nThink about it: When you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good. Or when you press a button on a toy, you're testing to see if it works.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:43.900\nIn science and school, tests are a bit more formal, but the idea is the same.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:51.700\nWe design an experiment or ask questions to learn something new or confirm what we already think we know.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:59.600\nFor example, a doctor might order a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or your teacher might give you a quiz to see if you understand the lesson.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:05.000\nSo, a test is just a tool to help us learn and understand the world better. It's all about finding answers!\n```"
  },
