    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're diving into the basics of testing.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:18.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out if something works correctly.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:24.200\nWe test things all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:34.700\nWhen you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like the taste.\nWhen you ask a friend for advice, you're testing their knowledge on a subject.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:43.800\nIn more formal settings, like school or work, tests help us understand what we've learned or how well something performs.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:53.600\nSo, testing is all about checking if something does what it's supposed to do.\nRemember, it's a simple way to check functionality.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
