    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:18.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:29.700\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, meeting a certain standard, or even just to see what's inside.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:39.600\nFor example, a doctor might run blood tests to see if you're healthy, or a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:45.400\nAnother example is testing a lightbulb. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:51.300\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, it failed.\n\n00:51.300 --> 01:02.300\nSo, remember, a test is a process to check something. It helps us confirm, understand, and improve things all around us.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:05.999\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
