    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:18.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:38.700\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. For example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:45.500\nOr, when you click a link on a website, you're testing if it takes you to the right page.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:52.600\nLet's say you're baking a cake. You might test the batter by sticking a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:57.500\nThat's a test. So, a test is just a way to check something and make sure it's doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:57.500 --> 00:58.900\nIt\u2019s a simple but powerful tool. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
