    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_034028.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHello everyone and welcome!\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:12.900\nToday we're going to explore something really important: the test.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:18.100\nNow, a test is basically a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: you take a cake out of the oven and you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:28.300\nThat's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:33.200\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:39.000\nYou flip the switch, and if it lights up, the lightbulb passes the test.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:45.000\nSo, a test helps us confirm results, find issues, and make sure things are as they should be.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:47.800\nRemember, testing is all about checking and confirming.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:50.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
