    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_034114.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:21.800\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get. Think of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:29.200\nOr, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:34.400\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test! You're testing your recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:40.300\nAnother example? Let's say you want to know if a toy car works.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:45.600\nYou put in batteries and turn it on. If it moves, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:54.700\nSo, a test is just a process to see if something works, if something is true, or to learn more about something.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:59.800\nRemember, tests help us understand the world around us!\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
