    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_034201.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHey there, welcome!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:03.800\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:03.800 --> 00:06.900\nNow, in everyday language, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:09.000\nThink of it as a question or a challenge that helps us learn more.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:09.900\nSo, what does that mean?\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:13.800\nWell, imagine you're baking a cake. You might test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:17.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done!\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:20.100\nOr, think about a doctor checking your temperature.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:22.300\nThat's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:24.800\nTests aren't just for cakes and doctors though!\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:25.600\nThey're everywhere.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:30.100\nWe use them to see if a lightbulb works, to check if our spelling is correct, or even to see if a toy needs new batteries.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:35.800\nBasically, a test is a simple way of getting information and confirming if something is working or true.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:40.400\nIt's a tool for learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:42.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
