    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T03:57:28.571966",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_035728.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_035728.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nWhat is a test, really? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:25.500\nIt\u2019s a method to gather information and see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:29.300\nThink of it like this: your doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:35.700\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge about a subject. See? Different types of tests, same idea.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:50.400\nAnother example is baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:57.000\nSo, a test is just a procedure we use to check something, whether it\u2019s your health, your understanding, or even if a cake is ready. It helps us make informed decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6d2b0fd3-f68f-4b75-b6a7-54300d4df8c7": {
