    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_035812.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:19.800\nIt's a process of asking a question or performing an action to see what happens.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:27.700\nThink about it like this: You might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp. The light turning on is the result of the test!\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:33.900\nOr, maybe you taste a new food to test if you like it. Your reaction, good or bad, tells you the result.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:45.000\nTests are everywhere! Doctors use tests to diagnose illnesses, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even scientists use tests to prove their theories.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.500\nThey all help us learn and understand the world around us. So, remember, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:54.500 --> 00:62.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
