    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_040411.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but we're talking about something a little broader: a way to find out if something works, or if it's true.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:28.200\nYou're checking to see if it lights up.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:34.800\nOr, let's say you bake a cake, and you want to know if it tastes good. You take a bite. That bite is a test!\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:38.500\nYou're checking the flavor.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:45.100\nBasically, a test is any process that helps you gather information and make a decision.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:48.800\nIt's a way to learn and confirm things.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:56.900\nSo, whenever you try something out to see if it works, you're performing a test. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
