    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_040714.mp4",
    "subtitles": "[WebVTT]\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.100\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like an investigation. We use tests to see if something is working correctly, to measure its quality, or even to check our own understanding.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:32.000\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. A teacher gives you a quiz to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:46.400\nAnd a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar. So, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all share the same goal: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:56.600\nWhether it's checking your reflexes, solving a math problem, or even just trying a new flavor of ice cream, you're performing a test. That's the basics of what a test is!\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI."
