    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_041244.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nToday we're going to talk about tests. Now, a test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:21.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:33.200\nThat's a test! It helps you decide if the cake is ready. In school, tests help your teachers see how well you understand the things you've been learning.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:45.400\nMaybe it's a quiz about animals, or a math test with addition problems. These tests show what you know and might point out areas where you could learn more.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:51.400\nFor example, a simple test for a lightbulb is to see if it lights up when you flip the switch.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:57.400\nIf it does, the test passes! If it doesn't, the lightbulb might be broken.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:02.200\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of checking something to see if it works, or if you understand it.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:07.800\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:08.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
