    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_042747.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.400 --> 00:02.200\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:03.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.700 --> 00:06.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:08.100\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:11.800\nThink about it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:14.300\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:14.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:18.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test and is ready to eat.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:22.900\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:26.500\nEach time you try to balance, you're testing your ability.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:27.800\nYou might fall, but that's just part of the test!\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:37.800\nSo, a test helps us understand something better, whether it's about cake, bikes, or anything else.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:41.500\nIt's a way to gather information and learn.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:46.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4d2daf77-df6b-4b1f-ab8e-0cd09f0e6bb9": {
