    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_042842.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:13.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\nYou poke it with a toothpick, right?\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:31.100\nIn a more formal setting, tests help us understand if something works as expected.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:45.100\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\nThese tests give us information.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:53.900\nA good test is reliable, meaning it gives similar results each time it's used, and valid, meaning it actually measures what it's supposed to measure.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.500\nSo, from baking cakes to checking your health, tests are all about gathering information to make informed decisions.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
