    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_043050.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_043050.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a way to check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done. That toothpick test tells you if the batter is still gooey or if the cake is ready to eat.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:35.900\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down is a test! It shows you what not to do next time.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:44.600\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like checking the weather before you go outside.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:51.200\nThe important thing is that a test gives you information. It helps you understand something better.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn and explore! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
