    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_043900.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:19.000\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true, or working correctly.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.000\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:33.000\nAnother example is testing a new recipe \u2013 you taste it to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:40.000\nSo, a test involves checking something, looking for results, and then understanding what those results mean.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:47.000\nWhether it's a health check, a school quiz, or even just tasting food, tests help us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:52.000\nBasically, a test is a simple process to gain information.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:54.000\nThat's it!\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:62.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
