    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_044159.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.200\nSimple tests! Think of a test as just a way to find out something, anything really.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:21.000\nIt's like asking a question and then figuring out the answer. For example, you might test if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:30.800\nIf it comes out clean, the test says \"cookies are ready!\" Or, think about a battery test. It checks how much power is left.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:37.900\nIf the light turns green, that means the battery is good. Another example is testing a lightbulb.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:44.500\nYou flip the switch. If the light comes on, the test passes, and the bulb works! If it doesn't, well, time for a new bulb.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:57.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a method to check if something is working, true, or ready. It helps us make decisions!\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:02.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
