    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_044632.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so you're hearing the word \"test\" a lot,\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.500\nbut what does it actually mean?\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:09.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:11.500\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:16.500\nThink of it this way: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:18.000\nYou do a test!\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:20.500\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:23.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you the cake is ready.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:29.000\nOr maybe you want to see if you know your ABCs. Someone gives you a test,\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:33.000\nmaybe they show you letters and you have to name them.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:35.000\nThat shows how much you know!\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:41.000\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.000\nIt can be a quiz, a physical experiment, or even just trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:51.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
