    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_045118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:10.300\nnot the kind you take in school,\n\n00:10.300 --> 00:14.500\nbut a way of checking if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:18.500\nThink of it like this: a test is simply a way\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:21.700\nto find out if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:26.300\nFor example, you might test a lightbulb by screwing it in to see if it lights up.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:30.400\nOr, you could test a toy car by winding it up to see if it moves.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:36.000\nThe test is the act of checking, and the result tells you if the lightbulb works or the car moves.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:41.500\nAnother example is baking a cake. The test is tasting the cake!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:46.500\nIf it tastes good, the recipe and your baking worked.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:50.000\nIf it doesn't, you know something went wrong.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:56.300\nSo, a test is just a simple way to check if something works the way it should.\n\n00:56.300 --> 00:59.200\nKeep exploring and you'll see tests are everywhere!\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:01.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
