    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_045212.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.600\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:30.000\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, checking if you understand a lesson, or even checking if a new medicine is safe.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:36.600\nBasically, you perform an action or ask a question, and then you see what happens.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:46.500\nIf the lightbulb turns on, the test passed! If you answer the question correctly, you passed that part of the test.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:56.300\nThink of it like baking a cake. You're testing if your ingredients and instructions will result in a delicious cake.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:06.300\nYou follow the recipe, bake it, and then taste it. The taste is the result of your \"cake test\"!\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:16.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n01:16.100 --> 01:26.800\nIt gives us information, helps us learn, and lets us know if things are working as they should.\n\n01:26.800 --> 01:29.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
