    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_045639.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how much you know about something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it like a check-up for your brain!\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:29.600\nIt helps you and your teachers understand what you've learned and what you might need a little more help with.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:40.000\nTests can come in lots of different forms. You might have multiple-choice questions, where you pick the best answer from a few choices.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:50.400\nOr maybe you'll have to write out the answer yourself. Sometimes, it's even a practical test, like showing you can ride a bike or bake a cake!\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:00.800\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem like \"2 + 2\". A spelling test might ask you to spell the word \"cat\".\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:04.700\nThese simple questions help show if you understand the basics.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:13.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to help you learn. It shows what you know and where you can improve.\n\n01:13.600 --> 01:16.900\nDon't be afraid of them!\n\n01:16.900 --> 01:18.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
