    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_045929.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:01.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.700 --> 00:02.500\nToday we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:03.900\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:07.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:10.800\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a cookie is sweet.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:12.300\nYou taste it \u2013 that's your test!\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:16.700\nIn more formal situations, tests are used to check if things are working correctly,\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:18.400\nor to see how well something performs.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:21.600\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:25.700\nOr, a car manufacturer might test a new car to see if it's safe.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:28.900\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:33.700\nThey can be simple, like tasting a cookie, or complex, like testing a rocket.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:36.500\nThe main idea is always the same: to get information.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:37.900\nThat's the basics of what a test is all about!\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:39.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
