    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:13.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:21.100\nIt's a method for gathering information. Think of it like this: a taste test tells you how something tastes.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:26.900\nA spelling test shows how well you can spell. Tests aren't just for school, though.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:37.700\nWhen a doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever. When you try on a new pair of shoes to see if they fit, that's a test!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:49.600\nSo, whether it's a quiz, an experiment, or even just trying something out, a test is all about gathering information and learning something new.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:57.200\nTests help us understand things better. To recap: a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:05.200\nWe use them everywhere, from school to the doctor's office, to learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:08.899\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
