    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:22.300\nIt's a process or a procedure designed to measure or evaluate.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:30.800\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:39.300\nOr, a teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:54.200\nThere are lots of different kinds of tests. A simple test could be tasting a new food to see if you like it. Another example is checking the weather to see if you need a jacket.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:01.600\nBoth of these are ways of gathering information, and that's what a test is all about. So, remember, a test is a way to learn something new, measure something, or evaluate something. It helps us gather information and make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0b102b6e-5396-4572-8dcc-d3fb896c7080": {
    "id": "0b102b6e-5396-4572-8dcc-d3fb896c7080",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:19:48.733051",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T05:05:17.320043",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_050517.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_050517.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nDon't worry, not the kind you stress about!\nIn computer programming, a test is simply a way to check if your code is working correctly.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you test it by pushing it to see if it rolls.\nComputer tests do the same thing, but with code.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:42.400\nThey run your code with specific inputs and then check if the output matches what you expect.\nFor example, if you write code to add two numbers, a test would give it 2 and 3, and make sure the result is 5.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:47.500\nIf it is, the test passes!\nIf it isn't, something's wrong.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:56.400\nTests help you find bugs early, making your code more reliable.\nThey're a super important part of good programming.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:04.300\nSo, remember, tests are your friends!\nThey help you make sure your code does what it's supposed to do.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9e48f49f-0c4c-4ae4-975f-60a14d67187b": {
