    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_050558.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:04.700\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:07.300\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:12.600\nA test is just a procedure or a set of questions designed to measure something.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:16.400\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your spelling skills.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:20.200\nA taste test figures out which flavor of ice cream you like best.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:23.100\nYour doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:29.000\nSo, tests can be written, like in school, or they can be hands-on, like trying to assemble a new toy.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:31.700\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:38.800\nIn short, a test is a tool we use to learn something about ourselves, about objects, or about the world around us.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:41.400\nThey help us understand things better.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:44.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "08eeb58b-4684-49a6-b831-d2eb9c9af6a9": {
    "id": "08eeb58b-4684-49a6-b831-d2eb9c9af6a9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:19:49.681956",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T05:06:43.680215",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_050643.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_050643.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:25.700\nThe test? Sticking a toothpick in it! If it comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's a test!\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:30.600\nOr, imagine you're checking if your shoes fit. You put them on and walk around.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:36.200\nIf they feel good, they pass the test! If they pinch, they fail.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:47.800\nSo, a test is all about checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or tells you what you want to know. It helps you learn and make decisions.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:54.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "fe96f3f9-e409-4e51-b010-671c4411507f": {
    "id": "fe96f3f9-e409-4e51-b010-671c4411507f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:19:50.183203",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T05:07:36.016833",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_050735.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_050735.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we're talking about something a little different.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:23.100\nA test, in a broader sense, is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.500\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and you taste it.\nThat taste is a test to see if the cake is good.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:40.500\nOr, you try to turn on a light switch.\nIf the light comes on, that's a test that shows the lightbulb is working.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:49.900\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\nSo, a test helps us verify or confirm something.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:58.100\nIt could be anything from making sure your shoes fit properly to checking if a computer program is running smoothly.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:12.800\nBasically, it's a way to gather information and make sure things are as they should be.\nIn short, a test is a way of checking if something works or is true, using a simple observation or action.\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:16.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
