    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:26.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process that helps us see if something is working correctly, or to learn more about it.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:35.500\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:44.100\nOr, if you\u2019re learning to ride a bike, falling down is a test to see if you\u2019ve got your balance right.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:49.300\nAnother example? A doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:59.100\nSo, tests come in many different forms, but they all share the same goal: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:09.300\nIn short, a test is a method to learn something, check something, or prove something.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:12.900\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is!\n\n01:12.900 --> 01:16.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
