    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, in its simplest form, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:25.200\nIt helps us check if something is working, or if we understand something. Think of it like this: a teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:38.100\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health. Even baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if the ingredients and recipe will create something delicious!\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:49.200\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light switch turns on the light. Or they can be more complex, like scientists testing a new medicine.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:56.600\nThe important thing is that they give us information to help us make decisions or learn something new.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:04.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a way of gathering information to see if something works or if something is true.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:11.500\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, from quizzes to medical exams.\n\n01:11.500 --> 01:15.000\nNow you know what a test is!\n\n01:15.000 --> 01:18.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
