    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you take in school, but tests in the world of software and programming.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:22.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if your code is working correctly. It's like a safety net, making sure everything does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:34.700\nImagine you've built a calculator. A test would be like giving it a problem, say 2 plus 2, and then checking to see if it gives you the right answer, which is 4.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:38.300\nIf it does, great! The test passes. If it gives you 5, well, something's wrong!\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:48.800\nTests help us find those errors early, before they cause bigger problems later on. They also make sure that when you make changes to your code, you don't accidentally break something else.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:55.700\nSo, tests are a fundamental part of writing good, reliable software.\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:05.699\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
