    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_053200.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:24.500\nIt helps us check if something is true, or how well something works. Think of it like this: you might test if your bicycle brakes are working by squeezing the levers.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:31.400\nThat\u2019s a test! Or, your teacher might give you a quiz to test how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:38.500\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. Sometimes they're formal, like a science experiment.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:50.600\nOther times, they're informal, like tasting a new dish to see if you like it. The important thing is that a test helps us gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:59.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out. It helps us confirm, or deny, an idea.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
