  "a276e86d-b7c4-40e6-885b-d4b894e6cc0e": {
    "id": "a276e86d-b7c4-40e6-885b-d4b894e6cc0e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:20:10.300208",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T05:39:29.573755",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_053929.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_053929.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.300\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something. It's like an experiment or a way to check how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:26.100\nThink about it like this: a spelling test in school helps your teacher see how well you've learned your spelling words.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:34.300\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste a small piece to test if it needs more sugar. That's a test too!\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:48.400\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on, or more complex, like a big exam. But the main idea is always the same: it's a way to gather information.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:58.500\nSo, a test helps us learn, improve, and understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e593ff9f-b72f-40df-8a78-c620a1e18a5d": {
    "id": "e593ff9f-b72f-40df-8a78-c620a1e18a5d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:20:10.742503",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T05:40:18.118685",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_054018.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_054018.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:23.900\nThink about it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:35.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. Or, if you're trying to remember your friend's phone number, you might try to say it out loud. That's a test to see if you remember it correctly!\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:47.200\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like checking the weather before you go outside.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:59.500\nThe main idea is that a test helps you learn something new or confirm something you already thought. So, a test is a way to check, verify, or learn.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:03.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
