    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_054145.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like this: a baking test tells you if your cake is ready, or a spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:30.000\nTests can come in many forms.\nThey might be written questions, like in school.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:42.100\nOr, they could be practical, like trying to fix a bike to see if you understand how it works.\nThe goal is always the same: to measure knowledge or skill.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:53.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check your understanding.\nIt helps you and others see what you've learned and where you might need some extra practice.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:56.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
