  "5f053309-0085-4833-af5e-030b9a251752": {
    "id": "5f053309-0085-4833-af5e-030b9a251752",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:20:16.281588",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T05:49:37.882216",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_054937.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_054937.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.300\nNow, you might think of tests as something scary from school, but in reality, a test is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like this: you buy a new lightbulb.\nTo test if it works, you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:30.400\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:36.600\nAnother example is baking a cake.\nYou follow the recipe, and then you taste it.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:45.400\nThe taste test tells you if you followed the recipe correctly.\nSo, a test is simply a way to verify something.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:54.900\nIt's about checking if something is doing what it\u2019s expected to do.\nIt can be as simple as flipping a switch or as involved as baking a cake.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:00.400\nThat\u2019s the basic idea!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
