    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T16:20:17.224841",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T05:51:19.604527",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_055119.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_055119.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:25.300\nIt\u2019s a process designed to measure your knowledge, skills, or abilities in a particular area.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:34.900\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks how well you spell words.\nA taste test checks how something tastes.\nA medical test checks your health.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:43.300\nFor example, if you're learning to ride a bike, your ability to balance and pedal is being tested.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:51.900\nOr, if you're baking a cake, the taste and texture after baking is a test of your recipe and baking skills.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:00.000\nSo, a test isn't just about getting a grade in school.\nIt's a way to evaluate something and learn from the results.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:03.100\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we need to improve.\n\n01:03.100 --> 01:06.700\nIn short, a test is a measurement tool.\n\n01:06.700 --> 01:07.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a8e7815f-093b-4b8d-8b90-f8cae89d2fcb": {
