    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_055249.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like an experiment, but often much simpler.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:35.400\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it! For example, if you're wondering if it's going to rain, you might look at the sky.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:48.300\nYou're testing the hypothesis that the sky's appearance can predict rain.\nOr, if you're trying a new recipe and taste it, you're testing if it needs more salt.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:57.100\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit. The important thing is you're trying to gather information to answer a question.\nSo, a test helps us learn and make decisions based on evidence. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
