    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_055819.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:22.900\nIt helps us see if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard. Think of it like this: You might test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:33.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! Or, imagine a doctor testing your eyesight by having you read letters on a chart.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:44.600\nThey're checking to see if you can see clearly. Tests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking the quality of products to evaluating your knowledge in school.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:54.800\nThey help us understand where we are and what we might need to improve. So, a test is just a check, a way to learn and make things better.\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:58.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
