    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_055912.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:06.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:08.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:12.500\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:16.500\nEssentially, a test helps us measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.000\nIt could be checking if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.500\nThe toothpick comes out clean? Test passed!\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:29.500\nOr, it could be a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:35.500\nFor example, when you try on a new pair of shoes, you're testing if they fit.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:38.500\nYou walk around, see if they're comfortable.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:39.500\nThat's a test!\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:45.500\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:52.000\nTo recap, tests are all about finding things out.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:56.500\nThey help us measure, evaluate, and get answers to our questions.\n\n00:56.500 --> 00:58.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
