    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_060754.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:27.800\nIt's a process to see if something works, or to check someone's knowledge or skills.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:41.200\nThink of it like this: a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:52.700\nOr, your teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n00:52.700 --> 01:03.000\nA test usually involves asking questions or performing actions and then looking at the results.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:09.600\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n01:09.600 --> 01:15.400\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n01:15.400 --> 01:21.900\nAnother example is taking a spelling test; the number of words you spell correctly shows how well you know your spelling.\n\n01:21.900 --> 01:32.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a way of finding something out by asking questions or performing actions and looking at the results.\n\n01:32.200 --> 01:35.200\nIt helps us learn and improve!\n\n01:35.200 --> 01:39.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
