    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_060925.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:21.600\nIt's like an experiment, but often more structured.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a plant needs more water.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:26.800\nSo, you give it some water and see what happens.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:33.000\nOr maybe you want to know if a new lightbulb works.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\nAnother test!\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.000\nTests aren't just for science, though.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:47.300\nWhen you take a quiz at school, that's a test to see what you've learned.\nWhen a doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:57.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\nIt\u2019s about asking a question and finding an answer.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5125a199-99a6-4170-8dbf-b91b62f63e16": {
    "id": "5125a199-99a6-4170-8dbf-b91b62f63e16",
