  "5e4fc8c2-0e85-4775-811b-e1078502d4f2": {
    "id": "5e4fc8c2-0e85-4775-811b-e1078502d4f2",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:34:58.179499",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T06:14:55.635781",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_061455.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_061455.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, maybe in school.\nBut what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's a process we use to check if something is true, or to measure how well something works.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:31.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\nYou test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:41.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test says they're ready!\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:48.600\nYou test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\nIf it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:57.800\nSo, a test is just a way to get information, whether it's about cookies, lightbulbs, or anything else.\nIt helps us make decisions based on evidence.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:06.200\nRemember, testing is all about learning and finding things out!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
