    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_061539.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:18.500\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, where you're trying to see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:30.900\nThe main idea behind a test is to check if something meets a certain standard or expectation. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.900\nOr, think about a taste test! That checks if you like the flavor of something.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:46.700\nAnother example could be testing a toy to see if it's safe for kids to play with. We check to make sure it doesn't have any small parts that could be swallowed.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:56.200\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something works, is true, or meets our expectations. It helps us learn and make sure things are as they should be.\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:03.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
