    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_062327.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:23.400\nIt helps us check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:31.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:39.200\nYou can test them by poking them with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies are ready!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:48.100\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. That test helps your teacher see if you understand how to spell certain words.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:52.100\nTests aren't always about grades, though.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:58.300\nYou might test a new toy to see if it's fun, or test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:01.800\nBasically, a test is just a way to get information and learn something new.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:05.400\nSo, remember, a test helps us check things and learn.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:06.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
