    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:05.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:08.600\nThink of it like an experiment where you're trying to get an answer.\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:13.800\nIt could be a quiz at school to see what you've learned, or even tasting a new food to see if you like it.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:17.300\nThe main point of a test is to gather information.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:22.300\nWe use tests to check if something works, if something is true, or if someone understands something.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:25.900\nFor example, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:30.100\nA chef might test their recipe to make sure it tastes good.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:33.400\nAnd you might take a practice test before a big exam.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:39.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information and learn something new.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:43.800\nIt helps us understand the world around us better.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:45.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
