    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:23.800\nIt helps us understand if something is working, or if someone knows something.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:30.000\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:36.200\nThat's a test! Or, a teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:41.600\nThat's another kind of test! Tests can be about all sorts of things.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:47.000\nThey can check if a light bulb turns on, if a bridge can hold weight, or even if you can remember the alphabet.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:53.000\nThe important thing is they give us information.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:59.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to learn something by observing or measuring.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.700\nThey help us understand how things work and what people know.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:05.300\nPretty useful, right?\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:08.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
