    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_064842.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: a cookie test. You bake a batch of cookies and you want to know if they taste good.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:25.400\nSo, you eat one! That's your test.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:31.500\nOr imagine you're checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:39.800\nIf it lights up, the test is passed! Tests can be simple, like those examples, or really complex.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:47.200\nBut at their core, they're all about gathering information and checking if something meets a certain requirement.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:54.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find things out.\n00:54.600 --> 00:55.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
