    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_064935.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true. But in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like this: You're baking a cake. You follow the recipe, but how do you know if it's good? You test it!\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:32.600\nYou look at it, smell it, and then, of course, you taste it. That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:36.900\nAnother example is a lightbulb.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:46.400\nBefore they sell lightbulbs, they test them to make sure they actually light up. They want to be sure they work before they get to your house.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:56.000\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it's supposed to. It's a way to make sure things are good!\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
