    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_070702.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:14.800\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:35.100\nFor example, if you try to open a door and it's locked, you've just performed a test to see if you could get in.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:42.800\nThe answer was \"no,\" it's locked! Another simple test is checking if a light switch works.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:55.400\nYou flip the switch, and if the light comes on, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails. So, tests are about checking things and getting a result, a simple yes or no, a pass or fail.\n\n00:55.400 --> 00:59.100\nThey help us understand if something is working as expected.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:01.300\nThat's the basic idea behind a test.\n```"
  },
