    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_072102.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.600\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer, or trying something out to see if it works.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:35.400\nTests help us learn and improve.\nFor example, when you're learning to ride a bike, you might wobble a bit at first.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:38.200\nThat wobble is kind of like a test, showing you where you need to adjust your balance.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:40.900\nOr, imagine a chef trying a new recipe.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:43.700\nThey taste it.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:51.200\nThey're checking if the flavors are right.\nSo, tests can be big or small, formal or informal.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:55.000\nThey're all about gathering information and figuring things out.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.600\nRemember, tests aren't scary, they're just a way to learn more!\n```"
