  "63219ff6-934a-4e26-958a-2fd7b4bd0801": {
    "id": "63219ff6-934a-4e26-958a-2fd7b4bd0801",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:35:41.890456",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T07:24:37.907108",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_072437.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_072437.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to check if something works as it should.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like this: You have a lightbulb, and you want to make sure it lights up.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:29.300\nYou put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:35.800\nYou're testing if the lightbulb is working. Or, imagine you bake a cake.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:42.300\nTasting it afterward is a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:42.300 --> 01:01.000\nSo, a test is simply a procedure designed to verify something. Whether it's checking if a lightbulb shines, tasting a cake, or answering questions in a classroom, tests help us understand if something is functioning correctly or meeting our expectations. That's the basic idea! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3dbda129-40cf-4d00-9a01-42f88a97632e": {
    "id": "3dbda129-40cf-4d00-9a01-42f88a97632e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:35:42.339056",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T07:25:29.413000",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_072529.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_072529.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.400\nWhat are they, and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to see how much you know about something.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: if you've been learning about animals, a test might ask you to name different animals or describe what they eat.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:32.900\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. Sometimes they're multiple choice, where you pick the best answer from a few options.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:40.800\nOther times, you might have to write out your answers, like in an essay. Imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:48.700\nA test is like checking to see if the cake is cooked all the way through. It helps you know if you need to bake it longer.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:59.700\nIn school, tests help your teachers see what you've learned and what you might need more help with. So, tests are just tools that help us learn and grow.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:03.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "880664f2-1b18-45d3-b97c-64c8a8d40783": {
    "id": "880664f2-1b18-45d3-b97c-64c8a8d40783",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:35:42.918272",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T07:26:21.865430",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_072621.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_072621.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.100\nNow, you've probably heard the word \"test\" used in lots of different ways, but at its core, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like a way to see if something is working correctly or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:35.800\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, a baker might taste a cake to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:49.100\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned. So, tests help us understand if something is working as it should.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:52.100\nAnother simple example:\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:55.100\npressing a button on a remote control\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:58.800\nis like a mini-test to see if the TV will turn on.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:01.200\nSee?\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:01.800\nTests are all around us!\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:12.400\nSo, remember, a test is a check to see if something is working or meeting a standard. It's a way to understand if things are as they should be.\n\n01:12.400 --> 01:15.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
