    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_072711.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:06.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:8.600\nThink of it like asking a question and then getting an answer.\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:12.200\nWe use tests all the time, whether we realize it or not.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:19.000\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like the taste.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:24.000\nOr, when you press the button on a remote control, you're testing to see if it turns on the TV.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:27.400\nThe \"test\" is the action you take, and the result tells you something.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:32.500\nAnother example could be a doctor testing your eyesight, or even a teacher giving a quiz.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:35.700\nThey're all using tests to learn something specific.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:41.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way of gathering information by trying something out.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:47.000\nTo recap: tests help us learn, explore, and confirm things.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:50.500\nThey're all around us in everyday life.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:52.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
