    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_072936.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.700\nNow, you've probably taken a test at school, but in general, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like a small experiment. Basically, you do something, and then you observe the result.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:29.800\nThe result gives you information. For example, a taste test tells you if you like a food or not.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:34.800\nOr, a simple tap on your knee tests your reflexes.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:41.000\nSee? We're gathering information.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:52.400\nAnother example could be checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in, flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:05.400\nIf it doesn't, well, the bulb probably needs replacing. So, a test is a simple way of checking something to learn more about it.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:10.400\nTo sum it up, tests help us understand, diagnose, or confirm information.\n\n01:10.400 --> 01:15.400\nThey're everywhere! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
