    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nNow, you might think of school exams, and that's one kind, but a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:24.600\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this:\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:32.500\nyou want to know if a lightbulb works.\nYour test?\nPlugging it in!\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:40.900\nIf it lights up, the test passes.\nIf it doesn't, it fails.\nAnother example: you want to know if your soup is hot enough.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:49.400\nYou test it by taking a spoonful and tasting it.\nSo, a test is really just a procedure to check if something is working correctly, or to see if something is true.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:59.600\nWe use tests every day, often without even realizing it!\nHopefully, this gives you a good basic understanding of what a test is.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
