    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_073257.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:26.000\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way. Think of it like this: if you want to know if water is hot, you can test it by carefully touching it.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:36.100\nThe feeling on your finger is the answer! Or, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you can test it by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:42.600\nIf it lights up, it passes the test! Tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:49.100\nThey can tell us if something is working correctly, if we understand a new concept, or even how good something is.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:57.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information and learn!\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
