    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_073602.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:20.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:24.700\nYou might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:34.700\nThe toothpick test tells you if the batter is still wet inside. Similarly, a doctor might order a blood test to check your vitamin levels.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:48.600\nOr maybe you take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a topic. These are all different kinds of tests, but they all share the same purpose: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:55.000\nSo, a test helps us understand if something is working correctly, if we've learned something, or if there's a problem we need to address.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
