    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_073815.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us check if something is working, if we understand something, or just to see what happens when we try something new.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe by making a small batch first to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:37.600\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge of a subject. For example, a car manufacturer tests new cars to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:45.800\nA doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you sick. Even trying a new flavor of ice cream is a kind of test!\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:55.700\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions. They're all about gathering information.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:59.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
