    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking. You can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:33.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:39.200\nYou test it by screwing it into a lamp. If it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:48.700\nIf not, well, it fails. So, a test helps us check if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:60.000\nIt can be as simple as checking a cake or a lightbulb, or much more complicated. Remember, tests are all about finding out information!\n\n00:60.000 --> 00:63.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
