    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.300\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:11.700\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:22.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you know something.\nThink of it like a mini-investigation.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:28.400\nThe main idea behind a test is to give it a specific input, and then check if you get the expected output.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:31.800\nIf you do, great, the test passes!\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:34.400\nIf not, something might be wrong.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:42.700\nFor example, imagine you're testing a lightbulb.\nThe input is turning the switch on.\nThe expected output is light.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:45.300\nIf the lightbulb doesn't light up, the test fails.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:52.400\nOr, think about a spelling test in school.\nThe input is the question, and the output is your answer.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:55.900\nIf your answer is correct, you pass that part of the test!\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:03.300\nSo, a test is basically a way to confirm things are working as they should, by checking the output against what you expect.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:06.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e71b21cd-01a0-45db-bc8d-46347ae91154": {
    "id": "e71b21cd-01a0-45db-bc8d-46347ae91154",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:35:52.783829",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T07:43:52.676327",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_074352.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_074352.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:17.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:21.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:25.200\nThat's a test! The toothpick comes out clean? The cake's ready.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:31.400\nAnother example: a doctor uses a test to see if you're sick. They might take your temperature.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:35.200\nHigh temperature? That's a clue!\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:39.000\nTests aren't just for cakes and doctors, though.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:43.600\nWe use them all the time, in all sorts of situations.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:59.200\nFrom checking if your phone's battery is charged to seeing if you understand a new topic in school, tests help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:01.600\nSo, a test is essentially a way to check or examine something to learn more about it.\n```"
  },
