    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.600\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:26.000\nYou're checking if the lightbulb does what it's supposed to do \u2013 light up.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.300\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs, though.\nThey can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:43.400\nMaybe you're testing if your cookies taste good, or if a new app works on your phone.\nIn each case, you're performing an action and seeing what happens.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:49.400\nIf the result is what you expected, the test passes.\nIf not, it fails.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:58.900\nSo, a test is simply a way to confirm if something is working as expected.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
