    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_074655.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, it's a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like this: imagine you're baking a cake. The recipe is your plan, and tasting the cake is the test.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:27.900\nDoes it taste good? Is it cooked all the way through? That's the test giving you information.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:31.500\nAnother example could be checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:36.100\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test! Does it light up?\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:38.700\nYes? Then it passes the test.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:40.700\nNo? Time for a new bulb!\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:45.300\nSo, a test is just a method to see if something meets a certain expectation.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:52.100\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:00.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
