    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.225 --> 00:01.065\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.065 --> 00:02.835\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:02.835 --> 00:03.925\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.925 --> 00:06.395\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.395 --> 00:08.865\nIt's a process used to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:08.865 --> 00:13.575\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:13.575 --> 00:17.055\nA taste test checks which snack you like better.\n\n00:17.055 --> 00:20.505\nAnd a stress test on a bridge checks how much weight it can hold.\n\n00:20.505 --> 00:22.795\nSo, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:22.795 --> 00:27.995\nThey give us information we can use to make decisions, improve our skills, or just learn something new.\n\n00:27.995 --> 00:31.295\nThey can be simple or complex, but the main goal is always to get some kind of result.\n\n00:31.295 --> 00:35.525\nRemember, a test isn't about passing or failing, it's about learning!\n\n00:35.525 --> 00:39.065\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
