    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_080025.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 and no, not the kind you take in school!\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:16.900\nIn the world of software and technology, a \"test\" is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like this: you build a LEGO car. A test is like pushing it to see if the wheels turn.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:27.800\nIf they do, great! The test passes.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:35.300\nIf they don't, the test fails, and you know you need to fix something.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:47.300\nTests can be really simple. For example, does a button on a website actually take you to the right page?\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:53.600\nOr, does a calculator app give you the correct answer when you type in 2 + 2?\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:00.000\nThese are all tests. Tests help make sure things are reliable and prevent errors.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:11.100\nThey're a super important part of building anything that involves technology. So, remember, a test is just a check to see if something works as expected.\n\n01:11.100 --> 01:14.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
