    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_080425.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:18.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like a puzzle: it asks you questions, and you use your knowledge to find the answers.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:37.000\nTests can come in many forms. You might have multiple-choice questions, where you pick the best answer from a list. Or maybe it's a true or false test, where you decide if a statement is correct.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:51.600\nSometimes, you even get to write out your answers in your own words! For example, a simple test could be asking, \"What color is the sky?\" The answer, of course, is blue! Or, \"Is a dog a type of cat?\" The answer to that is false.\n\n00:51.600 --> 01:03.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check your understanding. It helps you and your teachers see what you've learned and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:08.300\nIt\u2019s a learning tool! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
