    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_080609.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.900\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:28.900\nIt could be anything from a school exam to see what you\u2019ve learned, to a simple taste test to see which cookie you like better.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:42.100\nThe main idea is that you're performing an action or asking a question, and then observing the result.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:54.500\nFor example, a scientist might test if a new fertilizer helps plants grow. They'd give some plants the fertilizer and some plants none, and then compare how well they grow.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:00.600\nOr, you might test a new recipe by making it and seeing if it tastes good!\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:06.100\nSo, remember, a test is all about finding something out by trying something out.\n```"
  },
  "efc9cf17-7d41-43c2-9ff8-e06c43028df1": {
    "id": "efc9cf17-7d41-43c2-9ff8-e06c43028df1",
    "topic": "Test",
