    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_080653.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:26.100\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard. Think about it like this: When you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:38.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! Or, if you're learning to ride a bike, you might test your balance by letting go of the handlebars for a few seconds. That tells you how well you're doing.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:50.300\nTests are used everywhere, from checking if your computer program works, to seeing if a bridge is safe to drive on.\n\n00:50.300 --> 01:03.900\nThe main goal is always the same: to get information and make sure things are okay.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:07.600\nSo, a test is simply a way of checking something to see if it's working or meeting a standard. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
