    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_080824.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey there, welcome! Today we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:16.100\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:24.500\nThat's a test! Basically, you\u2019re performing an action to see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:30.500\nLet\u2019s say you're testing if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:37.200\nIf it lights up, the test passes! Or maybe you're testing if a toy car needs new batteries.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:46.800\nIf it moves slowly, the test tells you it\u2019s time for fresh ones. So, a test is just a method for evaluating something.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:55.800\nYou do something, observe the result, and then you know if it passes or fails. Pretty straightforward, right?\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:59.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
