    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_081729.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! \nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:12.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? \nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:24.800\nIt helps us understand if something is true, working, or correct. \nThink of it like this: a test can be as simple as tasting a new food to see if you like it.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:31.400\nThat's a test! \nOr, imagine you're checking if a light bulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:36.800\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:42.200\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:54.500\nIn science, scientists run tests to see if their ideas are right. \nTests help us make sure things are safe, reliable, and doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:05.100\nSo, a test is just a method to check something. \nIt can be simple or complex, but the goal is always the same: to learn more.\n\n01:05.100 --> 01:08.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
