    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:36.300\nThat's a test! Essentially, you're performing an action to see if something behaves the way you expect.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:46.200\nIt can be something simple, like checking if your shoes fit, or something more complicated, like a doctor running blood work.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:54.200\nThe point is, you're gathering information to make a decision.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:02.200\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:09.600\nOr, a student might take a practice quiz to test their knowledge before a big exam.\n\n01:09.600 --> 01:17.600\nThese are all tests! So, to recap, a test is a procedure designed to check something and give you information about it.\n\n01:17.600 --> 01:28.500\nIt helps you confirm if something is working, accurate, or meeting a certain standard. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
