    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_083056.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.700 --> 00:03.900\nToday, we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:07.100\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:09.700\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:09.700 --> 00:12.800\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:17.300\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:18.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:24.100\nOr, if you're buying a new phone, you might try out the camera to see if you like the picture quality.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:24.800\nThat\u2019s also a test.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:29.100\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:35.400\nThey can be as simple as checking the weather forecast before going outside, or more complex, like a medical exam.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:39.600\nThey all have the same basic goal: to learn something new.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:42.700\nIn short, a test helps us understand something better.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:44.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
