    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_083706.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nWhat are they, and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to check how well you understand something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:21.900\nIt could be anything from a quick quiz in school to a longer exam covering a whole semester's worth of material.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:32.600\nThe main goal is to measure your knowledge or skills. Think of it like this: If you're learning to bake a cake, you might give a slice to a friend to taste.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:41.100\nTheir feedback is like a mini-test \u2013 it tells you if you followed the recipe correctly and if the cake tastes good!\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:49.600\nOr, imagine learning to ride a bike. Successfully riding without falling is a test of your balance and coordination.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:59.400\nSo, tests help us see what we've learned and where we might need to focus our efforts. They're a useful tool for both learning and teaching.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
