    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_084653.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:25.700\nIt's a method for gathering information or checking if something is working properly.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:36.100\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling, right?\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:47.400\nOr a taste test helps you decide which cookie is the tastiest.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:59.700\nIn science and other fields, tests are used to prove ideas or theories.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:03.100\nFor example, you might test if a plant grows faster with more sunlight.\n\n01:03.100 --> 01:14.400\nYou'd give one plant lots of sun and another less, then compare the results.\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:20.300\nSo, a test is just a way to learn something new or confirm what you already suspect.\n\n01:20.300 --> 01:25.700\nIt involves a process, some kind of measurement, and then you look at the results.\n\n01:25.700 --> 01:30.600\nRemember: tests help us understand the world around us!\n\n01:30.600 --> 01:34.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
