    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_085155.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:07.500\nToday we're diving into something fundamental: a test!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:18.000\nIt's a method for figuring out if something works, if something is true, or even how well something performs.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: your doctor gives you a physical exam.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.800\nThat's a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.500\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake and you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:34.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test to see if the cake is done.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:41.000\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like tasting soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.000\nThe key is that a test gives you information to help you make a decision or understand something better.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:51.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:55.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
