    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_085339.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:23.100\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand something better.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:28.000\nThink about it like this: a chef tastes a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:32.900\nOr a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:39.600\nSee? They're both using tests to get information.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:46.300\nAnother example is a spelling test at school.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:52.900\nIt helps your teacher see what words you know and which ones you might need to practice more.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:00.300\nSo, tests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all have the same goal: to learn something new.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:04.900\nIn summary, a test is just a tool we use to gather information and improve our understanding.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:06.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
