    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something fundamental: the concept of a test.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:17.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:30.100\nYou don't just guess, right? You perform a test! You poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test result telling you the cake is ready.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:35.500\nOr imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:42.100\nThe test? You screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. If it lights up, the bulb passes the test!\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:48.700\nIf not, well\u2026 the bulb failed. Basically, a test is any procedure designed to give you information.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:57.700\nIt helps you make decisions based on evidence. So, remember: tests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
