    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:36:38.343043",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T09:01:11.624558",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_090111.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_090111.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:23.000\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, maybe in school.\nBut what exactly is a test?\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:29.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:35.400\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we know something well.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:41.600\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:45.800\nYou plug it in, and that's the test.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:49.400\nIf it lights up, great!\nIt passes the test.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:51.600\nIf it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:55.600\nAnother example: Imagine you're learning a new recipe.\n\n00:55.600 --> 01:00.400\nYou follow the instructions, and then you taste the food.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:04.000\nThat taste test tells you if you followed the recipe correctly.\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:11.200\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information, whether it's checking a light bulb or tasting food.\n\n01:11.200 --> 01:14.200\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n01:14.200 --> 01:17.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6eb88b32-5eac-4991-84e9-c8b8057a1b30": {
    "id": "6eb88b32-5eac-4991-84e9-c8b8057a1b30",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:36:38.766429",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T09:01:57.069688",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_090156.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_090156.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:17.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:28.900\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:42.100\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the \"done-ness\" test!\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:55.500\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works, you can try to turn it on. If it lights up, it passes the \"working\" test!\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:06.200\nBasically, a test helps us check if something is true or false, good or bad, working or not working. It's all about getting information.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:09.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new by asking a question and seeing what happens.\n\n01:09.800 --> 01:13.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
