    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_091205.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! \nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. \nThink of it like a simple question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:18.600\nDoes something work? Is something true? \n\n00:18.600 --> 00:27.300\nThe test helps you find out. \nFor example, you might test if a light bulb works by screwing it in and turning it on.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:34.800\nThe test is: does it light up? \nOr, you might test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:48.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! \nSo, testing is all about checking things, making sure they work, or confirming that something is true.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:55.000\nIt\u2019s a really important part of learning and building things. \nAnd that's the basics of testing!\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
