    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_091342.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:23.000\nIt\u2019s a process designed to evaluate or measure something, whether it's your knowledge, the quality of a product, or even how well an experiment worked.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:32.600\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your spelling skills.\nA taste test helps you decide which cookie is the tastiest.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:48.800\nAnd a medical test can help doctors figure out what's going on with your health.\nSo, in each case, we\u2019re doing something \u2013 asking questions, trying samples, taking measurements \u2013 to get information.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:58.800\nIt's all about gathering data to understand something better.\nTests help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:06.500\nRemember, a test is just a way to find something out!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f428769c-3bf2-4ea7-8ffa-556b42be90f5": {
    "id": "f428769c-3bf2-4ea7-8ffa-556b42be90f5",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:36:46.879797",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T09:14:22.878211",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_091422.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_091422.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in the world of science and research, a test is simply a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:27.000\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer based on what you observe. Essentially, a test is a procedure designed to confirm or deny a hypothesis.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:36.900\nThink of it like this: You think plants grow better with sunlight. Your test could involve growing one plant in sunlight and another in the dark.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:45.600\nThe results of your test, like how tall each plant grows, help you decide if your idea about sunlight was right.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:52.400\nRemember, a test doesn't always have to be complicated. It's just a way to gather information.\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:02.200\nSo, a test is a structured way to investigate something and draw conclusions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d8bef042-d30b-4f61-8a9c-d722ff79605e": {
    "id": "d8bef042-d30b-4f61-8a9c-d722ff79605e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:36:47.377707",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T09:15:11.456222",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_091511.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_091511.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.900\nNo, not the kind you cram for! In computer programming, a test is like a little check-up for your code.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:22.100\nThink of it this way: you build a car, right? You want to make sure it works before you drive it across the country.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:29.700\nTests do that for your code. They automatically run your code and see if it behaves the way you expect.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:43.400\nFor example, if you write code to add two numbers, a test would check if 2 + 2 actually equals 4. If it doesn't, the test fails, and you know you have a problem!\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:58.000\nTests help you find mistakes early, making your code more reliable and easier to understand. So, tests are basically automated checkers that help make sure your code does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:03.200\nPretty neat, huh? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b942b505-9aef-4132-996c-141d96f04114": {
