    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_091556.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:22.900\nIt's a process, or a procedure, designed to evaluate.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:31.500\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:47.600\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a topic. Even baking a cake is a kind of test! You're testing the recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:57.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a bridge is safe, to seeing if a new medicine works, or even just figuring out what kind of music you like.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:08.000\nThe important thing is that a test gives us information.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:14.800\nSo, remember, a test is a way to learn something by evaluating it.\n\n01:14.800 --> 01:17.700\nIt helps us understand the world around us.\n01:17.700 --> 01:24.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
