    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_092223.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey there, and welcome! \n\n00:02.000 --> 00:03.300\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:08.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you've learned something new.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:14.800\nThink of it like this: you might test a new toy to make sure it doesn't break, or you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:19.000\nTests can be big or small.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.700\nA simple test could be pressing a button to see if a light turns on.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:27.700\nA bigger test might be a whole exam at the end of a school year.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:38.600\nSo, to recap: a test is simply a way to check on something, whether it's a skill you've learned or the quality of a product.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:45.300\nIt helps us understand if things are working as they should.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:51.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
