    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_092300.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:06.200\nIn simple terms, a test is really just a way to find out information.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:12.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:13.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:18.100\nThe toothpick tells you whether the inside is cooked or not.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:21.300\nTests aren't just for baking, though.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:24.400\nA doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.500\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:31.500\nEven trying a new recipe is a test!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:33.700\nYou're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:38.900\nSo, a test helps us understand something better by giving us some kind of result.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:44.900\nBasically, it's a way to check something, learn something, or discover something new.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:47.200\nThat's the power of a test!\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:54.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
