    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.800\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:39.800\nOr, when you take a quiz in school, that's a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:49.200\nAnother example is baking a cake. You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:49.200 --> 01:00.000\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions. They're a way to check things and see if they're working as expected. They can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all help us learn and understand. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
