    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:18.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:25.700\nThat's a test! The toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:31.900\nThe cake passes the test! It's ready to eat.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:38.100\nOr imagine you're checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:44.100\nIf it lights up, it passes the test. If not, well, time for a new bulb.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:52.600\nTests help us understand things better, whether it's knowing when a cake is baked or if a lightbulb works. They give us information to make decisions.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:56.400\nSo remember, a test is just a way to learn more about something!\n\n00:56.400 --> 00:57.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
