    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:04.300\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:05.500\nwhat they are and why we use them.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:09.400\nBasically, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:11.400\nThink of it like an experiment.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:14.500\nWe're trying to see how something behaves or what it can do.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:18.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:23.000\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.500\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test, to see if your recipe works!\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:32.500\nSo, tests help us learn, understand, and make decisions based on the results.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:36.600\nThey give us valuable information that we can use to improve things.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:41.000\nThey are used in medicine, education, science and everyday life.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:43.000\nIn short, a test is a way to gain information.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
