    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:23.300\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:28.100\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:32.900\nThink about it like this: You want to know if a lightbulb works, right?\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:37.700\nSo, you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:44.800\nYou're testing if the lightbulb will turn on. Or maybe you\u2019re baking a cake and you want to know if it\u2019s done.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:50.600\nYou poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that\u2019s another test!\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:56.400\nYou\u2019re testing if the cake is cooked through.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:01.700\nTests can be simple, like those examples, or they can be more complicated.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:09.000\nBut the basic idea is always the same: it's a way to get information and see if something meets a certain requirement.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:15.900\nSo remember, a test is just a way to check something and find out if it works or if it's true.\n\n01:15.900 --> 01:19.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
