    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:14.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\nIt's a process we use to gather information.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:22.600\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:33.500\nOr, when a doctor checks your temperature, they're testing to see if you have a fever.\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:42.100\nSo, a test can be anything that helps us answer a question.\nIt's about observing something and drawing a conclusion.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:52.900\nWhether it's a science experiment, a quiz, or even just trying a new recipe, you're using a test to learn and understand the world around you.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:05.400\nTo recap, a test is a method for collecting data and answering questions.\nIt can be formal, like an exam, or informal, like tasting a cake.\nAnd they're all around us.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:11.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
