    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_094216.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:04.600\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:08.000\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:09.900\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:13.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:15.600\nYou can do a test! You stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:20.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test \u2013 it's ready!\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:22.700\nIf it's gooey, it fails \u2013 it needs more time.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:26.500\nAnother example: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:29.600\nMaybe they check your temperature or listen to your heart.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:31.400\nThese are all different kinds of tests.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:35.400\nSo, to recap, a test helps us learn something.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:38.200\nIt gives us information to make a decision.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:43.700\nIt's a simple way of checking if something is true or false, good or bad, ready or not.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:46.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
