    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_094627.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:11.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:17.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch \u2013 that\u2019s the test!\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:24.200\nIf it lights up, great! If not, well, the bulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:29.700\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs though.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:37.100\nImagine you're learning to ride a bike. You keep practicing, and each time you try, you're basically testing your skills.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:42.700\nAre you balanced? Can you pedal smoothly?\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:52.100\nSo, a test is just a way to check something. It could be checking if your bike skills are improving, or checking if a lightbulb is working.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:53.900\nIt's all about finding out information.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:55.800\nPretty straightforward, right?\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:58.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
