    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_094714.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:24.000\nNow, in general, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:29.200\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:34.400\nThat answer then helps you understand something better.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:39.600\nFor example, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:43.500\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:47.400\nSee? Both are tests! They help us learn and improve.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:51.300\nAnother example is testing your toys to see if they are working correctly.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:54.900\nOr you can test out your new bike to see if the brakes are working.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:00.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a process to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:02.400\nIt helps us understand things better!\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:06.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "116274a6-1c10-4799-aebc-2693b0d70139": {
    "id": "116274a6-1c10-4799-aebc-2693b0d70139",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:37:08.718936",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T09:48:29.506173",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_094829.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_094829.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. In the world of computers, a test checks if something is true or false.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:28.200\nFor example, we can test if a number is bigger than another number.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:34.900\nIs 5 greater than 3? Yes, that's true!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:39.400\nOr, we can test if two words are the same.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:43.900\nIs \"hello\" equal to \"hello\"? Again, true!\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:50.500\nBut is \"hello\" equal to \"goodbye\"? Nope, that's false.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:54.900\nSo remember, a test checks if something is true or false.\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:58.500\nWe use tests all the time in computer programs to make decisions.\n```"
  },
  "b2652dce-b5c4-408b-a097-a7664c09715d": {
    "id": "b2652dce-b5c4-408b-a097-a7664c09715d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:37:09.288933",
