    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_094912.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:21.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, so you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:28.400\nTests help us gather information and make decisions. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:37.200\nTeachers use tests to see how well you understand a subject. And even engineers use tests to make sure bridges are safe.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:48.100\nHere's another example: you might test if a toy car runs faster on a wooden floor or a carpet. You're finding out which surface is better for speed.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:57.100\nSo, remember, a test is really just a way to learn something new. It helps us understand the world around us.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:00.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
