    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:37:14.243921",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T09:56:10.494655",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_095610.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_095610.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.100\nA test is really just a way to find out something. It could be how well you know a subject, like in a school test, or it could be to check if something works properly.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if your cookies are done, you might do a \"test\" by sticking a toothpick in them.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:33.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cookies pass the test!\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:43.300\nOr, imagine you\u2019re building a tower of blocks. You might gently push it to \"test\" if it's stable.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:52.600\nIf it falls over, it failed the test, and you need to build it differently. So, a test is simply a method used to evaluate or check something.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:59.300\nIt helps us understand more about what we're looking at. In short, tests give us information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
