    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_095729.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:10.600\nWhat is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We test things all the time without even realizing it.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:25.200\nFor example, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you try turning it on. That's a test!\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:35.900\nOr, if you're baking a cake and want to know if it's done, you stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:51.100\nTests can be simple, like those, or more complicated, like the ones you take in school. But the basic idea is the same: you're trying to learn something or see if something works as expected.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:59.200\nSo remember, a test is just a way to get information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "190d2954-0f6e-4918-8700-7744cc3516fd": {
    "id": "190d2954-0f6e-4918-8700-7744cc3516fd",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:37:15.652070",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T09:58:37.501674",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_095837.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_095837.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.700\nNow, you've probably taken tests in school, but the idea of a \"test\" is much broader than just exams.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:28.500\nBasically, a test is any procedure designed to evaluate something. It could be checking if a light bulb works, seeing if a recipe tastes good, or even figuring out if a plant needs water.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:39.100\nThe main idea is simple: you do something, then you observe the result. If the light bulb lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:50.300\nIf the recipe tastes great, it passes the taste test! And if the plant's soil is dry, it fails the \"needs water\" test.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:58.900\nSo, a test helps you understand something about the world around you. It helps you make decisions based on evidence.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:03.600\nRemember, a test is just a way to check something and get information.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:07.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
