    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_100619.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you learn about numbers, and then you take a test to see if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:33.500\nTests can come in many forms, like multiple choice questions, true or false statements, or even short answer questions.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:41.400\nThey help teachers, and even you, understand what you've learned well and what you might need to practice a little more.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:51.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know how to spell words. Or a math test shows how well you understand math problems.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:57.000\nIt's all about checking your understanding.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:01.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to see what you know and help you learn even better.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:06.600\nIt's nothing to be afraid of! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
