    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_101435.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.600\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, whether it was a quiz in school or even just trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:26.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:30.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:33.900\nThe toothpick comes out clean? Great, the cake is ready.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:39.000\nIt's sticky? Needs more time.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:49.600\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, scientists use them to prove or disprove theories,\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:57.800\nand you can even test out a new skateboard trick.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:03.800\nSo, in short, a test is a method to gather information and see if something is true or working correctly. It's all about finding things out!\n```"
  },
