  "8800af78-8fa0-4bf8-916b-cb1ca6b95cad": {
    "id": "8800af78-8fa0-4bf8-916b-cb1ca6b95cad",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:37:25.926518",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T10:16:13.932391",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_101613.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_101613.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:18.200\nA test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're also getting evidence to support that answer.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:25.200\nTests are used everywhere! For example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:33.000\nA baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:40.900\nLet's say you want to know if a plant needs water. You could test it by touching the soil. If it feels dry, that's a test showing it probably needs water!\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:50.400\nOr, if you want to see if your toy car works, you put batteries in it. If it drives, the test shows it works!\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:02.000\nSo, tests help us learn and make decisions by giving us information. They can be as simple as touching something or as complex as a scientific experiment.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:08.700\nThat's the basic idea behind a test! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
