    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:14.000\nIn everyday language, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:28.600\nBut in the world of science and learning, a test is a specific procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:35.600\nFor example, if you're learning to bake, a taste test can tell you if your cookies are delicious.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:43.100\nOr, if you're studying for a history exam, the exam itself is a test of how much you've learned.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:51.500\nAnother test example is a medical test, like when your doctor checks your blood pressure, they are testing your health.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:59.200\nSo, in short, a test is a structured way to check on something, whether it's your cooking, your knowledge, or even your health.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:03.600\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we might need to work on.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
