    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_103442.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.200\nThink of a test as a way to check something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:20.900\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer to see if it's right.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:25.300\nIn science, a test can be an experiment.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:34.100\nImagine you want to know if plants grow better with sunlight. You could plant two seeds, give one sunlight and the other none.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:38.500\nThen, you watch and see which one grows taller.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:39.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:44.300\nOr, think about a medical test.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:48.400\nWhen you go to the doctor, they might take your temperature.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:52.600\nThat's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:54.600\nTests help us understand things better.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:00.200\nSo, a test is simply a way to find out if something is true, working, or present. It's all about gathering information to learn and understand.\n```"
  },
