    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_105140.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.900\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, and while those are a type of test, we're talking about something a little broader.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:28.600\nA test is basically a way to find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:33.000\nThink of it like this: You buy a new lightbulb, you want to test if it works, right?\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:45.700\nSo you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test! Or, if you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:57.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test showing your cake is ready. Tests help us learn and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:01.400\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something out and see if it passes or fails.\n```"
  },
