    "subtitles": "WEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.700\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:26.400\nThat toothpick is a test! In general, a test helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:36.800\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:45.000\nSo, tests can come in all shapes and sizes. Some are simple, like checking if a lightbulb turns on.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.500\nOthers are more complex, like a scientific experiment. The key thing is they all help us learn something or confirm something.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:03.700\nTo recap, a test is a way to check if something is true or working. It helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:07.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI."
