    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.500\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but we're talking about something a little broader.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:26.200\nA test is really just a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:33.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:39.800\nYour test is screwing it into a lamp and turning the switch. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:46.700\nAnother example: You want to know if an apple is ripe. Your test might be giving it a gentle squeeze.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:55.200\nIf it's firm but gives a little, it's probably ripe. So, a test is simply a way of checking something to see if it meets a certain requirement or expectation.\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:56.900\nIt's a question and an action, and the result tells you the answer. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
