    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:14.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:31.600\nA teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:46.300\nOr even baking a cake is a test! You're testing your recipe and your skills to see if you can make something delicious.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:56.900\nSo, tests help us understand things, check our knowledge, or see if something works. They come in all shapes and sizes, from simple quizzes to complicated experiments.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:04.100\nThey're all about gathering information. In short, a test is a method of inquiry, a way to gather information or assess something. Understanding this basic concept is the first step.\n```"
