    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_110432.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:26.000\nIt's a process designed to measure your knowledge, skills, or abilities on a specific topic.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:35.900\nThink of it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy. Or a chef tastes a dish to test if it's seasoned correctly.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:44.200\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned in class.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:53.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling words. A math test checks your ability to solve math problems. And a fitness test checks your physical strength and endurance.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to measure something. It helps us understand where we are and what we need to work on.\n```"
