    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like this: You have a lightbulb. To test if it works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:29.700\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn\u2019t, the test fails.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:41.200\nTests can be simple, like checking if a button works on a toy. Or they can be more complicated, like seeing if a new medicine helps people feel better.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:50.200\nThe important thing is that a test gives you information. It tells you if something is working correctly or if it needs to be fixed.\n\n00:50.200 --> 01:01.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is doing what it's supposed to do. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
