    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_110822.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_110822.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:20.800\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:26.400\nThink about it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:30.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:32.000\nYou taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.600\nSee? It\u2019s all about gathering information.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:41.200\nTests can be written, like a school exam.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:43.900\nOr they can be hands-on, like checking if a lightbulb works by plugging it in.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:45.800\nThe important thing is they help us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:55.700\nSo, to recap, a test is a process for finding out information, whether it's about your health, the sweetness of a cake, or your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:58.900\nIt's a simple way to learn and improve.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
