  "58c26b45-6c98-4edf-a8e9-5d29f3e17b0d": {
    "id": "58c26b45-6c98-4edf-a8e9-5d29f3e17b0d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:38:06.793921",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T11:17:43.868615",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_111743.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_111743.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE: The subtitle timings are approximate and based on the narration script provided. Adjust as needed for perfect synchronization with the actual audio.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:08.000\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly,\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:10.000\nor if you understand something.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:11.500\nIt's like a little detective game!\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:16.000\nBasically, a test compares what you expect to happen with what actually happens.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:19.000\nIf they match, great! The test passes.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.000\nIf they don't, then something's not quite right and the test fails.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.000\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.000\nThe test is: does it taste good?\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:33.000\nYou expect it to taste delicious, but if it tastes awful, the test failed!\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:38.000\nOr think about checking if your phone turns on. You expect it to power up when you press the button.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:41.000\nIf it doesn't, that's a failed test.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:46.000\nSo, remember, a test is all about checking if things are working as expected.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:51.000\nIt helps us find problems and make sure everything is running smoothly.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:54.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
