  "54893f57-a519-451b-ad95-dcd4a8b685cf": {
    "id": "54893f57-a519-451b-ad95-dcd4a8b685cf",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:38:18.267740",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T11:34:31.933437",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_113431.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_113431.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:06.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:14.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like checking if your bike tires have enough air. The main idea behind any test is to see if the thing being tested passes or fails.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:35.600\nWe do this by comparing it to what we expect, or what's considered \"normal.\" For example, a doctor might give you a test to check if you have a fever.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:46.200\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson. Even baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you\u2019re testing the recipe!\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:56.100\nSo, remember, tests help us understand if something is working as it should. They compare the actual result to what we expect.\n\n00:56.100 --> 00:59.900\nThat's the basics of testing!\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
