    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:09.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:19.800\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:30.100\nThink of it like an experiment, or a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:37.800\nBasically, you create a situation, then you observe what happens.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:42.000\nThat \"what happens\" is the result of your test.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:46.200\nFor example, a cookie recipe is a test.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:50.400\nYou mix the ingredients, bake it, and then you taste it.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:54.600\nThe taste is the result, telling you if the recipe works.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:58.800\nOr, think about checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:03.000\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:05.200\nDoes it light up?\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:07.200\nThat's your test!\n\n01:07.200 --> 01:13.500\nSo, tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:13.500 --> 01:18.200\nThey're all about asking a question and then seeing what the answer is.\n\n01:18.200 --> 01:24.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
