    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_115532.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.200\nHello, and welcome!\n\n00:01.200 --> 00:02.700\nToday, we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:05.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.100\nIt's how we find out if something is working correctly, or if we understand something.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:12.200\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:15.800\nIf the light comes on, the bulb passes the test. If it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:18.000\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.500\nWhen you take a quiz at school, that's a test to see how well you learned the material.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:26.600\nOr when a doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:30.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.000\nIt helps us learn, fix problems, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:37.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
