    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_115625.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_115625.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:09.900\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:16.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:25.200\nThink about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:29.800\nOr, a doctor might run tests to check your health.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:31.900\nIt's all about finding out information!\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.700\nFor example, a simple spelling test can show you which words you need to practice.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:41.600\nAnd testing a new toy car can tell you how fast it goes.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:44.600\nTests help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:53.700\nSo, remember, a test is a method for evaluating something, whether it's your understanding or the performance of an object.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:56.600\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n00:56.600 --> 00:57.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
