    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_115915.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:04.500\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:07.700\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:13.200\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if we understand something, or even just to see what's true.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a light bulb works, you test it by screwing it in and turning it on.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.500\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:29.200\nOr, if your teacher gives you a quiz, that's a test to see how well you understand the lesson.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:33.700\nTests can be big or small, simple or complex.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:41.400\nBut the main idea is always the same: to get some information or confirmation about something.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:47.500\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to find things out.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
