    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:08.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:14.600\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to see how much you know about something, or how well something works.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:17.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb still shines.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:28.400\nThere are all kinds of tests. You might take a spelling test at school to see how good you are at spelling words. Or, a car manufacturer might test a new car to make sure it's safe to drive.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:33.600\nThe goal is to find out information.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:39.700\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:42.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:42.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:48.400\nSo, tests help us measure things and learn more.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:53.900\nThey can be formal, like a big exam, or informal, like checking that cake.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:59.700\nBasically, a test is just a way to get answers.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
