    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_120605.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: tests.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:14.000\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.300\nIt's basically a way to find out information.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:28.300\nTests aren't just about school quizzes! Imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:36.300\nYou might taste the batter before baking \u2013 that's a test to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:45.500\nOr, if your flashlight isn't working, you might test the batteries to see if they're dead. These are all simple tests.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:55.100\nSo, tests help us confirm things, identify problems, and learn more.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:07.500\nThey can be formal, like a math exam, or informal, like checking the temperature of your bath water. Ultimately, a test helps you answer a question.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:16.300\nTo recap: tests are used to gather information, check if things are working properly, and to learn!\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:24.300\nThey come in many forms, from quizzes to simple everyday checks. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
