    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_120751.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:15.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out!\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:28.900\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:36.000\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:47.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a positive test \u2013 the cake is ready! Or, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:47.200 --> 01:00.300\nYou test it by turning it on. If it doesn't light up, that's a test telling you the bulb needs to be replaced.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:04.800\nSo, tests help us understand things better by giving us information.\n01:04.800 --> 01:13.100\nThey can be simple, like checking a cake, or more complicated, but the basic idea is always the same: ask a question, and use the test to find the answer.\n\n01:13.100 --> 01:16.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
