    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_120846.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:22.000\nIt could be a quiz at school, or a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:30.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking. You do a test!\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:36.600\nYou poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test result: the cake is done!\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:43.100\nAnother example is checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:49.900\nIf it lights up, the test passes. If not, the light bulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:59.100\nSo, to recap: a test helps us determine something about an object or a situation. It gives us information we didn't have before.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:00.300\nIt's a simple way to check and confirm.\n```"
