    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.500\nNow, you might think of school tests, but a test, in a broader sense, is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:23.600\nIt's a simple process of trying something and seeing what happens.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:33.500\nYour test? You screw it into a lamp and turn it on. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:38.900\nIf not, well, it failed.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:44.200\nAnother example could be checking if a cake is done.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:48.400\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:52.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:56.800\nThat's your test!\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:01.900\nSo, remember, a test is simply a procedure used to determine if something is working correctly or if a condition is met. It's all about observing the outcome. Thanks for watching! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
