    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:19.600\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on. That's a test!\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:27.600\nIt could be a quiz at school to see what you've learned in class. Or maybe trying out a new recipe to see if it tastes good. That\u2019s a test too!\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:33.900\nWe use tests all the time to get information and make decisions.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:45.200\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to figure out what\u2019s making you feel sick. Or a baker might test their oven temperature to make sure their cookies bake perfectly.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:54.900\nSo, tests help us understand things better and make sure things are working the way they should. They\u2019re all about finding out information.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:03.800\nBasically, a test is any kind of procedure designed to evaluate something. We perform them to learn and improve.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:07.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
