    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_122207.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:18.700\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:25.800\nWe use them all the time to check if things are working, or to see how much we know.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:37.800\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, in school, you take tests to show your teacher what you've learned.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:51.000\nSo, how does it work?\nWell, a test usually has a set of questions or tasks.\nYou answer the questions or complete the tasks, and then someone checks your answers or results.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:59.400\nFor example, a simple test could be asking \"What's two plus two?\".\nThe correct answer is four, so if you say four, you pass that part of the test!\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.400\nTests help us understand things better and make sure we're on the right track.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:05.900\nThey're a valuable tool for learning and improving.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:06.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
