    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:38:51.780605",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T12:30:42.762591",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_123042.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_123042.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.254 --> 00:04.884\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.884 --> 00:05.234\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.884 --> 00:08.824\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.284 --> 00:14.144\nIt's a set of questions or tasks designed to measure your knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:14.764 --> 00:18.554\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:18.994 --> 00:22.394\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:22.764 --> 00:24.774\nSo, tests can be used in lots of different situations.\n\n00:25.264 --> 00:29.044\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned in class.\n\n00:29.464 --> 00:34.654\nThese tests can be multiple choice, written answers, or even practical demonstrations.\n\n00:35.054 --> 00:38.694\nThey help your teachers understand how well you're understanding the material.\n\n00:39.024 --> 00:42.354\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:42.794 --> 00:45.414\nA math test sees if you can solve equations.\n\n00:45.864 --> 00:48.544\nBasically, a test helps to evaluate something and give you some results.\n\n00:49.054 --> 00:52.924\nTo recap, a test is a process used to evaluate something.\n\n00:53.384 --> 00:56.864\nIt\u2019s used to gather information and measure understanding or abilities.\n\n00:57.424 --> 00:58.594\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b60b6457-7289-44aa-9177-15f9f9475ad0": {
    "id": "b60b6457-7289-44aa-9177-15f9f9475ad0",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:38:52.214985",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T12:31:52.624554",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_123152.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_123152.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\nIt's like an experiment, but often much simpler.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works.\nYou put it in a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:24.400\nThat\u2019s a test!\nThe goal is to see if it lights up.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.200\nAnother example?\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:32.500\nYou taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:41.300\nYou're checking the flavor.\nSo, a test helps us answer a question, or see if something is working as expected.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:49.100\nWhether it\u2019s checking a lightbulb or tasting a cake, tests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:57.500\nIn short, a test is a method used to determine if something is true, accurate, or functioning correctly.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
