    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_130510.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.100\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like this: you have a toy car, and you want to make sure it runs. You put batteries in, turn it on, and watch it go.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:29.700\nThat's a test! You're testing if the car works.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:33.400\nAnother example? Let's say you bake a cake.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:37.100\nAfter it comes out of the oven, you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:45.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. That's a test!\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:54.500\nSo, a test is simply a way to see if something meets a certain requirement or works as expected.\n\n00:54.500 --> 00:57.600\nIt's a way to check and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:01.200\nThat's the basics of testing! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
