    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_130605.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:06.700\nNow, a test is basically a way to see what you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:09.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:10.700\nYou're testing to see if it lights up!\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:13.600\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:16.600\nIt could be a quiz at school, where you answer questions about what you've learned.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:19.700\nOr it could be a taste test, where you try different foods and decide which one you like best.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:22.500\nEven a doctor checking your reflexes is a type of test!\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:26.800\nSo, let's say you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:29.300\nYou might have a \"test\" where you try to ride without training wheels.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:31.900\nThat shows how well you've learned to balance.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:34.800\nSee?\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:37.900\nTests help us understand where we are and what we need to work on.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:39.700\nThey\u2019re all about checking and understanding.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:45.400\nTo sum it up, a test is just a way to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, your skills, or even the quality of a product.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:47.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
