    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_130941.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it as a question, or a series of questions, designed to give you an answer.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:17.000\nThe answer could be about anything!\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.000\nIt could be about your knowledge, like a quiz at school.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:27.000\nOr it could be about the quality of something, like testing a new toy to see if it's strong enough.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:31.000\nMaybe you\u2019re testing a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:33.000\nYou're trying it out, right?\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:38.000\nSo, examples! A spelling test checks your spelling skills.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:41.000\nA taste test checks how a food tastes.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:44.000\nAnd a strength test checks how strong something is.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:46.000\nSee? Each test gives you specific information.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:54.000\nBasically, a test is a systematic way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:57.000\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:02.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
