    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_131027.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.300\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:26.400\nThink of it like this: you use a ruler to measure how long something is, right?\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:35.000\nA test is similar, but instead of length, it measures knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:45.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks your spelling skills. A math quiz tests your understanding of math problems.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:54.200\nAnd a driver's test evaluates your ability to drive safely.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:57.800\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to give us information about what someone knows or can do. They help us understand where we are and what we might need to learn next. Tests are a tool for learning and improvement. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
