    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_131112.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you know something.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like this: you might test a new toy to make sure it doesn't break easily. Or, your teacher might give you a quiz to test how much you learned in class.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:36.700\nTests can be anything from a simple yes or no question to a more involved experiment. For example, you could test if a plant grows faster in sunlight or shade.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:44.900\nYou'd plant two identical plants, put one in the sun and the other in the shade, and then watch what happens.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:53.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something. It helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
