    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_131252.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:28.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer. The question we ask might be \"Is this light bulb working?\" or \"Can I name all the planets?\".\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:37.600\nThe test is the process of figuring out the answer. So, we might screw in the light bulb and flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:46.300\nOr we might try to recite the names of all the planets. For example, a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:51.700\nA chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:51.700 --> 01:04.700\nSee? Tests are all around us, helping us learn and understand things. So, remember, a test is simply a way to get information and check something out.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.200\nIt helps us know if something is working, correct, or meeting a certain standard. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
