    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_131740.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.700\nA test is basically a way to check how much you know about something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like a little quiz to see if you've learned the material. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:36.700\nYou might have a multiple-choice test where you pick the best answer, or a true or false test where you decide if a statement is correct.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:45.800\nSometimes you even get to write out your answers in short or long form.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:53.200\nFor example, imagine you're learning about animals. A test might ask, \"Which animal barks? A) Cat, B) Dog, C) Bird.\"\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:00.800\nThe answer, of course, is dog! Tests help teachers, and you, understand what you've mastered and what you might need to study a little more.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:04.400\nSo, in short, a test is just a tool to measure your knowledge and help you learn.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:07.800\nGood luck with your next one! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
