    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_133218.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:13.900\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us learn more.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:19.700\nThink of it like this: a baking test. You taste a cake to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:26.400\nOr a color test: you hold up fabric to see if the colors match. Even a simple quiz in school is a test!\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:31.100\nIt helps your teacher see what you've learned. So, tests are all around us!\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:38.200\nThey help us check things, learn new things, and improve things. They give us information to make better decisions.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:44.500\nBasically, a test is a method for gathering information! It helps us understand something better.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:47.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a1cebaf7-53ba-4756-8c1c-aa37691c2183": {
    "id": "a1cebaf7-53ba-4756-8c1c-aa37691c2183",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:39:16.963622",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T13:33:45.615007",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_133345.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_133345.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This is a placeholder for the actual subtitles.  The timing below is estimated and NEEDS TO BE REPLACED with the actual timings from the audio file.  The text is copied from the provided narration.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into a super important concept: tests.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:13.200\nThink of a test as a way to check something. It's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:21.600\nFor example, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy. A scientist might test a new medicine to see if it cures a disease.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:28.200\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test; you're checking if the ingredients and instructions will create something yummy!\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:35.300\nAnother simple test is checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:44.600\nIf it doesn't, well, you know you need a new bulb. So, tests are all about checking something to see if it meets a certain requirement or standard.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:52.200\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
