    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:12.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:20.800\nIt\u2019s like a measuring stick for your knowledge. Think of it like this: if you want to know how tall you are, you use a measuring tape.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:30.500\nIf you want to know how much you've learned in school, you take a test. Tests come in many forms. There are multiple-choice questions, true or false questions, and even essay questions where you write out your answers.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:39.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words. A math test shows how well you understand numbers and equations.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:48.600\nSo, tests help you and your teachers see what you've learned and what you might need to work on. They're a tool for learning and improvement.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
