    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_135430.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:12.500\nYou've probably taken them in school, but what is a test really?\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:19.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:24.600\nWe can test all sorts of things, like if a lightbulb works,\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:29.200\nor how well you understand a new concept.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:29.900\nThink about it.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:36.700\nA doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:41.200\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:45.900\nThese are all different kinds of tests, designed to give us information.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:50.000\nSo, a test helps us find out if something is working, true, or correct.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:53.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:55.000\nAnd that answer helps us make decisions.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:56.500\nRemember, tests are all about gathering information.\n```"
  },
