  "6fe3a620-e1f6-46c7-9936-8dcafdb024a1": {
    "id": "6fe3a620-e1f6-46c7-9936-8dcafdb024a1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:39:27.778031",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T14:00:46.325695",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_140046.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_140046.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey there, welcome! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:15.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:26.000\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:35.800\nIn science and school, tests are a bit more formal. They help us measure knowledge, skills, or even the quality of something.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:40.400\nFor example, a spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:50.200\nOr, a scientist might test water to see if it's safe to drink.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:57.300\nAnother example? Imagine you're building a tower of blocks. You might test its stability by gently pushing it to see if it falls.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:00.900\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and learning more.\n```"
  },
  "939af0be-a1b7-4e2b-a750-332f74e3fa8a": {
