    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:15.900\nNow, in its simplest form, a test is just a way to see what you know, or what something can do.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:28.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in, flip the switch, and poof, you know if it passes the test and lights up!\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:37.600\nTests can be anything from a spelling quiz at school to a doctor checking your reflexes.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:47.200\nThey all have the same basic goal: to get information. So, a spelling quiz tests your knowledge of words.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:52.300\nAnd the doctor's reflex test checks how quickly your body reacts.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:04.700\nBasically, a test gives you a result based on what you put in. Good results mean you passed! It's a simple way to measure something.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.000\nSo, remember, a test is a way to gather information,\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:12.700\nlike checking a lightbulb or taking a quiz.\n\n01:12.700 --> 01:16.700\nIt helps us understand how things work or what we know.\n\n01:16.700 --> 01:20.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
