    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_141446.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.367 --> 00:05.367\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.367 --> 00:16.067\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we're talking about how we check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.067 --> 00:24.967\nBasically, a test is a way to see if an idea, a product, or even a process does what we expect it to do.\n\n00:24.967 --> 00:39.367\nThink of it like this: If you build a toy car, you test it by pushing it to see if it rolls.\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you test it by sticking a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:39.367 --> 00:46.367\nAnother example is testing a light bulb.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch to see if it lights up.\n\n00:46.367 --> 00:52.967\nThat's a test!\nSo, a test is simply a way to check if something works as intended.\n\n00:52.967 --> 00:56.967\nIt helps us find problems and make things better.\n\n00:56.967 --> 00:59.967\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
