    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:16.900\nThink of it like a little check-up.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:25.600\nThe main idea behind a test is to get information.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:34.400\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. For example, when you try out a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like it.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:39.800\nOr, when you check the batteries in your remote, you're testing to see if they still have power.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:48.200\nThink about taking a spelling test at school. That tells your teacher, and you, how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:51.200\nOr a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.800\nSo, tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:08.200\nIn short, a test is just a way to gather information to see if something is right, works well, or is understood.\n\n01:08.200 --> 01:10.600\nPretty straightforward, right?\n\n01:10.600 --> 01:15.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
