    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_143715.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:10.400\n\u2013 not the kind you might take in school,\nbut a way of checking\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:12.200\nif something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:17.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know\nif your bike's brakes are working.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:19.800\nSo, you test them!\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:22.600\nYou squeeze the levers and see if the bike\nslows down.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:23.800\nThat\u2019s a test!\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:29.500\nIn general, a test is a procedure designed\nto see if something meets a specific requirement\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:31.600\nor works as expected.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:35.500\nIt could be as simple as checking if a light\nbulb turns on,\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:39.400\nor a bit more complex, like testing if a new\nrecipe tastes good.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:42.700\nThe goal is always the same: to find out\nif something passes or fails.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:47.300\nFor example, you might test a toy to make\nsure it's safe for kids.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:51.200\nOr a doctor might test your blood to check\nyour health.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:52.700\nBasically, anything can be tested!\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:59.800\nSo, to recap: a test is a simple way to check\nif something works correctly. It helps us make\nsure things are safe,\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.800\nreliable, and do what they're supposed to\ndo.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:06.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
