    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:39:48.414609",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T14:41:56.234279",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_144156.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_144156.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:06.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:11.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:18.500\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:23.500\nImagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might taste the batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:29.500\nOr, think about going to the doctor.\nThey might run some tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:36.000\nTests can be written, like a quiz in school, or they can be practical, like trying to fix a broken toy.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:43.500\nThe important thing is that a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:46.000\nThey give us information.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:52.000\nSo, a test is just a process to get information and understand something better.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ef36988c-7ffc-4de2-bbb3-544e00a8c3bd": {
    "id": "ef36988c-7ffc-4de2-bbb3-544e00a8c3bd",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:39:48.824438",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T14:43:30.420122",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_144330.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_144330.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:19.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific. Think of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:28.300\nIt could be anything from a quiz in school, to checking if a lightbulb works, or even figuring out if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:37.000\nThe main idea is that you do something, like ask a question or perform an action, and then you observe the result.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.900\nThat result gives you information.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:48.200\nFor example, if you're testing a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:53.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:58.000\nThat's a successful test.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:02.000\nOr, imagine you're testing if your phone is charged.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:05.600\nYou turn it on.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:10.300\nIf it turns on, great!\n\n01:10.300 --> 01:12.800\nThe test shows it has power.\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:17.800\nSo, a test is just a simple way to get answers and learn something new.\n\n01:17.800 --> 01:22.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5758f6a5-c2cb-4fdb-9503-3810ba5014b1": {
    "id": "5758f6a5-c2cb-4fdb-9503-3810ba5014b1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:39:49.396875",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T14:44:21.152711",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_144421.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_144421.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.200\nA test is simply a way to find out something about a person, a thing, or even an idea. Think of it like a question you're asking, and the test helps you find the answer.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:23.400\nTests can come in many forms. A school exam is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:31.900\nA taste test is a test of your opinion. Even checking if a lightbulb works is a test to see if it's broken or not.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:42.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health. Or a company might test a new product to see if people like it before they sell it.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:52.800\nSo, in short, a test is a method for gathering information. It helps us understand something better by providing evidence or data.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:56.800\nUnderstanding tests is a key part of learning and making informed decisions.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:01.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "406e0082-6ad1-4198-8ed3-5d84601c863b": {
    "id": "406e0082-6ad1-4198-8ed3-5d84601c863b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:39:49.815399",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T14:45:21.382006",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_144521.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_144521.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:37.000\nThat's a test! You're testing if the lightbulb lights up. Tests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your shoes are tied.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:46.600\nThe main goal is to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:49.200\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:52.800\nOr a doctor might check your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:55.400\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:07.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working, meeting a requirement, or just generally doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:10.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "cbaea742-3b4d-4b89-b9af-4ea132a091dd": {
    "id": "cbaea742-3b4d-4b89-b9af-4ea132a091dd",
