    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_145818.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:22.600\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:32.700\nYou stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:38.100\nThe toothpick tells you if the cake is ready.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:43.500\nOr, imagine you're checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:48.900\nYou flip the switch. The light turning on is the test showing the bulb is good.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:53.600\nTests help us make decisions. They give us information to work with.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:01.000\nWhether it's checking the temperature outside to decide what to wear, or taking a quiz to see what you've learned, tests are all about gathering information. So remember, a test is just a simple way to get an answer. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
