    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_150948.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. It can be used to check if something is working correctly, like testing if a lightbulb turns on.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:34.900\nOr, it can be used to measure something, like taking a temperature to see if you have a fever. For example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:47.300\nOr a builder might test a wall to make sure it's strong enough to hold up a roof. So, remember, a test is just a process used to find information or check something.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:51.300\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:53.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
