    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_151035.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.600\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:26.200\nThat's a test! You're testing if the lightbulb does what it's supposed to do: light up.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:32.000\nWe use tests all the time. A doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:41.700\nA baker might taste their cake batter to make sure it's sweet enough. These are all ways to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:53.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a method to check if something works or meets a requirement. It helps us make sure things are doing what they're supposed to be doing.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
