    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:40:15.730276",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T15:32:10.697050",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_153210.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_153210.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:16.600\nNow, don't worry, we're not talking about pop quizzes! A test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking. How do you find out?\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:26.400\nYou test it! You might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:32.000\nThe toothpick is your test. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:40.900\nSimilarly, a doctor might test your blood to see if you're healthy. Or a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:49.900\nTests help us make decisions and learn new things. They're everywhere, from baking a cake to discovering new cures.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:57.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information. It helps us understand something better.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6834b07f-2ad0-4a98-a73d-ce98e9e338cd": {
    "id": "6834b07f-2ad0-4a98-a73d-ce98e9e338cd",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
