    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:40:16.183638",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T15:32:56.220920",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_153256.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_153256.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:17.400\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:26.500\nIt could be finding out if you know something, like in a school test,\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:35.300\nor finding out if something works, like testing a new toy.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:41.300\nBasically, you do something and then you see what happens.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:53.300\nThat \"what happens\" gives you the information you're looking for. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. Or, imagine you're baking a cake. You're testing the recipe! If the cake tastes good, the recipe passed the test. If it's awful, well, the recipe failed!\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:59.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information by doing something and observing the result. It helps us learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
