    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_153706.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something fundamental: tests!\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:16.200\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:19.500\nIt's like a little experiment to see if you get the expected result.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:27.400\nImagine you're baking a cake. The test? Taking it out of the oven and poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:30.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:35.200\nOr, think about checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:39.700\nIf it lights up, the test passes! Tests help us find problems\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:44.200\nand make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:54.000\nThey're super important in lots of different areas, from baking to building bridges.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:58.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is doing what it should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3d95c3d0-a851-4e47-a538-5c53b5104f27": {
    "id": "3d95c3d0-a851-4e47-a538-5c53b5104f27",
