    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_153839.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:14.500\nThink of a test as a way to check what you know about a topic. It's like a little quiz to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:23.500\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. You might have multiple-choice questions, where you pick the best answer from a list.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:33.100\nOr maybe true or false questions, where you decide if a statement is correct. Sometimes you even have to write out your own answers!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:44.100\nFor example, if we're testing you on colors, a question might be: \"What color is the sky?\" The answer would be blue, of course!\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:50.400\nOr a true or false question: \"Grass is red. True or false?\" That's false!\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:02.400\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to see what you've learned. It helps you and your teachers understand what you know well, and what you might need to work on.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:08.100\nGood luck with your next test! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
