    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_154005.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.500\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something. It could be checking if you understand a lesson, like in school, or checking if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:28.600\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and then you taste it. That taste is a test to see if your cake is delicious!\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:37.700\nOr, imagine you build a birdhouse. You might watch to see if birds actually move in \u2013 that's a test of its usefulness!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:46.000\nTests help us learn and improve things. If your cake doesn't taste good, you can adjust the recipe next time.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:59.700\nIf birds don't use your birdhouse, you can try a different design. So, a test is really just a way of gathering information to see if something is working or needs to be changed.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:05.200\nPretty simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
