    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:40:22.942159",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T15:43:56.697119",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_154356.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_154356.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:15.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to see what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like a check-up for your brain. The main idea behind a test is to measure your understanding of a specific topic.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:34.000\nIt could be anything from remembering facts to solving problems. It's all about showing what you've learned.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:43.100\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. A math test sees if you can solve equations.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:54.800\nAnd even trying a new recipe is like a test to see if you can follow instructions! So, to recap, a test is a tool to measure knowledge or skills, helps identify strengths and weaknesses, and comes in many different forms.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:00.200\nPretty simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
