    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_155549.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.400\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something, right?\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:28.500\nMore generally, a test helps us understand if something is working as it should, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:38.900\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see if you understand the material.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:42.700\nSee? Different situations, same idea.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:53.200\nSo, to recap: a test is a procedure used to evaluate something, ensuring it meets expectations or functions correctly.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:59.100\nIt helps us gather information and make informed decisions.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
