    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_155634.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time!\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:32.400\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:38.200\nThe answer, whether the toothpick comes out clean or covered in batter, tells you if the cake needs more time in the oven.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:44.100\nOr, imagine you're buying a new toy. You might try it out to see if it works.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:51.000\nThat\u2019s testing it! So, tests help us understand something better by giving us information.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:57.400\nThey can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all share the same goal: to get an answer.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:01.000\nIn essence, tests are simply a way of learning! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
