    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_155935.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:15.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:25.900\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:37.400\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:49.500\nOr, a teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:49.500 --> 01:01.100\nThese tests usually involve questions or activities that help reveal specific information.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:12.700\nFor example, a simple taste test can tell you if you like a new flavor of ice cream.\n\n01:12.700 --> 01:19.600\nOr, a spelling test helps your teacher see if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n01:19.600 --> 01:26.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a method for gathering information, whether it's about your health, your knowledge, or even your taste preferences!\n\n01:26.500 --> 01:29.300\nTests help us understand things better.\n\n01:29.300 --> 01:34.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
