    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_160109.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.300\nNow, you might think of school exams, but a \"test\" in a broader sense is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:23.600\nIt's how we check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:33.900\nThe test? You screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:40.300\nOr maybe you want to see if a cookie is done baking. You poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:49.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test, and it tells you the cookie is ready.\n\n00:49.000 --> 01:01.000\nTests can be simple like that, or more complicated, but they all have the same basic idea: to get information and make a decision based on what we find out.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:05.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:08.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
