    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_160950.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.800\nNow, when you hear \"test,\" you might think of school, but tests are really just a way to see if something works or to check what you know about something.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake. You test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:27.900\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:32.500\nOr, imagine you build a tower of blocks. You test it by seeing if it can stand up on its own.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:39.400\nSo, a test is simply a way to find out if something is ready, correct, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:53.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand something better. Essentially, you are checking if the outcome matches your expectation.\n\n00:53.500 --> 01:01.500\nTo recap, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:05.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
