    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.100\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out. It's a process we use to gather information and see how something performs or whether it's working correctly.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:28.900\nThink of it like this: You take a spelling test to see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:36.000\nOr a doctor might run a blood test to check your health. In both cases, you're using a test to get answers.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:50.400\nAnother example is testing a new toy. You might play with it to see if it's fun and if it works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:02.000\nTests can be formal, like exams in school, or informal, like trying out a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:05.500\nSo, to sum it up, a test is simply a method for getting information or evaluating something.\n```"
