    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_162041.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.100\nWhat are they? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:17.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:24.000\nWe use tests all the time. A doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:29.900\nA teacher gives you a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:36.600\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test! You're testing if the recipe works.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:43.300\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:45.800\nYou flip the switch.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:48.300\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:50.800\nIf it doesn't, the test failed.\n\n00:50.800 --> 00:52.800\nSee? Pretty straightforward.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:03.200\nSo, remember, a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect. It's all about gathering information.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
