    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.900\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:21.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something or someone.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:30.900\nThink of it like this: you use a taste test to see if food is good, or a spelling test to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:39.600\nEssentially, a test helps us understand if something works, if someone knows something, or even if something is safe.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:45.400\nLet's say you're baking a cake.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:49.200\nYou might do a \"toothpick test\" \u2013 sticking a toothpick in the middle to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:50.900\nThat tells you if the cake is done!\n\n00:50.900 --> 00:55.800\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:00.100\nEach time you try, that's a test to see if you're getting better at balancing.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:07.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out more information.\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:09.700\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n01:09.700 --> 01:12.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
