    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_164142.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:19.400\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer. Tests can come in all shapes and sizes!\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:26.700\nYour doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. A chef might taste a sauce to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:33.100\nAnd you might take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:43.800\nSee how it works? Each test helps us gather information. The doctor learns about your health, the chef improves the flavor, and your teacher sees what you've learned.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:53.200\nSo, a test is really just a tool for learning and understanding. It helps us make better decisions based on information we gather.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:01.600\nIn short, a test is a method for getting specific information.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.000\nRemember to think about what you are testing and why!\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:08.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
