    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_164558.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.200\nNow, you might be thinking about school, but a test, in general, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:24.400\nBasically, a test checks if something is working correctly or if something is true.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:31.500\nFor example, think about checking if a lightbulb works.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:38.500\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\nOr, imagine you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:45.800\nYou stick a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the \"done\" test.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:56.000\nSo, a test is simply a way to check something.\nIt helps us understand if things are working as expected or if something is true or false.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
