    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_165726.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. It could be checking if a lightbulb works, if a cake is done baking, or even if you understand a new topic.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:29.900\nThe main idea is to find out if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:38.300\nThink of it like this: you might test the water in a pool to see if it's warm enough to swim.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:47.400\nOr, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Tests give us information that helps us make decisions.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:50.400\nFor example, a chef tests a sauce to make sure it tastes good.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:53.400\nA teacher gives you a quiz to see if you learned the material.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:56.400\nSee? Tests are all around us.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:08.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something to see if it's working correctly or if it's true. It gives us information to help us understand things better.\n\n01:08.200 --> 01:11.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
