    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_170614.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's a process or procedure designed to measure knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:25.800\nThink about it like this: when you take a spelling test in school, it helps your teacher see how well you understand spelling rules.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:34.000\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might taste the batter to test if it needs more sugar.\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:42.400\nAnother example is checking if a light bulb works before you put it in a lamp.\nYou're testing the bulb to see if it lights up.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:55.800\nSo, tests can be formal, like exams, or informal, like checking the cake batter.\nUltimately, they help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:05.000\nIn short, a test is a way to get information.\nIt can be used in lots of different situations to evaluate something.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:08.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
