    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_170826.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like this: a recipe is a test for delicious cookies! You follow the instructions, and the result tells you if the recipe works.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:36.700\nOr, imagine checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in, flip the switch, and the light either turns on, or it doesn't! That's a test.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:47.500\nTests can be simple, like tasting soup to see if it needs more salt, or more complex, like a medical exam to check your health.\n\n00:47.500 --> 01:00.000\nThe key is that they all involve doing something and observing the outcome to learn something new. So, in a nutshell, a test is just a procedure to gather information.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:03.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
