    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_171205.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might think of tests as scary exams, but in a broader sense, a test is just a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:26.200\nIt's a method for checking if something is true, or working correctly.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:30.400\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:39.700\nYou might stick a toothpick in the middle. That's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:46.900\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works. You screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:54.300\nIf the light turns on, the bulb passes the test. So, tests are everywhere, helping us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:06.700\nThey're simply a way to get reliable information about something. To recap, a test is just a procedure to determine something or verify if something works.\n\n01:06.700 --> 01:07.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
