    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_171332.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:10.000\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think about school, but tests are really just ways to check if something works like it should.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:18.000\nThink about it like this: Imagine you're baking a cake. You test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:25.000\nOr, if you're building a tower of blocks, you might gently push it to test its stability. Does it stand strong, or does it fall over?\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:32.000\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on. Or they can be more complicated, like figuring out if a new medicine works.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:41.000\nBasically, a test is just a way to find out if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:45.000\nSo, remember, tests help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:46.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
