    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_172514.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:05.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:10.900\nNow, a test is basically just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you know something.\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:17.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:18.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:24.100\nOr, let's say your mom asks you what two plus two is.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:27.000\nWhen you answer \"four,\" you're passing a test.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.900\nAnother example? A doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature or listening to your heartbeat.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:43.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to find out if something is true or working.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:48.200\nIt can be as simple as trying something out, or as complicated as a big exam.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:53.700\nTests help us learn and make sure things are going the way they should.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
