  "262feaf7-73e1-45a0-ba8d-7b5b5f55853d": {
    "id": "262feaf7-73e1-45a0-ba8d-7b5b5f55853d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:41:27.450203",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T17:30:33.390180",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_173033.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_173033.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:05.200\nToday, we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:07.800\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:10.400\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:13.700\nThink of it like this: you might test if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:16.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you they're ready!\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:21.000\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.000\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test is positive \u2013 the bulb works!\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:28.500\nIf not, well, you know it's time for a new one.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:32.000\nSo, a test is simply a procedure to check something and get a result.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.300\nIt helps us learn, understand, and make decisions.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:37.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
