    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_174234.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests!\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.300\nNow, a test is really just a way to see how much you know about something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like checking if a recipe worked \u2013 you taste the food! In the same way, a test helps us understand what we've learned.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:35.600\nIt can be a simple question, a problem to solve, or even a practical demonstration.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:40.300\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:45.000\nA math test checks if you can solve equations. And a driving test makes sure you can safely operate a car.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:49.700\nSee? Tests are all around us!\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:57.900\nSo, to recap, a test is a tool to measure knowledge or skill. It helps you and others see what you\u2019ve learned and where you can improve.\n\n00:57.900 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2fcb7549-b8b5-4710-af70-cb440768f504": {
    "id": "2fcb7549-b8b5-4710-af70-cb440768f504",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:41:34.957948",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T17:43:19.356041",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_174319.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_174319.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:12.300\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, maybe in school. But what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:22.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a set of questions or activities designed to measure your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:30.400\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:39.800\nOr, if you want to see if your friend knows their ABCs, you might ask them to recite them. That's another kind of test.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:52.700\nTests can be formal, like exams in class, or informal, like asking a friend a question. The main idea is that you're trying to gather information to learn something.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:61.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find things out. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
