    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_175131.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:18.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us gather information and see how well something works, or how much someone knows.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:27.700\nThink about it like this: a spelling test helps your teacher see which words you already know and which ones you need to practice.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:36.000\nOr imagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might taste a little bit of the batter \u2013 that's a mini-test to see if it needs more sugar!\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:47.300\nTests aren't just for school or cooking, though. Scientists use them to check if a new medicine works, and engineers use them to make sure bridges are safe.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:58.000\nSo, tests are all about finding things out and making things better. In short, a test is a structured way to get information about something.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:05.000\nWe use them to learn, improve, and make informed decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
