    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_175651.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and while that's true, a test in general is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\nHow do you find out?\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.800\nYou test it!\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:30.800\nIf it lights up, it passes the test.\nAnother example is baking.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:41.100\nYou test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test and is ready to eat!\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:48.900\nSo, a test is simply a procedure to see if something meets a certain requirement or works as expected.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:55.400\nIt's all about checking and verifying.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
