    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:13.800\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, a product's quality, or even the strength of a bridge.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:15.000\nThink about it.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:19.500\nWhen you take a quiz in school, that\u2019s a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:26.200\nOr, imagine a company making a new phone. They run tests to make sure the battery lasts long enough and the screen doesn't break easily.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:31.000\nAnother example? A doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:36.400\nSo, tests come in many forms, but they all share the same goal: to gather information and make an assessment.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:43.700\nBasically, a test helps us learn something specific by observing and measuring.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:47.400\nThey're everywhere, helping us understand the world around us.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:49.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
