    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_180147.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:20.700\nIn simplest terms, a test is just a way to see how much you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That toothpick is a kind of test!\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:42.100\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:54.400\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling words, and a math test shows how well you understand math problems.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:04.800\nTests help you too, because they show you what you're good at and what you might need to work on.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:11.800\nSo, to recap: a test is a tool for measuring knowledge or skill.\n\n01:11.800 --> 01:18.600\nIt's used in lots of different situations, from baking cakes to learning new subjects.\n\n01:18.600 --> 01:24.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
