    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:41:47.691893",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T18:05:08.567617",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_180508.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_180508.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.200\nNow, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you\u2019re healthy.\nOr, a teacher gives you a test to see how much you\u2019ve learned.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:37.000\nEven baking a cake involves a test \u2013 you check if it\u2019s done by poking it with a fork!\nAnother good example is when you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.900\nYou \"test\" it by plugging it in.\nIf it lights up, you know it's good.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:55.800\nIf not, it\u2019s probably broken.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:03.100\nIt's a simple but powerful tool we use every day.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a88460f2-49cd-47bd-b81f-6816b97b89d2": {
