  "627c0d3e-b0bc-4e9f-a4e4-b23af1927e36": {
    "id": "627c0d3e-b0bc-4e9f-a4e4-b23af1927e36",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:41:49.772283",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T18:08:13.105018",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_180812.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_180812.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:16.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:23.100\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer in a controlled way.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a plant needs water. The test is feeling the soil.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:34.300\nIf the soil is dry, the test tells you it needs water!\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:41.300\nOr maybe you want to see if your cookies are done. The test? Sticking a toothpick in them.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:48.300\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready! So, a test helps us learn or confirm something.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:54.700\nWe set up a situation, observe the results, and draw a conclusion.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:56.100\nTests are everywhere, helping us understand the world around us.\n```"
  },
