    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_181005.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:09.800\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:16.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:20.900\nIt could be your knowledge, your skills, or even the quality of a product.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like this: a spelling test measures how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:30.800\nOr a taste test can tell you which cookie is the tastiest.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:35.800\nTests help us understand where we stand and identify areas where we can improve.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:39.300\nThey give us results we can use to make decisions.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:46.500\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to diagnose an illness and figure out the best treatment.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:52.800\nUltimately, tests provide information to help us learn and grow.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:59.000\nSo, tests are a fundamental part of learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:01.400\nThey help us measure, learn, and improve.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:03.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
