    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something called a test.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:14.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. Think of it like asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:24.600\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold. Or, you might take a math test at school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:32.100\nThe test gives us information, or data, that we can use.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:37.500\nAnother example is baking a cake. You taste the batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:42.900\nThe taste is your test! Basically, anything that helps you learn or confirm something can be considered a test.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:54.400\nSo, to recap, a test is a process for gathering information. It can be used in many different ways, from checking your health to understanding how well you've learned something.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:00.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
