    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like asking a question and then getting an answer.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:26.900\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\nFor example, if you touch a hot stove, you're performing a test.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:30.600\nYou're testing whether it's safe to touch.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:34.800\nThe answer? Definitely not!\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:41.600\nOr, imagine baking a cake.\nYou might stick a toothpick in it to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:48.200\nThat's a test to see if the cake is done.\nA clean toothpick means it's ready.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:54.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information and learn something new.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:57.200\nIt's a question and an answer.\n\n00:57.200 --> 00:59.000\nHopefully, that makes things a little clearer.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
