    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_183215.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:08.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests, but don't worry, it's not the kind you stress about!\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:13.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:19.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:24.000\nYou use a toothpick \u2013 that's your test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:29.000\nYou poke the cookie, and if the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies pass the test and are ready to eat.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:35.000\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:39.000\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:44.000\nIf it lights up, it passes the test, and if not, it's probably broken.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:52.000\nSo, testing is really just a simple way to see if something is working correctly or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:57.000\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:01.000\nRemember, a test is just a check.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:04.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
