    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_183303.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.100\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car. A test is simply trying it out to see if it rolls!\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:29.000\nYou push it, and if it moves, the test passes. If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:36.200\nTesting isn't just for toys, though. Imagine a chef tasting their soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:41.800\nThat's a test too! Or a doctor checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:50.500\nAgain, that's a test. So, to recap, a test is a simple way to check if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:55.500\nIt tells you if it's working or not. And that\u2019s the basics of testing!\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
