    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_184159.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:05.500\nToday we're going to explore something really fundamental:\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:07.300\nthe concept of a test.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:10.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:12.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:16.300\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:19.800\nFor example, when you flip a light switch, you're testing if the light bulb works.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:23.100\nOr when you taste a new food, you're testing if you like the flavor.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:25.800\nIn science and math, tests help us confirm or deny ideas.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:30.100\nA scientist might test a new medicine to see if it cures a disease.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:33.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn more.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:37.700\nIt's all about exploring and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:39.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
