    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_184251.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: Tests.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:14.600\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way. We use tests all the time, even if you don't realize it!\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:35.100\nIf you try a new recipe and see if it tastes good, that's a test. Or, if you click a button on your phone to see if it works, that's also a test.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:49.300\nAt school, tests help your teachers see what you've learned. For example, a simple math test might ask, \"What is 2 + 2?\" Your answer helps show what you know about addition.\n\n00:49.300 --> 01:02.500\nAnother test could be a spelling quiz, seeing if you can correctly spell \"because\".\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:12.400\nSo, to recap: a test is a method for gathering information or checking something. They come in all shapes and sizes, and they're used to learn and improve things every day.\n\n01:12.400 --> 01:17.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
