    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_185934.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:18.900\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time!\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:25.700\nThink about a spelling test at school. It helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:33.800\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste the batter \u2013 that's a test to see if it needs more sugar!\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:41.900\nAnother example is checking if your bike tires have enough air. You can press on them to test if they feel firm.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:52.200\nIf they're squishy, they need more air. So, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:01.700\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to get information. And that's the basics of testing!\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:05.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
