    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_190041.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something fundamental: the Test.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:14.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:27.000\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate a characteristic, skill, or ability.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:33.200\nThink about it like this: a doctor gives you a blood test to see if you're healthy. That's a test!\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:39.800\nOr, a baker might taste a cake batter to check if it has enough sugar. That's also a test!\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:51.000\nEven pressing a button to see if a light turns on is a form of testing. So, tests are everywhere, helping us learn and improve.\n\n00:51.000 --> 01:00.700\nThey help us see if something is working correctly, or if something needs adjustment.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:10.800\nWhether it's in science, cooking, or even everyday life, tests are an important part of understanding the world around us.\n\n01:10.800 --> 01:14.400\nTo recap, a test is simply a process used to evaluate something.\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:17.900\nIt could be anything from a medical checkup to a simple experiment.\n\n01:17.900 --> 01:21.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
