    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_190138.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:06.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 and no, not the kind you cram for!\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:12.000\nIn this case, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see if something is true.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:17.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.000\nThe test is simply screwing it into a lamp and flipping the switch.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:23.000\nDoes it light up?\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:25.000\nThat's the result of your test!\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:30.000\nAnother example: maybe you want to know if your plant needs water.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:34.000\nYou can test it by sticking your finger in the soil.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:37.000\nIf it feels dry, the test tells you it needs water.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:40.000\nTests are all about finding things out.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:47.000\nThey can be simple, like checking a lightbulb, or more complex, but the basic idea is always the same: perform an action and see what happens to learn something.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:51.000\nSo remember, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
