    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:09.800\nToday we're going to explore something really fundamental: the test.\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:17.200\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:27.400\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\nThink of it like this: a teacher gives you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:34.600\nThat's a test!\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake, and you taste it to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:38.500\nThat's also a test!\nYou're testing the sweetness.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:45.100\nTests aren't just in school or in the kitchen.\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:55.500\nScientists use tests to prove new ideas.\nBasically, any time you're trying to learn something or check something, you're using a test.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:04.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information.\nIt helps us learn, improve, and understand the world around us.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:08.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
