    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, ability, or even the quality of something.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:26.900\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\nA taste test checks if you like a new flavor of ice cream.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:42.500\nAnd a medical test can help doctors figure out what's going on inside your body.\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same basic purpose: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:50.600\nWhether it\u2019s a pop quiz or a blood draw, a test helps us understand more about ourselves and the world around us.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:59.200\nIn short, a test is just a structured way of asking a question and getting an answer.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "992b7eb5-7383-4e63-80df-113f8a48bad2": {
    "id": "992b7eb5-7383-4e63-80df-113f8a48bad2",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:42:23.236180",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T19:06:24.632028",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_190624.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_190624.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:13.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:22.900\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. Think of it like this: your doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:29.600\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to see how much you've learned. The test gives us information.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:36.600\nLet's say you want to know if a cake is done baking. You can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:42.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That\u2019s a test.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.400\nAnother example is testing if a light bulb works by screwing it in. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:55.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a method for gathering information. It helps us check if something is working, true, or present.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:01.300\nIt\u2019s all about finding answers!\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:07.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
