    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_190711.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.100 --> 00:06.200\nToday we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:12.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.500\nWe want to see if something works, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:21.000\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:30.100\nOr, imagine you get new glasses.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:33.300\nYou read a sign to test your vision.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:35.600\nCan you see clearly?\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:37.500\nThat\u2019s another kind of test!\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:41.500\nTests help us understand if something is good, bad, right, or wrong.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:44.400\nThey give us information to make decisions.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:49.300\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something and get information.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:57.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
