    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:07.300\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.000\nIt's a process we use to see if something is true, works correctly, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:28.100\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:33.700\nOr, if you're buying a used car, a mechanic might test the engine to make sure it's running smoothly.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:39.500\nTests aren't just for school!\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:43.700\nAnother example is a doctor giving you a checkup.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:46.900\nThey\u2019re running tests to see how healthy you are.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:51.400\nSo, tests help us evaluate things, make decisions, and learn more.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:54.800\nBasically, they give us information.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:03.400\nTo recap, a test is a procedure used to gather information, check if something works, or see if it meets a standard.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:08.800\nIt's a fundamental tool for learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:11.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
