  "bf74f854-79f8-4831-b5aa-b223ff0404ac": {
    "id": "bf74f854-79f8-4831-b5aa-b223ff0404ac",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:42:31.163758",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T19:19:41.553770",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_191941.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_191941.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something fundamental: the Test.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:17.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:28.700\nThink of it like a detective gathering clues! You're looking for evidence to support your idea.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:35.900\nFor example, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you try screwing it into a lamp and turning it on. That's a test!\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:47.500\nOr, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it\u2019s done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the test passes!\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:57.200\nTests help us prove things, learn from mistakes, and make sure everything is running smoothly. So, remember, a test is all about checking something to see if it's right. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
