    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_192312.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:14.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests. Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:20.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:23.300\nYou do a test \u2013 you poke them with a toothpick!\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:25.800\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:28.700\nTest passed! Cookies are ready.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:42.300\nTests aren't just for baking though. Doctors use tests to see if you\u2019re healthy, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even your phone runs tests to make sure all its parts are working correctly.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:49.300\nAnother example: You want to know if a toy car needs new batteries.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:52.400\nYou try turning it on.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:54.700\nIt doesn\u2019t move?\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:00.000\nThat's a test telling you the batteries are probably dead.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:04.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:09.300\nto see if it works, if it's ready, or if it's even true.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:11.400\nPretty simple, right?\n\n01:11.400 --> 01:15.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
