    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_193649.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests, and no, not the kind you take in school \u2013 though some of the ideas are similar!\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:21.100\nIn this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like this: you buy a new lightbulb.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:31.100\nHow do you know if it works?\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:39.500\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test! You're testing if the lightbulb turns on.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:43.700\nAnother example: You write a letter and want to make sure you spelled everything right.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:47.900\nYou might ask a friend to read it over.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:48.900\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:54.000\nYour friend is testing your spelling. So, a test is really just a way to make sure something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:55.700\nIt\u2019s about trying something out and seeing what happens.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:56.700\nEasy, right?\n\n00:56.700 --> 00:59.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
