    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_194617.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:23.000\nIt's like a little experiment where you ask a question and see what the answer is.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:34.200\nOr maybe you take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:42.400\nSee? Different kinds of tests, but the same basic idea.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:52.400\nAnother example could be testing if a lightbulb works. You plug it in, and if it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:03.700\nIf it doesn't, well, you know the bulb is probably no good. So, to recap: a test is a method for gathering information.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:09.900\nIt helps us understand things better by giving us answers to specific questions.\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:16.000\nIt's a simple, but super useful tool! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
