  "fbaeb762-6bab-420e-93e7-33c544b0aa75": {
    "id": "fbaeb762-6bab-420e-93e7-33c544b0aa75",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:42:51.603325",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T19:52:44.481475",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_195244.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_195244.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:22.600\nIt's a process that helps us measure or evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, a product's quality, or even the safety of a new medicine.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:33.600\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your spelling skills. Or, a taste test helps decide which cookie recipe is the tastiest.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:37.600\nSee? Each one is designed to give us information.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:46.300\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your bath water is hot enough.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:55.400\nWhatever the form, the goal is always the same: to learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:06.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and make better decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "226130fa-af0d-47f0-98fe-7c3fe7d5737f": {
    "id": "226130fa-af0d-47f0-98fe-7c3fe7d5737f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-12-31T20:42:52.051422",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T19:53:38.547023",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_195338.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_195338.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:19.300\nToday we're talking about tests. Now, a test is really just a way to check how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: you take a math test at school to see how well you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:38.600\nOr, maybe you test out a new recipe to see if it tastes good. The main point is to gather information.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:45.000\nIt helps you figure out what you already know, and what you need to work on.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:51.400\nFor example, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down is a test! It tells you you need to practice your balance.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:57.800\nAnother example is a simple spelling test. It shows you which words you already know how to spell.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:01.100\nSo, in short, a test is simply a way to learn and improve by checking your knowledge or abilities.\n```"
  },
  "3b151e9c-c422-4bbb-bd33-e51a74358123": {
    "id": "3b151e9c-c422-4bbb-bd33-e51a74358123",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
