    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_195617.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:13.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see what you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like this: you're checking your knowledge.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:30.400\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. You might have a quiz in class, a driving test to get your license, or even a taste test to see which ice cream flavor you like best!\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:40.900\nThe goal is always the same: to evaluate something. For example, a math test checks your understanding of numbers and equations.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:47.200\nA spelling test sees if you can correctly write words.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:53.500\nAnd that ice cream taste test? It tests your personal preferences!\n\n00:53.500 --> 01:01.900\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method for evaluating knowledge, skills, or preferences.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:08.900\nIt helps us understand where we're at and what we might need to learn next.\n\n01:08.900 --> 01:10.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
