    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_200228.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:26.100\nSimply put, it's a way to find out something.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:34.800\nThink of it like an experiment, but often with a specific goal in mind.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:43.000\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:51.200\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.900\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try restarting it.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:08.600\nThat's a test to see if it fixes the problem!\n\n01:08.600 --> 01:16.300\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:25.500\nThey're a way to check your knowledge and skills.\n\n01:25.500 --> 01:34.700\nAnd in science, tests are used to prove or disprove ideas, like testing a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n01:34.700 --> 01:40.800\nSo, a test is just a way of gathering information and checking something out.\n\n01:40.800 --> 01:44.400\nRemember, it's all about finding answers!\n\n01:44.400 --> 01:48.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
