    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:07.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:12.400\nIt could be anything from a quiz in school to checking if a new recipe tastes good.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:17.400\nThink of it like this: a test is a question, and you're trying to find the answer.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:23.200\nIn school, the questions are usually written down, and you answer them on paper.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:28.000\nBut tests can be much more informal.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.700\nFor example, if you're trying to figure out if a plant needs water, you might poke the soil.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:36.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:40.800\nIf it's dry, the plant probably needs water.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:46.400\nOr, if you're testing a new phone app, you might click on different buttons to see if they work.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:48.000\nThat's a test, too!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:54.400\nBasically, a test is anything that helps you learn something new or confirm something you already suspect.\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:58.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
