    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_200711.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:23.900\nIt's a process designed to give us information. Think of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might use a toothpick.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:35.100\nSticking the toothpick in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test. Or, if you want to know if you\u2019re feeling sick, taking your temperature is another kind of test.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:47.000\nIt gives you information about your body. Tests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a lightbulb works to seeing how well you understand a new topic.\n\n00:47.000 --> 01:00.400\nThe key thing is that they provide us with data that helps us make decisions or learn something new. So, to recap, a test is just a method or procedure used to gather information.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:09.100\nIt could be as simple as checking a cake or as complex as a medical exam. They all aim to help us learn and understand.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:12.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
