    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.100\nNot the kind you worry about in school, but tests in the general sense.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:21.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:34.100\nThe test? Sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test \u2013 it's ready!\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:40.100\nOr imagine checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:54.600\nIf it lights up, the light bulb passes the test \u2013 it works! Tests help us understand if something is working correctly, if it meets a certain standard, or just to learn more about it.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:01.500\nFrom baking cakes to checking light bulbs, tests are all around us.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:05.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something!\n```"
