    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_201436.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:7.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:18.200\nIt\u2019s a process we use to gather information. Think of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it\u2019s sweet enough.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:27.500\nIn school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned. These can be quizzes, exams, or even just asking you questions in class.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:33.200\nThe goal is to check your understanding.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:38.900\nAnother example? A doctor might test your eyesight to see if you need glasses.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:44.600\nOr a car manufacturer might test a new car to make sure it's safe.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:58.500\nSo, a test is really just a method for checking something, whether it\u2019s knowledge, a skill, or even the quality of a product. It helps us understand more about what we're looking at. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "cecea273-1c33-4665-8caa-11259127abd5": {
    "id": "cecea273-1c33-4665-8caa-11259127abd5",
