    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_201548.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:22.100\nThink of it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in and turning it on. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:35.200\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand what you've been learning. They might be multiple choice, true or false, or even asking you to write out your answers.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:43.700\nAnother example: a chef might test their soup by tasting it to see if it needs more salt. They're testing the flavor!\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:54.400\nSo, tests are all about checking something to see if it's working, if it's correct, or if it's good. It's a simple way to get information.\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:58.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
