    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_201909.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nNot the kind you stress about in school, but the kind used to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like this: a test is simply a way to see if something passes or fails.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:34.100\nFor example, if you bake a cake, you can test it by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:44.300\nOr, if you build a birdhouse, you can test it by putting it outside and watching if birds actually use it.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:55.600\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and make sure everything is working correctly. It\u2019s about confirming that your work is solid.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:59.200\nTo recap, a test is a simple process of checking something to see if it meets a certain standard.\n```"
