    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:06.400\nToday we're going to explore something super important:\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:08.800\nthe concept of a test.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:17.700\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer,\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:21.100\nbut in a more structured and reliable way.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:23.800\nThink of baking a cake.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:26.300\nYou taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:29.700\nOr, imagine a doctor checking your temperature.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:32.400\nThat\u2019s a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:36.600\nEven using a ruler to measure how tall you are is a kind of test!\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:42.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a light bulb works to seeing how well you understand a new topic.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:45.800\nThe main idea is to gather information\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:47.800\nand learn something new.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:54.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn about something by asking a question and getting a clear answer.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:57.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
