    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_203234.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like a detective asking questions to solve a mystery. We use tests all the time!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:31.000\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:36.600\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:42.200\nThe toothpick coming out clean means the test passed!\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:49.000\nAnother example? Imagine you're building with blocks. You might test if your tower is strong enough by gently pushing it.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:55.800\nIf it falls, the test failed, and you need to build it differently!\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:02.700\nSo, tests help us understand things and make sure they're working as expected. They\u2019re all about checking and confirming.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:06.300\nIn short, a test is just a way to see if something is working or true.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:09.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
