    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_203447.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.300\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:23.500\nThink about it like this: When you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\nThat toothpick is your test!\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:32.700\nOr, when you go to the doctor, they might give you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:41.600\nAnother example could be testing a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\nThe action of screwing it in and flipping the switch is the test.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:56.500\nThe result, whether it lights up or not, tells you if the bulb is good.\nSo, remember, a test is simply a procedure to check something and see if it works or meets a certain requirement.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:04.800\nIt's a way to gather information and make sure things are as they should be.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
