    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.700\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, what they are, and why we use them.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:18.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if someone understands something.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:28.900\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, a teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:33.800\nTests can be written, like a quiz, or they can involve doing something, like a driving test.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:46.100\nAnother example? Baking a cake! Tasting it is a test to see if it tastes good. So, tests help us check, measure, and learn.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:53.600\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to give us information.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:62.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out. It helps us learn and improve!\n\n00:62.600 --> 00:66.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
