    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.999\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" before, right?\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:16.699\nBut what does it really mean?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:22.899\nWe use tests all the time, often without even realizing it.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:26.899\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:30.999\nYou might stick a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:34.999\nThat's a test!\nYou're testing if the cake is done.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:48.899\nOr think about checking the water temperature before you get in the shower.\nYou're testing to see if it's too hot or too cold.\nTests help us make decisions based on evidence.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:58.099\nWhether it's a school exam, a medical checkup, or just figuring out if that avocado is ripe, tests give us information.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:01.500\nThey help us understand something better.\nSo, a test is just a way of getting information to help you decide what to do next.\n```"
  },
