    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_204250.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so you're hearing the word \"test\" and maybe thinking about school.\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.500\nBut in this video, we're talking about a different kind of test.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:12.000\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:17.000\nBasically, it's a process to see if a thing does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.000\nFor example, you might test a lightbulb to see if it lights up.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.000\nOr, you might test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:34.000\nLet's say you build a birdhouse. You might test it by putting it outside and seeing if birds actually use it!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:36.500\nThat's a test!\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:40.500\nIt's just checking if your birdhouse works as a birdhouse.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:47.000\nSo, a test is a simple way to verify that something does what it's intended to do.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:51.500\nIt\u2019s a way to confirm or deny an idea.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:58.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
