    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:07.600\nA test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly,\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:10.800\nor to see how well something performs.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:17.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:17.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:20.100\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:24.600\nMaybe you're testing if your cookies taste good by giving one to a friend.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:28.900\nOr perhaps a doctor is testing your eyesight to see if you need glasses.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:33.100\nIn computers, tests are used to make sure software is doing what it\u2019s supposed to do.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:41.500\nSo, whether it's a lightbulb, cookies, your eyes, or computer code, a test helps us confirm things are working as expected.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:44.000\nBasically, it's all about checking and confirming.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:56.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
