    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nNow, in everyday life, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:39.000\nIn science, tests are more formal. They're a controlled way to see if an idea, what we call a hypothesis, is likely to be true.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:45.200\nWe change one thing, like adding fertilizer to a plant, and see what happens.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:51.100\nFor example, if you think fertilizer helps plants grow bigger, you could grow two plants.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:57.000\nYou give one fertilizer and the other none. Then, you measure them after a few weeks.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.600\nThat's a test! So, a test is really just a way of observing and learning.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:04.200\nYou change something, watch what happens, and then draw conclusions.\n\n01:04.200 --> 01:07.600\nAnd that\u2019s the basics of testing!\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:11.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
