    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_205258.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_205258.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:25.400\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works. Think about it like this: if you want to know if you're good at riding a bike, you take a test \u2013 you try to ride the bike! Or, if you want to see if a cookie tastes good, you take a test \u2013 you eat it!\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:34.100\nThe result tells you something. Tests can be used for all sorts of things. Your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:40.900\nTeachers give tests to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:47.700\nAnd scientists use tests to see if their ideas are right.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:57.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding out information. It's a simple way to check something and see what the result is.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
