    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_211424.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you cram for, but the kind you use to check something.\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:20.300\nThink of a test as a simple way to see if something is working the way it should. Basically, you\u2019re giving something a challenge and watching how it responds.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:29.500\nFor example, if you want to test if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. The test?\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:33.800\nDoes it light up?\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:43.100\nIf it does, it passes the test! If it doesn\u2019t, well, it failed.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:53.200\nAnother example: imagine you\u2019re testing if your toy car can roll down a ramp. You place the car at the top, let go, and see if it rolls.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:03.000\nThat rolling, or not rolling, is the result of your test. So, remember, a test is just a way to find out if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.600\nIt's all about observing the outcome. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
