    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_211813.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:15.900\nNow, a test, simply put, is a way to find out something. We use them all the time without even realizing it.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake. You taste the batter to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:25.800\nThat's a test! You're testing the sweetness.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:29.300\nOr maybe you're trying a new route to school.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:32.200\nYou're testing if it's faster than your usual way.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:38.600\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:51.400\nThe important thing is you're trying to learn something or confirm something.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:54.500\nSo, to recap, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:54.500 --> 00:55.900\nor checking if something is true.\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:57.000\nEasy peasy!\n\n00:57.000 --> 00:58.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
