    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_211917.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:04.700\nToday we're going to explore something really important: the test.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:07.300\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:11.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:14.800\nThink of it like a detective looking for clues.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:20.400\nWe use tests to check if things are working correctly, to measure something, or to see if we've learned something new.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:26.900\nFor example, your doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:31.600\nA teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:38.800\nOr, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and reliable.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:42.600\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:47.600\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the basic idea is always the same:\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:51.600\nto find out something we didn't know before.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:54.400\nThat's the core of what a test is all about!\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:55.200\nThat's the core of what a test is all about!\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:57.700\nThat's the core of what a test is all about!\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
