    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:48:45.067515",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T21:27:38.414036",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_212738.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_212738.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:9.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:14.400\nYou don't just guess, right?\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:17.400\nYou use a test! You might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:19.700\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:21.100\nThat means it's baked!\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:25.700\nTests aren't just for baking, though. Doctors use tests to see if you\u2019re healthy.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:32.700\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned in class. Even companies use tests to make sure their products work correctly.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:42.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something and learn more about it. It can be a toothpick in a cake, a quiz at school, or anything in between.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:46.500\nThey all help us understand things better.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:49.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
