    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:07.400\nToday we're going to explore something fundamental: the concept of a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:13.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:17.400\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:21.200\nThe test is whether it tastes good!\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:24.800\nOr, maybe you build a toy car.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:26.900\nThe test is whether it rolls.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:31.800\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:36.700\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:41.100\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:45.700\nEven trying a new recipe is a test to see if you like it!\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:52.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:55.800\nThat's the basics of testing!\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
