    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T21:38:22.910756",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_213822.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_213822.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but getting an answer that\u2019s more than just words.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:26.700\nA test helps us understand if something works, or if something is true. For example, a taste test tells us if we like a certain food.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:38.800\nOr, a spelling test shows us how well we know our words. Doctors use tests to see if we're healthy, and engineers use tests to make sure bridges are strong.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:49.300\nEven when you try a new game, you're kind of testing it out to see if you enjoy it! So, a test is really just a way to get information.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:56.900\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
