    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_215410.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:19.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: you take a test in school to show your teacher what you've learned.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:34.600\nBut tests aren't just for school. Imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it before it's finished to \"test\" if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:45.500\nOr, a company might test a new phone to make sure it doesn't break easily.\n\n00:45.500 --> 01:00.400\nSo, whether it's a quiz, a taste, or a stress test on a product, a test is all about gathering information and checking performance. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:04.000\nIn summary, tests are a fundamental way to evaluate knowledge or performance, appearing in many different forms.\n```"
  },
