    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:17.600\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.000\nThat's a test! The toothpick comes out clean? The cake passes the test.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:35.500\nIn science and everyday life, we use tests all the time. For example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:46.000\nOr, you might take a practice quiz to test your knowledge before a big exam. The key thing is that a test is designed to give you information, whether it's about a cake, your health, or how much you know.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:51.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method for gathering information.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
