    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:48:58.686931",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T22:13:31.916218",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_221331.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_221331.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of testing.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:23.300\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. Think about it: when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:32.900\nOr when you turn on a light switch, you're testing if the light bulb works. In science, tests are called experiments.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:43.300\nScientists use experiments to check if their ideas are correct. For example, they might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:52.300\nSo, testing is all about checking something to see if it works, if it's correct, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:60.300\nIt's a fundamental part of learning and discovering new things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "93d7bd67-4e02-4f13-9ea1-f48d6ad2fb8a": {
    "id": "93d7bd67-4e02-4f13-9ea1-f48d6ad2fb8a",
    "topic": "Test",
