    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_221413.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something really fundamental: the test.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:16.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking. You test them by sticking a toothpick in \u2013 if it comes out clean, they pass the test!\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:32.000\nOr maybe you're checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch. If it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:38.200\nIn school, tests help show what you've learned. In science, tests help prove or disprove ideas.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:51.900\nSo, a test is just a method for finding out if something is true, works correctly, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:58.300\nBasically, it's a way of checking. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b41e016d-0896-4b31-a04f-52b9be9b2fce": {
