    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_221453.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:21.900\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer. Think of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:32.600\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words. The test is the tool, and the result tells us something important.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:45.600\nTests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch. Or, they can be more complicated, like a science experiment with lots of steps.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:57.600\nBut the basic idea is always the same: we're trying to learn something by observing the outcome. So, remember, a test is just a way to get information!\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:01.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
