    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.100\nWell, in the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:25.700\nYou wouldn't just guess, right? You'd test it!\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:27.500\nMaybe you'd stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:31.800\nThat toothpick is your test. If it comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:34.600\nIf it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:40.000\nSame goes for other things. A doctor might run tests to see if you\u2019re healthy.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:45.400\nA company might test a new product before selling it.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:52.100\nBasically, a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:56.500\nIt's a way to check something and see if it meets a certain standard\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:00.800\nor tells us what we need to know.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:05.200\nSo, next time you hear the word \"test\", remember it\u2019s just a way to find things out!\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:08.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "cf41dbc3-aba6-4629-a5ff-433747204956": {
    "id": "cf41dbc3-aba6-4629-a5ff-433747204956",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:49:02.401005",
