    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_222414.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_222414.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.100\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:25.600\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, skill, or performance on a specific topic.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:35.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you're healthy, or a chef tastes food to see if it's delicious.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:51.100\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned in class.\nThese tests can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:51.100 --> 01:03.500\nThey help you and your teacher understand what you know well and what you might need to work on.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:15.900\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve equations, while a reading test might ask you to answer questions about a story.\n\n01:15.900 --> 01:23.500\nTests are a tool for learning and improvement, not something to be afraid of.\n\n01:23.500 --> 01:27.100\nSo, remember, tests are simply ways to check your understanding and help you learn.\n\n01:27.100 --> 01:30.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
