    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_223103.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:17.800\nNot the kind you take in school, but the kind we use to check if something works properly.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:28.600\nThink of it like this: a test is just a way to see if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:37.500\nFor example, if you bake a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:46.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:52.100\nOr, if you're building with blocks, you might test your tower by gently pushing it to see if it's strong enough to stand.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:57.800\nSo, a test is basically a way to check, confirm, or verify something. It helps us know if things are working as expected. Tests are everywhere! They help us build better things and make sure everything is safe. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
