    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_223152.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:23.600\nIt helps us understand if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:30.700\nThink of it like this: You're baking a cake, and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:36.000\nA simple test is poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:41.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:46.600\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:51.900\nFalling down is a test! It shows you what not to do next time.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:01.100\nTests aren't just for baking or biking, though. Scientists use tests to see if a new medicine works.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:07.500\nTeachers use tests to see how well students understand a topic.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:16.100\nBasically, anything you do to check or verify something is a form of testing.\n\n01:16.100 --> 01:22.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find things out.\n\n01:22.000 --> 01:28.800\nIt's about learning and improving. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
