    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHello everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.700\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:16.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:19.300\nIt could be to see if you understand a lesson, like a school test,\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:22.100\nor to check if something is working properly.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works. The test is turning it on.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:31.600\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn\u2019t, the test fails.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:34.400\nAnother example? Let\u2019s say you\u2019re baking a cake.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:39.800\nTasting it is a test to see if you added enough sugar. If it tastes sweet enough, you did a good job!\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:54.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is true, correct, or working as expected. It helps us learn and make sure things are right.\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:58.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ea921b9c-3d02-4637-8e0e-65ce52b49fd5": {
