    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_223547.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:19.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question, but instead of just talking, you\u2019re setting up a situation to get an answer.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done. You stick a toothpick in it \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:34.400\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready. Or, imagine you're checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:39.900\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:44.900\nTests aren\u2019t just in baking or fixing things. They're everywhere!\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:59.900\nYour doctor uses tests to check your health, and teachers use tests to see what you've learned. So, a test is just a method to gather information and see if something is true, correct, or working.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:06.200\nThat's the basic idea of a test! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
