    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us understand if something is working, or if we know something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like this: a spelling test helps your teacher see if you've learned how to spell certain words.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:28.700\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste a little bit of the batter \u2013 that\u2019s a test!\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:43.100\nYou're testing to see if it tastes good before you bake the whole thing. Tests can be big, like a final exam in school, or small, like checking the batteries in your flashlight to see if they still work.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:53.300\nThe important thing is that a test gives you information. It tells you something you didn't know before, or confirms something you already suspected.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:02.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information. It helps us learn and make sure things are working properly.\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:06.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "813c44ea-32e1-4289-8296-8daaeb3b8282": {
    "id": "813c44ea-32e1-4289-8296-8daaeb3b8282",
