    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_224613.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:60.9\n1\n00:00.228 --> 00:06.498\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something fundamental: the test.\n\n2\n00:06.498 --> 00:17.308\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, skills, or performance.\n\n3\n00:17.308 --> 00:24.068\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes their soup. That's a test to see if it needs more salt.\n\n4\n00:24.068 --> 00:29.628\nOr, when you try on a new pair of shoes, you're testing if they fit comfortably.\n\n5\n00:29.628 --> 00:42.178\nTests can be formal, like the ones you take in school to measure what you've learned. Or they can be informal, like kicking a ball around to see if it's properly inflated.\n\n6\n00:42.178 --> 00:52.688\nSo, remember, a test is just a method to assess or evaluate something, from soup to shoes to school subjects.\n\n7\n00:52.688 --> 00:57.948\nIt helps us understand more about the world around us and our own abilities.\n\n8\n00:57.948 --> 01:00.878\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3914dcd1-e05f-4a1b-bd15-22b4f1b263b1": {
