    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_224830.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:18.600\nYou've probably taken a lot of them, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:26.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:33.400\nIt helps us measure or evaluate skills, knowledge, or even abilities.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:40.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:47.000\nYou stick a toothpick in it - that's a test!\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:53.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:53.000 --> 01:03.900\nOr imagine taking a quiz at school. That's a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:10.700\nDoctors also use tests to check your health, like taking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n01:10.700 --> 01:23.100\nSo, tests help us understand things better by giving us information.\n\n01:23.100 --> 01:35.500\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, from simple everyday checks to more complex exams.\n\n01:35.500 --> 01:41.800\nThey all have the same goal: to learn something new.\n\n01:41.800 --> 01:49.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
