    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.700\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a more formal way.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:33.300\nWe use tests all the time to see how well we understand things, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:45.400\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how many words you know. Or, a doctor might run a test to see if you have a certain illness.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:54.200\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing the recipe to see if it turns out delicious!\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:04.500\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions. They can be used to measure knowledge, diagnose problems, or simply confirm that something is working as expected.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:09.000\nIn short, a test is a valuable tool for learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:14.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
