    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_231508.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned in class.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:32.400\nThere are lots of different kinds of tests. Some are written, like quizzes.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:40.200\nOthers are practical, like a driving test. And some are even physical, like testing how far you can jump.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:51.100\nThe important thing is that they all have a goal: to measure something specific. So, remember, a test is a method of evaluation.\n\n00:51.100 --> 01:02.100\nIt helps us understand where we stand, whether it's in learning, health, or any other area. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
