    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_231634.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_231634.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.400\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's how we check to see if something is true, or if something works like it should.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like this: your mom might test the temperature of your forehead to see if you have a fever. That's a test!\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:26.700\nOr maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:34.900\nTests aren't just for school or sickness, though. A scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:39.500\nA chef might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:46.800\nSee? Tests are all around us. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:51.200\nSo, a test is just a way to get information and see if something is true or effective.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:57.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d26f8d1f-ad1d-4604-98c8-a238078afc07": {
    "id": "d26f8d1f-ad1d-4604-98c8-a238078afc07",
