    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.300 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:23.800\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:29.600\nWe use tests all the time to see if something is working properly, or to check what we know.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:36.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy, or a teacher uses a test to see if you understand the lesson.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:44.800\nSo, what exactly is being tested?\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:53.100\nWell, it could be anything! For example, you might test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:56.700\nThat's a simple test.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:01.400\nOr, you might test your memory by trying to remember a list of words.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:02.900\nThe key thing is that you're trying to get information.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:08.400\nUltimately, tests help us learn and improve.\n\n01:08.400 --> 01:12.800\nThey show us where we're strong and where we need to focus more effort.\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:17.700\nSo, whether it's a quiz at school or checking if your bike tires have enough air, tests are a really useful tool.\n\n01:17.700 --> 01:21.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
