    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.190\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.190 --> 00:04.050\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.050 --> 00:08.150\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:08.150 --> 00:12.510\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:12.510 --> 00:16.770\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:16.770 --> 00:17.560\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.560 --> 00:21.430\nYou're checking to see if the cake is cooked all the way through.\n\n00:21.430 --> 00:24.680\nOr, when you go to the doctor, they might check your temperature.\n\n00:24.680 --> 00:27.680\nThat's also a test, making sure your body is within a healthy range.\n\n00:27.680 --> 00:32.240\nTests can be simple, like that toothpick, or more complicated, like a big exam at school.\n\n00:32.240 --> 00:38.070\nBut the goal is always the same: to get information and see if something is as it should be.\n\n00:38.070 --> 00:44.420\nSo remember, a test is just a way to check something and learn more about it.\n\n00:44.420 --> 00:47.240\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
