    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_232114.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nIt\u2019s how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\nThe test?\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.800\nScrewing it in and flipping the switch.\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:35.700\nOr, maybe you want to know if your cookies taste good.\nThe test is having someone try one.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:42.000\nIf they smile, that\u2019s a good sign!\nTests aren't just for physical things, either.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:48.300\nWe can test our knowledge with quizzes, or test our skills playing a game.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:54.600\nBasically, any time you're checking to see if something is the way you expect it to be, you're performing a test.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:05.600\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
