    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_232610.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you might test the temperature of your bathwater to make sure it's not too hot or too cold.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:27.800\nOr, a baker might test a cake by poking it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:38.000\nTests aren't just for bathwater and cakes, though. Doctors use tests to check your health, like taking your temperature or drawing blood.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:48.400\nStudents take tests in school to show what they've learned. Even engineers test bridges to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:56.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding out information about something.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:04.100\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, is safe to use, or meets a certain standard. Hopefully, that gives you a better idea of what a test is! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
