    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_232737.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.300\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something about something, or someone.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:28.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand better. The main idea is to check if something works, or if you know something.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:42.800\nOr, think about baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:57.400\nAnother example is checking if a light bulb works. You plug it in, and if it lights up, you know it passed the test! So, a test is simply a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:01.000\nBasically, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:03.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
