    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_233412.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:15.500\nToday we're talking about tests. Now, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you get the right answer. It helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if someone knows something.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:37.400\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick test. You stick a toothpick in, and if it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:43.400\nOr, think about taking a spelling test at school. It shows how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:49.400\nTests aren't just for school, though. Doctors use tests to check your health, and scientists use tests to prove their ideas.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:64.900\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something. It helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
