    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_233641.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:14.900\nNow, in the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:37.900\nFor example, when you try a new fruit, you're testing to see if you like the taste.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:49.500\nOr, if you push a door, you're testing to see if it's open or closed.\n\n00:49.500 --> 01:01.200\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand what you've been learning.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:12.900\nSo, tests can be big, like a final exam, or small, like trying a new snack.\n\n01:12.900 --> 01:16.500\nThe important thing is that they help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:16.500 --> 01:19.900\nThey give us information we didn't have before.\n\n01:19.900 --> 01:26.400\nTo recap, a test is a way of asking a question and getting an answer, helping us learn and understand things.\n\n01:26.400 --> 01:29.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
