    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_233725.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:22.700\nIt helps us check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:35.500\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy. Or maybe you're baking a cake, and you test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:48.000\nIn computers, we use tests all the time to make sure our programs are working the way we expect.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:58.600\nFor example, if we build a calculator, we might test it by giving it simple problems like 2 plus 2 to make sure it gives us the correct answer, which is 4!\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:02.100\nTests help us catch mistakes and make sure everything runs smoothly.\n```"
  },
