    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_233859.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. Think of it like this: it's a method we use to gather information.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:25.700\nThe main idea behind a test is to see how something performs or behaves under certain conditions.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:36.100\nThis could be anything! For example, a taste test tells us how good something tastes. Or, a spelling test shows us how well we know how to spell words.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:39.900\nAnother example?\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:43.800\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:55.900\nYou might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test! You're testing if the cake is cooked all the way through. So, to recap: a test is a way to get information about something by observing it or making it do something.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:02.100\nIt helps us understand and learn! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
