    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_234107.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:07.700\nIn everyday life, a test is simply a way to find something out, right?\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:09.000\nLike testing if a cake is done\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:10.300\nby poking it with a fork.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:14.400\nIn the world of technology, a test is really similar.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:17.900\nIt's a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:22.300\nWe use tests to make sure software, hardware, really anything technical,\nis doing what it should.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you test it by pushing it\nto see if it rolls.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:27.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:34.000\nOr, imagine you write a simple computer program to add two numbers.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:37.400\nYou test it by giving it different numbers to add and seeing if the answer\nis correct.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:43.300\nSo, a test is simply a way to verify that something works as expected.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:47.700\nIt helps us catch mistakes early and make sure things are reliable.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:50.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
