    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_234326.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHey there! Welcome.\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:05.100\nToday we're diving into the concept of a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:07.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:10.400\nIt helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:14.200\nThink about it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:17.900\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:18.900\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:22.500\nAnother example is a spelling test in school.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.800\nThat test checks if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.600\nThe result of the test, whether you pass or fail, gives you information about what you know and what you might need to learn.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:36.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a method to check something and learn more about it.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:39.200\nIt gives us information we can use!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:41.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
