    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_234910.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, so you're hearing the word \"test\" and wondering what it really means, right?\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:12.400\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find something out. It's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:19.200\nThink about it like this: a recipe test. You follow a recipe, and the \"test\" is whether the dish tastes good.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:26.000\nOr, a spelling test! You're tested on how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:36.600\nThe goal is to see what you know and what you might need to learn more about. Tests can be formal, like exams in school, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:47.400\nThey all have the same purpose: to check something and learn more about it. So, a test is really just a way to get answers!\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
