    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_235157.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:25.700\nIt helps us understand if something is working as expected, or if something needs improvement. Think of it like this: a chef tastes the soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:34.200\nOr, a doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy. In school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:43.400\nTests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb turns on. Or more complicated, like a science experiment.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:52.400\nThe important thing is they give us information. So, to recap, a test is a process designed to gather information and evaluate something.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:58.400\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:01.900\nThanks for watching!\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:03.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
