    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:13.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:20.800\nThink of it like a question you ask to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:26.400\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:42.300\nYour teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a lesson. A doctor might run a test to check your health. Even baking a cake is a test! You're testing if your recipe and ingredients will create something delicious.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:50.500\nFor example, a simple test could be asking \"What's two plus two?\" The answer, four, shows you understand basic addition.\n\n00:50.500 --> 01:00.200\nOr, if you try to start your car and it doesn't turn on, that's a test showing something might be wrong with the battery.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:09.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information. It helps us understand things better and solve problems.\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:16.500\nIt can be a question, an experiment, or even just observing something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "7168dcdc-b796-453e-a542-f86b264e767f": {
    "id": "7168dcdc-b796-453e-a542-f86b264e767f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:49:32.050225",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T23:55:47.615795",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260101_235547.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_235547.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:04.800\nToday we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:8.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:15.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:16.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:18.700\nIt either lights up, or it doesn't.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:23.700\nAnother example? Maybe you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:26.400\nYou stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:29.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:37.000\nSo, a test is really just a simple process: you have something to check, you perform an action, and then you see the result.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.700\nThat result tells you if your thing is working, true, or good enough.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:44.900\nPretty straightforward, right?\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:47.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
