    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260101_235930.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt helps us check if something is working, if something is true, or how well someone understands something.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like this: When you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:29.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:34.000\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:42.600\nEach time you try, you're testing your balance and coordination.\nTests aren't always about grades or scores.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:51.700\nThey can be simple experiments, observations, or even just asking a question to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:58.800\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.300\nSo remember, a test is just a way to gather information and check on things.\n```"
  },
