  "b8b68de5-cb17-468d-89c7-20fa24a6bd71": {
    "id": "b8b68de5-cb17-468d-89c7-20fa24a6bd71",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:49:33.803965",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T00:01:17.607354",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_000117.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_000117.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something scary from school, but really, a test is just a way to find out if something works the way it should.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like checking if your lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:28.000\nThat's a test! Essentially, a test compares what you expect to happen with what actually happens.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:38.700\nFor example, if you pour water into a glass, you expect it to fill up. If it leaks everywhere instead, that's a failed test!\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:49.400\nAnother example: If you plant a seed, you expect it to grow into a plant. If it doesn\u2019t sprout, you might say that test failed, and you need to try again with a different seed.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:60.900\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected. It's about comparing what you think should happen with what actually happens.\n\n00:60.900 --> 00:68.400\nSimple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
