    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_000932.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests!\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:14.400\nThink of a test as a way to check something. It\u2019s how we find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:23.700\nBasically, a test is a question or a challenge.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:31.000\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:37.900\nOr, when you're baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:45.600\nThe toothpick comes out clean, that's a pass! If it's gooey, the cake needs more time.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:53.400\nAnother example is a school test. It helps your teacher see how well you understand the things you've been learning.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:57.000\nSo, tests are all about checking something and getting an answer. They help us learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
