    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_001026.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:04.000\nToday we're going to talk about something super important:\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:04.700\nTests!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:06.200\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:08.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:12.100\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, or seeing how well you understand a topic in school.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:16.000\nThink about baking a cake. You might take a toothpick and poke it into the cake to see if it's done.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:16.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:21.200\nOr imagine a doctor checking your temperature to see if you have a fever. That's another kind of test.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:25.600\nTests help us understand if something is working properly or if we need to make adjustments.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:30.500\nSo, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:33.500\nWe use them all the time, in all sorts of situations.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:36.700\nRemember, tests help us learn and improve!\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:38.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
