    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:19.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:19.800 --> 34.300\nIt could be your knowledge on a subject, the strength of a material, or even the quality of your eyesight. Think of it like this: if you want to know if you've learned your ABCs, you take a test! Or, if you want to see how well a new bridge can hold weight, engineers will put it through a test.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:42.900\nIt's all about gathering data and getting answers.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:50.400\nFor example, a quiz in school is a test of your understanding. Doctors use tests to check your health.\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:02.100\nEven trying a new recipe is a bit of a test to see if you like it!\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.700\nSo, in short, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:09.300\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:12.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
