    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:28.300\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might use a toothpick test.\nYou poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:38.500\nOr, imagine you're checking if a light bulb works.\nYou flip the switch, and if the light comes on, the bulb passes the test.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:47.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a bridge is safe, to seeing if you've learned something new in school.\n\n00:47.800 --> 01:01.500\nThe main idea is to gather information and make sure things are as they should be.\nSo, tests are all about checking, finding out, and making sure things are working the way we expect.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:05.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
