    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_003108.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.200 --> 00:03.300\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:04.400\n\u2013 and no, not the kind you cram for!\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:07.000\nA test, in a general sense, is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:8.700\nIt's a procedure designed to gather information.\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by plugging it in.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:14.100\nThat\u2019s a test!\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:16.300\nAnother example is baking a cake.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:17.900\nThe taste is the test!\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:21.300\nDoes it taste good? That tells you something about your recipe and your baking skills.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.100\nOr, if you're trying out a new phone, you might test its camera by taking pictures.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:28.000\nThe quality of the pictures is the result of that test.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:35.000\nSo, basically, a test is any process that gives you information about something.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:39.000\nIt's a way to learn and explore the world around us.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:40.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c3525a22-fa62-4460-9ded-511da495c26b": {
    "id": "c3525a22-fa62-4460-9ded-511da495c26b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:49:42.731311",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T00:31:54.239397",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_003154.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_003154.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, you\u2019ve probably taken a test before, maybe at school. But what exactly is a test?\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:20.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:29.100\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is ready, you might stick a toothpick in it. That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:34.400\nThe toothpick tells you if the cake is cooked through.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:40.200\nAnother example? Checking the batteries in your remote. You're testing to see if they still have power.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:46.000\nTests can be simple or complex, but they all help us learn something new.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:60.200\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and see if something is working, ready, or true. It\u2019s a fundamental tool for learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:60.200 --> 00:62.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e612f2bc-c4f8-4a60-b44e-bc2bcb40c241": {
    "id": "e612f2bc-c4f8-4a60-b44e-bc2bcb40c241",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:49:42.950236",
