    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_003415.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nIn simple terms, a test is really just a way to find out something.\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:27.300\nThink about it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:34.900\nOr, imagine you're testing a toy car to see if it goes fast.\nYou wind it up and see how far it travels.\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:47.800\nTests are used for all sorts of things, from checking if your internet is working properly, to big medical tests that help doctors understand your health.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:59.200\nThey all have the same basic idea: to gather information and learn something.\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to find things out.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:04.400\nIt's a process of checking and observing.\nWe use them every day!\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:07.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
