    "id": "4beeaa5c-b8a1-4118-8808-e8de1b08d72c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:49:45.811526",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T00:40:59.730205",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_004059.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_004059.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:09.300\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:09.300 --> 00:17.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:26.100\nIt's a process designed to measure or evaluate something specific.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:35.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you're healthy, or a chef tastes a dish to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:40.400\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:45.800\nThey might be multiple choice questions, or even writing an essay.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:51.200\nThe point is to show what you know.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:56.600\nAnother example is a driving test.\n\n00:56.600 --> 00:58.500\nIt makes sure you know how to safely operate a car.\n```"
  },
  "4fc2ba4e-6a4d-4553-9e61-be73f92fb8d1": {
    "id": "4fc2ba4e-6a4d-4553-9e61-be73f92fb8d1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:49:46.081381",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T00:41:42.109694",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_004142.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_004142.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.800\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:23.400\nThink of it as a helpful question that gives us an answer. The main idea is simple: you present something, like a question or a problem, and you get a response.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:31.800\nThat response tells you something about the thing you're testing. For example, a simple quiz is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:39.600\nA taste test lets you know if you like a certain food.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:50.700\nEven checking if a light switch works is a kind of test! You flip the switch, and if the light turns on, the test passes.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:59.700\nSo, in short, a test helps us learn and confirm information. It\u2019s all about asking a question and getting an answer to understand something better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
