    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_005054.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of testing.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:20.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to see if something works as expected.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:31.100\nThink of it like this: you have an idea about how something should behave, and a test helps you confirm that it actually does.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:46.100\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you test it by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, you know the cake is done!\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:56.900\nOr, if you're building a tower of blocks, you might gently shake the table to test its stability. Testing is super important because it helps us catch mistakes early and make sure things are reliable.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.400\nSo, remember, testing is all about checking if things work the way they should, using simple methods to confirm our expectations. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
