    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out if something is working correctly, or to see how well someone understands something.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in. That's a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:31.500\nOr, when you take a quiz in school to see how well you learned the material, that's another kind of test.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:43.000\nWe use tests all the time to make sure things are safe, accurate, and effective. For example, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:52.700\nOr a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe for customers.\n\n00:52.700 --> 01:04.400\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something. It helps us confirm if things are working or if someone understands something.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:08.000\nTests are important for safety, learning, and making sure things are done right.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:11.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
