    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.700\nNow, you might think of school exams, but a \"test\" in a broader sense is really just a way to find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:29.500\nYou're testing if the lightbulb lights up.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:35.000\nOr, maybe you want to see if your cookies taste good. You take a bite! That\u2019s a taste test.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:42.300\nSo basically, a test is any procedure designed to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:50.200\nIt could be as simple as checking the weather before you go outside, or something more complicated like a medical test.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:58.000\nThe main goal is always to get some information. So, remember, a test helps us understand if something is working, true, or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
