    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nWhat are they, and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: if you're learning to ride a bike, a test would be seeing if you can balance and pedal without falling.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:33.500\nTests can come in many forms. Maybe it's a quiz with multiple-choice questions, or perhaps it's a practical test where you have to show someone how to do something.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:46.400\nFor example, a cooking test might involve making a simple dish. The important thing is that tests help us understand what we've learned and where we might need some more practice.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:52.800\nSo, remember, tests aren't scary. They're just tools to help us learn and grow.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:00.300\nThey show us what we know and guide us on what to study next. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
