    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.300\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:19.700\nIt's a process of trying something to see what happens, or checking something to see if it's working correctly.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:31.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, if you're baking a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:33.600\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:39.700\nAnother example is a lightbulb. We can test a lightbulb by plugging it in.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:47.400\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, the lightbulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:58.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something or find something out. It helps us learn and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:01.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
