    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:17.400\nIt's how we find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:21.200\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by turning it on.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:24.500\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If not, well, it failed.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:29.800\nAnother example is checking if water is hot enough for a bath. You might dip your toe in.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:32.300\nThat's a test! You're testing the water temperature.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:35.300\nSo, a test helps us confirm something.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:38.900\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, a recipe tastes good, or even if you understand a new idea.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:45.500\nTests are everywhere! They help us learn and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:48.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
