  "31f27ec6-4593-451e-8c7a-4e17b743021f": {
    "id": "31f27ec6-4593-451e-8c7a-4e17b743021f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:02.861696",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T01:28:21.685393",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_012821.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_012821.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find something out. Think of it like an experiment, but often with a specific right or wrong answer.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:25.100\nIt's a method for gathering information. For example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling words.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:35.300\nA taste test helps you decide which cookie you like best. Even a medical test, like checking your temperature, gives us information about your health.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:45.400\nSo, basically, a test is a structured way to ask a question and get an answer, helping us to learn and understand things better.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:51.100\nIt's a tool for discovery! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9ed199ae-22d1-4a65-8516-edf5f0f60f9e": {
