    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_013609.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. It helps us check if something is working correctly, or if we've learned something new.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like this: you might test a toy car to see if it rolls, or a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:35.800\nIn school, tests help your teachers see what you understand about a topic. They might ask you questions about things you've learned in class, or ask you to solve a problem.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:46.500\nFor example, a math test might ask you to add numbers together, like 2 + 2. Or a reading test might ask you what happened in a story.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:51.500\nTests aren't meant to be scary! They're just a way to see where you're at.\n\n00:51.500 --> 01:01.900\nSo, remember, a test is a way to find out something. It can be used to check if something works, or to see what you've learned.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:07.900\nIt's all about learning and growing! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
