    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_013655.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.700\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like this: You have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it\u2019s working. The test is screwing it into a lamp and flipping the switch.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:35.800\nIf it lights up, the test passes! Another example: you bake a cake, and the test is taking a bite to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:40.500\nDoes it taste sweet and delicious? Then the test passes!\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:50.000\nSo, a test is just a simple way to verify that something is doing what it's supposed to do. It's all about checking and confirming.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:53.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d4a69ad6-8c82-44c9-82eb-e30c79cc632a": {
