    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T01:39:22.620921",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_013922.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_013922.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.600\nWhat are they, and why do we even use them?\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:19.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:28.200\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You plug it in \u2013 that's the test \u2013 and then you see if it lights up.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:41.600\nWe use tests all the time, in school, for driving, even when doctors check your reflexes. For example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:48.100\nOr, a taste test can help you decide which cookie recipe is the best.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:56.100\nSo, a test is just a way to measure something, whether it's knowledge, skill, or even just preference.\n\n00:56.100 --> 00:59.100\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we might need to learn more about.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.700\nThanks for watching! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
