    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_015138.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:19.800\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or works the way we expect it to.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:32.800\nThink about it like this: you might test a cake recipe by baking it and seeing if it tastes good.\nOr, you might test a toy to see if it's durable enough to withstand some playtime.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:42.000\nIn science, tests are called experiments. Scientists create tests to see if their ideas about the world are correct.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:51.500\nTests can be big or small, simple or complex. But the main idea is always the same: to learn something new.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:59.900\nSo, remember, a test is a way to learn about the world around us by trying things out and seeing what happens.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
