    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_020249.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.900\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:19.600\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:24.000\nThe thing we're trying to find out about could be anything!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:33.900\nIs the water safe to drink?\nIs this cake delicious?\nDoes this light bulb work?\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:44.300\nWe use tests to get answers to these questions.\nFor example, a math test helps your teacher understand how well you understand math.\nA taste test helps you decide which ice cream flavor you like best.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:54.700\nA simple on/off switch is a basic test to see if an appliance is working.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information or an answer.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:01.500\nIt can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like trying a new food.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:07.500\nTests help us learn and make decisions.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:14.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
