    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:08.200\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:12.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:16.100\nIt helps us understand if something is working, is true, or is good.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:22.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:26.500\nOr, maybe you're baking a cake and you taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:27.800\nThat's another test!\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:31.500\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:36.400\nSo, tests help us learn and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:39.600\nThey're a fundamental part of learning and improving things.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:42.500\nIn short, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:45.200\nWe try something out and see what happens!\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:48.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
