    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_021001.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like checking if your lights turn on when you flip the switch.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:29.600\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\nDid your cookies bake all the way through?\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:34.000\nYou can test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.400\nDoes your toy car roll down the ramp?\nThat's another test!\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:52.000\nTests help us understand if things are working correctly, or if we need to make some changes.\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of checking if something does what it's meant to do.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:54.800\nIt's all about confirming things work as expected.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1d03be95-7b6f-4802-ae6e-fc8e320240a1": {
