    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_021128.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:18.300\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you take a cookie out of the oven and poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:22.200\nThat's a test! You're testing to see if it's done.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:32.900\nTests can be anything from a quick check to a really detailed examination. Like, maybe you're testing if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:41.000\nOr, you're taking a quiz at school to see how well you understand a topic. Both are examples of tests!\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:49.200\nThe main point is that a test helps us find out if something is working as expected, or if it needs some more work.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:57.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a check, big or small, to see if something is good to go.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "21aebb43-e168-47bd-b6e3-d31d1e0b077e": {
    "id": "21aebb43-e168-47bd-b6e3-d31d1e0b077e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:18.068981",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T02:12:11.615644",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_021211.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_021211.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:20.200\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:31.600\nYou might stick a toothpick in it. That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:38.000\nThe toothpick coming out clean tells you the cake is ready.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:44.300\nOr, imagine you want to see if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:50.600\nYou screw it into a lamp. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:57.000\nTests aren\u2019t just for cakes and lightbulbs. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.900\nTeachers use tests to see what you\u2019ve learned.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:04.400\nBasically, anything you do to check something and get information from it\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:08.100\ncan be considered a test.\n\n01:08.100 --> 01:18.600\nSo, a test is a designed experiment or procedure that helps us gather information and make a judgment.\n\n01:18.600 --> 01:22.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "44dbf038-5a26-4de5-832a-939aa5d9f7e5": {
    "id": "44dbf038-5a26-4de5-832a-939aa5d9f7e5",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:18.306712",
