    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_022118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but we're talking about tests in a broader sense: a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.900\nBasically, a test is any process designed to see if something is true, or to measure how well something works.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:36.200\nThink of it like this: you have a hypothesis, an idea, and the test helps you prove or disprove it.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:42.500\nFor example, a simple taste test is a test! You're trying to find out which flavor you like best.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:48.800\nOr, imagine you're building a tower of blocks. Each block you add is a little test to see if the tower stays standing.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:58.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something. It helps us confirm or deny an idea, or measure performance.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:02.100\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:03.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
