  "6bcfa939-0b8d-4fa2-9411-47b5d8119767": {
    "id": "6bcfa939-0b8d-4fa2-9411-47b5d8119767",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:22.277670",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T02:26:54.723007",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_022654.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_022654.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.300\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake. The test is when you poke it with a toothpick. If it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:30.600\nOr, imagine you're trying to fix a broken toy. You try different things, and each time you try something, that's a test to see if it worked.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:41.500\nAnother simple example is checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, it passed the test!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:51.800\nSo, tests are all about trying something out and seeing what happens. They help us learn, fix problems, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:59.900\nBasically, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
