    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:04.800\nToday we're going to explore something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:08.800\nNow, in the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:14.000\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're getting proof or evidence.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:17.300\nThe main point of a test is to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:22.700\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:26.800\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:27.900\nSee?\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:28.800\nBoth are tests!\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:35.300\nSo, a test is a method used to gather information or evidence to evaluate something.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:39.200\nIt helps us understand, confirm, or discover something new.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:45.500\nTests are all around us, and they help us make better decisions every day.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:49.400\nIn short: a test is a way to learn something by checking it.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:51.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6d554678-b4c0-4286-a124-c7701606e74f": {
