    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_023009.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. We want to see if something works, if something is true, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you test it by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:33.500\nOr, maybe you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:41.700\nYou test your balance by slowly letting go of the handlebars. If you stay upright, your balance is getting better! That's another test.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:45.500\nTests help us learn and improve.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:54.500\nThey give us information about whether we're on the right track. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:03.900\nIt can be a simple as poking a cake or as complex as a science experiment. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
