    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_024548.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.999\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to explore something really fundamental: what a test actually is.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:17.199\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:30.599\nThe goal of a test is to see how well someone understands something, or how well something works. For example, you might take a math test at school to show your teacher what you've learned.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:38.599\nOr, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and reliable.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:46.599\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might stick a toothpick in it \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:53.799\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. If it comes out with batter on it, it needs more time.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:03.399\nTests help us make informed decisions. So, remember, a test is just a way of gathering information to understand something better.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:06.900\nIt\u2019s about learning and improving. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
