    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_024951.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.000\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:27.900\nBasically, you\u2019re checking something out. You set up a situation, you observe what happens, and then you draw a conclusion.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:40.500\nFor example, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:53.300\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a new lightbulb works. You screw it into the lamp, flip the switch, and if the light comes on, that's a successful test!\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:03.500\nSo, a test is simply a way to check something and learn something new. Remember, it's all about observing and figuring things out.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
