    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_025235.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:08.700\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:13.600\nThink of it like this: you're trying to learn about a subject, or how well something works.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:16.600\nSo, how do we do that?\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:22.300\nWell, we create a situation, a set of questions, or a process, and then we observe the results.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:29.100\nFor example, if you want to know if a plant needs more water, you might give it a small amount of water and then check the soil to see if it's still dry.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:31.100\nThat's a simple test!\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:35.700\nOr, if you're learning your ABCs, a quiz asking you to identify letters is a test.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:41.500\nBasically, a test helps us understand something better by giving us information we can use.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:45.400\nSo, to sum it up: a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:49.200\nWe create a scenario, observe, and learn.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:52.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
