    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_030115.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:18.100\nWe use them all the time! Think about it. If you're baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:26.200\nThat's a test! Or, if you're trying to figure out if your phone is working, you might try making a call. That's testing too!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:34.700\nIn more formal settings, like school, tests help teachers see what you've learned. They're like a snapshot of your knowledge.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:44.700\nAnd in science, tests, or experiments, help us understand how things work. We change something and see what happens.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:51.900\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:00.700\nWhether it's checking a cake, your phone, or understanding a new subject, tests are all about finding things out.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:04.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3841e3dd-9d2e-4482-a1ee-0768c3e7d4bc": {
    "id": "3841e3dd-9d2e-4482-a1ee-0768c3e7d4bc",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:32.517814",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T03:02:09.578836",
