    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_030209.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:17.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true, correct, or working as expected.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:29.200\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is ready, you might use a toothpick.\nSticking the toothpick in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test!\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:37.900\nOr, if you want to see if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\nThat's another test!\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:49.800\nTests can be simple like that, or more complex, like a school exam.\nBut the basic idea is always the same: to check something and get an answer.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:59.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of gathering information.\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ba57c47c-fbd4-40b3-a5f7-ecc4887c4d05": {
    "id": "ba57c47c-fbd4-40b3-a5f7-ecc4887c4d05",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:32.790499",
