    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_030257.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.800\nNow, a test might sound scary, but it's really just a way to check what you know.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like this: you've been learning about apples, right?\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:37.100\nA test on apples would simply ask you questions about apples, like what color they are or if they grow on trees.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:45.000\nSo, a test helps show how well you understand something.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.900\nIt could be a quiz with multiple-choice questions, or maybe even just drawing a picture to show what you've learned.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:08.000\nFor example, if we were testing your knowledge of animals, you might be asked to name different types of animals. Or, if it was about numbers, you might need to solve a simple math problem.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:14.100\nBasically, tests are there to help you and your teachers see where you're doing great and what you might need a little extra help with.\n\n01:14.100 --> 01:17.700\nThey're a learning tool!\n\n01:17.700 --> 01:23.900\nRemember, don't stress too much, just do your best.\n\n01:23.900 --> 01:27.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c17dfb6a-3164-4799-8de3-29c94e0ae194": {
    "id": "c17dfb6a-3164-4799-8de3-29c94e0ae194",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
