    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_030343.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but tests are really just ways to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: You want to bake a cake. The recipe is like a plan, and baking the cake is like the test.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:35.800\nYou follow the recipe, and if the cake comes out delicious, the test is a success!\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:46.100\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in, flip the switch, and if it lights up, the bulb passed the test.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:53.100\nSo, tests help us learn and improve things. They show us what works and what doesn't.\n\n00:53.100 --> 01:02.900\nThey're used everywhere, from baking to building bridges. So remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
