    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.100\nToday, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:22.400\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:28.600\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:33.800\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:38.000\nThat's a test! Or, a doctor might check your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:43.300\nThey're both gathering information to learn something.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:48.600\nAnother example? Imagine you\u2019re baking cookies. You might try one to test if they\u2019re done.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:59.400\nIf they\u2019re soft and chewy, the test tells you they\u2019re ready to eat! So, remember, a test is just a way to learn about something by observing or trying something out. It helps us make decisions and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4e6d6a39-168a-430f-af4f-1a2ba9844869": {
    "id": "4e6d6a39-168a-430f-af4f-1a2ba9844869",
