    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_030829.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:21.800\nIt's like asking a question and looking for the answer. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:31.200\nOr, a teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject. Tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:42.600\nFor example, you might test if a toy car rolls faster on a smooth surface or a carpet. You roll the car on both, and see which is faster.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:49.100\nThat's a test! Or, you might taste two different cookies to test which one tastes better.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:55.600\nYou're gathering information! So, remember, a test is just a way to find something out,\n\n00:55.600 --> 01:02.900\nby asking a question and then finding the answer through observation or trying something out. It helps us understand the world around us.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:09.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
