    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_030909.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's how we check if something is working, if something is true, or even how good something is.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:24.000\nThink about it like this: When you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:33.000\nYou're testing if the cake is cooked all the way through. Or, if your phone isn't working, you might try restarting it.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:44.400\nThat's testing a solution to see if it fixes the problem. Tests are used everywhere, from checking if a lightbulb works to figuring out what you learned in school.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:54.900\nThey help us understand things better and make sure things are working the way they should. So, remember, a test is just a way to find things out!\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:58.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
