    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_031235.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you've probably taken tests in school, but in general, a test is really just a way to check if something works or if it's true.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, right? You might test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:27.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:33.000\nOr maybe you're buying a new phone. You might test the camera by taking a picture,\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:36.200\nor test the volume by playing a song.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:45.000\nTests help us make sure things are working the way they should. So, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it passes or fails.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:51.200\nIt's a way of getting information and confirming what we think is true.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:54.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
