    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_031721.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to see if something works, or if you understand something.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:34.600\nThat's a simple test! In school, tests help teachers see what you've learned. They might ask you questions or give you problems to solve.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:46.400\nIn science, tests can be experiments, like mixing two chemicals to see what happens.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:56.600\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. Or, if you bake a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:06.300\nSo, a test is just a way to check something, understand something, or learn something new. It\u2019s a way to get information.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:09.900\nIn short, tests are all about checking things.\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:16.300\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:19.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1126612d-024f-4408-a65c-4f05e1b33e36": {
    "id": "1126612d-024f-4408-a65c-4f05e1b33e36",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:38.541573",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T03:18:10.467648",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_031810.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_031810.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.800\nNo need to worry, these aren't the kind you cram for! In general, a test is simply a way to find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb is working.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:32.400\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's your test. If the light comes on, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, the lightbulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:40.200\nAnother example: Let\u2019s say you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:51.600\nYou can stick your finger in the soil. If it feels dry, that's a sign the plant needs water, and the test tells you to water it! If it's moist, the test tells you it's okay for now.\n\n00:51.600 --> 01:03.300\nSo, to recap, a test is just a simple way to check something. You perform an action, and then you look at the result to see if it passes or fails.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:08.200\nEasy peasy! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
