    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_033320.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:16.800\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in the world of science and technology, a test is really just a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: you build a birdhouse, right? A test would be to see if a bird actually uses it! You're testing if your birdhouse design is good.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.400\nAnother simple example is baking a cake. You test the recipe by tasting the cake to see if it's delicious.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:39.900\nIf it's not, you adjust the recipe and test it again! So, a test is simply a way to see if something is working correctly.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:51.600\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:55.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d1bdb49f-427e-41a7-8f5e-e0bb3095bb56": {
    "id": "d1bdb49f-427e-41a7-8f5e-e0bb3095bb56",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:50:43.942623",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T03:34:02.957347",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_033402.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_033402.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 but not the kind you take in school.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:18.600\nIn computer programming, a test is a way to make sure your code is working correctly. Think of it like checking your work to make sure you got the right answer.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:27.100\nBasically, you write a little bit of code that tests if another piece of your code is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:37.300\nFor example, if you have a piece of code that's supposed to add two numbers together, you can write a test that checks if it actually gives you the right sum.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:46.500\nSo, if you give it 2 and 2, the test should make sure it returns 4. If it doesn't, you know there's a problem!\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:54.700\nTests help catch mistakes early and make sure your programs are reliable. They're a crucial part of building good software.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:04.800\nIn short, tests are a way to automatically verify your code works as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3d14ce84-d1e2-4d19-8122-d486c8d3edfa": {
    "id": "3d14ce84-d1e2-4d19-8122-d486c8d3edfa",
