    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_033651.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore the basics of a test.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:17.500\nThink of a test as a way to find out something, or to check if something works.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:33.600\nIt's basically a question or a series of questions designed to give us information. The main idea behind a test is to see if a specific condition is met.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:39.400\nFor example, a simple test could be \"Is this light bulb working?\"\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:43.600\nYou try to turn it on, and if it lights up, the test passes.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:47.800\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:52.000\nAnother example could be tasting a cookie.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:54.700\nIs it sweet?\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:58.000\nYou taste it, and that's your test!\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:04.500\nYour tastebuds tell you if it passes the \"sweetness\" test.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:14.700\nTests are everywhere, from checking your phone's battery to taking a quiz in school. They help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:14.700 --> 01:24.000\nSo, in short, a test is a way to gather information or check a condition.\n\n01:24.000 --> 01:33.500\nIt can be simple or complex, but the goal is always the same: to learn something.\n\n01:33.500 --> 01:36.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
