    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:21.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:25.900\nThat's a test! It helps you find out if the cake is ready.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:33.200\nTests aren't just for baking, though. They're used everywhere.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:37.900\nA doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:42.600\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:49.900\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:56.900\nIt can be as simple as checking the weather before you leave the house, or something more complicated. The key takeaway is that tests help us understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
