    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_033826.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, what they are, and why we use them.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:18.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You turn it on \u2013 that's the test \u2013 and if it lights up, you know it's good!\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:32.800\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. A quiz in school is a test.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:42.400\nYour doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Even trying a new recipe is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if you can make it!\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:53.200\nThe main point is that tests give us information. They help us learn and improve.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:56.800\nSo, whether it's a pop quiz or a science experiment, remember that tests are all about learning something new. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
