    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:17.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are baked enough. You do a test \u2013 you poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:32.800\nIf it comes out clean, the test passes, and the cookies are done!\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:39.400\nAnother example could be checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:51.800\nIf the light comes on, that's a successful test! So, basically, a test helps us figure out if something is good to go, or if it needs a little more work.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:55.300\nIt's a simple way to make sure things are doing what they\u2019re supposed to do.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:56.300\nNow you know the basics of what a test is!\n```"
