    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:03.300\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:04.700\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:06.300\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:10.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:14.000\nIt's a process, or a procedure, that gives us information about something we want to know.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:19.500\nThink about it like this: your doctor might give you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:23.500\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:24.800\nSee?\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:27.900\nDifferent tests, different things we're trying to find out.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:34.700\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it, to seeing if a new medicine works.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:39.800\nThe important thing is that a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:45.900\nSo, to recap: a test is a procedure that gives us information.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:49.000\nIt helps us learn, check, and understand things better.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
