    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_035411.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.600\nNow, you might think of tests as scary exams, but in reality, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:25.000\nIt's a process to see if something is true, or if something works.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:30.600\nThink of it like this: a chef tests a sauce to see if it needs more salt. That's a test!\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:33.200\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:35.800\nSee? Tests are everywhere.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:46.700\nSo, how does a test work? Well, usually you have something you want to know, and you perform an action or ask a question to get an answer.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:56.600\nThe answer tells you something about what you're testing. For example, you might test a lightbulb to see if it works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:04.000\nIf it lights up, the test is successful! In short, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:11.400\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:11.400 --> 01:13.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
