    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_040531.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:14.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in and flipping the switch.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:26.600\nIf it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:32.200\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.800\nYou might test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the center.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:41.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is likely ready.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:51.500\nThat's another kind of test! Tests are super important in lots of things, from building bridges to writing computer programs.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:57.200\nThey help us make sure things are reliable and do what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:05.900\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something. It helps us know if it's working, or if it's true.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:07.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
