    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:17.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you understand something, or how well something works.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:28.000\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb is good before you screw it in. The main point of a test is to gather information.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:35.200\nWe use tests to find out what we know, and maybe more importantly, what we don't know.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:42.400\nFor example, a spelling test shows you which words you can spell correctly and which you need to practice.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:54.400\nOr, a food taste test helps you decide which flavors you like best. Even checking if your bike tires have enough air is a kind of test! You're testing the tire pressure.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:00.900\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:03.700\nIt's all about learning and improving.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:06.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
