    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:04.200\nToday we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:05.900\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:08.600\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to check if something works,\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:10.300\nor to see what something is like.\n\n00:10.300 --> 00:12.900\nThink of it like this: When you bake a cake,\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:15.500\nyou might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:16.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:18.900\nOr, if you're trying out a new video game,\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:21.000\nyou're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:23.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:26.600\nScientists use tests to prove their theories,\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:29.600\ndoctors use tests to diagnose illnesses,\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:32.700\nand even you use tests every day to make decisions.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:36.400\nBasically, a test helps you learn something or confirm something you already suspect.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:40.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding out information.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.800\nIt's a simple concept with a lot of power!\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:46.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
