    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_042822.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:07.300\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:10.100\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:15.700\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if the light switch works.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:20.300\nThe test is flipping the switch.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:23.800\nIf the light turns on, the test is successful!\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:26.500\nYou know the switch works.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:30.600\nIf the light stays off, the test failed and something's wrong.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:37.000\nAnother example is baking a cake. Tasting the cake is a test to see if you followed the recipe correctly and if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:44.600\nTests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:47.400\nSo, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:52.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
