    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.300\nThink of a test as a way to see what you know or what something can do.\nIt's really just a way to gather information.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:21.500\nSo, how does it work?\nWell, you present something with a challenge, and then you observe the result.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:29.100\nIf you're testing a cake recipe, you bake the cake and then taste it to see if it's good.\nThat's your test!\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:33.500\nAnother example?\nImagine testing a new light bulb.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:38.200\nYou screw it in and see if it lights up.\nThat's a simple test.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:49.800\nOr, in school, your teacher gives you a test to see how much you've learned about a certain topic.\nBasically, a test is a method for checking something.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:59.700\nIt helps us understand if something works the way it should, or if someone understands a concept.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
