    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_043749.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nIt\u2019s how we find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:27.500\nThink of it like this: you might test the oven to see if it's hot enough to bake a cake.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:40.000\nOr, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy.\nIn school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:46.500\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:56.100\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, then there\u2019s a problem.\nSo, tests help us understand things and solve problems.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:02.100\nIn short, a test is a way to check if something works or is true.\nIt helps us learn and improve. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
