    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_043833.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:18.100\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to see if something works, or if someone knows something.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like checking to see if your lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.900\nThat's a test! Tests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:38.500\nYour teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a subject. Or, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and reliable.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:49.200\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might test it by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:57.100\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down a few times is a test of your balance and coordination.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:03.200\nSo, a test is simply a way to check something, learn something, or prove something.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:06.800\nIt helps us understand how things work and improve them.\n```"
  },
  "213c9366-d9b2-48cf-b3a9-bc3766f4af0f": {
