    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE\nAll timings are approximate\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much someone knows about something, or how well they can do something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, you know it passed the test!\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:29.700\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. A spelling quiz is a test.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:36.900\nSo is a driving exam. Even trying a new recipe is kind of a test to see if you can cook it well.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:46.400\nThe important thing is that a test gives you information. If you get a good grade on your spelling quiz, you know you're doing well with spelling.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:57.400\nIf you pass your driving exam, you know you're ready to drive safely. So, to recap, a test is a tool to measure knowledge or ability.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:04.700\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we need to learn. Tests are a part of learning and growing!\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
