    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_044424.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.400\nIt's a method for gathering information or checking if something is working correctly.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:33.500\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:43.600\nA taste test checks which food you like best. Or, if your car isn\u2019t starting, a mechanic might run a test to see what\u2019s wrong with the engine.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:56.200\nTests can be simple, like asking someone a question, or complex, like a scientific experiment. The important thing is that they help us learn something new or confirm what we already know.\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:00.700\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information or check if something is working.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:04.800\nIt's used everywhere, from school to science to your own everyday life!\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:06.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
