    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_044607.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:04.000\nToday we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:06.000\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:07.000\nThink of it like a measuring stick for your knowledge.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:09.000\nSo, how does it work?\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:13.000\nWell, a test usually has questions, and your answers show what you've learned.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:17.000\nThese questions can be multiple choice, true or false, short answer, or even asking you to solve a problem.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.000\nFor example, if you're learning about animals, a test might ask you \"What do cows eat?\"\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:23.000\nor \"Is a whale a fish?\"\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:24.000\nSee?\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:25.000\nSimple stuff!\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.000\nTests aren't meant to be scary. They're just a tool to help you and your teachers see where you're doing great and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:32.000\nThey show what you know!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to measure your knowledge.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:36.000\nDon't stress, just do your best!\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:39.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
