    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_044732.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:25.800\nBasically, a test helps us see if something does what it's supposed to do. It gives us information.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:30.200\nLet's say you're baking a cake. You test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:37.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a successful test.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:42.200\nOr maybe you're checking if your shoes fit. You try them on, walk around a bit, and see if they're comfortable.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:46.800\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:57.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information and check if something is working correctly or meeting your expectations.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:07.700\nIt's a simple process we use every day, even if we don't realize it. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
