    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_045545.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:21.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses tests to learn about your health, or a chef tastes food to test its flavor.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:32.100\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even just activities.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:39.100\nTests aren't meant to trick you; they're designed to show what you know and where you might need a little more help.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:48.100\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of how to spell words. A math test sees if you can solve problems.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:55.100\nSo, remember, tests are just tools to help us learn and grow. They give us information!\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:05.500\nTo recap, a test helps us learn about something, whether it's your spelling skills, your health, or even how good a cookie tastes.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:09.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
