    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_045824.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something, to check or examine something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:35.300\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life! For example, if you want to know if a cake is ready, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:46.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done!\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:55.000\nOr, maybe you're checking if your bike tires have enough air. You can squeeze them; if they feel firm, the test tells you they're inflated enough.\n\n00:55.000 --> 01:02.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding something out, a simple way to check or examine something. It helps us make decisions based on the information we get.\n```"
  },
