    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_045909.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: the test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:19.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:29.800\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, if a recipe tastes good, or even if you've learned something new.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:37.300\nThe main idea behind any test is to gather information.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:44.800\nWe want to see if something meets a certain standard or if it behaves the way we expect it to.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:53.200\nThink of it like this: you test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:01.600\nAnother example? A doctor might give you a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:09.100\nOr a teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:14.400\nIn each case, the test is providing valuable information.\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:29.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a method of checking something to gather information and see if it meets a certain standard.\n\n01:29.200 --> 01:35.600\nHopefully, that clears things up!\n\n01:35.600 --> 01:39.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
