    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:25.200\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard. Think of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:30.900\nThat's a simple test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.600\nOr, imagine checking your tire pressure before a long drive. That's a test to make sure your tires are safe.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:51.100\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal. Whether it's a doctor checking your temperature, or a software developer checking their code, tests help us make sure things are as they should be.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:59.900\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check something and see if it's working the way we expect.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:04.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
