    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T05:19:24.641174",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_051924.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_051924.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:04.300 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:07.800\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:19.000\nIt's a process where you ask a question, perform an action, or present a challenge, and then observe the result.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.600\nThink about it like this: a baking test!\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.700\nYou want to know if your cake is done. You poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:32.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a positive test \u2013 the cake is ready!\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:34.900\nIf it's gooey, well, the cake needs more time.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:40.400\nOr, imagine testing if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:44.800\nIf it lights up, great! The lightbulb passes the test.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:47.700\nIf not, it's probably time for a new one.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:55.000\nSo, tests help us understand things, confirm if something is working, or identify potential problems.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.800\nThey're all about gathering information through observation.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
