    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_052607.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:25.800\nThat's a test! If the light turns on, it passes the test.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.500\nAnother example? If you\u2019re baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:44.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done \u2013 it passes the \u201cis it cooked?\u201d test. Tests help us catch mistakes and make sure things are working correctly before we move on.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:53.100\nSo, a test is basically a simple question, and we're just looking for the right answer. That's the basics of testing!\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:57.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
