    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_053415.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey there, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: tests.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:18.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:23.200\nYou don\u2019t just guess, right? You test them! Maybe you poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:27.900\nThat toothpick is your test. If it comes out clean, the cookies pass the test and they're ready.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:34.300\nIf it\u2019s gooey, they fail and need more time. Tests aren\u2019t just for baking, of course.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:40.700\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Schools use tests to see what you\u2019ve learned.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:51.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for finding something out. It helps us confirm or deny something is true.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:55.300\nIt's a simple concept with tons of uses in everyday life!\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
