    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_053943.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something, to see if it works or is true.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test to see if the cake is done!\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:27.500\nAnother example? A doctor gives you an eye exam. That's a test to check your vision.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:33.900\nOr maybe you're trying to guess what's inside a wrapped present. Shaking it gently is a little test to give you a clue!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:40.700\nSo, tests help us learn things. They help us make sure things are working right, or figure out the answer to a question.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:54.100\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the basic idea is always the same: to check something.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
