    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_054925.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:22.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It could be checking if a lightbulb works, or if you understand a new concept.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like this: you're trying to find out if something is true or false, right or wrong, working or not working.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:34.900\nLet's look at some examples. A spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:45.400\nA doctor might run tests to check if you're healthy. Even baking a cake is a test! You're testing if your ingredients and instructions will result in a delicious cake.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:53.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us learn, diagnose problems, and see if we're on the right track.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:55.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
