    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_055059.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:24.400\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:32.700\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your knowledge of how to spell words.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:41.000\nA driving test checks your ability to safely operate a car. And a taste test checks your preference for different flavors!\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:51.200\nTests can come in many forms, like multiple choice questions, written essays, or even practical demonstrations.\n\n00:51.200 --> 01:02.200\nThe important thing is that they give us information. They help us understand what we know, what we can do, and sometimes, even what we like.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:12.200\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is a method for gathering information to assess something. It's a tool we use to learn and grow.\n\n01:12.200 --> 01:15.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
