    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_060954.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:14.000\nDon't worry, not the kind you cram for. In this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your flashlight has batteries. The test is, you press the button.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:27.500\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:32.000\nAnother simple example: you bake a cake. The test? You taste it!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:36.200\nIf it's delicious, the test passes.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:40.400\nIf it's burnt or undercooked, well, the test fails.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:54.300\nTests are used all the time, in all sorts of situations, to make sure things are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:06.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way of checking something. It either passes, meaning it works, or it fails, meaning it doesn't.\n\n01:06.800 --> 01:12.300\nEasy peasy! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
