    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.400\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something works correctly.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:29.300\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you need to test if the wheels spin. A test is simply a procedure designed to see if something meets a specific requirement, or if it performs as expected.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:41.900\nIt's like asking a question and then seeing if you get the right answer. For example, if you want to test if a light bulb works, you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:51.200\nIf it lights up, it passes the test! Or, if you're testing a recipe, you follow the steps and taste the result.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:54.100\nDoes it taste good? That's your test!\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:04.300\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check if something works the way it should. It's all about making sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
