    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_061536.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:22.900\nIt could be checking if a light bulb works, or if you've learned something new.\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you taste it.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:26.700\nThat's a test!\nYou're checking if it tastes good.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:31.100\nOr imagine you're trying to open a door.\nYou try your key.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:39.400\nIf it opens, the key passes the test!\nTests are super important because they help us learn and improve.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:49.200\nWhether it's a school test showing what you've learned, or a simple check to see if your bike tires are inflated, tests give us information.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:59.100\nThey tell us what works and what needs fixing.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and learn from the results.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
