    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_062013.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:16.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a method of gathering information to see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking. You perform a test!\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:30.400\nYou poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you the cake is ready. Or maybe you want to know if your friend knows the answer to a question.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:36.200\nYou ask them! That's a test, too.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:43.200\nTests can be simple, like tasting soup to see if it needs more salt. Or they can be more complex, like taking a quiz at school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:53.400\nThe key thing is that a test is a way to get information. So, remember, a test is just a method of finding something out.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
