    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_062714.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:19.700\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something. It could be about your knowledge, your skills, or even your health.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: you\u2019re trying to understand something better, and a test helps you get there.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:38.600\nSo, how does it work? Well, you're given a set of questions or tasks, and your answers or performance are evaluated.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:43.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:51.600\nA doctor might run a blood test to see if you\u2019re healthy. Let's say you have a math test.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:56.600\nIt asks you to solve problems. Your answers tell the teacher how well you understand math concepts.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:01.600\nOr, imagine you're testing a new recipe. You taste it to see if it's good!\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:06.000\nBasically, a test is a tool.\n\n01:06.000 --> 01:11.200\nIt helps us learn and understand things by measuring or evaluating something.\n\n01:11.200 --> 01:13.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
