    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_063253.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nAlright, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it as a question you're asking, but instead of just getting an answer,\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:30.900\nyou're gathering evidence. Tests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:37.300\nImagine you're baking a cake. You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:43.700\nIf it comes out clean, that's your evidence the cake is ready!\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:57.300\nOr, think about a doctor. They might run tests to figure out what's making you feel sick. So, a test is basically a way to gather information to answer a question.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:04.300\nIt can be as simple as checking if your cake is cooked, or as complicated as a medical diagnosis.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:11.300\nThe key is that you're trying to learn something new. Tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:11.300 --> 01:14.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
