  "03c533b0-1cdc-47bf-950d-5cc602c1f1e1": {
    "id": "03c533b0-1cdc-47bf-950d-5cc602c1f1e1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:51:43.937622",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T06:34:40.984464",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_063440.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_063440.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.300\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if you get the expected answer.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:21.600\nA really simple example?\nImagine you're testing if a light bulb works.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:26.500\nYou flip the switch.\nIf the light turns on, the test passes!\nIf it doesn\u2019t, it fails.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:32.800\nOr, let's say you're testing if a cookie is sweet.\nYou take a bite.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:37.600\nIf it tastes sweet, the test passes!\nIf it tastes salty, well, the test fails.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:46.600\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to verify something.\nIt\u2019s a question you ask to get an answer, and that answer tells you if things are as they should be.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:55.700\nThat's it for the basics of testing!\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
