    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_063816.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.350 --> 00:03.230\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.230 --> 00:06.540\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:06.540 --> 00:12.220\nIt could be anything from a quiz at school to checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:12.220 --> 00:14.430\nThe point is to gather information.\n\n00:14.430 --> 00:18.920\nBasically, you do something, like answer a question or flip a switch, and then you observe the result.\n\n00:18.920 --> 00:21.610\nThat result tells you something.\n\n00:21.610 --> 00:27.260\nFor example, a doctor gives you a blood test to find out if you're healthy.\n\n00:27.260 --> 00:33.040\nOr you might test a recipe by baking a small batch before making a huge cake.\n\n00:33.040 --> 00:35.480\nThese tests give us valuable information to make decisions.\n\n00:35.480 --> 00:39.570\nSo, remember, a test is a process of gathering information through observation.\n\n00:39.570 --> 00:44.540\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:44.540 --> 00:47.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
