    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_063956.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.000\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:25.000\nWe use tests all the time to check if things are working correctly,\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:35.100\nor to see what someone knows.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:47.100\nThink about it like this: a baking test. You taste a cake to test if it's sweet enough. Or maybe a car test, where you drive it around to test if it handles well. In school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:55.500\nSo, whether it's tasting a cake, driving a car, or answering questions in class, a test is simply a way to gather information and learn more.\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:59.100\nIt\u2019s all about checking things out and understanding them better. In short, a test is a method for finding something out!\n```"
  },
