    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_064403.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:20.300\nThink of a test as a way to check something. Whether it's checking if you understand a lesson, or checking if a machine is working correctly, tests help us find out information.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:27.900\nSo, how does it work? Basically, you give something a challenge, and then you see how it responds.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:39.500\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words. You're given the words, which are the challenge, and then your answers show what you know.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:46.300\nAnother example is a taste test! Chefs use taste tests to see if a dish tastes good.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:56.500\nThey try the food, that's the challenge, and then they decide if it needs more salt or pepper. Tests are everywhere and help us learn and improve.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:04.700\nThey give us valuable feedback. Remember, a test is just a way to check something and learn from the results.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
