    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T06:48:50.844988",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_064850.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_064850.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:11.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:22.900\nIt's a process designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:33.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:43.900\nA teacher gives you a test to see how well you've learned the material. Even baking a cake is kind of a test \u2013 you're testing your recipe and baking skills!\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:54.200\nSo, tests can come in many forms. They can be quizzes, exams, experiments, or even simple observations. The goal is always the same: to gather information and make an assessment.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:56.200\nIn short, a test helps us understand where we are\n\n00:56.200 --> 00:59.000\nand what we might need to improve on.\n\n00:59.000 --> 00:59.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
