    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_065022.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:22.100\nIt helps us measure or evaluate something. Think of it like this: you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:28.600\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:35.100\nTests come in many forms. Sometimes they're written, sometimes they're practical, like testing if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:53.200\nSo, whether it's checking your knowledge, your health, or the functionality of an object, a test helps us get information and understand something better.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:03.100\nTo recap, tests are tools we use to learn about something and measure its properties.\n\n01:03.100 --> 01:08.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "591c3253-7ab8-464f-98f3-55efa7851c5f": {
    "id": "591c3253-7ab8-464f-98f3-55efa7851c5f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:51:49.271059",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T06:51:00.583309",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_065100.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_065100.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nWell, simply put, a test is a way of finding out something about someone or something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it like an investigation.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:33.000\nWe use tests to check how well we've learned something, or to see if something works the way it should.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:39.600\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:47.200\nOr a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it's safe and effective. Even when you bake a cake, you\u2019re kind of testing the recipe!\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:50.700\nYou\u2019re checking if it tastes good. So, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n```"
  },
  "e25e4591-e75e-42e4-a68e-c4fdaf95fa9b": {
    "id": "e25e4591-e75e-42e4-a68e-c4fdaf95fa9b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:51:49.507067",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T06:51:46.792137",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_065146.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_065146.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:20.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nThink of it like an experiment.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:30.600\nWe ask a question or present a challenge, and then observe the result.\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:43.400\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nOr a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\nEven trying a new recipe is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if you like the way it tastes!\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:54.800\nThe key thing to remember is that tests help us learn and make decisions based on information.\nThey give us evidence to understand something better.\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:58.300\nSo, whether it's a science experiment or a spelling bee, a test is all about discovering the answer.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b2f69a69-d9d1-48d8-9719-822fce101541": {
    "id": "b2f69a69-d9d1-48d8-9719-822fce101541",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:51:49.779269",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T06:52:39.720702",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_065239.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_065239.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, it's a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:17.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:20.500\nYou poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:29.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. In school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:34.800\nA math test shows if you understand addition, subtraction, multiplication and division.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:40.100\nA spelling test shows if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:45.400\nHere's another example. A doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:49.600\nOr you might test a new toy to see if it works.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:55.000\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:57.000\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n00:57.000 --> 00:58.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```\nExplanation of Changes and Key Points:\n\n* **Timing is Critical:** I have meticulously followed the timing instructions for each section, ensuring the animations and wait times add up correctly.  The `self.wait()` calls are the most important part, ensuring the visuals stay on screen for the duration of the narration.\n* **Image addition:** I have included an ImageMobject. Remember to add a png file named 'cake.png' to your folder.\n* **Visual Design:** I've incorporated the specified colors, rounded rectangles, bullet points, and font sizes.\n* **Code Structure:** The code is organized into sections with comments indicating the timing for each.\n* **Subtitles:** The subtitle timings are synchronized with the narration.\n* **Slow Animations:**  Animations use `run_time` values between 1.0 and 2.0.\n* **Long Wait Times:** The `self.wait()` durations are all several seconds long.\n* **Fade Outs:** The fade outs between sections are quick (0.5 seconds) to minimize dead time.\n\nTo use this code:\n\n1.  **Install Manim:** `pip install manim`\n2.  **Save:** Save the code as a Python file (e.g., `test_explanation.py`).\n3.  **Add Image:** Add the cake.png file in the same directory.\n4.  **Render:** Run the following command in your terminal: `manim -pql test_explanation.py TestExplanation`\n\nThis will render the animation at a lower quality for faster processing.  For higher quality, use `-pqh` or `-pqk`."
  },
  "62576678-8e6a-4c6b-a446-c40bc5a7e005": {
    "id": "62576678-8e6a-4c6b-a446-c40bc5a7e005",
    "topic": "Test",
