    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_070503.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:17.800\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of exams at school.\nBut a test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like this: You might test if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\nOr, you might test if your bike brakes work before going down a big hill.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:39.600\nYou're checking to see if something is working as expected.\nTests are important because they help us find problems and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:53.400\nMaybe your cookie recipe needs a little tweaking, or maybe your bike brakes need some adjusting.\nSo, to recap, a test is a way of checking something to see if it's working the way it should.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:00.600\nIt helps us identify issues and improve things.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
