    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! \nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:18.600\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. \nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it. \nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:28.600\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something is working the way it should, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:36.200\nIt can be anything from checking if a lightbulb turns on, to seeing if you understand a new topic in school.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:46.800\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. \nOr, a website might run tests to make sure all its buttons are working correctly.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:49.800\nSee? Tests are all around us!\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:59.300\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to check something to see if it works or meets a standard. \nEasy, right?\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
