  "ad341e47-250c-49cf-a539-fa2fffe29053": {
    "id": "ad341e47-250c-49cf-a539-fa2fffe29053",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:51:55.037946",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T07:08:57.701235",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_070857.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_070857.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.300\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:25.600\nIn computer programming, tests are used to make sure our code is working correctly.\nWe give the code some input, and then we check if the output is what we expected.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:34.600\nFor example, if we have a function that adds two numbers, a test would check if 2 + 2 really equals 4.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:43.100\nOr, if we have a function that's supposed to capitalize a word, we'd test if \"hello\" becomes \"Hello\".\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:55.100\nIf the code doesn\u2019t give us the right answer, then we know there's a bug we need to fix.\nSo, tests are super important for writing reliable and bug-free software.\nThey help us catch problems early!\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
