    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:16.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\nIt's a procedure we use to gather information.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: you have a question, and a test is how you try to answer it.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:35.800\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might use a toothpick.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:51.100\nSticking the toothpick in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test.\nOr, if you're wondering if you know your alphabet, someone might ask you to recite it.\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:51.100 --> 01:06.200\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\nThe important thing is that they help us learn something new or confirm something we already suspected.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:18.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information and answer a question.\nThey can be simple or complex, but they all serve the same purpose: to help us understand something better.\n\n01:18.000 --> 01:21.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
