    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.300\nOkay, so you're wondering what a test is?\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:06.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:07.700\nIt's a method we use to gather information.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:12.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:14.900\nYou wouldn\u2019t just guess, right?\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:17.900\nYou'd probably poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:18.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:22.200\nAnother example: A doctor uses tests to figure out if you're healthy.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:26.800\nThey might check your temperature, or take a blood sample.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:28.400\nThese are all different kinds of tests.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:30.400\nTests aren't just in baking or medicine.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:31.300\nThey're everywhere!\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:36.100\nYou might take a test in school to see how well you understand a subject,\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:40.800\nor a company might test a new product to make sure it works.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:45.700\nBasically, any time you're trying to learn something by observing or experimenting,\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:47.500\nyou're performing a test.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:52.100\nSo, a test is a way of finding something out by gathering information.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
