    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_072703.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHi everyone, and welcome!\nToday we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.700\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like this: You have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good.\nYou screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:28.400\nThat's a test!\nIf it lights up, the test passed.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:33.900\nIf it doesn't, the test failed.\nAnother example: You bake a cake.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:42.200\nTo test if it's done, you poke it with a toothpick.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\nThat's another test!\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:52.600\nSo, in short, a test is just a procedure to see if something meets certain requirements or works as expected.\nIt\u2019s a way to get information and confirm things are okay.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:60.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
