    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.799\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.799 --> 00:16.599\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:16.599 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb is good. You screw it in, and if it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:33.700\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. You might take a quiz at school, which is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:44.400\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it has enough salt. Even your doctor uses tests, like checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:52.400\nSo, tests help us understand things better. They show us what we've learned, or if something is working correctly.\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:05.100\nIt's all about finding out information! In short, a test is a way to evaluate knowledge or performance.\n\n01:05.100 --> 01:08.700\nFrom school quizzes to checking lightbulbs, tests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:11.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
