    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_073426.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE\nAll timings are approximate.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHello everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:13.900\nToday we're going to explore something really fundamental: the test.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:25.900\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:35.400\nIt\u2019s a process of asking a question and then trying to answer it in a structured way.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:42.100\nThink of it like this: You might test a cake recipe by baking it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:48.800\nOr, you might test if a light bulb works by plugging it in.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:55.500\nIn both cases, you\u2019re performing an action to get an answer.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:02.200\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. The teacher is testing your knowledge of spelling.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:11.800\nThe test itself is the set of questions, and your answers show how well you understand the material.\n\n01:11.800 --> 01:18.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to gather information or prove something.\n\n01:18.800 --> 01:24.700\nIt involves a question, an action, and an answer.\n\n01:24.700 --> 01:29.400\nHopefully, this gives you a clearer idea of what a test is all about.\n\n01:29.400 --> 01:33.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
