    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_073510.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:13.600\nWhat is a test, anyway?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:32.800\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on to test if that fixes the problem.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:41.800\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if the water is warm enough for a bath.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:54.100\nThe key is that you're trying to learn something by doing something.\nSo, a test helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something needs to be changed.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:59.800\nThat's the basics of testing!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
