    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:52:05.387960",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T07:42:33.823208",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_074233.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_074233.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.100\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:18.100\nThink about it. A doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:25.700\nOr a teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned in class. Even baking a cake is a kind of test!\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:38.300\nYou're testing the recipe to see if it turns out delicious. So, a test can be anything from a written exam to a science experiment, or even just trying something out.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:52.800\nThe main idea is to gather information and see the result. Whether it's finding out if you need glasses, or if your cookies are perfectly baked, tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:57.800\nIn short, a test is just a way to learn and discover.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:00.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "fbe410f9-8409-41c2-874c-c6b8d4628c15": {
    "id": "fbe410f9-8409-41c2-874c-c6b8d4628c15",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:52:05.600674",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T07:43:27.044758",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_074326.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_074326.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:66.0\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:16.300\nNow, a test is basically a way to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb lights up when you flip the switch. That's a simple test!\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:33.800\nIn science, tests are called experiments. Scientists use them to learn new things. For example, if you want to know if a plant needs sunlight to grow, you could put one plant in the sun and one in the dark.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:40.500\nThen, you see which one grows better. That's a test to see if sunlight helps plants grow.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:51.900\nAnother example is a taste test! If you're trying to decide which cookie recipe is best, you can have your friends taste both and tell you which one they like more. That's a test too!\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:58.900\nSo, a test is just a way to find out information by trying something out and observing what happens.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:03.900\nSimple as that!\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:06.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
