    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:23.100\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:35.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a spelling test to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:44.100\nA test can be anything from answering questions on paper to trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:53.900\nFor example, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:00.300\nOr, if you want to know if your cookie recipe is good, you bake the cookies and taste them. That's a test too!\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:07.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something. It helps us learn, understand, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:10.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
