    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:08.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:08.400 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:17.000\nThink of it like a question you ask to get an answer.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.500\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:27.200\nMaybe you're testing a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:33.700\nOr perhaps a scientist is testing a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:39.000\nHere's a simple example: You might test if a toy car rolls faster on a smooth floor or a carpet.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:42.800\nYou're \"testing\" which surface allows the car to go faster.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:49.000\nSo, to recap, a test is just a way to ask a question and get an answer by trying something out.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:52.200\nIt\u2019s a way to learn and discover new things!\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:52.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
