    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_074940.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:05.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:07.200\n\u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:11.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:13.600\nor how well you can do something.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:17.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:20.100\nYou plug it in \u2013 that's the test \u2013\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:20.900\nand see if it lights up.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:23.600\nTests come in all shapes and sizes!\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:25.600\nA pop quiz in school is a test.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:28.400\nA doctor checking your reflexes is a test.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:32.400\nEven trying a new recipe to see if it tastes good is a kind of test!\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:36.200\nFor example, if you want to know if you can ride a bike,\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:38.000\nyou try to ride it!\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:38.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:43.000\nOr, if you want to know if you remember the alphabet, someone might ask you to say it.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:43.900\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:48.600\nSo, tests help us understand what we know and what we need to learn.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.300\nThey show us where we're doing great and where we can improve.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:55.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
