    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:17.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like a detective, gathering clues to figure something out.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:36.400\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\nMaybe you're testing a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\nOr perhaps a doctor is running tests to figure out what's making you feel unwell.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:44.700\nIn programming, we use tests to make sure our code does what we expect it to do.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:51.700\nFor example, if you write a program to add two numbers, you can test it by giving it the numbers 2 and 2.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:58.700\nIf it gives you 4, then your test passes!\nIf it gives you something else, then there's a problem.\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:05.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is working or true.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:08.900\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n01:08.900 --> 01:12.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
