    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_075530.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:03.000\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:04.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:06.600\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:09.400\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:13.800\nFor example, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:18.000\nOr a doctor might run tests to find out what's making you feel sick.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:23.100\nImagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might taste the batter before you bake it.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:25.800\nThat's a mini-test! It helps you see if you need more sugar.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:32.300\nOr, before launching a rocket, engineers run lots of tests to make sure everything is safe and sound.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:37.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of gathering information and checking things out.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:41.200\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:42.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
