    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_075615.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true.\nBut in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to check if something is working the way it should, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes their soup to test if it needs more salt.\nOr a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever.\nWe're checking something!\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:33.500\nSo, a test involves some kind of action or observation, followed by a result.\nFor example, a car mechanic might test the brakes of a car.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:44.900\nThe action is applying the brakes, and the result is seeing if the car stops safely.\nIf it does, the brakes pass the test!\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:54.500\nBasically, tests help us understand things and make sure everything is running smoothly.\nIn a nutshell, testing is all about checking and confirming.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:02.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
