    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_080333.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if someone knows something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:33.100\nA taste test helps us decide if we like a new flavor. Even a simple battery test can tell us if a battery still has power.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:46.700\nSo, tests come in many forms. They can be written, like school exams, or physical, like testing how high you can jump.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:55.400\nThe goal is always the same: to gather information and learn something new. Basically, a test is just a way of asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand the world a little better.\n\n00:55.400 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
