    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_080753.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:14.000\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:24.100\nIt helps us find out if something works, or if it's true. Think of it like this: you might test a new lightbulb to see if it lights up.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:29.900\nThat's a test! Or maybe you taste a new cookie recipe to see if it's delicious.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:34.700\nAnother test! Tests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:42.800\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. Your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:51.800\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct. Really, anything you do to check something can be considered a test.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:62.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is working or true. It helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:62.500 --> 00:66.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
