    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_081720.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.000\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\nThink of it like this: you're testing if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\nIf it comes out clean, that's your \"yes\" answer, the cookies are ready!\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.400\nOr, maybe you're testing if your plant needs water.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:38.600\nYou stick your finger in the soil.\nIf it feels dry, that's your test telling you it's time to water it.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:47.900\nTests help us understand things better.\nThey can be simple, like checking the weather outside to see if you need a coat, or more complex, like a school exam.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:57.200\nThe main idea is always the same: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:01.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find things out.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:05.700\nIt\u2019s a question, and the answer helps us understand the world around us.\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:07.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
