    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.200\nIt's a procedure we use to gather information or evaluate something. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to find out if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:30.200\nOr, you take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a subject. Those are both tests!\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:38.900\nThey help us understand something better. For example, you might test the water in a pool to see if it's safe to swim in.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:51.900\nOr, you could test a new recipe to see if it tastes good. Tests can be formal, like a big exam, or informal, like trying out a new flavor of ice cream.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:04.300\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to learn something new or check the quality of something. It helps us make informed decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
