    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:11.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:19.700\nThink of it like a detective collecting clues.\nIt helps us understand something better, whether it's your knowledge on a subject, or even how well a new product works.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:27.500\nSo, how does it work? Well, a test usually involves asking questions or presenting challenges.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:36.500\nFor example, a spelling test checks your spelling skills, while a taste test helps decide which snack is tastier.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:50.600\nThe answers or results we get are then used to make a judgment or decision.\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like trying out a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n00:50.600 --> 01:02.000\nThe important thing is that they give us data to learn from.\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool for gathering information and making smarter choices.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:05.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
