    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_083234.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.500\nThink of a test as a way to check something. It's like giving something a grade or seeing if it works the way it should.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:24.400\nTests can be anything from a simple true or false question, to a longer exam, or even checking if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:37.000\nThe main idea is to see if something meets a certain standard or passes a specific requirement. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:43.200\nA taste test checks if food tastes good. And a medical test checks if you're healthy.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:55.700\nSo, to recap, a test is just a way to evaluate something and see if it meets the mark. It helps us understand what's working well and what might need some improvement.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:59.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
