    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_083403.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:18.000\nA test is simply a way to find out how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.700\nThink of it like checking to see if you\u2019ve baked a cake correctly.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:35.800\nYou might poke it with a fork to see if it\u2019s done. That\u2019s a test! In school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned. They can be written, like a quiz, or practical, like showing you can play a song on an instrument.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:42.300\nImagine you're learning to ride a bike. The test is whether you can actually ride it without falling!\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:49.700\nSo, tests are just ways of checking progress and understanding. They help us learn and improve.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:53.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a3686903-1595-4126-8ae6-79c77c12cc91": {
    "id": "a3686903-1595-4126-8ae6-79c77c12cc91",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T01:52:19.500996",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T08:35:12.141211",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_083512.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_083512.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.100\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:29.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. Tests can be used to check if something works, like testing a new toy to see if it lights up.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:41.500\nOr, they can measure how much of something there is, like testing how much sugar is in your juice.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:48.100\nWe even use tests to see how well we understand things, like the quizzes you take in school.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:56.900\nFor example, a doctor might test your temperature to see if you have a fever. Or, a baker might test a cake with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:08.900\nSee? Tests are everywhere! So, to recap, a test helps us learn more about something by giving us information.\n\n01:08.900 --> 01:18.800\nIt\u2019s a way of asking a question and getting an answer, whether it's about how well something works, how much of something there is, or how well we understand something.\n```"
  },
