    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_090418.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:09.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:10.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:14.300\nIt helps us figure out if something is working as it should, or if it's true.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:18.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:23.400\nOr, a teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:27.000\nTests aren't just for people, though!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:28.300\nWe test all sorts of things.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.000\nFor example, engineers test bridges to make sure they can hold a lot of weight.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:40.000\nAnd scientists test new medicines to see if they're safe and effective.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:44.300\nSo, tests are important because they give us information.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:48.100\nThey help us make better decisions and keep things safe.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:52.400\nRemember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:56.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
