    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_091608.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.300\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:12.000\nWhat are they, and why do we even use them? Simply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:22.000\nIt\u2019s a process designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is ready.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:30.000\nYou perform a simple test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:36.000\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. You might take a little test ride around the block.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:47.000\nIf you can do it without falling, you've passed the test of basic bike riding. So, tests help us measure things and see how well we're doing.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:59.000\nWhether it's a school exam, a recipe check, or a skill assessment, tests are a valuable tool for learning and progress.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
