    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_092250.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:26.800\nIt's a process designed to get information about a person, a thing, or even an idea. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a physical exam \u2013 that's a test to see how healthy you are.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:36.500\nOr, when you bake a cake and taste it, that's a test to see if it's good! We use tests all the time to learn and understand.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:43.800\nAnother example is when you take a quiz in school. It tests how well you understand the material.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:56.000\nOr, if you try a new recipe, you're testing to see if you like the taste. Basically, anything where you're trying to get information or prove something is a test.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:08.700\nSo, to recap: a test is a method for gathering information. From medical exams to baking experiments, tests help us learn and make decisions.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:12.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
