    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_092557.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:18.300\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:26.800\nIt's a process of asking a question and then seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:30.000\nThink of it like this:\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:33.200\nIf you want to know if your cake is done, you do a test.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:35.000\nYou stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:43.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test result \u2013 the cake is ready!\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:46.400\nAnother example? A spelling test!\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:49.600\nIt checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:51.700\nEach word is a question, and your spelling is the answer.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:54.600\nTests are everywhere, helping us learn, improve, and understand things better.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:56.000\nThey give us information.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:57.400\nThey help us make decisions.\n```"
  },
  "af2cd114-8b82-4aeb-93c2-1f184eaf7b3c": {
