    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_092639.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.100\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" before, but what does it really mean?\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:21.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:34.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready. You stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:46.000\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a toy car needs new batteries. You turn it on.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:57.600\nIf it doesn't move, the test tells you the batteries are probably dead. Tests help us understand things better and make decisions based on evidence. So, a test is basically a way of checking something to see if it's working correctly or if something is true. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
