    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_094042.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:12.100\nWhat are they and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.100 --> 01:17.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to see what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like this: your mom might \"test\" if you've cleaned your room by looking around.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:27.000\nOr a doctor might give you a quick test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:35.900\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned in class.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:40.500\nThey can be written tests with questions to answer, or they can be practical, like showing you know how to solve a problem.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:47.300\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:54.200\nAnd a math test shows if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:02.600\nTests are a tool to help you and your teachers see how you're doing, and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n01:02.600 --> 01:10.300\nSo, a test is just a way to check knowledge or skills.\n\n01:10.300 --> 01:13.100\nThey come in many forms and help us learn and grow.\n\n01:13.100 --> 01:16.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
