    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_094212.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but a \"test\" in a broader sense is really just a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:28.400\nIt's like asking, \"Does this do what it's supposed to do?\" Think about it. If you build a birdhouse, you might \"test\" it by watching to see if birds actually move in.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:42.700\nOr, if you're trying out a new recipe, the \"test\" is whether it tastes good. Even something simple, like pressing a light switch to see if the light turns on, that's a test!\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:52.700\nSo, a test is simply a way of confirming that something is functioning correctly. We set up the right conditions and then observe the result.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:59.800\nThat observation, that's the key! Testing helps us identify problems and improve things.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:06.600\nRemember to always question, observe, and test. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
