    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_094857.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand more.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:33.600\nThe main idea behind a test is to see if something meets a certain standard or works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:41.400\nFor example, a simple spelling test checks if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:49.200\nOr, think about taste-testing food! You're testing if you like the flavor.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:56.800\nEven a doctor checking your temperature is doing a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:04.300\nSo, in short, a test is a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:10.400\nIt can be as simple as tasting a cookie or as complicated as a science experiment.\n\n01:10.400 --> 01:14.100\nThe goal is always the same: to find something out.\n\n01:14.100 --> 01:19.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
