    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_095222.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:20.400\nA test is basically a way to see how much you know about something, or how well something works. Think of it like checking if you understand a lesson in school, or making sure a new toy does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:32.300\nSo, how does it work? Well, you're given a set of questions or tasks, and your answers or performance are then compared to a standard or expected result.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:41.400\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you can spell words correctly.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:47.800\nOr, imagine you're testing a new recipe. You follow the instructions, and then you taste it to see if it tastes good. That's a test!\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:54.600\nTests help us learn and improve. They show us what we know well, and what we need to work on.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:01.600\nSo next time you hear the word \"test,\" don't be scared! It's just a way to learn and grow.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
