    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T09:56:50.878117",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_095650.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_095650.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:16.100\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.100\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:37.900\nThink about it this way: a doctor gives you a check-up to test your health. Or, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:49.000\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned. These tests can be simple, like checking if a light switch works by flipping it on and off.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:59.900\nOr they can be more complex, like a science experiment. The important thing is that a test helps us learn something new or confirm what we already know.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information.\n```"
  },
