    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_100115.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.600\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something. We use tests all the time to check if something is working correctly,\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:28.300\nor to see how much we know about a subject. Think of it like this: you might test a new toy to see if it needs batteries.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:40.100\nOr, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. In school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:45.500\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:55.600\nIf it does, the test is a success! If not, something's wrong. So, a test is really just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:59.200\nIt helps us understand the world around us a little bit better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "72939ec3-2e16-4a0f-af67-ee062e7f3ef1": {
    "id": "72939ec3-2e16-4a0f-af67-ee062e7f3ef1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:45:52.665447",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T10:02:51.435513",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_100251.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_100251.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.800\nNot the kind you take in school, but tests in the world of computers and software.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:24.300\nBasically, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:32.800\nThink of it like checking if your car starts before you drive it. We want to make sure everything is running smoothly.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:41.400\nFor example, let's say you built a simple calculator. A test could be checking if 2 plus 2 actually equals 4.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:52.000\nOr, if you have a website, a test could be making sure that when someone clicks a button, the right page shows up.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:58.800\nTesting helps us find problems early, before they cause bigger issues down the road.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:01.800\nIt's like fixing a small leak before it floods the whole house.\n```"
  },
