  "ffa40e8d-67be-4dd5-9950-7fb7025c40e6": {
    "id": "ffa40e8d-67be-4dd5-9950-7fb7025c40e6",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:45:54.078884",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T10:05:16.189674",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_100516.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_100516.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests, and no, not the kind you worry about in school.\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:23.500\nIn the world of programming, a test is simply a way to check if your code is working correctly.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:34.700\nThink of it like this: You build a toy car, and you want to make sure it moves forward when you push it.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:43.100\nThat push is your test! In programming, we write little bits of code that automatically check if other parts of our code are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:49.700\nFor example, if you have a function that adds two numbers, a test would check if it actually adds them correctly.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:56.300\nSo, if you give it 2 and 3, does it give you 5? That's what the test verifies.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:02.700\nTesting helps us find mistakes early on, so we can fix them before they cause bigger problems later.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:09.100\nIt\u2019s a super important part of building reliable software.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:12.800\nSo, remember, tests are your friend!\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:17.800\nThey help you make sure your code works like it should.\n\n01:17.800 --> 01:21.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
