    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to explore something super important: a test!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:10.000\nNow, a test is basically a way to check or measure something.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:12.500\nThink of it like this: it's a way to find out how well you know something,\n00:12.500 --> 00:16.000\nor how well something works.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:18.500\nSo, what kind of things can we test?\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:22.500\nWell, think about a spelling test in school.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:24.500\nThat checks how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:28.500\nOr, imagine testing a new toy to see if it's strong enough to handle being played with.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:34.000\nAnother example could be testing the temperature of your bathwater to make sure it's just right.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:37.000\nYou're testing to see if it's too hot or too cold!\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:44.000\nBasically, a test helps us understand something better by giving us information or results.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:49.000\nIt helps us know if something is good, bad, correct, or incorrect.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:50.500\nThat\u2019s it!\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:53.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
