    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_101619.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:17.200\nThink of it like a question you ask to get an answer. We use tests all the time!\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:24.300\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might taste the batter \u2013 that\u2019s a test to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:32.600\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a light bulb is broken, you might try turning it on. That's a test too!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:45.900\nTests can be formal, like the ones you take in school, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit. The important thing is that they help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:45.900 --> 01:00.000\nThey help us confirm if something works, if something is true, or if something needs to be changed. So, remember, a test is just a way of asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:06.600\nIt's a tool for learning and problem-solving! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
