    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nThink of a test as just a way to check something.\nWe want to know if something works, or if something is true, so we put it to the test!\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:21.600\nFor example, imagine you bake a cake.\nThe test is whether it tastes good!\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:28.000\nYou try a slice, and that\u2019s your test.\nOr, let's say you're trying out a new lightbulb.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:34.200\nThe test is simple: does it turn on?\nIf it does, it passes the test!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:49.800\nTests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb works, or more complicated, like a math exam.\nBut the basic idea is always the same: we're trying to find out something by observing the result.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:56.800\nSo, a test helps us confirm or deny something.\nThat\u2019s the basics of what a test is.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:00.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
