    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:58.5\n1\n00:00.215 --> 00:04.365\nHey there, welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n2\n00:04.365 --> 00:16.065\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\nIt's a process we use to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well something is done.\n\n3\n00:16.065 --> 00:27.265\nThink about it like this: a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\nOr, your doctor gives you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n4\n00:27.265 --> 00:31.765\nAnother example?\nImagine you build a paper airplane.\n\n5\n00:31.765 --> 00:36.665\nYou throw it to test if it flies straight.\nIf it does, great!\n\n6\n00:36.665 --> 00:48.165\nIf not, you adjust it and test again.\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is an action, a procedure, that helps us evaluate something.\n\n7\n00:48.165 --> 00:58.500\nIt helps us understand, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
