    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:46:17.783723",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T10:35:30.386839",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_103530.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_103530.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:07.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.500\nIt\u2019s a question or a procedure designed to give us information.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:18.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:23.100\nYou perform a test \u2013 sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:27.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you the cake is ready!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:30.700\nAnother example: a spelling test.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:34.500\nIt checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:40.200\nOr a medical test, which helps doctors figure out what's going on with your health.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:48.200\nBasically, a test helps us understand something better, whether it's baking, spelling, or health.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:52.300\nThey provide information we can use to make decisions.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:55.800\nSo, a test is just a tool for gathering information.\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:57.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b9227ea8-b838-4084-8f5c-7d913c0f597d": {
