    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_104448.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.800\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:34.200\nOr, a chef might taste a dish to test if it needs more salt. In school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:43.700\nHere's another example: You might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:53.200\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If not, the lightbulb probably needs to be replaced.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:02.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us make sure things are working, or that we understand something correctly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
