    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_110330.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:25.700\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:38.500\nOr, if you press a light switch, you're testing if the light will turn on.\nIt's all about checking something to see if it works as expected, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:45.200\nImagine you're testing a toy car to see if it goes forward when you push the button.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:56.900\nSo, tests help us learn, explore, and make sure things are working properly.\nThey're a fundamental part of how we understand the world around us.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
