    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_110834.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:26.400\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: you might test the batteries in your remote to see if they're still good.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:32.800\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:33.800\nSee?\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:36.300\nIt\u2019s all about checking something out!\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:47.200\nSo, a test can involve checking if something works, figuring out how well something is doing, or even just seeing what something is made of.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:50.900\nIt\u2019s a really common way we learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:50.900 --> 00:54.900\nIn a nutshell, a test is a procedure used to evaluate something.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:01.800\nWe use tests all the time, big and small, to help us make decisions and learn new things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
