    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like this: you might test a new lightbulb to make sure it turns on.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:34.900\nOr your teacher might give you a quiz to test what you've learned in class.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:44.000\nTests can come in many forms. It could be a multiple-choice quiz, a practical demonstration, or even just observing how something behaves.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:58.400\nFor example, a doctor might test your reflexes by tapping your knee. This helps them see if your nerves are working properly.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:03.900\nSo, in short, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate performance, functionality, or knowledge.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:07.000\nIt's all about checking things out and making sure everything is as it should be.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:10.800\nHopefully, this gives you a basic understanding of what a test is!\n\n01:10.800 --> 01:12.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
