    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_111352.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nOkay, so what is a test?\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:18.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it as a question you ask to get an answer.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:33.200\nIt could be a quiz at school, a taste test for new ice cream, or even checking if your phone is working properly.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:39.300\nYou're trying to learn something by observing the outcome.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:45.400\nLet's say you're baking cookies.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:51.700\nYou test if they're done by poking them with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies pass the test!\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:55.400\nThat means they're ready to eat.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:01.600\nAnother example is checking if a light bulb works.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.500\nYou screw it in, and if it lights up, it passes the test, and you know it's good.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:12.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information.\n\n01:12.500 --> 01:17.400\nYou ask a question, perform an action, and see what happens.\n\n01:17.400 --> 01:19.700\nThat's testing in a nutshell!\n\n01:19.700 --> 01:23.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
