    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_112053.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:20.100\nIt's how we find out if something works, if something is true, or if something meets certain standards.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:31.100\nThink about it like this: you test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough. Or, a doctor might test your vision to see how well you can see.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:45.100\nA test can be a simple question, a hands-on experiment, or even a big exam in school. For example, a simple test could be asking \"Is the sky blue?\".\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:52.300\nThe answer, which we know is \"yes\", tells us something about the world. Another example?\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:59.500\nChecking if a lightbulb works by turning it on. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:11.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a method we use to evaluate something. It helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as expected.\n\n01:11.600 --> 01:15.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
