    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, in simple terms, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.600\nIt's like asking a question and then checking the answer. Think of it like checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:28.000\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test \u2013 and see if it lights up. If it does, the test passes!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.400\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste a little bit of the batter before you bake it.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:48.800\nThat's a test to see if you added enough sugar. Tests can be written, like a school quiz, or they can be practical, like that light bulb example.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:58.300\nBasically, a test helps you understand something better by giving you some information or feedback.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:01.900\nIt's a quick way to check if something is working or correct.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:05.500\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of finding things out.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:08.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
