    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_112501.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_112501.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:19.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a more formal way.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:24.600\nWe use tests to see what we know, what we can do, or even how something works.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:31.400\nImagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might taste the batter \u2013 that\u2019s a test!\nYou're testing if it tastes good before you bake the whole thing.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:38.200\nOr think about a spelling test at school.\nThat's testing your knowledge of how to spell words.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:45.600\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\nEngineers test bridges to make sure they're strong.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:56.400\nSo, tests are all about gathering information.\nThey help us make decisions, improve things, and learn more about the world around us.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b9e025d2-828e-4cc4-99d5-7a5ebc5312ac": {
    "id": "b9e025d2-828e-4cc4-99d5-7a5ebc5312ac",
