    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_112728.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a fundamental concept: Tests.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a method we use to gather information and see if something is true or works as expected.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:27.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:31.100\nOr, maybe you take a quiz in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:37.700\nBoth of these are tests! Another example?\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:45.500\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:52.500\nThat's a test too! So, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and check something.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:58.600\nWhether it's checking your health, your knowledge, or even if your cake is ready, tests help us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c62616e0-4d2a-4cb5-878a-f2658e34eeec": {
    "id": "c62616e0-4d2a-4cb5-878a-f2658e34eeec",
    "topic": "Test",
