    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_112915.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:24.700\nIt's a process to check if something is true, or to see how well something works. Think of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:36.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, a doctor might test your reflexes to see if your nervous system is working properly.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:46.200\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a lightbulb works to seeing how well you understand a new subject in school.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:56.500\nThey help us learn and make sure things are working as expected. So, a test is just a procedure designed to get an answer or assess performance.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:00.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
