    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_113004.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:24.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but really, a test is just a way to see if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: you want to bake a cake, right?\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:30.400\nThe test is tasting a little bit of the batter before you bake it.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:34.200\nDoes it taste good? Is it sweet enough?\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:37.800\nYou're testing the batter to make sure the final cake will be delicious.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:42.600\nAnother example could be checking if your bike brakes are working.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:45.000\nYou give them a squeeze before you ride, right?\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:46.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:50.600\nYou're testing to see if they'll stop you safely.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:55.200\nSo, a test is basically checking something to see if it's working as expected.\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:57.400\nIt helps us catch problems early and make sure things are right.\n\n00:57.400 --> 00:58.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
