    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:47:00.023809",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T11:38:28.670730",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_113828.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_113828.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:07.600\n\u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about someone or something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:18.000\nIt\u2019s like asking a question, but often with a specific method to measure the answer.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.700\nThink about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz to test what you've learned in class.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:28.500\nOr, a doctor might order a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:32.300\nEven a taste test of different ice cream flavors is a kind of test!\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:36.500\nTests help us understand things better.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:44.500\nThey give us information we can use to make decisions, whether it's figuring out what you need to study more, understanding your health, or just picking the best ice cream.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:52.600\nSo, remember, a test is a way to gather information in a structured way.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:56.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e71d34ff-d11a-4cb4-a4e5-68bfb5539d1a": {
