    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_114959.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:15.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:18.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:28.800\nYou do a test! You poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test result showing the cake is ready.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:34.300\nOr maybe you want to know if you understand a new concept.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:41.200\nYou might take a quiz. That quiz is a test to see how well you've learned.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:48.100\nTests aren't just for school or baking, though. A doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:55.300\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct. Really, any time you're trying to learn or confirm something, you're probably using a test of some kind.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:62.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method to gain information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
