    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_115509.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It\u2019s how we check if something is working, true, or correct.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:28.700\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done!\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:42.300\nTests can be big, like an exam in school, or small, like trying a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:49.100\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas about the world are right. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:54.300\nWe even test things every day without realizing it.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:01.600\nDid you check the weather before deciding what to wear? That was a mini-test!\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:07.600\nSo remember, a test is just a method for gathering information and making sure things are as they should be. They help us learn and improve. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
