    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:08.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:11.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:16.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:21.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:27.000\nFor example, when you flip a light switch, you're testing to see if the lightbulb works.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:36.300\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:40.100\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:41.800\nThe cake passes the test!\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:47.200\nSo, tests help us confirm things, check if something works, or even just learn more about the world around us.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:53.600\nThey're a fundamental part of learning and problem-solving. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
