    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_120244.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:28.700\nIn everyday life, you're constantly doing little tests.\nLike, if you press the light switch and the light turns on, that's a test that shows the light bulb is working.\nOr if you bake a cake and it tastes good, that's a test that shows you followed the recipe correctly.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:35.600\nAnother example is a doctor checking your temperature.\nThat's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:42.100\nTests can be simple, like checking if your shoes are tied, or more complicated, like a science experiment.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:50.800\nBut the goal is always the same: to find out something specific.\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it's right or working as expected.\n\n00:50.800 --> 01:03.800\nTests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:11.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
