    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T12:16:54.914179",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_121654.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_121654.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHi everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:06.700\nNow, what is a test?\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:10.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:15.000\nIt helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:17.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:20.500\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:21.800\nSee?\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:22.700\nLots of things can be tested!\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:26.500\nFor example, you could test if a lightbulb works by plugging it in.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:29.500\nIf it lights up, the test is positive \u2013 the bulb works!\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:32.500\nIf it doesn't, the test is negative \u2013 the bulb is broken.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:38.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something and find out information.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:40.500\nIt\u2019s all about finding answers!\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:42.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
