    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_122007.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_122007.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:22.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a process we use to gather information about something, whether it's your knowledge, a product's quality, or even the strength of a material.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:32.600\nThink of it like this: a spelling test shows how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:42.500\nA taste test helps you decide which ice cream flavor you like best.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:52.300\nOr, engineers might test a bridge to make sure it can handle heavy traffic.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:04.300\nSo, a test isn\u2019t just something you take in school. It\u2019s really any method used to learn more about a particular subject.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:08.700\nWe use tests every day, often without even realizing it!\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:14.400\nFrom checking if your oven is hot enough, to seeing if your shoes fit, you're performing a test.\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:18.000\nIn short, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n01:18.000 --> 01:21.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "da8b194b-d768-4ce8-b57f-bbc8cd42d7b8": {
