    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_122104.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.400\nIt could be testing if a light bulb works by turning it on.\nThe test: turning it on.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:26.800\nThe answer: does it light up?\nOr maybe you're tasting a new cookie to see if you like it.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:33.300\nThe test: eating the cookie.\nThe answer: delicious, or maybe not so much!\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:50.200\nTests can be simple, like those examples, or much more complex, like a medical test or a math exam.\nBut the basic idea is always the same: we're trying to learn something by doing something and observing the result.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:59.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find things out.\nWe ask a question, and then we look for the answer!\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
