    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_122545.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.900\nNow, a test is just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but often on a smaller scale.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:23.900\nWe use tests all the time to see if something works, or to check if something is true.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:31.000\nSo, what do we test? Well, lots of things!\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:41.100\nFor example, you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good. Or, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:51.200\nEven a simple \"yes\" or \"no\" question is a type of test. The key is that we're gathering information to make a decision or understand something better.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.600\nLet's say you're trying to figure out if a plant needs more water. You might test the soil by sticking your finger in it.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:08.800\nIf it feels dry, that's a test telling you it needs water! In short, a test is a way to get information and learn something new.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:12.400\nIt's a simple but powerful tool we use every day.\n\n01:12.400 --> 01:16.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
