    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_123353.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:07.600\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:12.100\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:17.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might use a toothpick.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:22.600\nSticking the toothpick in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:26.900\nAnother example?\nA doctor might give you a hearing test\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:31.500\nto see how well you can hear different sounds.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:35.600\nOr your teacher might give you a quiz\nto see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:42.200\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and checking things.\nThey help us make decisions\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:47.000\nand understand the world around us a little bit better.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:49.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
