    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_123459.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:16.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something works correctly, or if you understand something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it like a quick check-up.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:29.200\nThe main idea is to see if the result matches what you expect.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:43.600\nWe do this all the time! For instance, you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in.\nDoes it light up? Great, it passed the test!\nOr, if you\u2019re learning addition, a test might be a simple question like, \"What's 2 plus 2?\"\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:55.800\nIf you answer correctly, you passed that mini-test! So, tests help us confirm things and learn from any mistakes.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:03.000\nThey're everywhere, from checking if your food tastes good to ensuring a rocket can launch safely.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:05.800\nRemember, tests are valuable tools for learning and improvement.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:08.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
