    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_124436.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.600\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:26.800\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. Think of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by screwing it in and turning it on.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:29.700\nDoes it light up? That's the test!\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:40.200\nOr, if you want to know if a cake is done, you poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:49.200\nSo, a test is simply a procedure to see if something meets a certain standard, or to check if it works the way it should.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:58.200\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it! Remember, a test helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:01.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
