    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_125013.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something. Think of it like this: it's a way to check your understanding.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:22.900\nTests come in many forms. You might have a multiple-choice test, where you pick the best answer from a list.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:37.700\nOr, you could have a true or false test, where you decide if a statement is correct. Sometimes, tests even involve doing something, like building a model or giving a presentation.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:46.800\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling words. A math test checks how well you can solve math problems.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:58.300\nAnd a driving test checks if you can safely operate a car. So, to recap, a test is just a method for checking your knowledge or skills in a certain area.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:04.900\nThey help you and your teachers see what you've learned and where you might need a little more practice.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:08.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
