    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_125509.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:30.300\nThink of it like checking if your lights turn on when you flip the switch. The switch is the \"input,\" and the light turning on is the \"output.\" The test is you flipping the switch and seeing if the light actually comes on.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:36.900\nAnother example: Let's say you\u2019re baking a cake. You taste it to make sure it tastes good.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:45.000\nThat's a test! You're checking if your recipe and baking skills produced the desired result, a yummy cake.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:56.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of verifying that something is doing what it's supposed to do. It's all about checking the output against what you expected.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:00.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a2982e50-bc2d-45ea-8486-31382dd49a89": {
