    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_125555.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.500\nNow, you might be thinking of school exams, but a test in a broader sense is really just a way to find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like this: you're trying to bake a cake. You test the oven to make sure it's hot enough, right? That's a test!\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:30.100\nOr maybe you're checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in. That's another test.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:38.500\nWe use tests to check everything from our phone's battery life to making sure a bridge is safe to cross.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:51.200\nBasically, a test is any process that gives you information or confirms something. So next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a way to check things out.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:54.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
