    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_125729.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:19.300\nBasically, a test is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you poke them with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:26.800\nIn school, a test helps your teacher see how well you understand what you've been learning.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:40.100\nIt could be answering questions on paper, solving a math problem, or even giving a presentation.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:47.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. A science test might ask you about the planets.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:56.600\nAnd a reading test shows how well you understand stories. So, tests are simply tools that help us see how much we know about something. They give us a chance to learn and improve!\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:00.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
