    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_125823.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in general, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:25.300\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:35.800\nThink about it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:43.400\nOr, you might test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:47.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:54.900\nAnother example is testing a lightbulb. You turn it on, and if it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:58.800\nIf it doesn't, then it failed. Simple as that.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:08.000\nSo, a test is just a way of finding something out, whether it's about your health, a cake, or even a lightbulb.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:16.200\nTests help us make sure things are working and doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:16.200 --> 01:21.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
