    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_125904.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\nOkay, so you're wondering what a test is, right?\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:08.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:08.300 --> 00:14.600\nIt helps us check if something is working correctly, or if someone knows something.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like this: if you want to see if your bike tires have enough air, you can do a simple test - you squeeze them!\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:28.000\nIf they feel soft, they need more air.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:30.700\nAnother example?\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:35.200\nLet's say your teacher gives you a quiz.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:39.600\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:42.300\nIt helps your teacher understand what you've learned in class.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:48.600\nTests aren't just for school though.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.800\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy, and scientists use tests to discover new things.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:56.200\nSo, a test is really just a way to check or examine something to learn more about it.\n```"
