    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_130940.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_130940.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.000\nNow, you might think of tests as something scary, like in school, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as it should.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like checking if your lightbulb still works. You flip the switch \u2013 that's the test.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:29.800\nIf the light comes on, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:34.900\nOr imagine you're baking a cake. You taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:41.000\nThat taste is the test. A good taste means the test is passed, and you can serve it.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:52.500\nSo, a test is really just a simple way to confirm that something is doing what it's supposed to do. It helps us find problems and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:56.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
