    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.800 --> 00:05.800\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:11.300\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is really just a way to find out if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:17.500\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:18.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:24.400\nAnother example?\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:27.800\nImagine baking a cake.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:30.200\nTasting it afterwards is a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:33.900\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:37.600\nThey help us understand if something is functioning correctly\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:41.300\nor if we need to make some adjustments.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:49.500\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:58.100\nIt could be anything from trying a new recipe to seeing if your phone can connect to the internet.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:00.500\nIt's all about verifying the outcome.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
