    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_132812.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:16.200\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:29.900\nYou do a simple test \u2013 you poke them with a toothpick! If it comes out clean, they're ready.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:42.400\nTests aren't just for baking, though. They can be quizzes at school to see how well you understand a subject. Or maybe a doctor does a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:47.200\nThe idea is always the same: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:52.000\nFor example, a spelling test helps your teacher know which words you need more practice with.\n\n00:52.000 --> 01:03.200\nA taste test helps you decide which brand of soda you like best. See? Tests are everywhere, big and small, helping us understand the world around us.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:08.800\nSo, a test is simply a method for gathering information.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:11.800\nIt can be a quiz, an experiment, or even just poking a cookie.\n\n01:11.800 --> 01:17.600\nIt helps us learn and make better decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
