    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_132859.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.700 --> 00:04.500\nToday, we're going to explore what a test is,\nin the simplest way possible.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:07.900\nBasically, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:14.900\nYou do a test! You poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:20.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test says the cake is ready.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:22.900\nIf it's gooey, the test says it needs more time.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:27.600\nTests aren't just for baking, though.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:30.400\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:33.700\nSchools use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:38.200\nEven when you try a new recipe, you're testing to see if you like it!\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:46.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for checking something to see if it works, is correct, or is good enough.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:49.300\nIt helps us make decisions.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:52.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
