    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_133047.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_133047.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. It could be anything from checking if a lightbulb works to seeing how well you understand a new topic.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:27.900\nBasically, you present something with a question or a challenge, and then you observe the result.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:34.200\nIf the lightbulb turns on, the test passed! If you answer a question correctly, that's also a pass.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:41.700\nThink about baking a cake. You test the oven temperature to make sure it's hot enough.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:46.900\nYou test the batter to see if it's the right consistency. Those are all tests!\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:53.400\nAnother example is checking if your shoes fit. You try them on, walk around, and see if they're comfortable.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:00.000\nThat's testing, too! So, remember, a test is just a way of getting information by observing the results of a question or challenge.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:08.300\nIt's a simple but super important tool for learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n01:08.300 --> 01:11.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "75e9add1-6ec3-4e4c-8fd0-c1e743ad15a1": {
