    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_133839.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:11.300\nToday we're going to talk about tests. Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:18.500\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer. It could be anything from a spelling test in school,\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:28.900\nto a test you run on your computer to see if it's working correctly. The main idea is to perform an action or ask a question, and then look at the result.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:37.400\nThat result, or the answer, tells you something about the thing you're testing. For example, if you're testing a cake recipe, you bake the cake, and then you taste it.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:45.200\nThe taste is the result of the test! Or, if you're testing a lightbulb, you screw it in and see if it lights up.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:52.200\nThe light, or lack of light, is the result. So, remember, a test is just a way to get information. You do something, and then you see what happens!\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:55.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
