    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_135028.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:15.500\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to find out information.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:21.600\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:27.700\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:36.900\nYour doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. A chef might taste-test a new recipe to see if it's delicious.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:45.100\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:53.300\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works. You put it in a lamp, flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:00.900\nAnother example is checking if a cake is done baking. You stick a toothpick in the center, and if it comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:08.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of getting information or checking if something is working as it should.\n\n01:08.200 --> 01:14.000\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are right.\n\n01:14.000 --> 01:14.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
