  "7f6a03bc-d6a1-47f3-865a-ce882272438c": {
    "id": "7f6a03bc-d6a1-47f3-865a-ce882272438c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:48:18.509007",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T13:56:32.078214",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_135631.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_135631.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat are they, and why do we even use them?\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:18.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, if you understand a new concept, or even if a recipe tastes good!\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:30.000\nBasically, we use tests to get information.\nThink about it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you test it with a toothpick.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:40.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\nOr, in school, a test helps your teacher see if you've learned what they've been teaching.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:51.200\nIt's a way to measure your understanding.\nTests come in all shapes and sizes, from multiple choice questions to hands-on experiments.\n\n00:51.200 --> 01:02.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and gather information.\nIt helps us understand if something is working or if we've learned something new.\n\n01:02.800 --> 01:06.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "36828ede-f886-48be-be6e-a2b7ecfa11b4": {
