    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_135717.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:16.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\nYou can't just look at it, right?\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:30.600\nSo, you do a test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in!\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test, and it's done!\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:42.000\nTests are used all the time.\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy, teachers use tests to see what you've learned in class, and even builders use tests to make sure a bridge is strong enough.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:53.400\nThe key is that a test provides evidence to help you make a decision or understand something better.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:57.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ae1a23e9-0882-4c15-95b9-4eb85f69acb1": {
    "id": "ae1a23e9-0882-4c15-95b9-4eb85f69acb1",
    "topic": "Test",
