    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:48:19.545124",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T13:58:20.521347",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_135820.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_135820.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:08.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:10.700\nThink of it like a little investigation.\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:15.500\nThe main idea behind a test is to gather information.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:18.800\nYou ask questions or perform actions, and then look at the results to draw a conclusion.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:23.300\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you can spell words correctly.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:28.100\nOr, a taste test might see which cookie people like the best.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:33.800\nLet's say you're testing a new light bulb.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:36.600\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:40.500\nIf it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:44.000\nIf not, the bulb probably isn't working.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:45.300\nSee?\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:45.700\nSimple!\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:53.500\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make decisions based on evidence.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:57.200\nThey give us valuable information.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:00.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
