    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_140035.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, a test is really just a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:24.600\nIt\u2019s like a simple yes or no question. Think about it this way: you might test if a light bulb works by screwing it in.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:28.800\nDoes it light up? If yes, it passes the test! If not, it fails.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:33.200\nOr imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:42.800\nYou can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test and it's ready to eat!\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:53.800\nSo, in short, a test is simply a way to see if something meets a certain requirement or standard. It helps us know if things are working correctly.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
