    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_142756.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.400\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. The \"something\" could be anything!\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:31.500\nIt could be a cookie, and the test might be whether it tastes good. Or it could be a light bulb, and the test is whether it lights up.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:38.000\nLet\u2019s say you want to know if a toy car works. The test is simple: you try to turn it on!\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:44.000\nIf it moves, it passes the test. If it doesn\u2019t, it fails.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:50.000\nAnother example: You want to know if it's raining. You look outside.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:56.500\nIf you see rain, you pass the \"is it raining?\" test!\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:00.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something meets a certain requirement.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:03.700\nIt's a simple concept we use every day.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:06.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
