    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_144142.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_144142.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:13.600\nA test is basically a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but with a specific question in mind.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:25.400\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. For example, if you're baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:33.600\nOr, if you're trying to figure out which key opens a door, you\u2019re testing each one until you find the right fit.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:40.300\nThese tests help us understand things better. They give us information we didn't have before.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:48.200\nSo, a test is simply a way to ask a question and get an answer. It helps us learn and solve problems.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:51.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9c0d35a7-7eff-41d7-a898-955f16cb721d": {
    "id": "9c0d35a7-7eff-41d7-a898-955f16cb721d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:48:47.029055",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T14:42:34.117077",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_144234.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_144234.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey there, welcome! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.800\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:26.100\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer. Think of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:38.400\nOr, a teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned in class. Tests can be anything from a simple yes or no question, like \"Is it raining?\", to something more complicated, like solving a math problem.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:46.600\nThe goal is always to learn something new.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:54.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a tool for gathering information. It helps us learn about ourselves, about the world around us, and about all sorts of interesting things.\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:58.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b0a8e1f6-8a72-4ae6-83c7-55ddbf75cc9a": {
    "id": "b0a8e1f6-8a72-4ae6-83c7-55ddbf75cc9a",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:48:47.495646",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T14:43:27.012367",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_144326.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_144326.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.200\nA test is basically a way to find out something, right? It's how we check if something is true, or how good something is.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see how well you understand the lesson.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:30.400\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake and you taste the batter. That\u2019s a mini-test to see if you need more sugar!\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:40.100\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal. A science experiment is a test to see if your hypothesis is correct.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:45.500\nTrying a new flavor of ice cream? That\u2019s a taste test to see if you like it.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:55.000\nSo, in short, a test is just a method for gathering information and making decisions. They help us learn and improve.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "fd6d2089-9a9a-4f5e-a809-052bd7f867e9": {
    "id": "fd6d2089-9a9a-4f5e-a809-052bd7f867e9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:48:47.986108",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T14:44:22.793253",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_144422.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_144422.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 01:19.300\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like this: You want to bake a cake, so you follow a recipe. The \"test\" is tasting the cake after you bake it.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:32.000\nDoes it taste good? Is it moist enough?\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:36.100\nThat tells you if your cake-baking process worked!\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:39.100\nOr, imagine you're trying out a new lightbulb.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:42.600\nThe \"test\" is simply turning it on.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:43.900\nDoes it light up?\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:45.800\nYes? Great!\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:49.600\nNo? Then something's probably wrong.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:53.200\nSo, a test is really just a simple way to check something.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:02.400\nWe perform tests every day, often without even realizing it. It's all about making sure things are working as expected.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:08.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
