    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:19.100\nThink of it like this: you want to see if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:23.200\nYou stick a toothpick in it, right? That's a test!\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:31.900\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something has a specific quality.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:42.300\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:51.800\nSo, tests are everywhere! They help us learn, diagnose problems, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:51.800 --> 01:01.300\nThey can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb turns on, or more complex, like testing a new medicine.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:09.200\nThe important thing is they give us information.\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:14.400\nTo sum it up, a test is a process for evaluating something to see if it meets a certain standard\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:19.800\nor performs in a specific way. Pretty useful, huh?\n\n01:19.800 --> 01:25.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
