    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This subtitle file was automatically generated.  Please check accuracy and edit as needed.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.800\nNow, a test is just a way to find out something, or to see how well you know something.\nThink of it as a check-up for your brain, or for a product.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:28.100\nThe main idea is simple: you present something, and then you see what happens.\nFor example, a school test checks what you've learned in class.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:34.000\nOr, a taste test checks how good food tastes.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.400\nLet's say you bake a cake.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:42.800\nYou can test it by tasting a slice.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:46.300\nIs it sweet enough?\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:47.900\nIs it cooked all the way through?\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:49.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:52.800\nAnother example: a doctor might test your reflexes by tapping your knee.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:05.400\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same basic goal: to get information.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:08.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
