    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_150721.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:01.900 --> 00:03.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:06.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:07.700\nIt's like asking a question\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:08.400\nand seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:08.400 --> 00:11.000\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.600\nThink about baking a cake. You test if it's done\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:16.900\nby sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:20.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:24.600\nOr, when you're learning to ride a bike, you're testing your balance.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:27.700\nYou try, you wobble, and eventually, you learn to stay upright.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:28.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:31.400\nTests help us understand things better\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:33.700\nand see if something works.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:37.800\nThey can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoelaces are tied.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:41.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:43.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
