    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_150836.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nOkay, so you're hearing the word \"test\" and maybe feeling a little stressed?\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:15.900\nDon't worry! A test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like this: you're testing if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:32.300\nIf it lights up, the test passes! In school, a test checks what you've learned.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:43.600\nIt could be questions about a book you read, or problems to solve in math. For example, a math test might ask you what 2 + 2 equals.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:50.100\nIf you answer 4, you passed that part of the test!\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:53.700\nTests help you and your teachers see what you understand well and what you might need a little more help with.\n```"
