    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_151257.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:13.700\nBut don't worry, it's not the kind you need to study for! A test, in general terms, is simply a way to check if something works correctly, or to find out information about it.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:19.300\nThink of it like this: a taste test tells you if food is yummy.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:23.600\nOr, when you get a new toy, you might test it out to see if it does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.100\nMaybe it's a toy car, and you test its speed.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:34.900\nSimilarly, scientists use tests to learn new things. They might test a new medicine to see if it makes people feel better, or test a new material to see if it's strong.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:42.900\nThe goal is always to learn something new or confirm that something is working as expected.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:50.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something out and get information.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:59.800\nIt can be as simple as tasting food or as complex as a scientific experiment.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
