    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like an investigation.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.800\nWe're trying to answer a question.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:24.300\nThere are all kinds of tests. You've probably taken tests at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:35.900\nBut tests aren't just for school. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature or blood pressure.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:47.600\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. Or, you might test if a toy car needs new batteries by seeing if it still moves.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:57.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a process for learning something. It helps us answer a question by gathering information. We try something out, observe the result, and then learn from it.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
