    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_151924.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to learn about something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.000\nThink of a test as a way to find out if something works like it should. It's like checking if your bike's brakes work before you go down a big hill!\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:26.300\nBasically, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:33.300\nIt could be testing a new toy to see if it's safe, or a doctor testing your reflexes to check your health.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:41.500\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done. That's a test!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:52.900\nOr, when you try on a new pair of shoes to see if they fit, that's also a test. So, tests help us make sure things are working correctly and safely.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:00.900\nThey're all about checking and confirming. Remember, a test is a way to see if something works as expected.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:04.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
