    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_152010.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:20.000\nA test, in simple terms, is a way to check if something works correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:33.300\nThat's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:41.200\nAnother example is a medical test. A doctor might order a blood test to see if you have enough iron in your body.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:48.400\nThe results of that test tell the doctor something important.\n\n00:48.400 --> 01:02.200\nOr, think about testing a new toy. You play with it to see if it's fun and if it works the way it's supposed to. So, a test is just a way of gathering information to make sure things are working as expected or to learn something new.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:05.000\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:06.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
