    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_153011.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:27.200\nIt's a process to see if something works, or if something is true.\nThink of it like this: When you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:34.500\nThat's a test!\nOr, if you're fixing a lightbulb, you might flip the switch to test if it's working.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:46.700\nSo, tests can be formal, like a quiz, or informal, like checking your cake.\nThe main idea is to gather information and confirm something.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:56.600\nWhether it\u2019s checking if your code works, if a medicine is safe, or just seeing if your shoes fit, a test helps us know for sure.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:04.300\nIn short, a test is an examination or trial to determine something's characteristics or effectiveness.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
