    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:33.400\nIn science, we use tests all the time.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:40.500\nFor example, you might test if a plant grows faster in sunlight or in the shade.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:44.900\nYou'd give one plant sunlight, one plant shade, and then compare how they grow.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:46.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:50.600\nOr maybe you want to test if a toy car needs new batteries.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:53.700\nYou put in fresh batteries and see if it goes faster.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:54.800\nAgain, that's a test.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:00.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out something by trying it out and seeing what happens.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:02.800\nIt's a simple way to get answers!\n\n01:02.800 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
