    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_154046.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.700\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:17.900\nYou've probably taken a bunch of them in school, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:27.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to see what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:34.800\nIt's like a measuring stick for your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:43.500\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if you can jump high, you take a little jump test!\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:52.200\nSomeone measures how high you can go. Tests in school are similar.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:02.800\nThey help teachers see how well you understand the things you've been learning.\n\n01:02.800 --> 01:13.400\nFor example, a spelling test checks your spelling skills. A math test shows how well you can solve math problems.\n\n01:13.400 --> 01:23.600\nTests can be quizzes, exams, or even activities.\n\n01:23.600 --> 01:31.000\nThey all help us understand what we've learned and where we might need some extra help.\n\n01:31.000 --> 01:41.400\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is just a tool to measure knowledge or ability.\n\n01:41.400 --> 01:45.000\nIt's a snapshot of what you know at a particular moment.\n\n01:45.000 --> 01:48.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
