    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_155039.mp4",
    "subtitles": "WEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.300\nThink of a test as a way to see if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:26.300\nIt's like checking if your favorite toy still needs batteries. Basically, a test asks a question and gives you information based on the answer.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:33.900\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light switch turns on the light.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:36.900\nYou flip the switch, and if the light comes on, the test passes.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:42.000\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.100\nAnother example? Baking a cake! You taste it.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:54.300\nIf it tastes good, the \"taste test\" passes. If it's burnt, it fails.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:05.100\nTests help us find problems and make sure things are working correctly. So, in short, a test is just a simple way to check if something is doing what it should.\n\n01:05.100 --> 01:08.700\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it!\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:12.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI."
  },
