    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T15:55:54.237514",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_155554.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_155554.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:14.000\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, whether it was in school or online. But what is a test, really?\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:22.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process of asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:34.900\nThink of it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by plugging it in. The question is, \"Does this lightbulb light up?\" And plugging it in is the test.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:41.100\nAnother example is baking a cake. You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:50.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! So, tests help us learn and check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:50.900 --> 01:01.200\nBasically, a test is just a way to get information. We ask a question and then find the answer by observing or experimenting.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:07.600\nIt's how we learn and improve things! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
