    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_160739.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:23.500\nIt's a process used to gather information or evaluate something. Think of it like this: You might test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:32.600\nOr a doctor might run a blood test to check your health. Even trying different routes to school to see which is fastest is a type of test!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:38.500\nTests help us make decisions. If the cake isn't done, we bake it longer.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:49.000\nIf your blood test shows something concerning, the doctor knows what to do next. And if one route is faster, you'll probably take it again!\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:59.500\nSo, tests are all about gathering information to help us understand something better and make informed choices.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:03.700\nThey're everywhere around us!\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:09.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
