    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:26.100\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. The main point of a test is to see if something is working correctly, or to measure how well something performs.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:36.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:46.900\nAnother example is testing a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids to play with. The important thing is that a test gives us information we didn't have before.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:55.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a process for gathering information and seeing if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:00.800\nIt helps us understand things better and make informed decisions.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:03.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
