    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_162123.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:06.050\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:06.050 --> 00:11.950\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.950 --> 00:17.150\nThink of it like a question, but instead of just asking, we're looking for proof, or evidence, to answer it.\n\n00:17.150 --> 00:19.920\nSo, what kind of things can we test?\n\n00:19.920 --> 00:26.520\nWell, imagine you want to know if a cake is done, you can poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:26.520 --> 00:29.820\nIf it comes out clean, that's a test showing it's ready.\n\n00:29.820 --> 00:35.040\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp and see if it lights up.\n\n00:35.040 --> 00:35.970\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:35.970 --> 00:41.090\nBasically, a test helps us confirm something, or see if something is true.\n\n00:41.090 --> 00:45.690\nWe gather information and use it to make a decision.\n\n00:45.690 --> 00:48.970\nRemember, a test is just a way to find things out!\n\n00:48.970 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
