  "00fb6208-e8f5-4786-a85e-cad31300261e": {
    "id": "00fb6208-e8f5-4786-a85e-cad31300261e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:49:50.750815",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T16:26:24.527093",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_162624.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_162624.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:34.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! Or, if you want to know if a plant needs water, you can test the soil by feeling it. Dry soil means it needs a drink.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:39.800\nTests aren't just for baking or gardening. They're used everywhere!\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:48.000\nFrom checking if your phone is working properly to figuring out if you understand a new idea.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:56.000\nSo, a test is just a way to check something and get information. That's the basics of what a test is.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
