    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_163034.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:09.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:19.200\nAt its most basic, a test is simply a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:38.000\nThat something could be anything: if you understand a lesson, if a plant needs water, or even if a cookie tastes good.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:47.000\nThe main idea is that we perform an action, or ask a question, and then observe the result.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:51.000\nThat result gives us information.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:54.000\nFor example, a quiz in school is a test to see how well you learned the material.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:58.000\nChecking the soil of a plant to see if it's dry is a test to see if it needs watering.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:02.000\nAnd taking a bite of a cookie is a test to see if you like the flavor!\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:09.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for getting information.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:13.000\nWe do something, we see what happens, and then we learn from the outcome.\n\n01:13.000 --> 01:16.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
