    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_164125.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like a way to see if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:23.200\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Well, you can test if a light bulb works by turning it on.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:31.200\nThat's a test! Or, if you're baking a cake, you can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:36.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's another test!\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:48.300\nTests can be big or small, simple or complicated, but the basic idea is always the same: you're trying to find out something about something else.\n\n00:48.300 --> 01:00.800\nYou're checking to see if a condition is met. So, to recap, a test is just a way to check if something is true or working correctly, using a simple procedure.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:08.600\nIt can be as simple as turning on a light or checking a cake. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
