    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_164533.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out, or to see how well something works.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:30.900\nThat's a test! Or, if you're learning to ride a bike, trying to balance without falling is a test of your skills.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:40.500\nTests can be formal, like the ones you take in school, or informal, like checking if the water is hot enough for a bath.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:54.400\nThe important thing is that they give you information. Whether it's about your knowledge, a product\u2019s quality, or even just the temperature of water, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:04.300\nSo, to recap, a test is a process used to discover information or evaluate something. Pretty simple, right?\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
