    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_164754.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.200\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is ready.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:33.100\nYou use a toothpick, right? That's a test! Basically, we use tests to see if something is working as it should, or if something is true.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:40.700\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:48.300\nOr, a teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:55.900\nSo, the toothpick test tells you if the cake is baked. The doctor's test tells you about your health. The school test tells you what you've learned.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:03.500\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all help us understand something better.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:09.000\nTests are useful in all sorts of situations.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:12.500\nThey help us make decisions and learn new things.\n\n01:12.500 --> 01:15.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
