    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_164853.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nYou might think of tests as something scary, like in school, but really, a test is just a way to see if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like checking if your bike tires have enough air.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:23.000\nWe do tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:33.000\nIf you try turning on a light and it doesn't work, you're testing the lightbulb.\nDoes it work? No. That's the result of your test.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:35.100\nAnother example:\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:43.100\nWhen you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like it.\nYou taste it, and then you know if the recipe passed the test!\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:47.800\nSo, in short, a test is simply a way to check if something works or if it\u2019s good.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:53.900\nIt's about finding out information.\nThat's all there is to it!\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:00.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
