    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_165053.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.900\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, whether it's a quiz in school or even just trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:29.500\nBasically, a test is a way to check if something works, or if something is true. Think of it like this: If you build a birdhouse, you might test it by putting it outside and seeing if birds actually move in.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:38.800\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you test it by sticking a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean. That tells you it's done!\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:47.200\nTests help us learn and improve. If the birdhouse doesn't attract birds, you know you need to make some changes.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:59.800\nIf the cake isn't done, you know to bake it a little longer. So, a test is just a method to find out if something is working correctly or if your assumptions are right.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:08.399\nTests are everywhere, helping us learn and build better things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
