    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:25.100\nYou can do a test, like sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:30.600\nTests are used everywhere. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:41.000\nTeachers use tests to see how well you understand a subject. Even your computer runs tests all the time to make sure everything is working correctly.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:56.900\nSo, a test is basically a question or a procedure designed to find out information. It could be a written exam, a physical examination, or even just observing something to see if it behaves the way you expect.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:05.500\nIn short, tests help us understand and evaluate things. They give us information to make better decisions.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:09.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
