    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_171414.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:14.500\nThink of a test as a way to check what you know about something. It's like a measuring stick for your understanding.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:25.400\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes. You might have a simple quiz with multiple-choice questions, or maybe a longer exam with essay questions.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:35.300\nThe goal is always the same: to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:49.700\nFor example, imagine you\u2019re learning about colors. A test might ask you, \"What color is the sky on a sunny day?\" The answer, of course, is blue!\n\n00:49.700 --> 01:01.900\nOr, if you're learning about animals, a test might ask you to name a mammal. So, remember, a test is simply a way to assess your knowledge.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:11.200\nIt helps you and your teachers see where you're doing well and where you might need a little extra help. Don't be afraid of tests; see them as a chance to show off what you've learned!\n\n01:11.200 --> 01:14.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
