    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_172138.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.000\nOkay, so you\u2019ve probably heard the word \"test\" before, but what does it actually mean?\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:10.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:14.000\nIt's like asking a question and then seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:18.000\nThink about it this way: a taste test lets you find out which cookie is tastiest.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.000\nA spelling test shows you how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:27.000\nAnd a medical test helps doctors understand what's going on inside your body.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.000\nBasically, tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:39.000\nThey can be as simple as checking if a light bulb works, or as complex as figuring out if a new medicine is safe.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:43.000\nThe main idea is always to get information and see what the result is.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:49.000\nSo, a test is just a way of learning something through observation or experiment.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:53.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
