    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer, or trying something out to see if it works.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:27.200\nThe main idea behind a test is to get information. It helps us understand how well something performs, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:36.000\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:42.800\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:54.300\nAnother example is a strength test at a gym. It checks how much weight you can lift.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:03.500\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to give us useful information.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:07.100\nTo sum it up, a test is a check-up!\n\n01:07.100 --> 01:14.000\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
