    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_175353.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:22.900\nIt helps us check if something is working, or if someone knows something. Think about it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you\u2019re healthy.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:32.600\nOr, in school, you take a test to show what you've learned. A baking test might involve tasting a cake to see if it's delicious.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:46.200\nSo, tests help us measure or evaluate something. They can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your phone is working by making a call.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:56.500\nBasically, it's a process of checking and finding out information. To sum it up, a test is a way to gather information about something.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:05.500\nWhether it's your health, your knowledge, or even the quality of a cake, tests help us understand the world around us better.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:09.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1cc1c34a-4eb7-4a87-a5c2-e5fdf046a1eb": {
    "id": "1cc1c34a-4eb7-4a87-a5c2-e5fdf046a1eb",
