    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_175814.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_175814.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:18.300\nAt its most basic, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:29.300\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\nThink of it like this: you're testing if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:39.400\nOr you're testing if the water's too hot by dipping your toe in.\nIn more formal situations, tests help us understand if something works as it should.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:49.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nA math test checks your understanding of numbers and equations.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:60.500\nAnd a medical test helps doctors figure out what's going on inside your body.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:60.500 --> 00:64.100\nIt can be simple, like testing cookie dough, or more complex, like a school exam.\nThe goal is always to check and see what's what.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "87a9272c-de57-4da7-87a6-de71fdebf87c": {
    "id": "87a9272c-de57-4da7-87a6-de71fdebf87c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
