    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_175918.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_175918.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.100\nToday, we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:09.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:12.400\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:15.600\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:19.700\nOr, a teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:21.500\nThe test provides information.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:29.000\nAnother example: if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:32.200\nYou're testing if the cake is ready.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.700\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and see where things stand.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:40.500\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c73cc8ce-03e9-429a-b3e0-50efa8d67380": {
    "id": "c73cc8ce-03e9-429a-b3e0-50efa8d67380",
    "topic": "Test",
