    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:50:48.261901",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T18:00:13.360791",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_180013.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_180013.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:09.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:17.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works, so you flip the switch.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:23.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.000\nThe result of the test tells you something.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.400\nDid the light turn on? Great, the lightbulb passed the test.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:32.600\nDid it stay dark? Well, the lightbulb failed.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:37.600\nAnother example: your mom asks if you brushed your teeth.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:40.500\nShe's testing if you did your chore.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.500\nIf you say yes and she smells minty toothpaste, you pass!\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:52.200\nThese simple checks, these tests, help us understand the world around us and make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:57.100\nSo remember, a test is just a way to check something!\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:02.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
