    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_180643.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.999\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.399\nSimply put, a test is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you have a question, and the test helps you find the answer.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:21.000\nThere are all kinds of tests! Think about a multiple-choice quiz in school. That's a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:26.000\nOr imagine trying a new recipe. The finished dish is a test of whether you followed the instructions correctly.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:34.800\nAnother example could be checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in, flip the switch, and boom! The light coming on is a successful test.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:41.900\nIf it doesn't light up, well, the test failed.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:56.300\nSo, to recap, a test is a method for figuring something out, confirming something, or seeing if something works. It's a fundamental part of learning and problem-solving in almost every area of life.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:05.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
