    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you test them with a toothpick.\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:26.200\nIn the world of technology, tests are used to make sure things work the way they should.\nMaybe you're building a website and you want to test if the buttons work.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:35.900\nOr maybe you're writing some code and want to test if it gives you the right answer.\nFor example, a test could be clicking a button on a website to see if it takes you to the correct page.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:43.100\nOr it could be entering \"2 + 2\" into a calculator program and checking if the answer is \"4\".\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:56.100\nTests help us find mistakes and make sure everything is working perfectly.\nSo, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:06.300\nIt\u2019s like a simple experiment to confirm things are behaving as expected.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:09.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
