    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.400\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:22.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:36.400\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, a product's quality, or even the strength of a bridge.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:48.400\nThink of it like this: a pop quiz in school is a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:57.400\nOr, when you buy a new phone, the company has run many tests to make sure it works properly.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:06.500\nEven a doctor giving you a checkup is performing tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:15.600\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n01:15.600 --> 01:24.700\nThey can be formal, like a standardized exam, or informal, like trying a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n01:24.700 --> 01:33.800\nBasically, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n01:33.800 --> 01:42.200\nTo recap, a test is a process for evaluation.\n\n01:42.200 --> 01:48.900\nIt helps us understand something better through observation and measurement.\n\n01:48.900 --> 01:52.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
