    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer. We use tests all the time, even if you don't realize it.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:33.900\nFor example, when you flip a light switch, you're testing to see if the light will turn on.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:36.900\nOr, if you're baking cookies,\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:42.900\nyou might poke them with a toothpick to test if they're done.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:45.900\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:48.000\nGreat!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:49.500\nThe cookies passed the test.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:58.100\nTests help us understand if something is working as expected, or if we need to make changes.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:03.700\nThey can be simple, like checking a lightbulb, or more complex, like taking a quiz at school.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:08.800\nBut they all serve the same purpose: to learn and to check.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:12.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something\n\n01:12.400 --> 01:14.800\nand see if it works!\n\n01:14.800 --> 01:18.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
