    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_182550.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.700\nToday we're going to talk about tests. What are they and why do we use them?\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:23.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It helps us understand if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake recipe by baking it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:36.000\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Tests can be big or small.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:45.100\nA simple test could be checking if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch. A more complex test might involve lots of steps and measurements.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:54.000\nThe important thing is that a test gives us information. So, remember, a test is just a way of checking something. It helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:56.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
