    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_184459.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:15.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:18.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if the water is hot enough for a bath.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:29.200\nYou dip your toe in. That's a test! Tests help us see if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:39.200\nIn school, you take tests to see how well you understand a subject. A doctor might run tests to figure out why you're feeling sick.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:50.200\nFor example, a car mechanic might test a car battery to see if it's still good. Or a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:56.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information by checking something.\n\n00:56.300 --> 00:58.700\nIt's a simple but powerful tool we use every day.\n```"
