    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.400\nIt helps us understand if something is working, or if something is true. Think of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you might screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:29.700\nThat's a test! You're testing if the lightbulb lights up.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:34.000\nOr, imagine you want to know if a cake recipe is good.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.700\nYou bake the cake according to the recipe, and then you taste it.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:43.100\nThat's another test! You're testing if the cake tastes good.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:47.500\nSo, a test is just a process to check something.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:51.900\nIt can be as simple as turning on a lightbulb, or as complex as a scientific experiment.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:54.700\nThe main idea is to gather information\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:58.200\nand learn something new.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:02.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
