    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_191208.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to explore something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, in school, you take a test to show what you've learned.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:37.000\nTests can be written, like a quiz, or practical, like a driving test.\nThey help us measure and understand things.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:46.000\nFor example, a simple taste test can tell you if you like a new flavor.\nA spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:52.700\nAnd a strength test measures how much you can lift.\n\n00:52.700 --> 01:03.500\nSo, remember, a test is a tool.\nIt helps us learn, measure, and understand.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:07.200\nFrom simple taste tests to important medical exams, tests are all around us.\n```"
  },
