    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_191942.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something fundamental: the Test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:17.500\nNow, you might think of tests as scary exams, but in a general sense, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it as a question, followed by looking for the answer. For example, if you want to know if a cake is done, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:42.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your answer \u2013 the cake is ready! Or, if you're buying a new pair of shoes, you test them by walking around to see if they're comfortable.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:58.600\nBasically, we use tests all the time to check things, learn new things, or make decisions. So, next time you hear the word \"test\", remember it's just a way of finding something out.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:02.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
