    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_193054.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:10.800\nAlright, let's talk about tests! In the simplest terms, a test is just a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:16.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb turns on after you screw it in.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:25.000\nThat's a test! You're testing if the lightbulb is working.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:34.900\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even just asking questions in class.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:45.000\nOutside of school, tests are everywhere. When you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like it.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.900\nWhen a doctor checks your temperature, they're testing to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:03.000\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly. They're a way to gather information. Remember, tests are a way to learn, not just to get a grade. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
