    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_193143.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.300 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:04.500\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:08.900\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:12.700\nIt\u2019s how we check if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:17.500\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by plugging it in.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:20.600\nDoes it light up?\nThat's your test result!\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:24.600\nOr, if you\u2019re trying to remember your friend's phone number, you test yourself by trying to recite it.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:27.100\nDid you get it right?\nThat's another test.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:32.200\nSo, tests can be super simple, like checking a lightbulb, or a bit more complex, like taking a quiz at school.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:36.900\nBut the idea is the same: we use a test to learn something new or to confirm something we already think we know.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:38.900\nBasically, it gives us answers!\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:40.900\nThat\u2019s the core idea of a test.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:43.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
