    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_194149.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like checking to see if you learned your ABCs, or if your toy car still runs.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:37.200\nThe main idea behind a test is to get information.\nIt helps us understand what's going right, and what needs a little more work.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:41.800\nFor example, your teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:46.400\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:47.000\nSee?\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:47.500\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:59.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check knowledge or functionality, giving us information to improve or understand things better.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:04.400\nWe use them all the time in school, at the doctor, and even with our toys!\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:06.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
