    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, welcome! \n\n00:04.900 --> 00:12.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:19.100\nNow, a test, in the simplest terms, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:25.800\nIt helps us see if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:29.800\nThink of it like this: You might test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:33.400\nThat's a test! \n\n00:33.400 --> 00:37.100\nOr, your teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge on a subject.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:37.900\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:45.100\nTests can be physical, like testing how much weight a bridge can hold, or they can be more abstract, like testing your understanding of math problems.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:47.500\nThe main idea is always the same: to find out something specific.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:59.400\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a procedure designed to evaluate or check something. It helps us understand how well something works or what its properties are.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:04.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
