    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_195606.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:16.200\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:23.900\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if the answer matches what we expect.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:33.000\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:42.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, think about checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:49.900\nYou flip the switch, and if the light turns on, it passes the test. Basically, a test helps us confirm things.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:53.800\nIt gives us confidence that something is the way it should be. So, tests are all about checking and confirming. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
