    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_195739.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:18.700\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in the world of science and technology, a test is simply a way to find out if something works the way we expect it to.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:28.700\nThink of it like this: you have an idea, you build something based on that idea, and then you test it to see if it actually does what you planned.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:36.100\nFor example, imagine you build a paper airplane. The test is to throw it and see if it flies!\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:43.500\nOr, if you're baking a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it's delicious.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:58.900\nTests can be simple, like those, or really complicated, involving lots of data and fancy equipment. But at the end of the day, they all have the same goal: to give us information and help us improve things.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:06.700\nSo, tests help us understand the world around us and make things better.\n\n01:06.700 --> 01:08.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
