    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_200815.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:20.100\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true, or correct, or working as it should.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:28.100\nThink about it like this:\nWhen you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a mini-test!\nYou're testing if the cake is done.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:36.600\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again.\nThat's a test to see if a simple restart fixes the problem.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:49.500\nTests are used everywhere, from checking if a lightbulb works to figuring out if you understand a new concept in school.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:59.600\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are functioning properly.\nIn short, a test is a simple way to check something.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
