  "6d9eb483-f9c2-4996-9c3a-f7885baa2d7e": {
    "id": "6d9eb483-f9c2-4996-9c3a-f7885baa2d7e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:52:07.625642",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T20:08:58.091197",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_200857.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_200857.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but usually with questions or tasks.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:27.700\nThe whole point of a test is to measure your knowledge or skill. It helps you, and maybe your teacher or instructor, understand what you already know and what you still need to learn.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:35.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you spell words. A math test checks your math skills.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:43.800\nEven when you try out a new recipe, you're essentially doing a test to see if it tastes good! You're testing the recipe.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:51.000\nSo, tests help us learn and improve by showing us where we stand. They aren't always scary! They're just a tool.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:56.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "23f9523c-e877-44d8-8596-4607be2c9ab3": {
    "id": "23f9523c-e877-44d8-8596-4607be2c9ab3",
    "topic": "Test",
