    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_200946.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.200\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:27.100\nBasically, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:35.700\nIt could be checking your knowledge, your skills, or even how well something works.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:41.200\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:44.000\nA taste test checks if you like the flavor of a food.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:46.600\nAnd a stress test on a bridge checks if it can handle heavy weight.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:49.400\nSo, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:52.200\nThey give us information to make decisions.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:54.800\nDid you pass the spelling test? Great!\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:57.400\nDid you like the new flavor? Awesome!\n\n00:57.400 --> 00:59.100\nIs the bridge safe?\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:01.000\nEssential!\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:05.700\nIn short, tests are tools we use to learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:08.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
