    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T20:17:12.364053",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_201712.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_201712.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to check your health. Or, when you bake a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:33.700\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand what you've been learning. They can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:44.700\nThe key is that they're designed to measure your knowledge or skills. So, a spelling test checks your spelling, while a math test checks your math skills.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:56.000\nA history test might ask you about important events from the past. Tests aren\u2019t meant to be scary; they\u2019re just a way to see what you know and what you might need a little extra help with.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:03.800\nBasically, a test is a check-up for your brain! I hope that helps you better understand what a test is.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:07.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
