    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:24.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we know something well.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:33.800\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:43.300\nOr, a teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:52.800\nFor example, you could test a lightbulb by turning it on. If it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:02.900\nYou could also test a recipe by following the instructions and tasting the final product. If it tastes good, you know the recipe works.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:09.500\nSo, tests are all about finding answers and making sure things are as they should be.\n\n01:09.500 --> 01:13.100\nThey help us learn and improve.\n\n01:13.100 --> 01:16.700\nRemember, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n01:16.700 --> 01:20.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
