    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_203029.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:15.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:31.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:45.700\nFalling down a few times is kind of a test to see how well you're balancing.\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like tasting food to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:55.800\nThe key is, a test helps us learn and understand something better.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:03.100\nIt helps us confirm, learn, and improve.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
