    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:05.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:09.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.600 --> 00:14.900\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:19.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:21.400\nYou poke it with a toothpick, right?\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:24.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:28.700\nThe toothpick comes out clean, the test is passed, and the cake is ready.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:34.000\nOr, imagine you're checking if a light bulb works. You flip the switch.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:37.600\nThe light turns on, the test is passed, and you know the bulb is good.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:41.600\nSo, tests help us confirm things, check for problems, or just learn more.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:45.600\nThey're everywhere, from baking to science experiments.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:52.500\nBasically, if you're trying to figure something out, you're probably doing a test!\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:56.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
