    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.400 --> 00:05.400\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:10.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but really,\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:15.900\na test is just a way to find out if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:19.700\nThink of it like this: You buy a new lightbulb.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:23.600\nTo test if it works, you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:25.100\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:29.200\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:33.000\nYou test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the center.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:35.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:36.900\nThat's another test!\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:42.400\nSo, a test is simply checking something to see if it meets a certain requirement or standard.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:49.200\nWe use tests every day, often without even realizing it. They help us make sure things are working correctly\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:53.800\nand doing what they're meant to do.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:57.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
