    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_204530.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we're talking about checking if something is working as expected.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:22.700\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you need to test if it rolls. That's a test!\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:35.800\nSo, a test is basically a way to make sure something is doing what it's supposed to do. For example, if you write a recipe, you test it by cooking it to see if it tastes good.\n00:35.800 --> 00:53.900\nOr, if you\u2019re building a website, you test it by clicking on all the buttons to make sure they work. Tests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on, or more complex, like running a program to see if it gives you the right answer.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:04.400\nThe important thing is that you're verifying that everything is functioning properly. So, in short, a test is a way to confirm things work.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:08.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
