    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_205325.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:17.400\nToday we're diving into something fundamental: tests.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:27.500\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if the answer is what you expect.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:33.900\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might test it by sticking a toothpick in \u2013 if it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:40.300\nThat's a test!\nOr, if you're making sure a lightbulb works, you turn it on.\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:48.400\nTests help us find problems and make sure things are working the way they should.\nThey're used everywhere, from baking to building bridges.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:53.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is working or true.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:56.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
