    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_205420.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something. Think of it like a check-up for your brain!\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:23.800\nTests can come in all sorts of forms. Sometimes they're written, like a quiz with multiple choice questions.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:34.600\nOther times, they might be practical, like showing someone how to bake a cake. The goal is always the same: to see what you've learned.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:43.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. A math test checks if you can solve equations.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:53.800\nAnd a driving test checks if you can safely operate a car. So, remember, a test is just a tool to measure your understanding.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:02.300\nDon't be afraid of them! They help you and your teachers see where you're strong and where you might need a little more practice.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
