    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the concept of a test.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:14.800\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like this: a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. That's a test!\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:36.200\nOr, when you take a quiz at school, that's a test to see what you've learned. Tests can be formal, like a big exam, or informal, like checking if your bike tires have enough air.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:46.300\nAnother example is using a thermometer to test if you have a fever. The thermometer gives you a number that tells you if your temperature is normal or not.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:55.600\nSo, to recap: a test is a method to evaluate or determine something. It helps us understand things better.\n\n00:55.600 --> 01:01.600\nAnd remember, tests aren't always scary! They're just tools to help us learn.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
