    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_210024.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:23.000\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life. Think about it: When you try a new recipe, you're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:36.500\nOr, if you press a button on a remote control, you're testing to see if it works. In science and education, tests are more formal, but the idea is the same.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:47.400\nWe use them to see what someone knows, or how something behaves. For example, a spelling test shows how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:58.300\nA science experiment tests a hypothesis, like whether plants grow faster with more sunlight.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:09.900\nSo, to recap, a test is a method for gathering information. It helps us understand things better by providing evidence.\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:15.400\nWhether it's trying a new food or conducting a scientific experiment, tests are all about learning.\n\n01:15.400 --> 01:19.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
