    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_210633.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:59.6\n1\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n2\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.400\nToday, we're talking about tests.\n\n3\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nA test is basically a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n4\n00:12.700 --> 00:18.500\nIt helps us understand if something is working the way it should or if someone knows something.\n\n5\n00:18.500 --> 00:24.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n6\n00:24.300 --> 00:29.700\nOr, your teacher might give you a quiz to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n7\n00:29.700 --> 00:32.500\nSee? Different kinds of tests, different things they're checking.\n\n8\n00:32.500 --> 00:37.500\nAnother simple example is testing a new toy. You play with it to see if it's fun and if it works properly.\n\n9\n00:37.500 --> 00:38.800\nThat\u2019s a test too!\n\n10\n00:38.800 --> 00:47.300\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or understanding.\n\n11\n00:47.300 --> 00:53.100\nIt\u2019s all about learning and finding things out!\n\n12\n00:53.100 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
