    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_211634.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.440\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.440 --> 00:07.140\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well something works.\n\n00:07.140 --> 00:08.800\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb turns on.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:09.480\nThat's a test!\n\n00:09.480 --> 00:14.320\nThe main idea is to see if something meets a certain standard or passes a specific requirement.\n\n00:14.320 --> 00:20.210\nSo, if you take a quiz in school, that's a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:20.210 --> 00:26.470\nOr, if a company checks a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids, that's a test too.\n\n00:26.470 --> 00:31.080\nFor example, you might test a recipe by making it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:31.080 --> 00:34.820\nOr, you could test a new phone app to see if it crashes.\n\n00:34.820 --> 00:39.200\nBasically, anything you check to see if it works the way it should, is a test.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:48.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a process that checks if something works, meets a requirement, or if you understand something.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:50.840\nIt's all about finding out information.\n\n00:50.840 --> 00:52.410\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
