    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:17.100\nNot the kind you take in school, but the kind used to check if something works the way it should.\nThink of it like this: a test is just a way to see if something is doing its job.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:24.700\nFor example, let's say you bake a cake.\nYou can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:31.700\nOr, imagine you're building a toy car.\nYou can test if the wheels are on correctly by giving it a push.\nIf it rolls straight, that's a successful test.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:39.700\nSo, a test is simply a way to confirm something is functioning as expected.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:50.400\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\nThey help us make sure things are safe, reliable, and doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:53.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
