    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_213159.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and to test if it's done, you stick a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:34.700\nOr, imagine you\u2019re trying to turn on a light. The test is simple: you flip the switch.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:46.100\nIf the light comes on, it passes the test; the lightbulb is working. If it stays dark, the test fails, and something might be wrong.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:55.900\nTests are all about checking if things are doing what they're supposed to do. They help us identify problems and make sure everything is running smoothly.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:05.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something works. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
