    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_213549.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.500\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but the word \"test\" really just means checking something to see if it works, or if it's true.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like trying a new recipe. You test it to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:36.800\nIn science, we often use tests to see if our ideas are right. For example, if you think plants grow better with more sunlight, you could test that by giving some plants lots of sun and others less. Then you can compare them!\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:43.200\nOr imagine you're testing a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids. You're checking to see if it breaks easily.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:51.600\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of checking something.\n\n00:51.600 --> 01:01.200\nWhether it's a recipe, a scientific idea, or a toy, testing helps us learn and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
