    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_213819.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.200\nToday we're going to explore something called a test.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:12.000\nNow, in everyday language, a test is just a way to find out something, right?\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.400\nLike a quiz in school, or even testing the water before you jump in a pool!\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:23.000\nIn a more formal sense, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate or assess something.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.100\nIt could measure your skills, knowledge, performance, or even the quality of a product.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:32.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:38.500\nOr a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt. They\u2019re using the test to gather information and make a decision.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:48.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a method for evaluating something, whether it's your understanding of a subject, the quality of a product, or even your own abilities.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:54.500\nIt helps us learn and make informed choices.\n\n00:54.500 --> 00:59.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1d17210f-ef09-4850-9027-0bb1ae4e4235": {
    "id": "1d17210f-ef09-4850-9027-0bb1ae4e4235",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:53:09.535145",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T21:39:03.542566",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_213903.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_213903.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean exams in school. A test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like this: You have a lightbulb. To test if it works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:29.100\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:34.100\nAnother example? Let's say you bake a cake.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:44.200\nYou test it by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done \u2013 test passed!\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:53.300\nIf it's gooey, it needs more time \u2013 test failed. So, a test is simply a way to verify if something is working correctly.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:55.700\nIt's checking if the result is what you expect.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:57.400\nAnd that's the basics of testing!\n\n00:57.400 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
