    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_214049.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:22.700\nIt's a process designed to gather information. Think of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:29.700\nThat's a test! Or, if you want to know if your phone is charged, you look at the battery icon.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:39.800\nThat's another kind of test. Tests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking the weather before you go outside.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:48.800\nThe goal is always the same: to get data and learn something new. So, a test helps you to check something.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:59.000\nIn short, a test is a method for gathering information to determine a quality, ability, or characteristic of someone or something.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
