    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_214630.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but a test, in a general sense, is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:30.900\nIt's a process of checking or examining something to see what it's like, or how well it works.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:43.100\nThink about it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:51.400\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken, you might test it by screwing it into a lamp. If it lights up, it's working!\n\n00:51.400 --> 01:05.000\nSo, a test is simply a way to gather information and make a decision. It helps us understand something better.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:08.600\nTo recap, tests are processes used to examine or check something, like a cake or a lightbulb, to see if it meets certain conditions.\n```"
  },
