    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE: These are example subtitles.  They are NOT timed to the code above. You will need to use a subtitle editor to sync them to the audio.\n\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.700\nSimple, basic tests. Think of a test like a way to find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:22.400\nIt's like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:27.200\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You test it with a toothpick.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:40.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. Tests can be written, like a quiz in school, or they can be practical, like testing a toy to see if it's safe.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:48.100\nThe main goal of a test is to get information, to see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:58.900\nSo, remember, tests are all about checking things. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
