    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_220024.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:08.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:11.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:13.000\nIt's like an experiment, but a little more organized.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:15.000\nThink about it this way.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:20.000\nImagine you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:23.000\nYou could test it by not watering it for a few days and seeing if it wilts.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:30.000\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:33.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:38.000\nTests are used everywhere, from checking your eyesight at the doctor to figuring out if a new medicine works.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:43.000\nThe key is to have a clear question and a way to get an answer.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:49.000\nSo, a test helps us learn new things by gathering information in a structured way.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
