    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:15.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:21.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready, so you poke it with a toothpick.\nThat poke is a test!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:26.800\nIt helps you decide if the cake needs more time in the oven.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:32.200\nTests are everywhere!\nYour doctor gives you tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:40.600\nTeachers give you tests to see how much you've learned.\nEven your phone has tests to make sure all its parts are working correctly.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:51.200\nFor example, a lightbulb test: does it turn on when you flip the switch?\nOr a taste test: does that new recipe taste good?\nThese are both types of tests.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.700\nSo, basically, a test is any procedure designed to evaluate or check something.\nIt helps us make decisions based on the results.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:07.500\nIn short, tests help us learn, diagnose, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:11.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
