    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_220419.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.400 --> 00:05.300\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:07.900\nNow, in everyday life, a test is basically a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:10.200\nThink of it like an experiment or a check-up.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:13.800\nA test helps us see if something is working correctly, or if a statement is true or false.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:16.800\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:20.300\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:26.800\nLet's say you bake a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:30.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:30.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:37.000\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and make a decision based on that information.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:43.000\nIt's used everywhere, from science to cooking, to even playing games.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:45.900\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:49.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
