    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:29.300\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done baking,\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:33.100\nyou might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:39.500\nThe toothpick comes out clean? The cake is ready. It comes out with batter? Needs more time.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:45.900\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:49.500\nYou screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:55.500\nIf it lights up, the test tells you it's working. If it doesn't, well, it's probably time for a new one.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:04.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get a result.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:06.800\nIt helps us understand if something is working,"
