  "17f77544-7dfb-4ac7-9f2c-5489cbf6566b": {
    "id": "17f77544-7dfb-4ac7-9f2c-5489cbf6566b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:53:31.841653",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T22:12:41.116359",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_221241.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_221241.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:20.900\nNow, you probably already know what a test is in general, but in this context, a test is really just a way to see if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch \u2013 that's the test.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:33.700\nIf the light comes on, the test is passed! If it doesn't, well, it failed.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:44.100\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake and you poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test showing the cake is done.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:54.800\nSo, basically, a test is a simple procedure to confirm something. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:59.700\nThey help us make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:05.000\nThat's it! A quick check to see if something is correct.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:11.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
