    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:53:33.572013",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T22:14:51.391489",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_221451.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_221451.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of testing.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:15.800\nNow, don't worry, this isn't a pop quiz! In simple terms, a test is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and you take a bite to see if it tastes good. That's a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:30.100\nOr, imagine you're building with LEGOs. You put two pieces together and see if they click. That's another test!\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:36.000\nTests are important because they help us find problems early.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:45.200\nIf your cake doesn't taste right, you can adjust the recipe. If your LEGOs don't fit, you can try a different piece.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:57.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly. It's about finding problems and fixing them so things work better in the long run.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:01.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "cb6c814a-0afc-465f-a788-a1deefaa2f3b": {
    "id": "cb6c814a-0afc-465f-a788-a1deefaa2f3b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:53:34.155413",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T22:15:30.228094",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_221530.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_221530.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.100\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something specific about a person or thing.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like a mini-experiment to get information. For example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:32.700\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your overall health.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:46.500\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test! You're testing your recipe and skills to see if you can make a delicious treat.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:54.700\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same basic goal: to learn something new. They help us understand things better and make informed decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d759b55e-6ab9-45b9-a6c4-741faa0dfe03": {
    "id": "d759b55e-6ab9-45b9-a6c4-741faa0dfe03",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
