    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_221618.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_221618.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE: The times below are suggestions. Adjust as needed to sync perfectly with the audio.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:16.400\nNow, a test is really just a way to check what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like a measuring stick for your brain! It helps us see how much you've learned about a certain topic.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:40.100\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes, like multiple choice questions, short answer questions, or even hands-on activities.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:48.200\nFor example, if you're learning about animals, a test might ask you to name different animals or describe their habitats.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:57.600\nOr, if you're learning to bake, a test might involve actually baking a cake to see if you understand the recipe.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:04.600\nSo, in short, a test is a tool to see how well you understand something. It\u2019s a way to measure your knowledge and skills.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:08.100\nAnd remember, it's okay if you don't know everything!\n\n01:08.100 --> 01:11.700\nTests are just a way to learn and improve.\n\n01:11.700 --> 01:14.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
