    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_221904.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" thrown around,\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.800\nbut what does it really mean?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:09.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:13.600\nThink of it like an experiment, but often on a smaller scale.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:18.000\nWe use tests all the time to see if something is working, or to check its quality.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:23.700\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:27.000\nThat's a test to see if it's done!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.100\nOr, when you buy a new phone, you might try making a call.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:34.700\nThat's a test to see if the phone works.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:38.300\nTests help us make decisions based on evidence.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:43.100\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:53.000\nTo recap, a test is a process to gather information and check if something works or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:58.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
