    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:19.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. Think of it like this: it's an experiment, or a process, designed to give us information.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:24.900\nImagine you're baking a cake. To test if it's done, you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:35.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test result telling you the cake is ready. Or, think about checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:40.900\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test is positive!\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:51.700\nSo, tests are everywhere, helping us understand the world around us. They involve performing an action and observing the result to learn something.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:59.700\nIn essence, a test is a simple way to gather information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
