    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:53:56.411727",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T22:51:43.733656",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_225143.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_225143.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore something really fundamental: the test.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:17.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:27.900\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you test it by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:30.400\nAnother example?\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:38.300\nLet's say you're learning a new language. A quiz on vocabulary is a test to see how well you've learned those words.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:46.200\nOr, if you build a bridge with LEGOs, you might test it by putting some weight on it to see if it's strong enough.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:54.100\nSo, a test is basically an action you take to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:02.300\nIn short, it's a way to find out if something works as it should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
