    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works, so you screw it into the lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:27.400\nThat's a test! You\u2019re testing if the lightbulb lights up.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:32.600\nAnother example is a recipe. Following the recipe is a test.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:44.500\nIf you follow the instructions and the cake turns out great, the recipe passed the test. But if it's a disaster, well, the recipe might need some adjustments!\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:56.000\nSo, a test is basically a procedure to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation. It helps us understand if things are working as they should.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:02.400\nThat's the basic idea behind testing. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
