    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:22.700\nIt could be anything! We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:29.500\nThink about it: a taste test tells you if you like a new flavor of ice cream.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:36.300\nA spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:42.900\nAnd a doctor might run tests to check your health.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:52.600\nSo, tests help us measure, evaluate, or figure something out. They give us data, which is just a fancy word for information.\n\n00:52.600 --> 01:02.300\nLet's say you water two plants differently. Testing, or observing, how they grow tells you which watering method works best.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:06.900\nBasically, a test is just a way to learn something new or confirm what we already suspect.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:10.700\nIt\u2019s all about gathering information.\n\n01:10.700 --> 01:14.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
