    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_231334.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:19.000\nYou've probably taken a few in school, but what is a test, really?\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:27.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:34.000\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:40.700\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if your cake is done, you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:46.500\nThat's a test! If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:52.300\nOr maybe you want to see if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:58.800\nIf it lights up, it passes the test. Tests can be simple, like checking the cake, or more complicated, like a quiz at school.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:00.700\nThe important thing is they help us understand things better.\n```"
