    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:04.000\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:06.800\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:10.100\nIt's like checking if your bike tires have enough air before you go for a ride.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:12.400\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:16.000\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:19.300\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to make sure it tastes good.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:20.800\nThese are both simple tests!\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:26.300\nEssentially, a test helps us understand if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:30.500\nIt can be a simple observation, a question with a yes or no answer, or something more complex.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:33.500\nThe goal is always the same: to gain information.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:37.400\nSo, tests help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:42.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
