    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_231506.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_231506.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:21.500\nIt\u2019s a process designed to give us information about something specific. Think of it like this: you might taste a cake to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:30.900\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. In school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:40.900\nTests can take many forms. They can be written quizzes, physical exams, or even just trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:50.100\nThe important thing is that they give us data. So, to recap: a test is a procedure that provides information.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:58.000\nIt helps us learn, understand, and make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
