    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_231604.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you probably think of school when you hear that word, but a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:25.700\nIt's how we check if something works, or if something is true. Think about it like this: you might test if your shoes fit before you buy them.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:30.900\nYou try them on! Or maybe you test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:35.200\nYou follow the instructions and then taste the result. See? Testing is all around us.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:46.800\nSo, a test is basically a procedure, a set of steps, that helps us gather information and make a decision.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:55.300\nIt could be a quiz in class, a taste test in the kitchen, or even just checking if the light switch turns on the light.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:59.100\nIt\u2019s all about finding out.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:08.800\nTo recap, a test is a process to learn about something, using steps to get information.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:15.100\nWe use tests every day to make decisions, big and small.\n\n01:15.100 --> 01:16.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
