    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nOkay, so you're curious about tests!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:19.700\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it as an experiment or a way to check if something is working or true.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:34.800\nFor example, you might take a math test at school to see how well you understand addition.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:44.900\nOr, a doctor might order a blood test to check if you're healthy.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:46.600\nSee?\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:49.900\nDifferent kinds of tests, but they all share the same goal:\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:51.600\nto get information.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:57.000\nAnother example could be testing a new recipe.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:01.100\nYou follow the instructions, bake the cake, and then taste it.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:03.800\nThe taste test tells you if the recipe is good\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:06.000\nor needs adjusting.\n\n01:06.000 --> 01:12.700\nSo, remember, a test is a process used to gather information, check understanding, or evaluate performance.\n\n01:12.700 --> 01:18.400\nThey come in many forms and help us learn and make informed decisions.\n\n01:18.400 --> 01:21.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
