    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:12.400\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:18.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking. You use a test!\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:24.600\nYou poke them with a toothpick. If it comes out clean, the test says they're ready.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:37.300\nIn science and math, tests are used to confirm ideas. For example, if you think all birds can fly, you might test that by observing different types of birds.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:45.300\nIf you find one that can't, like a penguin, your test shows that your original idea wasn't quite right.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:58.500\nTests help us learn and improve our understanding. They can be simple or complex, but the basic idea is always the same: to gather evidence and see if it supports a claim.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:09.200\nSo, remember, a test is a tool to check if something is true or working as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
