    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:11.700\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:21.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:31.700\nThat something could be anything \u2013 your knowledge, your skills, or even the quality of a product.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:34.900\nThink about it like this:\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:37.700\na spelling test measures how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:40.800\nA cooking test might measure how well you can bake a cake.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:44.900\nAnd a durability test on a phone checks how well it can handle being dropped.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:48.300\nTests help us understand where we are, what we need to improve on,\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:51.100\nand if something is working as it should.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:52.800\nThey give us information and help us make better decisions.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:54.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a measurement tool.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:55.200\nIt helps us learn and grow!\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:58.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
