    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_234002.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 but don't worry, it's not a pop quiz!\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:16.100\nA test is simply a way to find out something specific. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:24.300\nFor example, you might test if a light bulb works by turning it on. The light turning on is the answer!\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:32.100\nOr, you could test how fast you can run by timing yourself. The time you get is the result of your test.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:40.700\nTests are used everywhere, from checking if a recipe tastes good to making sure a bridge is strong enough to hold cars.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:53.100\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things work as expected. So, remember, a test is just a way to get information and find out something new.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
