    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it like a check-up for your brain, or for a new gadget.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:36.800\nThe main goal of a test is to measure knowledge or ability. It helps us understand what we've learned or what a device can do.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:40.600\nFor example, a spelling test shows how well you can spell words.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:49.000\nOr, a stress test on a bridge checks its strength and safety. See? Different things, same basic idea.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:54.900\nSo, a test is a way of measuring something to see how well it performs or how much knowledge someone has. It helps us learn and improve! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "996dfa02-7e6e-4f6d-b044-4b79e912eedb": {
    "id": "996dfa02-7e6e-4f6d-b044-4b79e912eedb",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:54:35.223667",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T23:50:30.264692",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_235030.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_235030.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:19.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about someone or something. It could be a set of questions, a task you need to complete, or even just observing how something behaves.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:28.800\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks how well you know your words.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:35.900\nA taste test lets you decide which food you like best.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:51.900\nAnd a doctor might run tests to see how healthy you are. Tests help us make decisions and learn new things. They give us information that we can use to improve, understand, and explore the world around us.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:55.700\nSo, whether it\u2019s a quiz at school or an experiment in a lab, tests are all about finding answers.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:58.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d4b2b15d-8306-44af-87ed-82868ccca94e": {
    "id": "d4b2b15d-8306-44af-87ed-82868ccca94e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:54:35.691181",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-02T23:51:14.226253",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260102_235114.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_235114.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:16.300\nToday we're going to learn about tests.\nThink of a test as a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:25.400\nIt could be a test to see if you know your ABCs, or a test to see if something is working correctly.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:34.200\nBasically, a test is a set of questions or tasks designed to measure knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:41.000\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or a chef might taste a dish to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:47.800\nAnother example is checking if a light bulb works.\nYou plug it in, and that's the test!\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:52.700\nIf it lights up, it passes the test.\nIf it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:56.100\nSo remember, a test is just a simple way to check something.\n\n00:56.100 --> 00:58.500\nIt helps us understand more about the world around us.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ad4d34f0-420c-4238-bbf4-103e4da71c69": {
    "id": "ad4d34f0-420c-4238-bbf4-103e4da71c69",
    "topic": "Test",
