    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_235208.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:25.200\nIt's like a measuring stick for your knowledge. Think about it like this: If you want to know if you can bake a cake,\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:28.500\nyou follow a recipe and then\u2026 bake a cake!\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:31.800\nThe cake itself is the test.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:42.500\nDid it rise? Does it taste good? Those are the results. In school, tests can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.200\nThey help your teachers see how well you\u2019re understanding the material.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:59.800\nAnd even outside of school, you take tests all the time! Trying a new recipe, learning a new game, even figuring out which route to take to get somewhere faster\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.500\n- those are all little tests you\u2019re running in your head.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:14.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check your understanding. It helps you and others see what you know and what you might need to learn more about.\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:18.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
