    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260102_235340.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:04.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:09.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:16.100\nIt\u2019s how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:20.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:23.700\nYou do a test \u2013 you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:27.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you it's ready!\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:30.200\nAnother example?\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:34.000\nLet\u2019s say you\u2019re learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.600\nEach time you try, you\u2019re essentially testing your balance.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:42.300\nYou might wobble, but that\u2019s the test giving you feedback.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:47.700\nYou learn from each wobble, and eventually, you pass the test and ride smoothly!\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:52.400\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:56.000\nIt helps us learn, improve, and understand things better.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:57.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
