    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_000332.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:21.100\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true. Think about it like this: you want to bake a cake.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:29.600\nBefore your guests arrive, you might take a small bite \u2013 that's a test! You're testing to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:38.500\nOr, imagine you're buying a new toy. You\u2019ll probably play with it for a few minutes to see if it's fun and works the way it should. That's another test!\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:42.100\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:49.400\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:58.900\nAnd you use tests all the time without even realizing it! So, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:06.600\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working the way they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
