    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_000549.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:19.800\nIt's a process, or a series of actions, designed to see if something is true, or to measure something.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:29.100\nThink about it like this: you might take a spelling test at school. That test helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:34.700\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:40.300\nAnother example? Let's say you're baking a cake.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:51.900\nYou might poke the cake with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done!\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:56.900\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.200\nWhether it's in school, at the doctor's, or even in the kitchen,\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:03.700\ntests help us understand the world around us.\n```"
  },
