    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_000733.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:16.300\nToday we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:26.600\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:33.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand more.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:41.000\nAt its core, a test involves running a procedure or experiment to observe and measure a result.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.200\nThis result then gives us information.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:51.700\nFor example, think about a taste test.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:54.700\nYou try two different cookies and decide which one you like better.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:55.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:58.700\nOr, maybe you take a quiz at school to see how much you've learned about a subject.\n\n00:58.700 --> 00:59.600\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.800\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and learning something new.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:07.700\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the basic idea is always the same:\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:11.500\nobserve, measure, and learn.\n\n01:11.500 --> 01:14.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
