    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_001048.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:18.100\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something. It\u2019s a process we use to gather information and see how well something works, or how good someone is at something.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:28.100\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:42.600\nA taste test helps you decide which cookie tastes better. Or, a stress test on a bridge makes sure it's safe for cars to drive on.\n\n00:42.600 --> 01:00.500\nSo, tests can be used for lots of different things, from checking your knowledge to making sure things are working properly. Basically, it's a way to answer a question or solve a problem by getting some real-world results.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:07.399\nTo sum it up, a test is a method for gathering information, whether it\u2019s about your spelling, cookie flavors, or even bridge safety. They help us learn and make better decisions.\n\n01:07.399 --> 01:07.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
