    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:25.600\nIt's a process we use to gather information or check if something is working correctly. Think of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:35.000\nOr, if you want to see if your bike brakes are working, you might squeeze the levers and see if the bike stops. That's another test.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:39.400\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:47.800\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned. Scientists use tests to prove if their ideas are right.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:57.400\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick. So, remember, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:05.800\nIt's a simple process that helps us understand the world around us better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
