    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_002316.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:08.500\nnot the kind you take in school,\nbut tests in the context of\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:11.300\nchecking if something is working correctly.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:14.800\nBasically, a test is a procedure designed\nto see if something behaves the way it\u2019s\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:16.400\nsupposed to.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if\na light bulb works, so you screw it in and\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:22.700\nflip the switch.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:24.700\nIf the light turns on, the test passes!\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:31.200\nAnother example: you\u2019re baking a cake, and\nthe recipe says it's done when a toothpick\ninserted into the center comes out clean.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:34.200\nThat toothpick test tells you if the cake\nis cooked through.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:39.200\nSo, in short, a test is just a way of checking\nif something is doing what it\u2019s meant to do.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:44.700\nTesting helps us catch problems early and\nmake sure things work the way they should.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:47.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
