    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:19.400\nThink of it as a question you ask to get an answer.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:26.800\nTests can take many forms.\nMaybe it's a quiz in school to see what you've learned.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:33.400\nOr it could be testing a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:37.600\nEven checking if a lightbulb works is a kind of test!\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:46.000\nYou're testing to see if it lights up.\nSo, in all these cases, you're asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:49.600\nDoes the student know the material?\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:52.300\nDoes the recipe taste good?\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:54.200\nDoes the lightbulb work?\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:01.800\nThat's what tests are all about!\nThey help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:15.200\nTo recap, a test is a method of finding information, and they come in all shapes and sizes.\nThey help us understand if something works as expected or meets a certain standard.\n\n01:15.200 --> 01:18.899\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
