    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_002657.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:17.600\nThink of a test as simply a way to check if something works, or if something is true. It's like a little investigation to see if things are as they should be.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:27.200\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. Or, a doctor might use a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:29.700\nSee? Pretty straightforward.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:35.900\nLet's say you're baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:42.500\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:53.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to find out if something is correct or working properly. It helps us make sure things are just right.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:57.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
