    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:23.700\nIt's a procedure designed to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:30.600\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:37.500\nThat's a test! The toothpick tells you if the inside is still gooey.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:44.600\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. Each time you try, you're testing your balance.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:51.700\nYou might wobble and fall, but that's feedback. It tells you what to adjust.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:58.800\nSo, tests can be quizzes at school, experiments in a lab, or even just trying something new. They help us learn and improve.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:05.000\nBasically, a test is just a structured way to get information. It gives us results we can use.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:11.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
