    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:55:06.418326",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T00:33:41.397831",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_003341.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_003341.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.700\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but really, a test is just a way of finding something out.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works. You screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:26.500\nYou're testing if the lightbulb lights up.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:32.900\nOr, maybe you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done. You poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:39.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's the test, and it tells you the cake is ready.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:52.600\nBasically, a test is any action you take to check if something is true or working correctly. It can be super simple, like checking if your shoes are tied, or more complex, like a medical test.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:58.400\nSo remember, a test is just a way to get information. It helps us understand things better!\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:04.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0d4bc033-987e-41d7-80f5-329f25fb1f16": {
    "id": "0d4bc033-987e-41d7-80f5-329f25fb1f16",
    "topic": "Test",
