    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_003430.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_003430.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of a test.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:19.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about someone or something. Think of it like asking a question to see what the answer is, or trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:28.600\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. For example, a school test helps teachers understand what students have learned.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:38.800\nA taste test lets you decide which flavor of ice cream you like best. And a medical test helps doctors figure out what's going on inside your body.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:49.700\nSo, whether it's a quiz at school, trying a new recipe, or a check-up at the doctor, a test is all about gathering information.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:55.800\nIt's a simple way to learn more. In short, a test helps us discover something.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:04.600\nIt can be about knowledge, preferences, or even our health. It allows us to gain a better understanding.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:08.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
