    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_003520.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:25.400\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\nThink about it like this: a chef tastes a soup to see if it needs more salt \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:35.800\nOr, when you try on a shoe to see if it fits \u2013 that\u2019s another test!\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:48.700\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb works by turning it on.\nOr, they can be more complex, like a doctor using blood tests to see if you\u2019re healthy.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:59.900\nThe goal is always the same: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:08.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out.\nIt's about asking questions and looking for answers.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:11.600\nIt's a key part of learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n01:11.600 --> 01:15.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
