    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_003651.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.700\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:26.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:36.400\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, or seeing how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:43.500\nThe main idea is to present something, then observe the result.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:53.200\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:00.300\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge on a specific topic.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:07.400\nThink of it like this: Baking a cake is a test!\n\n01:07.400 --> 01:16.300\nYou follow a recipe, then see if the cake tastes good.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:23.100\nIf it does, the test was successful.\n\n01:23.100 --> 01:33.900\nIf not, you know something needs to be adjusted next time.\n\n01:33.900 --> 01:41.000\nSo, tests help us learn, diagnose, and improve things.\n\n01:41.000 --> 01:48.200\nThey\u2019re all about gathering information to make better decisions.\n\n01:48.200 --> 01:50.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
