    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_003833.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:17.200\nNow, a test isn't just something you take in school. It's really any process we use to check if something works, or to see what its properties are.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch. That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:29.800\nThe outcome tells you if the bulb is good or burned out.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:34.400\nOr, let\u2019s say you're baking a cake. You taste the batter.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:39.000\nThat\u2019s a test to see if you need more sugar!\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:48.600\nWe use tests all the time, big and small, to learn and make better decisions.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:55.700\nSo, a test is simply a way to gather information about something. It helps us understand how things work and make sure they\u2019re doing what they\u2019re supposed to.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:58.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
