    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_004535.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:03.800\nToday we're going to explore something super important:\n\n00:03.800 --> 00:04.300\nTests!\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:05.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:08.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like this: you test if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:12.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:14.500\nWe use tests all the time, in all sorts of ways.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:16.900\nA doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:19.300\nA teacher uses tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:22.500\nEven your phone uses tests to make sure all its apps are working correctly.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:23.400\nSo, examples?\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:24.800\nA spelling test, a blood test,\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:27.700\neven just trying to see if a lightbulb works is a little test.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:31.300\nThey all help us understand if something is working the way it should, or if something needs to be fixed.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:34.500\nBasically, a test is a way to find out information and make sure things are right.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:35.300\nEasy peasy!\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:37.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
