    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_004757.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:22.400\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life. For example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n00:22.400 --> 00:26.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test telling you the cake is done.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:39.200\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:48.900\nTests help us learn if things are working the way they should, or if we need to make changes. They're a fundamental part of understanding how things work around us.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:55.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something and get an answer.\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
