    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:58.4\n1\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n2\n00:03.200 --> 00:06.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n3\n00:06.300 --> 00:09.100\nIt's a process designed to get information.\n\n4\n00:09.100 --> 00:12.900\nThink of it like asking a question and then finding the answer.\n\n5\n00:12.900 --> 00:17.100\nFor example, a spelling test helps us see how well someone knows how to spell words.\n\n6\n00:17.100 --> 00:20.400\nOr, think about a taste test!\n\n7\n00:20.400 --> 00:23.000\nYou try different foods to see which one you like best.\n\n8\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.800\nIn science, you might test a hypothesis, like if plants grow better in sunlight or shade.\n\n9\n00:27.800 --> 00:30.900\nYou set up an experiment and observe the results.\n\n10\n00:30.900 --> 00:38.600\nSo, a test can be a quiz in school, a way to check if something is working correctly, or even just a way to see what your favorite flavor is.\n\n11\n00:38.600 --> 00:44.900\nBasically, it's a method for gathering data and understanding something better.\n\n12\n00:44.900 --> 00:47.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
