    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_005957.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see if something is true.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:34.600\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:39.800\nThat's a test! So, tests help us confirm things.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:47.600\nThey tell us if something is good, bad, right, or wrong.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:58.100\nThey're super useful for solving problems and making sure things are working as they should. In short, a test is a simple way to find out information.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:01.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
