    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:55:30.655296",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T01:08:45.169708",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_010845.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_010845.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process, or a series of actions, designed to reveal information.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy, or a teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:35.300\nA test doesn't always have to be a formal exam. For example, you might \"test\" if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:45.300\nIf it lights up, the test is successful! Or, you might \"test\" a recipe by making it and seeing if it tastes good.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:56.400\nSo, to recap, a test is any method used to gather information and learn something new. They help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:56.400 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
