    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_012151.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:25.800\nIt\u2019s how we check if something is true, or how well something works. Think of it like this: if you want to know if an oven is hot, you might carefully touch it to test the temperature.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:35.400\nOr, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp and see if it lights up. Those are both simple tests!\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:45.600\nTests can also be more formal, like a spelling test in school. That test helps your teacher see how well you understand spelling rules.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:55.500\nSo, tests help us understand things better, whether it's checking if an oven is hot or seeing how well you know your ABCs.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:03.100\nEssentially, a test is just a way of finding answers. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
