    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_012400.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests. A test, in its simplest form, is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like a question you ask to get an answer. It could be a quiz at school to see how well you understand a topic, or even something you do every day, like testing if the water is too hot before you jump in the shower.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:29.500\nYou're testing the water!\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:33.000\nLet's say you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:36.500\nYou stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:43.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:53.700\nSo, a test is just a simple way to get information. You perform some action, observe the result, and learn something new.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:58.300\nIt helps us make better decisions and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
