    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_012611.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHello everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:03.600\nToday we're going to explore the concept of a test.\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:07.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:09.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:10.900\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:15.400\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might taste the batter before putting it in the oven \u2013 that's a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:20.600\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again. That's a test to see if it fixes the problem!\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:24.800\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. It helps show what words you know.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:27.000\nOr a medical test can check if you are healthy.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:34.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new. It helps us understand things better, whether it\u2019s about cake batter, a broken phone, or even ourselves.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:37.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
