    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_013216.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:07.600\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:14.500\nIt could be a quiz at school, a medical exam, or even just trying a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:18.900\nThe core idea is the same: you\u2019re doing something to get information.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:24.300\nThink about it like this: you might take a spelling test to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:29.700\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:31.300\nSee?\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:32.600\nDifferent situations,\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:34.800\nsame basic principle.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:38.800\nAnother example?\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:41.600\nImagine you're baking cookies.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:45.000\nYou taste one to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:46.700\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:49.000\nYou're testing the flavor.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:52.800\nSo, tests are all about learning something new by trying something out.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:55.700\nThey help us understand things better.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:58.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
