    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_013320.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find out if something works as it should.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.800\nOr, imagine you buy a new toy. You play with it to see if all the buttons work. That's also a test!\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:35.700\nTesting helps us make sure things are safe, reliable, and do what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:50.500\nWhether it's testing a cake, a toy, or even a bridge, tests give us valuable information.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:59.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of checking if something works correctly. It's all about finding out information!\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
