    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_014157.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.300\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something, right? It's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works. So, you put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:28.500\nIf the light bulb lights up, the test passes. If it doesn\u2019t, the test fails.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:34.200\nAnother example could be a taste test. You try a new cookie to see if you like it.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:43.100\nYour reaction, whether you like it or not, is the result of the test.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:52.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something. It helps us understand if things are working as expected.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:56.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
