  "e29775d5-49b3-4fbf-bd40-361187a456b6": {
    "id": "e29775d5-49b3-4fbf-bd40-361187a456b6",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:56:00.326071",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T01:49:10.515645",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_014910.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_014910.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:18.200\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something. Think of it like this: it's a set of questions or tasks designed to measure your knowledge, skill, or even your opinion about something.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:29.900\nFor example, a simple quiz in school is a test to see how well you understood the lesson. Or, a taste test is a test to see which flavor people prefer.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:44.500\nA doctor might even run tests to figure out what's making you feel unwell. So, whether it's a pop quiz, a survey, or a medical exam, a test is all about gathering information.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:51.200\nThey help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions. That's testing in a nutshell!\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:54.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "467b4d78-9545-46e2-963b-fe0d4e9939ec": {
    "id": "467b4d78-9545-46e2-963b-fe0d4e9939ec",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
