    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T01:50:01.915586",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_015001.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_015001.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests, a fundamental idea in pretty much everything we do.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:19.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer that tells you more.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:26.700\nThe \"something else\" could be anything! It could be a cookie recipe, to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:35.700\nIt could be a new medicine, to see if it helps people get better. Or even a lightbulb, to see if it actually lights up.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:44.500\nThe test is the process you use to check it. For example, if you want to test a cookie recipe, you bake the cookies and then taste them.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:53.300\nIf you like them, the test was successful! If the lightbulb lights up when you plug it in, it passes the test.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:03.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new by observing and evaluating. It helps us make sure things work the way they should!\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:07.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
