    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_015201.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.800\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.800 --> 00:05.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:09.100\nThink of it like an experiment, but often a bit more straightforward.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:13.100\nWe use tests all the time to see if something works, if something is true, or just to understand something better.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:17.600\nFor example, you might test a recipe by making it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:23.400\nOr a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:27.900\nEven trying out a new video game is a type of test \u2013 you're testing if you like it!\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:31.900\nBasically, a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:37.300\nThey can be simple or complicated, but they all share the same goal: to learn something new.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:39.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
