    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_015422.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like a way to check your understanding.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:31.000\nSo, how does it work? Well, a test usually involves answering questions or performing tasks.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:41.800\nThe answers or results are then compared to a standard or a correct answer key.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:49.100\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:51.400\nOr, a taste test might check which flavor of ice cream you like best.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:53.700\nTests help us learn and improve.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:55.300\nIn short, a test is just a tool to measure knowledge or performance.\n```"
