    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:56:07.952479",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T01:59:30.852591",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_015930.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_015930.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something fundamental: the concept of a test.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:15.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information or evidence to see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake. You test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:27.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:35.100\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken. You test it by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:42.300\nIf it lights up, the bulb is fine! Tests help us make decisions and understand things better.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:49.500\nThey're used everywhere, from baking to science to checking if your homework is correct.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:55.100\nSo remember, a test is just a simple way to find out if something is what we expect it to be.\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:58.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
