    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nThink of a test as a way to check something. It's how we find out if something is working the way it should, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:20.400\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:25.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:34.700\nOr, think about checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:45.200\nTests aren't just for cakes and lightbulbs though. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, and scientists use tests to prove their ideas.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:58.200\nBasically, a test helps us learn something important about the world around us. So, remember, a test is a way to check something and find out if it's working or true.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:01.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
