    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nA test is basically a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you know something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:32.400\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. You might take a written test in school, or a scientist might run a test in a lab.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:43.500\nA computer programmer tests their code to make sure it doesn\u2019t have any errors.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:51.500\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:59.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:11.700\nSo, a test is just a way to get information and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:11.700 --> 01:18.300\nTo recap, tests help us check things, find problems, and make sure we're on the right track.\n\n01:18.300 --> 01:23.300\nThey\u2019re used everywhere, from the kitchen to the classroom!\n\n01:23.300 --> 01:26.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
