    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about a certain subject. Think of it like a measuring stick for your knowledge.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:25.800\nThey come in all shapes and sizes. You might have multiple choice questions, where you pick the right answer from a few options.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:35.300\nOr maybe fill-in-the-blanks, where you complete a sentence. Some tests even ask you to write out your answers in your own words.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:46.100\nFor example, a simple test could be asking \"What color is the sky?\" Or \"What is one plus one?\" These are easy, right?\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:55.000\nThe point is, tests help you and your teachers understand what you've learned and what you might need a little extra help with.\n\n00:55.000 --> 01:04.200\nSo, in short, a test is just a tool to check your knowledge. It helps identify what you know and what you're still learning.\n\n01:04.200 --> 01:07.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
