    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_021533.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.400\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but tests are just a way of finding out information about something.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:25.600\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get. The main idea behind a test is to check if something works correctly, or to see what its qualities are.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:35.500\nThink of it like this: a taste test is a test to see how something tastes! Or a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:41.100\nAnother example is a battery test. It tells you how much power your battery has left.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:51.700\nSo, tests can be about anything, from checking if your cake is done by poking it with a fork, to seeing if a new app works on your phone.\n\n00:51.700 --> 01:00.400\nBasically, a test is a way to get information and learn something new. They help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:04.099\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
