    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.600\nToday, we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:10.500\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.500 --> 00:13.600\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:17.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:20.100\nYou do a test!\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:23.500\nYou might poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:26.800\nIf it comes out clean, the test tells you they're ready.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:31.200\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:34.200\nFalling down is part of the test!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:37.300\nIt shows you what not to do next time.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:42.000\nSo, a test can be anything from a simple check to a more formal experiment.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:48.800\nThe important thing is that it helps us learn and understand something better.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:49.800\nThat\u2019s the basic idea!\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:56.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
