    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_022524.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time in everyday life, whether we realize it or not.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:32.000\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:37.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a pass! The cake is ready!\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:42.800\nOr, imagine you're checking if a light bulb works. You flip the switch.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:48.400\nIf the light turns on, the test is successful. It means the bulb is good!\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:58.400\nTests can be simple or complex, but the basic idea is always the same: to check something and see if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:03.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out if something works, or if it's good enough.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:04.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
