    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:18.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like an experiment, but often with a set of questions or tasks.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:28.700\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:34.100\nImagine you're baking a cake. You taste the batter to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:39.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:45.500\nOr, let's say you're trying to figure out which route to take to school.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:50.000\nYou might try one route one day, and another the next, to see which one is faster.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:51.800\nAgain, that's a test!\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:58.200\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your bathwater is too hot.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:01.800\nThe important thing is that they help us learn and make better decisions.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:06.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of gathering information.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:08.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
