    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_023058.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:24.900\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:29.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your new lightbulb works.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:39.500\nSo, you screw it in and flip the switch. That\u2019s a test! The result tells you if the bulb is good or if it\u2019s broken.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:49.800\nOr imagine you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:58.100\nSo, tests are all about checking things, big or small. They help us learn and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:01.900\nIn short, a test is a way to find out information.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:04.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
