    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_023700.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:20.800\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out information or check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:31.900\nThink of it like this: you take a quiz in school to test your knowledge, or a doctor runs tests to check your health.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:41.000\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on, or more complex, like running a computer program to see if it works as expected.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:47.500\nThe important thing is that they give you results.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:59.600\nFor example, you might test a recipe by making a small batch first. Or, if you're building a birdhouse, you might test if the roof keeps the rain out. See? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:09.300\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is a way to gather information, verify something, or see if something works properly.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:14.400\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:19.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
