    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_023749.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:14.800\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works as it should.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:28.200\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer. Essentially, a test helps us understand if something is right or wrong, true or false, pass or fail.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:37.700\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. For instance, when you flip a light switch, you're testing if the light bulb works.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:43.300\nIf it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:48.100\nOr imagine baking a cake. You test it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:52.900\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's another test!\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:04.200\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is simply a way to verify if something meets a certain standard. It tells us if things are working the way they're supposed to.\n\n01:04.200 --> 01:07.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
