    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.100\nWhat is a test, really? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:28.700\nIt could be checking if a light bulb works, checking if you understand a new concept, or even checking if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:39.100\nEssentially, you're performing an action or asking a question to get an answer, and that answer tells you something about the thing you're testing.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:48.000\nFor example, if you press the power button on your TV and it turns on, that's a test, and the result tells you the TV is working.\n\n00:48.000 --> 01:00.800\nOr, if you take a multiple-choice quiz and get most of the answers right, that test shows you understand the material. Tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:04.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get information about it.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:08.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
