    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_025358.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something works correctly, or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your new toy car runs well, so you give it a push and watch it go! That's a test!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.400\nAnother example is when a baker tastes their cake batter.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:38.700\nThey're testing to see if it tastes good before they bake the whole cake. Or, even simpler, flipping a light switch to see if the light turns on. That's a test too!\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:49.900\nSo, basically, a test is any action you take to see if something meets your expectations or works the way it should.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:56.200\nIt helps you learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
