    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:13.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to see what you know or can do.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:21.200\nThink of it like a check-up, but for your brain! It helps us understand how much you've learned about a specific topic.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:29.400\nTests can come in lots of different forms. Maybe it's a multiple-choice quiz where you pick the right answer, or perhaps it's a written exam where you explain your thinking.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:41.400\nSometimes, it can even be a practical demonstration, like showing you know how to ride a bike. For example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of words.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:49.200\nA math test checks your ability to solve problems. And a cooking test might check if you can follow a recipe.\n\n00:49.200 --> 01:02.100\nSo, in short, a test is a tool used to measure knowledge or skills. It helps you and your teachers understand what you've mastered and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.799\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
