    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_025932.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_025932.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:24.200\nIt's how we gather information and see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:37.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, maybe you take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:48.300\nEven baking a cake is a sort of test \u2013 you're testing the recipe to see if it turns out delicious!\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:53.900\nSo, a test can be a question, an experiment, or even just an observation.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:06.100\nThe important thing is that it helps us learn something new. Tests help us understand the world better and make informed decisions.\n\n01:06.100 --> 01:10.400\nTo recap, a test is a method for gathering information to determine the truth or quality of something.\n\n01:10.400 --> 01:14.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
