    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_030035.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:08.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:21.500\nIt's a process of asking a question and looking for an answer.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:27.000\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:29.900\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:34.600\nYou might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:35.800\nThat poke is a test!\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:40.400\nOr, think about checking the weather forecast.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:42.800\nThat's testing to see if you need an umbrella.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:45.800\nIn school, tests help us see how well we've learned something.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:51.500\nBut tests aren't just for school.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:54.500\nThey're used everywhere to check if things are working, or to understand something better.\n\n00:54.500 --> 00:57.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of asking a question and finding the answer.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:00.400\nIt's a tool for learning and understanding.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:02.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
