    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_030753.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:07.200\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to see what you know or can do.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like this: imagine you're learning to ride a bike. The first few times you try, you might wobble a lot.\nBut after some practice, you can ride smoothly.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:28.000\nA test would be like riding your bike and showing someone you can stay balanced and steer.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:32.000\nTests aren't just in school, either!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:37.000\nWhen you try a new recipe, tasting the food is a test to see if it's good.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:45.000\nOr when you download a new app, using it is a test to see if it works the way you expect.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:51.000\nSo, tests help us understand what we've learned or how well something works.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:57.000\nThey can be a bit nerve-wracking, but they're also a great way to see how far you've come!\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
