    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_032012.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:17.900\nA test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:24.900\nTests help us see if things are working correctly, or if they need some fixing.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:34.300\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\nA medical test helps a doctor figure out what\u2019s going on with your health.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:44.800\nFor example, a taste test can tell you if you like a new flavor of ice cream.\nOr, a spelling test shows you how well you know your words.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:52.600\nBasically, any time you\u2019re checking something to see if it\u2019s right or working properly, you\u2019re doing a test!\n\n00:52.600 --> 01:03.800\nSo, tests are all about checking things.\nThey can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all help us understand something better.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:07.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
