    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_032418.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:21.000\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:28.700\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:38.300\nOr, when you learn something new in school, your teacher gives you a test to see how much you understand.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:47.900\nFor example, a simple test could be asking, \"What color is the sky?\" The answer, blue, tells you something!\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:58.400\nAnother test could be tasting food to see if it's sweet or sour. So, to recap, a test is just a method for getting information.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:02.000\nIt helps us learn things about ourselves, the world around us, and everything in between.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:04.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "8a9b57f5-ca36-4678-9fae-3701dbbf9529": {
    "id": "8a9b57f5-ca36-4678-9fae-3701dbbf9529",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:57:07.879143",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T03:25:07.872893",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_032507.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_032507.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration: 66.9\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why they're important.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:07.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:12.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:13.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:17.200\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:21.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:25.200\nOr, a doctor might run blood tests to check your health.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:28.800\nAnother example is testing a new lightbulb to see if it actually lights up.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:34.400\nThe result of a test can be pass or fail, good or bad, or provide specific information.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:42.300\nTests are used everywhere, from schools to hospitals to factories, to make sure things are safe and reliable.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:44.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something!\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:47.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
