    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_032635.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:13.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:18.900\nIt's like asking a question and then figuring out the answer.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:27.500\nThink about it like this. A teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:35.400\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:43.300\nEven tasting a new food is a kind of test to see if you like it!\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:56.100\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes. Multiple choice questions, written answers, even physical activities can be tests. The important thing is they help us learn something new or confirm what we already know.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:08.600\nSo, to recap: A test is a way to gather information and learn something. It helps us understand things better, from school subjects to our own health.\n\n01:08.600 --> 01:11.800\nPretty useful, right?\n\n01:11.800 --> 01:14.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
