    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_033121.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:21.800\nIt's a process we use to check if something is working, or to see what something is made of, or even to figure out what you know.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:30.200\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you can test it by screwing it in and turning it on.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:37.300\nIf it lights up, the test is passed! Or, imagine you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:43.900\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If it comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:56.900\nTests are all around us. Doctors use tests to check your health, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even your car goes through tests to make sure it's running smoothly.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:06.200\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
