    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:03.900\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:05.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:10.300\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.300 --> 00:13.800\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:16.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:20.600\nOr, you might take a test in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:22.100\nSee?\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:23.600\nDifferent kinds of tests, same idea.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:27.900\nAnother example could be testing a new recipe.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:31.600\nYou follow the instructions, and then you taste it to see if it's good!\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:32.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:43.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a procedure or a method used to determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:47.800\nIt helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:49.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
