    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_033436.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like this: you might test if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:35.600\nOr, a doctor might test your temperature to see if you have a fever. Tests help us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:40.600\nFor example, a scientist might test different fertilizers.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:48.000\nOr, you might take a test in school to show what you've learned. See? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:53.500\nSo, to recap, a test is just a process to gather information.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:56.000\nIt helps us understand things better and make informed choices.\n```"
  },
  "8f2f1d1b-df37-4268-a063-9be4cbb8885e": {
    "id": "8f2f1d1b-df37-4268-a063-9be4cbb8885e",
