    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_033523.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:28.900\nIn many areas, like science or school, tests help us see if something is true or correct. For example, a math test checks if you understand addition.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:38.500\nOr a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:41.500\nAnother example? Baking a cake!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:55.100\nTasting it afterwards is a test to see if you used the right ingredients and baked it properly. So, tests are all about figuring things out and confirming whether something is working as expected.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:02.300\nThey help us learn and improve.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:09.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something. It helps us understand if things are working the way they should.\n\n01:09.800 --> 01:17.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
