    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This subtitles file was auto-generated based on the prompt.\nIt may not be perfectly accurate. Please review and edit as needed.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:22.300\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\nThink of it like this: a chef might test a sauce to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:35.900\nOr, you might take a practice quiz to see how well you understand a subject.\nTests can be formal, like exams in school, or informal, like trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:44.900\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\nA scientist might run tests to see if a new medicine works.\n\n00:44.900 --> 01:00.300\nThe key is that a test gives us information that helps us make decisions.\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information, whether it's about your knowledge, your health, or anything else.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:06.500\nIt helps us understand things better.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
