    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:07.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:13.100\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer in a structured way.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:16.900\nThink of it like this: you're testing the waters to see if they're cold before you jump in!\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:21.100\nTests can be formal, like a school exam that checks what you've learned.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:27.100\nOr they can be informal, like trying a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:29.900\nThe recipe is the test, and your taste buds are giving you the results!\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:34.600\nAnother example? Imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:37.600\nYou screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:40.600\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:43.300\nIf it doesn't, well, you know the bulb needs replacing.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:47.600\nTests help us learn, improve, and make decisions.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:51.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a method to get information.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:55.700\nWe use them all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
