    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.100\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:17.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:26.000\nIt helps us understand if something works, how well something performs, or even what something is made of.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.700\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by screwing it in and turning it on.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:37.900\nIf it lights up, the test passes! Another example is tasting food to see if it's good.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:50.700\nThat's a test too! Tests aren't just for lightbulbs and food, though. They're used in all sorts of areas, like science, medicine, and even everyday life.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:01.100\nThey help us learn, improve, and make better decisions. So, remember, a test is simply a way to learn something by trying something out. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
