    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:57:39.384645",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T04:05:22.914656",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_040522.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_040522.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information. It's a process designed to measure knowledge, skill, or ability.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:28.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done. You might use a toothpick, stick it in, and if it comes out clean, you know it's ready.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:37.200\nThat toothpick is essentially performing a test! We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:45.200\nA doctor might order blood tests to check your health. A teacher gives quizzes to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:55.300\nEven trying a new recipe is a test to see if you like it! So, remember, a test is just a tool for gathering information.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:03.100\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make better decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
