    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_040817.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:02.700\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:06.400\nNow, a test is simply a way\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:07.800\nto find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:15.200\nThink of it like an investigation.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:16.900\nWe want to know more, so we perform a test.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:20.200\nThe main idea is to see how something behaves under certain conditions.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:24.700\nFor example, a taste test tells you how good something tastes.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:28.200\nOr, a spelling test shows how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:32.100\nLet\u2019s say you want to know if a plant needs more water.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:34.200\nThe test?\nYou poke your finger in the soil.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:36.200\nIf it's dry, the plant needs water!\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:38.700\nAnother example: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:40.700\nYou stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:43.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:47.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a method to gather information.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:52.800\nIt helps us understand things better by observing how they react.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:55.900\nWe ask a question, and the test helps us find the answer.\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:58.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
