    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.799\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.799 --> 00:15.500\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.100\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:33.200\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:38.300\nOr, a doctor might check your temperature to test for a fever.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:43.100\nSee? It\u2019s about gathering information to understand something better.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:49.200\nAnother example is baking a cake.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:55.600\nYou can test if the cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:55.600 --> 01:01.100\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:04.300\nIf it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:13.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or gives us the information we need.\n\n01:13.100 --> 01:18.700\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n01:18.700 --> 01:24.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
