    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.500\nThink of a test as a way to check something out. It's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:24.000\nA test usually involves doing something specific and then observing what happens. For example, a taste test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:29.400\nYou taste two different cookies to see which one you like better. That's a test!\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:39.200\nOr, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better. Another simple test is checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:48.100\nYou screw it in and see if it lights up! The action is screwing it in, and the observation is whether or not it shines.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:55.500\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. They help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:04.300\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check something by doing something and watching what happens. Simple as that!\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5e507ab4-be5c-43c5-8abd-f3512aa5af6f": {
    "id": "5e507ab4-be5c-43c5-8abd-f3512aa5af6f",
