    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T04:16:03.050881",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_041602.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_041602.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nNow, you might be thinking of school exams, but a test, in a general sense, is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just asking, you're actually doing something to get the answer.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:35.600\nFor example, a taste test tells you if you like a food. A simple light switch is a test \u2013 you flip it on, and if the light comes on, the switch works!\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:46.900\nOr, if you're baking a cake, poking it with a toothpick is a test to see if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, then the cake is ready.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:57.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information by trying something out. It helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
