    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:06.000\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:10.000\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like an experiment, where you try something to see what happens.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:15.000\nTests are used everywhere!\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:18.000\nYour doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:21.000\nA chef might taste a dish to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.000\nAnd in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.000\nFor example, if you want to know if a plant needs water, you can test it by giving it some water and seeing if it perks up.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:37.000\nOr, if you're building a tower with blocks, you can test its strength by adding more blocks to see if it falls.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:47.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to learn something new or check if something is working.\nIt involves doing something and observing the result.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:50.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
