    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_042830.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:15.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in reality, a test is just a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:31.900\nThat's a test! In the world of computers and technology, tests are used to make sure that programs and systems are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:41.800\nFor example, imagine you have a calculator app. A test would be to input \"2 + 2\" and see if it gives you \"4\".\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:51.600\nIf the answer is right, the test passes! If it's wrong, the test fails, and that tells us something needs to be fixed.\n\n00:51.600 --> 01:00.600\nSo, tests are basically a way to make sure everything is working correctly. They help us find problems and make things better.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:04.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
