    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_044604.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you might test if a cake is done by sticking a fork in it.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:23.400\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! In school, tests help us check what we've learned.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:38.000\nThey can be quizzes, exams, or even just simple questions your teacher asks. The important thing is that they help you and your teacher understand what you know well, and what you might need to practice more.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:52.900\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem, checking your understanding of addition. Or, a reading test could ask you questions about a story, showing if you understood what you read.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:02.100\nSo, remember, tests are just tools to help us learn and grow. They show us where we're strong and where we can improve.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
