    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_044725.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like an experiment or a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:32.000\nThe basic idea is that you create a situation or ask a question, and then you observe the result.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:38.000\nThis result gives you information.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:44.000\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:49.800\nYou flip the switch. If the light comes on, the test passes!\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:57.600\nAnother example is a spelling test. You write down a word. If it's spelled correctly, you pass that part of the test.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.900\nSo, tests are all about gathering information by observing what happens in a controlled situation.\n01:00.900 --> 01:02.900\nThey help us understand how things work and whether they are performing as expected.\n01:02.900 --> 01:06.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
