    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_045041.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:18.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. We want to see if something works, if something is true, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: you might test a new toy to see if it's fun. Or you might test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:42.000\nIn science, tests are often called experiments. Scientists might test a new medicine to see if it helps people feel better, or they might test a new type of fertilizer to see if it helps plants grow.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:54.200\nThe important thing is that a test gives us information. So, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and check if something meets our expectations.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:00.700\nIt helps us learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
