    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_045601.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:15.900\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:29.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:36.500\nA test helps us check if something is working correctly, or to see how well we understand a topic.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:41.500\nFor example, a doctor might give you a physical exam to test your overall health.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:46.500\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to test your knowledge of what you've learned.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:54.500\nImagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might taste the batter to test if it's sweet enough.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:02.500\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works by turning it on.\nIf it lights up, the test is passed.\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:06.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method of investigation,\n\n01:06.000 --> 01:10.400\na way to get information and check if something is true,\n\n01:10.400 --> 01:13.800\ncorrect, or working as it should.\n\n01:13.800 --> 01:17.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
