    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_050613.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.900\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in this case, a test is really just a way to see if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:24.000\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer to confirm things.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb.\nTo test it, you screw it in and flip the switch.\nIf the light turns on, the test passes!\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:37.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.900\nThat\u2019s a successful test!\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:55.500\nSo, whether it's checking a lightbulb, baking a cake, or even something more complicated, a test is simply a way to find out if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:07.200\nWe set up a situation, observe the result, and then decide if everything is okay.\nTesting helps us make sure things are reliable and do what we expect.\n\n01:07.200 --> 01:10.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
