    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:25.400\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:29.300\nThink of it like this: You have a lightbulb, and you want to make sure it turns on.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:32.700\nThe test is plugging it in and flipping the switch.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:33.800\nDid it light up?\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:34.800\nGreat, it passed the test!\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:37.800\nAnother example could be baking a cake.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:39.200\nThe test is tasting it!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:42.100\nDoes it taste good?\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:44.200\nIs it cooked through?\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:46.900\nThat\u2019s how you test if your recipe worked.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:52.000\nSo, a test is really just a way to see if something is functioning correctly or meeting a specific standard.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:56.100\nIt\u2019s a simple way to confirm things are working as expected.\n\n00:56.100 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
