    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:08.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:14.000\nThink of it like this: you\u2019re testing if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:16.500\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:20.500\nAnother example is a spelling test at school.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:24.000\nThe test checks if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:27.000\nIf you spell them right, you pass that part of the test.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.000\nSo, basically, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:37.500\nIt helps us understand if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:39.900\nRemember, tests are all about checking things out!\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:41.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
