    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_051514.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but really, a test is just a way to find out if something works or if something is true.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if your bike tire has a leak, you can test it by pumping it up and seeing if it goes flat.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:35.900\nOr, if you're trying a new recipe, the taste is the test! Essentially, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:47.500\nYou have a question, you do something, and the result gives you the answer. So, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people feel better.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:59.900\nA baker tests their oven to make sure it's baking at the right temperature. In short, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected or to find out more information.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:05.900\nIt\u2019s all about gathering evidence! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
