    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_051559.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:24.200\nIt's a method we use to check if something is true, accurate, or working as it should.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:33.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:44.100\nA baker uses a test to make sure their cake is cooked all the way through. And you might take a test in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:57.400\nSo, tests can be all sorts of things! They can be questions you answer, experiments you perform, or even just observations you make. The important thing is they help us gather information.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:05.300\nTo recap, a test is a process for gathering information to determine if something is correct, functional, or present. It\u2019s a fundamental tool we use in many aspects of life.\n```"
