  "2de183f4-7045-477f-9e86-55c40f265144": {
    "id": "2de183f4-7045-477f-9e86-55c40f265144",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:58:43.584679",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T05:29:28.834465",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_052928.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_052928.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.600\nNot the kind you take in school, but tests in the world of software. A test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch. If it does, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails, and you know something is wrong.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:32.800\nFor example, imagine you're building a calculator. You'd want to test if 2 + 2 actually equals 4, right? Or that 10 minus 5 equals 5. These are simple tests.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:40.500\nTesting helps us catch mistakes early so we can fix them before they cause bigger problems.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:48.600\nIt's like a safety net, making sure our software is reliable and does what we expect.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:59.300\nIn short, tests help us build better software!\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
