  "2bea9664-b8c7-4295-84a9-9bbb5ea7cb2f": {
    "id": "2bea9664-b8c7-4295-84a9-9bbb5ea7cb2f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:58:47.792052",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T05:34:55.104728",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_053455.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_053455.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE Paragraph alignment set to center\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in general, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:26.100\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer. The basic idea is pretty simple: you have something you want to check, like a light bulb.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:30.900\nSo, you screw it in and flip the switch. That's your test!\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.600\nIf the light bulb turns on, it passes the test. If it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:39.800\nThink about baking a cake. You taste it.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:43.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:46.800\nYou're checking if it tastes good.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:57.600\nOr, when you get a new toy, you play with it to see if it's fun. That's a test too! So, tests help us see if things are working correctly, tasting good, or even being fun.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.900\nThey're a simple way to check things out.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:04.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
