    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_053631.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.200\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:24.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\nIt could be your knowledge on a subject, your ability to perform a task, or even the quality of a product.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:36.000\nThink of it like this: if you want to know how well you understand math, you take a math test.\nIf a baker wants to know if their bread is good, they test it by tasting it!\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:47.800\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\nMultiple choice questions, written essays, or even physical demonstrations are all different types of tests.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:56.500\nThe main goal of a test is to give us information.\nIt helps us understand where we are, and what we need to improve on.\n\n00:56.500 --> 00:58.500\nSo, a test is just a tool for learning and evaluating.\n```"
  },
