    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_053932.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.000\nYou've probably taken a bunch of them in school, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check your knowledge or skills on a particular topic.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:17.000\nIt helps you see what you know well and what you might need to study more.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: if you're learning to bake a cake, a taste test is a test to see if you got the recipe right.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:29.000\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, trying to ride without training wheels is a test to see if you've mastered balancing.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:36.000\nTests come in many forms, like multiple choice questions, short answer questions, or even practical demonstrations.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:40.000\nThe important thing is that they help measure your understanding.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:48.000\nSo, a test is just a way to see how much you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1af1e5b0-ba87-4954-a193-a24e5a1d2aeb": {
