    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_054641.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information or see how well something works.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like this: you're trying to bake a cake. You follow a recipe, but to test if it's done, you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:31.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Tests aren't just for cakes, though.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:42.100\nDoctors use tests to check your health, teachers use tests to see how much you've learned, and even scientists use tests to prove their ideas.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:54.500\nFor example, a scientist might test if a new fertilizer helps plants grow taller. They\u2019d grow some plants with the fertilizer and some without, then compare the results.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:04.900\nSo, tests are just a way to check something, learn something, or prove something.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:08.500\nThey help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:12.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
