    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:19.900\nThink about it like this: a taste test. You're trying to figure out which cookie is the tastiest.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:28.000\nYou sample each one, and the results of your tasting are the data from your test. Or imagine a spelling test at school.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:37.900\nIt helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words. The test itself is a set of questions, and your answers show what you've learned.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:47.100\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all share the same goal: to gather information.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:57.500\nSo, a test is just a way to learn something new or confirm something you already suspect. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
