    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.000\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:21.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It could be checking if you understand a lesson, or if a new medicine works, or even if a cake is ready to come out of the oven!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:28.800\nThe main idea is to gather information and see if something is working as expected, or if something is true.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:36.200\nThink about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see if you learned the material.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:45.900\nOr, when you bake, you might poke the cake with a toothpick. If it comes out clean, that\u2019s a test to see if it's baked through.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:57.000\nSo, tests help us learn, improve things, and make sure things are working correctly. They are a fundamental part of learning and discovery.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
