    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_055718.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:15.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:26.100\nIt's like an experiment, but often shorter and more focused.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:29.900\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:37.100\nOr, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:37.900\nThose are tests!\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:45.000\nThey help us learn information.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.100\nAnother example could be trying on a new pair of shoes. You're testing to see if they fit comfortably.\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:03.200\nThe result of the test is the information you get \u2013 whether the cake is ready, your blood sugar level, or if the shoes fit.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:18.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a procedure designed to gather information. It can be something simple, like tasting food, or something more complex, like a scientific experiment.\n\n01:18.000 --> 01:21.200\nTests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:21.200 --> 01:28.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
