    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_060416.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:18.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:27.600\nThat's a test! The toothpick tells you if the cake is ready.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:37.500\nIn school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:45.900\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve problems, showing you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:54.900\nOr, a spelling test checks if you know how to write words correctly. Essentially, tests are just tools for learning.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:00.200\nThey show what you already know and what you might need to practice more.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:05.000\nSo, don't be scared of tests! Think of them as helpful checkpoints on your learning journey.\n```"
