    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_061216.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:09.400\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:15.500\nIt\u2019s like asking a question and then getting an answer that helps us understand more.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:18.700\nThink about it this way: a spelling test helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:23.200\nOr, a taste test lets you decide which flavor of ice cream you like best.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:25.200\nThose are both tests!\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:28.200\nThey help us measure knowledge, preferences, or abilities.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:35.300\nAnother example?\nWhen you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test showing the cake is done.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:41.100\nSo, a test can be anything from a formal exam to a quick check.\nIt helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:46.700\nBasically, a test is a process used to gather information.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:56.300\nIt can be used to find out what you know, what you like, or even if something is working correctly.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:00.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
