    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.500\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:18.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:22.000\nIt helps us measure knowledge, skills, or performance.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz to test how well you understand the lesson.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:36.300\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:44.700\nAnother example: a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:57.600\nOr, before a company releases a new phone, they test it thoroughly to make sure it doesn't break easily.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.500\nSo, tests come in many forms, but their main purpose is to evaluate something.\n```"
