    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_062522.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:07.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests, but don\u2019t worry, it\u2019s not the kind you need to study for!\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.000\nIn this case, a \"test\" is simply a way of checking if something works as expected.\nThink of it like this: you buy a new lightbulb.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:21.000\nTo test it, you screw it into a lamp and turn the switch.\nIf the light comes on, the bulb passes the test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:23.600\nIf it doesn't, the bulb fails.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:31.000\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\nA chef might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\nA doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel sick.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:38.600\nBasically, a test is just a quick way to see if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:46.000\nSo, remember, a test is a way of checking something to see if it works correctly.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:49.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
