    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.400\nToday, we're going to talk about tests. Now, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:27.700\nYou test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:33.100\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:38.600\nTests are used everywhere.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:44.200\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:49.700\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:53.800\nEven engineers use tests to make sure bridges are strong enough.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:56.600\nSo, a cookie test checks for doneness.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:00.600\nA medical test checks for health.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:05.300\nA school test checks for knowledge.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:11.600\nSee the pattern? Basically, a test helps you understand if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n01:11.600 --> 01:17.300\nThey give you information to make decisions.\n\n01:17.300 --> 01:25.100\nTests can be simple or complex, but they all help us learn something.\n\n01:25.100 --> 01:28.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
