    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_063315.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.600\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:23.300\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, whether it's a quiz in school, or even trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:31.400\nBasically, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:39.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:47.300\nYou test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:53.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you they're ready!\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:03.000\nOr, maybe you're checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:09.000\nYou screw it in, and if it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:18.800\nSo, a test is just a simple way of checking something to see if it works, if it's correct, or if it meets a certain requirement.\n\n01:18.800 --> 01:23.400\nIt's all about finding answers.\n\n01:23.400 --> 01:29.300\nRemember, tests help us learn and improve.\n\n01:29.300 --> 01:32.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
