  "71cccc14-b95a-44ee-8961-0aba0635f494": {
    "id": "71cccc14-b95a-44ee-8961-0aba0635f494",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:59:32.074915",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T06:37:16.113334",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_063716.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_063716.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.300\nNow, you might be thinking about school, but a test is really just a way to check if something works like it should.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it as a simple question you're asking something. The main idea behind a test is to see if something passes or fails based on certain rules.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:30.700\nWe give it a task and watch what happens. For example, imagine you're testing a new lightbulb.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:38.600\nThe test is: \"Does it turn on?\" If it lights up, it passes! If it stays dark, it fails.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:46.500\nAnother example: you taste a new cookie. The test is: \"Does it taste good?\"\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:57.700\nYour answer, yes or no, is the result of the test. So, a test is basically a way to check if something meets our expectations.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.200\nIt helps us make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.800\nor are up to a certain standard. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0b3981c9-ab22-47f5-8212-da4337e512a9": {
    "id": "0b3981c9-ab22-47f5-8212-da4337e512a9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
