    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_063828.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:21.400\nThink of it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in and turning it on. If it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:33.400\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand the material. They can be quizzes, exams, or even just asking questions in class.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:45.100\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem, testing your understanding of addition. Or a spelling test checks if you know how to write words correctly.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:54.000\nTests aren't just about getting a grade. They help you and your teachers figure out what you already know and what you might need to work on.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:59.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something, whether it's a lightbulb or your knowledge.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:05.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "15934af8-d76f-4f4e-95ce-f114d3f75266": {
