    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_063937.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:18.600\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, or a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:25.800\nThere are all sorts of tests. You might take a test at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:35.700\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Even baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if the recipe works!\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:43.900\nFor example, if you want to know if a toy car needs new batteries, you can test it by trying to turn it on.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:51.800\nIf it doesn't move, that's a sign the batteries are probably dead. Tests help us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:51.800 --> 01:02.300\nSo, to sum it up, a test is a way to gather information and see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:06.600\nIt\u2019s how we learn, solve problems, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:06.600 --> 01:07.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
