    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_064228.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:24.900\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, we're talking about testing in general.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:30.900\nA test is simply a way to check if something works as it should, or to see what something is like.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.900\nThink of it like this: You test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:45.300\nThat's a test! Or, a chef might test a sauce to see if it needs more salt. That's a test too!\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:56.400\nWe use tests all the time to make sure things are working correctly, or to learn more about them.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:06.200\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel sick. Or a scientist might run tests on a new material to see how strong it is.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:16.000\nTests help us understand things better. So, to recap, a test is just a way to check something or learn about it.\n\n01:16.000 --> 01:22.500\nIt's a simple but powerful tool we use every day! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
