    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:14.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like a question you ask to see if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:36.200\nWe use tests all the time, even if you don't realize it! For example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:47.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done. Or, if you're trying to turn on a lightbulb, you flip the switch.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:56.700\nIf the light comes on, that's a test that the bulb and the switch are both working. So, a test is just a way to get information by checking something.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.300\nIt helps us understand if things are working the way they should. Basically, we ask a question, and the test gives us the answer. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
