    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_064846.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:01.900 --> 00:04.200\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:4.900\nIt could be anything, really!\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:07.400\nWe use tests to see if something is working correctly,\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:09.200\nor to find out more information about it.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:14.200\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:17.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:23.100\nOr, a doctor might run tests to check your health, like a blood test.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:26.800\nThese tests help them understand what's going on inside your body.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:32.100\nAnother example: you could test a new toy to see if it's safe for kids.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:35.800\nYou'd look for sharp edges or small parts that could be dangerous.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:41.500\nSo, tests help us learn, check, and make sure things are as they should be.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:45.900\nThey're a really important part of understanding the world around us.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:50.900\nBasically, a test is just a way to gather information and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:50.900 --> 00:52.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
