    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_065020.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:24.600\nIt helps us check if something is true, or if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:36.000\nThink of it like this: You might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:47.300\nOr, a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:57.400\nIn computers, we use tests to make sure our programs are working correctly. For example, if we write a program that adds two numbers, we can test it by giving it 2 and 3 and seeing if it gives us 5.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:00.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a method of checking if something is correct or working as expected.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:03.800\nIt's all about finding out the truth!\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:06.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
