    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_065308.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:14.700\nNow, you probably think of tests as something you take in school, but the basic idea is much broader.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:21.500\nA test is simply a way to find out something. It's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:35.700\nThink of it like this: a chef might taste a soup \u2013 that's a test to see if it needs more salt. Or a mechanic might check your car's engine \u2013 that's a test to see if everything is working properly.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:49.500\nEven checking if a light switch turns on the light is a simple test! So, tests help us understand things, identify problems, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:59.200\nThey are everywhere, in many forms, all giving us important information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2ac61499-5a4f-46c1-a4f7-29e9b6128fb3": {
    "id": "2ac61499-5a4f-46c1-a4f7-29e9b6128fb3",
    "topic": "Test",
