    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_070653.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.000\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about someone or something. Think of it like gathering information.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:21.800\nIt can be a quiz at school, to see what you've learned. Or it could be a taste test, to see which snack you like best.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:37.400\nEven a doctor checking your temperature is a type of test, to see if you have a fever. So, a quiz checks your knowledge, a taste test checks your preferences, and a temperature check looks for health indicators.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:39.700\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:46.500\nBasically, a test helps us understand things better by giving us some data or a result.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:48.200\nThat\u2019s the core idea.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:54.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4f0ba622-a271-46f6-9431-b3cb81d5557e": {
    "id": "4f0ba622-a271-46f6-9431-b3cb81d5557e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:59:53.868408",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T07:07:37.810721",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_070737.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_070737.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:15.400\nYou've probably taken lots of them, but what is a test, really?\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:32.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:41.300\nIn school, tests can be quizzes, exams, or even projects. They help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:48.200\nOutside of school, tests can be driving tests, or even just trying a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:55.100\nThe recipe is the test! So, a test is just a way to check understanding or ability.\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:57.000\nRemember, tests aren't scary, they're just tools for learning!\n```"
  },
  "bbce2b58-f977-4cb3-9765-d66fc058c26f": {
    "id": "bbce2b58-f977-4cb3-9765-d66fc058c26f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T13:59:54.378993",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T07:08:32.022213",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_070831.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_070831.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nBasically, a test is a way to find something out. It's a process designed to gather information.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:19.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a plant needs water. So, you check the soil. That's a simple test!\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:29.700\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your soup is hot enough. They help us understand something better.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:37.300\nFor example, a doctor might run a test to see if you have a cold. Or a chef might taste their food to test the seasoning.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:41.800\nSee? Tests are everywhere, helping us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:54.300\nSo, in short, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something is true or correct. It helps us understand the world around us.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
