    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_070958.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:07.200\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:11.600\nSo, what is a test?\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:13.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:17.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready,\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:20.000\nso you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:20.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:24.100\nYou're checking to see if the cake is cooked through.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:25.900\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:28.400\nA doctor might do a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:33.000\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.500\nA mechanic might test your car battery to see if it's working.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:45.800\nBasically, a test helps us gather information and make decisions based on that information.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:53.300\nIt's all about checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or if it's working correctly.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:58.000\nSo, next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a way of checking things!\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:02.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
