    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_071529.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school or exams, but in general, a test is really just a way of finding something out.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:25.800\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:32.700\nThink of it like this: you might test if the lightbulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:46.300\nThe switch is the action, and whether the light turns on or not is the result. That's a test!\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:53.600\nOr maybe you test the temperature of your soup by carefully taking a spoonful.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:00.900\nThe spoonful is the action, and whether it's hot, cold, or just right, tells you the result.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:08.200\nSo, tests are all around us. They help us learn, understand, and make decisions.\n\n01:08.200 --> 01:15.500\nThey are a way to find out if something is true or false, or whether it works the way we expect it to.\n\n01:15.500 --> 01:19.100\nTo sum it up, a test is simply a procedure to determine something.\n\n01:19.100 --> 01:20.100\nThat's it!\n\n01:20.100 --> 01:23.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
