    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:00:08.895996",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T07:26:09.125696",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_072609.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_072609.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:22.400\nIt helps us check if something is true, or how well something works.\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:31.100\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\nIn school, tests help teachers see how much you've learned.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:40.500\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nA math test sees if you can solve math problems.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:53.800\nAnd a science experiment is actually a test to see if your idea about something is right!\nSo, a test is basically a way to get information and see if something is accurate or effective.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:59.700\nIt's all about finding answers.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
