    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.799\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.799 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like this: you might test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:35.100\nOr, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy. The goal is to get information, to know something for sure.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:39.400\nFor example, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:49.500\nA chef might taste their food to test the seasoning. See? Tests are all around us, helping us understand things better.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:57.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us confirm if something is working, true, or correct. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "978ec551-439c-4f8a-9f0c-f3322401876a": {
    "id": "978ec551-439c-4f8a-9f0c-f3322401876a",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:00:10.040512",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T07:27:32.777525",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_072732.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_072732.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHello, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:14.700\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it as an experiment, but maybe a little simpler. The main idea is to ask a question, or present a challenge, and then see what happens.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:33.500\nThe result of that action gives you information. For example, a taste test tells you how something tastes.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:46.700\nA spelling test tells you how well you can spell. Even checking if the light switch works is a simple test to see if the lightbulb is good.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:53.600\nSo, remember, a test is a way to learn more by asking a question and observing the answer. It's a fundamental way of figuring things out. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6f9e3f52-c521-4ef2-9279-a274d23b8808": {
    "id": "6f9e3f52-c521-4ef2-9279-a274d23b8808",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:00:10.824671",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T07:28:17.390380",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_072817.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_072817.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:08.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find something out,\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:11.700\nor to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:15.500\nThink of it like this: you take a sip of your coffee\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:17.900\nto test if it's hot enough.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:18.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:23.500\nIn science, tests are often called experiments.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:30.300\nScientists create a situation where they can observe something and see what happens.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:36.700\nFor example, they might test how well a plant grows with different amounts of water.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:41.700\nThe amount of water is what they're changing, and the plant's growth is what they're measuring.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:46.800\nAnother example is taking a quiz at school.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:50.500\nThat's a test to see how much you've learned about a subject.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:55.300\nTests help us learn, understand, and improve things all around us.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:00.800\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and see what's going on.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:03.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f4d883f8-e1dd-45fd-9894-f61ffe698a01": {
    "id": "f4d883f8-e1dd-45fd-9894-f61ffe698a01",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:00:11.437386",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T07:29:00.701221",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_072900.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_072900.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.300\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:12.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand more.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.300\nThink about it: a recipe test lets you know if your cake will turn out delicious. A taste test helps you decide which ice cream flavor you like best.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:32.200\nEven when you try on clothes, you're testing to see if they fit! In school, tests check what you've learned in class.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:46.100\nThey help teachers and students see what needs more attention. So, whether it's baking a cake, picking a flavor, or learning in school, a test is just a way to explore and learn!\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:57.600\nSo, to recap: a test is an experiment, a question, or a way to find out information. It's all about learning and understanding.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
