    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_073916.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.700\nToday we're talking about tests. \n\n00:13.700 --> 00:20.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out if something is working the way it should, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like checking if your lightbulb works by flipping the switch. That flip is a test!\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:35.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. Did you check the weather before going outside?\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:42.500\nThat's a test \u2013 you're testing your assumptions about what to wear. Or maybe you tried a new recipe.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:48.700\nTasting it is a test to see if it's good! \n\n00:48.700 --> 00:55.200\nBasically, a test is just a way to gather information and make sure things are right. It helps us catch mistakes and improve things.\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:58.800\nSo next time you hear the word \"test\", remember it's just a simple way to check things out. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
