    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests,\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:09.600\nwhich are really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.600 --> 00:13.500\nThink of it like this: a test asks a question,\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:18.500\nand your answer helps us understand what you know, or how something works.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:20.900\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:24.400\nLike, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:29.300\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:35.100\nEven a simple taste test, like trying a new flavor of ice cream, is a way to test if you like it!\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:40.200\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:44.700\nThey come in many forms, from simple questions to complicated experiments.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:49.700\nThe key is they give us data, and that data helps us learn.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:55.800\nBasically, a test is just a structured way to explore and learn something new.\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:57.800\nThis video was created by\n\n00:57.800 --> 00:59.000\nApilage AI.\n```"
