    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_074353.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:14.800\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:18.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:30.900\nYou stick a toothpick in it, right? That's a test! The toothpick helps you check if the inside is cooked. Similarly, a test can be used to see if you understand a new concept, or if a machine is working properly.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:43.800\nFor example, your teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge about a specific topic. Or, a mechanic might run a diagnostic test on your car to see if there's anything wrong.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:59.000\nSo, a test is a method to examine, evaluate, or assess something. From checking if your cake is baked to taking a quiz at school, tests help us understand and confirm things.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
