    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.400\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:20.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like a question you ask to see if you know the answer.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:26.400\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:31.900\nThink about it. When you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:42.100\nWhen you see if a light switch works, you're testing if the light will turn on. In school, tests help your teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:53.200\nThey might ask you questions about a book you read, or give you a math problem to solve. So, remember, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:00.300\nIt's a way to learn and see what you already know.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.900\nTests can be big or small, easy or hard, but they all have the same purpose: to help us find something out.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:07.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
