    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_075147.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.300\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:10.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:16.400\nThink of it like checking the temperature of a cake to see if it's baked.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:27.600\nSo, how does it work? Well, a test usually involves answering questions or completing tasks.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:32.300\nThese questions or tasks are designed to show what you've learned or what skills you have.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:36.600\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:39.500\nOr, a math test shows if you understand math problems.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:40.700\nSee?\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:41.900\nPretty straightforward.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:47.300\nTests help us understand what we already know and what we still need to learn.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:57.000\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is just a tool to measure knowledge or skills. It gives us a snapshot of where we are and helps us plan for the future.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
