    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_075533.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:02.600\nToday we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:03.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.800 --> 00:06.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:07.800\nIt's like asking a question\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:08.500\nand seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:12.700\nThink about it this way: If you want to know if a cake is done,\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:14.600\nyou might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:15.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:17.700\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:22.500\nOr maybe you're trying to figure out which toy your dog likes best.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.900\nYou could offer him a few different toys and see which one he plays with the most.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:26.900\nThat's another kind of test!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:30.600\nSo, tests help us learn, confirm things, and make decisions.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.000\nThey can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb works, or more complicated, like taking a school exam.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:39.500\nBut the basic idea is always the same: find something out.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:43.300\nIn short, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:44.000\nand get a result.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:46.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
