    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.200\nNow, you might be thinking about school, but in general, a test is just a way of finding out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:29.200\nThink of it like this: you want to see if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:34.200\nSo, you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:39.200\nThe result tells you if the lightbulb is good or not.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:44.200\nAnother example?\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:47.200\nLet's say you want to know if your plant needs water.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:52.000\nYou can stick your finger in the soil. If it feels dry, that's your test telling you it needs watering.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:55.600\nSo, a test is simply a way to check something and get a result.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:58.600\nIt helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:00.100\nRemember, tests are all around us, helping us understand the world better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
