    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_080237.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:19.500\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we just mean a way to find out something about something else. It's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:28.700\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or a teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:37.700\nIt's all about gathering information. For example, you might test the water in your pool to see if it's safe to swim in.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:45.600\nOr you might test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a fork. If the fork comes out clean, it's ready!\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:57.400\nSo, basically, a test is just a procedure we use to learn more about something. It helps us make decisions and understand the world around us a little better.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
