    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_080454.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the Test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out if something is working correctly, or to see how well it performs.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:20.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:26.200\nThe test? You screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:32.800\nAnother example: You're baking a cake. You test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:47.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test and is ready. Tests are used everywhere, from checking your spelling on a document, to making sure a car is safe to drive.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:57.200\nThey help us catch mistakes and ensure things are working the way they should. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:04.600\nIt's a simple but powerful tool we use every day. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
