    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:08.300\nnot the kind you take in school,\nbut a basic way to check\n\n00:08.300 --> 00:10.700\nif something is working correctly.\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:13.900\nThink of a test like a simple question\nyou ask.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:17.000\nYou want to know if the answer is \"yes\"\nor \"no,\"\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:19.500\nor maybe \"true\" or \"false.\"\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:23.600\nFor example, let's say you want to know\nif your lamp is working.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.100\nThe test is simply turning it on.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:30.400\nIf the light comes on, the test passes!\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:33.500\nIf it doesn't, the test fails,\nand you know something is wrong.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:37.500\nAnother example: imagine you\u2019re baking\ncookies.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:41.700\nYou can test if they\u2019re done by sticking\na toothpick in one.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:44.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean,\nthe cookies are ready.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:45.900\nThat\u2019s a test!\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:51.100\nSo, a test is just a way to check if something\nis doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:54.800\nIt helps us identify problems and make\nsure things are working properly.\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:57.100\nThis video was created by\n\n00:57.100 --> 00:57.900\nApilage AI.\n```"
  },
