    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_081310.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:08.500\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to see how well you know something\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:11.500\nor how well something works.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:13.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb turns on.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:14.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:17.000\nTests help us understand if we're on the right track.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:20.600\nIn school, tests show what you've learned in class.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:23.500\nIn science, tests can show if a new medicine is effective.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:29.200\nFor example, if you take a spelling test and get all the words right, that means you're a good speller.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:36.100\nOr, if a company tests a new phone and it doesn't break when dropped, that's a good test result.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:42.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to evaluate knowledge or performance.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:45.800\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:48.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
