    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_081411.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.400\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:6.500\nWhat is a test?\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:11.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:14.100\nThink of it like an investigation.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:18.700\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:22.900\nFor example, when you try a new food and see if you like the taste, that\u2019s a test!\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:29.000\nOr, when you press a button on a remote control to see if it works, that's also a test.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:34.000\nTests help us understand if something is working as expected, or if it needs to be fixed.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:37.000\nAnother example is a school test.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:39.300\nIt helps your teacher understand what you've learned.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:42.000\nSo, tests are all about figuring things out.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.500\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:52.000\nTo recap, a test is a process to gather information about something.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:56.700\nIt can be simple, like tasting food, or more complex, like a school exam.\n\n00:56.700 --> 00:59.300\nThe goal is always to learn and understand.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
