    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_081741.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.600\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean exams at school. A test is really just a way of checking something to see if it works, or if it's true.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:24.500\nThink about it like this: If you want to know if a light bulb is working, you put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:31.900\nOr, if you want to know if a cookie recipe is good, you bake a batch and try them. That's another kind of test.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.500\nTests help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:51.200\nThey show us what's working and what needs to be fixed. So, whether it's checking a toy, trying a new recipe, or taking a quiz, tests are a simple way to find out if something is right.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:55.900\nBasically, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
