    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_081918.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is basically a way to see if something is working correctly, or to check the quality of something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:21.500\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it tastes good, or test a toy to make sure it's safe to play with.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:34.800\nIn everyday life, tests help us make sure things are safe, reliable, and meet certain standards. For example, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:50.700\nOr, when building a bridge, engineers perform tests to make sure it can hold a lot of weight. So, tests are important for checking anything from simple things like a cake, to more complex things like a bridge.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:00.200\nIn short, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something. We use tests everywhere to make sure things are as they should be.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:03.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
