    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This VTT file was generated automatically.\nNOTE It may contain inaccuracies. Please review and edit as needed.\n\n00:00.209 --> 00:01.129\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.129 --> 00:02.599\nToday we're diving into something\ncalled a \"test.\"\n\n00:02.599 --> 00:05.699\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a\nway to find out something, or to see how\nwell you know something.\n\n00:05.699 --> 00:12.279\nThink of it like this: you might test a\ncake to see if it's baked all the way\nthrough by poking it with a fork.\n\n00:12.279 --> 00:13.139\nThat's a test!\n\n00:13.139 --> 00:15.189\nOr, you might take a spelling test at\nschool to see how well you know your\nspelling words.\n\n00:15.189 --> 00:20.379\nTests can come in many forms, like quizzes,\nexams, or even just trying something out to\nsee if it works.\n\n00:20.379 --> 00:24.689\nThe important thing is that a test helps us\ngather information and understand something\nbetter.\n\n00:24.689 --> 00:29.529\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to\nfigure out what's making you feel sick.\n\n00:29.529 --> 00:33.629\nOr, an engineer might test a new bridge to\nmake sure it's strong enough.\n\n00:33.629 --> 00:36.899\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to learn or\ncheck something.\n\n00:36.899 --> 00:38.849\nIt gives us information we can use.\n\n00:38.849 --> 00:39.869\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
