    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_082457.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.214 --> 00:05.414\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.414 --> 00:12.814\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.814 --> 00:24.714\nIt's a process of asking a question and then trying to answer it.\n\n00:24.714 --> 00:29.914\nThink about it like this: if you're baking a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:29.914 --> 00:41.514\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. That's a test! Or, if you're trying to figure out if a toy car needs new batteries, you might turn it on.\n\n00:41.514 --> 00:56.114\nIf it doesn't move, that's a test showing the batteries are dead. So, tests help us learn, check things, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:56.114 --> 01:07.114\nThey can be as simple as tasting your food to see if it needs more salt, or as complicated as... well, maybe we'll talk about complicated tests in another video!\n\n01:07.114 --> 01:10.414\nFor now, remember: a test is a way to ask a question and get an answer.\n\n01:10.414 --> 01:13.914\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ebc6c671-25d8-4224-a781-2908367520dd": {
