    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:18.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb is good.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:32.500\nSo, you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test! Another example is baking a cake.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:37.800\nYou follow the recipe, put it in the oven, and when it comes out, you taste it.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:43.100\nDoes it taste good? That's a test of whether you followed the recipe correctly.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:51.700\nBasically, a test is a process where you try something out and then check the results to see if it passed or failed.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:56.600\nIt helps you know if things are working the way you expect them to.\n\n00:56.600 --> 00:60.200\nSo remember, tests are all about checking if things are doing what they're supposed to do!\n```"
  },
