    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:15.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:20.700\nIt\u2019s a process, a tool, used to measure or evaluate.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like checking if a cake is done.\nYou wouldn't just guess, right?\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:30.600\nYou might stick a toothpick in it.\nThat toothpick is your test!\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:39.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\nThat's a successful test!\nAnother example?\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:49.800\nA doctor checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\nThe thermometer is the test, and your temperature is what's being measured.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:57.800\nSo, tests can be used to check all sorts of things, from baking to health, to even how well you understand a new subject.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:01.400\nThey give us information to make decisions.\nIn short, a test helps us know something we didn't know before.\n```"
