    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.200\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like checking if your lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:36.300\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Maybe you want to test if a recipe tastes good, or if a new toy is fun to play with.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:44.000\nIn computers, we use tests to make sure our programs are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:51.700\nFor example, we might test if a calculator program gives the right answer when you type in two plus two.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:59.000\nSo, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected. It's a question we ask, and then we look for the answer.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:01.900\nIf the answer is what we wanted, the test passes!\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:06.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
