    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_090058.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:22.400\nIt's a process we use to gather information.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:35.300\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a blood test to find out about your health, or a teacher gives you a quiz to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:44.400\nSo, how do tests work? Usually, you'll be presented with questions or tasks, and your answers or performance are evaluated against a standard or a set of rules.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:54.600\nFor example, in a spelling test, you're given words to spell, and your spelling is checked against the correct spelling.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:05.700\nOr, if you're testing a cake to see if it's done, you might stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:16.700\nTests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to provide information.\n\n01:16.700 --> 01:20.700\nThey help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n01:20.700 --> 01:24.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
