    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_090730.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.700\nNow, you might be thinking of school exams, but a test is really just a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:20.600\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:29.600\nThink about baking a cake. You taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:37.100\nOr, when you get a new toy, you push the buttons to test if they all work.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:44.600\nIn computers, tests are used to make sure programs are running correctly and doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:52.200\nWe give the program some input, and then we check if the output is what we expect.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:56.700\nIf it is, great! The test passes.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:01.300\nIf not, we know there's a problem.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:05.800\nSo, a test is simply a check, a way of verifying that something is working as expected.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:17.300\nIt's a fundamental part of making sure things are reliable. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
