    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_091041.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.600\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:01.600 --> 00:07.800\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:16.700\nThink of it like asking a question, but designed to give you a measurable answer.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:23.000\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:34.600\nFor example, when you bake a cake and poke it with a toothpick, that's a test!\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:39.100\nYou're testing if the cake is done.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:43.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test says \"Yes, it's ready!\"\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:50.200\nAnother simple test is checking the temperature outside to see if you need a jacket.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:53.900\nBasically, a test helps us gather information to make decisions.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:00.000\nIt\u2019s about observing something, and then using what we observe to understand something else.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:01.500\nSo, a test is a question, an observation, and an answer all rolled into one.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:05.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
