    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_092408.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:06.500\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:11.100\nIt could be checking if you understand a topic, like in a school exam.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:17.100\nOr it could be checking if something works, like testing a new toy to make sure it's safe.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:20.400\nThe main idea is to get information.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:27.200\nWe perform a test to see if we can confirm something or find out if something is not working as expected.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:32.000\nThink about baking a cake. You might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:41.800\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out why your bike's tire is flat.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:44.800\nYou might test it for leaks to find the problem.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:52.000\nSo, a test is a way to gather information and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:55.200\nIt's all about checking and confirming.\n\n00:55.200 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
