    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:60.3\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:17.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something. It could be your knowledge, your skills, or even how something works.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like this: If you want to know how well you understand a new topic in school, you take a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:39.700\nOr, if a company wants to make sure a new product is safe, they run tests on it. Tests can be anything from answering questions on paper to performing a task in a lab.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:45.900\nThe important thing is that they give us information. They help us understand something better.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:56.800\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is a tool that helps us measure and learn. It's a way to check our understanding and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:00.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
