    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_093813.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_093813.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:18.200\nA test is really just a way to find out what you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like this: a test helps measure your understanding.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:37.100\nSo, how does it work? Well, you're usually given a set of questions or tasks to complete.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:47.200\nThese could be multiple choice, true or false, or even something hands-on.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:57.300\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words. Or, a driving test shows if you can safely operate a car.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:04.800\nBased on your answers or performance, you get a score or grade.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:14.700\nThis score then shows how well you did on that particular test.\n\n01:14.700 --> 01:22.000\nRemember, tests aren't meant to be scary. They\u2019re just tools to help you learn and improve!\n\n01:22.000 --> 01:29.300\nTo recap, a test is a measurement tool that helps you understand your knowledge or abilities.\n\n01:29.300 --> 01:34.600\nIt uses questions or tasks to give you a score.\n\n01:34.600 --> 01:41.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
