    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_093946.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out about something. We use tests all the time to learn new information.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like this: a test is like asking a question and getting an answer. It could be a quiz at school to see what you've learned, or a taste test to see which cookie you like better. Even trying out a new recipe is a test!\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:32.400\nYou're testing if it tastes good. For example, if you want to know if an object floats, you can test it by putting it in water.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:46.200\nOr, if you want to see if a lightbulb works, you can test it by plugging it in. The result of the test, whether it's floating or lighting up, gives you information.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:59.900\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information by trying something out and seeing what happens. It's all about learning and discovering new things!\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:06.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
