    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:26.000\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:30.300\nThe test is whether or not the lightbulb lights up.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:34.600\nIf it does, the test passes. If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:39.400\nAnother example? Imagine you\u2019re baking a cake.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:42.700\nYou taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:46.100\nThat taste is a test. You\u2019re checking the sweetness.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:52.600\nSo, basically, a test is any process you use to see if something is working correctly or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:55.700\nIt's all about checking! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
