    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_094701.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: Tests.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.800\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.700\nYou wouldn't just guess, right?\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:31.000\nYou\u2019d probably poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:35.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:39.600\nThe toothpick comes out clean? Great, the cake is ready.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:43.900\nThe toothpick is gooey? Needs more time.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:57.900\nIn science, we use tests all the time to see if our ideas are right. We might test if a new medicine works, or if a plant grows better in sunlight or shade.\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:01.500\nBasically, a test is a question we ask something, and then we look at the answer to learn more.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:05.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:09.900\nIt helps us understand the world around us.\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:13.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
