    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.799\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you take in school, but the kind we use to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:11.799 --> 00:20.600\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good. You put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:24.800\nYou're testing if the lightbulb works.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:31.699\nTests can be simple, like that lightbulb example. Or they can be a little more complex.\n\n00:31.699 --> 00:38.500\nImagine a doctor checking your temperature. That's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:44.399\nOr a baker tasting their cake batter to see if it needs more sugar. That\u2019s a test too!\n\n00:44.399 --> 00:54.100\nSo, basically, a test is just a way to check if something is doing what it\u2019s supposed to do. We use them all the time in everyday life.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:57.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
