    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_095221.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:07.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:18.900\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:23.300\nWe use tests all the time! Your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:26.600\nA chef tastes their food to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:29.700\nOr, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:36.900\nFor example, imagine you want to know if a plant needs water. You can test it by sticking your finger in the soil.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:39.600\nIf it feels dry, the plant probably needs water!\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:40.900\nThat's a simple test.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:45.000\nSo, to recap: a test helps us learn something.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:49.600\nIt's a method of gathering information in a clear and organized way.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:52.900\nHopefully, now you have a better understanding of what a test is.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:54.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
