    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_095303.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNo need to panic, these aren't the stressful kind! In this case, a test is really just a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:22.100\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:31.500\nIf the light comes on, great, the lightbulb passes the test. If it doesn't, well, you know the bulb needs replacing.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:37.600\nAnother example is checking if your cookies are done. You might poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:52.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies are ready \u2013 they passed the toothpick test! So, a test is simply a way to see if something meets a specific requirement or works as expected.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.700\nIt's a simple check to make sure everything is running smoothly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
