    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_100705.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_100705.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:20.100\nIt\u2019s how we gather information. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:28.300\nA chef tastes their soup to see if it needs more salt. Or, you might take a quiz in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:32.900\nAll of these are tests! They help us understand something better.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:43.100\nSo, whether it's checking your temperature, sampling a flavor, or answering questions, a test is just a way to learn more.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:55.200\nRemember, tests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all help us get information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3a599db7-f6d6-489e-9016-992a37a200b0": {
    "id": "3a599db7-f6d6-489e-9016-992a37a200b0",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:02:02.013754",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T10:07:52.218436",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_100752.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_100752.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.200\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:10.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:18.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:26.000\nIt's how we find out if something works, if something is true, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:31.000\nThink about it like this: When you bake a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:34.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:36.000\nThat's a test.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:42.800\nOr, imagine you\u2019re buying a new phone.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:49.000\nYou might test out the camera and the screen before you buy it to make sure they work the way you want.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:49.900\nThat's also a test!\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:56.000\nSo, tests are basically a way to gather information and make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:01.000\nThey help us understand and improve things all around us.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:03.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b88a63ad-3f7a-4256-bba0-6fc93481d919": {
    "id": "b88a63ad-3f7a-4256-bba0-6fc93481d919",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:02:02.741758",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T10:09:06.498843",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_100906.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_100906.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nThink of it like an experiment, but instead of chemicals, we're testing ideas, skills, or knowledge.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:30.500\nThe main goal of a test is to see how well someone understands a topic or can perform a task.\nThis helps us understand what they know and what they might need help with.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:40.500\nFor example, a spelling test shows us how well you can spell words.\nA math test shows how well you understand numbers and equations.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:52.300\nEven trying out a new recipe is a kind of test to see if it tastes good!\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn more about what we know and can do.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:58.200\nThey help us grow and improve!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "74ce8b13-fb57-4014-890a-2c2845b329c8": {
    "id": "74ce8b13-fb57-4014-890a-2c2845b329c8",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:02:03.275789",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T10:09:51.704748",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_100951.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_100951.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:29.200\nTests can be used to check if something is working correctly, like testing if a light bulb turns on. Or, they can help us understand something better, like taking a quiz to see how much we learned about a topic.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:37.900\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you\u2019re healthy. A baker might taste their cake to test if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:49.300\nEven a game is a kind of test, testing your skills! So, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:57.900\nIt helps us understand things better and make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "373aca01-5c76-4104-b26c-8417fb5fb5bd": {
    "id": "373aca01-5c76-4104-b26c-8417fb5fb5bd",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:02:03.827665",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T10:10:38.232088",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_101038.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_101038.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:16.100\nYou've probably taken a test before, maybe in school. But what is a test, really?\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:23.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out what you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:28.200\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you can test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:38.200\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test. In school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:48.000\nA spelling test checks your spelling, a math test checks your math skills. Tests aren't scary, they just help us learn!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:57.600\nSo, to recap: A test is a way to measure knowledge or ability. It uses questions or tasks to see what you know or can do.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:01.200\nTests help us understand where we are and what we need to learn next. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
