    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_102000.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:16.100\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.500\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:39.600\nThink of it like this: you try a new food \u2013 that's a test to see if you like it!\nMore formally, a test is a procedure to evaluate something.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:49.300\nThis could be anything from a multiple-choice quiz at school to checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:59.000\nThe quiz tests your knowledge, and flicking the switch tests the bulb's functionality.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:06.500\nFor example, a doctor might run blood tests to check your health.\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:13.900\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n01:13.900 --> 01:21.400\nThese are all different types of tests, but they all have the same basic goal: to get information.\n\n01:21.400 --> 01:28.900\nSo, a test is simply a way to gather information and evaluate something.\n\n01:28.900 --> 01:33.400\nIt helps us understand more about the world around us.\n\n01:33.400 --> 01:35.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
