    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_102707.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:18.500\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like this: you have a recipe for cookies, and you want to make sure they taste good.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:30.900\nYou follow the recipe, bake the cookies, and then\u2026 you taste one! That taste is your test.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.100\nTests aren't just for cookies though.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:45.400\nImagine you're building a toy car. You need to test if the wheels spin correctly, if the motor works, and if it goes straight.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:52.300\nEach of those checks is a test. So, a test is simply a way to verify that something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:56.100\nIt's a crucial step in making sure things are reliable and work the way we want them to. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
