    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_102836.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:05.400\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:19.200\nIt\u2019s a process of asking a question or performing an action and then observing the result.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:24.200\nThink about it like this: If you want to see if a plant needs water, you might poke the soil.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:25.000\nThat\u2019s a test!\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:30.900\nThe result \u2013 is the soil dry or moist? \u2013 tells you if the plant needs watering.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:37.500\nOr imagine you're trying to bake a cake. You follow the recipe, and then you taste the cake.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:39.800\nThe taste test tells you if you did everything right.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:48.100\nSo, tests are all about learning and understanding through observation. They help us make decisions and improve things.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:53.800\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is all about!\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:58.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
