    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_103014.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.100\nNow, you might think of a test as something you take at school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:26.700\nIt's a procedure designed to see if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:33.100\nThink of it like this: You want to bake a cake. The test is whether the cake tastes good!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:39.500\nYou follow the recipe, then you taste it. That taste test tells you if you succeeded.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:46.400\nOr, imagine you're trying to fix a broken toy. You try different things, each attempt is a test, until the toy works again.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:56.500\nSo, a test is simply a way to gather information and learn. It helps us understand the world around us.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:01.900\nRemember, testing isn't about being right or wrong, it's about learning and improving.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:05.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "cdedd6b4-a1b2-4edb-aadd-7d8c816e1674": {
