    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_104519.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as it should, or to see how well you know something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run tests to check your health.\nOr, you take tests in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:31.500\nThe main idea is to get some kind of result or answer based on a specific set of questions or procedures.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:41.600\nFor example, a simple test could be tasting a new food to see if you like it.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:49.400\nOr, checking if a light bulb works by turning it on. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:59.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking things. It helps us learn, diagnose problems, and make sure everything's running smoothly.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.200\nThat's the basics of what a test is all about. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
