    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_104643.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.000\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to see if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.200\nIn everyday life, we use tests all the time.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:33.000\nWhen you try a new recipe, you're testing if it's good.\nOr when you check the weather forecast, you're using information that was gathered through tests.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:41.500\nTests can also be more formal, like a quiz in school.\nThat's testing your knowledge on a specific subject.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:52.000\nOr a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\nSo, to recap, a test is just a procedure to find out something about something else.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.000\nIt helps us understand if things are working correctly or if something needs attention.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:01.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
