    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_104916.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:26.300\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it's true or false. Think about it like this: a baker might test their cake by poking it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:34.600\nOr, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words. Tests can be all sorts of things!\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:42.800\nAnother example is testing a toy car to see if it can drive down a ramp. We give it a push and watch what happens.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:53.300\nThe result of the test tells us something about the car. So, in short, a test is just a way to check something out and learn more about it.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:59.600\nIt's a simple way to find answers. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
