    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:19.800\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:30.100\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:41.300\nA test helps us understand if something is working, if we know something, or if something is true.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:48.600\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:58.800\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:09.000\nIn school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:16.300\nFor example, a simple quiz asking \u201cWhat color is the sky?\u201d is a test.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:27.000\nYour answer shows if you know the answer. Another example is baking a cake to test a new recipe.\n\n01:27.000 --> 01:33.800\nThe taste tells you if the recipe is good.\n\n01:33.800 --> 01:40.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:40.800 --> 01:49.100\nThey can be simple or complex, but they all serve the same purpose: to help us find out something!\n\n01:49.100 --> 01:51.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
