    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_105722.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:06.900\nIn everyday life, we use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:11.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:13.900\nIt's a process of checking or examining.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:15.100\nThink about it.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:19.000\nWhen you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:21.400\nThat's a test to see if it's done!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:27.100\nOr, if your car isn't starting, the mechanic might run a diagnostic test to figure out what's wrong.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:31.600\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:36.200\nThese tests help your teacher understand how well you understand the material.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:44.300\nSo, a test can be a simple check, or a more formal exam, but the goal is always to learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:54.800\nIn short, tests are a valuable tool for gathering information and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:57.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
