    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, a test is really just a way to check if something is working like it should.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good. The test is simply screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:30.300\nIf it lights up, it passes the test! If it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:34.100\nAnother example?\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:37.900\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:45.300\nYou can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If it comes out clean, the cake is done! That's another test!\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:52.700\nSo, basically, a test is just a simple way to find out if something is doing what it's supposed to do. It's a question with a yes or no answer.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:55.300\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
