    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_110811.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.999\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:14.899\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information. Think of it like a detective collecting clues!\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:26.299\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. A test could be anything from checking if a lightbulb works, to taking a quiz in school.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:37.199\nThe main idea is to see how something performs or what someone knows. For example, you might test a cake recipe by baking it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:44.499\nOr, a doctor might run tests to figure out why you're feeling sick.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:51.799\nAnother example is checking if your toy car runs smoothly. If it does, it passes the test! If it doesn\u2019t, then it fails.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:58.599\nSo, a test is just a method of finding something out. It helps us understand things better and make decisions.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:02.499\nIn short, a test helps us gather information to see how something works or what someone knows.\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:06.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
