  "67e70bd4-45e5-4379-84a9-5290321f9ff1": {
    "id": "67e70bd4-45e5-4379-84a9-5290321f9ff1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:02:47.786806",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T11:12:27.420965",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_111227.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_111227.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.000\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests \u2013 and not the kind you stress about in school.\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:15.600\nIn the world of computers and software, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you push it to see if it rolls. That's a test!\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:32.900\nIn software, we write little instructions, or \"tests,\" that automatically check if a program does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:43.200\nFor example, if you have a calculator app, a test might check if 2 + 2 equals 4. If it does, the test passes!\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:53.900\nIf it doesn't, something is wrong. Tests help us catch mistakes early, making sure our programs are reliable and work as expected.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:03.500\nThey are a super important part of building good software. So, remember, a test is just a check to see if something works.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:08.500\nAnd good testing means better software for everyone!\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:10.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d7d7a4aa-1f43-4b12-a54c-4ec6a2d811bd": {
    "id": "d7d7a4aa-1f43-4b12-a54c-4ec6a2d811bd",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:02:48.461243",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T11:13:18.681074",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_111318.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_111318.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.700\nNow, you've probably heard the word \"test\" used in lots of different ways, but at its most basic, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:25.800\nIt's a method we use to gather information. Think of it like this: you might test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:34.100\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:48.200\nIn both cases, you're performing an action to get an answer. Tests can be formal, like the ones you take in school, or informal, like checking the weather before you go outside.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:57.100\nThe important thing is that a test helps you learn something new, confirm something you already suspect, or make a decision.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:04.700\nSo, a test is a simple way to find something out. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
