    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_112958.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:17.200\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school exams. A test is really just a way of checking if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:28.800\nThink of it like this: you might test a new lightbulb to see if it lights up. Or, a baker might test their oven temperature to make sure it's hot enough to bake a cake.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:33.300\nHere\u2019s another example.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:39.100\nImagine you're building with LEGOs. You might test if a piece fits by trying to connect it.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:43.500\nIf it works, great! If not, you try a different piece.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:54.100\nThat's a test! So, remember, a test is simply a way of finding out if something is working, correct, or true. It's all about checking things!\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
