    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_113845.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_113845.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:08.400\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.400 --> 00:17.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:27.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\nThink about it: a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or a teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:33.900\nFor example, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:37.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:43.000\nOr, if you're buying a new pair of shoes, you try them on to test if they fit.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:53.900\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and make sure things are working the way they should.\nIn short, tests help us understand things better!\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
