    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:16.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it as a question and answer session, but not necessarily with people.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:26.700\nThe \"something else\" could be anything.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:33.900\nIs this cake delicious? Does this plant need water? Will this toy car roll down the ramp?\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:41.100\nWe use tests to answer these questions. For example, you might test a cake by tasting it. That's a test!\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:46.700\nOr you might test if a plant needs water by checking the soil.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:53.700\nIf it's dry, it probably needs water. So, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:01.600\nIt's a question, and the way we answer that question is the test itself. We observe, we measure, and we learn. That's the basics of testing! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
