    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_114907.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: tests.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:18.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it into the lamp.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:33.200\nYou\u2019re testing it! In science and math, tests help us prove ideas and solve problems.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:45.200\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake. You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:54.900\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, you might test your balance by slowly lifting your feet off the ground.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:04.900\nSo, tests are all about checking things! They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:09.300\nRemember, testing is a valuable tool in all sorts of situations.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:11.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
