    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:03:16.056986",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T11:49:57.118817",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_114957.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_114957.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:16.000\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.500\nIt could be about you, about an object, or even about an idea.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:33.000\nBasically, it's a procedure designed to evaluate something, usually by giving you a score or a result.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:43.400\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks your spelling skills. A taste test tells you which food tastes better.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:53.600\nAnd even pressing buttons on your phone to see if it works is a type of test.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:02.000\nSo, tests help us learn, compare, and make decisions. They come in all shapes and sizes, from simple questions to complex experiments.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:10.400\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\n\n01:10.400 --> 01:14.000\nTo sum it up, a test is a method of gathering information to evaluate something.\n\n01:14.000 --> 01:17.600\nPretty simple, right?\n\n01:17.600 --> 01:21.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c12adaa3-21e4-4b67-91e1-8ee36dcc1e0a": {
    "id": "c12adaa3-21e4-4b67-91e1-8ee36dcc1e0a",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:03:16.631414",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T11:50:46.591334",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_115046.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_115046.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something scary, like a pop quiz, but really, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like baking a cake. You test the cake by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:29.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, you know the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:34.800\nOr, imagine you're trying to turn on a light. You flip the switch.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:40.100\nIf the light comes on, the test passed! The lightbulb is working!\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:50.700\nTests help us understand if things are working as expected. They're a way of checking, confirming, and making sure everything is good to go.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:57.900\nSo next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a simple way of figuring things out!\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
