    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_115221.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:11.300\nYou've probably taken a lot of them, but what is a test really?\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:18.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:24.300\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, skills, or performance in a specific area.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:29.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:32.800\nYou test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:35.700\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:40.300\nOr, imagine you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:42.900\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:45.600\nIf it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:51.300\nSo, tests can be as simple as checking if a lightbulb works, or as complex as a school exam.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:54.700\nThey all share the same goal: to get information.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:58.000\nAnd that information helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:58.000 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
