    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_115355.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:09.700\nNo need to panic, we're not grading anything.\n\n00:09.700 --> 00:17.500\nIn this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: you test a lightbulb by screwing it in and seeing if it lights up.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:24.700\nThat\u2019s a test!\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:32.500\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might test the cake by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:38.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that means the cake is done, and the test passed!\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:40.100\nIf it's gooey, the test failed, and it needs more time.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:51.700\nEssentially, a test gives you information. It tells you whether something meets a certain requirement, or if it's behaving the way you expect.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:56.600\nIt's a simple way to confirm things are working as they should.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:01.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a check. It helps us understand if something is working properly.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
