  "9864b2da-9f23-4296-85a0-cfcfa835b43d": {
    "id": "9864b2da-9f23-4296-85a0-cfcfa835b43d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:03:20.699488",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T11:56:24.870412",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_115624.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_115624.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.900\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something.\nThink of it like a question you ask to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:25.800\nIn science, tests are super important for understanding how things work.\nWe use them to see if our ideas, called hypotheses, are correct.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:37.000\nFor example, imagine you want to know if a plant grows better with more sunlight.\nYou could test this by giving one plant lots of sun and another plant only a little.\nThen you see which one grows taller.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.400\nOr think about a spelling test at school.\nIt checks if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:47.800\nSo, a test is simply a way to check something, prove something, or learn something new.\n\n00:47.800 --> 01:00.000\nIt helps us find out if what we think is true, actually is.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:03.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
