    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_120140.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:01.300 --> 00:04.100\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:04.100 --> 00:07.200\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:11.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if the water's warm enough for a swim.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:13.200\nYou dip your toe in \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:17.300\nOr, maybe you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:21.200\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:23.400\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:29.100\nBasically, a test is a process, or an action, designed to give you information about something.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:33.800\nIt helps you answer a question, prove an idea, or check if something is working properly.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:42.400\nSo, whether it's checking the water temperature or seeing if a lightbulb works, tests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
