    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_120227.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:19.200\nThink of it like asking a question and then trying to find the answer.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:26.100\nTests are used everywhere! Your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:37.000\nTeachers give tests to see how well you're learning. Even baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing the recipe to see if it comes out right!\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:40.600\nFor example, a simple test could be dropping a ball.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:46.800\nDoes it bounce? That's the result of the test!\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:54.800\nOr, you could test if a light bulb works by flipping the switch. Does it light up? That tells you something.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:02.800\nSo, a test is just a way of gathering information and learning about something.\n\n01:02.800 --> 01:06.100\nIt's a simple process of asking a question and finding the answer through observation or experimentation.\n\n01:06.100 --> 01:09.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
