    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_121557.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHello and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:24.100\nThink of it like gathering clues. You perform an action or ask a question, and the result gives you insight.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:32.200\nFor example, a spelling test helps you learn how well you know your words. A taste test tells you which flavor you like best.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:47.600\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that says the cake is done! Tests can be formal, like exams in school, or informal, like checking if your food is hot enough before you eat it.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:56.300\nThe key thing is they help us understand things better. So remember, tests are tools for learning and discovery.\n\n00:56.300 --> 00:59.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1e47cea0-6e98-4cd0-a3cf-8c174afd0fb7": {
