    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_122744.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_122744.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:20.100\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out information. Think of it like asking a question, but sometimes the question is a bit more involved than just \"what's your favorite color?\".\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:32.800\nA test can help us measure something, like how strong you are, or how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:41.000\nFor example, a spelling test helps us see how well you know your words.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.200\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might test the batter to see if it's sweet enough. You take a little taste! That's a test, too!\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:55.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information. It helps us learn and understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "82461ebb-b567-4bee-8838-b9afffe830c0": {
    "id": "82461ebb-b567-4bee-8838-b9afffe830c0",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:03:45.739744",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T12:28:27.724296",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_122827.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_122827.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey there, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:12.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:27.000\nIn science, tests help us prove if our ideas are correct.\nWe come up with a hypothesis, which is like a guess, and then we design a test to see if that guess holds up.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:41.100\nFor example, imagine you think plants grow taller in sunlight.\nYour test could be planting two identical plants, putting one in the sun and one in the shade, and measuring them each day.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:51.400\nTests aren't just for science, though!\nYou take tests in school to see what you've learned, and doctors run tests to figure out if you're healthy.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:58.700\nSo, a test is just a method of checking something to learn more.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
