    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_123112.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:18.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of someone telling you the answer,\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:27.400\nyou're getting the answer from, well, the test itself.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:33.500\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Lots!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:39.600\nYou could test if a light bulb works by turning it on. That's a test!\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:45.700\nOr, a doctor might test your blood to see if you're healthy. That's another kind of test.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:51.700\nLet\u2019s say you\u2019re baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:56.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! See? Easy peasy.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:02.100\nBasically, a test is a process designed to evaluate or assess something.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:06.300\nWe use tests every day, often without even realizing it.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:10.500\nThey help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:10.500 --> 01:14.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
