    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_123345.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well you understand something.\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:26.900\nThe main idea is to ask questions or give tasks that show what you know.\nThese questions can be written, spoken, or even practical, like building something.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:36.000\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nA math test checks if you can solve problems.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:49.000\nEven a taste test is a type of test, checking if you can identify different flavors.\nSo, a test is just a tool to measure your knowledge or skills in a specific area.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:56.200\nIt helps you and others understand what you've learned.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
