    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_123438.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:05.300\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:06.400\nspecifically,\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:09.600\nwhat a test is and why we use them.\n\n00:09.600 --> 00:12.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:14.300\nor check something.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of water\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:20.600\nto see if it's hot enough for tea.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:23.700\nTests can be used for all sorts of things!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:26.300\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:29.700\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:33.700\nEven a baker tests their cake to make sure it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:37.100\nSo, a test is really just a way to get data.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:42.400\nIt helps us understand something better, whether it's your knowledge, your health,\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:44.300\nor even a delicious cake.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:49.800\nHopefully, now you have a better understanding of what a test is all about.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
