    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_123537.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.800\nIt's like asking a question and looking for the answer.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:24.400\nThink about it. When you take a spelling test in school, your teacher is trying to find out how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:33.500\nOr, if you bake a cake and taste it, you're testing whether it tastes good. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:47.600\nSo, tests help us learn, confirm, or understand something. They can be formal, like a science exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:58.500\nThe main idea is to get information and make a judgement. In short, a test is a method for gathering information to evaluate or assess something.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:03.900\nI hope that clears things up. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
