    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_125017.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the concept of a test.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:28.400\nYou can test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:35.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:42.800\nTests aren't just for baking though. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:49.900\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned. Even scientists use tests to prove their ideas.\n\n00:49.900 --> 01:00.700\nFor example, a quick spelling test might show you need to practice a certain word. Or a simple taste test can tell you if you need more salt in your soup.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:11.600\nSo, a test is really just a way of gathering information and making decisions.\n\n01:11.600 --> 01:21.000\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n01:21.000 --> 01:24.600\nSo remember, a test is a method for gathering information about something.\n\n01:24.600 --> 01:27.200\nIt helps us understand more and make better choices.\n\n01:27.200 --> 01:30.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
