    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:27.000\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:36.100\nThink about it: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done. That's a test!\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:45.300\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again to see if that fixes it. Another test!\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:56.400\nSo, a test helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:03.600\nTests can be simple like those examples, or they can be more complex, like a math exam.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:07.100\nThe key is that they help us learn and improve.\n```"
