    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_125501.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE\nAll subtitles will be displayed for the duration of each slide.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to see what you know or what you can do. Think of it like checking your understanding of something.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.400\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. Sometimes it's a written quiz with multiple choice questions, like \"What color is the sky?\".\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:36.800\nOther times it might be a practical test, like showing you can ride a bike or bake a cake.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:49.400\nLet's say you're learning your ABCs. A test might be asking you to write the letter \"A\" or to say the alphabet out loud. Or, if you're learning to play the piano, a test could be playing a simple scale.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:60.200\nSo, to recap: a test is a tool to measure knowledge or skill. It can be written, spoken, or even a hands-on activity. And they help us see how we're progressing.\n\n00:60.200 --> 00:66.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
