    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_130135.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the concept of a test.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:27.800\nThat's a test! Tests help us see if something is working correctly, if something is true, or even how well someone understands a topic.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:38.100\nFor example, your doctor might run blood tests to check your health. Or, you might take a quiz at school to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:42.900\nAnother example? Maybe you want to see if a new toy works.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:48.700\nYou turn it on, and if it lights up and makes noise, it passes the test!\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:59.500\nSo, a test is just a method for finding out information. To recap, tests help us confirm, evaluate, and learn.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
