    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_130627.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:20.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:33.200\nYou can test it by touching the soil. If the soil is dry, that's a sign it needs water! That's a test!\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:39.400\nOr, maybe you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:45.600\nYou can test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:50.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies are ready! Again, that's a test!\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:54.100\nSo, tests help us understand things better by giving us information.\n```"
