    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_131146.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:25.400\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it's meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:35.700\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:46.000\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\nThe test results show your current level.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:56.300\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking your eyesight to making sure a bridge is safe.\nThey give us valuable information that helps us make decisions and improve things.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:01.500\nSo, a test is just a simple way to check something and find out how it's performing.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
