    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_131629.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:04.700\nToday we're diving into something super important:\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:05.300\nTests!\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:09.100\nNow, a test is basically a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:12.900\nThink of it like this: you're making cookies, right?\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:15.200\nYou taste one to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:16.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:19.600\nIn science, we test ideas to see if they're true.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:24.400\nMaybe you think plants grow faster with more sunlight.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.300\nYou could test that by giving some plants lots of sun and others less, then see what happens.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:33.600\nOr, imagine you're building with blocks.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:37.900\nYou might test if your tower is strong enough by gently pushing it.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:39.800\nIf it falls over, it fails the test!\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:44.700\nTests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:47.700\nSo, remember, tests are all about checking things out.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:50.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
