  "72a9076e-14e5-4664-80bc-82c0604bee5b": {
    "id": "72a9076e-14e5-4664-80bc-82c0604bee5b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:04:26.096507",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T13:25:49.107389",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_132548.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_132548.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.900\nHey there, welcome to a super quick introduction to tests!\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:19.500\nA test, at its core, is really just a way of finding out something.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer, you're actually checking to see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:33.400\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Well, almost anything!\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:42.100\nYou could test if a lightbulb works by turning it on. You could test if you know your colors by pointing at things and naming them.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:51.500\nOr even, you could test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake's ready!\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:60.300\nBasically, a test helps us confirm something, learn something new, or even just check if things are working the way they should. Tests are all around us, helping us understand the world better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
