    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_132709.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true, but in general, a test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:28.200\nWe use tests to see if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard. Think about it like this: you might test a new toy to see if it's fun to play with.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:38.800\nOr, a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it has enough sugar.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:47.900\nIn computers, we test software to make sure it doesn't have any bugs.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:57.000\nSo, tests help us make sure things are good to go, whether it\u2019s a toy, a cake, or a computer program.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:01.200\nBasically, a test is a way of checking if something works as expected.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:03.500\nWe check the result against what we expect to happen.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:06.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
