    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_134403.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_134403.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:13.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:22.100\nIn science, tests help us see if our ideas about how things work are actually correct.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:31.300\nFor example, imagine you think plants grow better with more sunlight. To test this, you could grow two plants, giving one lots of sun and the other very little.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:37.400\nThen you'd watch to see which one grows taller. That's a simple test!\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:46.200\nAnother example could be a taste test to see which cookie someone prefers. So, remember, a test is just a way to explore and learn by asking a question and then observing the results.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:51.900\nIt\u2019s all about finding answers! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
