    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_134719.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what is a test?\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if someone knows something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:24.200\nThink about it like this: your doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:30.200\nOr, your teacher might give you a quiz to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:39.000\nEven baking a cake is a test! You're testing if the recipe works and if you can follow the instructions.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:45.400\nSo, tests come in many forms, but they all share the same basic idea: to gather information and evaluate something.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:51.300\nWhether it's checking your oven temperature or assessing your knowledge, tests help us learn and improve. In short, a test is a process used to evaluate something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
