    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_134957.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:15.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it as a structured question, or a series of questions, designed to give you an answer.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:25.100\nWe use tests all the time! Imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:29.100\nYou might taste the batter before it goes in the oven \u2013 that's a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:33.100\nOr, think about taking a quiz in school.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:37.100\nThat's a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:41.100\nAnother example? A doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:47.100\nSo, tests come in many forms, but they all share the same purpose: to gather information and help us understand something better.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:49.000\nIn short, a test is a tool for gathering information.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:49.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
