    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_135146.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.000 --> 00:03.300\nToday, we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:06.000\nA test is basically a way to check how much you know about something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:09.500\nThink of it like this: you learn about animals, and then a test helps you see how well you remember what you learned.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:13.500\nTests can come in lots of forms.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:16.700\nMaybe it's multiple choice, where you pick the right answer from a few choices.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:20.200\nOr maybe it's a fill-in-the-blank, where you need to remember a specific word.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:23.000\nSometimes it's even a project, like building a model or writing a story!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.600\nSo, if you're learning about planets, a test might ask you to name all the planets in order.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:33.700\nOr, if you're learning about addition, it might ask you to solve a few simple math problems.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:42.000\nBasically, tests are tools to help you and your teachers understand what you've learned and what you might need a little more help with.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.900\nRemember, they're not scary, they're just a way to learn!\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:47.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
