    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_135952.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like an investigation. We use tests every day, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:37.700\nFor example, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:54.100\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken, you might try turning it on. If it doesn't light up, that's a test showing it's probably time for a new bulb.\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:01.400\nTests help us learn, make decisions, and understand the world around us. They can be simple like that lightbulb, or more complicated, but the basic idea is always the same: to get information. So, a test is just a way to get answers.\n```"
  },
  "4e0f2ac8-e3ab-43f0-a683-71d1447ef125": {
    "id": "4e0f2ac8-e3ab-43f0-a683-71d1447ef125",
    "topic": "Test",
