    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_140917.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.200\nWhat is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer. It can be a written exam in school, of course.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:28.600\nBut it can also be something much simpler. For example, if you're baking a cake and you poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done, that's a test!\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:38.400\nYou're testing if the cake is cooked through. Or, if you try a new recipe and ask a friend if they like it, that\u2019s also a test.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:47.600\nYou're testing if the recipe is any good! So, a test is really just a method to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:55.400\nWhether it's a pop quiz or trying a new flavor of ice cream, you're always testing things in your everyday life.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:02.500\nRemember, tests help us learn and improve. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
