    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true, but in general, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:26.900\nIt's a simple method to evaluate something. Think about it like this: a chef tastes their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:34.700\nOr, a mechanic might run a diagnostic test on your car to see if the engine is running smoothly. See? It's all about checking something out.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:44.100\nFor example, in software, we write tests to make sure our code does what we intended. Or, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:59.100\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a procedure to determine if something is functioning correctly or has the qualities we expect. It's a fundamental way of understanding how things work.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:06.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
