    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:30.600\nIt could be as simple as seeing if your cookies taste good after baking them. You take a bite, and that's your test.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:36.800\nIf they taste great, your recipe passed! Or maybe you're checking if your car starts.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:50.000\nYou turn the key, and if the engine roars to life, the car passed the starting test. So basically, a test helps us understand if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:58.900\nIt gives us information to make decisions. Tests are everywhere, helping us make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
