    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_145539.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE\nAll subtitles are timed to match the audio,\nbut since the video is fully timed,\nthe subtitles are more of a helpful guide.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:27.100\nIn general, tests help us understand if something works as expected.\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:33.200\nOr, think about a doctor giving you a check-up.\nThat's a test to see if you're healthy!\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:41.300\nAnother example: before a company sells a new toy, they test it to make sure it's safe for kids to play with.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:52.200\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working right.\nThey\u2019re a really important tool for all sorts of things.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:04.100\nTo sum it up, tests are a way to check something and see if it meets a certain standard.\nThey help us learn, improve, and ensure things are safe and effective.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:07.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
