    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_145937.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.000\nNow, you probably already know what a test is,\nlike a quiz at school.\nBut in a broader sense, a test is just a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:28.100\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if your cake is done,\nyou can test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:39.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\nOr, if you want to know if it's raining outside, you can look out the window.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:51.000\nSeeing raindrops is a test that tells you it\u2019s raining.\nSo, a test is simply a way of checking something, proving something, or gaining information.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:57.900\nRemember, it's all about finding things out!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1321ecdc-78e0-49e1-acaf-d1f71153a5f6": {
    "id": "1321ecdc-78e0-49e1-acaf-d1f71153a5f6",
