    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_150041.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:23.000\nIt helps us understand if something is true, correct, or working the way it should.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: a cookie test!\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:38.800\nYou bake a batch of cookies, and then you try one. That taste test tells you if they're delicious, need more sugar, or maybe need to bake a little longer.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:43.200\nOr, imagine testing a lightbulb.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:49.200\nYou plug it in. If it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn\u2019t, well, it fails.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:58.300\nTests are everywhere, helping us learn and improve things. They are a fundamental part of understanding the world around us.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:04.400\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check something and see if it meets a certain standard. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
