    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nThink of a test as a way to see what you know or how well something works.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.500\nIt's like asking a question and then finding the answer.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:33.300\nFor example, if you're learning to ride a bike, a test might be trying to ride without training wheels.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:42.200\nThe result, whether you succeed or wobble, tells you how well you're learning.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:55.000\nOr imagine a chef tasting a soup \u2013 that's a test to see if it needs more salt. Scientists use tests all the time to see if their ideas are correct, and students take tests to show what they've learned in school.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.500\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way of finding out information. It helps us understand something better, whether it's our own knowledge or how something else works.\n```"
