    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests, and no, not the kind you take in school.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:20.900\nWe're talking about tests, or experiments, as a way to figure things out.\nBasically, a test is just a way to see what happens when you change something.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:29.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a plant needs more sunlight.\nYou put one plant in the sun and keep another in the shade.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:36.200\nThat's your test!\nThe plant in the sun is getting the \"treatment,\" the thing you're testing.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:47.100\nThe plant in the shade is your \"control,\" it shows you what happens without the treatment.\nSo, you watch them both, and see which one grows better.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:54.000\nThat tells you if sunlight makes a difference.\nAnother example: trying out a new recipe?\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:00.500\nThat\u2019s a test!\nYou're testing if the ingredients and instructions will make something delicious.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:07.000\nTests help us learn and discover new things every single day.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:16.600\nRemember, a test changes something and then observes the result.\nPretty simple, right?\n\n01:16.600 --> 01:22.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
