    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:66.1\n1\n00:00.229 --> 00:05.669\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n2\n00:05.669 --> 00:08.859\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n3\n00:08.859 --> 00:14.139\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know or can do.\n\n4\n00:14.139 --> 00:15.929\nIt's like checking your understanding of something.\n\n5\n00:15.929 --> 00:23.329\nThink of it this way: Your teacher gives you a quiz after a lesson. That's a test!\n\n6\n00:23.329 --> 00:27.599\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike, and you finally ride it without help.\n\n7\n00:27.599 --> 00:29.869\nThat's a test of your balance and coordination.\n\n8\n00:29.869 --> 00:36.139\nTests come in many forms, from quizzes and exams to practical demonstrations.\n\n9\n00:36.139 --> 00:39.679\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of words.\n\n10\n00:39.679 --> 00:43.219\nA science experiment tests a hypothesis.\n\n11\n00:43.219 --> 00:47.459\nEven playing a video game can be a test of your skills!\n\n12\n00:47.459 --> 00:55.239\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to measure your knowledge or ability. It helps you and others see what you've learned and where you can improve.\n\n13\n00:55.239 --> 00:57.009\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
