    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_152614.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:21.900\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:31.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking. You perform a test \u2013 you poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:41.100\nIf it comes out clean, the test is successful, and your cookies are ready!\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:49.000\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken. You put it in a lamp and turn the switch.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:57.000\nIf the light comes on, the test shows the bulb is working. If not, well, it's time for a new bulb.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:03.600\nTests are all around us, helping us learn and make decisions. They give us information.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:06.900\nRemember, a test is just a way to learn something!\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:11.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
