    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_152740.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.400\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:21.000\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. Think of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:29.800\nYou perform a test \u2013 you poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the test shows the cake is done!\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:36.400\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:48.000\nIf it lights up, the test is positive, the bulb works! If it doesn\u2019t light up, the test is negative, and the bulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:57.300\nSo, a test is just a process of checking something to see if it meets a certain condition or if it works as expected.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:04.200\nTests help us learn and make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
