    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_152919.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.600\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, we mean a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: you want to bake a cake, so you follow the recipe. The test is tasting the cake to see if you followed the recipe properly.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:29.000\nDid you use enough sugar? Is it cooked all the way through?\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:34.500\nAnother example is a lightbulb. The test is simply turning it on.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:40.600\nIf it lights up, it passes the test! If it doesn't, well, it failed.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:46.700\nTests help us find problems and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:59.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is working the way it should. It helps us identify issues and make improvements.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:00.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
