    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_153126.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:19.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:28.600\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:38.300\nIt could be anything from a school exam to a medical checkup, or even just tasting a new food to see if you like it.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:44.900\nThe main idea is that you\u2019re trying to measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:53.800\nIn a math test, you're being evaluated on your math skills.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:02.500\nWhen you test a recipe, you're evaluating how good it tastes.\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:11.200\nFor example, imagine you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n01:11.200 --> 01:17.900\nYou can test this by touching the soil.\n\n01:17.900 --> 01:24.600\nIf it feels dry, that's a sign it needs water.\n\n01:24.600 --> 01:33.300\nOr, think about testing if a light bulb works.\n\n01:33.300 --> 01:36.100\nYou plug it in, and if it lights up, the test is positive!\n\n01:36.100 --> 01:44.800\nSo, a test is really just a process of asking a question and getting an answer to help you understand something better.\n\n01:44.800 --> 01:48.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
