  "3c4c1d04-aaef-484a-968f-c5571896baed": {
    "id": "3c4c1d04-aaef-484a-968f-c5571896baed",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:50.698428",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:34:35.946407",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_153435.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_153435.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:19.300\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:27.700\nIt's a method we use to gather information and see how well something performs or works.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:36.700\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\nOr, a taste test tells you which food you prefer.\nWe can even test a new toy to see if it's durable and fun!\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:40.400\nSo, tests help us measure, evaluate, and learn.\nRemember, a test is just a way to get information!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0989aead-680c-47a3-9276-c017da86f0fe": {
    "id": "0989aead-680c-47a3-9276-c017da86f0fe",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:51.275527",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:35:22.915044",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_153522.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_153522.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:23.000\nIt helps us understand if something is working, or if we know something.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:33.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:35.900\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:40.800\nA test can be as simple as checking if a light bulb turns on.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:43.700\nThat\u2019s a test! Does it light up?\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:48.600\nYes or no? Or it could be more complex, like a long exam.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:55.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to help us gather information and learn something new. It helps us check, verify and understand. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2e8a6e06-d8f3-4390-bb46-48df821d45b2": {
    "id": "2e8a6e06-d8f3-4390-bb46-48df821d45b2",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:51.831764",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:36:14.977287",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_153614.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_153614.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, it's a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:18.900\nThink of it like asking a question and then getting an answer. This \"answer\" helps you learn more.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:25.400\nFor example, a taste test! You try a new flavor of ice cream to see if you like it.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:36.300\nOr, a spelling test at school helps your teacher see how well you know your words. Even checking if your car keys open your car door is a kind of test!\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:45.500\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information. It helps us learn, discover, and make decisions.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:51.500\nIt's all about finding things out! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c57294b8-c8eb-4a5a-adab-2ea00d327890": {
    "id": "c57294b8-c8eb-4a5a-adab-2ea00d327890",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:52.376839",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:36:58.592783",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_153658.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_153658.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:29.200\nYou're testing to see if the cake is done. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:37.000\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. A teacher gives tests to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:54.900\nEven trying out a new recipe is a test to see if you like it! So, whether it\u2019s a quiz in class, checking the temperature of your food, or even trying a new game, remember that tests are all about gathering information and learning something new.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:01.700\nThey help us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5a3e2ecb-cb6c-4abf-b060-9c1b31b75dfc": {
    "id": "5a3e2ecb-cb6c-4abf-b060-9c1b31b75dfc",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:52.900154",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:37:51.933230",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_153751.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_153751.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHi everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.000\nToday, we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:24.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about a certain subject.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:30.800\nThink of it like a measuring stick for your brain.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:37.300\nIt helps you, and maybe your teacher, see what you've learned and what you might need a little more help with.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:48.800\nSo, how does it work? Well, tests usually involve answering questions.\nThese questions can be multiple choice, where you pick the best answer from a few options, or they can be fill-in-the-blanks, or even short written answers.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:56.400\nFor example, a math test might ask you what's two plus two.\nThe answer, of course, is four!\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:03.000\nOr, a science test might ask what color is the sky.\nThe answer is blue!\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:13.600\nBasically, tests are a way to check your understanding.\nThey're not meant to be scary, but rather a helpful tool to guide your learning journey.\n\n01:13.600 --> 01:18.700\nRemember, everyone learns at their own pace!\n\n01:18.700 --> 01:23.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ec475c6b-68a6-4b01-a106-41a7e505d4fe": {
    "id": "ec475c6b-68a6-4b01-a106-41a7e505d4fe",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:53.557831",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:38:40.654669",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_153840.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_153840.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:22.700\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if your cake is ready,\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:31.900\nyou can test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.500\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:44.100\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. You test your balance by trying to ride without holding on.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:49.600\nEach try is a little test to see how you're doing.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:54.400\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information.\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:56.000\nIt helps us understand things better,\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:58.000\nwhether it's a cake, a bike ride, or something much bigger.\n```"
  },
