  "a4df7f36-bc4a-4f19-b56d-5a72b13baf3d": {
    "id": "a4df7f36-bc4a-4f19-b56d-5a72b13baf3d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:55.928890",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:41:39.784812",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_154139.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_154139.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:22.700\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:27.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is baked.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:33.100\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:44.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test! Or, imagine you're testing if a toy car needs new batteries.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:54.300\nYou turn it on, and if it moves slowly, that's a test showing the batteries are weak.\n\n00:54.300 --> 00:57.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c4b4ba3d-e454-4059-b0d1-e130e8242b84": {
    "id": "c4b4ba3d-e454-4059-b0d1-e130e8242b84",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:05:56.488184",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T15:42:23.512561",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_154223.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_154223.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nOkay, so you're hearing the word \"test\" and maybe feeling a little nervous, right?\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:07.600\nDon't worry! In its simplest form, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:13.700\nIt's how we check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:18.800\nThink about it like this: a chef might test a soup by tasting it to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:27.500\nOr, maybe you test a new toy to see if it's fun to play with!\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:35.800\nIn school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even just activities.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:45.700\nThe point is to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:51.600\nSo, a test is simply a method for finding something out.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:55.900\nIt could be about soup, toys, or even what you learned in class!\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:59.400\nRemember, tests are just tools to help us learn and grow.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:01.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ac62337b-ec8c-4173-818d-4c793ddd7c70": {
    "id": "ac62337b-ec8c-4173-818d-4c793ddd7c70",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
