    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_154348.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:13.500\nIn pretty much every area of life, we use tests to figure things out.\nA test is simply a way to gather information and see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:24.100\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\nIn school, we take tests to see how well we understand a subject.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:29.900\nA simple test might be checking if a light bulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:32.600\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:41.100\nAnother example is baking a cake.\nYou can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:54.200\nSo, a test is just a process to check something, big or small.\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:57.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c57dd450-2827-46da-8911-41c884274f85": {
