    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:31.700\nThe main idea is that you're trying to measure or evaluate something. It could be anything!\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:39.000\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:46.300\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:48.000\nEven checking if a lightbulb works is a kind of test!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:58.400\nLet\u2019s say you want to know if a plant needs water. You could stick your finger in the soil. If it feels dry, that's a test suggesting the plant needs water. See? Simple!\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:02.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:06.400\nIt helps us understand the world around us better.\n\n01:06.400 --> 01:09.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
