    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_154740.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.100\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:04.100 --> 00:15.400\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something else. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer that tells you more.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:19.100\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:24.500\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might taste the batter \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:27.200\nIt tells you if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:31.900\nOr think about checking if your bike tires have enough air.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.900\nYou press on them \u2013 that\u2019s a test to see if they're properly inflated.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:44.400\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking the weather before you go outside.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:51.900\nThe important thing is that they give us information we didn't have before. So, a test is simply a process of gathering information to learn something new.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:59.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
