    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_155742.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests! A test, at its core, is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.400\nThat's a test! You're testing to see if the batter comes out clean.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:32.100\nIn school, tests help your teachers see what you've learned. They might ask you questions about a book you read or have you solve a math problem.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:42.200\nThese are all tests to measure your understanding. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:51.800\nA science test might ask you to explain a scientific concept.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:57.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it works, if it's ready, or if you understand it. It helps us learn and improve! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
