    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.200 --> 00:02.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:08.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you use a toothpick to test them.\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:11.100\nThe toothpick comes out clean? The cookies pass the test!\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:14.700\nIn everyday life, we use tests all the time.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:17.400\nA doctor gives you a checkup to test your health.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:21.100\nA teacher gives you an exam to test your knowledge.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:26.400\nSo, tests help us understand if something is working as expected, or if something needs attention.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:29.500\nThey give us information that helps us make decisions.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:30.900\nThat's really all there is to it.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:35.100\nThey can be simple, or they can be complex, but the core idea is always the same: to check and see.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:36.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
