    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_160452.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you might dread in school, but the kind that help us understand something better.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:20.000\nBasically, a test is a way to gather information. It\u2019s like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.700\nThe test? You poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:37.900\nAnother example: you want to know if your toy car needs new batteries.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:40.900\nThe test? You try to turn it on.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:46.600\nIf it doesn't go, the batteries probably need replacing. Simple, right?\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:57.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and find out information. It helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
