  "1253db40-1033-408a-b5ca-a0584391d6af": {
    "id": "1253db40-1033-408a-b5ca-a0584391d6af",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:06:28.464255",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T16:22:49.225400",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_162249.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_162249.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.000\n\u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:10.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:10.300 --> 00:15.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:16.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:21.500\nIn school, tests help us see how well we've learned something.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:26.300\nYour teacher might give you a math test to see if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:29.500\nOr maybe a spelling test to check your vocabulary.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:33.800\nTests aren't just for school, though.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:38.000\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:42.900\nMechanics test your car to make sure it's running smoothly.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:53.300\nSo, tests are all about checking something to see if it works, if you understand it, or if it's in good condition.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:59.100\nThey help us learn and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:01.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3c254d45-fd18-42a9-95f8-c1dccf676b3c": {
    "id": "3c254d45-fd18-42a9-95f8-c1dccf676b3c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:06:28.924522",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T16:24:02.067517",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_162401.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_162401.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:17.500\nNow, you might be thinking of a school exam, but a test, in a general sense, is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:30.300\nIt's a process or procedure designed to evaluate, assess, or measure. Think of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:38.100\nThat's a test! Or maybe you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken, so you try turning it on.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:44.600\nAnother test! The results of a test help us make decisions or understand things better.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:55.100\nFor instance, a doctor uses tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick. A mechanic uses tests to find out why your car isn't working.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:05.200\nSo, a test is simply a way to get information. In short, a test is any method used to gather data or assess something.\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:16.300\nIt helps us understand, diagnose, or evaluate, using simple actions like poking a cake or more complex scientific procedures.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:19.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
