    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.100\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:25.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:34.100\nIt's a process of asking a question or setting up a situation to see what happens.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:42.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a light bulb works, you can test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:51.300\nThe \"test\" is turning on the lamp, and the result tells you if the bulb is good or not.\n\n00:51.300 --> 01:01.400\nAnother example is a taste test. You try a new food to see if you like it. The tasting is the test, and whether you enjoy it or not is the result.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:09.700\nSo, in short, a test is a way to gather information, to answer a question, or to see if something works as expected.\n\n01:09.700 --> 01:17.500\nTests help us learn and make decisions every day.\n\n01:17.500 --> 01:22.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
