    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:65.2\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:21.400\nIt's a process we use to gather information, usually to see how well something works or how good someone is at something.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:33.400\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:38.700\nIt helps you decide if you need to make any changes.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:45.900\nTests aren't just for school or baking.\nScientists use tests to see if new medicines work.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:53.100\nEngineers test bridges to make sure they're safe.\nSo, tests are everywhere!\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:58.900\nThey help us learn, improve, and make important decisions.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:01.600\nIn short, a test is just a way of finding out information.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
