    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, it's basically a way to check something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:19.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:26.900\nIn general, a test helps us understand if something works the way it should, or if it has a certain quality.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:37.100\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\nOr, a teacher gives tests to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:42.500\nLet's say you build a toy car.\nYou might test if it can roll down a ramp.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:46.300\nIf it does, great! It passed the test.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:50.100\nIf it doesn't, you know you need to make some adjustments.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:53.900\nSo, a test is simply a way to evaluate something.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:01.200\nand see if it meets certain requirements.\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
