    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_165859.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.400\nToday, we're diving into the basics of testing.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:27.500\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:42.800\nIn everyday life, you're constantly doing tests!\nLike, tapping your phone screen to see if it turns on, or tasting your food to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:57.200\nIn school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand the material.\nFor example, a simple math test might ask, \"What's 2 + 2?\"\nIf you answer \"4,\" you've passed the test!\nOr, a spelling test might ask you to spell \"cat.\"\nIf you spell it C-A-T, you got it right!\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:02.100\nSo, testing is all about checking if something is correct or working properly.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.800\nIt helps us learn and improve things.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:08.400\nPretty simple, right?\n\n01:08.400 --> 01:12.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "39b419e8-e17e-447a-8982-79c8537b6365": {
    "id": "39b419e8-e17e-447a-8982-79c8537b6365",
