    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_170001.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.500\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, we\u2019re talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: a test is a simple question you ask to get a clear answer.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:32.700\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Well, you can test if a light bulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:42.700\nIf it lights up, the test passes! Or, you can test if a cookie is done baking by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:51.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookie is ready. Another example is testing if a website is loading by typing the address in your browser.\n\n00:51.800 --> 01:02.700\nIf you see the page, the test worked! Basically, a test is just a way to confirm that something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:06.300\nIt's a simple way to check and make sure things are working as expected.\n```"
  },
