    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_171025.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.100\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something, to see if it works or if it's true.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like a little experiment.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:27.700\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might use a toothpick to test if the cake is done.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:34.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that means the cake is baked all the way through. That's a test!\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:42.500\nOr, if you're trying to learn your ABCs, your teacher might give you a quiz to test how well you know them.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.300\nTests aren't always scary; they're just tools to help us understand things better. They help us learn and improve.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:53.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of checking something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5115c175-e0f4-4816-9abd-2ebf0102d801": {
    "id": "5115c175-e0f4-4816-9abd-2ebf0102d801",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:07:02.304552",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T17:11:06.560687",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_171106.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_171106.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in computer programming, a test is simply a way to check if your code is working the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:28.800\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car and then test it by pushing it to see if it rolls.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:39.900\nIn coding, we write little programs that test our bigger programs. For example, if you write a program that\u2019s supposed to add two numbers, a test might feed it \"2 + 2\" and check if the answer is \"4\".\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:43.500\nIf it is, great! The test passes.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:52.900\nIf it's not, then something's wrong with your code. So, tests help us find bugs and make sure our programs are reliable.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:00.200\nThey're a super important part of writing good code. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
