    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_171718.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_171718.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:58.2\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand what we're looking at.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:22.200\nThink about it like this: you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:26.500\nOr maybe a doctor orders a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:35.900\nSee? Different questions, different answers. Tests can be simple, like flipping a coin to see if it lands on heads or tails.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:50.500\nOr they can be more complex, like a science experiment where you're testing a specific idea. So, in a nutshell, a test is a process that helps us gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:58.200\nIt's all about asking questions and finding the answers. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
