    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_171856.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it works. You screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:27.900\nAnother example could be a spelling test in school.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:34.400\nThe test checks if you know how to spell certain words correctly. Or maybe you're baking a cake.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:40.800\nYou can taste it to test if it has enough sugar. If it tastes good, the test passes!\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:49.700\nSo, a test helps us understand something, confirm something, or make sure something is working as it should. It's all about checking and verifying.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:56.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
