    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_172339.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What are they, and why do we even use them?\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:17.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process designed to measure your knowledge, skill, or even just your opinion about something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like this: a quiz in class is a test to see how well you understand what you've been learning.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:30.500\nOr maybe you take a taste test to see which cookie you like better. That's a test too!\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:39.600\nAnother example could be a doctor running tests to figure out what's making you feel sick. They might check your temperature or run blood work.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:46.200\nAll of these are different kinds of tests. So, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:54.700\nThey give us information that we can use to make decisions or learn more. They're a fundamental part of learning and discovery.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:58.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
