    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:32.400\nThink of it like asking a question, but with a little more structure.\nWe use tests every day, without even realizing it.\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like the taste.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:46.600\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again \u2013 that's a test to see if it fixes the problem!\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:57.800\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if the oven is hot enough.\nThe goal is always the same: to gather information and learn something new.\nSo next time you're \"testing\" something, remember you're just asking a question in a smart way.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
