    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.231 --> 00:02.041\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.041 --> 00:04.341\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.791 --> 00:05.961\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.961 --> 00:09.891\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.891 --> 00:13.551\nIt helps us understand how well something works, or what its properties are.\n\n00:13.991 --> 00:17.691\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:18.061 --> 00:22.071\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to test what you've learned in class.\n\n00:22.461 --> 00:28.151\nAnother example could be testing a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids to play with.\n\n00:28.151 --> 00:30.721\nWe might drop it, pull on it, and see if anything breaks.\n\n00:31.181 --> 00:32.971\nAll of these are ways to test something.\n\n00:33.391 --> 00:35.731\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n00:36.171 --> 00:40.491\nWe perform tests to learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:40.491 --> 00:43.411\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
