  "368d1574-3d86-478d-95da-20066402538f": {
    "id": "368d1574-3d86-478d-95da-20066402538f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:07:15.095268",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T17:28:59.943728",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_172859.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_172859.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:11.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt could be about anything!\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:20.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\nA teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:30.600\nEven trying a new recipe is like a test \u2013 you're testing whether it tastes good!\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:43.600\nYou ask a question, do something to find the answer, and then see what the results tell you.\nFor example, you could test if a toy car rolls faster on carpet or tile.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:52.300\nYou roll it on both and see which goes further.\nBasically, tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:57.700\nThey're all around us!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c1f9c3b1-94da-491a-b218-c0a0ff26b67c": {
    "id": "c1f9c3b1-94da-491a-b218-c0a0ff26b67c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:07:15.684640",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T17:29:47.153945",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_172947.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_172947.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something scary, like in school, but a test is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:25.800\nIt's a procedure designed to check if something is true, or to measure something specific.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor might do a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:38.200\nOr, a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar. See?\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:44.800\nIt\u2019s just a way to get information. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:58.200\nWhen you try a new brand of cereal to see if you like it, you're performing a test! So, remember, a test is simply a method to discover information or verify something. It's a way to check, measure, and learn. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e65fb895-2605-4852-85f7-f608ff952e78": {
    "id": "e65fb895-2605-4852-85f7-f608ff952e78",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:07:16.222073",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T17:30:30.673726",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_173030.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_173030.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.300\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out. It's like asking a question, but instead of just listening for an answer, we're looking for proof.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:28.800\nThink of it like this: a baking test checks if a cake is done by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:37.900\nOr, a spelling test sees if you know how to spell words correctly. You write them down, and someone checks your answers. That's the test!\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:46.100\nSo, a test can be anything from a quiz in school to checking if a new toy works properly.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:56.100\nBasically, if you're trying to find something out in a structured way, you're probably doing a test. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "573d84b2-b9cb-4384-b9f5-1fce978fb379": {
    "id": "573d84b2-b9cb-4384-b9f5-1fce978fb379",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:07:16.715245",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T17:31:17.350963",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_173117.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_173117.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:06.700\nIn everyday life, we often use tests to see how well we understand something,\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:08.300\nor how good we are at something.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:13.900\nIn the world of software and development, a test is basically the same idea.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:20.100\nIt's a way to check if a piece of code is working correctly and doing what it\u2019s supposed to do.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like this: you write some code that's supposed to add two numbers together.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:33.700\nA test would be like giving it the numbers two and three, and then checking if the answer is five.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:37.500\nIf it is, the test passes! If it's anything else, the test fails,\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:40.400\nand you know there's a problem with your code.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:44.800\nTests help us catch mistakes early and make sure our software is reliable.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:47.300\nThey're like a safety net for your code.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:51.800\nSo, tests are crucial for making sure code works as expected.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:57.000\nThey're a way to verify, using examples, that what you've built does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:57.000 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "24417bf4-a195-4517-be4f-8d21f9b94df9": {
    "id": "24417bf4-a195-4517-be4f-8d21f9b94df9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:07:17.233466",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T17:32:03.341071",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_173203.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_173203.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.300 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:18.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It could be finding out how well you know a subject, or if a medicine works, or even if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:28.800\nBasically, you're trying to answer a question. You do something, observe the results, and then use those results to draw a conclusion.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:39.700\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! It's done!\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:43.800\nOr, think about a spelling test.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:51.100\nYou get a list of words and write them down. The teacher checks your answers and sees how many you got right.\n\n00:51.100 --> 01:00.300\nThat shows how well you know your spelling. So, a test is a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.500\nIt helps us understand things better!\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:05.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
