    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.300\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in the world of technology, a \"test\" is really just a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and you taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:32.100\nOr, if you build a tower out of blocks, you gently push it to see if it's sturdy.\nAnother test!\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:41.500\nIn computers, tests help us make sure that websites, apps, and even video games are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:51.400\nThey help us find problems before they become big issues.\nBasically, a test is a simple way to see if something works as expected.\n\n00:51.400 --> 01:02.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a way of checking if something is working right.\nIt can be as simple as tasting a cake or pushing a tower of blocks.\n\n01:02.600 --> 01:08.000\nThey help us find problems and make sure things are running smoothly.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:10.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
