    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_175302.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nIt's how we find out if something works the way it's supposed to, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like testing a lightbulb.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:30.600\nIf it lights up, the test is a success!\nOr imagine a doctor checking your temperature.\nThat's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:41.500\nTests can be as simple as tasting a new food to see if you like it, or as complex as a science experiment.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:49.700\nThe key is that you're trying to get an answer, or confirm something.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:53.200\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
