    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_175533.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:18.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:22.500\nYou poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:26.100\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:28.100\nThe cake is probably done.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:30.200\nIt comes out gooey?\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:32.000\nIt needs more time.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.600\nTests can be anything from a simple observation, like checking the weather,\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:38.700\nto a more formal procedure, like a spelling quiz in school.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:40.700\nAnother example?\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:44.700\nImagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:48.200\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:50.900\nIf the light comes on, the test passed!\n\n00:50.900 --> 00:53.700\nIf not, well, the bulb's probably bad.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:00.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and make a decision based on what you find out.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:04.200\nIt's all about learning and understanding!\n\n01:04.200 --> 01:07.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
