    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:07:39.434643",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T18:05:36.510750",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_180536.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_180536.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:17.200\nNow, what is a test exactly? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like this: If you're learning to ride a bike, trying to ride around the block is a test to see if you've learned how to balance.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:40.400\nOr, if you're baking a cake, tasting it is a test to see if you used the right amount of sugar. Tests come in all shapes and sizes, from school exams to trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:50.600\nThey help us understand where we are and what we need to learn. So, remember, a test is just a way to check your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:54.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
