    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_180635.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.000\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:31.700\nOr, a doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel unwell.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:45.500\nTests can come in many forms. There are written tests, like quizzes you take in school. There are physical tests, like running a mile to see how fit you are.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:57.800\nAnd even simple observations can be a kind of test, like watching how a plant grows to see if it's getting enough sunlight.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:04.800\nSo, whether it's a pop quiz, a science experiment, or just paying attention to the world around you,\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:08.800\ntests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:12.500\nThey help us see if something works, or if it needs to be improved.\n\n01:12.500 --> 01:14.900\nThat's tests in a nutshell!\n\n01:14.900 --> 01:18.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
