    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_180717.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:16.900\nIn its simplest form, a test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookie is ready.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:34.100\nSo, you poke it with a toothpick \u2013 that's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cookie passes the test.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:43.600\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Maybe you're testing if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:55.900\nOr testing if your car has enough gas by looking at the fuel gauge. The important thing is that a test gives you information. It helps you decide if something is working correctly or if it needs some attention.\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:59.500\nSo, a test is a simple way to check if something is working or is in the right condition.\n```"
