    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.700\nA test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like an experiment, but often with questions or tasks you need to answer or complete.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:36.300\nThe main idea is that a test helps us measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:42.100\nIt could be your knowledge, your skills, or even your understanding of a topic.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:47.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know how to spell words.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:56.100\nA math test shows how well you understand math problems.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:07.800\nImagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might test if it\u2019s done by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:11.900\nThat\u2019s kind of how tests work in general.\n\n01:11.900 --> 01:22.400\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to measure something, usually with questions or tasks, to see what you know or how well you can do something.\n\n01:22.400 --> 01:26.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
