    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:20.600\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.200\nYou can stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:34.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:40.300\nAnother example? Maybe you want to know if a toy car needs new batteries.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:45.800\nYou turn it on. If it goes fast, the batteries are good.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:50.300\nIf it barely moves, the batteries probably need replacing.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:51.900\nThat\u2019s a test too!\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:57.600\nSo, tests are all about figuring things out by trying something and observing the result.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.300\nThey help us understand the world around us.\n```"
