    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:04.100\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.100 --> 00:06.700\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:11.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:14.100\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:19.300\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:23.700\nOr, you might take a test in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:27.700\nTests can be written, like multiple choice questions, or they can be hands-on, like building something.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:32.900\nFor example, a taste test can tell you which flavor of ice cream people like best.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:37.600\nOr, a simple battery test can tell you if a battery is still working.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:41.800\nThe main thing is, a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:45.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to get information.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:52.200\nIt can be used in many different situations to answer questions and learn new things.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
