    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_183737.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.400 --> 00:03.060\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.060 --> 00:04.860\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:04.860 --> 00:07.610\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:07.610 --> 00:10.210\nIt could be a written exam at school, sure,\n\n00:10.210 --> 00:14.360\nbut it's also how you check if a cake is done by poking it with a fork.\n\n00:14.360 --> 00:16.250\nYou're testing its readiness!\n\n00:16.250 --> 00:20.480\nAnother example is using a remote control.\n\n00:20.480 --> 00:22.800\nWhen you press a button, you're testing if the TV will respond.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:28.180\nThe button is the input, and the TV turning on is the result of the test.\n\n00:28.180 --> 00:32.140\nSo, a test involves giving something an input and seeing what the output is.\n\n00:32.140 --> 00:36.660\nIf the output is what you expected, the test passes.\n\n00:36.660 --> 00:39.590\nIf not, well, then something needs fixing!\n\n00:39.590 --> 00:44.890\nIn short, a test is a structured way to check if something works as it should.\n\n00:44.890 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
