  "19b56346-fd3a-4859-9668-bac20ef8a071": {
    "id": "19b56346-fd3a-4859-9668-bac20ef8a071",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:08:05.146880",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T18:38:21.725796",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_183821.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_183821.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:24.200\nTests can be all sorts of things. A doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:31.600\nA chef might taste a sauce to see if it needs more salt. And you take tests in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:44.200\nFor example, a simple taste test can tell you if your drink is too sweet. Or, observing if a plant grows when watered is a test to see if water helps plants live.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:55.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn more. It helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ebd989dd-b93e-43dd-b9a7-b498ae23a4ff": {
    "id": "ebd989dd-b93e-43dd-b9a7-b498ae23a4ff",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:08:05.856436",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T18:39:19.412845",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_183919.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_183919.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.900\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something about something.\nIt could be about you, like a quiz in school, or about something else entirely, like checking if a bridge is safe.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:31.900\nThe main idea of a test is to gather information.\nWe use questions, experiments, or observations to see how something works or what it's like.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:41.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, a chef tastes their food to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:53.600\nEven when you try a new video game, you're testing it out to see if you like it!\nSo, to recap, tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:00.500\nThey're all about gathering information through a process.\nAnd that's the basic idea behind a test!\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:04.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b4f4b0d4-4124-47a2-968a-10249293f414": {
    "id": "b4f4b0d4-4124-47a2-968a-10249293f414",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:08:06.623306",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T18:40:00.067816",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_183959.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_183959.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:26.100\nIt helps us see if something is working, if something is true, or how well someone understands something.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:33.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:40.900\nYou use a toothpick \u2013 that's your test!\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:52.000\nOr, imagine you're learning your ABCs. Your teacher might give you a quiz \u2013 that's a test too! It shows how well you've learned your letters.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:55.400\nTests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all help us learn and improve.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
