    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_184813.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:07.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 01:05.000\nIt's a process designed to give us information about a person, a thing, or even an idea. Think of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might poke it with a toothpick. That's a test! The toothpick comes out clean? Great, it's ready. Comes out gooey? Needs more time. Or, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. You might test your balance by taking your feet off the ground for a second. That's a test too! You\u2019re figuring out how well you can balance. So, tests can be formal like school exams, or informal like checking a cake. They all help us understand something better. They give us data, or information, to make decisions. In short, a test is simply a way to gather information.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4bac6db8-dd28-4aaa-a1b2-a24d248321e8": {
