    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_184900.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:19.600\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're gathering evidence.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:28.800\nTests can be big, like a school exam, or small, like checking if your cookies are done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:39.300\nIn school, a test helps your teacher see how well you understand the material. At home, testing your cookies tells you if they're ready to eat!\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:43.800\nAnother example? Checking if your bike tire is flat. That's a test!\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:47.900\nYou're testing the tire's air pressure.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:58.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of gathering information and checking something. It helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
