    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_185617.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works the way it\u2019s supposed to.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:24.500\nIt\u2019s like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:35.500\nThe test? You flip the switch. If the light comes on, the test passes!\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:38.700\nAnother example: you baked a cake and want to know if it's done.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:49.300\nThe test? You stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:57.400\nSo, a test is just a way to make sure something is working correctly by observing the results. It's a simple but powerful tool for understanding how things work. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```\nNote: The image files \"lightbulb.png\" and \"cake.png\" are placeholders.  You will need to provide your own image files or replace these with other Manim elements. Also, make sure these image files exist in the same directory as the Python script, or specify the correct path."
