    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_185709.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it like this: you might test a new light bulb to make sure it turns on, or test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:35.800\nIn more formal situations, tests help us understand and measure things. For example, your teacher might give you a test to see how well you've learned the material in class.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:48.800\nOr a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. So, tests come in many forms, but the main idea is always the same: to find out information about something.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:57.500\nThey can be simple checks, like seeing if your shoes fit, or more complicated, like a science experiment.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:05.700\nThe key is to have a clear goal and a way to measure the results. Remember, tests help us learn and improve!\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:09.399\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "6bba3bf9-4343-4b3b-94d7-9c8ae028d807": {
