    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_185808.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.999\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:14.599\nToday we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:23.599\nThink of a test as a way to check how well you understand something. It's like a quick quiz to see what you've learned.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:32.699\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes. Sometimes they're written, like filling in the blanks or answering questions.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:46.999\nOther times, they might be practical, like showing you can do something. For example, a cooking test might involve baking a cake, or a driving test checks your skills behind the wheel.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:57.799\nSo, why do we even have tests? Well, they help you and your teachers see where you're doing great and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:04.599\nIt's all about learning and improving! Remember, a test is just one tool to help you grow.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:11.599\nIn short, a test is simply a way to evaluate knowledge or skills. It can be written, practical, or even oral.\n\n01:11.600 --> 01:17.199\nAnd the main goal is to help you learn and get better.\n\n01:17.200 --> 01:19.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
