    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_192145.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNo need to worry, it's not that kind of test! In this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as it should.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.400\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you use a toothpick to see if it's done. That's a test!\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:36.700\nAnother example: a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Or, before launching a new website, developers run tests to make sure all the buttons and links work correctly.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:46.800\nSo, testing is really just a process of checking something to see if it passes a certain standard or works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:57.000\nIn summary, tests help us confirm things are working properly and identify any problems. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
