    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb is good, so you screw it into a lamp. That's a test!\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:31.100\nThe result tells you if the bulb works or not. Another example is checking if your car starts.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:42.900\nTurning the key is the test, and the engine either starting or not starting is the result. So, tests help us understand if things are functioning as they should.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:51.000\nThey're a way of verifying something. To recap, a test is a simple procedure to check if something works.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:58.200\nIt gives us a result to confirm its functionality. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
