    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_194222.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:16.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like this: you might take a spelling test in school to see how many words you can spell correctly.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:33.700\nTests aren't just for school, though. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or a chef might taste their food to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:42.900\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and check something.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:49.900\nFor example, think about baking a cake.\n\n00:49.900 --> 01:02.500\nYou test the batter by poking it with a toothpick to see if it comes out clean, which means it\u2019s done. Or, you might test the temperature of a room to see if you need to turn on the air conditioning.\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:10.600\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check your knowledge or the quality of something. It helps us understand things better and make informed decisions.\n\n01:10.600 --> 01:18.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
