    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_194328.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you use a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.000\nThat's a test! In school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:39.300\nIn science, a test might involve running an experiment to see if a hypothesis is correct.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:48.000\nEven your doctor uses tests, like checking your temperature, to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:56.700\nSo, tests can be used for lots of different things, and they all have one goal: to give us information.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:01.000\nFor example, if your toy car doesn't move, you might test the batteries to see if they're dead.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:08.000\nIf the batteries are good, you might test the switch. See how that works?\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:11.300\nTests help us find answers.\n\n01:11.300 --> 01:19.000\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check something. It helps us learn, solve problems, and make sure things are working properly.\n\n01:19.000 --> 01:22.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
