    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but the word \"test\" just means trying something out to see how it works.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:28.500\nThink of it like this: a chef might test a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:40.500\nOr, before releasing a new phone, companies test it to make sure it doesn't break too easily.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:47.700\nSo, a test is simply a way to get information.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:56.300\nYou do something, observe what happens, and then use that information to learn or make decisions. For example, you might test different types of plant food to see which one helps your flowers grow best.\n\n00:56.300 --> 00:59.800\nBasically, a test is just a simple experiment. It helps us understand how things work and make better choices. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
