    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_195239.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:27.100\nThink of it like checking if you've learned what you've been studying. There are lots of different kinds of tests.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:41.300\nYou might have a multiple-choice test where you pick the best answer, or a true or false test where you decide if something is right or wrong.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:52.300\nSometimes, you might even have to write out your answers in an essay. For example, if you're learning about animals, a test might ask you to name different types of animals or explain what they eat.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:59.100\nOr if you're learning about math, a test might give you some problems to solve.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:05.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to help you see what you've learned.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:09.000\nIt helps you and your teachers know what you understand.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:12.400\nand what you might need to work on a little more.\n\n01:12.400 --> 01:15.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
