    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_200618.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:14.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but with a specific goal in mind.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:27.000\nWe use tests all the time to see if something is working correctly, or to check our understanding.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:33.000\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:38.800\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand the lesson. See? Simple!\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:46.200\nAnother example is testing a new lightbulb to see if it turns on. If it does, the test passes!\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:57.200\nIf it doesn't, well, the lightbulb probably needs replacing. So, to recap, a test is just a method for gathering information or checking if something works.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:01.000\nIt helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:04.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
