    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_200704.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.100\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:08.600\nNow, you've probably taken a test at school,\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:15.400\nbut in general, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:22.200\nIt's a process designed to check if something is working correctly, or to see what its properties are.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:34.200\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.200\nEven checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in is a kind of test!\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:45.800\nWe use tests to make sure things are safe, effective, and meet our needs.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:51.600\nSo, a test is really just a way of gathering information.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:53.100\nIt helps us understand the world around us better.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:53.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
