  "48313947-9102-4e4e-9c62-773a1935ffd5": {
    "id": "48313947-9102-4e4e-9c62-773a1935ffd5",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:09:11.601873",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T20:07:55.696813",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_200755.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_200755.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:17.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:22.000\nWe use them all the time, even if we don\u2019t realize it.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:30.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:32.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:42.300\nTests aren't just for baking, though. They help us measure knowledge, skills, or even how something works.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:51.900\nImagine you're learning to ride a bike. Each time you try and see if you can balance, you're essentially testing your balance skills.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:01.500\nOr when a doctor checks your reflexes with a little hammer? That's a test to see if your nerves are working properly.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:13.300\nSo, a test is just a method, a way to gather information. It can be as simple as tasting soup to see if it needs more salt, or as complex as a school exam.\n\n01:13.300 --> 01:19.900\nThe goal is always the same: to learn something new.\n\n01:19.900 --> 01:23.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
