    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_200843.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:04.700\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:06.900\nNow, what is a test?\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:10.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:14.000\nIt's like an experiment, but often on a smaller scale.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:19.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:21.000\nYou perform a test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:23.600\nYou stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:28.200\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test and it's ready.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:32.500\nOr imagine you're trying to figure out which lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:36.200\nYou test each one by turning it on.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:38.600\nThe one that doesn't light up?\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:40.600\nThat's the one that failed the test.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:44.500\nSo, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:50.400\nIt helps us learn, figure things out, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:54.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5349a36f-197f-433d-8873-6bf3d878e58b": {
    "id": "5349a36f-197f-433d-8873-6bf3d878e58b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:09:12.648534",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T20:09:32.820298",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_200932.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_200932.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey there, welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process designed to gather information and see if something is true, or working correctly.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:26.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:35.000\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned. So, tests can come in many forms, from simple checks to complex experiments.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:43.500\nThey all share the same goal: to give us answers. They help us understand things better and make informed decisions.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:53.400\nIn short, a test is a tool for learning and verifying. It helps us confirm or deny our assumptions about the world around us.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:00.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
