    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:65.0\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.700\nThink of a test as a way to check something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is, or trying something to see how it works.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:25.900\nThe main idea behind a test is to see if something meets a certain standard or works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:40.300\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words. Or, before a new toy goes on sale, engineers test it to make sure it's safe and won\u2019t break easily.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:48.100\nAnother example could be a taste test! You might try two different kinds of cookies to see which one you like better. That's a test too!\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:58.600\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to check something, to see if it works or meets a certain standard. It helps us learn and improve things.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:05.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
