  "4fe7ccdb-0888-4d58-9506-23cbdd03c047": {
    "id": "4fe7ccdb-0888-4d58-9506-23cbdd03c047",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:09:36.105995",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T20:41:08.613890",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_204108.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_204108.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:22.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:31.600\nThink of it like asking a question and then getting an answer. Tests can be used for all sorts of things!\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:38.200\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're sick.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:47.200\nOr, a baker might test a cake to see if it's ready to come out of the oven.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:53.800\nLet's say you want to know if your dog knows how to sit. You could give him a test!\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:02.700\nYou say \"Sit,\" and if he sits, he passes the test! If he doesn't, he needs a little more practice.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:10.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out. It's a question followed by an answer.\n\n01:10.000 --> 01:14.400\nAnd tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:14.400 --> 01:17.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a6d1b5bb-574d-4fd8-a5f1-7eb865c4b56b": {
    "id": "a6d1b5bb-574d-4fd8-a5f1-7eb865c4b56b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:09:36.659847",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T20:41:56.487204",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_204156.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_204156.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.500\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see if something is true.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of your bath water to see if it's hot enough, or you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:37.700\nIn more formal settings, like school, tests help teachers see how well you understand the material. They can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:49.500\nAnd in science, scientists use tests to prove or disprove their ideas. For example, they might test a new medicine to see if it really helps people.\n\n00:49.500 --> 01:00.800\nSo, a test is basically a way to gather information and make sure things are working as expected.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:04.300\nRemember, tests are a part of learning and growing.\n```"
  },
