    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.000\nWe use tests all the time, whether we realize it or not!\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:25.000\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done!\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:34.000\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp. If it lights up, the test is positive \u2013 the bulb works!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:42.000\nTests help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:51.000\nThey can be as simple as tasting a new food to see if you like it, or as complex as a medical exam.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:56.000\nThe key is that a test gives you information to answer a question.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
