    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_205747.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:29.400\nThat's a test! In more formal situations, tests help us understand if something is true, or works as expected.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:40.700\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, in school, a test helps your teacher see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:45.300\nLet's say you're baking a cake. You might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:50.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. That's a test!\n\n00:50.500 --> 01:04.400\nSo, a test is really just a way of getting information by checking something. They come in all shapes and sizes, but they all serve the same basic purpose: to find out something.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:15.600\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method for checking something to see if it works or if it's true. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b66f8c5c-b1e5-475f-962a-cfd9829cf9ee": {
    "id": "b66f8c5c-b1e5-475f-962a-cfd9829cf9ee",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:09:48.321416",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T20:58:37.446268",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_205837.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_205837.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 and no, not the kind you cram for!\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:16.700\nIn the world of software and technology, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:28.800\nThink of it like checking if your lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch. Basically, we give the program something to do, and then we check if the result is what we wanted.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:38.200\nFor example, if we have a calculator program and we tell it to add 2 + 2, the test checks if it actually gives us 4.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:41.800\nIf it does, great! The test passes.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:57.700\nIf it gives us something else, like 5, then the test fails, and we know something's wrong. Tests help us find and fix problems early, making sure our software is reliable and does what it's supposed to.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:09.600\nThey're a super important part of building good software. So, to recap, tests are like little detectives, making sure everything is working correctly.\n\n01:09.600 --> 01:13.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "51e0cc26-c17c-4315-8fdf-b83e9f56b804": {
    "id": "51e0cc26-c17c-4315-8fdf-b83e9f56b804",
    "topic": "Test",
