    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_205929.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the Test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:19.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like this: you test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:32.400\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done! Tests are used everywhere.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:44.900\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Teachers use tests to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:55.700\nAnd even engineers use tests to make sure bridges are strong enough. A test can be as simple as observing something, or as complicated as a detailed scientific experiment.\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:06.500\nFor example, you might test if a light bulb works just by flipping the switch. Or, you might test if a plant needs water by feeling the soil.\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:19.100\nTesting helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are safe and reliable. So remember, a test is just a way to find out if something is working or true.\n\n01:19.100 --> 01:22.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
