    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like an experiment, or a challenge.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:21.200\nWe use tests all the time to see how well something works, or to check if something is true.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:26.100\nThink about it. When you're baking a cake, you might taste the batter.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:31.900\nThat\u2019s a test! You're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:42.500\nOr, imagine a doctor checking your temperature. That's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:53.500\nTests can be simple, like tasting batter, or more complex, like a science experiment. But the basic idea is always the same: to get information.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:57.200\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information and learning something new. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
