    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_210329.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:08.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:12.700\nIt's a process or procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: your doctor gives you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:28.100\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:30.300\nSee? Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:36.000\nFor example, a simple test could be asking yourself, \"Do I know my ABCs?\"\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:38.500\nIf you can recite them, you pass!\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:45.300\nOr, a more complex test might be a driver's exam to see if you're safe to drive a car.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:57.500\nSo, a test is just a structured way to gather information and measure something, whether it's your knowledge, your skills, or even your physical health.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:02.100\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we might need to learn next.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
