    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:07.500\nToday, we're diving into something really important: tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:17.500\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:20.300\nYou use a toothpick, right?\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:21.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:25.300\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something works,\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:27.200\nif something is true, or if something is ready.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:30.900\nWe can test all sorts of things.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:34.900\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:40.200\nOr, a doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel unwell.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:42.600\nEven trying out a new recipe is a kind of test!\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:49.900\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to get information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:53.900\nIt's a valuable tool for learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
