    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_211400.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nA test is simply a way to see how much you know about something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like checking if a plant is growing well.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:26.100\nYou check its height and leaves to see if it's healthy.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:31.700\nA test does the same thing, but for your brain!\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:41.700\nTests can come in many forms. Multiple choice, where you pick the best answer. True or false, where you decide if a statement is correct.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:55.900\nOr even fill-in-the-blank, where you provide the missing information. For example, a simple test might ask: \"What color is the sky?\" You'd answer \"blue.\" Or, \"Is a dog a cat?\" You'd answer \"false.\" Easy, right?\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:07.300\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is just a tool to measure your understanding. It helps you and your teachers see what you've learned and what you might need to work on.\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:11.700\nRemember, tests are just one part of learning!\n\n01:11.700 --> 01:18.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
