    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:09:59.569758",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T21:15:13.927372",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_211513.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_211513.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey there, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:11.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:23.400\nIt's a method we use to gather information and see if something is working, true, or present.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:32.100\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:40.800\nEven checking if a light switch works is a kind of test! So, tests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like trying out a new game.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:51.400\nThe main goal is always to get some kind of answer. We use tests every day to learn and make decisions.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:56.900\nBasically, a test is a question we ask the world, and the result is the answer.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.100\nI hope that helps! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
