    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_211757.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true!\nBut in general, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:31.900\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and to test if it's done, you stick a toothpick in.\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test \u2013 it\u2019s ready!\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:42.600\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\nYou screw it into a lamp, and if it lights up, it passes the test.\nThe lightbulb works!\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:51.500\nSo, a test is really just a simple way to find out if something meets a certain requirement.\nIt helps us make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:51.500 --> 01:00.000\nRemember, tests are everywhere, helping us every day.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:03.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
