    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:23.600\nIt could be to see if a lightbulb works, or if you understand a new concept. Think about it like this: You're baking a cake, and you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.800\nYou're testing to see if the cake is done.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:35.600\nOr imagine you're learning to ride a bike. Each time you try, you're testing your balance and coordination.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:45.000\nTests aren't just for school. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, and engineers use tests to make sure bridges are safe.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.400\nSo, a test is just a process to gather information and see if something is working as it should.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:00.700\nTo recap, a test is a way to discover something, like checking if a cake is baked or if a lightbulb lights up.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:08.100\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working correctly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
