    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_212558.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:19.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:24.600\nIt could be anything from checking if a lightbulb works to figuring out how well you understand a new topic.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:31.900\nThink of it like this: you try to turn on a light switch. That's a test!\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:38.600\nIf the light comes on, the test passed. If it doesn't, the test failed and something needs fixing.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:45.300\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. You're being tested on your knowledge of spelling.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:53.700\nIf you get most of the words right, you pass. If you get a lot wrong, you might need to study a bit more.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:56.100\nSo, a test is really just a way to check if something is working, or if you know something.\n\n00:56.100 --> 00:57.800\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:57.800 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
