    "subtitles": "```webvtt\n    WEBVTT\n    \n    00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\n    Okay, let's talk about tests!\n    \n    00:05.200 --> 00:15.300\n    What exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n    \n    00:15.300 --> 00:21.100\n    It helps us understand if something is true, or how well something works.\n    \n    00:21.100 --> 00:27.000\n    Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking. The test? You poke it with a toothpick.\n    \n    00:27.000 --> 00:33.000\n    If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That\u2019s a test.\n    \n    00:33.000 --> 00:37.900\n    Or, imagine you're trying to learn a new skill, like riding a bike.\n    \n    00:37.900 --> 00:47.600\n    Falling down a few times? That's part of the testing process! You're testing your balance and learning what works and what doesn't.\n    \n    00:47.600 --> 00:56.500\n    So, to recap: a test is a method for checking something. It can be used to see if something is true, ready, or how well you're doing.\n    \n    00:56.500 --> 01:00.000\n    It's all about learning and understanding. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n    ```"
  },
