    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_214647.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.500\nYou've probably taken a bunch, but what is a test, really?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:16.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\nIt's a process designed to gather information.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: a baking test helps you check if a cake is done.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:29.000\nYou might poke it with a toothpick.\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\nThat's your test result, telling you the cake is ready!\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:35.400\nOr, imagine you're testing if a toy car works.\nYou put in batteries and turn it on.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:41.800\nIf it moves, the test passes!\nIf it doesn't, well, you know it needs fixing.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:47.800\nSo, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:54.000\nYou have a question, you perform a test, and the results give you the answer.\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:01.700\nRemember, tests help us learn and understand the world around us.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
