    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_214822.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:20.100\nIt's a process we use to get information about something specific.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.500\nYour test? You poke it with a toothpick. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:39.300\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. Your test is whether you can pedal and balance without falling.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:47.100\nEach attempt is a mini-test, helping you improve. So, tests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:54.200\nWhether it's baking a cake, riding a bike, or anything in between, tests help us learn and understand. They give us feedback.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:59.600\nRemember, a test is just a tool to help us find something out. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
