  "38e548a6-5f42-4887-96f0-a072f2561ccf": {
    "id": "38e548a6-5f42-4887-96f0-a072f2561ccf",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:10:28.423493",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T21:49:11.156950",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_214911.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_214911.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHello, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information or see if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You turn it on \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:35.700\nMore formally, a test evaluates something against a standard or expectation.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:42.500\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.300\nOr, a doctor might run tests to check if your body is healthy.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:56.100\nTests can be simple or complex. A simple test might be asking a friend if they like pizza.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:03.200\nA more complex test could involve scientists running experiments in a lab.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:10.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something, gather information, and see if it meets a certain standard.\n\n01:10.000 --> 01:14.200\nIt helps us understand the world around us.\n\n01:14.200 --> 01:14.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "dbefda41-4fab-41d3-9f2f-2de1d2b225b8": {
    "id": "dbefda41-4fab-41d3-9f2f-2de1d2b225b8",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:10:28.968769",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T21:50:00.790990",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_215000.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_215000.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it like a little investigation.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:30.800\nThe main idea is that you ask a question, or set up a situation, and then watch what happens to get an answer.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:44.500\nIt could be anything from a simple taste test to see if you like a new flavor of ice cream, to a more complex science experiment.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:55.900\nFor example, if you want to know if a plant needs more sunlight, you can put one plant in the sun and another in the shade, and then test, or check, which one grows better.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:07.300\nOr, if you want to see if your dog knows a trick, you can give the command and test if he does it!\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:16.800\nSo, a test is all about observing and learning.\n\n01:16.800 --> 01:20.400\nYou ask a question, you try something out, and then you see what the result is.\n\n01:20.400 --> 01:25.400\nThat result helps you learn and understand.\n\n01:25.400 --> 01:29.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f7dfab42-27d8-4d02-82ca-8c41a54ce109": {
    "id": "f7dfab42-27d8-4d02-82ca-8c41a54ce109",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:10:29.748720",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-03T21:50:47.391015",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260103_215047.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_215047.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE\nAll timings are approximate.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests, and no, not the kind you dread taking in school.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:22.600\nIn this case, a test is just a way to check if something works the way it should. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb is good, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:26.900\nThe basic idea is pretty simple. You have something you want to evaluate, you put it through a specific process, and then you see what happens.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:34.700\nIf your cake recipe says to bake for 30 minutes, you're testing if that time is right. You bake it and then check if it's cooked through.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:44.300\nAnother example: If you're building a birdhouse, you might test its sturdiness by gently shaking it to see if the pieces stay together.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:53.900\nSo, tests are all about checking things and making sure they work as expected.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:05.000\nIn short, tests help us confirm if something is working correctly.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:08.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
