    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.200\nToday we're going to explore something really fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something works, or to check if something is true.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:21.600\nWe use tests all the time! For example, when you flip a light switch, you're testing if the light bulb works.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:27.400\nOr, if you're baking a cake, tasting the batter is a test to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:34.200\nScientists use tests to prove or disprove ideas, and doctors use tests to diagnose illnesses.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:39.700\nSo, to recap, a test is a simple way to check something.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:48.100\nIt helps us understand if things are working as they should or if we need to make some changes.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:56.500\nTests are everywhere, helping us learn and improve all the time.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:00.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
