    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_220338.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:72.7\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:14.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to see how much you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling, while a fitness test checks your physical abilities.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:35.100\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes. They can be written, like a multiple-choice quiz, or practical, like showing someone how to bake a cake.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:42.500\nMaybe you're being tested on your understanding of math problems, or your ability to play a musical instrument.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:52.300\nThe important thing to remember is that tests help us learn and improve. They show us what we already know and where we might need a little more practice.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:56.900\nSo don't be afraid of tests! They're just tools for learning.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:09.100\nIn short, a test is a way to evaluate your knowledge or skills in a specific area. They come in different forms, and help us identify strengths and weaknesses.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:12.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
