    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.100\nIt's a process or procedure designed to measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.100\nThink of it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:39.100\nA chef tastes a dish to test if it's seasoned correctly.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:51.500\nOr maybe you try a new recipe to test your cooking skills. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:51.500 --> 01:02.700\nThey can be as simple as feeling a piece of fabric to test its softness, or as complex as a science experiment to test a new theory.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:07.700\nThe important thing is that a test gives you information.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:17.300\nSo, to recap: A test helps us find something out, it measures or evaluates something, and it provides information we can use.\n\n01:17.300 --> 01:22.700\nTests are everywhere, helping us understand the world around us.\n\n01:22.700 --> 01:27.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
