    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_220851.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:23.400\nThink of it like this: you taste a new cookie to test if you like it. Or, you try on a shirt to test if it fits.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:35.000\nIn school, tests are a way for your teachers to see how much you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even just asking questions in class.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:43.700\nThe goal is to measure your understanding of a topic. For example, a math test might have problems like 2+2.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:52.300\nAn English test might ask you to write a sentence. These tests show what you know about adding numbers or forming sentences.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:06.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new or check what you already know. It helps you and your teachers understand what you're doing well and what areas you might need to work on.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:10.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
