    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:21.600\nIt's a process of asking a question and then trying to answer it.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:34.400\nThink about it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by plugging it in. The question is, \"Does the lightbulb work?\" and the test is plugging it in.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:50.300\nOr, a doctor might test your reflexes to see if your nervous system is working correctly. The question is, \"Are your reflexes normal?\" and the test involves tapping your knee.\n\n00:50.300 --> 01:00.800\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like tasting a new recipe to see if it needs more salt.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:04.400\nThe key is that a test helps us gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:07.500\nSo, tests help us answer questions and understand things better!\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:09.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
