    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_221614.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something, or to see how well something works.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.600\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:32.600\nThere are all kinds of tests. You might take a test at school to see how much you've learned about a subject.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:39.800\nOr a doctor might run a test to check your health.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:47.000\nFor example, a simple test could be squeezing a lemon to see if it's juicy. The juice is the result of the test!\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:56.100\nOr, checking if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch. If it lights up, the test passes. So, a test helps us understand something better, or to make sure things are working properly. They're all about finding things out.\n```"
  },
