    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.000\nOkay, let\u2019s talk about tests.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:11.000\nYou\u2019ve probably taken a lot of them in school, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:15.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:19.000\nIt's a process designed to gather information.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:26.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, you might test a recipe by making a small batch before baking a huge cake.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:29.000\nThe goal is to get some results.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:33.000\nFor example, a multiple-choice quiz is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.000\nA taste test helps you decide which ice cream flavor you like best.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:45.000\nEven trying to turn on a light switch to see if the power is on is a simple test!\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.000\nSo, a test is just a way to learn something new or confirm something you already suspect.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:58.000\nIt\u2019s all about gathering information and seeing what happens.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
