    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_223734.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.100\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:26.800\nIt could be checking if something works, if you understand something, or even if something is true. Think of it like this: you might test the temperature of bathwater to make sure it's not too hot or too cold.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:39.400\nOr, you might take a quiz at school \u2013 that's a test to see how well you\u2019ve learned the material. Even a scientist running an experiment is doing a test to see if their idea is correct.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:49.100\nSo, tests come in many forms, but the basic idea is always the same: you're trying to find out something specific. They help us learn, improve things, and make sure everything is working as it should.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
