    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_224026.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something works correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:28.000\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:40.000\nIn science, tests are super important! Scientists use them to see if their ideas, called hypotheses, are correct.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:48.300\nFor example, if you think plants grow taller with more sunlight, you can test that by growing some plants in the sun and some in the shade, and then comparing their height.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:57.700\nAnother example is when you're learning something new. Your teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand the topic.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:05.600\nTests help us see what we know and what we still need to learn. So, remember, a test is just a way to check things. It helps us learn, improve, and discover new things! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
