    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_224523.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: Tests!\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.600\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake and you use a toothpick to check if it's done. That toothpick is performing a small test!\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:34.400\nIn science and other fields, tests are more formal. They involve following a specific procedure to get a reliable result.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:47.300\nFor example, a doctor might order a blood test to check your cholesterol levels. Or, an engineer might test a bridge design to make sure it can hold a certain amount of weight.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:57.100\nSo, testing is all about verifying something. It helps us understand, improve, and build things with confidence.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:06.700\nRemember, tests are everywhere, from baking a cake to building a bridge. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
