    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_225724.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like checking if something is working, or seeing how well you understand a new topic.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:23.300\nThere are lots of different kinds of tests. Maybe you've taken a quiz at school to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:33.800\nOr perhaps your doctor orders a blood test to check your health. In the world of computers, we use tests to make sure our programs are working correctly.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:47.000\nFor example, we might test if a button on a website takes you to the right page. Or we could test if a simple math program gives the correct answer, like 2 plus 2 equals 4.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:57.400\nTests help us catch mistakes and make sure things are working as expected. So, to recap, a test is a method for checking something.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:06.900\nIt can be used to measure knowledge, assess health, or ensure the quality of software. It's all about finding out information!\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:10.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ddd348b3-5d5a-477f-a382-0f02163d3050": {
