    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_225820.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of testing.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:16.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and then you taste it. That taste test tells you if you followed the recipe correctly and if the cake is delicious.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:38.800\nIn many fields, tests are used to verify that things are working properly. For example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:49.700\nOr, a car manufacturer might test a new car model to make sure it's safe.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:59.200\nLet's say you're building a simple website. You might test if the buttons work, if the images load correctly, and if the text is easy to read.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:07.700\nTesting helps us catch mistakes early and make sure everything works smoothly.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:19.200\nSo, testing is all about checking and verifying. It\u2019s a vital process that helps ensure quality and reliability in almost everything we do.\n\n01:19.200 --> 01:23.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
