    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE\nAll timings are approximate.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:10.800\nWhat is a test?\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:21.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us see if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:28.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:38.800\nWe use tests all the time. When you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like it.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:47.800\nWhen a doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:52.000\nEven just trying to open a door is a little test to see if it's unlocked.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:56.000\nSo, tests are all about finding things out.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.600\nThey help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:02.000\nTests are important because they give us information.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:05.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
