    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_230455.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:21.700\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:29.100\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:35.600\nIf the light turns on, the lightbulb passes the test. If it doesn't, well, it failed.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:42.100\nAnother example is a spelling test at school.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:50.700\nThe test checks if you know how to spell certain words. A good score means you passed, showing you know your spelling.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:57.700\nSo, a test is just a way to check something and see if it meets our expectations.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:04.200\nIt can be as simple as checking a lightbulb, or more complex, like a medical exam.\n\n01:04.200 --> 01:07.700\nThe point is, it gives us information.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:14.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
