    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_230910.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.400\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but in general, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:29.400\nYou're testing if the lightbulb turns on.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:35.100\nAnother example is baking a cake.\nYou taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:39.700\nThat's a test, too!\nYou're checking the flavor.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:49.400\nBasically, a test is any process you use to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:56.400\nYou try something out, and then you see what happens.\nIt's a simple way to learn and confirm things.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:03.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something works or meets a certain requirement.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.000\nFrom lightbulbs to cake, we're testing things all the time!\n\n01:06.000 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
