    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_231022.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.200\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests. A test is basically a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see what something is like.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's cooked by poking it with a fork. If the fork comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:33.800\nIn science, tests are used to see if an idea is true. For example, you might test if a plant grows better in sunlight or shade.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:41.000\nYou'd put one plant in the sun and another in the shade, and then watch to see which one grows taller.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.200\nTests also help us understand things. Like, a doctor might give you a test to figure out what's making you feel sick.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:57.500\nSo, a test is just a way of finding things out and making sure things are working as they should. It's all about checking and learning!\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
