    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:20.000\nIt's a question, experiment, or procedure designed to see how something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:29.400\nThink about it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might use a toothpick. That toothpick is your test!\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:38.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test. Or, imagine you're trying to figure out if a new light bulb works.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:46.300\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If the light turns on, that's your test, and the light bulb passes!\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:55.600\nTests help us learn and understand the world around us. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:55.600 --> 01:05.700\nIt could be a toothpick in a cake, a light bulb in a socket, or even a quiz at school. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
