    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_232846.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: Tests.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:20.100\nA test, simply put, is a way to find out how well you know something, or how well something works.\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb is working \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:26.600\nWe use tests all the time. In school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:33.000\nBut it's not just about school. A chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:39.400\nOr, before a car is sold, it goes through lots of tests to make sure it's safe.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:52.600\nSo, tests help us understand, evaluate, and improve things.\nThey give us information we can use.\n\n00:52.600 --> 01:02.700\nWhether it's a quiz in class or checking if your bike brakes work, a test helps us know where we stand.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:06.300\nTo sum it up, tests are a tool for learning and improving.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:09.500\nThey help us measure knowledge, performance, or quality.\n\n01:09.500 --> 01:13.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
