    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests,\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:06.500\nwhat they are, and why we use them.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:11.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how well you know something\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:13.700\nor how well something works.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:19.500\nIt\u2019s like checking if you understand a lesson or seeing if a new toy actually does what it\u2019s supposed to.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:23.400\nThink about a spelling test in school.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:26.500\nIt shows how many words you can spell correctly.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:30.600\nOr imagine testing a recipe by making it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:35.600\nTests help us measure knowledge, skills, or even the quality of something.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:44.200\nSo, whether it's a quiz at school, a taste test in the kitchen, or even checking if a lightbulb works, it's all about finding something out.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:53.200\nIn short, a test is a way of checking something to see how well it performs or how much you know.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:57.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
