    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_233325.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:17.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like this: you take a test in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:36.200\nOr, a doctor might run a test to check your health. The main idea is that a test gives us information.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:46.300\nWe can then use that information to make decisions or understand things better.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:56.400\nFor example, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt. Or a builder might test a material to see if it's strong enough.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:09.600\nSo, tests help us measure, evaluate, and learn. They can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all have the same goal: to gain knowledge.\n\n01:09.600 --> 01:19.400\nTo recap, a test is a method to get information about something. We use this information to learn, improve, and make informed choices.\n\n01:19.400 --> 01:23.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
