    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_234146.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer. Tests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:26.100\nImagine you're baking a cake, and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:32.600\nYou might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:39.100\nOr, maybe you're at the doctor. They might take your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:45.600\nSo, a test is just a procedure designed to gather information.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:57.000\nWe do them all the time, often without even realizing it. It's about checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or tells us something specific.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:02.900\nIn short, tests help us learn, diagnose, and make decisions based on evidence.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:04.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
