    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260103_235915.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something, to see if it works or if it's correct.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe by making a small batch to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.700\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:44.900\nTests aren't just for cooking or medicine, though. We use them all the time! When you take a quiz at school, that's a test of what you've learned.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:54.600\nWhen you try to turn on a light and it doesn't work, you've just tested the lightbulb and found out it's not working.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:04.300\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something. It could be a recipe, your health, or even a lightbulb.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:09.700\nTests help us understand if things are working the way they should.\n\n01:09.700 --> 01:12.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
