    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_000257.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:27.000\nIt's a process that helps us understand\nif something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.700\nThink about it like this:\nif you want to know if a lightbulb works, you can test it by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:40.500\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:49.600\nYou might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:58.700\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to.\nThey're everywhere, from checking your spelling to making sure a bridge is safe.\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:01.400\nTests are a vital part of life.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "eed3458d-1a6e-4598-b957-1a5fee9cace9": {
    "id": "eed3458d-1a6e-4598-b957-1a5fee9cace9",
