    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_000342.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:13.700\nNow, a test is basically just a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:28.800\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. The main idea behind a test is to see if something is true or false, correct or incorrect, or just to measure how much of something there is.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:37.800\nFor example, a spelling test shows how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:43.200\nOr, think about tasting a new food. Your taste buds are testing if you like it or not!\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:53.400\nYou're performing a test. Even checking if the lights work by flipping a switch is a simple test.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:03.000\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information and learning something new.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.500\nRemember, tests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all help us understand the world a little better.\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:07.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
