  "ea141d70-35b5-4f28-ab4c-81a2ce099089": {
    "id": "ea141d70-35b5-4f28-ab4c-81a2ce099089",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:12:19.009228",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T00:07:48.951746",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_000748.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_000748.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 and no, not the kind you cram for!\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:16.500\nIn computer programming, a test is simply a way to check if your code is working the way you expect it to.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:40.300\nA test in programming is similar. You run your code, and then you \"taste\" the result to see if it matches what you predicted.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:47.000\nFor example, if you write code to add 2 and 2, a test would check if the answer is actually 4.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:53.700\nOr if you're building a website, a test might check if a button actually takes you to the right page.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:04.400\nTests help you catch mistakes early, making your programs more reliable. So, tests are a way of checking if your code is working.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:07.000\nAnd they're super important for building good software.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:11.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2baf5757-7ddb-4a07-a879-b6ff74b095bf": {
    "id": "2baf5757-7ddb-4a07-a879-b6ff74b095bf",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
