    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey there, welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.000\nToday, we're talking about something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:11.000\nNow, in everyday life, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.000\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it this way: if you want to know if a cake is done baking,\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:20.000\nyou might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:21.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.000\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:25.000\nGreat, the cake's ready.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:29.000\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:32.000\nYou could try turning it on.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:34.000\nIf it lights up, it's working.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:35.000\nThat's another test!\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:40.000\nWe use tests all the time to see if things are working correctly, or to learn new information.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:43.000\nSo, a test is just a simple way to check something out.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:49.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
