    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_001433.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.300\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:08.600\nwhat they are, and why they're important.\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:12.200\nBasically, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:16.300\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:20.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is baked all the way through.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:23.600\nSo, you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:24.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.700\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:33.000\nYour ability to stay balanced and pedal is being tested every time you try.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.200\nTests aren't always scary exams in a classroom.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:39.700\nThey're simply ways to check something.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:43.800\nThey help us understand where we're at, and what we might need to work on.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:53.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something, whether it's your knowledge, your skills, or even if a cake is ready.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:58.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
