    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_001806.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test actually is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:14.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:18.400\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:24.800\nYou don't just guess, right? You perform a test! You might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:30.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test result! You know the cake is done.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:35.200\nOr maybe you're checking if your phone charger works.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:47.800\nYou plug it in, and if your phone starts charging, that's a positive test. Tests can be simple, like checking a cake, or more complex, like a school exam.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:55.200\nBut at its core, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new. So, remember, a test helps us understand things better.\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:57.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
