    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_001852.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.900\nNow, in general, a test is just a way to see how well something works, or how much of something there is.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on, or figuring out how much water is in a glass.\nBasically, we're trying to find out some information.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:34.100\nWe could test a toy to see if it's safe for kids.\nOr, maybe you've taken a quiz at school \u2013 that's a test to see what you've learned!\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:44.200\nFor example, a simple test for a cookie recipe is to bake one cookie first.\nIf it tastes good, then the recipe probably works!\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:54.000\nOr, if you want to know if your bike tires have enough air, you can press on them.\nIf they feel firm, they're probably good to go.\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:05.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information about something.\nIt helps us understand if something works, or how much of something we have.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:09.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
