    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_002143.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:17.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, it's a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well something works.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:26.000\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you do a simple test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it!\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:30.600\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's a test!\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:38.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Your teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:51.500\nOr, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and works correctly. The goal is always to learn something new, or to confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:59.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information. It helps us understand things better.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:03.199\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
