    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_002227.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test is just a way to see what you know or what you can do. Think of it like checking if a lightbulb works \u2013 you turn it on, and that\u2019s your test!\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:23.600\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. Sometimes it's a quiz in school, where you answer questions.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:30.500\nOther times, it's like a taste test for new cookies \u2013 you try them and see which one you like best.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:37.400\nLet\u2019s say you're learning to ride a bike. The test is whether you can balance and pedal without falling.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:46.700\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. The test is how it tastes and looks when it\u2019s done.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:55.900\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to find out something. It helps us learn and improve. It's about understanding, not just getting a right or wrong answer.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:01.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ae58b1c7-efbc-4f95-9055-b2a051919620": {
    "id": "ae58b1c7-efbc-4f95-9055-b2a051919620",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:12:32.783317",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T00:23:28.730503",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_002328.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_002328.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! \nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:21.000\nNow, in everyday life, a test is simply a way to check something.\nThink about it like this: you might test the water temperature before getting in the shower, or test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:33.600\nIn science and math, tests are used to see if an idea, or a hypothesis, is correct.\nWe do experiments, and the test is the results we get.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:47.600\nFor example, imagine you think fertilizer helps plants grow faster.\nYou could test this by giving one plant fertilizer and another plant only water, and then see which one grows taller.\nThe comparison of their growth is your test!\n\n00:47.600 --> 01:00.200\nSo, tests are all about checking things, comparing results, and figuring out if our ideas are right or wrong.\nThey help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:07.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
