    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_002937.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it like checking if your bike tires have enough air.\nYou're performing a test to see if they're ready to ride.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:31.500\nIn the world of, say, cooking, you might test if your cake is done by poking it with a toothpick.\nIf it comes out clean, it passes the test!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:38.100\nOr, imagine a toy car.\nYou might test it by pushing it to see if it rolls smoothly.\nThat\u2019s a test too!\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:45.500\nSo, tests are all about making sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\nThey help us find problems and fix them.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:53.200\nThey are a fundamental part of making sure things function properly.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:56.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
