    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_003021.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:22.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you poke them with a toothpick.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:33.400\nIn a more formal setting, a test helps us understand how well someone knows something, or how well something works.\nFor example, a spelling test shows how well you know your spelling words.\nOr, a car manufacturer might test a new car to see if it's safe.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:43.700\nWe use tests to measure, to learn, and to improve.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:49.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check up on things.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:53.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
