    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_004155.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:18.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is just a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:29.800\nThat's a test! You\u2019re testing the lightbulb.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:40.000\nAnother example is checking if your cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:53.600\nTests help us learn, improve things, and make sure everything is working the way it should. So, basically, a test is a simple way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:57.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
