    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:17.000\nIt helps us understand if something is working the way it should, or if someone knows what they're supposed to know.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you've learned your words.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:28.000\nOr, a doctor might run a test to check if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:30.000\nTests can be used for all sorts of things!\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:36.000\nAnother example is testing a new toy. We might try it out to make sure it's safe and fun before giving it to kids.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:41.000\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and checking things out.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:44.500\nRemember, a test helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:51.000\nIn short, a test is a method for evaluating knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
