    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_005317.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:04.100\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.100 --> 00:05.900\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, maybe in school.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:07.900\nBut what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:13.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well something works.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:17.200\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:18.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:23.000\nOr, if you want to see if you know your ABCs, someone might ask you to recite them.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:23.900\nThat's another test!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:28.900\nTests can come in many forms: quizzes, exams, experiments, even just trying something out.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:36.400\nThe goal is always to gather information and see if you've met a certain standard or achieved a certain result.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:39.000\nSo, a test helps us understand something better.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:41.700\nRemember, it's all about learning and figuring things out.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:43.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
