    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_005358.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.300\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:06.800\nToday we're going to explore something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:11.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:15.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:21.000\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.600\nOr, a doctor might run a test to check your health.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:25.500\nSee?\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:28.800\nDifferent tests, different questions, different answers.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:36.000\nAnother example could be testing if a toy car needs new batteries. You try turning it on!\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:40.600\nIf it works, the batteries are probably okay.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:44.400\nIf it doesn't, the batteries probably need replacing.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:44.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:48.500\nSo, a test is just a process to gather information.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:53.000\nIt helps us understand things better and make decisions.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:57.500\nIt's all about asking questions and finding answers.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
