    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_005837.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:05.200\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:07.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:13.300\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:15.300\nThink of it as a little experiment!\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:19.200\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:23.300\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:27.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test!\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:29.100\nIt tells you the cake is done.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:35.400\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a toy car needs new batteries.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:37.800\nYou try turning it on.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:41.100\nIf it doesn't move, that\u2019s a test showing the batteries are probably dead.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:44.900\nSo, testing helps us understand things and make decisions.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:48.600\nIt's all about finding out information.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.800\nBasically, a test is a question, and the result is the answer.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:54.100\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:57.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "74565134-d14c-4898-aa3c-74ab7bd2dc7f": {
    "id": "74565134-d14c-4898-aa3c-74ab7bd2dc7f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:13:07.656090",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T00:59:19.902401",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_005919.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_005919.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:09.600\nAt its most basic, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:09.600 --> 00:17.100\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don\u2019t realize it. Think of it like this: you taste a new food to test if you like it.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:28.400\nOr you press a button to test if the light will turn on. In science and many other areas, a test is a procedure designed to prove or disprove something.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:39.700\nWe call that something a hypothesis, which is just a fancy word for a guess. For example, you might hypothesize that plants grow better in sunlight.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:48.900\nTo test this, you could put one plant in the sun and another in the shade. Then, you observe them to see which grows taller.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:55.200\nThat's a test! So, tests are simply ways to check if something is true or not.\n\n00:55.200 --> 00:58.400\nThey help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
