    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_010250.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.700\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:09.800\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:17.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:31.000\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:36.800\nThat test helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:41.700\nOr, if you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:46.900\nThat's a test, too!\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:49.700\nYou're checking if the cake meets your expectations.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:53.900\nTests aren't just for school or baking.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.300\nScientists use tests to check if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:01.400\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:06.700\nSo, a test is really just a method for getting information and making sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:06.700 --> 01:09.600\nIt's all about checking and learning!\n\n01:09.600 --> 01:12.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
