    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_010927.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:04.600\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:09.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:13.400\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:17.700\nOr maybe you buy a new toy and press all the buttons to make sure they all work properly.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:18.800\nThose are both tests!\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:25.000\nIn computers and software, tests are used to make sure that programs are doing exactly what they're designed to do.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:29.500\nSo, if we\u2019re building a calculator app, we might test to see if 2 plus 2 really equals 4.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:34.500\nOr, for a website, we might test if clicking a button takes you to the right page.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:38.400\nTesting helps us find mistakes early and make sure everything is working perfectly.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:41.700\nTo recap, a test is simply a check to see if something is working as expected.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:43.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
