    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.000\nHello everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:08.000\nToday we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:14.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:22.000\nBoom, you've performed a test!\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:28.000\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs, though.\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:35.000\nTeachers give tests to see how much you've learned.\nEven bakers test their cakes by poking them with a toothpick to see if they're done.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:42.000\nSo, a test is just a way to check something and see if it meets a certain standard.\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:52.000\nWhether it's a school exam or checking if your car starts, tests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
