    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T01:19:48.867775",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_011948.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_011948.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.100\nNow, you probably already know what a test is \u2013 maybe you think of school or quizzes. But in general, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:25.700\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:36.600\nThink about it like this: A doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy. A baker might taste their cake batter to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:42.100\nOr, you might even test a new video game before it's released to make sure it works properly.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:45.900\nBasically, a test helps us answer a question.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:49.700\nIs the cake tasty? Are you feeling well?\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:53.500\nDoes the game run smoothly?\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:55.500\nBy performing the test, we get the information we need\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:58.500\nto make a decision or understand something better.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:02.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a process for gathering information.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:04.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "60b76e87-8338-478f-9a3f-c945df3532f7": {
