    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_012048.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:27.300\nIt could be checking if you know something, like a quiz at school. Or it could be checking if something works, like testing a new toy to make sure it's safe.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:32.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if your cookies are done, you might use a toothpick to test them.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:44.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies are ready! That's a test! Another example is a doctor checking your temperature \u2013 that\u2019s a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:53.400\nSo, a test is just a way to find out information about something. We use tests all the time to learn new things and make sure things are working properly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
