    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_013150.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:20.200\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like an experiment, but often much simpler. We use tests all the time to check if something is working properly, or to see how well someone understands a topic.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:45.900\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, in school, you take tests to show your teacher what you've learned. Even your phone goes through tests to make sure all its features are working.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:58.000\nSo, a test is really just a structured way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation. Whether it's a quick quiz or a complex scientific experiment, the basic idea is always the same: to learn something new or confirm what we already know.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
