    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_013321.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:20.800\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer. Think of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:28.000\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:34.000\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works. You can test it by plugging it in.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:39.700\nIf it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:50.200\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a toy needs new batteries to seeing if you understand what you've learned in school.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:61.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something and see if it works or if it's true. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
