    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:14.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information. It's like asking a question, but often in a more organized way.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like this: your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a quiz at school to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:38.700\nTests can be written, spoken, or even involve doing something, like a physical exam.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:49.800\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works by plugging it in. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:49.800 --> 01:04.000\nAnother test could be asking a friend, \"What's two plus two?\" Their answer tells you if they know basic math.\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:07.400\nSo, to recap, a test is a method to gather information or check something.\n\n01:07.400 --> 01:18.200\nThey come in many forms, from simple everyday checks to more complex, formal assessments. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
