    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:13:41.108415",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T01:41:17.014702",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_014116.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_014116.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:16.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:26.600\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand something better.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:33.400\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:40.200\nOr, a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever. These are all tests!\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:49.500\nTests can be formal, like a school exam that shows what you've learned. Or informal, like wiggling a loose tooth to see if it's ready to come out.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:60.000\nThe important thing is that a test gives us information. It helps us make decisions and learn new things. So, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and answer a question. It's a fundamental tool we use every day. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "bcf66ef7-e728-4171-a6f9-4df7f0f6a6ba": {
    "id": "bcf66ef7-e728-4171-a6f9-4df7f0f6a6ba",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
