    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T01:42:10.097419",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_014209.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_014209.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:10.000\nWhat is a test? Simply put, it's a way to check something.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:16.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done. You poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:21.700\nTests help us learn if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:30.200\nMaybe you're taking a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words. Or a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:34.200\nAnother example? Imagine you build a toy car.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:39.000\nYou give it a push to see if it rolls. That's testing your car!\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:50.200\nSo, a test is just a simple way to see if something is true, correct, or working properly. Tests help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:53.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a01270c9-7924-47f7-891a-49b19f557feb": {
