    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_014254.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment or a question you ask to get information.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.900\nWe use tests all the time! For example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:31.300\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned in class. And even baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing the recipe to see if it works!\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:42.900\nSo, tests can be anything from answering questions on paper to trying out a new recipe. The important thing is that they help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:53.900\nThey give us results that we can then use. In short, a test is a method for gathering information and seeing how something works or what someone knows.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3ddc1b21-653f-4cfe-9e91-78cf35305f8b": {
