    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_014336.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.300\nIt helps us check if something is working, if something is true, or how well something is done. Think of it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. Or, imagine a taste test!\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:31.700\nYou try different foods to see which one you like best. Doctors use tests all the time to see if you\u2019re healthy.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:39.000\nThey might test your vision or your reflexes. So, a test is just a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:49.300\nIt can be a question, a process, or even an experiment. It gives us information and helps us make decisions.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:58.600\nTests are used everywhere, from school to science to everyday life!\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:02.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "29a4445b-6bf1-440c-95ef-e43f60dc896c": {
    "id": "29a4445b-6bf1-440c-95ef-e43f60dc896c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:13:43.475773",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T01:44:41.710280",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_014441.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_014441.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.500\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like this: You have a lightbulb. A test would be screwing it into a lamp to see if it lights up.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:29.500\nIf it does, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails, and you know there's a problem.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:35.000\nAnother simple example is checking if your car starts. You turn the key.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:40.500\nDoes the engine roar to life? Pass! Does it just click? Fail!\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.700\nSo, a test is really just a way to confirm that something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:46.300\nWe try something, and then we see if the results match our expectations.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:47.800\nThat's it!\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:57.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
