    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_014931.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:14.700\nToday, we're diving into the basics of testing.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:25.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if it's doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:34.800\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:44.600\nIn everyday life, we're constantly testing things. When you try a new lightbulb, you're testing to see if it lights up.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:50.600\nWhen you kick a soccer ball, you're testing how far you can kick it.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:52.600\nTests help us identify problems and make improvements.\n```"
