    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_020536.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:06.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how much you know about something,\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:08.400\nor how well you can do something.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:11.300\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:13.500\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:17.700\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:20.400\nThere are written tests with questions and answers, like in school.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:24.800\nBut there are also practical tests, like a driving test where you show you can actually drive a car.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:29.600\nImagine you're learning to bake cookies.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:31.300\nThe test is tasting the cookie!\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:34.400\nDoes it taste good?\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:36.900\nIs it cooked properly?\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:40.100\nThat tells you how well you followed the recipe.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.800\nSo, a test is just a process for finding out information.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:48.400\nIt helps us understand what we know, what we can do,\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:51.500\nand what we still need to learn.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
