    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.300 --> 00:02.200\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:03.900\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:06.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:08.700\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe by tasting it.\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:09.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:09.700 --> 00:12.300\nOr maybe you test your car's brakes before driving down a steep hill.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:12.900\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:16.200\nIn school, you take tests to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:17.800\nA doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:20.400\nEven scientists use tests to prove their ideas.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:24.300\nSo, a test is just a way to get information and make sure things are as they should be.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:26.000\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:28.200\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:29.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
