    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:06.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:11.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:16.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:19.500\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like this: you might test if your cookies are done baking by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:28.200\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:28.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:32.000\nOr maybe you test a new phone to see if the camera works.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.800\nYou take a picture, and if it looks good, the camera passed the test.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:39.800\nSo, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:42.000\nThey give us information to make decisions.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.500\nWhether it's baking cookies or checking a phone, tests are all about learning something new.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:53.800\nIn short, a test is a way to get information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:54.300 --> 00:57.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
