    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_021523.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE: The subtitles are based on the provided narration and timing.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\nThink of it like asking a question and then finding the answer.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:20.400\nWe use tests all the time!\nA doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:30.700\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to check what you've learned.\nEven trying a new recipe is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if it tastes good!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:47.800\nThe goal of a test is to get data, or facts, that help us understand something better.\nSo, whether it's a science experiment, a medical checkup, or even just trying out a new game, you're performing a test.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:55.200\nThey help us learn and make better decisions.\nSo remember, a test is a way to get information.\n\n00:55.200 --> 01:02.100\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
