    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_022319.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.000\nAt its most basic, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:09.000\nWe use them all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if an apple is ripe.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:15.000\nYou might give it a squeeze.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:16.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:20.000\nYou're testing its firmness to see if it's ready to eat.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:23.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.000\nYou insert a toothpick to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:27.000\nThat's another test!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.000\nYou're checking if the cake is cooked all the way through.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:35.000\nSo, a test is really just an action or procedure designed to reveal information about something.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:41.000\nWhether it's checking an apple or baking a cake, tests help us make informed decisions.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:43.000\nThey give us data!\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:47.000\nThey are really important in a lot of different fields.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:51.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
