    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but a test is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:24.200\nIt's a process of asking a question and getting an answer. Think about it like this: a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:32.700\nOr a baker might test a recipe to see if it tastes good. In both cases, they're doing something to get information.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:44.800\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb works by flipping the switch. Or they can be more complex, like a doctor running blood tests to understand your health.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:57.600\nThe key is that a test helps us learn something we didn't know before. So, remember, a test is simply a way of gathering information by asking a question and observing the answer.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:03.000\nTests are everywhere! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
