    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_022810.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:17.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:29.800\nThink of it like asking a question and then getting an answer, but in a more formal way.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:38.600\nThe main idea behind a test is to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:43.200\nWe want to know if it works the way it's supposed to, or if it has a certain quality.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:47.800\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:53.200\nA taste test checks if food tastes good. And a strength test checks how much weight someone can lift.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:56.100\nSee? They all check something specific.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:03.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and see if it meets our expectations.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:05.300\nIt helps us understand more about the world around us.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:06.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
