    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:24.100\nThat's a test! Basically, a test tells you whether something passes or fails a certain requirement.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:32.800\nIt helps you understand if something is working correctly. For example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:43.200\nOr, a teacher gives you a test to see if you understand the lesson. Even checking if the light switch works before you leave a room is a mini-test!\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:55.000\nYou're checking if it passes the \"turns on the light\" requirement. So, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:55.000 --> 01:02.500\nIt helps us make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
