    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_023241.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:03.900\nToday we're diving into something super important:\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:04.600\nTests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:07.900\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:11.600\nThink of it like this: you're testing if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:15.100\nThe main idea is to give something a try and see what happens.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:17.900\nDid you get the result you expected?\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:18.900\nThat's a successful test!\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:23.900\nFor example, maybe you're baking cookies. You taste one to test if you added enough sugar.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:28.500\nOr, if you're building with LEGOs, you test if the tower stays standing.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:29.500\nSee?\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:30.700\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:35.500\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is simply checking something to make sure it works correctly.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:42.900\nWhether it's cookies or lightbulbs, testing helps us understand if things are doing what they should.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
