    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_023331.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:07.600\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:15.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\nYou might use a toothpick \u2013 that's your test!\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:28.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\nThat's a positive test result.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:35.000\nIf it's gooey, not ready yet \u2013 a negative test result.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:42.700\nTests aren't just for baking, of course.\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even scientists use tests to prove or disprove their ideas.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:53.100\nSo, a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\nIt\u2019s a way of checking something to see if it meets a certain requirement or standard.\n\n00:53.100 --> 01:00.300\nThat's the basic idea behind tests!\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
