    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_023423.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:20.600\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:28.700\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Well, almost anything! You might take a quiz in school, which is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:39.500\nOr a doctor might run a blood test to check your health. Even baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if the recipe works!\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:48.200\nFor example, imagine you want to know if a plant needs more water. You can test this by touching the soil.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:56.900\nIf it feels dry, that's a test result that suggests you should water the plant.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:03.900\nSo, to recap: a test is a process of asking a question and getting an answer, whether it's about knowledge, health, or even baking.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:06.700\nIt helps us learn and understand things better.\n```"
