  "5ee0275c-0b38-4027-84f1-8095e953bbcb": {
    "id": "5ee0275c-0b38-4027-84f1-8095e953bbcb",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:14:22.838946",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T02:35:55.222084",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_023555.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_023555.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test is basically a way to see how much you know about something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like a measuring stick for your knowledge.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:33.300\nIt helps you, and your teachers, understand what you've learned and what areas might need a little more work.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:45.600\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes. You might have a multiple-choice test where you pick the best answer, or maybe a true or false quiz.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:51.600\nSometimes, you even get to show what you know by writing out your answers in a longer format.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:58.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. A math test sees if you can solve equations.\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:05.800\nTests aren't meant to be scary! They're just a tool to help you learn.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:12.900\nSo, remember, a test is a way to measure what you know. It helps you and others understand your learning progress.\n\n01:12.900 --> 01:16.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "861bcf2f-628d-4bd7-a79d-ad849431721f": {
    "id": "861bcf2f-628d-4bd7-a79d-ad849431721f",
