    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_023732.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, welcome! \n\n00:07.100 --> 00:15.600\nToday we're going to explore something super important: Tests! \n\n00:15.600 --> 00:20.200\nWhat exactly is a test? \n\n00:20.200 --> 00:24.800\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:31.200\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works. That's a test! You're testing the bulb to see if it lights up.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:37.600\nAnother example: a cookie recipe. You're testing it to see if the cookies taste good.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:48.200\nOr even simpler, when you weigh yourself on a scale, you're performing a test to find out your weight. So, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:54.700\nThey give us information and let us know if something is working as expected, or if something needs to be changed. They're everywhere!\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:56.300\nIn short, a test is a way of checking something to learn more about it.\n\n00:56.300 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
