    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.500\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take at school, but in general, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:25.700\nIt's a process to check if something is working, or to see what its properties are.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:32.500\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:41.000\nOr, imagine you\u2019re checking if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp. That's a test!\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:46.100\nYou're testing the bulb to see if it lights up.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:51.200\nAnother example: you might test if a toy car can roll down a ramp.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:56.300\nYou let it go, and observe what happens. That's your test!\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:01.400\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of finding something out by observing what happens.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:04.900\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:13.000\nIn short, tests help us learn and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
