    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.600\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:20.800\nIt could be anything from a simple check to see if a lightbulb works, to a more complex exam that measures your knowledge.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:30.700\nBasically, you perform an action or set up a situation, and then you observe the result.\nThat result gives you information.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:44.700\nFor example, if you want to know if your cake is done, you can stick a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test result, and it tells you your cake is ready!\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:54.800\nOr maybe you're testing if a toy car works.\nYou put batteries in it, turn it on, and if it moves, the test is successful!\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:04.600\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to get information about something by observing the outcome of a specific action.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:08.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c6da755c-999d-42ed-8e35-e70d40ccfbdf": {
