    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_024818.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:18.900\nA test is basically a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:28.800\nIt helps us understand if something is working, if something is true, or even how well someone understands a topic.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:35.800\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:42.800\nYou flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:52.000\nOr, imagine taking a quiz in school. That's a test to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:55.000\nScientists use tests all the time to see if their ideas are correct, like testing a new medicine to see if it makes people feel better.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n```"
  },
