    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_025120.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:20.600\nIt's a process we use to evaluate or assess something.\nTests can come in many forms.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:29.800\nA common example is a school exam, designed to see how well you understand a subject.\nBut it's not just about grades!\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:44.100\nYou might test a recipe to see if it tastes good, or test a new toy to see if it's durable.\nFor example, when you try a new brand of coffee, you\u2019re basically testing it to see if you like the flavor.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:52.200\nOr, if you're trying to fix a broken lamp, you might test different lightbulbs until you find one that works.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:03.500\nSo, in short, a test is a method to gather information, evaluate something, and learn more.\nIt's all about finding out the answer!\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:07.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
