    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_025434.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what is a test?\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:31.100\nOr, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health. Even baking a cake is a test!\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:38.000\nYou're testing your recipe and your baking skills. Tests can be written, like exams.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:48.200\nThey can be physical, like a sports tryout. Or they can be observational, like watching how a plant grows under different conditions.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:59.500\nThe key is they all have a purpose: to give us information. So, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information about something.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:08.500\nWhether it's a school exam, a medical checkup, or a cooking experiment, it's all about learning and understanding.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:12.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
