    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_025901.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:11.000\nWe use them all the time!\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like this: you're trying a new recipe, that's a test!\nYou're testing to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:24.000\nIn school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:28.000\nThey can be multiple choice, true or false, or even just writing out the answer.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:35.000\nAnother example?\nImagine you\u2019re checking if your bike brakes are working.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:39.000\nYou give them a squeeze \u2013 that\u2019s a test!\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:42.000\nYou're testing if they stop the bike.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.000\nTests help us learn and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:51.000\nSo, a test is basically a way to check something out.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:58.000\nWhether it\u2019s your knowledge, a recipe, or your bike brakes, tests give us important information.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
