    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_025935.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:23.400\nIt's a process we use to gather information.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:28.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:37.000\nYou use a toothpick \u2013 that's your test!\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:47.100\nIf it's gooey, it fails, and needs more time in the oven. See?\nAnother example: a doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\nBlood tests, eye exams, all tests!\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:50.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to help us learn something or check something.\nIt gives us evidence to make decisions.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
