    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_030853.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.200\nSimply put, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready, so you stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:34.200\nIn general, tests help us understand if something is working correctly or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:41.100\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:48.000\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:58.200\nAnother example? A car company might test a new car to make sure it's safe before selling it.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:01.700\nSo, whether it's baking a cake, studying for school, or building a car, tests are all about checking and understanding.\nBasically, a test is a simple way to get information and make sure things are as they should be.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
