    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_031608.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:22.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we know something well.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\nYou turn it on \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:35.900\nIf it lights up, it passes.\nIf not, it fails.\nTests can be anything from a quick quiz in school to a medical exam at the doctor's.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:44.400\nThey help us measure and understand different things.\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your words.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:56.600\nA taste test checks how yummy something is!\nSo, tests are a simple way to check things, understand what we know, and see if something is working as it should.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
