    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.500\nToday we're talking about tests, a simple but important concept.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:07.900\nA test is basically a way to check something.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:11.900\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:14.700\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:17.500\nA spelling test checks your spelling skills, right?\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:20.800\nOr maybe you've seen a battery test.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:23.000\nThat checks if a battery still has power.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.600\nEven tasting food is a kind of test!\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:29.200\nYou're testing if you like the flavor.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:34.100\nSo, to recap, a test is just a method for finding out about something.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:40.400\nIt helps us understand if something works, if something is true, or even if we simply like it.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:46.900\nFrom quizzes to checking if your bike tires have enough air, tests are all around us.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:48.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
