    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_031901.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nThink of a test as a way to check something. It could be checking if a lightbulb works, or if a cake tastes good, or even if you know your ABCs.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:24.900\nBasically, a test helps us find out if something is working as expected, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:36.100\nSo, if you're testing a toy car, you might see if it goes fast enough. If you're testing a recipe, you'd taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:46.700\nTests can be simple, like looking at something to see if it's broken, or they can be more complex, involving lots of steps and measurements.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:56.700\nThe important thing is they give us information. So, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something passes or fails.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
