    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:04.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:07.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:17.000\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:20.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:24.500\nOr, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:27.000\nTests aren't always scary!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:33.000\nFor example, you might test if a light bulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:35.500\nIf it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:40.000\nAnother example is tasting food to test if it's delicious.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:42.500\nSee? Tests are everywhere.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:46.500\nSo, a test is just a simple way to check something and get an answer.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:52.000\nThey help us learn and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
