    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_032341.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_032341.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNow, you might be thinking of school exams, but in this case, a test is really just a way to see if something works like it should.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like checking if your shoes fit. You try them on, walk around, and see if they're comfortable. That's a test!\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:26.900\nOr maybe you're baking a cake. You taste the batter to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:31.800\nThat's another test! In science, we use tests to see if our ideas are right.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:48.300\nFor example, if you think watering plants makes them grow taller, you could test that by watering some plants and not watering others, then comparing their height.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:59.100\nThe results of the test tell you if your idea was on the right track. So, a test is simply a way to check something to see if it works or if it's true.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
