    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_032730.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:16.900\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something. It's how we check if something is true, or if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:30.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe by cooking it. The \"test\" is the cooking process, and the result tells you if the recipe is good or needs some tweaking.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:40.300\nOr, imagine you're testing a toy car to see how far it can go. You push it, and the distance it travels is the result of your test.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:47.500\nTests can be used to check all sorts of things, from your spelling skills to the strength of a bridge.\n\n00:47.500 --> 01:00.600\nThe key is to have a clear goal and a way to measure the outcome. So, a test is simply a process of checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:04.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
