    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_033329.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests!\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test is really just a way to see how well you know something.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:36.900\nThe main idea behind a test is to give you questions or tasks related to a specific topic, and then check your answers to see what you've learned.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:43.800\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:50.700\nOr a math test might ask you to solve some simple equations.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:54.600\nAnother example is a taste test!\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:58.500\nYou try different foods and tell someone which one you like best.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:01.200\nThat's a test too!\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:02.100\nIt\u2019s testing your preference.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:14.700\nSo, in short, a test is just a way to measure knowledge or ability. It helps you and others understand what you already know and what you might need to learn more about.\n\n01:14.700 --> 01:18.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
