    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_034133.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something, or to see if something works the way it should.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:33.900\nOr, imagine you're testing a new toy car to see how fast it goes. You're performing a test!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:39.200\nTests happen all around us.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:51.200\nDoctors use tests to check your health. Teachers use tests to see what you've learned. So, a test is just a method for gathering information and understanding if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:51.200 --> 01:02.200\nIn short, a test helps us confirm if something is working correctly or meets a specific requirement. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
