    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_034319.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:19.000\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we're talking about a way to check or evaluate something. Think of it like this: you're trying to figure out if something works, or if it's good enough.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:24.700\nA test helps you find out.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:32.800\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake. You might take a toothpick and poke it in the middle. If it comes out clean, that's a test showing the cake is done.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:40.300\nOr, if you're trying out a new toy, you might play with it for a while to test if it's fun and durable.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:47.800\nTests can be simple, like that, or more complicated, depending on what you need to know.\n\n00:47.800 --> 01:04.400\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it meets certain requirements or expectations. It helps us learn and make better decisions.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:09.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
