    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_034649.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:12.900\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:20.200\nIt helps us measure or evaluate something to see where it stands.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:26.400\nThink of it like this: You might test a cake to see if it's baked all the way through by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:31.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:36.000\nOr, a doctor might test your eyesight to see how well you can see.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:38.400\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:51.200\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. They can help us understand if we've learned something new, like a quiz in school. Or they can help us see if something is working correctly, like testing a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:55.600\nSo, a test is simply a procedure designed to find out information.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:57.900\nIt's a way of measuring or evaluating something.\n\n00:57.900 --> 00:58.500\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:58.500 --> 00:59.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
