    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_035203.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:22.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a light bulb works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:28.400\nTests can be big or small, simple or complex.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:39.400\nMaybe you\u2019re testing a recipe to see if it tastes good, or testing a new toy to see if it's safe.\nScientists use tests all the time to learn about the world.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:51.900\nThey might test if a plant grows better in sunlight or shade.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information by doing something and observing the result.\nIt\u2019s all about checking things out!\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
