    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_035433.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.220 --> 00:01.270\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.270 --> 00:02.020\nToday we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:02.680 --> 00:03.730\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.730 --> 00:07.050\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:07.670 --> 00:12.260\nThink about it like this: When you take a spelling test at school, it shows how many words you can spell correctly.\n\n00:12.790 --> 00:17.930\nOr imagine you're trying out a new recipe.\nYou taste it to test if it's good!\n\n00:17.930 --> 00:20.080\nMaybe it needs more salt, or less pepper.\n\n00:20.080 --> 00:21.730\nTests help us understand and improve things.\n\n00:22.130 --> 00:26.660\nAnother example is when a doctor checks your temperature.\nThat\u2019s a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:27.040 --> 00:31.310\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but their main purpose is to give us information.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:35.910\nTo recap, a test is a method to evaluate knowledge or performance.\n\n00:35.910 --> 00:38.770\nThey help us measure, learn, and improve.\n\n00:39.220 --> 00:41.190\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
