    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:15:40.795525",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T04:12:13.425178",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_041213.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_041213.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:11.300\nToday we're talking about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:20.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it as a question, or a set of questions, designed to measure your knowledge, skills, or even abilities.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:27.100\nIt's like checking if a lightbulb works. You try to turn it on, and that's the test.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:33.600\nIf it lights up, it passes! In school, tests help teachers see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:44.400\nIf you're baking a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it needs more sugar. Tests come in many forms, but they all help us understand something better.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:53.100\nSo remember, a test is just a way to find things out. It helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:56.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "395587c9-4adf-4294-ba55-dcc1277f4333": {
    "id": "395587c9-4adf-4294-ba55-dcc1277f4333",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:15:41.394536",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T04:13:07.783851",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_041307.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_041307.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:19.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:28.600\nFor example, a cookie recipe is a test! You follow the instructions, then you taste the cookie.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:36.200\nThe taste is the \"answer\" telling you if the recipe worked.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:43.800\nOr imagine you\u2019re trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:51.400\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. If the light turns on, the bulb passes the test!\n\n00:51.400 --> 01:01.700\nSo, tests help us learn, check things, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:05.300\nA test can be as easy as tasting a cookie or as complicated as checking if a bridge is safe.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:08.300\nThe important thing is that it helps you get information.\n\n01:08.300 --> 01:11.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
