    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_041459.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.800\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:23.000\nIt helps us understand if something works, is true, or is good enough. Think of it like this: you might test a new recipe by tasting it.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:33.000\nThat taste test tells you if you need more salt, sugar, or something else. Or imagine a doctor running tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:39.800\nThey might check your blood pressure or run a blood test. These tests give them important information.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:47.200\nAnother example is a school test. It's a way for teachers to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:54.600\nSo, tests come in many forms, but they all share the same purpose: to give us information and help us make decisions.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:04.600\nThey help us confirm things, improve things, and learn things. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:10.200\nIt gives us information.\n\n01:10.200 --> 01:15.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
