    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_042857.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you only do in school, but really, a test is just a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like this: a test helps us see if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:31.600\nFor example, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:39.000\nOr a baker might taste their cake to test if it's sweet enough. See? Different kinds of tests, same idea.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:44.500\nAnother simple example is checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:49.900\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passed! If it doesn't, well, it failed.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:57.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a simple way to check something. It helps us understand if things are the way we expect them to be.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:00.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
