    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_043156.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.300\nNow, you might think of school exams, but a test, in general, is really just a way to check if something is working correctly or is what we expect it to be.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:30.700\nThink of it like this: If you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it\u2019s sweet enough. Or, if you buy a new toy, you'll probably play with it to test if all its buttons work.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:40.300\nIn science and technology, tests are used all the time. For example, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:53.100\nOr, an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it can hold a lot of weight. So, a test is simply a way to find out if something meets a certain standard or works as it should.\n\n00:53.100 --> 01:01.100\nIn short, tests help us to check, verify, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:04.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
