    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_043725.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_043725.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:12.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. For example, a simple quiz in school is a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:30.900\nOr, imagine testing the temperature of your bath water to see if it's too hot or just right. You're testing it!\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:38.400\nTests aren't just for school or baths, though. Scientists use tests to see if a new medicine works.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:50.900\nBakers test their cake batter to make sure it\u2019s the right consistency. Basically, any time you're trying to learn something by observing or measuring, you're doing a test.\n\n00:50.900 --> 01:01.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to gather information and learn something new. It helps us understand the world around us.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
