  "6679b116-275a-41fc-9227-34813c8c6bf1": {
    "id": "6679b116-275a-41fc-9227-34813c8c6bf1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:16:02.434706",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T04:39:18.432425",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_043918.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_043918.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.200\nNow, you've probably taken lots of tests in school, but in general, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works. The test is to screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:28.400\nIf the light comes on, it passes the test!\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:34.600\nAnother example is baking a cake. You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:43.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's the test! So, essentially, a test is just a procedure or action designed to give you information about something.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:49.800\nIt helps you decide if it's working, if it's correct, or if it's ready.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
