    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_044143.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.700\nToday we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:07.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:12.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb is good.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:14.900\nYou put it in a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:16.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:19.100\nIf the light turns on, the test passes.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:20.400\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:23.400\nTests aren't just for light bulbs, though.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:25.700\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:28.200\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:30.300\nEven scientists use tests to prove their ideas.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:33.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:37.100\nIt can be as simple as flipping a switch, or something much more complicated.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:41.900\nThe important thing is, it helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:44.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
