    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_045800.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_045800.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.800\nA test is simply a way to check something or find something out. Think of it like a question you're trying to answer, but in a more formal way.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:29.700\nTests can be used to see if something works, like testing a new toy to make sure it's safe. Or, they can be used to measure something, like a doctor using a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:41.500\nEven a simple quiz at school is a test, designed to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:51.300\nFor example, you might test a battery to see if it has enough power. Or, you could test the temperature of water to see if it's hot enough for a bath.\n\n00:51.300 --> 01:02.200\nThese tests help us make decisions based on the results. So, remember, a test is just a way to check, measure, or find something out.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:05.800\nIt helps us learn and make better decisions.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
