    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something, to see if it works, or to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:38.300\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to test the seasoning. In school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:50.100\nTests can be as simple as asking someone a question, or as complex as a long exam. The important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:50.100 --> 01:01.100\nMaybe the blood test shows you need more vitamins, the soup needs more salt, or you need to study a little harder.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:04.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and learn from the results.\n01:04.700 --> 01:12.100\nIt helps us understand where we're at and what we need to do next.\n\n01:12.100 --> 01:15.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
