    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:18.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:27.900\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Well, lots!\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:33.200\nWe can test if a lightbulb works by turning it on. That's a test!\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:38.500\nWe can test if a cookie tastes good by eating it. That's another test!\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:48.800\nOr, maybe you take a quiz in school to test what you've learned.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:57.100\nEssentially, a test helps us confirm something or learn more about it.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:05.400\nWe set up a specific situation, observe what happens, and then draw a conclusion based on what we see.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:16.500\nIt\u2019s a simple way to gather information and check if things are working as expected.\n\n01:16.500 --> 01:24.200\nTo recap, a test is a process to evaluate something and get results.\n\n01:24.200 --> 01:31.000\nRemember to always be curious and keep testing things out!\n\n01:31.000 --> 01:31.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
