    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.400 --> 00:02.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:05.100\nA test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:06.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:07.700\nTests can be used for all sorts of things!\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:13.100\nMaybe you want to test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, it's ready!\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:17.700\nOr perhaps you want to test your knowledge of animals with a quiz.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:21.300\nYou answer the questions, and the quiz tells you how much you know.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.400\nAnother example is testing a new toy.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:28.000\nYou play with it to see if it's fun and durable.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:34.200\nBasically, a test helps us learn more about something by putting it through a process and observing the results.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.300\nSo, to recap, a test is a procedure designed to get information about something.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:44.200\nIt can be a simple observation or a complex experiment.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:47.000\nThe goal is always to learn and understand.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:48.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
