    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_051048.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\nThink of it like an experiment or a way to check if something is true.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:24.200\nThe main idea behind a test is to see if a certain condition or action leads to a specific result.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:32.200\nIf it does, then the test passes.\nIf it doesn't, well, then it fails.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.900\nFor example, imagine you're testing if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:43.000\nYou screw it into a lamp.\nIf the light turns on, the test passes!\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:48.100\nThe bulb works.\nBut if the light stays off, the test fails.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:52.900\nThe bulb is no good.\nAnother example: a taste test!\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:03.200\nYou try a new cookie.\nIf you like it, it passes your taste test!\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something, to see if it works or if it's true.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:07.200\nIt's all about finding out the answer.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
