    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey there, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.500\nToday, we're going to talk about something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:08.500\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way of finding out something.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:15.000\nYou might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:16.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:19.500\nBasically, it's a procedure we use to gather information.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:24.500\nIt could be a written exam in school to see what you've learned.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:29.500\nOr, it could be a scientist running an experiment to see if a new medicine works.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:34.500\nFor example, you might test if a toy car needs new batteries by trying to turn it on.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:38.500\nIf it doesn't work, the test tells you it probably needs new batteries.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:43.000\nSo, a test helps us understand something better by giving us information.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:49.000\nTo sum it up, a test is a simple procedure we use to collect information and find something out.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:52.500\nIt's all about learning and understanding!\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:56.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
