    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.000\nA test is basically a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cookie is baked enough, so you test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:27.100\nIf it comes out clean, the cookie is done! In general, a test helps us determine if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:38.500\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. Or, a taste test helps you decide which ice cream flavor you like best.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:52.600\nSo, tests come in many forms, but they all share the same purpose: to evaluate or assess something. They help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n00:52.600 --> 01:01.200\nIn short, a test is a way of checking something to see if it meets a need, a requirement, or a standard.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:09.200\nI hope this helps you understand the basic idea of what a test is. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
