    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_052010.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.500\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:27.200\nThink of it like this: you want to see if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:37.800\nBasically, a test helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:50.400\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, your teacher might give you a quiz to see if you understand the material.\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:02.800\nSo, tests can be about anything!\nFrom checking if a lightbulb works, to seeing if a bridge is safe, to even finding out what kind of ice cream you like best.\n\n01:02.800 --> 01:09.300\nThey all involve checking something.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:15.400\nTo sum it up, a test is simply a way to check if something works, meets expectations, or is in a certain condition.\n\n01:15.400 --> 01:19.300\nHopefully, that clears things up.\n\n01:19.300 --> 01:25.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
