    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_052050.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.200\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:23.100\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:28.300\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.000\nYou could poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:39.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. See?\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:50.500\nAnother example: A doctor might do a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:54.100\nSo, a test is simply a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:57.700\nIt can be used to check anything, from a cake to your health to your knowledge. It helps us understand more about the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
