    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_053357.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, it\u2019s a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:28.100\nFor example, you might take a spelling test to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:35.100\nOr, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:40.100\nSee? It\u2019s about gathering information.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:45.100\nTests can be written, spoken, or even hands-on.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:53.900\nImagine baking a cake. You taste it to test if it needs more sugar. Or, you might test the temperature of bathwater to make sure it\u2019s not too hot.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:03.800\nSee how tests are a part of everyday life? So, to recap: A test is a method for gathering information or evaluating something.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:07.400\nIt helps us understand and learn.\n\n01:07.400 --> 01:09.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4d0a581f-a4d2-4d05-9f90-0394a0b26a70": {
    "id": "4d0a581f-a4d2-4d05-9f90-0394a0b26a70",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:16:45.493421",
