    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_053453.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_053453.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This VTT file does not perfectly align with the audio.  It is a rough approximation.\nNOTE Due to the nature of the prompt, the subtitles are not as useful as they would normally be.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us see if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe by cooking it to see if it tastes good. Or, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:35.100\nTests can be about anything! For example, your teacher gives you a test in class to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:44.400\nA scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better. Even playing a video game can be seen as a test of your skills!\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:53.600\nSo, a test is basically just a way of gathering information and learning something new. It helps us understand things better.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:57.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f820d96b-4c20-4c69-8d3a-ea07e5eda9ba": {
    "id": "f820d96b-4c20-4c69-8d3a-ea07e5eda9ba",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:16:45.967168",
