    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_053537.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:19.100\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:25.500\nSo, how does it work? Well, you usually have a goal in mind.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:29.300\nMaybe you want to see if a lightbulb lights up.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:34.900\nThat's your goal. The test is flipping the switch!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:40.500\nIf the bulb lights up, the test passes. If it doesn\u2019t, it fails.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:46.100\nAnother example: You're baking a cake, and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:51.700\nThe test? Sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:57.300\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done! If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:01.000\nBasically, a test is a simple way to confirm something is the way you expect it to be. And that's it! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
