    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_053620.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:18.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:23.600\nThink of it like a detective gathering clues.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:33.300\nTests can be about anything. In school, you might take a test to see how well you understand a subject, like math or science.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:39.800\nBut tests aren't just for school! A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:49.400\nA chef might taste a dish to test its flavor. So, tests help us learn, diagnose, and improve things. They give us information we didn't have before.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:52.000\nIn a nutshell, a test is just a process for getting answers.\n```"
  },
