    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.600\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:24.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:30.300\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:38.500\nYou screw it in, flip the switch, and see if it lights up.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:46.700\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\nA driving test shows if you can safely operate a car.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:52.100\nEven a simple taste test tells you if you like a new flavor.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:55.800\nSo, a test is just a method of gathering information to make a judgment.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:04.500\nThey come in many forms, but the basic idea is always the same: to assess something.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:08.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
