    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_055512.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.100\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in general, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might take a bite \u2013 that's a test to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:31.100\nOr, imagine you\u2019re building with blocks. You try to stack them high to test if your tower is strong enough to stand.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:41.400\nTests help us find problems and fix them. Software developers, for example, write tests to make sure their apps don't crash.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:53.200\nScientists use tests to see if their experiments work. So, whether it's cake, blocks, or code, tests help us learn and improve.\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:59.200\nIn short, a test is a way of checking if something does what it should.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:01.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
