    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.400 --> 00:02.100\nToday we're going to talk about something super important:\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:02.600\na test.\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:04.700\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we basically mean a way to find out how much you know about something,\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:06.400\nor how well something works.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:07.500\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb is good.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:08.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:09.100\nSo, a test is really just a way to get information.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:12.500\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:16.000\nOr, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:17.300\nSee?\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:18.000\nDifferent situations, same idea.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.300\nAnother example could be testing a new toy to see if it's durable and safe to play with.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:23.400\nWe're using the test to learn something.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:27.900\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to gather information and find out about something.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:29.400\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:30.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
