    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:22.200\nIt's how we check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:37.000\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test! The lightbulb either lights up, passing the test, or it doesn't, failing the test.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:48.500\nAnother example is taking a quiz at school. It's a test to see how much you've learned about a subject.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:58.900\nSo, to recap, a test is a simple way to check if something is working or to find out information.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:02.500\nIt can be as simple as checking a lightbulb or as complex as a science experiment.\n```"
