    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.100\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.100 --> 00:06.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:12.100\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see how well something performs.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:17.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:21.300\nYou poke it with a toothpick, right? That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:26.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:31.000\nOr, imagine you're checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:35.500\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:38.500\nIf the light turns on, the bulb passes the test.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:43.700\nTests help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:53.400\nThey can be simple, like checking a cake, or more complex, but the basic idea is always the same: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
