    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:19.100\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:29.100\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. Think about it.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:38.200\nWhen you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:47.300\nOr when you flick a light switch, you're testing if the light bulb works.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:56.800\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:02.400\nThey aren't scary, just a way to check understanding.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:08.000\nFor example, a simple multiple-choice quiz is a test.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:13.600\nSo is a science experiment to see if a plant grows in sunlight.\n\n01:13.600 --> 01:20.700\nSee? Tests are all around us, helping us learn and discover new things.\n\n01:20.700 --> 01:27.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for finding something out, whether it's about cooking, science, or what you learned in class.\n\n01:27.800 --> 01:34.200\nIt helps us explore and understand the world better.\n\n01:34.200 --> 01:41.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
