    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:13.000\nWhat is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:18.600\nIt's like asking a question and then seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:24.400\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:30.200\nThink about it. When you bake a cake, you might taste it to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:36.000\nThat's a test! Or, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken, you might try turning it on.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:46.900\nThat's another test. Tests can be more formal too, like a quiz at school to see how well you understand a topic, or a doctor checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:58.400\nThe goal is always the same: to get information and learn something new. So, a test is just a way of gathering information to answer a question.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:03.500\nIt can be something simple or something complex, but it always helps us learn and understand the world around us better.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:07.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
