    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_063453.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like asking a question and then seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:35.500\nThe main idea is to check if something works, or if it's the way it's supposed to be.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:42.700\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:49.900\nOr, you might take a test in school to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:49.900 --> 01:04.500\nAnother example could be testing a new lightbulb to see if it lights up. If it does, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, the lightbulb probably needs fixing.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:13.100\nBasically, a test helps us understand things better by checking them.\n\n01:13.100 --> 01:21.400\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something, like your health, your knowledge, or even a lightbulb.\n\n01:21.400 --> 01:29.000\nIt helps us see if things are working correctly or if they need some attention.\n\n01:29.000 --> 01:34.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
