    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T06:36:46.066303",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_063645.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_063645.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:30.000\nThe lightbulb turning on is a test that it's good. Another example could be checking if your cookies taste good.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:34.300\nYou bake them, then you taste one! That's a test.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:46.100\nIn science and math, tests help us prove if our ideas are correct. We run experiments, collect data, and then analyze the results.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:55.300\nIf the results match what we expected, then our idea passes the test. Tests help us learn and improve things all around us.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:06.200\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is true or working as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
