    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.900\nNot the kind you cram for, but the kind you use to check if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like this: a test is just a way to see if something passes or fails.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:33.200\nIt's a simple question with a yes or no answer.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:38.800\nFor example, if you bake a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:44.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! It's done.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:52.500\nOr, if you're checking if a lightbulb works, you flip the switch. If it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:53.700\nIf not, well, it fails.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:59.800\nSo, a test is simply a way to confirm if something is working correctly.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.700\nIt's all about checking, confirming, and making sure things are behaving as expected.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:06.200\nPretty straightforward, right?\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:08.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
