    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:06.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:12.100\nnot the kind you stress about in school, but tests as a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:18.100\nThink of it like this: you want to bake a cake, but how do you know if it's done?\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:20.200\nYou test it!\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:23.600\nA test is simply a way to see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:29.200\nMaybe you poke the cake with a toothpick, and if it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:32.800\nAnother example?\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:36.400\nImagine you're buying a new toy.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:40.700\nYou might press all the buttons to make sure they work.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:42.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:45.800\nYou're checking if the toy functions as it should.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:51.800\nSo, a test is just a simple way to check if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:55.500\nIt helps us catch problems early and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
