    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_064509.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nThink of a test as simply a way to find out something.\nIt\u2019s like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:23.900\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like it.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:35.700\nOr when you flip a light switch, you\u2019re testing to see if the light bulb works.\nScientists use tests, or experiments, to learn about the world.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:45.400\nThey ask a question, design a test to answer it, and then look at the results.\nLet's say you want to know if a plant needs sunlight.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:55.100\nYou could put one plant in the sun and another in the dark, then watch to see which one grows better.\nThat's a simple test!\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:02.100\nSo, a test is just a process for getting information.\nWe ask a question, do something to find the answer, and then see what happens.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:08.300\nTests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:08.300 --> 01:11.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
