    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_065058.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:22.200\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:28.200\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:33.100\nYou screw it in, flip the switch, and see if it lights up. That's a test!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:37.500\nOr imagine baking a cake.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:41.900\nYou taste it to see if it's sweet enough. That\u2019s another kind of test.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:46.300\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:51.200\nIn school, you might take a quiz to see how well you understood a lesson.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:54.900\nDoctors use tests to check your health.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:04.600\nEngineers test bridges to make sure they're safe.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:06.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out something about something.\n\n01:06.800 --> 01:14.700\nIt helps us understand if something is working as expected, or if something needs to be improved.\n\n01:14.700 --> 01:19.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0064c10a-81f6-49a9-b5b9-a15f40debfca": {
    "id": "0064c10a-81f6-49a9-b5b9-a15f40debfca",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:17:45.091128",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T06:51:40.096312",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_065139.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_065139.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.600\nWell, simply put, a test is just a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:20.500\nIt could be anything! You can test a new recipe to see if it tastes good, or a doctor might run tests to check your health.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:30.400\nBasically, you're trying to answer a question. Let's say you want to know if a toy car will go faster down a ramp if you make the ramp steeper.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:37.700\nYou could test that by making ramps of different heights and seeing which one makes the car go the fastest.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:45.900\nOr, imagine you\u2019re testing a new type of glue to see if it's strong enough to hold two pieces of wood together.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:55.400\nYou'd glue them and then try to pull them apart! So, a test is all about asking a question and then doing something to find the answer.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:02.200\nIt's how we learn and discover new things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
