    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_065443.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but often with a specific question in mind.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:29.600\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it! For example, when you try a new recipe, you're essentially testing it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:37.600\nOr, when you click a link online, your computer is running a quick test to make sure the website is safe.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:49.800\nTests can be written, like a school exam, or practical, like checking if a light bulb works. The important thing is that a test gives us information.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:61.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method for gathering information and answering a question. It helps us learn and make informed decisions.\n\n00:61.800 --> 00:64.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
