    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.600\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school quizzes. A test is really just a way to check something and see if it works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:28.100\nThink about it like this: you might test a new recipe by making it and tasting it. Or, you might test a toy to see if it's strong enough for kids to play with.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:36.400\nIt's all about trying something out to learn more about it. So, let's say you want to see if your plant needs water.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:44.700\nYou can test it by sticking your finger in the soil. If the soil feels dry, then it probably needs watering.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:46.900\nSee? A simple test!\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:55.700\nIn short, a test is a way to examine something and find out if it's working correctly or to learn more about it.\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:04.300\nIt\u2019s a way of getting information through observation or experimentation. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
