    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_072719.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.600\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:18.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:27.100\nIt's like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer, we're looking for evidence to prove something.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:35.100\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:43.100\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:46.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:55.700\nThese are all tests.\nSo, a test can be anything from a quiz in school, to checking the temperature of your bathwater.\nIt's a procedure that helps us learn more and make decisions based on the results.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:58.400\nIn short, a test is a way to gather information and see if something is true.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
