    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_073113.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.300\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:7.500\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:10.000\nIt's like an experiment or a check-up.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:18.600\nWe use tests all the time, in lots of different ways. Think about it: when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:21.000\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, you're testing your balance.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:28.100\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand the material. They can be written exams, quizzes, or even projects.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:31.000\nThe idea is to see what you've learned.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:39.200\nSo, a test is basically a method to gather information and see where we stand. Whether it's baking, biking, or learning, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:42.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
