    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_073154.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a really important concept: the test.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.600\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working like it's supposed to. It's like when you bake a cake \u2013 you might stick a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:27.200\nThat's a test! In general, a test is just a procedure designed to see if something meets certain requirements or expectations.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:40.000\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health. Or, when you\u2019re learning to ride a bike, falling is kind of a test to see if you\u2019ve got the balance thing down yet!\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:47.900\nSo, tests help us understand if things are working correctly, from baking cakes to checking your health.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:57.200\nThey give us information and help us improve. Remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:00.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
