    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_073241.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:04.100\nToday we're going to talk about something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.100 --> 00:06.800\nNow, you might think of a test as something you take in school,\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:08.400\nand that's definitely one kind of test.\n\n00:08.400 --> 00:12.400\nBut in general, a test is just a way of finding out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:17.600\nIt's a procedure designed to check, examine, or evaluate something.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:20.600\nThink of it like this: You want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:21.900\nSo, you test them!\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:24.600\nYou might poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:28.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test result \u2013 the cookies are ready!\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:31.300\nOr maybe you want to know if your new toy works.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:34.500\nYou put batteries in it and turn it on.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:36.700\nIf it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:37.700\nIt works!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:40.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:44.900\nIt helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:46.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
