    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_073908.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:18.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: you\u2019re testing to see if the lightbulb in your lamp works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:31.000\nIf the light comes on, the test passed! Tests are everywhere. A doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:44.500\nA chef tastes their soup to test if it needs more salt. In school, you take tests to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:50.000\nSo, just remember, a test is a way of finding out if something is right, working, or true.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:53.700\nIt helps us make sure things are as they should be. That's the basics of testing! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2a6f5e39-0fc7-49a1-a068-e1446004b9c1": {
    "id": "2a6f5e39-0fc7-49a1-a068-e1446004b9c1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:18:24.284412",
