    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_074036.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:24.300\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see how well something works or if something is true.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:32.100\nThink of it like this: You want to know if your cake is done baking. You use a toothpick to test it!\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:39.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test. Or, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:46.900\nYou test your balance and coordination. Each wobble and successful moment is a mini-test.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:57.600\nTests are used in all sorts of things, from checking if a lightbulb works to seeing how well you understand a new topic in school.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.500\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:03.000\nSo, a test is basically just a way of checking things out.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
