    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_074210.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.800\nNow, a test, simply put, is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:25.200\nIt helps us check if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:35.700\nThink of it like this: you take a spelling test in school to see if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:42.100\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:48.500\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:52.300\nIf it does, the bulb passes the test! If it doesn't, well, it fails.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:02.000\nAnother example? Imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:07.500\nSo, tests are basically just ways of finding out information by checking something.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:13.400\nThey help us understand things better and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:13.400 --> 01:18.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
