    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_075104.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. It's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like this: you might test if a light bulb works by screwing it into a lamp. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:34.200\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. The test checks if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.200\nOr, maybe you bake a cake and taste it. That's a test to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:53.300\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly. From simple light bulbs to complex recipes, tests are all around us.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:00.460\nThey give us information and help us make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
