    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:23.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you understand something or if something is working correctly.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:34.100\nFor example, your teacher might give you a math test to see if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:39.200\nOr, a doctor might give you a blood test to check if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:44.000\nSee? Different kinds of tests for different reasons.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:50.600\nAnother example: You could test if a lightbulb works by plugging it in. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:53.900\nIf it doesn't, well, it failed the test.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out if something is true, working, or understood.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.100\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are in order. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
