    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_080035.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it's true.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if your cake is baked, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:31.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. Another example is a spelling test in school.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:37.900\nIt checks how well you know your spelling words. Tests aren't just for school or baking, though.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:45.600\nScientists use tests to prove their theories. Doctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:57.800\nSo, a test is really just a way to get information and make sure things are as they should be. To recap, a test helps us check something to see if it\u2019s working or true.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:05.100\nWe use them all the time, in all sorts of ways! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
