    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_080255.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:01.900 --> 00:04.900\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:07.700\nIt's like asking a question, but often with a specific goal in mind.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:14.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\nThe test?\nSticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:17.500\nIf it comes out clean, the test says it's ready!\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:22.700\nOr imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is working.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:24.900\nDoes it light up?\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:29.100\nTests help us confirm things, identify problems, or just gather information.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:35.700\nSo, remember, a test is a simple process to get an answer.\nIt can be anything from baking a cake to checking a lightbulb.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:39.000\nThe important thing is that it helps you learn something new.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:42.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
