    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:06.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:7.400\nThink of it like a question you're asking,\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:9.000\nand the answer helps you learn more.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:11.500\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:15.700\nImagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done inside.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:20.500\nOr, think about checking the water in a pool before you swim.\nThat's a test to make sure it's safe!\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:25.700\nEven when you try a new flavor of ice cream, that's a little test to see if you like it.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:32.900\nBasically, a test helps you understand something better, whether it's a cake, water, or even your own taste buds.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:36.800\nThey give you information to make decisions.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:41.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:43.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
