    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_080726.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a really important concept: the test.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:15.700\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:39.900\nIt could be anything from a quiz in school to checking if a lightbulb works.\nBasically, we design a test to give us information.\nWe set up a situation, observe what happens, and then use that information to draw a conclusion.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:51.500\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:51.500 --> 01:02.800\nOr, if you're learning a new language, a test could be trying to have a simple conversation.\n\n01:02.800 --> 01:06.500\nSo, remember, a test is a way to gather information and answer a question.\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make decisions.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
