    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_080831.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:30.600\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:39.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is likely done.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:40.900\nOr, if you're trying to fix a broken light,\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:42.500\nyou might test if it works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:44.100\nOn? Great!\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:44.800\nOff?\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:45.700\nNeeds more work.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:53.300\nSo, a test is really just a way to find out information.\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:59.000\nRemember, tests are all about checking and verifying.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
