    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_082210.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:21.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you might test if your shoes fit before buying them.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:31.800\nOr a baker might test the oven temperature before baking a cake.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:40.400\nIn science, a test, also called an experiment, helps us figure things out.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:45.400\nWe change something and then see what happens.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:54.200\nFor example, if you want to know if plants need sunlight, you could put one plant in the sun and another in the dark.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:59.200\nThen, you watch to see which one grows better. That's a test!\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:04.200\nTests are all about asking questions and finding answers.\n\n01:04.200 --> 01:15.000\nBy carefully observing and comparing, we can learn so much about the world around us.\n\n01:15.000 --> 01:24.000\nRemember, a test is just a way of checking something to see what happens.\n\n01:24.000 --> 01:25.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
