    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.100\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.100 --> 00:05.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:07.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:12.200\nThink of it like an experiment or a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:16.800\nBasically, you perform an action, and then you observe the result.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:18.700\nThat result tells you something.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:25.400\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:33.000\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works, you screw it in and flip the switch. If the light comes on, the test shows the bulb is good.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:41.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information by doing something and seeing what happens. It's all about observation and learning.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:44.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
