    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_083558.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.400\nThink of a test as a way to check how well you know something. It's like a measuring stick for your knowledge.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:27.800\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes. Sometimes it's a written quiz, other times it might be a practical demonstration, like showing you know how to bake a cake or build a tower.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:41.000\nThe main goal is always the same: to see what you've learned.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.300\nFor example, if you're learning your ABCs, a test might be pointing to a letter and saying its name.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:57.300\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, the test is whether you can balance and pedal without falling.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:03.700\nSo, remember, a test is simply a tool to see how much you've learned and where you might need a little more practice. It's a chance to show off your skills!\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:08.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "506b2e02-af90-4afc-8eea-5a3039d373de": {
    "id": "506b2e02-af90-4afc-8eea-5a3039d373de",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:19:09.494334",
