    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_083641.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.900\nNow, a test is basically a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:35.300\nIn general, a test involves giving something a specific input, and then seeing if it produces the expected output.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:44.100\nFor example, if you give a plant water, you expect it to grow. That's a simple test of whether the plant is healthy.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:52.900\nOr, if you press the brake pedal in your car, you expect the car to slow down. That's a test of your brakes.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:00.400\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a method for determining if something functions correctly by checking its output after a specific input.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:02.900\nKeep that in mind, and you'll be testing things all the time!\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:07.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
