    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_083727.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.900\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:25.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand something better.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:35.900\nThink of it like this: You have a plant, and you want to know if it needs water. You might poke the soil \u2013 that's a little test!\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:44.900\nIf the soil is dry, the test tells you the plant probably needs water.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:53.900\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken. You try turning it on.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:03.700\nIf it doesn't light up, that's another test, and the result is that the bulb is likely faulty.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:13.500\nTests can be anything from simple observations to complex experiments, but the goal is always the same: to get information.\n\n01:13.500 --> 01:25.100\nSo remember, a test is just a way of asking a question and getting an answer to help us learn. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
