    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_084935.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:20.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:27.700\nIt's like checking if your bike tires have enough air. You might squeeze them \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:35.900\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you stick a toothpick in it to see if it comes out clean. That's another test!\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:47.800\nThese small actions help you know if your tires are good to go, or if your cake is ready to eat. So, a test helps us confirm something, big or small.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:55.500\nWe use tests every day without even realizing it. Remember, it's all about checking and understanding.\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:59.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
