    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_085110.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE: The following subtitles are timed based on the script and animation timings provided, but may need adjustment to precisely match the recorded narration.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's baked all the way through by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:28.300\nIf it comes out clean, then the cake passes the test! Another example is testing a lightbulb.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.100\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:39.900\nIf it doesn\u2019t, well, it failed! Tests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb works,\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:52.400\nor more complicated, like taking a school exam. But the basic idea is always the same: to evaluate something and see if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:59.200\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check if something is working or performing as expected.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:05.600\nIt helps us know if things are good to go!\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:08.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
