    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_085831.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.700\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:28.700\nThe test? You screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. If the light comes on, the test is passed!\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:35.000\nOr, imagine you want to know if your cookies are done baking. You poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:41.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test telling you they're ready.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:57.200\nSo, a test is really just a procedure to check if something is true or false, working or not working, or meeting a certain standard. It helps us make decisions and learn new things.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:00.800\nIn short, a test helps you find out something specific.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:04.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
