    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_090937.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests!\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.500\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like a little experiment. We're trying to see if we get the expected result.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:38.600\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might do a \"taste test\" to see if it's sweet enough. Or, if you're building a tower of blocks, you might \"test\" its stability by gently pushing it to see if it falls.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:43.700\nThese are all mini-tests! They help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:51.300\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in. You're testing to see if it lights up.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:59.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to see if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:01.800\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:05.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "7fdefbef-911f-493c-8463-6c1fbaf6642e": {
    "id": "7fdefbef-911f-493c-8463-6c1fbaf6642e",
