    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_091027.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:21.500\nThink about it like this: you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:26.100\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:34.500\nSee? Different scenarios, same idea. Each test has a specific purpose and helps us understand something better.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:44.000\nFor example, baking a cake is a test! You're testing your recipe and your baking skills to see if you get a delicious result.\n\n00:44.000 --> 01:01.200\nOr, trying a new route to work is a test to see if it saves you time. So, remember: a test is just a way of gathering information, whether it's about your knowledge, your health, or even the best way to bake a cake!\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:07.500\nIt\u2019s all about learning and understanding. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
