    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_091546.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:64.5\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.800\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:24.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:33.000\nThink of it like this: imagine you're learning to bake cookies.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:39.600\nA test would be like someone asking you questions about the recipe or watching you bake to see if you follow the steps correctly.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:46.200\nTests can come in many forms.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:51.800\nThey might be written, like a quiz with multiple-choice questions.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:56.600\nOr they could be practical, like showing you can ride a bike after taking lessons.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:00.600\nThe point is to measure your understanding or skill.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:08.000\nFor instance, a spelling test checks your knowledge of words, while a driving test checks your ability to operate a car safely.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:16.100\nSo, tests help us understand what we've learned and where we might need more practice.\n\n01:16.100 --> 01:21.000\nThey're a tool for learning and growth, not something to be afraid of.\n\n01:21.000 --> 01:24.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
