    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_092125.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:05.200\nToday we're tackling something super fundamental:\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:07.500\nthe concept of a \"test.\"\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out, to check if something is true, or to see how well something works.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:19.600\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:20.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:26.800\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, you might test your balance by slowly letting go of the grown-up holding on.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:27.900\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:34.100\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes still fit.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:37.600\nThe main goal is always the same: to get information.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:42.100\nSo, a test is just a way of asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
