    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:05.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:06.100\nspecifically,\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:06.900\nwhat a test\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:08.600\nactually is.\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:11.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:12.500\nout information about\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:13.100\nsomething.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:15.300\nThink of it like asking a question\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:16.300\nand getting an answer.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:20.000\nIt could be a math test in school, where\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:22.100\nyou're testing your knowledge of numbers.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:25.200\nOr, it could be a taste test, where\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:26.900\nyou're figuring out which flavor\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:27.900\nyou like best.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:32.000\nEven checking if a lightbulb works is a\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:33.100\ntype of test!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:34.500\nYou're testing if it lights up.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:38.400\nSo, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:41.200\nThey give us data, which we can then use\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:43.800\nto make decisions or learn something new.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:46.900\nRemember, a test is just a method for\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:48.700\ngathering information.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:54.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
