    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_092815.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:17.100\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:29.300\nThink of it as a question you ask to see if you get the answer you expect.\nWe use tests all the time, without even realizing it.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:40.500\nFor example, when you flip a light switch, you're testing if the light will turn on.\nOr, when you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:51.700\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\nThey can be quizzes, exams, or even just asking you questions in class.\nThe goal is to see if you understand the material.\n\n00:51.700 --> 01:01.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a way of checking something, whether it's a lightbulb, a recipe, or your knowledge.\nIt helps us understand if things are working as expected.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e84c59b0-7893-4f85-8b72-902de6e4cb30": {
