    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_092903.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:16.400\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:27.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand something better.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:33.000\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:38.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:43.600\nOr, you might test a toy to see if it works by pressing the button.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:49.300\nIf it lights up and makes noise, the test passed!\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:55.300\nTests can be big, like a school exam, or small, like checking if your shoes are tied.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:59.300\nBasically, anything you do to check something or find something out can be considered a test.\n```"
  },
