    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_093348.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:04.800\nToday we're diving into the basics of something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:07.200\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean a school exam.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:13.100\nA test is really just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:17.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:22.700\nYour test is screwing it into a lamp and flipping the switch.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:25.300\nDoes it light up?\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:26.700\nThat's the result of your test!\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:31.000\nAnother example: you want to know if your soup needs more salt.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:32.500\nYou taste it.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:36.100\nTasting it is your test, and whether it's salty enough is the result.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:40.800\nSo, a test is simply a procedure you follow to get information.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:44.400\nYou do something, you observe the outcome, and that outcome tells you something.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:45.800\nSimple as that!\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:56.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
