    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_093858.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.400\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like this: you have a new lightbulb.\nTo test if it works, you screw it in and flip the switch.\nDoes it light up?\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:27.500\nThat's your test!\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:33.900\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou can test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:36.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, your cake is ready.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:42.300\nThat's another test!\nSo, a test is simply a procedure you use to see if something meets your expectations.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:48.700\nWhether it\u2019s a lightbulb, a cake, or even checking if your shoes fit, you're performing a test!\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:54.300\nIn short, tests help us confirm things are working correctly.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
