    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_094544.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests! You've probably taken a bunch of them in school,\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:06.000\nbut what exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:09.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to see what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:13.500\nIt helps measure your understanding of a topic or your skill in a certain area.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:18.400\nThink of it like this: if you're learning to ride a bike, a test might be trying to ride without holding on.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:23.700\nOr if you're learning to bake cookies, the test could be seeing if you can follow the recipe and make them taste good!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:27.600\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. Some are written, like quizzes,\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:32.000\nand others are hands-on, like a science experiment. The important thing is that they give us\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:33.900\ninformation about what we've learned.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:37.200\nSo, a test is just a way to check your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:39.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
