    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_094939.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:19.000\nToday we're diving into something super fundamental: the test.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:25.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to see if something works as expected.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:34.100\nThink of it as a way to check if your answer is right, or if a product does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:40.100\nIt can be as simple as tasting a cookie to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:42.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:49.400\nOr, imagine you're building a tower of blocks. Each time you add a block and it doesn't fall, you've passed a little test.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:53.500\nAnother example is a spelling test in school.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:55.800\nIt checks if you've learned how to spell the words correctly.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:02.400\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working properly.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:06.600\nThey're everywhere, from baking to building to learning.\n\n01:06.600 --> 01:08.600\nThey give us important information.\n\n01:08.600 --> 01:14.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
