    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_100111.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nNow, a test, in the simplest terms, is just a way to see what you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:19.200\nThink of it like checking your understanding.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:27.200\nThere are all sorts of tests. You might take a quiz in school to see how well you learned the material, or a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:38.500\nA chef might even taste food to test if it has enough seasoning! For example, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down a few times is like a test.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:44.700\nIt shows you what not to do and helps you get better.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:58.000\nOr, imagine baking a cake. Tasting it afterwards is a test to see if it tastes good and if you followed the recipe correctly.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:06.100\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a method for checking knowledge, ability, or quality.\n\n01:06.100 --> 01:09.000\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:11.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
