    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_100812.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:07.700\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:14.000\nThink of it like this: you\u2019ve been learning about, say, different types of fruits.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.600\nA test would then ask you questions to see if you can identify a banana, an apple, or an orange.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:28.200\nTests aren't just about getting a grade, though. They're a useful tool to see what you've learned well and what you might need to study more.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:37.100\nFor example, if you ace the questions about apples but struggle with oranges, you know to focus on learning more about oranges.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:43.900\nSo, tests help you understand where you are in your learning journey.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:50.200\nThey highlight your strengths and show you where you can improve.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:54.300\nRemember, everyone learns at their own pace!\n\n00:54.300 --> 00:57.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
