    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_101718.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it like this: you get a new toy, and you press the button to see if it makes the right sound.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:28.600\nThat's a test! In school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:41.100\nA cooking recipe is tested by following it and seeing if you get a delicious meal. Even scientists use tests, like experiments, to prove their ideas.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:52.300\nSo, tests are all around us, making sure things are doing what they're supposed to do. Essentially, a test is a way to confirm something.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:59.400\nIt can be big or small, simple or complicated. It's all about finding out if something works or if something is true.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
