    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_101852.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, and what they actually are.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like an experiment, but with a specific goal in mind. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:36.500\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're kind of testing it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:45.200\nOr, if you press a button on a remote control and the TV turns on, that's a test to see if the remote is working.\n\n00:45.200 --> 01:00.200\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit. The important thing is, you're trying to learn something new or confirm something you already suspect.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:03.100\nSo, a test helps you check if something is true, works correctly, or meets your expectations.\n01:03.100 --> 01:03.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
