    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_102432.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something super fundamental: a test!\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:15.100\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:20.300\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:27.300\nThink about it. A taste test tells you if you like a new flavor.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:34.400\nA spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:41.500\nEven checking if your light switch works is a kind of test \u2013 does it turn on the light? Yes or no?\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:53.600\nSo, a test helps us learn, understand, or confirm something. We ask a question, perform an action, and then observe the result.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:00.500\nThat result gives us information. In short, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:02.200\nIt's a way of gathering information and making a judgment.\n01:02.200 --> 01:07.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
