    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_102825.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like an experiment or a check-up. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:36.700\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like the taste. Or, when a doctor checks your temperature, they're running a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:48.100\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:56.200\nSo, whether it's trying a new food, getting a medical check-up, or taking an exam, a test helps us gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:56.200 --> 00:57.000\nRemember, tests are just tools to help us understand the world better.\n```"
  },
  "7f2c16f5-d1a9-4b80-aee1-dad011a6db30": {
    "id": "7f2c16f5-d1a9-4b80-aee1-dad011a6db30",
