    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_103206.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It could be about you, or about anything really.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like a question with a specific way to answer it.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:30.200\nSo, for example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:37.100\nYou screw it in, flip the switch, and see if it lights up! That's the test.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:43.900\nThe result tells you if the bulb is good or bad.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:50.700\nAnother example is a spelling test in school. You're given words and asked to spell them correctly.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:56.700\nThe test shows how well you know your spelling.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.300\nBasically, tests help us understand things better by giving us a clear way to measure or check them.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.700\nThey help us make decisions and learn new things.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:07.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
