    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_103640.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we're talking about testing things to see if they work.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:22.700\nBasically, a test is a way to check if something meets a certain standard or does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:36.200\nThink about it like this: if you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\nOr, if you're building a toy car, you might push it to see if the wheels turn properly.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:45.800\nThese are simple examples, but the idea is the same.\nTests help us make sure things are working correctly before we rely on them.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:57.000\nThey\u2019re a way of finding out if something passes or fails.\nSo, to recap, a test is a method to evaluate something against a set of criteria.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
