    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:28.900\nIt could be checking if you understand a lesson, like the tests you take in school.\nOr, it could be checking if something works correctly, like testing a new toy or a computer program.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:37.400\nThe main idea is to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:41.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you can spell words correctly.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:45.000\nA taste test checks if food tastes good.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:56.500\nSee? Different situations, same idea. So, to recap: A test is a way to check something against a standard. It helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working properly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
