    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_103824.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:09.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:11.000\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:12.500\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:18.000\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.000\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, the test is whether you can balance without falling.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:31.000\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your coffee is hot enough before you drink it.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:37.000\nBasically, anything that helps you gather information and make a decision can be considered a test.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to discover something.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:44.000\nIt helps us answer questions and learn more.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:47.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
