    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_104230.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_104230.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer, or trying something out to see if it works.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:26.500\nTests help us learn and improve. For example, when you take a spelling test at school, it shows you which words you need to practice.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:35.500\nOr, when a baker tries a new recipe, they're testing if it tastes good!\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:53.900\nAnother example is a product test. Companies test their products to make sure they are safe and work properly before they sell them.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:01.800\nSo, tests can be big or small, simple or complex, but they all have the same goal: to gather information and see if something is true or correct. In short, a test is just a way of finding out something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b6777f97-afea-4090-abf5-621dc2f34119": {
    "id": "b6777f97-afea-4090-abf5-621dc2f34119",
