    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:20:44.761170",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T10:43:23.753568",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_104323.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_104323.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.300\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but a test is really just a way of finding out something.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:28.200\nIt's a process to check if something is working correctly, or to see how good something is. Think about it like this: you might test a new recipe by making a small batch to see if you like the taste.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:38.400\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Tests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:49.800\nOr they can be more complicated, like testing a new car to see how safe it is. The main idea is always the same: to get some information.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:60.600\nSo, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something and give us useful information about it. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
