    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_104430.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:07.300\nSimply put, it's a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:12.600\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:16.400\nWe use tests every day without even realizing it.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:21.800\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're essentially testing it.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:26.700\nYou're finding out if you like the taste and if it works.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:31.100\nOr, if your car won't start, you might test the battery to see if that's the problem.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:36.700\nTests can be simple, like pressing a button to see if a light turns on.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:40.300\nOr they can be more complex, like a medical exam.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:45.500\nThe important thing is that they give us information we didn't have before.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:51.100\nSo, a test helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:55.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "8d227274-c7e3-4d23-98d3-c57eaa4f00dc": {
