    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_104533.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something.\nThink of it like asking a question, but often with a more structured approach.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:28.300\nThe goal of a test is to see if something is working as it should, or to measure its qualities.\nFor example, you might take a spelling test to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.500\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:43.900\nLet's say you're baking a cake.\nYou might test it with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:49.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, it means the cake is ready!\nThat\u2019s a simple test.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:55.100\nSo, tests help us understand and evaluate things.\nThey give us information.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:01.700\nTo sum it up, tests are a way to learn about something by asking a question or measuring a quality.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:05.300\nThey help us make informed decisions.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
