    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:19.000\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:29.700\nThat toothpick is performing a test! In science and other fields, tests are used to gather information and see if something is true or false.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:38.800\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health, or an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it's strong enough.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:51.100\nThese tests help us learn and make better decisions. So, tests are all about checking things, whether it's a cake or a bridge, to see how they measure up.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:54.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
