    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_104929.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:19.400\nIt could be about anything! Think of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:28.700\nWe use tests all the time. For example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:37.700\nThat toothpick is your test! Or, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken, you might try turning it on.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:42.800\nThat's a test too! So, a test helps us gather information.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:50.300\nWe perform an action and observe the result. That result then tells us something about the thing we're testing.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:58.700\nIn short, a test is a question, an action, and an answer all rolled into one. Pretty simple, right?\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
