    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:14.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like an experiment or a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:32.800\nThe main idea behind a test is to give you information.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:44.900\nIt could be used to see how well you understand a subject, like in a school exam.\nOr, it could check if a new medicine is safe and effective.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:47.500\nIt helps us make decisions based on evidence.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:50.100\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you have a vitamin deficiency.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:52.700\nOr, you might test your new phone charger to make sure it's actually charging your phone.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:53.800\nSee?\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:54.600\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:10.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to gather information and learn something new.\nThey can be simple or complex, but they all have the same goal: to help us understand the world around us better.\n\n01:10.200 --> 01:13.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
