    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_110106.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.900\nHey there! Welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:01.900 --> 00:08.800\nA test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:16.600\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:21.900\nIn everyday life, we use tests all the time.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:30.300\nImagine you're baking a cake. You taste the batter to see if it's sweet enough. That's a test!\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:38.700\nOr, when you try on a new pair of shoes to see if they fit, that's another kind of test.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:48.300\nIn school, tests help your teachers see how much you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:57.100\nFor example, a multiple-choice quiz tests your knowledge of facts.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:06.800\nA science experiment tests a hypothesis.\n\n01:06.800 --> 01:18.600\nThey all help us understand things better. So, remember, a test is a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:18.600 --> 01:23.600\nIt helps us check if something is working, fits right, or if we've understood a lesson.\n\n01:23.600 --> 01:28.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
