    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_110423.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.500\nWell, a test is simply a way to find out more about something.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:20.600\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:27.600\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:36.700\nThink about baking a cake. You might taste a little bit of the batter before putting it in the oven. That's a test to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:45.900\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again. That's a test to see if it fixes the problem.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:55.100\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like checking if the water in the shower is warm enough.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:03.900\nThe main thing is, they help us understand something better.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:12.500\nThey give us information to make decisions or solve problems.\n\n01:12.500 --> 01:18.600\nSo, a test is just a way of gathering information.\n\n01:18.600 --> 01:23.400\nIt could be anything from tasting batter to taking an exam.\n\n01:23.400 --> 01:29.000\nThey all help us learn!\n\n01:29.000 --> 01:34.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
