    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:14.500\nToday we're diving into the concept of a test.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:28.200\nIt could be about you, like a quiz in school, or about something else entirely, like testing if a new toy is safe.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:34.000\nThe basic idea is that you present a question or a situation, and then you see what happens or what the answer is.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:39.800\nThat result tells you something.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:45.600\nThink about it like this: a taste test!\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:53.100\nYou try a new flavor of ice cream, and that's the test.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:58.900\nYour reaction \u2013 whether you like it or not \u2013 is the result.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:06.400\nOr, imagine testing a light bulb.\n\n01:06.400 --> 01:12.800\nYou screw it in, and if it lights up, the test passes.\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:16.400\nIf it doesn't, well, it failed.\n\n01:16.400 --> 01:23.900\nSo, a test is just a process to get information.\n\n01:23.900 --> 01:29.800\nYou ask a question, you perform an action, and you observe the outcome.\n\n01:29.800 --> 01:33.900\nThat outcome is the information you were looking for.\n\n01:33.900 --> 01:37.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c093cad5-12d0-418e-af66-9869f46fc716": {
    "id": "c093cad5-12d0-418e-af66-9869f46fc716",
