    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_111118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:05.200\nWhat are they and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:07.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:10.600\nIt helps us measure knowledge, skills, or even abilities.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:14.500\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you test it with a toothpick.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:17.300\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:20.300\nSimilarly, in school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:23.700\nThey can be quizzes, exams, or even projects.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:27.600\nFor example, a spelling test checks your spelling skills, and a math test checks your understanding of numbers.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:31.700\nThe results of these tests give valuable insights.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:36.000\nThey show what you understand well and where you might need some extra help.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:38.900\nSo remember, tests aren't scary.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:42.200\nThey're just tools to help you learn and grow.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:44.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
