    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_113125.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:25.700\nTests help us understand how well something works, or if something is true. For example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:31.000\nOr, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt. See? It's all about gathering information.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:36.800\nAnother good example is a baking test. Before baking a whole batch of cookies, you might bake just one, to test the recipe.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:48.400\nThen, you can adjust the ingredients to make the cookies perfect! So, tests help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:62.000\nIn short, a test is a way to get information and check if something is right or working as expected.\n\n00:62.000 --> 00:65.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
