    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:19.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information or evaluate something. Think of it like checking if something works, or seeing how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:29.600\nIt can be anything from a simple yes or no question, like \"Is the light on?\", to a more complex exam in school.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:40.100\nThe goal is always the same: to get a result or measure something. For example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:46.100\nOr, you might take a quiz online to test your knowledge of a certain subject. See? Tests are all around us!\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:58.400\nSo, to recap, a test is a process used to evaluate or measure something, providing us with information and results.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:09.400\nWhether it's a school exam or a simple observation, tests help us understand the world better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
