    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.999\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.699\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: you might test a new toy to make sure it doesn't break easily. Or, your teacher might give you a quiz to test what you've learned in class.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:33.499\nSo, a test basically compares what you expect to happen with what actually happens. If they match, great!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:43.999\nIf not, then you know something needs to be fixed or learned better. For example, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:57.299\nOr, you might try a practice question before a big exam to test your knowledge. In short, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:02.399\nThey're a valuable tool in all sorts of situations.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:05.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
