    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_114139.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like checking if your shoes fit before you go for a run.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:37.600\nBasically, you try something out and see what happens. If you want to know if a cake is done, you can test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:45.500\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready! Or, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you can screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:55.400\nIf it lights up, it passes the test. So, tests help us learn and make sure things are working correctly. They can be big or small, but the main idea is always the same: try it out and see what you get!\n\n00:55.400 --> 00:58.900\nThat's the basics of testing. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
