    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_115045.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:18.300\nA test is basically a way to see what you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works \u2013 the test is seeing if it lights up!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:39.600\nThere are all kinds of tests, from the quizzes you take in school to the taste tests where people try new foods.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:47.400\nThe goal is always the same: to get information.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:51.300\nFor example, a math test shows how well you understand numbers, and a spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:51.300 --> 01:01.400\nImagine you're learning to ride a bike. A test could be simply seeing if you can ride across the driveway without falling.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:04.900\nIf you can, great! You passed that test.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:12.200\nIf not, you know you need more practice.\n\n01:12.200 --> 01:18.500\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and understand things better.\n\n01:18.500 --> 01:21.900\nIn short, a test is a way to gather information and check our understanding.\n\n01:21.900 --> 01:24.400\nPretty simple, right?\n\n01:24.400 --> 01:27.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
