    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_115331.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something super fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you've probably taken tons of tests in school, but at its core, a test is simply a way to gather information.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:28.400\nIt's a structured process designed to see what you know, or how well something works.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:33.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:41.100\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. See? It's about checking something.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:48.600\nTests can be quizzes, experiments, or even just observations.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:59.200\nThe important thing is they give us useful information to make decisions. So, a test helps us find out if something is true, correct, or effective.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:03.600\nTo recap: a test is a method for gathering information,\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:07.000\nlike checking for health or tasting food.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:10.700\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:10.700 --> 01:14.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "910c9ce0-57a0-4c0b-8c4e-c70414e89d7e": {
