    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_115419.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:19.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It's a process or procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:39.400\nOr, a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a fever. In school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:46.500\nThey can be quizzes, exams, or even projects. For example, a spelling test checks your spelling skills.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:56.700\nA math test checks your math skills. And a science experiment can be a test to see if a hypothesis is correct.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:04.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us learn and understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
