    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_115522.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.300\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:21.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:25.900\nThat's a test! You're testing to see if the batter comes out clean.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:34.500\nIn general, tests are used to see if something works, if it's correct, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:44.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health. Or, a car company might test a new car to see if it's safe.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:54.800\nSo, tests help us understand things better by giving us information. They're used everywhere, from baking a cake to building a rocket!\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:58.800\nKnowing how to test things helps us make sure things are working the way they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
