    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_120854.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:16.300\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:20.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:26.100\nYou stick a toothpick in it, right?\nThat's a test!\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:31.800\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\nThe cake passes the test, it's ready.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:36.900\nThe toothpick comes out gooey?\nThe cake fails, and needs more time in the oven.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:42.000\nTests are everywhere!\nYour doctor gives you tests to check your health.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:52.100\nYou take tests in school to show what you've learned.\nEven trying a new recipe is a kind of test to see if you like it.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:55.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:59.100\nand see if it meets a certain standard or gives you the information you need.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
