    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_121117.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.700\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:01.700 --> 00:02.600\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:05.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:08.900\nIt could be checking if you understand a topic, like after you've studied for school.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:13.400\nOr it could be checking if something works, like making sure a new phone can make calls.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:15.800\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:18.600\nYou use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:21.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:22.500\nAnother example?\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.800\nA doctor gives you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:32.000\nSo, a test is a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:37.700\nWe use tests all the time to learn, to improve, and to make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:38.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
