    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_121352.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.600\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:13.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:23.100\nIt's a process of asking a question or presenting a challenge, and then observing the response.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:33.200\nThink about it like this: A spelling test checks your knowledge of how to spell words.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:36.400\nA taste test tells you which food you prefer.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:43.400\nEven a medical test, like checking your temperature, is a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:45.900\nTests help us learn and understand.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:50.300\nThey can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like trying a new recipe.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:53.000\nThe key is that a test gives us information that we didn't have before.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:54.300\nSo, tests are all about learning and discovery!\n```"
  },
  "33e7a2ef-214f-4288-b11d-4019001b9230": {
    "id": "33e7a2ef-214f-4288-b11d-4019001b9230",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:21:48.589021",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T12:15:22.066222",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_121521.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_121521.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 and no, not the kind you take in school!\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:22.000\nIn the world of software, a test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you want to make sure it rolls.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:31.300\nYou test it by pushing it. If it rolls, great! The test passes.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:45.500\nIn software, we do the same thing but with code. We write little instructions to check if our program is doing what we expect.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:52.600\nFor example, if we have a function that's supposed to add two numbers, a test would check if it actually gives us the correct sum.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:59.700\nAnother example could be testing that a button on a website does what it's supposed to when you click it.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:09.400\nSo, tests are like little detectives, making sure everything is running smoothly and helping us catch mistakes early on. They're a super important part of building reliable software. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "848acf44-b1fb-4a3d-86f6-a2342bda41bf": {
    "id": "848acf44-b1fb-4a3d-86f6-a2342bda41bf",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:21:49.202002",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T12:16:12.011109",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_121611.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_121611.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey there, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:19.300\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process that helps us measure or evaluate.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:28.700\nThink about it like this: a baking test! You bake a cake, then you taste it. That taste test tells you if you need more sugar or maybe less baking time next time.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:38.100\nOr, imagine a spelling test at school. It shows you which words you've mastered and which ones you still need to practice.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:46.900\nTests aren't just for baking or school, though. They're used in all sorts of ways to check things, learn things, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:57.600\nBasically, a test gives you information. So, remember, a test is a method for gathering information and evaluating something.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:07.300\nIt can be as simple as tasting a cake or as complex as a scientific experiment.\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:09.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
