    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_121829.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:17.600\nA test, at its core, is simply a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:27.100\nThat's a test! Basically, a test helps you figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:35.600\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:46.300\nTests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb turns on. Or they can be more complex, like testing a new car's safety features.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:55.400\nNo matter the complexity, the goal is always the same: to get information and make sure things are as they should be.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:03.400\nSo remember, a test is just a way to check something! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
