    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:23.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking. You could guess, or you could test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:29.100\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready! Tests aren't just for cookies, though.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:36.100\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Teachers use tests to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:47.500\nEven engineers test bridges to make sure they're strong enough. So, a test is basically a question, or a process, designed to give you an answer.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:55.500\nIt helps you understand something better. To recap, a test helps us learn something by providing evidence.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:02.900\nIt can be used in all sorts of situations. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
