    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_122205.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school,\nand that's true!\nBut in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:31.500\nBasically, it's like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer.\nThink about it like this: you bake a cake, and then you taste it \u2013\nthat's a test to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:39.400\nOr, you build a tower with blocks, and then you gently push it \u2013\nthat's a test to see if it's stable.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:47.800\nAnother example is checking if your flashlight works by pressing the button.\nThe light turning on is a successful test!\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:57.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to see if something does what it's supposed to do.\nIt helps us learn and improve things.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:04.900\nIn short, tests are checks, plain and simple.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
