    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_122248.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:07.100\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:11.200\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:15.700\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:20.400\nThink about checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:23.200\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:26.800\nIf the light comes on, the bulb passes the test!\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:32.000\nOr imagine baking a cake. You taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:36.200\nThat taste test tells you if you need more sugar.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:43.000\nSo, tests help us check if something is working, if something is correct, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:45.700\nThey give us information to make decisions.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:52.000\nTo recap, a test is a method for gathering information about something.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:57.600\nWe use them to check things and make sure they're working as expected.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
