    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_123338.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.400\nWell, simply put, a test is a way of finding something out.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:27.600\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand something better.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like this:\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:34.400\na teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:37.800\nOr, maybe you try out a new recipe to test if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:41.200\nSee? It\u2019s about gathering information!\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:48.600\nFor example, you might test if a toy car needs new batteries by turning it on.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.200\nIf it moves slowly, the test tells you the batteries are probably weak.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:58.600\nAnother example is testing the temperature of bathwater to make sure it's not too hot.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:04.600\nSo, a test is just a way to check things out and learn something new.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:07.600\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:09.800\nThat's testing in a nutshell!\n\n01:09.800 --> 01:13.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
