    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:21.900\nIt's a process designed to gather information. Think about it like this: you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:28.900\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. Both are examples of tests!\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:43.400\nWe use tests all the time to evaluate, measure, and understand things. They can be formal, like a big exam, or informal, like quickly checking if your shoes are tied.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:55.300\nThe key is that they help us learn and improve. So, remember, a test is a structured way to gather information and see what we know or what needs to be adjusted.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
