    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:27.300\nThat's a test! Basically, a test helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain expectations.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:35.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words. A taste test checks if food tastes good.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:48.000\nSo, tests can come in all shapes and sizes. They can be simple, like checking if your shoes are tied, or more complex, like a medical test.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:57.800\nThe important thing is that they give us information. In short, a test is a process designed to evaluate performance or quality.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
