    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_125148.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_125148.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:18.400\nA test is simply a way to find something out or see if something is working correctly.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:28.200\nThat's a test! Tests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:44.600\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy. And even engineers use tests to make sure bridges are strong enough to hold cars.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:54.800\nSo, a math quiz is a test, a blood pressure check is a test, and even shaking a package to see if something's broken is a kind of test!\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:05.500\nBasically, anything you do to check or evaluate something is a test. In short, a test helps us gather information and make decisions. It\u2019s a way to see if something meets a certain standard or answers a question.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
