    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_125327.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:06.500\nYou've probably taken a bunch of them in school,\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:08.500\nbut what is a test, really?\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:13.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about someone or something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:16.800\nIt helps us measure knowledge, skills, or even just a quality.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done,\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:24.800\nyou can test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:28.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.400\nOr, if you want to know if someone knows their alphabet, you give them a test asking them to write it out.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:38.800\nTests can be written, spoken, or even involve doing something.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:42.400\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:47.300\nSo, a test is a simple way to learn about what we're examining.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:52.500\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we need to work on.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
