    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:07.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:20.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done,\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:24.200\nso you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:24.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:29.200\nThe toothpick comes out clean, the test is passed.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:31.300\nIt comes out gooey, the test failed.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:32.300\nSee?\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:32.700\nEasy!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:38.300\nIn school, tests help your teachers see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:42.800\nA math test checks if you know your numbers,\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:45.000\na spelling test checks your words.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:51.900\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to find out something, whether it's about a cake or about what you've learned.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:53.900\nIt gives you information.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:00.400\nTo recap, tests help us check things, like cake or knowledge, and they give us useful information.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
