    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we\u2019re going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.300\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, we\u2019re talking about a way to check if something is working correctly or meeting certain standards.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: a test is a way to ask a question and get an answer that helps you understand something better.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:39.600\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch. The question is: \"Does the light bulb work?\" And the answer tells you whether it passes the test or not.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:51.900\nAnother test might be tasting food to see if it's salty enough.\nSo, to summarize, a test is simply a way to check something to see if it works or meets a requirement.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:59.400\nIt helps us understand if things are behaving as expected.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
