    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_130424.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_130424.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:18.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer, we're using a process to get a result.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:26.600\nFor example, a simple test could be like checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:32.200\nOr, imagine a taste test. You try two different cookies and decide which one you like better. That's a test too!\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:38.100\nTests help us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:49.500\nThey can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like deciding which route to take to work.\n\n00:49.500 --> 01:00.600\nIn both cases, we're using a test to gather information.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:04.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out through a process. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
