    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_130656.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:11.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You plug it in, and that's your test!\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.000\nIf it lights up, great! It passed the test.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.300\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs, though. They're used everywhere!\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:31.100\nYour doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:35.700\nOr, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:43.100\nSo, a test is really just a method to gather information. We perform an action, then observe the result.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:52.000\nThat result tells us something about whatever we're testing. Whether it's a lightbulb, your health, or your knowledge, tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.100\nIn short, a test is a way to find out information by doing something and seeing what happens.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
