    "subtitles": "**\n```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:24.800\nIt helps us see if something is true, or working correctly, or even just what you know about a subject.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:35.200\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:45.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a sign the cake is ready! Or, a doctor might give you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:58.800\nSo, tests are all about getting information. They can be simple, like checking if the lights turn on when you flip a switch, or more complex, like a big exam at school.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.400\nThe key is, a test helps us understand something better.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:05.800\nIn short, a test is a process that provides information to determine if something is working, true, or correct.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
