    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:16.500\nToday we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:22.800\nThink of a test as simply a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:29.100\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:39.200\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:47.300\nImagine you're baking a cake.\nYou test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:56.900\nOr, think about checking if a lightbulb works.\nYou flip the switch, and if the light comes on, the bulb passes the test.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:05.200\nSo, a test is really just a simple way to verify something.\nIt helps us make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:13.600\nIn short, a test confirms if a condition is true or false.\n\n01:13.600 --> 01:17.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
