    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_134957.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.900\nNow, a test is basically a way to check if something works, or if you know something.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:18.700\nThink of it like a little experiment or a quiz.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:25.800\nWe use tests all the time! A doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.800\nA baker might taste their cake batter to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:34.000\nAnd, of course, you take tests in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:36.200\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works by plugging it in.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:38.000\nDoes it light up?\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:38.800\nYes?\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:39.500\nThen the test passed!\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:41.900\nOr, if you're learning your ABCs, a test might be writing them down to see if you remember them all.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:49.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information or check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:51.500\nIt helps us learn and improve! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
