    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_140509.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.900\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something really fundamental: the concept of a test.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:15.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it as an investigation.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:26.900\nYou ask a question, and the test helps you find the answer. For example, a spelling test helps your teacher see if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:36.300\nOr, a taste test can help you decide which flavor of ice cream you like best. It's all about gathering information.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:49.400\nTests can come in many forms. There are written tests, physical tests, even tests you do without realizing it, like trying a new route to school to see if it's faster.\n\n00:49.400 --> 01:02.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a method for discovering something, whether it's your spelling skills, your favorite ice cream, or the fastest way to get somewhere.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:07.500\nIt's a simple way to learn! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
