    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_141557.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.000\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like a detective looking for clues! Basically, you perform an action, and then you look at the result to see if it matches what you expected.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:34.200\nFor example, if you want to test if a light bulb works, you screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:42.600\nOr, if you want to test if water boils at 100 degrees Celsius, you heat it up and check the temperature.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:53.600\nTests are super important in all sorts of things, from checking if your new phone is working properly, to scientists testing new medicines.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:07.200\nThey help us make sure things are safe and reliable. So, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working or true by performing an action and seeing the result.\n\n01:07.200 --> 01:10.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5d22d331-3034-424f-b3c7-b58ecf97c199": {
