    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.800\nNow, a test, at its most basic, is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it as a question we're asking and then trying to get the answer.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:34.500\nTests help us see if something is working, if something is true, or if someone understands something.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:44.400\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:53.900\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to see if you understood the lesson.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:03.400\nEven checking if the light switch works is a kind of test!\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:18.300\nYou flip the switch, and if the light comes on, the test passed. So, tests are all about gathering information and figuring things out.\n\n01:18.300 --> 01:26.600\nThey can be big and complicated, or small and simple, but they all serve the same purpose: to learn something new.\n\n01:26.600 --> 01:35.400\nRemember, tests are just a tool to help us understand the world better.\n\n01:35.400 --> 01:37.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
