    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_142640.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let\u2019s talk about tests.\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.500\nIn everyday life, we use the word test to describe trying something out\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:08.500\nto see how well it works.\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:12.300\nIn the world of software and engineering, it's pretty much the same idea.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:15.500\nA test is a way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:19.800\nThink of it like baking a cake.\nYou taste it to test if it\u2019s sweet enough, right?\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:23.700\nWell, software tests do something similar, but for code.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:27.800\nWe write specific instructions to check if the code is giving us the results we want.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:34.300\nFor example, if you're building a calculator, you might test if 2 plus 2 equals 4.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:40.700\nOr, if you're building a website, you might test if a button takes you to the right page when you click it.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:53.000\nSo, basically, testing is all about making sure things work as they should, catching errors early, and making sure the final product is reliable.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:57.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
