    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:23:15.883176",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T14:28:27.450673",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_142827.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_142827.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're getting proof.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:26.700\nIt helps you understand if something is working the way it should. For example, if you're baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:31.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:40.400\nOr, if you're learning a new language, a quiz is a test to see how well you're understanding the vocabulary.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:50.200\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly. They give us valuable information.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:56.500\nThey're all about gathering evidence. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
