    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_143721.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there, and welcome!\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:16.300\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\nNow, you might be thinking of school exams, but a test, in general, is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: you have a brand new lightbulb, and you want to see if it lights up.\nThe test is simply screwing it into a lamp and flipping the switch.\nIf it lights up, it passes the test! If not, well, it failed.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:33.200\nAnother example: imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:40.000\nYou use a toothpick to poke the center.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done.\nIf it's still gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:46.800\nSo, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:56.000\nIt helps us understand if things are doing what they should.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:02.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
