    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_144057.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:19.000\nNow, a test, in the simplest terms, is a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.600\nThink of it like a question, but instead of just asking, we use a process to get an answer.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:35.400\nWe use tests all the time! Imagine you're baking a cake. You taste the batter \u2013 that's a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:48.700\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if your toy car needs new batteries, you try to turn it on. If it doesn't work, that's a test telling you the batteries are probably dead.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:59.600\nTests can be formal, like exams at school, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit. The key is that they help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.100\nSo, remember, a test is a process that gives us an answer to a question.\n```"
  },
