    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:23:24.217616",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T14:41:51.682025",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_144151.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_144151.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:33.600\nWe use tests all the time! Like when you try a new recipe to see if it tastes good, that's a test!\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:47.800\nOr when you push a button to see if a light turns on, that's a test too! Even playing a game to see if you can win is a kind of test.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:57.400\nSo, a test can be anything from a school exam to a simple experiment. The main idea is to check if something is working correctly, if something is true, or just to learn more about it.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:05.000\nBasically, a test is an action performed to evaluate something, revealing information about its properties or abilities. Remember, tests help us learn and improve things.\n```"
  },
  "b7089f71-756a-463f-847e-ffeb756d342f": {
    "id": "b7089f71-756a-463f-847e-ffeb756d342f",
    "topic": "Test",
