    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_144253.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.250 --> 00:05.390\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.390 --> 00:17.250\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.250 --> 00:25.040\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works. You screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:25.040 --> 00:32.830\nThe lightbulb either turns on, passing the test, or it doesn't, failing the test.\n\n00:32.830 --> 00:36.630\nAnother example? Checking if your shoes fit!\n\n00:36.630 --> 00:49.110\nYou put them on and walk around. If they\u2019re comfortable, they pass the \"fit test.\" So, a test is just a simple way to see if something meets a certain requirement.\n\n00:49.110 --> 01:00.410\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it. Basically, you have something to check, you perform an action, and then you see the result.\n\n01:00.410 --> 01:05.900\nPretty simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
