    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_145617.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.500\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to see how well you know something,\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:07.100\nor how well something works.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:11.000\nThink of it like this: you take a spelling test in school to see how many words you can spell correctly.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:12.800\nThat's testing your knowledge.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:17.000\nOr, imagine you're building a bridge out of blocks.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:19.800\nYou might gently push on it to test its strength.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:21.300\nThat's testing how well something works.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:26.600\nTests can be written, like quizzes, or practical, like trying something out.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:30.900\nFor example, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:34.900\nA doctor might check your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:36.400\nIt's all about finding out information.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:41.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to evaluate knowledge or performance.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:46.700\nIt helps us understand something better by gathering information.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:48.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
