    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_150139.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:14.500\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: a test is just a simple question you ask to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:29.000\nIf you do, great! The thing you tested is working. If not, then there's probably a problem.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:38.100\nFor example, you might test if a light bulb works by flipping the switch. If the light comes on, the test passes!\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:45.200\nOr, you might test if your shoes fit by trying them on. If they're comfortable, the test passes.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:55.600\nSo, a test is simply a way to confirm something is doing what it's supposed to. It's all about asking a question and seeing if the answer is right.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
