    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_150541.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:65.8\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something super important: the test.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.100\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information or check something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer. Tests can be anything from a simple yes or no question, to a more complex series of problems.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:37.100\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:48.400\nEven baking a cake is kind of a test; you're testing the recipe to see if it works! The main goal of a test is to give us information and help us improve.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:62.100\nWhether it's checking your knowledge, your health, or even a recipe, tests are all about learning. So next time you hear the word test, remember it's just a way to learn and discover!\n\n00:62.100 --> 00:65.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
