    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:15.900\nWhat is a test, exactly? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:22.700\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we know something.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:34.100\nThink of it like this: you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:41.000\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your overall health.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:47.900\nEssentially, a test is a question or a series of questions designed to give us information.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:54.800\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might taste a little bit of the batter. That's a test!\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:02.000\nYou're testing to see if it tastes good. Another example is checking if a lightbulb works before you install it.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:09.100\nYou're testing to make sure it lights up! So, tests help us confirm things, learn new things, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:19.800\nThey're a fundamental part of learning and problem-solving. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
