    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_151719.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:21.600\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:25.300\nIt could be a written exam at school, sure,\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:30.900\nbut it's also how you check if your cake is done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.600\nThe toothpick comes out clean? That's your test!\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:44.300\nOr imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:52.000\nYou screw it in. If it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, the lightbulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:52.000 --> 01:07.100\nSo, a test is really just a simple procedure to see if something is true, working, or correct. Whether it's checking your spelling or seeing if your computer program runs, you're running a test.\n\n01:07.100 --> 01:15.900\nIn short, tests help us learn and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:15.900 --> 01:25.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
