    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey there, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the concept of a test.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:16.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like an experiment, but often a bit more structured.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:31.200\nIt helps us measure or evaluate things. For example, a spelling test helps us see how well you know your words.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:38.000\nOr, imagine baking a cake. You taste it \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:44.400\nYou're checking if the cake is sweet enough, cooked right, and tastes good.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:50.800\nAnother example? Checking if your phone's battery is charged. That's a quick test to see if it's ready to use.\n\n00:50.800 --> 01:01.900\nTests are everywhere, helping us learn and make decisions. So, a test is basically a way to gather information and see where things stand. It helps us understand something better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
