    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T15:31:01.076261",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_153100.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_153100.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:15.900\nIn simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:35.300\nWe use tests all the time! For example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a teacher might give you a quiz to check if you understand the material.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:40.500\nThe test, in both cases, is helping us understand something we didn't know before.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:45.900\nLet's say you want to know if a cake is done. You can insert a toothpick.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:51.300\nIf it comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is ready! See? Simple!\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:57.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for getting information.\n\n00:57.000 --> 00:59.400\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n```"
  },
  "c628c279-b297-4376-96ed-590ffbbd86cb": {
    "id": "c628c279-b297-4376-96ed-590ffbbd86cb",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
