    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_153145.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:13.100\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works like it should. It's basically asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:18.600\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake. The test is tasting it!\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:22.200\nDoes it taste good? Is it cooked all the way through?\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:31.400\nThat taste, that\u2019s your answer. Or, if you're building with blocks, the test is whether your tower stands up straight.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:40.400\nIf it falls over, that's a failed test. So, a test is simply a way to confirm if something meets a certain requirement.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:48.800\nWe use tests every day, even without realizing it. It\u2019s all about checking if something is working as expected.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:52.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a4fe4175-4915-4619-a6b4-4578e605dcf8": {
    "id": "a4fe4175-4915-4619-a6b4-4578e605dcf8",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
