    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_153228.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something, or someone, to see how well they perform or how well they know something.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:26.100\nThink about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test! It checks what you've learned in class.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:32.800\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to see if it's sweet enough. That's a test too! You're testing the flavor.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:43.900\nOther examples include a doctor using tests to see if you're healthy, or even testing the water in a pool to make sure it's clean.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:55.400\nSo, tests help us understand things better by giving us information. They help us evaluate, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:04.300\nIn short, a test is a way to examine something to learn more about it. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a1712bfd-1bf7-4fac-a199-3062c37ef656": {
    "id": "a1712bfd-1bf7-4fac-a199-3062c37ef656",
