    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_153316.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something, right?\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:23.500\nIt could be about you, or something you're working on. Think of it like a little experiment.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:33.400\nBasically, you set up a situation, and then you observe what happens.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:43.000\nFor example, a taste test tells you which food someone prefers. Or, a spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:53.500\nAnother example is testing a toy to see if it's safe for kids. You check for small parts that could be swallowed, or sharp edges.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:59.200\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and checking things out.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:02.400\nTo sum it up, a test is a controlled way of finding something out.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:04.500\nYou create the situation, and then you see the results.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:05.800\nSimple as that!\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:08.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
