    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_153400.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:17.300\nA test, simply put, is a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:26.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, they're ready!\nIn school, tests are used to see how well you understand what you've been learning.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:35.500\nLike a math test checks if you can do addition and subtraction.\nOr a spelling test sees if you know how to write words correctly.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:41.800\nAnother example is testing a new toy to see if it works like it should.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:45.700\nDoes it light up?\nDoes it make noise?\nThese are all little tests.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:54.700\nSo, tests help us understand if something is working, if something is ready, or if we understand something.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:01.400\nThey are a way to get information and learn.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
