    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:03.700\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:03.700 --> 00:05.100\nNow, what is a test?\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:07.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:10.100\nIt's like asking a question and then checking the answer.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:12.900\nThink of it this way: you might give your dog a treat if they sit.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:13.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:16.600\nYou're testing if they know how to sit.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:22.000\nOr, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test to see if the cake is done.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.300\nTests help us learn and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:31.200\nThey can be simple, like checking if your shoes are tied, or more complicated, like a doctor running blood work.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:36.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:39.500\nIt\u2019s about learning and confirming something.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:41.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
