    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_153535.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:18.500\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see what something is made of.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:26.300\nThink about it like this: If you want to know if a lightbulb works, you put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:32.800\nOr, if you want to know if a cake is done, you poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, it passes the test!\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:44.300\nTests help us make sure things are safe, reliable, and doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:51.600\nFrom checking your tire pressure to making sure a bridge is sturdy, tests are happening all around us.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:59.700\nSo, a test is simply a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
