    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_153830.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:12.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something, to see if it's working correctly, or to measure its quality.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:18.400\nThink of it like this: you get a new toy, and you play with it to test if it actually works.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:26.000\nIn other areas, a test could be a quiz at school to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:29.500\nOr maybe a doctor runs a test to check your health.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:33.600\nThe idea is always the same: to get information and learn something.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:41.000\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:45.800\nOr an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it's strong enough.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:50.300\nSo, tests are all about checking things!\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:56.400\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:56.400 --> 00:59.000\nAnd that\u2019s the basics of what a test is!\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:04.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
