    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_154038.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something called a test.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. The main idea behind a test is to see if something meets a certain standard or if it works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:31.700\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb turns on. You flip the switch \u2013 that's the test.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:40.200\nIf the bulb lights up, it passes the test! Another example could be tasting a cake to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:53.900\nYour taste buds are doing the test, and if you think it's sweet, it passes. So, to recap, a test is just a procedure to check if something works or meets a requirement.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:59.900\nIt's all about finding things out! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
