    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_154117.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer. It\u2019s how we measure or check things.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.200\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:32.400\nYou turn it on. If it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:45.600\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. You're being tested on your knowledge of spelling.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:52.900\nSo, to recap, a test is just a method to check something, whether it's if a lightbulb works or how well you know your spelling words. It helps us understand and measure things around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
