    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_154633.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you taste it to see if it's good. That's a test!\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:28.300\nEssentially, a test is just a way to evaluate something.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:38.200\nIt could be anything! Maybe you're testing if a new light bulb turns on, or if your bike brakes work properly.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:48.200\nYou're just checking to see if it passes or fails. For example, you could test if a toy car rolls downhill.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:52.200\nYou let it go, and if it rolls, it passes the test!\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:58.100\nIf it doesn't, it fails. Simple, right?\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:09.000\nSo, tests are all about checking how things work, making sure they do what we expect them to. They help us find problems and make things better.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:12.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
