    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_155523.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.600\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:28.400\nIt helps measure your understanding. Think of it like this: If you're learning to ride a bike, a test might be seeing if you can balance without holding on for a few seconds.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:39.300\nOr, if you're learning your ABCs, a test could be pointing to the right letter when someone says it.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:44.300\nTests aren't just about grades in school. They're used everywhere!\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:53.300\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. A chef might taste their food to test if it needs more seasoning.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:03.800\nSo, a test is just a tool to check knowledge or ability. They come in many different forms, but the goal is always the same: to measure something.\n```"
  },
