    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:07.500\nnot the kind you take in school, but the kind that helps us check\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.100\nif something works the way it's supposed to. Think of it like this:\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:16.100\nyou're baking a cake. A test is like tasting a little bit\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:19.200\nof the batter before you put it in the oven.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:21.800\nYou want to make sure it tastes good\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:24.200\nand has the right ingredients.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:28.300\nIn general, a test is a way to find out if something is working correctly.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:32.300\nMaybe you're testing a new lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:35.700\nOr maybe you're testing a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:41.300\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to check if something is doing what it\u2019s designed to do.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:47.500\nIt helps us catch problems early and make sure everything is working as expected.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:55.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
