    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_155821.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.900\nNow, a test might sound scary, but it's really just a way to see how much you've learned or how well something works.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:21.500\nThink of it like this: you take a quiz at school to see how well you understand the lesson.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:27.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.700\nThat taste is also a kind of test.\nBasically, a test gives you information.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:49.300\nIt helps you know where you're doing well and where you might need to focus more.\nSo, whether it's a pop quiz, a science experiment, or even just trying out a new recipe, remember that tests are there to help you learn and improve.\nThey give you feedback.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:56.600\nSo, in short: a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:07.700\nIt can be used to check your knowledge, how well something works, or even how good something tastes!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
