    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_160212.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:01.600 --> 00:02.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:05.700\nSimply put, it's a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:07.800\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:08.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:08.300 --> 00:10.100\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:13.300\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned in class.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:16.900\nIn the kitchen, you might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:21.000\nFor example, a math test shows if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.700\nOr, a simple test could be pressing a button to see if a toy makes a sound.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:27.500\nIf it does, the test passes!\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:30.200\nIf not, something might be wrong.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:33.000\nSo, a test is just a way to find out information.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.800\nIt helps us understand things better and see if they're working as expected.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:39.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
