    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_160639.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in the world of science and technology, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:29.200\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:38.000\nOr, if you're building a toy car, you might test it by pushing it across the floor to see if the wheels turn. That's another test.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:47.300\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we need to make some changes.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:58.800\nTests are super important for making things better and more reliable. So, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
