    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_161804.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey there, welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:20.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:31.400\nTests help us see if something works as expected, or if it meets certain standards. We use them all the time, in all sorts of areas.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:41.500\nFor example, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words. Or, a doctor might run tests to check your health.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:49.600\nEven checking if your car starts in the morning is a kind of test!\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:59.600\nBasically, a test gives us information. It helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.200\nSo remember, tests are all about checking things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
