    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_162023.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.800\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:05.300\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:8.200\nIt's a process, really, where we ask a question or present a challenge, and then observe the result.\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:16.000\nThink about it like this: a cookie taste test! You try the cookie \u2013 that's the challenge \u2013 and then you decide if it's delicious or not.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:17.300\nThat's the result!\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:21.700\nOr, consider a spelling test in school. The teacher gives you words to spell \u2013 the challenge \u2013 and your written answers show what you know.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:27.300\nTests aren't just in classrooms or kitchens, though. Scientists use tests to see if a new medicine works.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:30.300\nEngineers test bridges to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:38.300\nBasically, anytime you're trying to learn something or check if something works, you're probably using a test.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:43.500\nSo, a test is a method to gather information, whether it's about cookies, spelling, or something much bigger!\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:47.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
