    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like an experiment, but often with a specific goal in mind.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:32.600\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:42.900\nFor example, if you're baking a cake and you poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done, that's a test!\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:49.900\nThe toothpick is your tool and you're testing if the cake is cooked through.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:56.900\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out which light switch turns on the lamp.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:04.000\nYou flip each switch, one by one, to see which one works. That's another kind of test!\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:11.100\nSo, a test is a method for gathering information.\n\n01:11.100 --> 01:16.300\nIt can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:24.800\nThe main idea is that you're trying to answer a question or confirm something.\n\n01:24.800 --> 01:28.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
