  "b64ca7f4-32bd-44f3-a422-e2896a18057b": {
    "id": "b64ca7f4-32bd-44f3-a422-e2896a18057b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:08.693221",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T16:59:22.281930",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_165922.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_165922.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nHey there, welcome! Today we're diving into what a test actually is.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a method we use to gather information.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:20.100\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of your bath water to see if it's too hot or too cold.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:27.300\nOr a doctor might test your reflexes to check your nervous system.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:31.900\nAnother example is a taste test! You try a new flavor of ice cream to see if you like it.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:44.800\nSee? We test things all the time, often without even realizing it. So, a test is just a way to explore and learn about something by trying it out or observing it closely.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:52.600\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```\n\n**Explanation of Changes and Visuals:**\n\n*   **Images:** The code includes placeholders for images (`bath_water.png`, `doctor_reflexes.png`, `ice_cream.png`).  You MUST replace these with actual image files in the same directory as your Manim script or provide the correct path.  These images help to illustrate the examples given in the narration.\n*   **Rounded Rectangles:** Added RoundedRectangles behind the text for visual appeal and readability.\n*   **Colors:** Used the requested color palette (GOLD, BLUE\\_B, GREEN\\_B, TEAL\\_A, ORANGE, PINK).\n*   **Timing:**  The timing is now exactly as specified in the request, with the correct `self.wait()` values to hold each slide on screen for the full duration of its corresponding narration segment.\n*   **Font Sizes:** Used the specified font sizes for titles, headers, and body text.\n*   **Animations:** Made animations smooth and slow with `run_time` values between 1.4 and 2.0.\n*   **Structure:** Followed the requested structure (title, content sections with examples, summary, ending).\n*   **FadeOut:** Added FadeOut to clear the screen after each section to avoid visual clutter.\n*   **Image Placement:** I have used `.next_to()` to place the images under the text in the given scenes.\n*   **Subtitle:** Added subtitles for the video\n\n**To use this code:**\n\n1.  **Install Manim:**  Make sure you have Manim installed (`pip install manim`).\n2.  **Save the Code:** Save the code as a Python file (e.g., `test_explanation.py`).\n3.  **Place Images:** Put the image files (e.g., `bath_water.png`, `doctor_reflexes.png`, `ice_cream.png`) in the same directory as the Python file.  You can use any images you like, but make sure they're appropriate for the content.\n4.  **Render the Video:** Run Manim from the command line:\n    ```bash\n    manim -pql test_explanation.py TestExplanation\n    ```\n    This will render the video in low quality (`-ql`) and play it when finished (`-p`). You can use `-pqh` for high quality.\n5.  **Add Audio and Subtitles:** Use a video editor (like OpenShot, DaVinci Resolve, or Adobe Premiere Pro) to add the narration audio and the generated subtitles to the video."
  },
  "5477c4ac-4062-42d9-8ae4-8e582073a925": {
    "id": "5477c4ac-4062-42d9-8ae4-8e582073a925",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:09.578000",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:01:00.371620",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_170100.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_170100.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something, or to see how well something works.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:30.500\nThe main idea is to gather information. We use tests all the time!\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:37.500\nFor example, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:47.700\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt. Even playing a video game is a test of your skills!\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:58.400\nSo, let's say you're baking cookies. You might test the oven temperature to make sure it's right. Or, you might test one cookie before baking the whole batch to make sure the recipe is good.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:02.000\nIn short, a test is just a way to learn something by checking things out.\n```"
  },
  "646e7367-a880-4eb6-826a-f80ea3f6d75c": {
    "id": "646e7367-a880-4eb6-826a-f80ea3f6d75c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:10.159545",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:01:58.790036",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_170158.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_170158.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:26.000\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a test!\nOr maybe you're trying to figure out if your friend likes pizza.\nYou ask them!\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:31.400\nThat\u2019s also a test!\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:34.500\nIn science, tests can help prove or disprove a theory.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:43.700\nTests come in all shapes and sizes, from simple questions to complicated experiments.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:57.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information and see where things stand.\nIt helps us learn, improve, and understand the world around us.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "8477b07e-20d2-471c-9185-220a63061c28": {
    "id": "8477b07e-20d2-471c-9185-220a63061c28",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:10.769652",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:02:41.504837",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_170241.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_170241.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! \nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like an experiment or a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:32.300\nEssentially, you're trying to answer a question. \nFor example, a doctor might run a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:38.800\nOr, a teacher gives you a test in school to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:46.800\nLet's say you're baking a cake. \nYou might test the cake with a toothpick. \nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:55.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a process used to evaluate or determine something. \nIt helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:58.100\nIt's a fundamental tool used in many different areas of life.\n\n00:58.100 --> 00:58.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "65b46ae9-1237-42d6-b25f-acfaf888b0eb": {
    "id": "65b46ae9-1237-42d6-b25f-acfaf888b0eb",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:11.386258",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:03:34.324253",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_170334.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_170334.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.700\nThat's a test! You're checking if the light bulb can do its job.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:32.100\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:39.600\nTeachers use tests to see how well you understand a subject, like a quiz on what you learned in class.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:50.400\nSo, a test is just a way to find out if something is working correctly or if something is true. It's a simple check, and we use them all the time!\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:53.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "66b6d555-35c9-43e7-b86a-d4d0c37db3ca": {
    "id": "66b6d555-35c9-43e7-b86a-d4d0c37db3ca",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:12.023706",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:04:21.830271",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_170421.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_170421.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: You want to know if the cake is ready. You poke it with a fork, that's a test!\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:31.700\nIf the fork comes out clean, the cake passes the test, it's done! Or, maybe you're taking a quiz at school. That's a test too!\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:37.300\nIt helps your teacher see how well you understand the lesson.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:52.400\nTests can be big or small, like checking if your shoelaces are tied, or a really important exam. Basically, any time you're trying to figure something out by checking it, you're doing a test.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:59.900\nSo, a test is just a way to get information. It helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
