    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_171119.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it like an investigation.\nWe ask a question, and the test helps us find the answer.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:33.800\nThe important thing to remember is that a test should be fair and reliable.\nIt needs to accurately measure what it's supposed to measure.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:39.800\nFor example, a math test should test your math skills, not your reading comprehension.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:46.700\nImagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might test the oven temperature to make sure it's hot enough.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:53.600\nOr, if you're a doctor, you might run tests to figure out what's making a patient sick.\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:05.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a process for gathering information, and it\u2019s essential to ensure it's fair and accurate.\n\n01:05.100 --> 01:14.600\nUnderstanding the basics of what a test is will help you in all sorts of situations.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
