    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_172619.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:17.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:32.600\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. When you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good.\n00:32.600 --> 00:38.100\nOr when you press a button on a toy, you're testing if it makes a sound.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:47.600\nIn computers and science, tests are super important. They help us find mistakes and make sure everything is working correctly.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:55.100\nFor example, we might test a new app to see if it crashes, or test a medicine to see if it's safe.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:02.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. We use them to make sure things work, are safe, and do what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:05.800\nThanks for watching!\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "352dda00-7b42-4681-83ca-8986c4d78fc3": {
    "id": "352dda00-7b42-4681-83ca-8986c4d78fc3",
