    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_172953.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, what they are, and why they're important.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:21.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process or procedure used to determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in. That's a simple test!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:35.200\nAnother example is a recipe test. You follow the instructions and see if the cake turns out as expected.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:42.900\nOr, if you're building with LEGOs, you might test if your structure is strong enough to hold a certain weight.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:56.000\nSo, a test is all about gathering information and learning something new. It helps us confirm if things are working correctly and gives us the information needed to improve things.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
