  "b9317ef9-cbcf-4cdb-9292-34dd1683d301": {
    "id": "b9317ef9-cbcf-4cdb-9292-34dd1683d301",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:46.390122",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:53:28.819975",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_175328.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_175328.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nA test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're getting proof.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:25.400\nFor example, a taste test helps you find out which food tastes best. Or a spelling test shows you how well you know your words.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:35.200\nTests help us understand things better and learn new things. Imagine you have two plants, and you want to know which one grows faster.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:40.900\nYou could water them both the same and measure their growth over time. That's a test!\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:49.800\nYou're testing which plant is the faster grower. So, tests are all about gathering information in a structured way.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:58.900\nThey help us prove or disprove ideas and learn more about the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3539620d-8f22-422f-97f5-ac2b09ea34ca": {
    "id": "3539620d-8f22-422f-97f5-ac2b09ea34ca",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:25:46.888588",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T17:55:30.562787",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_175530.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_175530.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.700\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake. To test if it's done, you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:30.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test is successful! The cake is ready.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:37.100\nOr, imagine you're trying to start your car. You turn the key; that's a test!\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:43.700\nIf the engine starts, the test passes. If it doesn't, well, something's wrong.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:50.300\nSo, a test is simply a way to evaluate something, using a specific action or condition.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:55.100\nIt helps us understand if things are working as they should.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:01.100\nAnd that's tests in a nutshell! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
