    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_181125.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:03.900\nToday we're diving into something super important:\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:04.400\na test.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:04.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:07.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something,\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:09.700\nor how well you can do something.\n\n00:09.700 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:14.000\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:15.700\nIf it lights up, it passes.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:18.600\nTests can be written, like a quiz in school,\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:21.200\nor practical, like seeing if you can ride a bike.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:25.500\nA written test might ask you questions about animals, like \"What color is a polar bear?\".\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:29.000\nA practical test could be trying to bake a cake to see if you can follow a recipe.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:33.500\nSo, to recap, a test helps us measure knowledge or skills.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:37.000\nIt can be on paper, or it can involve doing something.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.400\nEither way, it\u2019s all about finding out what you know or can do.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:42.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "bc19e5b7-eda8-439e-a149-80fea069acda": {
    "id": "bc19e5b7-eda8-439e-a149-80fea069acda",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
