    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_181230.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but really, a test is just a way of finding something out.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:25.100\nIt's a process we use to check if something works, or if it's true.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:31.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your bike tire has enough air.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:37.900\nYou can test it by squeezing the tire. If it feels firm, it passes the test!\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:43.500\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:49.100\nYou can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:57.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test too! So, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it meets a certain requirement. It helps us make sure things are working the way they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
