    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:03.100 --> 00:04.400\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:07.700\nNow, a test isn't just something you take in school.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:14.800\nIn general, a test is simply a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:20.100\nThink of it like this: you might \"test\" the temperature of your bath water to see if it's just right.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:24.600\nOr, a chef might \"test\" the sauce to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:26.100\nIt\u2019s all about gathering information.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:30.600\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:37.300\nOr, a car mechanic might test your car's battery to see if it needs replacing.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:39.000\nSee?\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:40.900\nTests help us understand things better.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:44.800\nSo, remember, a test is a way to get information.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:49.300\nWe use them all the time to learn and make better decisions.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:51.000\nThat's the basics of a test!\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:52.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
