    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_182117.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.400 --> 00:07.500\nToday, we're going to explore what a test is,\nin the simplest way possible.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.200\nThink of a test as a way to check something.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:18.400\nIt's how we find out if something works, if something is true,\nor if something is good enough.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:23.200\nImagine baking a cake.\nYou take a bite, right?\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:25.800\nThat's a test!\nYou're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:32.500\nOr, think about checking if a light bulb works.\nYou flip the switch; that's a test to see if it lights up.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:39.500\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal,\nlike tasting that cake.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:44.500\nThe main idea is always the same: you're trying\nto gather information to make a decision.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:52.000\nSo, a test is just a way of checking something\nto see if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
