    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_182918.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.500\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in this case, we're talking about testing something to see if it works, or if it's true.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:27.900\nBasically, a test is a way to check if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:40.200\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:46.300\nOr, if you're checking if a light bulb works, you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:54.000\nIf it lights up, the test passes. Testing isn't just for cakes and light bulbs.\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:04.000\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are right, and engineers use them to make sure things are safe.\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:09.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something works the way it should.\n\n01:09.800 --> 01:14.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
