    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_183846.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: tests!\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:22.100\nNow, a test, in the simplest terms, is just a way to find out something. It's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true, works correctly, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:34.200\nThink about it like this: a recipe is a test. You follow the instructions, and the result tells you if the recipe works \u2013 hopefully, you get a delicious cake!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:39.000\nOr imagine a lightbulb. You plug it in; that's a test.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:41.800\nDoes it light up? Yes or no.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:51.800\nTests can be simple, like checking if a switch turns on a light, or more complex, like a doctor running blood work to check your health.\n\n00:51.800 --> 01:06.900\nThe key thing is that a test gives us information we didn't have before. So, to recap: a test is a process to gather information and determine if something meets a specific condition or standard.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:10.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
