    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_184242.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:19.600\nNow, a test is just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but instead of complicated lab equipment, you\u2019re usually just asking a question or trying something out.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:29.000\nThe main idea behind a test is to see how something responds under certain conditions.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:33.500\nFor example, a simple taste test!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:44.600\nYou try a new cookie to see if you like it. That\u2019s a test! Or, if you're playing a game and try a new strategy, that's testing if that strategy works.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:52.300\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. It tests your knowledge of how to spell words.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:03.400\nThe test result, your score, shows how well you did. So, remember, a test is really just a way to learn more and see how things work.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:07.000\nIt helps us understand what we know and what we still need to learn.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:10.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
