    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_184353.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. It could be anything from a school exam to see how much you've learned, to a taste test to see which cookie is the yummiest!\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:30.300\nEven checking if a light bulb works is a type of test. You're testing if it's functional.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:42.900\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. You poke it in, and if it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:49.700\nAnother test could be checking the weather forecast. You're testing what the weather will be like tomorrow.\n\n00:49.700 --> 01:00.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of getting information. It helps us learn, decide, and understand things better.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
