    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_184453.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.800\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, maybe in school. But what exactly is a test?\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:26.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, skills, or performance in a specific area.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:35.200\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:43.300\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works. You screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:50.900\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If not, well, the lightbulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:50.900 --> 01:01.900\nTests help us understand where we are and what we need to learn or improve. So remember, a test is just a way to check things out and learn along the way.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:05.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
