    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_184551.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.900\nNow, a test is just a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:30.200\nThe main idea behind a test is to see if something meets a certain standard or if something is working correctly.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:43.200\nIt helps us understand what's going on. For example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, when you take a quiz at school, that's a test to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:53.800\nAnother example is when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it tastes good!\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:57.700\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is a way to check something out and get some information. It's like a mini-experiment to help us learn and improve.\n```"
  },
