    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:24.600\nWe use tests all the time to see if something is working correctly, or if we understand something.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:32.700\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:43.000\nOr, you might take a test in school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:52.200\nAnother example could be testing a new recipe. You follow the instructions, and then you taste it to see if it's good.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:01.400\nIf it tastes great, the recipe \"passed\" the test! If not, maybe you need to adjust the ingredients.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:04.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:12.800\nIt helps us understand if things are working as expected or if we need to make some changes. Tests are everywhere!\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:16.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
