    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_185940.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:22.900\nIt's like a detective trying to figure out if something is true or correct. Think about it this way: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:31.700\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:42.500\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test! You're testing your recipe to see if it comes out delicious.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:53.100\nSo, a test helps us understand something better and see if it works the way we expect it to. Whether it's a quiz, a medical exam, or even trying out a new game, tests are all around us, helping us learn and improve.\n\n00:53.100 --> 01:03.000\nTo sum it up, a test is a way to check something and see if it's correct or works as expected.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:05.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ed49e2df-089d-4518-8613-1a80b083322b": {
    "id": "ed49e2df-089d-4518-8613-1a80b083322b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:26:28.474295",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T19:01:08.246281",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_190107.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_190107.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.300\nNo, not the kind you cram for! In this case, a test is simply a way to see if something works as expected.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch. The main idea behind a test is to compare what you expect to happen with what actually happens.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:29.100\nIf they match, great! The test passes.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:36.700\nIf they don\u2019t, well, you know something needs fixing. For example, let's say you're baking a cake.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:47.000\nYour test might be: \"Does the cake taste good?\" You expect it to taste delicious. If it does, the cake passed the taste test!\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:58.000\nOr imagine you build a tower of blocks. Your test is: \"Does the tower stand up?\" If it falls, the tower failed the test.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:08.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple check to confirm things are working the way they should.\n\n01:08.400 --> 01:12.000\nIt's about comparing expectations with reality.\n\n01:12.000 --> 01:15.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
