    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T19:01:55.144822",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_190155.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_190155.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:14.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and then seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:25.200\nThink about it: when you bake a cake, you test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:36.600\nOr, when you go to the doctor, they might run tests to see how healthy you are. These tests could involve checking your temperature or taking a blood sample.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:41.200\nTests aren't just in cooking or medicine. They\u2019re everywhere!\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:51.500\nYou take tests in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:51.500 --> 01:02.600\nSo, a test is really just a tool we use to learn more about something. It helps us understand, evaluate, and make decisions.\n\n01:02.600 --> 01:06.200\nTo recap, a test is a way to gather information and learn about something.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:09.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
