    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_190239.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:12.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests! A test, at its core, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:18.700\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:23.600\nYou're testing if the cake is done.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:31.200\nTests are used everywhere. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:44.200\nA teacher gives tests to see how well you understand a subject. Even a software developer uses tests to make sure their program doesn't crash.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:57.400\nSo, we use tests to learn something, to confirm something, or to prevent problems. Basically, it's a way to get information by putting something to the\u2026 well, test!\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:01.000\nIn short, tests help us understand how things work and make sure they're working properly.\n```"
  },
