    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_191309.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.300 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:09.400\nNow, in its simplest form, a test is just a way to check something,\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:12.300\nto see if it works or if it's true.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:16.700\nThink of it like this: you might \"test\" the water in a pool to see if it's warm enough to swim.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:21.400\nOr, a baker might \"test\" a cake with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:23.400\nSo, what are some other examples?\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:27.500\nWell, your doctor might give you a medical test to check your health.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:31.100\nOr, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:33.800\nThe idea is to get information or prove something.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:41.000\nBasically, a test is any process designed to evaluate something and give us results.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:46.700\nIt can be as simple as tasting a new food or as complex as a scientific experiment.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:51.800\nThe goal is always to learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:57.600\nTo recap: a test helps us check something, provides evidence, and gives us information.\n\n00:57.600 --> 00:59.500\nSimple as that!\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
