    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_192114.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.500\nToday, we're diving into the basics of tests.\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:26.000\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate a characteristic, skill, or quality.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.700\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your spelling abilities.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:39.400\nA taste test checks how something tastes.\nOr, a medical test checks your health.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:43.200\nThey all have a purpose \u2013 to give us information.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:47.000\nSo, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:50.800\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:50.800 --> 00:52.800\nIf it's still gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:54.000\nSee? Simple!\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:59.200\nIn short, a test helps us understand something better by giving us a measurable result.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:00.100\nHopefully, that clears things up.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:00.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
