    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:12.700\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:34.200\nWe use tests all the time to see if something is working correctly, or to see how much we know about a topic.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:45.800\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold. Or, when you're learning something new in school, your teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:56.100\nTests can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch. Or they can be more complex, like a big exam at the end of the year.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:04.100\nThe important thing is that they help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:12.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a way of finding something out.\n\n01:12.100 --> 01:15.900\nIt can be used to check if something is working or to measure your knowledge.\n\n01:15.900 --> 01:19.300\nRemember that and you're off to a great start!\n\n01:19.300 --> 01:22.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
