    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_192425.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:17.500\nAt its most basic, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:29.100\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:40.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:48.400\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you\u2019re testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:56.500\nOr when you press a light switch, you're testing if the light will turn on.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:04.100\nIn science, tests are called experiments, and they help us understand how things work.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:11.200\nImagine you want to know if sunlight helps plants grow.\n\n01:11.200 --> 01:19.300\nYou could test this by putting one plant in the sun and another in the dark, and then seeing which one grows taller.\n\n01:19.300 --> 01:22.900\nThat's a simple test!\n\n01:22.900 --> 01:30.500\nSo, remember a test is a structured way to ask a question and get an answer.\n\n01:30.500 --> 01:37.500\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:37.500 --> 01:42.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
