  "82820338-be46-490d-a6ba-711cf1767548": {
    "id": "82820338-be46-490d-a6ba-711cf1767548",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:26:43.636888",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T19:27:44.792720",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_192744.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_192744.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in computer programming, a test is a way to check if your code is working correctly.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like this: you build something, and then you test it to make sure it does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:31.100\nSo, how does it work? Well, you basically tell the computer what you expect the outcome to be.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:39.300\nFor example, if you have a piece of code that adds two numbers, you might test it by giving it 2 and 3.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:50.000\nIf the code gives you 5, then the test passes! If it gives you anything else, the test fails, and you know you need to fix your code.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:57.900\nTests are super important because they help catch mistakes early on, making sure your programs run smoothly.\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:06.100\nThey also give you confidence that your code is working as intended. They're like a safety net, catching any errors before they cause bigger problems.\n\n01:06.100 --> 01:14.300\nIn short, tests are a fundamental part of programming, helping us build reliable and robust software.\n\n01:14.300 --> 01:17.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
