    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_193043.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, a \"test\" is just a way of checking if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like this: you buy a new lightbulb. You wouldn't just assume it works, right?\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:27.500\nYou'd screw it in and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:32.800\nOr imagine you bake a cake. You poke it with a toothpick to see if it\u2019s done. That's another test!\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:37.500\nTests help us catch mistakes early.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:42.200\nIf the lightbulb doesn't turn on, you know to get a new one.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:51.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, you know the cake is ready. So, a test is simply a way to verify if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:55.700\nChecking if your shoes fit before you buy them? That's a test too!\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:00.600\nIt's all about making sure things are right.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:04.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
