    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:21.700\nIt's like an experiment or a check-up.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:27.700\nWe use tests all the time to see if something is working correctly, or to learn more about it.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:33.900\nThink about a simple lightbulb.\nWe can \"test\" it by plugging it in.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:41.200\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, something's wrong.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:48.500\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:55.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test too!\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:04.600\nSo, tests help us understand things better, and make sure they're doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:08.100\nThey're a fundamental part of learning and problem-solving.\n\n01:08.100 --> 01:11.700\nRemember, a test is just a method for finding something out.\n\n01:11.700 --> 01:15.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
