    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_194217.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.500\nNow, you might think of school exams, but a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it should.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:20.300\nIt's like a little experiment to see if things are going according to plan.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:28.300\nImagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might test it by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that means the cake is done!\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.900\nThat's a test! Or, think about checking if a light bulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:37.700\nDoes it light up? That's your test!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:40.500\nSo, a test is simply a way to see if something passes or fails.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:51.200\nIt helps us catch problems early and make sure everything is working as expected. Remember, testing is important in lots of different areas, from baking to building to, well, almost everything!\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:54.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
