    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_194954.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nNow, you might be thinking about school exams, but a test is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see what something is made of.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes their soup to test if it needs more salt. That's a test!\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:34.100\nOr a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. The main idea is to perform an action or observation and then compare the result to what you expect.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:39.500\nIf they match, great!\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:46.900\nIf not, you know something needs attention. For example, you might test a lightbulb by screwing it in.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:52.300\nIf it lights up, the test passes. If it stays dark, the bulb probably needs replacing.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:01.800\nSimple as that! So, a test is just a way of checking things. It helps us make sure things are working as they should and helps us identify problems.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:05.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
