    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests, and no, not the kind you stress about in school.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:18.500\nWe're talking about tests in the programming world.\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if your code is working correctly.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like checking your work after solving a math problem.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:35.300\nSo, how does it work?\nWell, you write some code, and then you write a separate piece of code to specifically check if that first piece of code does what it's supposed to.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:46.500\nFor example, if you write a program that's supposed to add two numbers, you can write a test that gives it 2 and 2, and then makes sure it returns 4.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:57.500\nIf the program returns 4, the test passes!\nIf it returns anything else, the test fails, letting you know there's a problem to fix.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:06.700\nTesting helps you catch mistakes early and makes sure your code is reliable.\nTests are a crucial part of software development.\n\n01:06.700 --> 01:10.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
