    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:27:04.315730",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T20:00:25.533015",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_200025.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_200025.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if you understand your math homework, you might take a practice quiz. That's a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:28.500\nOr maybe your doctor wants to check if you're healthy. They might run some medical tests.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:34.300\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. They can be written, like a school exam, or practical, like a driving test.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:46.300\nThe main goal is always the same: to measure your knowledge or ability.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:56.200\nSo, tests help us understand where we are and what we might need to learn next. They are important tools to help us grow and improve.\n\n00:56.200 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
