    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_200816.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:15.400\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:26.300\nYou're testing the lightbulb.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:29.300\nAnother example: If you want to know if your cookies taste good, you take a bite!\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:32.900\nThat's a taste test.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:48.700\nSo, tests help us understand if things are doing what they're supposed to. They can be simple, like checking a lightbulb, or more complicated, but they all have the same goal: to find out if something is true or working as expected.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:57.600\nTests are all around us, helping us learn and improve things every day.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
