    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_200910.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:17.700\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but instead of mixing chemicals, you're checking someone's knowledge or skills.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:26.900\nSo, how does it work? Well, a test usually has questions or tasks that someone needs to answer or complete.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:38.100\nTheir answers or performance are then graded or evaluated against a standard. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:48.200\nA math test checks if you can solve equations. Even a taste test is a kind of test, seeing if you can tell the difference between flavors!\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:60.400\nBasically, tests help us see what someone knows or can do. To sum it up, a test is a tool for measuring knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:60.400 --> 00:66.000\nPretty simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
