    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_201000.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:05.200\nAt its core, a test is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:07.600\nThink of it like asking a question\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:08.300\nand then looking for the answer.\n\n00:08.300 --> 00:12.400\nWe use tests all the time, without even realizing it.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:16.100\nFor example, if you're baking a cake and you poke it with a toothpick,\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:17.400\nthat's a test!\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:19.300\nYou're testing to see if it's done.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:22.500\nOr, if you try a new recipe, you're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.700\nAnother example is when your doctor checks your temperature.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:27.800\nThat's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:32.000\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking the weather before you go outside.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:38.300\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:42.900\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:45.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
