    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.800 --> 00:06.800\nToday we're tackling something fundamental:\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:09.600\nwhat is a test?\n\n00:09.600 --> 00:14.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well something performs or how much someone knows.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:20.800\nThink of it like checking if your cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:21.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:24.500\nThere are tests for all sorts of things.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:27.500\nA math test checks your knowledge of numbers.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:30.000\nA spelling test checks how well you can spell.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:33.300\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:36.800\nAnother example?\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:40.000\nImagine you're trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:42.300\nYou taste it to see if it's good.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:43.500\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:46.800\nYou're evaluating the recipe's success.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:55.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, your health, or even how delicious a cake is.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:58.400\nIt helps us understand and learn.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
