    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_202424.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:22.700\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:27.900\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:33.100\nYou test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:38.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:44.100\nOr, if you're checking if a light bulb works, you flip the switch.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:55.900\nIf the light turns on, the bulb passes the test. So, a test is really just a simple way to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation. It helps us know if things are working the way they should. Remember: question, answer, result! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
