    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:12.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you take in school, but tests in the context of\u2026 well, testing things!\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:23.200\nBasically, a test is a way to find out if something works as expected.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:26.600\nIt\u2019s like checking to see if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:36.000\nThat's a test! Think about baking a cake. You follow a recipe, and then you taste it.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:43.900\nThat taste test tells you if you followed the recipe correctly and if the cake is good.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:51.900\nOr imagine building with LEGOs. You might build a tower and then gently push it to see if it's strong enough to stand.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:59.900\nThat\u2019s testing its stability! So, tests help us confirm that something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:08.700\nWe try something, and then we observe the result.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:11.700\nTo recap, a test is a simple way to check if something works.\n\n01:11.700 --> 01:20.999\nWhether it\u2019s a light bulb, a cake, or a LEGO tower, testing helps us learn and improve.\n\n01:20.999 --> 01:22.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
