    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_204051.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly or if you know something well.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:25.400\nThink about it like this: when you learn a new song, you might try to sing it to test if you remember the words and the tune.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:32.700\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:38.300\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. In school, you might take a quiz.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:47.900\nAt the doctor's office, they might run tests on your blood. The point is always the same: to find out something specific.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:59.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check things. They help us learn, improve, and make sure everything is working as it should.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
