  "c8f57ac9-39c2-464d-b983-20125ce2f069": {
    "id": "c8f57ac9-39c2-464d-b983-20125ce2f069",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:27:40.992177",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-04T20:51:51.145694",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_205151.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_205151.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:13.900\nWhat are they, and why do we even need them?\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:23.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you understand something.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:33.700\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you use a toothpick to see if it's done. That toothpick is a little test!\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:42.500\nIn school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned. They can be quizzes, exams, or even just asking you questions in class.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:48.600\nFor example, a test might ask you what two plus two equals. If you answer four, you pass that little test!\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:59.500\nTests aren't meant to be scary. They're just tools to help everyone learn and improve. So, remember, a test is just a way to check understanding, like a toothpick in a cake! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "dede4539-3ac2-4bc5-a30c-b62d07cbb4ff": {
    "id": "dede4539-3ac2-4bc5-a30c-b62d07cbb4ff",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
