    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_205255.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_205255.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.900\nWe use tests all the time! Think of it like this: a cookie recipe is like a set of instructions.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:31.700\nYou're testing to see if you can follow those instructions and end up with delicious cookies.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:39.500\nOr, maybe you're testing a new lightbulb to see if it works. The test is whether it lights up or not.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:53.100\nTests can be super simple, like checking the weather outside to see if you need a jacket. Or, they can be a little more complex, like taking a quiz in school to see what you've learned.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:56.700\nSo, basically, a test is just a way to check something, see if it works, or find out information.\n\n00:56.700 --> 00:59.800\nPretty useful, right?\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:00.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
