    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.900 --> 00:06.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you dread in school,\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:08.700\nbut the kind that help us figure things out.\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:12.700\nA test is basically a way to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:16.800\nThink of it like checking if your lightbulb is working.\nThat's a simple test!\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:19.800\nYou flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test passes.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:24.800\nAnother example could be testing a recipe.\nYou follow the instructions, bake the cake, and then taste it.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:27.200\nDoes it taste good?\nThat's your test result!\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:32.100\nTests help us understand things better and make sure everything is running smoothly.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:37.300\nSo, tests are simply a way of checking if something is working as expected.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:39.000\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:41.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
