    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_211033.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you stress about in school, but a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:17.900\nThink of a test like a little detective. It asks a question and then looks for the answer.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:25.900\nThe main idea is to see if something meets our expectations.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:29.900\nDoes a light bulb turn on when you flip the switch? That's a test!\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:35.200\nDoes your phone connect to Wi-Fi? Another test!\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:46.700\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it. For example, when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:54.500\nOr, before you leave the house, you might check the weather app. That's a test to see if you need a jacket.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:06.900\nSo, a test is simply a way to confirm if something is working as it should. It's all about checking, observing, and making sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:10.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
