    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:38.600\nThat's a test! Basically, a test helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:47.400\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it has enough salt.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:57.100\nOr, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:08.000\nSo, tests are all about checking things, making sure they're good enough, or figuring out what needs improvement.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:18.900\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, from tasting soup to taking a big exam. The main idea is to find out information.\n\n01:18.900 --> 01:29.100\nTo recap, tests are checks or evaluations that help us understand if something is working as expected or meets a specific requirement.\n\n01:29.100 --> 01:32.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
