    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_212908.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: You build a toy car. A test would be pushing it to see if it rolls.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:30.400\nOr, if you're baking a cake, tasting a little bit before it's done is a test to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:39.100\nIn computers, tests are small pieces of code that check if other parts of the code are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:43.500\nIf the test passes, great! Everything's working.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:47.900\nIf it fails, it means something needs to be fixed.\n\n00:47.900 --> 01:02.700\nSo, tests are simply a way to make sure things are working as expected, whether it's a toy car, a cake, or lines of computer code.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:06.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
