    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_213955.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if the water in your pool is safe to swim in, so you use a test strip.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:27.400\nThat strip changes color, and you compare it to a chart. That comparison tells you if the water is good, or if it needs some chemicals.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:39.000\nSimilarly, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health. Or, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:49.400\nThat's a test too! So, a test is just a method to find out information about something, by observing or measuring it in some way.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:56.700\nIt helps us make decisions based on the results. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
