    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:34.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\nTests are used everywhere.\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even engineers use tests to make sure bridges are strong enough.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:41.100\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works.\nYou turn it on.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:46.500\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\nIf it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:57.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something, to see if it works, is correct, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:04.600\nThey help us learn and make sure things are safe and reliable.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
