    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_214755.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.100\nToday we're talking about tests. Now, you might think of school tests, but in the world of technology, a \"test\" simply means checking if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like this: you build a Lego car, right? A test is pushing it across the floor to see if the wheels turn.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:34.900\nOr, if you bake a cake, the test is taking a bite to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:41.000\nIn computers, we test software. Does this button do what it says? Does this website load correctly on different phones?\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:49.400\nWe run tests to find problems before other people do. Testing makes sure things are reliable and work as expected.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:58.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking if something does what it's supposed to do. Pretty simple, right?\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
