    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_215338.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:12.400\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:24.700\nIt's like asking a question or performing an action to see what happens. Think about it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you do a simple test, right?\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:31.100\nYou poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:36.200\nOr imagine you're checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:47.900\nYou flip the switch. If the light comes on, the bulb passes the test. Tests are used all the time to make sure things are working correctly, from your car engine\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:59.700\nto the apps on your phone. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something to see if it's working as expected. It helps us identify problems and make sure everything is running smoothly.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:03.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
