    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_221819.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:6.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:16.300\nThink of it like an investigation. We're trying to discover information about a person, a thing, or even an idea.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:22.200\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:29.400\nImagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might test if it\u2019s done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:36.300\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, think about taking a quiz in school.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:44.500\nThat's a test to see how much you've learned. Another example is a doctor using a test to check your health.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:51.000\nThey might take your temperature to test for a fever.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:57.500\nSo, a test is just a tool we use to learn something new. In short, a test is a method for gathering information.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.400\nIt helps us understand things better, whether it's about baking a cake, learning in school, or staying healthy.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:04.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
