    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_222048.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:14.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:29.900\nYou \"test\" it by screwing it in and turning it on.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:35.800\nThe test is whether the lightbulb lights up. If it does, it passes the test!\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:47.100\nIf it doesn't, it fails. Another example: a chef might \"test\" their soup by tasting it to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:58.400\nThe taste is the test, and whether it's delicious or not is the result. So, a test is simply a way to see if something meets a certain requirement.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:01.300\nWe perform the test, and we get a result that tells us if it passed or failed.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:03.800\nThat's the basic idea!\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:04.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
