    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_223648.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of your bath water to see if it's too hot or too cold.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:29.500\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:38.300\nTests aren't just for baths and baking, though! Scientists use tests to see if their ideas about the world are correct.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:47.400\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's making you sick. So, a test is basically just a way to gather information.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:59.200\nThey can be simple or complicated, but they all help us learn something new.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:07.700\nSo, to recap: a test is a procedure used to find something out. It's a way of asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:11.300\nAnd they're used everywhere, from your kitchen to a science lab!\n\n01:11.300 --> 01:14.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
