    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nNow, a test, at its core, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:17.400\nThink of it as a question you're asking something, and then getting an answer.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:24.200\nThe \"something\" could be anything, like how well you know a subject, or if a piece of equipment is working properly.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:29.900\nThe main idea is to see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:35.300\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:40.400\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:42.800\nThese tests give us useful information!\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:49.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method of evaluating something.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:53.900\nIt helps us understand where we stand and what we need to improve.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:56.400\nThat\u2019s the basics of a test!\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:00.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
