    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_224059.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_224059.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the concept of a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like this: You have a plant, and you want to know if it needs water. You might stick your finger in the soil. That's a test!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:31.800\nOr maybe you\u2019re wondering if your oven is hot enough to bake a cake. You can set a timer and then check the temperature gauge.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:37.400\nThat's a test too. Tests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:50.000\nThe key is that you\u2019re trying to answer a question or confirm something. So, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn more.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:60.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
