    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_224434.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test is.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:16.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your oven is hot enough to bake cookies. You set the temperature, wait a bit, and then carefully put your hand near the oven door. That's a test!\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:33.300\nOr, maybe you're checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:36.900\nLight? Test passed! No light? Time for a new bulb.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:39.500\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking the oven.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:47.800\nThe main idea is that a test gives us information. They tell us if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:57.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn and confirm things.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
