    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_225057.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see how well something performs or if something is true.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:28.300\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you can use a toothpick.\nSticking the toothpick in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:38.800\nOr, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp.\nIf it lights up, that's a test that tells you it's good.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:50.600\nTests are everywhere!\nFrom checking your spelling with a spellchecker, to a doctor checking your temperature, to even trying a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n00:50.600 --> 01:00.500\nThey all help us learn and make decisions.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something out and get some information.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:04.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
