    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_225151.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:26.300\nIt's like an investigation, but usually a little more structured.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:36.200\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:44.400\nThink about it: you taste a new food to test if you like it.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:52.600\nOr, you might try to turn on a light to test if the power is on.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:57.800\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:03.100\nThey can be written exams, quizzes, or even projects.\n\n01:03.100 --> 01:08.600\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem.\n\n01:08.600 --> 01:14.100\nA science test could ask you to explain a concept.\n\n01:14.100 --> 01:17.500\nThe goal is to show what you know.\n\n01:17.500 --> 01:29.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a method to discover information, from finding out if you like broccoli to showing what you've learned in class.\n\n01:29.000 --> 01:32.900\nIt's all about finding things out!\n\n01:32.900 --> 01:38.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
