    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_225340.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests!\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:17.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer, you're also looking for proof.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:22.900\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:30.100\nYour doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. A chef tastes food to test if it's seasoned right.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:36.200\nEven playing a game is like a test of your skills!\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:45.000\nSo, let's say you want to know if a plant needs water. You might poke the soil. If it feels dry, that's a test suggesting it needs water.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.800\nOr maybe you're testing if a toy car needs new batteries. If it moves slowly, that's a sign the batteries might be weak.\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:05.300\nBasically, a test helps you gather information to make a decision. It's all about observing, checking, and figuring things out.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:08.900\nHopefully, this gives you a good introduction to what tests are all about.\n\n01:08.900 --> 01:12.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
