    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.400\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:7.500\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:11.900\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:16.400\nThink about testing a new recipe.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:19.600\nYou follow the instructions, and then you taste it.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:21.800\nThat taste is the result of your test.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:25.700\nOr, imagine checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:27.800\nYou flip the switch.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:30.700\nIf it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:35.600\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if something needs to be fixed.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:40.400\nThey\u2019re used in everything from cooking to science to making sure your car is running smoothly.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:45.300\nBasically, a test is a way to gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:53.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out something by asking a question and seeing the answer.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:58.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
