    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_230417.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:20.400\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to check something, or see how well something works.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a fork to test if it's done.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:38.800\nTests can be used to check all sorts of things. Maybe you're taking a test in school to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:48.600\nOr perhaps you're testing out a new toy to see if it's fun. Even a doctor uses tests, like checking your temperature, to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:56.400\nSo, a test is basically a way to find out information. It helps us understand something better by observing or measuring it. Remember, testing is all about learning and understanding! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
