    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if the water is hot, so you touch it carefully.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:23.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:30.600\nIn school, tests help your teachers see how well you understand what you've been learning.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:33.800\nThey can be quizzes, exams, or even just asking you questions in class.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:41.500\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve a problem like \"2 + 2.\"\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:43.900\nThe test checks if you know the answer is 4.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:50.200\nOr, a spelling test might ask you to spell \"cat.\"\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:53.000\nIt's checking if you know how to write the word correctly.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:59.400\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.000\nIt helps us understand what we know and what we might need to learn more about.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:04.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
