    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_231410.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like this: you might test a lightbulb by plugging it in to see if it lights up.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:39.400\nIn science, tests are often experiments used to prove or disprove an idea.\nFor example, you could test if a plant grows better in sunlight by putting one plant in the sun and another in the shade, and then comparing their growth.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:46.900\nAnother example: if you're baking a cake, you can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:57.700\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something works or to prove an idea.\nWe use tests all the time, in all sorts of situations.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
