    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260104_231811.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_231811.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.200\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:01.200 --> 00:02.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:03.600\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:06.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:09.200\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate your knowledge, ability, or even the quality of something.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:14.900\nA taste test tells you if you like a certain flavor.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:18.100\nAnd a medical test helps doctors understand what's going on inside your body.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:23.200\nTests can be short quizzes, long exams, or even just trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:27.000\nThey help us learn where we're strong and where we need to improve.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.500\nSo, whether you're taking a test in school or trying a new recipe, remember that tests are all about learning and understanding.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:34.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "98e70c69-263e-4185-b260-17e1a453fb52": {
