    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_231859.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:28.600\nThat's a test! More formally, a test helps us figure out if something is working correctly or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:36.200\nFor example, a school exam tests your knowledge. Or, a doctor might run tests to check your health.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:40.800\nAnother example? Imagine you're building a tower of blocks.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:47.800\nYou test its stability by gently pushing it. If it falls, you know you need to adjust something.\n\n00:47.800 --> 01:00.400\nSo, tests can be big or small, but they all help us understand and improve things. Basically, a test is just a check to see if something works the way it should.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:07.100\nIt helps us learn and make better choices. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
