    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_233152.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered exactly what it means?\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:20.200\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something. We use tests all the time to learn more about ourselves, the world around us, and even how well we understand things.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:27.900\nThink about it like this: when you take a quiz at school, that's a test to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:36.200\nOr, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might taste a little bit of the batter \u2013 that\u2019s a test to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:48.400\nTests can be formal, like exams, or informal, like trying out a new recipe. The key is that they help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:53.300\nSo next time you hear the word \"test\", remember it's just a way of finding things out!\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:58.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
