    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:15.400\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like this: you might test if a cake is done by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:36.300\nOr, imagine you're testing if a light bulb works. You plug it in, and if it lights up, boom, it passes the test.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:49.600\nTests aren't just for cakes and light bulbs, though. We use tests all the time to learn new things, figure out what we know, and even see if something is working correctly.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:58.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a method for gathering information and seeing if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:04.900\nIt's about asking a question and getting an answer. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
