    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_234613.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:15.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: a cookie recipe is a test. You follow the instructions, and then the cookie comes out!\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:30.900\nThe cookie itself is the result of the test. Or, imagine you're trying to figure out if your plant needs water.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:34.900\nYou stick your finger in the soil. That's a test!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:42.200\nIf the soil feels dry, the test tells you it needs water. If it's moist, you know it's okay.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:51.200\nSo, a test is just a process, a method, a way of figuring something out or seeing if something works.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.100\nIt involves a question and some kind of observation to find an answer. Now you understand the basics of tests!\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
