    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:04.400\nToday we're going to explore something really fundamental:\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:04.700\na test.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:06.500\nNow, what is a test?\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:10.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:10.500 --> 00:13.300\nIt's a way to gather evidence and see how well something performs\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:15.100\nor if it's working correctly.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:17.000\nThink about it like this:\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:19.900\na spelling test checks your knowledge of words.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:24.400\nOr, imagine a taste test where you try different foods to see which one you like best.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:29.500\nEven a simple experiment, like seeing if a plant grows faster in sunlight or shade, is a type of test.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:34.100\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and figuring things out.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:41.100\nThey can be used to measure knowledge, preferences, or even the effectiveness of something.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:45.600\nThey are a really important tool for learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:47.200\nThat's the basics of what a test is!\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:49.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
