    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260104_235143.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:26.600\nIt helps us understand if something works, if we've learned something, or if something is true. Think of it like this: if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:37.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, in school, you take tests to show what you\u2019ve learned in class.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:46.300\nAnother example is a product test. Companies test their products to make sure they're safe and work correctly before they sell them to you.\n\n00:46.300 --> 01:02.600\nSo, tests are all about finding out information and making sure things are working as they should. To recap, a test is an evaluation, it can be used in everyday life, and it helps us learn and improve.\n\n01:02.600 --> 01:06.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
