    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE: The subtitles are a placeholder. Precise timing would be needed to sync with the audio.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, or a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:26.300\nThe main idea behind a test is to give something a challenge and then see how it responds. This helps us understand its properties or behavior.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:32.700\nFor example, if you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:40.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. Or, imagine you're testing a new toy car.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:46.000\nYou might see how far it can roll, or how fast it goes. That's a test too!\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:56.700\nSo, a test is simply a method for finding out information about something. It could be anything from baking a cake to checking if a new medicine works.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:03.800\nThe key is to observe the result and learn from it. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2ba7d4b6-6a2e-475c-9bf0-bfa6c51c0930": {
