    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_000320.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:19.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking. You poke it with a toothpick, right? That's a test!\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:25.800\nThe toothpick tells you if the inside is still gooey or nice and firm.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.800\nTests aren't just for baking, though. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:40.900\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned in class. Even programmers use tests to make sure their code is working correctly.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:52.500\nSo, whether it's a toothpick in a cake, a blood draw at the doctor's, or a quiz at school, a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:58.600\nIt's all about understanding something better. That's the basic idea behind a test!\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:02.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
