    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_000538.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:19.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something is working as expected.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on after you flip the switch.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:30.200\nThat's a test! We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:44.500\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, tasting the batter is a test to see if it's sweet enough. Or, checking the weather forecast before you leave the house is a test to see if you need an umbrella.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:54.000\nSo, a test helps us confirm something is correct, identify problems, and ultimately, make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:56.600\nIt's a simple, yet incredibly useful tool. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
