    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_000719.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:21.400\nIt could be anything! We test how well we know our multiplication tables, or how strong a bridge is, or even how tasty a new recipe is.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:31.800\nThe main idea behind a test is to ask a question or perform an action and see what happens. The result of that question or action gives us some data.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:46.400\nFor example, a simple taste test: you try a new cookie. Your reaction, like \"Wow, this is delicious!\" or \"Needs more chocolate,\" is the result of the test.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:53.300\nOr, think about a spelling test at school. Your score shows how well you've learned the words.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:02.700\nSo, a test helps us understand something better by giving us information we didn't have before. It helps us learn and improve.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:08.500\nRemember, a test is just a way to gather information.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:10.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
