    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:26.500\nYou're checking to see if the lightbulb passes the \"does it light up?\" test.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:32.100\nTests are used everywhere!\nA doctor might run blood tests to check your health.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:37.700\nA teacher gives you a quiz to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:49.600\nEven baking a cake involves tests, like checking if it's cooked through by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:49.600 --> 01:03.300\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something meets a specific requirement or works as expected.\nWe use them to learn, diagnose, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:13.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
