    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_001155.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: you build a birdhouse, right? A test would be putting it outside to see if birds actually use it.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:36.700\nOr, if you bake a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it tastes good. Tests help us find problems and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:47.100\nSo, if the birds ignore your birdhouse, you know you need to make some changes. If the cake is too dry, you adjust the recipe.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:58.400\nBasically, a test is a simple way of checking to make sure something works the way you expect it to. It's all about trying things out and learning from the results.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:01.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
