    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_001423.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into something fundamental: what is a test?\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:14.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. It's a method for gathering information.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:26.100\nWe use tests all the time, whether we realize it or not. Think about it: When you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like it.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:37.300\nOr, if you tap your brakes lightly, you're testing them to see if they're working. In school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:47.600\nTests can be formal, like a multiple-choice exam, or informal, like checking if the stove is hot by holding your hand near it.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:59.000\nThe important thing is that a test provides us with data or evidence. So, remember, a test is just a process for gathering information about something.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
