    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_003351.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:13.400\nNow, you might think of school exams, but a \"test,\" in general, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:17.700\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a lightbulb works,\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:25.600\nso you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:26.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:30.700\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might stick a toothpick in\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:33.100\nto see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:34.200\nThat's another test!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:37.000\nTests help us make decisions.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:40.500\nDoes the lightbulb need replacing?\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.100\nIs the cake ready to eat?\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:44.700\nThey give us information.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:51.700\nSo, a test is simply a way of gathering information by observing or experimenting.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:57.300\nIt's a basic way to learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:00.799\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
