    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_004219.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:17.700\nToday we're talking about tests!\nNot the kind you take in school necessarily, but a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: a test is simply a way to ask a question and get an answer.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:38.000\nSo, what kind of questions?\nWell, anything!\nFor example, you might test if a lightbulb turns on when you flip the switch.\nThe question is, \"Does the lightbulb work?\"\nAnd the answer is either yes, it lights up, or no, it doesn't.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:44.600\nAnother example is testing a recipe.\nYou follow the instructions and then taste the result.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:48.200\nIs it delicious?\nThat's a successful test!\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:51.800\nIs it terrible?\nThen something went wrong.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:55.100\nBasically, a test helps you confirm something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:58.400\nIt's all about asking a question and finding the answer.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:01.300\nTests are everywhere, helping us make sure things work the way they should.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:09.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
