    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_004818.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.200\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:23.400\nIt helps us figure out if something works the way it should, or if it's good enough.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:33.300\nThink about it like this: a chef tastes the soup to test if it has enough salt.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:43.200\nOr, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:53.800\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand the lessons.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:57.500\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:03.200\nIf it does, the light bulb passes the test! If not, well, it needs to be replaced.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:17.000\nSo, a test is just a way to find out information, to see if something is working correctly, or to measure its quality. It's all about checking!\n\n01:17.000 --> 01:22.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
