    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_005912.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.000\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or to find out more information about it.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a light bulb works, you can test it by screwing it into a lamp. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:36.900\nOr, if you want to see if your cookies taste good, you can test them by taking a bite.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:50.500\nTests can be simple, like that, or more complicated, but they all have the same basic idea: to see if something meets a certain standard or gives us the information we're looking for.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:55.900\nSo, in short, a test is a way to check something. That's it!\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
