    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:31:00.326745",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T01:09:17.901123",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_010917.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_010917.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:10.600\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and while that's true,\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:16.300\na test in a broader sense is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:19.500\nIt's a method for gathering information.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you can test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:29.900\nThe result, whether the bulb lights up or not, tells you something.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:35.200\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:38.400\nYou test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:41.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:42.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:49.500\nSo, a test is simply a procedure designed to provide information about something.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:53.700\nIt helps us learn, understand, and make decisions.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:57.300\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:01.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e62a7d1c-a4e4-4437-8c62-e1674ba0cedb": {
    "id": "e62a7d1c-a4e4-4437-8c62-e1674ba0cedb",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:31:00.951888",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T01:10:18.856338",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_011018.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_011018.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:27.200\nIt could be checking your knowledge, like a school quiz, or checking if something works, like testing a new toy.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:31.800\nThe main idea is to see if something meets a certain standard or performs as expected.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:36.900\nThink of it like this: a cookie recipe is a test for your baking skills.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:42.300\nDoes the cookie taste good? Did you follow the instructions correctly?\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:47.700\nHere\u2019s another example. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:53.300\nThey check things like your blood pressure and heart rate. Each one is a test!\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:56.600\nSo, to recap, a test is just a process for evaluation.\n```"
  },
