    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_011247.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:04.700\nToday, we're going to explore something super important: tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:06.400\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:10.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:15.300\nIt's a method to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:18.800\nThink about it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:23.500\nOr, a teacher gives you a test to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:25.300\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:27.700\nThey help us measure things and learn more.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:31.100\nFor example, you might test a toy to see if it's durable.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:34.400\nOr, you might test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:37.900\nThe key is to have a clear question and a way to get an answer.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:41.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a process for gathering information.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:46.700\nIt helps us evaluate, understand, and improve things.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:49.400\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is all about.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:51.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
