    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_011548.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works, so you flip the switch \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:31.700\nOr maybe you're baking a cake, and you stick a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean. That\u2019s a test too!\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:43.800\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. They help us confirm things, identify problems, and make sure everything's running smoothly.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:53.900\nSo, whether it's checking a lightbulb, baking a cake, or even taking a quiz at school, you're using the power of the test.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:01.400\nRemember, a test is just a way to check something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
