  "535ea904-1e1a-4d90-a81a-50930d7ff63e": {
    "id": "535ea904-1e1a-4d90-a81a-50930d7ff63e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:31:11.715823",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T01:23:15.064220",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_012314.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_012314.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:62.5\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.900\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:27.200\nThat's a test!\nIf the light comes on, the test passes.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:34.100\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\nAnother example is checking if your car's brakes are working.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:42.200\nYou gently press the brake pedal while driving slowly.\nIf the car slows down smoothly, the test is good.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:50.300\nIf you hear a screech or the car doesn't stop, then there's a problem.\nSo, in short, a test is simply a way to verify that something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:54.900\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
