  "21a487f4-9836-4ff5-9636-ddc1ff4704e9": {
    "id": "21a487f4-9836-4ff5-9636-ddc1ff4704e9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:31:29.212802",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T01:42:57.031065",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_014256.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_014256.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like an experiment, but often much simpler. Basically, you do something, and then you see what happens.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:35.700\nThe \"doing something\" is the test, and \"what happens\" gives you information.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:44.500\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you can poke it with a toothpick. That's the test!\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:48.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is probably done.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:52.100\nIf it's covered in batter, it needs more time. See?\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:01.600\nAnother example: a spelling test! The test is writing the words. The results tell you which words you know how to spell and which ones you need to practice.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:07.800\nSo, a test is just a method to learn something new or confirm something you already suspect.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:11.400\nIt's a way to gather information.\n\n01:11.400 --> 01:15.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3f593d54-1e4e-4d96-9943-c8b8ead464f1": {
    "id": "3f593d54-1e4e-4d96-9943-c8b8ead464f1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:31:29.856699",
