    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_015407.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, what they are, and why they\u2019re important.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:19.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works \u2013 the test is turning it on!\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:43.100\nIf it lights up, it passes the test. In school, tests help your teachers see what you've learned. They can be in many forms, like a quiz, a written exam, or even a practical demonstration.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:54.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks your spelling skills, and a math test checks your ability to solve problems. So, tests are a tool to measure knowledge or skill.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:01.100\nThey help you and others understand what you already know and what you might need to learn more about. They\u2019re a helpful part of the learning process. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
