    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:16.900\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:27.700\nThink of it like a detective looking for clues to understand something better.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:31.900\nWe use tests all the time, without even realizing it.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.100\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:40.300\nOr, a student might take a quiz to test how well they understand a lesson.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:44.500\nThe goal is to get information and see if something is working as expected,\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:48.700\nor if something needs to be improved.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:52.900\nAnother example?\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:56.500\nImagine you're building with LEGOs.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:01.500\nYou might test the connection between two bricks to see if they're strong enough to hold the whole tower up.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:10.600\nSo, remember: a test is simply a way to check something and gather information.\n\n01:10.600 --> 01:16.100\nIt helps us understand, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:16.100 --> 01:19.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
