    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_020023.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:05.200\nToday, we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:08.800\nNow, in everyday life, a test is just a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of your bathwater to see if it's just right.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:17.500\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:20.700\nBasically, it's a procedure designed to give you a specific result.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:22.300\nSo, how does this work?\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:26.800\nWell, you have something you want to learn about, and then you perform an action that gives you a result.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:31.700\nFor example, if you wanted to test if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:35.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:36.900\nThat's the test and the result.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:41.500\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to gain information by performing an action and observing the result.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:45.700\nIt helps us to understand something better.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:46.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
