    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_020315.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you dread,\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:08.500\nbut the kind that help us understand things better.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:10.200\nA test is basically a way to check something.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:14.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:15.300\nThat\u2019s a test!\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:19.400\nTests help us see if something is true or false, good or bad, working or broken.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:22.900\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:25.900\nA chef might taste a dish to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:31.100\nOr, a programmer might run a test to see if their code does what it's supposed to.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:37.700\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something and learn more about it.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:42.700\nIt can be as simple as flipping a switch or as complex as a medical exam.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:43.900\nNow you know what a test is!\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:46.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
