    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:07.000\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:14.000\nIt could be checking if you understand a lesson, or checking if something is working properly.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.600\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:25.500\nThat's one kind of test.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:30.500\nOr, a mechanic might test your car's battery to see if it's holding a charge.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:31.800\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:38.600\nBasically, we're gathering information to see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:45.000\nSo, a test helps us understand if something is good, bad, or needs improvement.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:47.500\nIt's a way to get answers.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:51.100\nRemember, tests can be used in lots of different situations.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:52.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
