  "817d2922-35d2-43ef-ad6c-70b1832e635f": {
    "id": "817d2922-35d2-43ef-ad6c-70b1832e635f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:31:48.702593",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T02:05:24.008646",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_020523.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_020523.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:18.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. It's like asking a question, but instead of just listening for the answer, we're looking for evidence.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:26.100\nThink about it this way: a recipe test tells you if a recipe works before you make it for your friends.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:37.200\nOr, a medical test helps doctors understand what's happening inside your body.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:50.500\nEven when you try a new video game, you're testing whether you like it! Tests help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:59.800\nThey can be big or small, formal or informal, but the important thing is that they give us information. So, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "78c31211-acbd-4535-b08e-d28598408d87": {
    "id": "78c31211-acbd-4535-b08e-d28598408d87",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:31:49.250510",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T02:06:06.206542",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_020606.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_020606.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:22.300\nWe use tests all the time. For example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done. That's a test!\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:29.100\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again. That's testing to see if it fixes the problem.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:36.600\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned. These tests help your teacher understand if you're getting the main ideas.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:53.000\nSo, whether it's checking a cake or taking an exam, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:53.000 --> 01:01.600\nTo recap, a test is a method to discover information. It helps us understand things better by giving us answers.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
