    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, you might think of tests as something stressful in school, but really, a test is just a way to see if something is working or doing what it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: Imagine you bake a cake. To test if it's done, you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:35.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, if you build a tower of blocks, you might gently push it to test its stability.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:49.400\nIf it doesn't fall over easily, it passes that test. So, a test can be anything from checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch, to seeing if a toy car rolls down a ramp.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:57.800\nIt's all about checking something to see if it works as expected. In short, tests help us learn and improve things!\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e8efd792-7dcf-47c1-bd1c-34a5930b6bd3": {
