    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.300\nToday, we're diving into the concept of a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:09.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something, kind of like giving it a little examination.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:12.900\nWe use tests all the time to see if something works, if it's true, or even just to learn more about it.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:17.800\nThink about it like this: you might test a new recipe by cooking it.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:21.400\nThe \"test\" is the cooking process, and the result tells you if the recipe is good!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:26.300\nOr imagine a toy. You test it by playing with it to see if it's fun and doesn't break.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:32.300\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like trying out a new pen to see if it writes smoothly.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:39.300\nSo, in short, a test is a process for finding out something about something else.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:43.900\nIt\u2019s all about gathering information and making discoveries!\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:47.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
