    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in. A test can be anything from a simple yes or no question, like \"Is this apple red?\", to something more complex, like a spelling quiz.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:39.100\nThe goal is to see if something meets a certain standard or if it behaves the way we expect.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:44.200\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you\u2019re healthy.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:49.300\nOr, you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:51.200\nSee? Tests are all around us!\n\n00:51.200 --> 01:03.500\nSo, to recap: tests help us gather information and check if things are working correctly or meeting certain requirements.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:06.500\nThey're a fundamental part of learning and problem-solving.\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:11.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
