    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:13.100\nWhat is a test, really? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:23.900\nIt's a process or procedure designed to evaluate something. Think of it like this: a recipe test lets you see if a new cake recipe tastes good.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:34.200\nA spelling test helps your teacher see how well you know your words. Or, imagine testing the water in a swimming pool to make sure it's safe to swim in.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:45.700\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from figuring out if your toy car can make it down a ramp, to making sure a bridge is safe for cars to drive on.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:53.300\nBasically, if you want to learn something by trying it out and seeing what happens, you're doing a test!\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:61.400\nSo, a test is a way to gather information and learn. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
