    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nWhat are they and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much someone knows about something, or how well they can do something.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:23.600\nThink of it like this: you might have a spelling test in school to see how well you know your vocabulary.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:36.100\nOr a driving test to show you can safely operate a car. Tests can be written, like multiple choice questions, or they can be practical, like showing a skill.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:46.000\nFor example, a chef might take a taste test to check the seasoning of a dish. A scientist might run a test to see if a hypothesis is correct.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:58.500\nSo, tests help us measure knowledge, skills, and abilities. In short, tests are tools we use to evaluate understanding and performance.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:02.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
