    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:06.600\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:08.900\nThink about it: a spelling test tells you how well you know your words.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:12.400\nA taste test lets you decide which cookie tastes better.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:16.600\nThe main idea behind any test is that it gives you information.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:19.900\nIt helps you measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:24.000\nYou're checking to see if something is true, correct, or working as expected.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:28.800\nFor example, a doctor might run blood tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:34.800\nOr, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and effective.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:41.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of gathering information to learn more about something.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:46.300\nIt helps us understand, measure, and evaluate.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:47.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
