    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_022949.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:20.400\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:30.000\nTests can be all sorts of things. It could be a quiz at school to see what you've learned.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:36.800\nOr, it could be checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:42.000\nThe point is, you're trying to get information.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.700\nFor example, imagine you want to know if your cake is ready.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:50.800\nYou might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:50.800 --> 00:54.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:57.000\nIf it's sticky, it needs more time.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:01.700\nSee? Simple! So, to recap, a test is a procedure or process designed to gather information about something.\n01:01.700 --> 01:05.600\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:06.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
