    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_023505.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:24.500\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard. Think of it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:29.400\nThat's a test! You're checking if the cake is cooked all the way through.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:35.600\nOr, imagine a doctor checking your temperature. That's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:47.700\nTests can be big or small, simple or complicated. But the main idea is always the same: to get information and see if something passes or fails.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:53.900\nSo, in summary, a test is just a way to check something and find out if it's working as expected.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
