    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:21.500\nIt's a process that helps us understand or evaluate something better.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:27.600\nThink about it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you're sick.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:36.100\nA teacher uses a test to see what you've learned. Even baking a cake is a test!\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:44.500\nYou\u2019re testing if the ingredients will combine and bake into something delicious.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:49.900\nLet\u2019s say you want to know if your plant needs water.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:53.500\nYou can stick your finger in the soil.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:57.400\nIf it feels dry, that's your test telling you it's time to water the plant.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:05.600\nOr maybe you're checking if your phone is charged. You look at the battery icon.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:12.600\nThat's a test showing you the battery level. So, in a nutshell, a test is a simple way to gather information and make decisions.\n\n01:12.600 --> 01:19.800\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
