    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_023837.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:21.900\nNow, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:39.700\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake and you taste it to see if it's sweet enough \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:47.100\nIn science, we use tests to see if our ideas, called hypotheses, are right.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:53.300\nFor example, if you think plants grow better with more sunlight, you can test that by giving some plants lots of sun and others very little.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:59.500\nThen, you watch to see what happens. Another example is when you're learning something new in school.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:06.900\nThe quizzes and exams? Those are tests to see how well you understand the material.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:14.300\nSo, tests are simply ways to find out information and see if things are the way we expect them to be.\n\n01:14.300 --> 01:16.700\nThey help us learn and improve.\n\n01:16.700 --> 01:22.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "7d618636-b515-49e2-a984-6970db358735": {
    "id": "7d618636-b515-49e2-a984-6970db358735",
