    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_023927.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.960\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:01.960 --> 00:05.030\nIn its simplest form, a test is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:05.030 --> 00:07.550\nWe use tests every day, even without realizing it.\n\n00:07.550 --> 00:09.810\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a light switch works.\n\n00:09.810 --> 00:10.930\nYou flip it.\n\n00:10.930 --> 00:11.730\nThat's a test!\n\n00:11.730 --> 00:16.480\nThe core idea is that you're performing an action, or applying something, to see what the result will be.\n\n00:16.480 --> 00:20.930\nSo, if you're baking a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:20.930 --> 00:23.740\nOr a doctor might run blood tests to check if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.740 --> 00:27.250\nTests help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n00:27.250 --> 00:30.530\nThey can be big and formal, or small and informal.\n\n00:30.530 --> 00:33.500\nBut they all serve the same purpose: to give us information.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:39.560\nSo remember, a test is simply a way to get information by performing an action or applying something and observing the result.\n\n00:39.560 --> 00:42.140\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
