    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_024752.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nNow, a test is just a way of finding out if something is true or correct.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You plug it in, and that's your test. The light either turns on, meaning the bulb passes the test, or it doesn't, meaning it fails.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:29.900\nSimple, right?\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:38.100\nLet\u2019s say you want to know if your plant needs water. You can test it by sticking your finger in the soil.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:46.200\nIf it feels dry, the test tells you it needs water. If it feels moist, it\u2019s probably okay.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:52.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It helps us make decisions based on whether something passes or fails.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:56.400\nTests are everywhere! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
