    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_025231.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:07.300\nHi everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about what a test is, at its most basic level.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:21.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\nIt helps us measure or assess something, like how well you understand a topic, or how strong a material is.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you can do a simple test \u2013 stick a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:41.500\nOr, if your doctor wants to know if you have a fever, they'll use a thermometer to test your temperature.\nTests can be anything from a quick quiz to a complex scientific experiment.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:51.900\nThe important thing is they give us data to make informed decisions.\nSo, a test is a process to gain information, usually through a measurement.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:03.900\nWe can use it to check anything, from cakes to temperatures to knowledge!\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:07.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
