    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_025707.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.200\nHello! Today, we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:12.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:19.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your toy car works. You put in batteries and try to drive it.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:23.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:28.300\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You taste it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:32.700\nThat\u2019s another test!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:40.500\nTests can be as simple as checking if a light bulb turns on, or as complex as a doctor running bloodwork.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:52.900\nThe main idea is that you\u2019re trying to find out something specific. So, to recap: a test is a method used to determine if something meets a certain requirement or standard.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:56.100\nIt helps us confirm if things are working as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
