    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:24.300\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer. In everyday life, we use tests all the time.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:35.800\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:43.500\nOr, when you try on a new pair of shoes, you're testing if they fit comfortably.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:51.200\nAnother example is checking if your bike tires have enough air. You might press on them to see if they feel firm.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.800\nThat's a test too! So, a test is just a simple way to see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.100\nIt helps us make sure things are working the way they should.\n01:03.100 --> 01:05.600\nIn short, tests are all about checking things!\n01:05.600 --> 01:06.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
