    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_031043.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, and no, not the kind you cram for!\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:20.700\nIn this context, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:28.800\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb and you want to know if it\u2019s good.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:35.000\nYou screw it into a lamp \u2013 that's the test! The main idea is to give something a try and see what happens.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:42.700\nIf the lightbulb lights up, the test passes. If it doesn't, the test fails. Simple, right?\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:56.200\nAnother example: If you bake a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it\u2019s yummy. Or, if you write a sentence, reading it back is a test to see if it makes sense.\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:02.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.800\nIt's about giving something a try and seeing what happens.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:08.600\nThat's all there is to it!\n\n01:08.600 --> 01:12.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
