    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_031336.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_031336.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good. You screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:32.300\nOr maybe you're baking a cake, and you stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done. That's another test!\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:40.200\nSo, a test is simply a way of finding out if something meets your expectations.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:47.700\nIf the lightbulb lights up, the test passes. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:47.700 --> 01:00.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it, to make sure things are working correctly. In short, tests help us confirm things work as intended.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "97702557-f646-42dd-9c3d-eb12761de1d1": {
    "id": "97702557-f646-42dd-9c3d-eb12761de1d1",
