    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_031520.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:16.700\nA test, in simple terms, is a way to find out what you know about something. Think of it like a measuring stick for your knowledge.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:27.000\nTests can come in many forms. You might have a multiple-choice test where you pick the best answer, or a fill-in-the-blank test where you complete a sentence.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:38.400\nSometimes it's a practical test, like showing you can ride a bike or bake a cake.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:52.100\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words. A math test checks your understanding of numbers and equations.\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:01.700\nThe important thing is that a test helps you, and your teachers, understand what you\u2019ve learned and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:05.300\nSo, to recap, a test is just a tool to measure your knowledge.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:08.900\nIt helps you see what you know and what you still need to learn.\n\n01:08.900 --> 01:12.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
