    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_032118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake.\nYou test it to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:29.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\nThat means it's ready.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:35.600\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\nYou test yourself by trying to balance.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:42.200\nEach time you ride a little further without falling, you're passing a little test and getting better.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:48.800\nSo, a test is simply a method to find out if something is working correctly, or if you've learned something new.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:56.900\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we need to work on.\nI hope you found this helpful!\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "53e479c1-31c5-4b6e-a5f8-83b3cce54d47": {
    "id": "53e479c1-31c5-4b6e-a5f8-83b3cce54d47",
