    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_032343.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:19.300\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you might poke one with a toothpick.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:24.500\nThat's a test! In everyday life, we use tests all the time.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:33.500\nYour doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Or, maybe you take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:44.300\nSo, essentially, a test helps us understand the condition, quality, or value of something. It gives us information!\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:53.900\nFor example, a taste test can tell you if a new recipe is delicious. Or a spelling test shows you how well you know your words.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:08.800\nTests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all have the same goal: to give us answers. So, the next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a way of checking something out!\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:12.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
