    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_032655.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.800\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:04.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out!\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:09.100\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:17.300\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you're healthy, or a chef tastes food to test if it's seasoned correctly.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:20.300\nTests come in many forms.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:23.900\nThere are written tests, like quizzes in school, where you answer questions.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:27.000\nThere are physical tests, like seeing how high you can jump.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.700\nAnd there are even tests that machines do, like a car safety inspection.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:34.600\nFor example, a simple test is asking someone \"What's your name?\"\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:38.200\nThe answer tells you something about them.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:40.500\nOr, a math problem is a test of your math skills.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:47.500\nBasically, any time you're trying to get information or measure something, you're using a test.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:51.900\nSo, a test is just a way to check something out and learn more about it!\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
