    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_032912.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:19.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It could be about you, like a quiz in school, or about something else entirely, like checking if your cookies are baked all the way through.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:27.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works. Your test is to screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:32.800\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If not, it fails.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:37.500\nAnother example? Checking if your car has enough gas.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:42.300\nThe gas gauge is your test.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:50.100\nIf it reads \"full,\" you're good to go. If it's on \"empty,\" well, you know what to do.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:57.900\nTests help us make decisions and learn new things. They're all around us!\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:06.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information. It's a question we ask, and the results help us understand something better.\n01:06.800 --> 01:11.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
