    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_032955.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_032955.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.300\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:17.200\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like an experiment, but often focused on measuring knowledge or skills.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:35.200\nBasically, you present someone with questions or tasks, and their answers or performance give you information.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:45.300\nFor example, a spelling test tells you how well someone knows their spelling. Or a taste test can tell you which flavor people prefer.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:54.500\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. There are written tests, practical tests, even tests you don't realize you're taking!\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:03.900\nThe key is that they're designed to give you data. So, a test is a method for gathering information through questions or tasks.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:09.400\nHopefully, now you have a better understanding of what a test is and how it works.\n\n01:09.400 --> 01:14.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "99413274-8e47-41f2-8bef-d713accf2f97": {
    "id": "99413274-8e47-41f2-8bef-d713accf2f97",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:32:56.990851",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T03:30:43.423286",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_033043.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_033043.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe by tasting it.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:41.300\nOr, a doctor might test your vision to see how well you can see. In computers, we write tests to make sure our code is doing what we expect it to do.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:50.600\nFor example, if we write code to add two numbers, we can test it by giving it 2 and 3, and making sure it gives us 5.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:59.500\nTests help us find mistakes early on and make sure our programs are reliable. They're a really important part of building good software.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:00.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is working as it should!\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:00.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
