    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_034136.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:11.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests. Now, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:23.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a process we use to check if something is working, or to see how well something is done.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:29.100\nThink of it like this: You might test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:36.100\nOr a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar. See? It's all about checking something!\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:43.100\nTests can be simple, like pressing a button to see if it works. Or they can be more complicated, like taking a quiz in school to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:55.500\nThe important thing is that a test gives us information and helps us understand something better. So, remember, a test is just a way to find something out by checking it.\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:59.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
