    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_035030.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking. You do a test \u2013 you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:27.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:35.100\nTests aren't just for cakes, though. We use them all the time.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:42.900\nA doctor might give you a test to see if you're sick. A teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:51.900\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in, and if it lights up, it passes the test. It works! If it doesn\u2019t light up, it fails.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:58.300\nSo, a test is just a way to find out if something is working properly or if something is true.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:02.400\nThey help us learn and make decisions.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
