    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_035411.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:23.500\nIt helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:32.000\nThink about it like this: your doctor gives you a test to check your health.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:40.500\nOr, you might test a recipe to see if it tastes good. In school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:49.800\nFor example, a simple test for a lightbulb is to screw it in and see if it lights up.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:57.700\nIf it does, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails. So, tests help us understand things better by giving us information.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.600\nIn short, a test is a check, an examination, or a procedure\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.200\nthat helps us determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n```"
  },
