    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_035539.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:08.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you dread in school,\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:10.700\nbut tests in a more general sense.\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:16.100\nBasically, a test is a way of finding something out.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:22.200\nIt's a process you use to check if something is working, if something is true, or to learn more about something.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:26.300\nThink about it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:32.400\nOr, you might test a new recipe by cooking a small batch before making a huge meal for everyone.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:35.900\nEven trying on clothes at the store is a kind of test to see if they fit!\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:44.200\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and make a decision based on that information.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:48.700\nWe use tests all the time, often without even realizing it.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:51.400\nThey help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
