    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_035706.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:28.800\nThink of it like this: if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:38.200\nOr, if you're buying a used car, you might take it for a test drive to see if it runs smoothly.\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:48.600\nSo, basically, a test is any procedure designed to evaluate the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:59.100\nIt helps us make decisions and ensure things are working as expected.\nIn short, tests are important for checking quality and making sure things work!\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
