    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_040140.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:03.500 --> 00:07.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 \n\n00:07.000 --> 00:11.800\nnot the kind in school, but tests as a way of checking if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:16.500\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you want to make sure it actually moves.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:20.500\nThe \"test\" is turning it on and seeing if it drives.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:22.800\nBasically, a test is a procedure\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:26.500\ndesigned to see if a specific condition is met.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:27.700\nWe use tests all the time\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:29.700\nin everyday life.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:32.700\nIs the lightbulb working? You flip the switch \u2013\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:33.900\nthat's a test!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:36.300\nIs the oven hot enough?\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:38.900\nYou check the temperature gauge \u2013\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:39.300\nanother test!\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:43.000\nIn more complex situations, like building a website,\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:46.600\ntests help us make sure each part is functioning correctly.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:50.100\nIf a button is supposed to take you to a new page,\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:52.300\na test will confirm that it does.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:56.500\nTests help us catch problems early, so we can fix them before they cause bigger issues.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:01.500\nSo, tests are simply a way to verify things are working as expected.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:04.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
