    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_040308.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:18.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like a way to check your understanding. It could be a written quiz in school, like remembering the capitals of different countries.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:38.400\nOr it could be more practical, like testing how fast you can run a race.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:49.000\nEven trying a new recipe is a kind of test to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:59.500\nSo, tests help us understand what we've learned and where we might need a little more practice. They're not meant to be scary, just helpful tools.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:03.000\nTo recap, a test is a way to measure knowledge or ability. It can be a quiz, a physical challenge, or even an experiment.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
