    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:24.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:33.000\nThink of it like this: you might give your dog a treat to test if he knows how to sit. The treat is the prompt, and his sitting is the result.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:41.500\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake and you taste the batter. That\u2019s a test to see if it\u2019s sweet enough!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:51.100\nTests are everywhere, from science experiments to classroom quizzes. They help us learn and make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:51.100 --> 01:01.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding things out. It has a prompt, and a result, and it helps us understand something better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
