    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of what a test really is.\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:16.500\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:29.100\nIf it lights up, it passes the test! In many areas, like science or school, tests are used to see if something is true or if someone understands a concept.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:38.000\nFor example, a scientist might test if a new medicine works, or a teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:52.800\nSo, a test can be as simple as checking if your shoes fit, or as complex as a big exam. The main point is, it's all about finding out information and checking if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:03.000\nHopefully, that gives you a better understanding of what a test is. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
