    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:08.900\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:12.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:17.900\nThink of it like an experiment, but not always in a lab.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:22.800\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:28.700\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:35.300\nOr, if you're trying to figure out why your toy car isn't working, you might test different batteries to see if that's the problem.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:43.400\nTests help us confirm if something is true or false, good or bad, working or not working.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:52.900\nSo, whether it's a quiz at school, trying out a new game, or figuring out why your flashlight isn't turning on, you're using tests to learn and understand the world around you.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:58.000\nBasically, a test is just a way to get information.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:00.500\nHopefully, that clears things up!\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
