    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are, and why we use them.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:16.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:37.600\nFor example, a spelling test helps us see how well we know our words. Or, if you try a new recipe, tasting it is a test to see if it's good!\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:48.400\nScientists use tests to check if their ideas are correct. They might do an experiment to see if a plant grows better in sunlight or shade.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:59.300\nSo, tests are just tools to help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:02.400\nThey can be big or small, simple or complicated, but the basic idea is always the same: ask a question, and find an answer.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
