  "c92ed792-4f64-449d-9bc8-327cee6a5a60": {
    "id": "c92ed792-4f64-449d-9bc8-327cee6a5a60",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:33:47.811059",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T04:31:40.221338",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_043140.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_043140.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:17.100\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information or see how well something works.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:30.400\nThink of it like this: you might test a new cookie recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:42.900\nIn science, tests, also known as experiments, are even more structured. We change one thing, called a variable, and see how it affects something else.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:58.900\nFor example, you could test whether plants grow faster in sunlight or in the shade. You would keep everything else the same, like the amount of water, and just change the light.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:06.400\nSo, remember, a test helps us learn and understand things better by exploring how different factors affect each other. It's all about asking questions and finding answers. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
