    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_043640.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.300\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:06.900\nA test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:10.200\nIt\u2019s like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:14.100\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:18.900\nThink about it. When you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:21.700\nThat\u2019s a test to see if the cake is done.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:28.300\nOr, when you try on a new pair of shoes, you walk around to test if they fit comfortably.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:36.200\nTests can be formal, like the ones you take in school to show what you've learned, or they can be informal, like checking if the water is warm enough before you jump in the pool.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:45.200\nBasically, a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:48.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information!\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
