    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:18.600\nWe use tests all the time to check if something is working correctly, or to see if something is true.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:30.700\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in to test if it's done.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:40.500\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down is a test of your balance.\nEach time you try, you're testing yourself.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:52.400\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking the batteries in your remote.\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:04.700\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to get information.\nIt helps us understand if something works, if something is true, or if we're on the right track.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:09.400\nNow you know! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
