    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:36.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. For example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like it.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:46.200\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken, you flip the switch \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:56.100\nIn school, tests help your teachers see what you've learned. And in science, tests are called experiments.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:04.700\nScientists use experiments to see if their ideas about the world are correct.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:13.300\nThey might test if a plant grows faster with more sunlight, for example.\n\n01:13.300 --> 01:17.000\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and answer a question.\n\n01:17.000 --> 01:26.000\nIt can be as simple as trying something new or as complex as a scientific experiment. That's the basics of testing!\n\n01:26.000 --> 01:29.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
