    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_050442.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.121 --> 00:01.711\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:01.711 --> 00:03.861\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.861 --> 00:07.091\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.091 --> 00:11.661\nIt's a process we use to gather information or check if something is true or correct.\n\n00:11.661 --> 00:15.981\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:15.981 --> 00:17.591\nYou perform a test!\n\n00:17.591 --> 00:20.181\nYou stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:20.181 --> 00:23.481\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test \u2013 it's done!\n\n00:23.481 --> 00:28.211\nOr, imagine you're taking a spelling test at school.\n\n00:28.211 --> 00:32.401\nThat test helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:32.401 --> 00:34.571\nThe score you get shows how well you did.\n\n00:34.571 --> 00:43.451\nSo, a test is just a method for getting information, whether it's about a cake, your spelling, or anything else you can think of.\n\n00:43.451 --> 00:45.991\nIt helps us understand something better.\n\n00:45.991 --> 00:48.881\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
