    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_051141.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a really fundamental idea: the test.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:16.400\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but often a bit more structured.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:27.200\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. For example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like it.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:42.400\nOr, when you turn on a light switch, you're testing if the light bulb works. Tests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like figuring out if a toy needs new batteries.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:53.400\nThe key is that you're performing an action or asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:05.200\nSo, remember: a test is a process to discover information. It can be as simple as trying something new, or as complex as a scientific experiment.\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:08.800\nHopefully, this gives you a basic understanding of what a test is!\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:12.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
