    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:16.900\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we're talking about a way to check something. Think of it like a simple question you ask to see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:27.700\nThe main idea behind a test is to get information. This information helps us understand if something is good, bad, right, or wrong.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:33.900\nFor example, think about a spelling test. It checks if you know how to spell certain words.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:42.300\nOr, imagine testing a new toy to see if it's safe for kids to play with. These are all different kinds of tests.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:51.900\nSo, to sum it up, a test is just a way to get information and check if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:58.900\nIt's a simple, but powerful, tool. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
