    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a really important concept: the test.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:28.400\nThink of it like a detective trying to solve a mystery. They gather clues, which are like your inputs, and then they look at the result, which is like the output of the test, to see if everything adds up.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:37.800\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, the test is tasting it! You're checking if it tastes good and is cooked all the way through.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:46.300\nOr, if you\u2019re checking if a light bulb works, you flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:54.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check something. You do something, and then you see what happens.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:01.700\nIf the result is what you expect, the test passes! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
