    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:07.000\nwhat they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:11.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:14.800\nIt's a process designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:18.400\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:22.400\nOr, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:24.500\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test!\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:28.800\nYou're testing your recipe and your baking skills to see if it comes out delicious.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:32.600\nSo, tests help us measure things and understand where we are.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:37.400\nThey help us improve, learn, and make better decisions.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:40.600\nThey can seem a little scary sometimes, but remember, they're just a tool for learning.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:46.000\nTo recap, tests are evaluations used to assess knowledge, abilities, or performance.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:50.500\nThey're all around us, helping us learn and improve.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:54.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
