    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_054743.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.400\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:23.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\nIt's a process of asking a question, or performing an action, to see what the result will be.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.300\nThink of it like this: a cooking test!\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:33.700\nYou try a little bit of the soup to see if it needs more salt.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:40.900\nOr maybe you're testing a lightbulb to see if it works by plugging it in.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:51.100\nSee?\nYou're asking a question \u2013 \"Does this lightbulb work?\" \u2013 and performing an action to find the answer.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:58.700\nTests are used everywhere, from science experiments to checking if you know your multiplication tables.\nThey help us learn, improve, and understand the world around us.\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:02.300\nSo remember, a test is just a way to find something out.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
