    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_055647.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:10.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, it's a way to check something.\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:18.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:25.200\nTests help us see if something is working as it should or if something needs fixing.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:34.800\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Or a teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:46.800\nAnother example? Before a company releases a new phone, they run tons of tests to make sure the battery lasts long enough and the camera takes good pictures.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:56.000\nSo, tests are all about checking things! In short, a test is a process to evaluate or assess something.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:03.400\nIt helps us understand its quality or performance. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
