    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_060009.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, we're using the word \"test\" to mean trying something out to see how it works.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like an experiment, but usually on a smaller scale.\nSo, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:30.600\nIt's a way to check if something does what it's supposed to do.\nWe're looking for proof that it works correctly.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:46.200\nFor example, if you bake a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it tastes good!\nOr, if you build a birdhouse, putting it outside and watching if birds use it is a test to see if it's well-designed.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:52.600\nEven trying out a new recipe is a form of testing!\nYou're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:52.600 --> 01:02.900\nBasically, tests help us learn and improve things.\nThey give us valuable information about whether something is successful or needs more work.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:11.700\nRemember, a test is simply a way to find out if something works!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
