    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_060925.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE\nAll timestamps are approximate due to the dynamic nature of text rendering.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.900\nThink of a test as a way to check your understanding of something. It's like a little quiz that helps you see what you know and what you might need to learn more about.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:29.100\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. You might have a multiple-choice test where you pick the right answer, or a fill-in-the-blank test where you write in the missing word.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:37.500\nThey're used in school to see how well you're learning, but adults take tests too, like when they're learning a new skill!\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:45.000\nFor example, if you're learning to ride a bike, a test might be seeing if you can balance without falling.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:56.700\nOr, if you're learning to bake a cake, the test is how good the cake tastes! So, remember, a test is just a way to check your understanding.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.800\nIt helps you learn and grow. Don't be afraid of them!\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:04.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f968dbe5-4256-4ba7-91e7-a22af22689bd": {
    "id": "f968dbe5-4256-4ba7-91e7-a22af22689bd",
