    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_061012.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find out if something works as it should.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you test it by poking it with a fork to see if it's cooked through.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:32.000\nThat's a test! Or maybe you buy a new flashlight, and you test it by turning it on to see if the light works.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:38.900\nAgain, a test! Tests help us identify problems and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:47.700\nThey can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb is working, or more complex, like testing a new medicine.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:59.600\nThe important thing is that they give us information about something. So, remember, a test is simply a way of checking if something is working the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:05.900\nIt helps us learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
