    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_061255.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. It's how we find out if something is working correctly, or if we've learned something new.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like this: your mom might \"test\" the temperature of your forehead to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:37.000\nOr, after learning about animals in school, your teacher might give you a quiz \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.300\nAnother example could be testing a new toy. You might push all the buttons to make sure they all work.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:51.200\nThat's testing too! So, a test is a way to evaluate or examine something to see what its properties are or how well it performs.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:57.500\nIt's all about checking and understanding. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
