  "7f1c1b1c-3b8b-465c-a5f5-0f06ebf7bedb": {
    "id": "7f1c1b1c-3b8b-465c-a5f5-0f06ebf7bedb",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:35:14.739174",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T06:15:23.377708",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_061523.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_061523.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.400\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in the world of science and engineering, a test is really just a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:28.900\nThink of it as an experiment with a goal. Basically, a test is when you apply a certain condition or input, and then you carefully observe the result.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:37.800\nFor example, if you want to test if a light bulb works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:42.600\nThe result? Either the bulb lights up, or it doesn't! That's a test.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:48.200\nAnother example: a taste test! You try a new flavor of ice cream.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:56.300\nYour input is the ice cream, and your observation is whether you like it or not. That's a simple test too.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:09.400\nSo, a test is just a way to learn something by trying something out and seeing what happens.\n\n01:09.400 --> 01:13.000\nIn summary, tests help us understand how things work\n\n01:13.000 --> 01:16.300\nand whether they meet our needs.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:19.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
