    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_061826.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:09.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests, what they are and why they're important.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:26.000\nWe use tests all the time, whether we realize it or not. Think about it: a doctor might run a test to see if you're sick.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:33.000\nA baker might taste their cake batter to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:40.000\nOr, you might even test out a new video game to see if you like it!\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:52.000\nSo, tests help us learn and make decisions. They give us information we didn't have before. They can be simple or complicated, but they all have the same goal: to give us answers.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:54.000\nThat\u2019s testing in a nutshell!\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:56.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
