    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_062043.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:18.100\nNow, a test, at its most basic, is just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like an experiment, but often with a specific right or wrong answer.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:27.500\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\nWhen you taste a new food to see if you like it, that's a test!\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:38.400\nOr, if you try a different route to school to see if it's faster, you're running a test.\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:48.000\nIn science, tests can prove or disprove an idea.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:57.600\nA simple example is baking a cake: you're testing your recipe!\nIf it tastes good, you passed the test!\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:03.500\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information and see if something is true or works as expected.\n01:03.500 --> 01:06.300\nIt's all about learning and finding things out!\n01:06.300 --> 01:13.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
