    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:04.000\nWhat is a test, really?\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:06.100\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:10.000\nThink of it like this: you test a lightbulb to see if it works, right?\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:13.700\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:17.200\nThey're a way to check your knowledge on a specific subject.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:22.200\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve problems to see if you understand addition or subtraction.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:27.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.200\nYou taste the batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:31.800\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:37.000\nSo, tests are everywhere, helping us learn and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:45.300\nBasically, a test is just a way to check something, whether it's your understanding of a topic, or the sweetness of cake batter.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:48.200\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:50.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
