    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_063629.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.900\nNot the kind you stress about in school, but the kind that helps us figure things out.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:17.800\nBasically, a test is just a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your toy car is working,\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:25.900\nso you put batteries in it and turn it on.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:28.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:31.800\nOr, maybe you want to know if an apple is ripe.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:34.900\nYou might squeeze it gently \u2013 that's another test!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:37.200\nYou're testing its ripeness.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:40.000\nTests can be simple, like that, or more complicated.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:43.800\nBut the idea is always the same: to get information about something.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:51.700\nSo, to recap: A test is a way to check something and get information.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:57.900\nWe use them all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:01.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
