  "8cd1c002-a41a-4f8b-bc80-dbfa3ff234d9": {
    "id": "8cd1c002-a41a-4f8b-bc80-dbfa3ff234d9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:35:33.866423",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T06:40:27.281355",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_064027.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_064027.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.000\nNow, you've probably taken a test before, whether it's in school or online, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well something works.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:30.300\nThink of it like this: if you want to see if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:39.200\nOr, if you want to know if you understand a new math problem, you might try solving it yourself. That's also a test!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:44.900\nTests aren't just about grades or scores. They help us learn and improve.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:55.400\nThey show us what we already know and what we still need to work on. So, remember, a test is just a tool to help us understand and grow.\n\n00:55.400 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5de4f8d1-4df8-4221-83ea-7d6a733f87df": {
    "id": "5de4f8d1-4df8-4221-83ea-7d6a733f87df",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:35:34.486501",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T06:41:11.287180",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_064111.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_064111.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:23.300\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see what we get.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:33.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy. A teacher uses tests to see how well you've learned something.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:42.700\nThe main idea behind a test is to ask a question, or a series of questions, and then look at the answers to learn something new.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:50.700\nFor example, a simple taste test can tell you if you like a new food. Or a spelling test can show you which words you need to practice.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:56.900\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal. But they all have the same goal: to learn something!\n\n00:56.900 --> 00:59.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to explore and discover.\n```"
  },
