    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:30.500\nThink of it like this: a teacher might give you a test in school to see how much you've learned about a subject.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:45.500\nOr, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it's safe and effective. Basically, a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:47.200\nIt could be a written exam, a practical demonstration, or even a simple observation.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:48.900\nFor example, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by screwing it in and turning it on!\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:49.600\nSee?\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:50.600\nSimple!\n\n00:50.600 --> 01:03.500\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to check knowledge, performance, or functionality. It helps us understand things better and make informed choices.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:06.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
