    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_064505.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:11.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:19.900\nIt's like asking a question, but instead of just asking, you're doing something to get the answer.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:28.500\nThink about it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:34.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is probably ready.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:40.300\nAnother example? A doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:49.200\nOr, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:53.700\nSo, tests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:59.100\nThey help us understand things better, whether it's about a cake, your health, or even your spelling.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.200\nUltimately, tests are a valuable tool for learning\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:05.400\nand making informed decisions.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:07.800\nApilage AI.\n```"
