    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_064713.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:13.200\nWhat are they, and why do we take them? Simply put, a test is a way to check your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:21.600\nThink of it like this: you\u2019ve been learning about apples, and a test would ask you questions to see if you understand apples.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:29.700\nTests can come in many forms. It might be a multiple-choice quiz, where you pick the right answer from a few choices.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:40.300\nOr maybe it\u2019s a written test where you answer questions in your own words. Sometimes it\u2019s even a practical test, like showing someone how to ride a bike.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:49.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. A math test checks if you can solve math problems.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:58.600\nThe goal isn\u2019t to trick you, but to see what you've learned. So, to recap, a test is a tool used to measure what you know or can do.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:05.600\nIt helps you and your teachers understand your strengths and where you might need a little more practice.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:09.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
