    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.300\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:32.200\nThe basic idea is to present something, and then see how it responds.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.800\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:42.600\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's your test.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:51.900\nIf the light comes on, great! If not, the bulb might be broken. Another example is a taste test.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:58.400\nYou try a new flavor of ice cream. Your reaction \u2013 whether you like it or not \u2013 is the result of the test.\n\n00:58.400 --> 01:02.100\nSo, a test is just a way of gathering information.\n```"
