    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_065648.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works. Think of it like checking your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:24.600\nThere are all sorts of tests. You might take a math test at school to see how well you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:32.900\nOr, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and reliable before selling it to the public.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:44.400\nFor example, you might test your knowledge of colors by naming them as someone points to them. Or, you could test a toy car by seeing how far it can roll.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:53.800\nThese are simple ways to understand how tests work. So, remember, a test is just a method for checking something.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:04.000\nIt could be your knowledge, a product's quality, or anything else you want to evaluate. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
