    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_070101.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:18.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process we use to gather information and see how well something performs, or understand its qualities.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:25.800\nThink about it like this: a taste test for ice cream! You're testing to see which flavor you like best.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:33.200\nOr, imagine a spelling test at school. That test helps show how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:45.800\nAnother example could be testing a new toy to see if it works the way it should. Tests can be formal, like exams, or informal, like trying a new recipe.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:58.800\nThe main idea is that we're trying to learn something by doing something. So, in a nutshell, a test is an activity designed to gather information or evaluate performance.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:05.800\nIt helps us learn and understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
