    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_070548.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:13.600\nThink of a test like a way to check something.\nWe want to find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:20.200\nFor example, imagine you bake a cake.\nYou might use a toothpick test to see if it's done.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:28.100\nYou poke the cake with a toothpick, and if it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\nIt's ready!\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:36.800\nAnother example is a lightbulb.\nTo test if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:47.500\nSo, a test is simply a method to see if something meets a certain standard or performs as expected.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:54.600\nIt helps us understand if something is good to go.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
