    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.210 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.900\nThink of a test as a way to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:24.300\nIt's like a little quiz to check your knowledge. The basic idea is simple: you get questions, and you answer them.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:35.900\nYour answers are then compared to the correct answers to see how many you got right.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:48.500\nFor example, if you're learning about animals, a test might ask you \"What sound does a dog make?\" or \"What does a cat eat?\".\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:59.900\nAnswering these questions correctly shows you understand the material. So, tests help you and your teachers figure out what you know and what you might need to work on a bit more.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.300\nThey're just a tool to help you learn better.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:06.900\nTo recap, a test is a tool to check your understanding,\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:11.500\nusing questions and answers to see how well you've learned something.\n\n01:11.500 --> 01:14.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
