    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_074836.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:04.200\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:07.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:12.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookie is done baking, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:13.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:17.100\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\nThe cookie passes the test!\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:22.500\nAnother example: your doctor gives you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.900\nThey ask you to read letters on a chart.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:28.500\nIf you can read them clearly, you pass the vision test!\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:36.500\nSo, basically, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something, and it gives us information we can use to make decisions.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:42.600\nWhether it's a cookie, your eyesight, or anything else, tests help us understand the world around us a little bit better.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
