    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:36.000\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. For example, your doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:42.600\nTests can be written, like a quiz, or they can be physical, like a blood test.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:49.500\nThe important thing is they give us information.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:56.400\nLet's say you want to know if a plant needs water. You can test it by poking your finger in the soil.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:07.800\nIf it's dry, the plant probably needs water! If it's wet, it's likely doing just fine.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:14.200\nSo, in short, a test is a tool to help us learn something new or confirm something we suspect.\n\n01:14.200 --> 01:17.000\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n01:17.000 --> 01:23.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
