    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.600\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you do a simple test \u2013 you poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:33.100\nIf it comes out clean, the cookies pass the test! In science, math, or even everyday life, we use tests to see if something is true, correct, or working properly.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:42.900\nFor example, your doctor might run tests to check your health. Or, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:54.600\nThese tests help us understand things better and make sure everything is as it should be. So, tests are like checkpoints, helping us confirm information.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:05.400\nIn short, a test is a way to verify something. It can be as simple as poking a cookie or as complex as running a scientific experiment.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:13.000\nThey all serve the same purpose: to check and confirm. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
