    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:36:30.064921",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T07:52:53.829402",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_075253.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_075253.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:10.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind in school, but the kind that checks if something works.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:21.800\nBasically, a test is a way to see if something does what it's supposed to do. Think of it like this: you have a new lightbulb, and you want to make sure it lights up.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:27.800\nThe test is simply screwing it into a lamp and flipping the switch. Does it light up?\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:30.400\nYes? Then the test passed!\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:38.000\nAnother example: imagine you bake a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:43.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's a test!\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:54.600\nSo, to recap, a test is just a simple way to confirm something is working correctly. It\u2019s all about checking to see if we get the expected result.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:58.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3e26559b-4186-46af-9253-f7c2e5bbf562": {
    "id": "3e26559b-4186-46af-9253-f7c2e5bbf562",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:36:30.751823",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T07:53:50.650328",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_075350.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_075350.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:12.200\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:20.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:29.600\nIt's a method of measuring or checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or if it's working correctly.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:39.100\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:48.800\nA taste test checks if you like the flavor of something. Or, maybe your doctor gives you a physical exam \u2013 that\u2019s a test to check your overall health.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:58.400\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal. The important thing is that they provide information. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:58.400 --> 00:59.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn and check something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
