    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.000\nThink of it like asking a question,\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:09.000\nbut instead of just getting an answer,\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:10.500\nyou're getting proof.\n\n00:10.500 --> 00:12.000\nTests are used everywhere!\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:15.500\nImagine you're baking a cake. You test if it's done\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:18.000\nby sticking a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean,\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:19.000\nthat's a successful test!\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.000\nOr, think about learning a new skill. A quiz in class is a test\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:25.000\nto see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:27.000\nAnother example? A doctor might run tests\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.000\nto see if you're healthy. They might check your temperature\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:32.000\nor blood pressure.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.000\nAll of these are different types of tests,\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:37.000\nbut they all have the same goal:\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:40.000\nto gather information and see if something is true.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:46.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a method used to determine something. It's a way of\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:49.000\ngetting solid evidence to answer a question.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
