    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_080341.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\nThink of it as asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:23.700\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:28.900\nThat's a test!\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:32.500\nIf it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:37.800\nSee?\nA question and an answer.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:43.700\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\nEach time you try, you're testing your balance.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:52.800\nIf you stay upright, great!\nIf you fall, you adjust and try again.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:00.800\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\nIt's a simple concept that helps us understand the world around us.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e7d1b769-1729-4339-a809-49304a8dfd8b": {
    "id": "e7d1b769-1729-4339-a809-49304a8dfd8b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:36:38.703376",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T08:04:36.421626",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_080436.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_080436.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:12.500\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:15.000\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:18.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:23.100\nThat's a test! If it lights up, great. If not, it's probably broken.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:27.500\nAnother example? Imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:31.100\nYou taste it to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:34.700\nThat's a test too! You're testing the flavor.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:44.500\nWe use tests all the time to learn and improve things. Basically, a test is a question, and the result tells you the answer.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:56.000\nSo, a test is a method to determine the characteristics or capabilities of something, or to see if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
