  "4e667d26-beca-4029-bac7-c0b0f5a9cbf7": {
    "id": "4e667d26-beca-4029-bac7-c0b0f5a9cbf7",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:36:42.867432",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T08:10:41.146246",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_081040.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_081040.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:11.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:19.600\nThink of it like this: it's a tool we use to check your understanding.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:28.300\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:37.000\nIt could be answering questions on a piece of paper, like in a math quiz.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:48.900\nOr it could be showing someone you can ride a bike. The goal is always the same: to see what you've learned or what skills you've developed.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:57.000\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. A cooking test might check if you can follow a recipe. So, remember, a test is just a way to see what you know and can do. It helps you and others understand your progress. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
