    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_081423.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.230 --> 00:04.930\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.930 --> 00:11.230\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:11.230 --> 00:15.630\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:15.630 --> 00:18.130\nThink of it like this: you want to see if a light bulb works,\n\n00:18.130 --> 00:21.230\nso you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:21.230 --> 00:22.830\nThat's a test!\n\n00:22.830 --> 00:25.230\nYou're testing if the light bulb is functional.\n\n00:25.230 --> 00:28.630\nTests aren't just for light bulbs though.\n\n00:28.630 --> 00:31.230\nA doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.230 --> 00:34.430\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:34.430 --> 00:38.030\nThey all work the same way: they're a way to gather information.\n\n00:38.030 --> 00:40.330\nAnother example?\n\n00:40.330 --> 00:41.530\nBaking a cake!\n\n00:41.530 --> 00:45.630\nYou test if it\u2019s done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:45.630 --> 00:48.030\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:48.030 --> 00:55.030\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get information.\nIt can be used for almost anything!\n\n00:55.030 --> 00:59.530\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
