    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_081612.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.600\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:33.400\nIt helps us understand what we've learned or what we need to work on.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:36.500\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:39.600\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:43.200\nYou might test it with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:44.900\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:45.900\nGreat!\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:47.700\nThe cake is done.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:54.900\nSo, tests can be used in lots of different ways, from school to cooking, and even to see if your new phone is working properly.\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:57.200\nBasically, a test helps us confirm something or learn something new.\n```"
  },
