    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_081841.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nWhat are they, and why do we take them? Simply put, a test is a way to check your knowledge or skills on a specific topic.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like a quick way to see how much you've learned. For example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:33.500\nA math test might ask you to solve problems you've been practicing. A test isn't about tricking you; it's just about seeing what you understand.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:44.800\nTests can come in different forms, like multiple-choice questions where you pick the best answer, or short answer questions where you write a brief response.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:56.600\nNo matter the format, the goal is the same: to show what you know. So, remember, a test is just a tool to measure your understanding. Don't be afraid of them!\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:01.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
