    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_083142.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something. It could be a person, an object, or even an idea.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: a baking test. You taste the batter before baking to see if it needs more sugar. That's a test!\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:28.100\nOr, maybe your doctor checks your temperature when you're sick. That's also a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:39.200\nTests can be written, like a quiz at school, or hands-on, like trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:49.400\nThe important thing is that they give us data or clues to understand something better. So, a test is basically a tool to learn and explore.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:53.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
