    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_083457.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:09.000\nnot the kind you stress about in school,\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:13.000\nbut the kind used to check if something works.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:17.000\nBasically, a test is just a way to find out if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.000\nThink about it like this: you get a new lightbulb and you screw it in.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.000\nThe test is whether the light turns on.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:27.000\nOr, if you're baking a cake, the test is whether it tastes good!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.000\nIt's all about seeing if the expected result actually happens.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:36.000\nWe use tests every day without even realizing it.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:41.000\nFrom checking if your phone is charged to making sure your shoelaces are tied,\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:42.000\nwe're constantly testing things.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.000\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to check if something works correctly.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:52.000\nIt's about comparing what you expect to happen with what actually happens.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:54.000\nThis video was created by\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:55.000\nApilage AI.\n```"
