    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE\nAll timings are approximate due to the dynamic nature of speech.\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:07.000\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:12.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:16.700\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:21.300\nThink about it like this: You might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.800\nOr maybe a doctor runs a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:27.400\nThose are both examples of tests!\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:32.800\nAnother example is testing a recipe. You follow the instructions and \"test\" to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:36.500\nIf it doesn\u2019t, you might adjust the ingredients.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:45.000\nSo, a test helps us understand something better, whether it's our knowledge, our health, or even our cooking skills.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:47.300\nIt\u2019s all about finding out information.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:51.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
