    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_085328.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:27.400\nTests help us understand if something works, or if we know something. For example, a spelling test shows us how well we know our spelling words.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:33.500\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar. That's a test too!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:36.800\nAnother example? A doctor might run some tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:43.600\nTests are all about gathering information. So, to recap: a test is a process designed to evaluate or understand something.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:58.200\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, from baking to spelling, and they help us learn and improve.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:01.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
