  "020909f8-9d57-44d3-aa14-c6ae3c4f1ca4": {
    "id": "020909f8-9d57-44d3-aa14-c6ae3c4f1ca4",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:37:20.989795",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:36.482705",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_090036.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_090036.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE\nAll timestamps are approximate due to the dynamic nature of animation.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like this: you might test if a cake is done by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:36.500\nOr, you might test if your toy car needs new batteries by trying to drive it. If it barely moves, that's a test showing you need new power.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:43.400\nTests aren\u2019t just for cake or cars. Scientists use tests to see if their ideas are right.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:52.900\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's making you sick. Basically, a test is a way to check something and learn more about it.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:01.600\nSo, a test is just a way to ask a question and see what the answer is, helping us learn about the world around us.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "72e73460-172b-4d57-95de-8b70106ea177": {
    "id": "72e73460-172b-4d57-95de-8b70106ea177",
