  "76321d9b-c030-439c-a99e-28ca7de8c693": {
    "id": "76321d9b-c030-439c-a99e-28ca7de8c693",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:37:25.317878",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:07:01.440472",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_090701.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_090701.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:04.900\nWhat is a test anyway?\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It could be finding out if you know your multiplication tables, or if a cake is done baking, or even if a new medicine works.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:24.800\nBasically, we perform an action, and then we observe the result. The action is the 'test', and the result gives us information.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:29.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you can spell words correctly.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:34.800\nYou write down the words, and your score tells you how well you did.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:38.600\nAnother example?\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:44.400\nImagine you're checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:48.700\nIf it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:51.600\nIf it doesn't, the bulb is probably broken.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:59.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a method we use to get information by doing something and seeing what happens.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
