    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_090756.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in this case, a test is really just a way to see if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb lights up when you flip the switch.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:33.000\nThat's a simple test! So, the main idea is this: you have something you want to check, and you perform an action or look for a specific result to see if it passes the test.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:44.700\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:52.000\nAnother example: You have a new toy. The test is: Does it turn on when you press the power button?\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.300\nIf it does, it passes! So, a test is just a simple way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:05.300\nRemember, look for a specific result after you do something. That's your test!\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:08.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
