    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_091710.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:22.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:28.400\nThe toothpick is the test! The main goal of a test is to give you information.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:34.200\nIt could be about the quality of a product, the knowledge someone has, or even how well a system is working.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.000\nLet's look at some examples. A doctor gives you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:48.500\nA teacher gives you an exam to see what you've learned. And a company might test a new phone to make sure it doesn't break easily.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:52.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a process used to gather information.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:56.000\nIt helps us understand something better and make informed decisions.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "cbd42090-1874-43e2-bd57-566c5326d9e4": {
    "id": "cbd42090-1874-43e2-bd57-566c5326d9e4",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:37:32.387201",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:18:00.531165",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_091800.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_091800.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question to see if you know the answer, or trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:28.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. For example, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:34.000\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. See? Checking something!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:40.400\nAnother example could be testing a new toy to see if it works properly.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:43.100\nDoes it light up? Does it make the right sounds? That's a test!\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:51.200\nSo, in short, a test is a process or procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:51.200 --> 01:03.200\nIt helps us figure out if something is correct, working, or meeting certain standards. We use them all the time, often without even realizing it!\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:06.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a9d70185-b735-4ecb-a2b7-8c8f3ab64f53": {
