    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_092352.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nHey there, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:13.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, think of it as a way to check something, to see if it works or if it's correct.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:20.700\nIt's like checking if your cookies are baked enough. You might poke one with a toothpick \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:25.900\nOr maybe you're testing your knowledge for a school quiz. That's a test too!\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:32.200\nAnother example could be testing if a lightbulb works by plugging it in. Does it light up?\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:35.000\nYes? Then it passes the test!\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:44.100\nSo, a test is simply an action we take to evaluate something. It helps us understand if things are working the way they should.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:46.900\nSimple, right?\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:49.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9507de1a-4eb7-45e2-99df-925aad8ade3c": {
    "id": "9507de1a-4eb7-45e2-99df-925aad8ade3c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:37:38.327370",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:24:39.781016",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_092439.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_092439.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.500\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in general, a test is just a way to check if something is working the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: you\u2019re baking a cake, and you want to make sure it\u2019s done. You might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:30.100\nThat toothpick is your test! If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:36.500\nOr imagine you're trying to turn on a light. The test is simple: you flip the switch.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:42.400\nIf the light comes on, the test passed! If it doesn't, something is wrong.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:51.800\nSo, a test is really just a way of asking a question and seeing what the answer is. It helps us make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:55.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
