    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_092533.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:27.200\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You plug it in \u2013 that\u2019s the test \u2013 and seeing if it lights up tells you if the bulb is good or not.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:38.100\nIn school, a test helps your teacher understand what you've learned about a certain subject.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:42.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:47.700\nOr, a math test shows if you understand how to solve problems.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:52.500\nTests aren't scary! They're just tools to help us learn and grow.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:56.100\nThey show us what we already know and where we might need some extra help.\n\n00:56.100 --> 00:59.700\nSo next time you take a test, remember it's just a way of checking things, like checking if that lightbulb shines bright.\n```"
