    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_092624.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true, but in the world of science and computers, a test is simply a way of checking if something is working as expected.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:29.200\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and you test it by sticking a toothpick in. If it comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:32.700\nOr imagine you\u2019re building a robot.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:40.900\nYou might test its arm by making it lift a small weight. If it lifts the weight, the arm passes the test.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:51.900\nSo, a test is just a method to see if something meets a certain requirement or standard. It helps us find problems and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:59.200\nIt's a fundamental part of learning and building things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
