    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, it's a way to check if something works, or to see what something is like.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it like this: You might test the temperature of your bath water to make sure it's not too hot or too cold.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:28.600\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:38.700\nTests can be simple or complex. A quick taste test of your food is a simple test. A more complex test might involve using special equipment to measure something very precisely.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:47.700\nFor example, a baker tests their oven to make sure it's baking evenly. A student takes a test to show what they've learned.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:54.400\nThe important thing is that a test gives us information. It helps us understand something better.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:06.500\nSo, in short, a test is a way of checking or evaluating something. It provides valuable information to help us make decisions or learn new things.\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:10.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
