    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_092818.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:19.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:26.400\nIt's how we check if something is working, or if we understand something, or even if we know something.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:33.600\nThink about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:45.500\nOr, a doctor might give you a blood test to check if you're healthy. Even baking a cake is a kind of test!\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:51.900\nYou're testing your recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:58.300\nSo, tests can be formal, like exams, or informal, like trying out a new game.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:02.500\nThe key is they help us learn and improve.\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:05.500\nThey give us information we didn't have before.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:09.100\nRemember, tests aren't always about right or wrong answers, they're about learning.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:19.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
