    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_093115.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:24.700\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a physical test to check your health.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:32.200\nOr, you might take a quiz at school \u2013 that's a test to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:41.000\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\nSome are quick and easy, like a simple yes or no question.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:50.700\nOthers can be long and complex, like a science experiment.\nThe key thing is that they help us learn something new.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:01.600\nFor example, a taste test helps us figure out which flavor we like best.\nA test of strength tells us how much weight we can lift.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information.\nIt helps us learn, understand, and make better decisions.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
