    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_093209.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:07.100\nIn simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer, you're also getting some kind of proof.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.400\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:20.400\nThat test helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:26.800\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might test the cake with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:30.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that means the cake is ready!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:41.900\nSo, whether it's a quiz in class, checking if your food is cooked, or even a scientist running an experiment, they're all using tests to get information and learn something new.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:45.200\nTests are all about finding things out!\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:56.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
