    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:37:50.221840",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:41:47.584880",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_094147.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_094147.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.400\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works correctly.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:22.800\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works.\nThe test is screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:33.900\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:36.200\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:43.000\nAnother example?\nImagine you're baking cookies.\nYou can test if they're done by poking one with a toothpick.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:47.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, they're ready!\nThat's a test too.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:58.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is working the way it should.\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it!\n\n00:58.000 --> 00:59.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
