    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.200\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests, which are basically just ways to find out if something is working correctly.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:16.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:28.600\nThat flip of the switch is your test! Tests can be simple, like checking if your shoelaces are tied, or more complicated, like a doctor running blood work.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:41.000\nIt all boils down to performing an action and seeing if the result is what you expect. For example, a baker might taste their cake batter before baking to test if it has enough sugar.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:47.900\nOr, before sending an email, you might read it over to test for any spelling mistakes.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:54.600\nSee? Tests are everywhere! So, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something does what it\u2019s supposed to do.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:58.800\nIt's all about performing an action and checking the result.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:05.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
