    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_100025.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:19.900\nThink of it like this: you're trying to turn on a light. You flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:24.100\nYou're testing if the lightbulb works. If the light comes on, the test passed.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:28.300\nIf it doesn't, the test failed.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.000\nAnother example? Maybe you\u2019re baking a cake. You taste the batter. That's a test!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:37.600\nYou're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:40.600\nSo, a test is really just a way of checking something.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:43.600\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly,\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:57.300\nor if it meets a certain standard. We use tests to learn, to improve things, and to make sure things are safe and reliable.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
