    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_100325.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.900\nA test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well something is doing.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:21.400\nThink of it like this: you test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:28.300\nIn other areas, a test could be anything from a quiz at school to checking if your car's brakes work.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:37.500\nA quiz tests your knowledge, while checking your brakes tests their functionality. Another example is testing a lightbulb.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:41.700\nYou turn it on. If it lights up, the test passes. If it doesn\u2019t, it fails.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:49.000\nTests help us find problems and make sure things are safe and reliable.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:58.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. It could be knowledge, functionality, or anything else!\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
