    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:38:20.828082",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T10:15:52.550810",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_101552.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_101552.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:23.400\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer. Think of it like this: You might test if your cookies are done baking by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:30.600\nOr, you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp. These are all little tests!\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:37.200\nAnother example is when a doctor checks your temperature. That's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:48.200\nTests aren't just for science or school; they're everywhere! So, remember, a test helps us gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:56.200\nWe use tests all the time to understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
