    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_101725.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_101725.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:24.600\nIt helps us see if something works the way it's supposed to, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:33.500\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nA food taste test checks if people like the flavor of a new recipe.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:42.400\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health. Tests can be big or small, simple or complex.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:55.000\nThe important thing is that they give us information. They help us understand something better and make decisions based on what we learn.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:57.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it works or meets a standard.\n```"
  },
