    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_101810.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:30.400\nFor example, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:36.100\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:41.300\nSee? Different things, but both are tests.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:50.500\nAnother example? You might test if your bike brakes are working before you ride. You squeeze the handles and see if the bike stops. That's a test too!\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:54.000\nSo, remember, a test is a way to gather information or check something. It helps us understand things better.\n```"
