    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_102035.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nHey there, welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:04.400\nEver wondered what a test actually is?\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:08.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:13.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, right?\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:16.200\nSo, you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:16.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:19.400\nThe toothpick is testing the cake.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:24.200\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. The first few wobbly rides?\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:25.800\nThose are tests!\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:28.700\nYou're testing your balance and coordination.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:32.300\nTests help us understand, learn, and improve.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:37.600\nThey can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your coffee is hot enough.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:40.500\nThe main point is, they give us information.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.500\nSo, a test is just a way of finding something out.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:56.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "458d8de3-5262-4036-a1f0-ff0bec8a141b": {
    "id": "458d8de3-5262-4036-a1f0-ff0bec8a141b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:38:24.550505",
