    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_102126.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. It's like asking a question, but instead of just listening to the answer, we're looking for proof.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:23.000\nThink about it. When you bake a cake, you might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:32.700\nThe toothpick coming out clean is the proof. Or, if you're buying a new phone, you might test the camera by taking a picture.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:39.200\nThe picture quality is your proof of how good the camera is. Tests are used everywhere!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:50.300\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even scientists use tests to see if their ideas are right.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:59.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather evidence and find out something.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:03.400\nWhether it's a toothpick in a cake or a picture from a phone, it's all about finding the proof.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
