    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_103052.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:18.600\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. It's how we find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you taste it. That taste test is checking if the cake is good!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:32.200\nAnother example? A doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:48.900\nOr, when you're learning something new, a quiz is a test to see if you understand the material. Tests can be big and formal, like a final exam, or small and informal, like checking if your shoelaces are tied.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:59.000\nThe main thing is, they help us learn and improve! So, remember, a test is a check to see if something is working or true.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:05.600\nIt can be a taste, a quiz, or even a doctor's visit. Tests are all around us!\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:09.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
