    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:09.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you take in school, but how we check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like this: a test is just a simple way to see if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:18.000\nFor example, let's say you baked cookies. You might test them by taking a bite to see if they taste good.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:24.000\nOr, if you're building a tower of blocks, you might gently push it to test if it's stable.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:29.000\nTests help us find problems early, before they become bigger problems.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:35.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply checking if something works as expected.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:42.000\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:48.000\nThey help us make sure things are safe, reliable, and just plain good!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:53.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
