    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_103718.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: a test.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like a friendly check-up for your brain or maybe even a new gadget.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:34.500\nSo, how does it work? Well, you're usually given a set of questions or tasks.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:48.200\nFor example, in a math test, you might have to solve equations. Or, if you're testing a new toy, you might see if it can withstand being dropped a few times.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:52.900\nThe answers or the results of the tasks are then compared to a standard or an expected outcome.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:06.200\nDid you get the math problems right? Did the toy survive the drop? These comparisons tell us how well you performed or how well the thing being tested performed.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:12.700\nIn short, a test helps us measure knowledge, skills, or the quality of something.\n\n01:12.700 --> 01:19.100\nIt\u2019s a tool for learning and improvement.\n\n01:19.100 --> 01:25.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
