    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_104249.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:31.600\nYour test is to screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:37.100\nIf it lights up, the test is passed! If it doesn't, then the test failed.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:42.600\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs, though. We use them all the time.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:48.100\nA doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:53.600\nA teacher uses tests to see if you understand the material.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:02.300\nEven bakers test their cake batter to make sure it's ready to bake.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:11.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a procedure to determine if something is working correctly or if a statement is true.\n\n01:11.000 --> 01:17.600\nIt's a simple but powerful way to check things out.\n\n01:17.600 --> 01:19.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
