    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:38:47.692216",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T10:50:23.730681",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_105023.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_105023.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:18.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is, or trying something out and seeing what happens.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:26.000\nThink about it like this: If you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick test to see if it's done.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:38.200\nYou poke the toothpick in, and if it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down is part of the test.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:52.200\nYou're testing your balance and learning what works. Tests can be big and formal, like school exams, or small and informal, like tasting a new recipe to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:02.400\nThe important thing is that they help us learn and understand things better. So, a test is simply a check to see if something is working or true.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:06.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3f7489df-afa5-433d-8c37-8a8c87cfe125": {
    "id": "3f7489df-afa5-433d-8c37-8a8c87cfe125",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
