    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_105110.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:33.700\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good. Or when you push a door, you're testing if it's open or closed.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:43.700\nIn school, tests help us understand how well you've learned something. They can be multiple choice, short answer, or even a project!\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:53.000\nThe goal is to see what you know and where you might need some extra help.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:56.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding out information. It's like asking a question and looking for the answer. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "524a9600-5844-46db-8b0d-a80433aae571": {
    "id": "524a9600-5844-46db-8b0d-a80433aae571",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
