    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_105245.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, where you try something out to see what happens.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:20.400\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Well, lots!\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:25.600\nYou can test if a lightbulb works by turning it on. That's a test.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:31.800\nOr, a doctor might test your reflexes by tapping your knee. That's another test.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:42.000\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing your recipe to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:52.100\nTests help us understand the world around us. They give us information and help us make better decisions.\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:05.800\nBasically, if you want to know something for sure, a test can help you find out. In short, a test is a simple way to try something and see what the result is.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.400\nWhether it\u2019s a lightbulb, your knee, or a cake, tests are all about gathering information.\n\n01:09.400 --> 01:13.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
