  "8976ded5-4343-4d67-9f25-c4d131cb9d52": {
    "id": "8976ded5-4343-4d67-9f25-c4d131cb9d52",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:38:50.973380",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T10:54:20.227541",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_105420.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_105420.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: you might taste a cake to test if it's sweet enough. In science and many other fields, tests help us prove or disprove an idea.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:39.800\nWe create a controlled situation, the test, and observe what happens. For example, you might test if a plant grows faster in sunlight versus shade.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:50.100\nYou'd put one plant in the sun and one in the shade, then measure their growth. The results, or how much they grew, help you decide if your idea, that sunlight helps plants grow faster, is likely true.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:58.900\nSo, a test is a process to gather information and see if something is true or not. It's all about finding answers!\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
