    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_110138.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:06.340\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.340 --> 00:9.780\nIt's a process we use to gather information\n\n00:09.780 --> 00:11.340\nand see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:11.340 --> 00:17.220\nThink about it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might do a simple test.\n\n00:17.220 --> 00:19.960\nYou stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:19.960 --> 00:22.630\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:22.630 --> 00:28.560\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. You might test your balance by slowly lifting your feet.\n\n00:28.560 --> 00:32.910\nEach wobbly moment is a mini-test, showing you how well you're doing.\n\n00:32.910 --> 00:35.160\nSo, a test is a way of checking something.\n\n00:35.160 --> 00:41.000\nIt can be a quiz in school, a science experiment, or even just trying something new to see what happens.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:44.540\nIt's all about learning and gathering information.\n\n00:44.540 --> 00:47.680\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
