    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of a test.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:21.500\nIt could be to see if you understand a topic, like in school, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a light bulb works.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:29.900\nSo, you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:34.600\nThe light turning on means the test passed.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:42.000\nOr, maybe you take a quiz in class to see how well you understand the material. That quiz is a test too!\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:46.700\nIt shows you, and your teacher, what you've learned.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:54.900\nTests can come in many forms, from simple questions to complex experiments. The important thing is that they help us learn and improve.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:02.300\nSo remember, a test is just a way to find things out.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
