    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_110846.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:19.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you use a toothpick to test them.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.600\nThe toothpick comes out clean? Great! The test tells you they're ready.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:33.800\nIn school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:42.500\nAnd in science, tests are used to prove or disprove ideas, like testing if a new medicine actually works.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:54.200\nFor example, a taste test helps decide which ice cream flavor is the most popular. Or, a simple spelling test shows which words you know how to spell.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:02.700\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and seeing where things stand. They help us learn and improve.\n\n01:02.700 --> 01:07.800\nIn short, a test is just a way of checking to see if something is true, correct, or working as expected.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:11.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
