  "1cd3b2bf-224f-4045-a38f-bc57ba9c9c83": {
    "id": "1cd3b2bf-224f-4045-a38f-bc57ba9c9c83",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:39:11.424235",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T11:17:23.983554",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_111723.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_111723.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.600\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something or someone.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:22.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:29.300\nThat's a test! It helps you decide if the cake needs more time in the oven.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:38.200\nIn everyday life, tests are everywhere. A doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:47.100\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:57.300\nThe results of the test give us information. For example, if the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. If your blood test shows low iron, you might need to eat more spinach.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:03.100\nTests help us make decisions based on evidence. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get information.\n```"
  },
