    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_112145.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in general, a test is just a way to find out if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch \u2013 that's a simple test! Or, checking if your recipe tastes good.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:35.400\nThe main idea is to create a situation where you can observe the result. If the light bulb lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:42.400\nSame with your recipe, if it tastes great, the test passes. If not, you need to adjust something.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:50.600\nTests help us make sure things are reliable and working as expected.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:62.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something, see the result, and make improvements. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
