    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_112642.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test is.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:19.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're collecting information to understand something better.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:29.400\nTests can be anything from a simple quiz at school, to checking if a lightbulb works, or even trying a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:39.000\nThe key is that you're performing an action and observing the result. For example, a spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:50.400\nOr, if you're baking a cake, tasting it is a test to see if you need more sugar. So, a test is all about learning and gathering information.\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:00.200\nIt helps us understand things better by trying something out and seeing what happens. Remember, testing is how we learn and improve!\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:03.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
