    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_113714.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:03.500\nToday we're diving into something super important: Tests!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:04.900\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:07.000\nSimply put, it's a way to check something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:10.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done.\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:13.000\nYou poke it with a fork \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:16.700\nOr maybe you want to see if you know your ABCs.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:18.700\nSomeone asks you to recite them \u2013 that's a test too.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:23.200\nTests help us understand if something works, if we've learned something, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:27.600\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:31.800\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to test what you've learned in class.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:35.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:39.700\nIt helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:41.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ece9c461-a94c-4a8c-a890-f25fb8d95f51": {
    "id": "ece9c461-a94c-4a8c-a890-f25fb8d95f51",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:39:28.488793",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T11:38:15.725782",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_113815.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_113815.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.100\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school exams. A test, in a general sense, is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:24.100\nThink of it like this: you test if your shoes fit before you buy them, right? You try them on!\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:35.000\nOr, you might test if your recipe is good by tasting the food as you cook. In the world of science and engineering, tests are super important.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:42.200\nImagine you're building a bridge. You'd want to test the materials to make sure they're strong enough to hold the weight.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:49.600\nOr if you're writing a computer program, you'd test it to make sure it does what it's supposed to do without crashing.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:57.000\nSo, a test is really just a way to see if something works correctly. It helps us find problems and make things better.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "03e4dcc5-d2e7-4a2c-a0c6-f25d7962ed31": {
    "id": "03e4dcc5-d2e7-4a2c-a0c6-f25d7962ed31",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
