    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_113911.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.300\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:20.500\nIt helps us understand if something is working, or if something is true.\nSo, how does it work?\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:32.100\nWell, we perform some action or observation, and then we look at the results.\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:42.300\nOr, you might take a practice test before a big exam to see how well you know the material.\nThe results of these tests give us information.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:45.900\nAnother example?\nThink about baking a cake.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:55.100\nYou taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\nBasically, a test is a simple way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:03.000\nRemember, it's all about finding out the answer to a question.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "b050eb91-e3a1-4c1a-b0ca-09679a898e7e": {
    "id": "b050eb91-e3a1-4c1a-b0ca-09679a898e7e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:39:29.750885",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T11:40:15.100441",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_114014.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_114014.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: Tests.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:19.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something, to see if it works or if it's true.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:29.700\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of water to see if it's hot enough for tea. Or, a doctor might give you a test to check your health.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:41.300\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand the material. For example, a math test might have questions to see if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:48.300\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:52.200\nRemember, tests aren't scary. They're just tools to help us learn and understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "8d601419-2d10-4921-91c4-e2c650f8cd42": {
    "id": "8d601419-2d10-4921-91c4-e2c650f8cd42",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:39:30.362380",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T11:41:24.617167",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_114124.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_114124.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:18.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information and see what someone knows or can do.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:31.400\nThink of it like a doctor checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\nIt could be a simple quiz in school, a driving test to get your license, or even a taste test to see which cookie is the yummiest!\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:43.700\nThe main idea is to use a specific set of questions or tasks to measure something.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:52.100\nFor example, a math test helps show how well you understand numbers and equations.\nA spelling test shows how well you know how to write words correctly.\nA cooking test might show how well you can follow a recipe.\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:04.500\nSo, to recap: a test is a tool for gathering information and measuring skills or knowledge.\nIt helps us understand where we are and what we might need to learn next.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:08.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
