    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_115331.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to see if something works or if something is true.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:33.800\nBasically, you're trying to find out if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:41.800\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:46.700\nOr a teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:57.700\nAnother example is testing a recipe. You follow the instructions, and then you test it by tasting it! Does it taste good? If so, the recipe passes the test.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something works, is true, or meets a standard.\n```"
