    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_115443.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, it's a way to check something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:19.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:27.100\nIn science and math, tests are more formal ways to find out if something is true or works as expected.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:39.600\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, in software, programmers run tests to make sure their code does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:56.300\nSo, tests help us learn and confirm things. They can be simple, like that cake test, or more complex, but the main idea is always the same: to get information and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:04.300\nIn short, tests help us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
