    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_120720.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something really fundamental: the test.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.200\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:19.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works. Your test?\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:26.400\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. If the light comes on, the test passed!\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:31.100\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:44.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's your test saying the cake is done. Essentially, a test is a procedure to determine if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:51.300\nIt\u2019s a way to gather information and make a decision. Simple, right?\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:55.900\nThat's testing in a nutshell!\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:57.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
