    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_121701.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:21.400\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:31.700\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a test at school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:41.500\nIn programming, we test our code to make sure it does what we expect it to do.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:54.000\nFor example, if you write a program that adds two numbers, you'd test it with different numbers to see if the answer is always right. If it's not, then you know there's a problem and you can fix it.\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:00.800\nSo, a test helps us prove that something works, or helps us find out what's wrong so we can make it better.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:07.600\nIt's all about gathering information. In short, tests are a method to gain insights.\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:13.200\nThey help us to verify the expected behaviour. Tests are everywhere!\n\n01:13.200 --> 01:16.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
