    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_121920.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. Think of it as a way to find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:20.000\nWe use tests all the time! Imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:25.400\nYou might stick a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean. That's a test!\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:34.700\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try restarting it. That's also a test to see if that fixes the problem.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:43.800\nTests can also be more formal, like a quiz in school. That quiz is testing your knowledge on a specific subject.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:52.900\nSo, basically, a test is any procedure designed to evaluate something. It\u2019s a way to get information.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:59.000\nSo, remember, tests are all about checking things. They help us understand if something is working, true, or correct.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
