    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_121959.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.000\nYou've probably taken a lot of them in school,\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:06.400\nbut what exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:09.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:11.300\nhow much you know or can do.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:14.300\nIt's like a snapshot of your knowledge or skills\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:15.500\nat a specific moment.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:19.400\nThink about it like this: a math test checks your\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:22.300\nunderstanding of numbers and equations.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:26.200\nA driving test shows whether you can safely operate a car.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:30.100\nEven baking a cake can be a test \u2013 did you follow\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:32.100\nthe recipe correctly and does it taste good?\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:35.600\nSo, tests help us measure things and see how we're progressing.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:39.500\nThey give us feedback and can point out areas where\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:41.700\nwe might need to learn more.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:44.900\nThey're not always fun, but they're a valuable\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:48.200\ntool for learning and improving.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:53.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
