    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_122059.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:12.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process we use to gather information.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:19.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\nYou use a toothpick, right?\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:28.300\nSticking it in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test.\nOr maybe you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.000\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.800\nTests aren't just for baking or lightbulbs.\nThey're everywhere!\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:43.600\nDoctors use tests to check your health.\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:49.600\nBasically, a test is any procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:49.600 --> 01:02.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a method for collecting information and evaluating something.\nIt helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:08.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
