    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_122232.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_122232.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:21.000\nA test, at its core, is simply a way to find out something. It's a procedure designed to evaluate or measure something, like your knowledge, your ability, or even the quality of a product.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. That's a test!\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:34.700\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson. That's a test, too!\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:48.700\nEven trying out a new recipe is a kind of test to see if you like it. Tests can be formal, like a standardized exam, or informal, like tasting a new flavor of ice cream.\n\n00:48.700 --> 01:01.400\nThe key is that you're gathering information and making a judgement based on the results. So, to recap, a test helps us evaluate or measure something to learn more about it.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:05.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
