    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:36.900\nIn science, we use tests all the time. We might test if a plant grows faster in sunlight or in shade. We do this by planting two plants, putting one in the sun, one in the shade, and then observing the results.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:43.300\nAnother example? Imagine you want to know if a new toy car is faster than your old one.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:49.400\nYou could race them both, and that's a test! You're testing which car is faster.\n\n00:49.400 --> 01:02.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find information. You ask a question, you set up a situation, and then you observe the results to get your answer.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:07.800\nPretty simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
