    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_123412.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:17.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something. Think of it like this: you learn about a topic, and a test helps you see if you understood it.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:27.200\nTests can come in all shapes and sizes. You might have a multiple-choice test, where you pick the best answer from a few options.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:37.400\nOr maybe a true or false test, where you decide if a statement is correct. Sometimes, you might even have to write out your answers.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:47.000\nFor example, if you're learning about animals, a test might ask you to name different types of birds, or what a lion eats.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:54.000\nThe goal is to show what you've learned. So, a test is just a tool to check your understanding.\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:02.100\nIt helps you and your teacher see what you've mastered and what you might need to work on.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.700\nRemember to study and do your best!\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:09.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
