    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:08.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:13.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:16.700\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:29.100\nTests help us measure things, like how well you understand a subject, or even how strong a material is.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:34.400\nFor example, a spelling test helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:41.500\nOr, engineers might test a bridge to make sure it can hold a lot of weight safely.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:49.700\nSo, tests come in many forms and they're used for lots of different things, but the main idea is always the same: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:52.300\nThey give us valuable insights.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:58.200\nIn summary, tests are tools for learning and measuring.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:01.400\nThey help us understand more about ourselves and the world around us.\n```"
  },
