    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.500\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:24.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:30.400\nIt's how we check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:35.900\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:43.900\nFor example, you might test if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:51.100\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:53.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:01.600\nThat's a test! Tests are used everywhere, from making sure your phone works to checking if a bridge is safe.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.800\nThey help us understand things better and make sure everything is running smoothly.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something.\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:13.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
