    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_124641.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.999\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.999 --> 00:15.600\nToday we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.599\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:23.599 --> 00:30.099\nIt's like checking your knowledge on a specific topic.\n\n00:30.099 --> 00:36.599\nThink of it like this: Imagine you're learning to bake a cake.\n\n00:36.599 --> 00:43.100\nThe test is tasting the cake to see if you followed the recipe correctly.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:46.600\nDid you add enough sugar?\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:49.500\nDid you bake it long enough?\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:55.699\nSimilarly, in school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned in class.\n\n00:55.699 --> 01:00.799\nFor example, a multiple-choice quiz is a type of test.\n\n01:00.799 --> 01:04.700\nSo is writing an essay, or even answering questions out loud.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:07.900\nThe goal is always the same: to show what you know.\n\n01:07.900 --> 01:13.400\nSo, tests are just tools to measure understanding.\n\n01:13.400 --> 01:17.500\nThey give you and your teachers valuable information.\n\n01:17.500 --> 01:21.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3ad123d8-52e0-4d1b-951e-45efec8e6300": {
    "id": "3ad123d8-52e0-4d1b-951e-45efec8e6300",
    "topic": "Test",
