    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_124736.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, what they are, and why they're important.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:17.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:26.700\nIt's like checking your understanding of a topic.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:36.100\nThink of it like this: if you're learning to bake a cake, you might test it by tasting a small piece to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:42.700\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, you test yourself by trying to balance and pedal.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:49.300\nTests in school are the same idea! They help you and your teacher see what you've learned and what you might need a little extra help with.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:57.800\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve some problems. A spelling test might ask you to write words correctly.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:07.400\nThese tests show how well you understand those subjects. So, remember, a test is just a tool to help you learn and grow.\n\n01:07.400 --> 01:13.000\nIt\u2019s nothing to be afraid of!\n\n01:13.000 --> 01:18.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
