    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_124953.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.000\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:19.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:26.200\nThe test? You poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a sign the cake is ready!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:32.200\nOr, maybe you want to know if you studied enough for your history exam.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:38.200\nThe test? You practice answering some questions beforehand.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:45.200\nTests aren't just for school or baking though. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, and engineers use tests to make sure buildings are safe.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:58.900\nBasically, anything where you want to check something or learn something new can involve a test. So, a test is just a way of gathering information to see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:03.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
