    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_125129.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a fundamental concept: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:13.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:24.300\nIt's how we gather information or check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:31.500\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:38.700\nOr, a teacher gives you a quiz to check what you've learned in class.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:41.700\nEven baking a cake is a test!\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:48.900\nYou're testing your recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:51.500\nSo, a test can be anything from a formal exam to a simple experiment.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:56.400\nThe key is that it gives us data or feedback.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:00.500\nWhether it's a pass or fail, a high score or a low score, the result of the test gives us valuable information.\n```"
