    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.100\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we're not just talking about school quizzes.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:23.000\nA test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:29.900\nThink of it like this: you want to bake a cake. The test is tasting the batter before you bake it.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:35.500\nYou're checking if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:41.100\nOr imagine you're building a tower with blocks. The test is seeing if the tower stands up straight.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:51.200\nSo, a test could be anything from checking if a light bulb turns on, to making sure your phone can connect to the internet.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:53.900\nIt's all about verifying that something is doing what it's designed to do.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:56.400\nIn short, a test confirms functionality. That\u2019s the basic idea of what a test is!\n```"
