    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_130306.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:20.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process designed to gather information.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:37.400\nThe toothpick tells you if the inside is still gooey or perfectly baked. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:45.700\nYour doctor might run blood tests to check your health. Your teacher gives you quizzes to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:55.300\nEven a taste test, like trying a new flavor of ice cream, is a way to gather information and see if you like it.\n\n00:55.300 --> 00:59.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to collect information and learn something new. It helps us understand things better.\n```"
  },
