    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:07.100\nToday we're diving into something fundamental:\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:07.700\nthe test.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:11.500\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:15.500\nIt's a process we use to check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:17.700\nThink about it like this: you might test a cake\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:20.200\nto see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:22.700\nIf it comes out clean, you know it's ready!\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:26.700\nOr, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:27.800\nAnother example?\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:31.200\nYou take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:34.700\nSo, a test can be anything from a simple check to a complex experiment.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:37.400\nThe key is, it's all about finding out information.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:41.000\nBasically, a test is a way to gather data and learn something new.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:43.900\nIt helps us understand the world around us.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:45.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
