    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey there, welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:15.900\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:19.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking,\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:32.200\nso you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test! It helps you figure something out. In general, tests help us see if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:44.200\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health. Or a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:57.700\nSo, to recap, a test is any process that helps you evaluate or check something. It could be a simple observation, a physical check, or even a written exam.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.300\nThe goal is always the same: to get information and make a decision based on that information.\n```"
