    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.700\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:19.000\nIt's a process to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well someone understands a topic.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:32.800\nOr, a doctor might give you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:35.800\nSchools use tests to measure what students have learned.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:46.600\nSo, whether it's checking the flavor of food, your eyesight, or your knowledge, a test is all about getting information.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:52.200\nIt helps us understand something better or make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:53.700\nIn short, a test is a way to evaluate or assess something.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:55.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f930eca3-06f3-42b3-9227-2c4500788eee": {
    "id": "f930eca3-06f3-42b3-9227-2c4500788eee",
