    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:40:44.318619",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T13:15:24.201588",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_131524.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_131524.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:21.200\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something specific. It's a process where we ask a question, or set up a situation, and then carefully observe the results.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:31.700\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might use a toothpick. Sticking it in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test!\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:41.100\nOr, if you're trying to see if a toy car needs new batteries, you turn it on and see if it moves. That's a test too!\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:55.400\nTests help us confirm things, solve problems, and learn new things. So next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's simply a way to check something out and get an answer.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:00.300\nThanks for watching! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
