    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb is working, that's a test! Essentially, a test asks a question, and you try to answer it correctly.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:40.400\nThese questions can be written, like in a school exam, or they can be practical, like trying to bake a cake to see if you know the recipe.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:49.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a car manufacturer might test a new car to see if it's safe to drive.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:55.300\nTests help us learn and improve things. So, in short, a test is a way to check knowledge or performance.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:00.900\nIt asks a question, and the answer tells us something important.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:03.600\nThanks for watching! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
