    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_132957.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:12.900\nWhat are they and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to see what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:20.800\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, you know it's good!\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:32.800\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. A pop quiz at school, a taste test for new food, or even a doctor checking your reflexes \u2013 all these are tests.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:39.800\nThey help us measure something. For example, a spelling test shows how well you know your spelling.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:44.800\nA balance test helps a doctor see if you're steady on your feet.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:49.800\nSee? Different tests, different purposes.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:58.000\nSo, tests are just tools to help us understand and measure things. They help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
