    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:16.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to check if something works like it's supposed to. Think of it like this: you want to know if your favorite toy car still runs.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:21.000\nSo, you put in batteries and try it out. That's a test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.800\nIt could also be something like checking if a light bulb lights up when you flip the switch.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.100\nThat's testing the light bulb and the switch! Or even simpler, tasting a cookie to see if it's delicious.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:36.400\nYou\u2019re testing the cookie! Basically, a test helps us find out if something is good, bad, broken, or working perfectly.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:41.700\nWe try something, and then we look at the result. That result tells us if our thing passed the test.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:52.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something does what it's meant to do.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:55.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
