  "c9ab325b-34a2-4fe2-b6cf-2ef11c4ce60c": {
    "id": "c9ab325b-34a2-4fe2-b6cf-2ef11c4ce60c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:41:03.862716",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T13:54:44.112187",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_135443.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_135443.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:17.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific about something else.\nThink of it like this: a test is a question we ask to get an answer.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:26.000\nFor example, a math test checks your understanding of numbers and equations.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:35.300\nA taste test tells you if you like the flavor of a new food.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:42.700\nOr, think about testing the batteries in your remote control to see if they still have power.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:46.000\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make decisions.\nThey're everywhere, from school to science, and even in cooking!\nThey help us understand the world around us.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9f0e8bd5-4ea2-4d51-bf2f-35eb44a43ba0": {
    "id": "9f0e8bd5-4ea2-4d51-bf2f-35eb44a43ba0",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:41:04.482608",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T13:56:00.823424",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_135600.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_135600.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:04.300\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:07.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.400 --> 01:01.800\nWe use them all the time to check our understanding or to see how well something works.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:11.500\nThink about it like this: You take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n01:11.500 --> 01:19.000\nOr, maybe you're baking a cake and you taste the batter - that's a mini-test to make sure it tastes good!\n\n01:19.000 --> 01:26.000\nAnother example: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n01:26.000 --> 01:33.000\nOr, an engineer might test a new bridge to make sure it can hold a lot of weight.\n\n01:33.000 --> 01:39.000\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions based on what we learn.\n\n01:39.000 --> 01:46.000\nThey can be formal, like exams, or informal, like tasting that cake batter.\n\n01:46.000 --> 01:49.500\nUltimately, they help us learn and improve.\n\n01:49.500 --> 01:51.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
