    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_135759.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:05.100\nToday we're going to explore something fundamental:\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:07.800\nwhat is a test?\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:10.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out\nsomething about someone or something.\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:15.000\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes a soup\nto test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:18.900\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school\nto see how well you know your words.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:23.200\nTests can be formal, like a science exam,\nor informal, like checking if your bike tires have enough air.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:26.900\nThe important thing is, they help us measure\nor learn something.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:32.300\nWe use tests to see if things are working\ncorrectly, if people understand a topic, or even just to compare different things.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:37.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather\ninformation.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:40.700\nIt helps us understand the world around us\nbetter.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:42.300\nThis video was created by\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:43.100\nApilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0d4ea54a-6482-41a3-91a8-8a5dfaae3cc7": {
