    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_140014.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.799\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.799 --> 00:12.219\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.219 --> 00:25.069\nIt\u2019s how we check if something is true, or how well something works. Think of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you put it in a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:25.069 --> 00:32.969\nThat's a test! Or, if you\u2019re baking a cake and want to know if it\u2019s done, you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:32.969 --> 00:42.699\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is ready. Tests aren't just for lightbulbs and cakes, though.\n\n00:42.699 --> 00:52.479\nDoctors use tests to see if you\u2019re healthy, and teachers use tests to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:52.479 --> 00:59.029\nSo, remember, a test is just a method for finding something out. It helps us understand the world around us.\n\n00:59.029 --> 01:01.799\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
