    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_141152.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests, what they are, and why we use them.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:11.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:17.000\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see how much you learned in class.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:23.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake and you taste it to see if it's sweet enough \u2013 that's a test too!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:31.000\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. We test new medicines to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:34.500\nWe test bridges to make sure they can hold cars.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:37.500\nWe even test video games to make sure they're fun!\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:44.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and see how things are going.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:52.000\nWhether it's a school exam or checking the flavor of your cooking, tests help us learn and improve.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:54.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
