    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:16.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:26.600\nIt's like an investigation, where we gather information to answer a question.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:31.000\nThink about it this way: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:38.100\nOr a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:43.500\nSee? Different kinds of tests, same basic idea.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:57.000\nLet's say you want to know if a cake is done. You can do a simple test: poke it with a toothpick! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's a test!\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.400\nSo, a test is just a process for getting information.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:03.900\nIt helps us understand something better, whether it's our health, our knowledge, or even if a cake is perfectly baked.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:06.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
