    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_142007.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:32.600\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing to see if you like it.\nOr, when you press a button on your phone, you're testing to see if it works.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:47.600\nTests aren't just for cooking or phones, though.\nScientists use tests to learn about the world, doctors use tests to diagnose illnesses, and teachers use tests to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:59.300\nSo, remember, a test is a way to learn something new or confirm something you already suspect.\nIt's all about asking questions and finding the answers!\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
