    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_142316.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.300\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:21.700\nThink of it like a little investigation.\nIt's how we gather information.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:29.700\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, think about baking a cake.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:42.600\nYou might taste the batter to test if it has enough sugar.\nAnother example: when you learn something new, like riding a bike, you're essentially testing yourself to see if you can do it.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:54.500\nYou try, you maybe fall, you try again until you succeed.\nSo, a test is a method of checking or trying something to gain information about it.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:04.500\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
