    "subtitles": "```webvtt\n    WEBVTT\n    \n    00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\n    Hey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n    \n    00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\n    Now, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n    \n    00:16.500 --> 00:20.600\n    Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n    \n    00:20.600 --> 00:27.500\n    You stick a toothpick in it, right? That's a test! The result of the test tells you something.\n    \n    00:27.500 --> 00:33.100\n    If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n    \n    00:33.100 --> 00:44.100\n    Tests aren't just for baking, though. A doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature.\n    \n    00:44.100 --> 00:55.300\n    Or, in school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned. So, remember, a test is a simple way to check something and get information.\n    \n    00:55.300 --> 01:00.400\n    It could be about anything, from a cake to your health to your knowledge.\n    \n    01:00.400 --> 01:05.000\n    Tests give us answers!\n    \n    01:05.000 --> 01:06.000\n    This video was created by Apilage AI.\n    ```\n    \n    NOTES:\n    *   **Image Placeholders:**  I've used placeholders like `ImageMobject(\"toothpick.png\")`. You'll need to replace these with actual image files in the same directory as your Manim script.\n    *   **Timing:** I've meticulously followed the timing instructions. Please double-check that the total duration matches your audio.\n    *   **Customization:** Feel free to adjust colors, font sizes, and animations to your liking.\n    *   **File:** Remember to save the Manim code in a `.py` file (e.g., `test_explanation.py`) and the images in the same directory.\n    \n    To render the animation, use the command: `manim -pql test_explanation.py TestExplanation`\n    \n    Let me know if you have any other questions or need further adjustments!"
