    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_143322.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:14.300\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into something called a \"test.\" \n\n00:14.300 --> 00:25.600\nNow, a test, simply put, is a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:29.700\nThink of it like this: you take a quiz in school \u2013 that's a test to see how much you learned.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:42.500\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. See? Tests help us understand things better. \n\n00:42.500 --> 00:52.800\nFor example, a car company might crash a car into a wall to test its safety.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:03.300\nOr, you might ask your friend some questions about a movie to test if they were paying attention.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:13.800\nSo, tests come in many forms, from written exams to real-world experiments. They all help us learn and improve.\n\n01:13.800 --> 01:17.400\nBasically, a test is a way to check something out.\n\n01:17.400 --> 01:23.300\nWe use them all the time to learn, grow, and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:23.300 --> 01:26.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
