    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_143912.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:20.800\nThink of it like checking if your oven is hot enough to bake a cake. You might use a thermometer \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:32.800\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards. For example, a doctor might run blood tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:40.700\nOr a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand the lesson.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:47.500\nImagine you build a tower out of blocks. To test if it's sturdy, you might gently push it.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:54.300\nIf it falls, it fails the test! If it stays standing, it passes.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:03.100\nSo, tests are all about checking things. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
