    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_144738.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, in simple terms, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's good.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:29.600\nOr, a doctor might test your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:37.600\nTests aren't just for cakes and fevers, though! They can be used to check all sorts of things.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:45.000\nA student takes a test to show what they've learned in class.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.400\nA company might test a new product to see if it works well.\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:06.300\nThe goal is always to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:12.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n01:12.000 --> 01:18.400\nIt helps us understand if things are working correctly, if we've learned something new, or if a product is ready to be used.\n\n01:18.400 --> 01:24.600\nIt's all about gathering information!\n\n01:24.600 --> 01:29.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
