    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_144830.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:03.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.700 --> 00:07.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:10.600\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:14.400\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:18.400\nThink about it: when you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like it.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:24.500\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if your phone charger is working, you plug it in \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:28.900\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:33.000\nIn science, tests help us prove or disprove ideas.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:39.600\nSo, whether it's a pop quiz or a science experiment, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:42.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4e785fd3-d2fa-49fc-8258-0f2f0062e049": {
    "id": "4e785fd3-d2fa-49fc-8258-0f2f0062e049",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:41:40.774884",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T14:49:21.576419",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_144921.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_144921.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:10.100\nWhat are they? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:20.300\nThink of it like this: you might test if your cake is done by poking it with a toothpick. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:30.300\nIn science and other fields, tests are more formal. We use them to see if an idea, or a hypothesis, is correct.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:42.600\nFor example, you might hypothesize that plants grow taller with more sunlight. To test this, you'd grow some plants in the sun and some in the shade and then compare their heights.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:51.600\nIf the plants in the sun are taller, that supports your idea! Tests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:59.700\nThey give us evidence to back up our claims. So remember, a test is just a way to check something and see if it's true.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:03.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
