    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_145853.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to see how much you know about something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You turn it on \u2013 that's the test \u2013 and if it lights up, you know it's good.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.000\nTests can come in lots of forms. Maybe it's a quiz in school, or a taste test for new ice cream flavors.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:41.500\nOr even a doctor checking your reflexes. In each case, we're trying to learn something about the person, thing, or idea being tested.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:53.400\nFor example, a spelling test helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words. A taste test helps a company figure out which ice cream flavor people like best.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:03.000\nSo, to recap, a test is just a way to gather information and see what's up. It helps us learn and improve things.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
