    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_150214.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:15.600\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt helps us understand if something is true, correct, or working properly.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\nYou might use a toothpick \u2013 that's your test!\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:33.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test and is ready.\nOr, imagine you're learning your ABCs.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:40.500\nYour teacher might give you a quiz to test how well you know them.\nThat quiz helps show what you've learned.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:48.300\nTests can be about all sorts of things, from checking if a light bulb works to seeing how strong a bridge is.\n\n00:48.300 --> 01:00.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and learn more about it.\nIt helps us confirm information or identify areas we need to work on.\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
