    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_150530.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of testing.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:28.300\nThink of it like this: you have a recipe for cookies, right? You bake them, and then you test them by taking a bite to see if they taste good.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:43.000\nIn science, you might test a new fertilizer on plants to see if they grow faster. Or, maybe you're testing a new toy to see if it's durable enough for kids to play with.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:54.400\nThe goal is always the same: to gather information and see if something meets a specific standard or expectation.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:01.900\nSo, whether it's tasting cookies, checking plant growth, or playing with a toy, a test helps us understand if something is working as it should.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:04.400\nRemember, testing is all about learning and improving.\n\n01:04.400 --> 01:09.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
