    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_152420.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nNow, you might be thinking about school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to see if something works as expected.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and you test it by tasting it. Does it taste good? That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:31.100\nOr, if you\u2019re building with LEGOs, you might test if your tower is strong enough to hold another brick.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:38.900\nTesting is super important because it helps us find problems and fix them before they become bigger issues.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:50.800\nImagine building a bridge \u2013 you'd definitely want to test it to make sure it's safe!\n\n00:50.800 --> 00:59.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly. It can be as simple as tasting a cake or as complex as testing a bridge.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:02.800\nTesting helps us build better things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "82e0294e-cef1-4abd-8c53-a8cb7ff6d513": {
    "id": "82e0294e-cef1-4abd-8c53-a8cb7ff6d513",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:42:08.681652",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T15:25:06.433468",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_152506.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_152506.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:24.700\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:33.900\nThink about it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch. If it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:42.100\nOr, maybe you're testing if a cookie is done by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, it's ready.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:50.300\nTests are used everywhere, from checking if your car is running smoothly to making sure a new medicine is safe.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:55.900\nThey help us understand if something is working as expected, or if it needs some fixing.\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:59.400\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it passes or fails. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e6dc3f10-24b8-4b90-9ec1-ad2c137f1f0d": {
