    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_152548.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.700\nNow, a test is basically a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:29.400\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb is working \u2013 that\u2019s a simple test. You screw it in, flip the switch, and see if it lights up!\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:40.500\nTests can be things like quizzes at school, where you answer questions to show what you've learned. Or, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:52.400\nFor example, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt. They're checking to see if it meets their expectations.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:58.600\nSo, in short, a test is a way to gather information and make sure things are working or understood correctly. It's all about checking and confirming! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
