    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_152740.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.220 --> 00:01.280\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.280 --> 00:02.570\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:02.830 --> 00:07.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true,\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:11.220\nbut a test in general is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:11.790 --> 00:14.370\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking, right?\n\n00:14.790 --> 00:17.240\nSo you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:17.240 --> 00:17.930\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.290 --> 00:21.370\nThe toothpick is helping you \"test\" if the cake is ready.\n\n00:21.640 --> 00:25.210\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:25.510 --> 00:28.680\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:28.960 --> 00:31.830\nThe light going on is the result of the test, telling you the bulb is good.\n\n00:32.220 --> 00:38.550\nEssentially, a test is any process you use to get information about something.\n\n00:38.760 --> 00:43.040\nWe run tests all the time, without even realizing it!\n\n00:43.460 --> 00:46.950\nSo remember, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n00:47.590 --> 00:50.210\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d1bf0902-47b3-4443-aefa-17c08e08fd88": {
    "id": "d1bf0902-47b3-4443-aefa-17c08e08fd88",
