    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_152829.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:09.100\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:14.400\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:17.700\nTests help us measure or evaluate things.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:23.400\nFor example, a spelling test in school tells us how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:27.400\nOr, a taste test can help you decide which kind of cookie you like best.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:30.900\nYou're trying different things to see what happens.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:37.400\nAnother simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works. You plug it in.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:40.500\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:43.600\nIf it doesn't, well, it failed the test.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:52.500\nSo remember, a test is just a way to learn more about something by observing the result of an action.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:56.000\nIt's a fundamental part of learning and discovery!\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:56.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
