    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:19.100\nToday we're talking about tests. Now, a test, in the simplest terms, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:28.800\nIt's how we find out if something works, if something is true, or even just how good something is.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:36.400\nThink about it like this: you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:42.400\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:48.400\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:54.400\nLet's say you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:00.500\nThe test is simple: you plug it in! If it lights up, the test is passed.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:04.500\nOr imagine you're testing if your plant needs water.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:08.100\nYou stick your finger in the soil.\n\n01:08.100 --> 01:11.900\nIf it's dry, it needs water.\n\n01:11.900 --> 01:14.100\nThat's a test!\n\n01:14.100 --> 01:19.800\nSo, tests are all about checking things.\n\n01:19.800 --> 01:26.200\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure everything is working as it should.\n\n01:26.200 --> 01:31.500\nThey're a fundamental part of understanding the world around us.\n\n01:31.500 --> 01:34.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
