    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:25.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:32.900\nThink of it like this: you might test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:40.400\nOr you might test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:47.500\nIn both cases, you're performing an action and observing the result to make sure it meets your expectations.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:54.600\nLet's say you're testing a new toy car.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:00.800\nYou push it, and the test is to see if it rolls forward. If it does, the test passes!\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:06.200\nIf it doesn't, well, something might be wrong.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:18.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a simple way to check if something is doing what it's supposed to do. It involves trying something out and seeing if the result is what you expected.\n\n01:18.800 --> 01:22.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
