    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_154009.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:11.400\nSimply put, it's a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:17.200\nThink of it like an investigation. You're trying to gather information.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:26.500\nThe thing you're finding out could be anything. Maybe you're taking a math test at school to see how well you understand fractions. Or maybe a doctor is running a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:38.900\nThe test gives you results, and those results tell you something important. For example, if your math test score is high, it shows you understand fractions well. If your blood test shows low iron, it tells you you might need to eat more iron-rich foods.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:45.900\nSee? Tests help us learn, diagnose, and understand all kinds of things.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:58.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool for gathering information. It helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:04.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
