    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.500\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:11.000\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.500\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it's true or false.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:19.000\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes their soup to test if it has enough salt.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:20.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:24.000\nOr, maybe you take a quiz in school.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:27.000\nThat quiz is testing your knowledge on a subject.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:29.000\nTests can be all sorts of things.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:34.000\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.000\nA scientist might run tests to see if their experiment worked.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:43.000\nWe even test products, like toys, to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:47.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to find out information.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:53.000\nIt's a check to see if something is right, working, or safe.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:54.500\nThat's the basic idea!\n\n00:54.500 --> 00:57.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e1ed587a-4fd6-43cc-9c90-f91e72327d16": {
    "id": "e1ed587a-4fd6-43cc-9c90-f91e72327d16",
