    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_160118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:06.200\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:10.100\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:12.700\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:15.400\nSo, what kind of things can we test?\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:17.600\nWell, almost anything!\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:23.100\nWe can test if a lightbulb works by turning it on.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:26.900\nThe test is the act of turning it on, and the result tells us if the bulb is good or not.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:33.200\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste the batter to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:35.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:38.000\nYou're testing the sweetness of the batter.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:44.500\nBasically, any time you perform an action to check something, you're running a test.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:48.200\nIt's a way to gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:52.500\nSo next time you're checking something, remember you're performing a test!\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:54.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
