    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_160405.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.300\nWhat is a test, exactly? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:27.400\nThink about it like this: a spelling test shows how well you know how to spell words. Or, a taste test helps you decide which food you like best.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:37.900\nTests can be used for lots of different things, from checking your understanding in school, to figuring out what kind of job you\u2019re best suited for.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:46.200\nFor example, if you're learning to play the piano, your teacher might give you a test to see if you've learned a new song.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:58.200\nOr, if you're applying for a job, you might take a skills test to show them what you can do. So, a test is just a tool to measure knowledge or ability.\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:08.100\nIt helps you, and others, understand where you're at and what you might need to learn next. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
