    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:20.000\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works.\nYou're testing it to see if it lights up!\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:28.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\nMaybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\nOr a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:45.300\nThe goal is always the same: to learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:45.300 --> 01:03.700\nTests help us make decisions and understand the world around us better.\nSo, to recap, a test is a procedure used to gather information, whether it's about your spelling skills, the taste of a sauce, or the effectiveness of a medicine.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:09.300\nIt\u2019s all about finding out!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
