    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T16:23:40.439268",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_162340.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_162340.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.400\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:25.500\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:35.100\nThink about it like this: When you're baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:42.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.900\nOr, imagine you're trying to guess which key opens a lock. You try each key, one at a time.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:51.700\nEach try is a test to see if that key is the right one.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:54.500\nSo, a test is just a way of checking things.\n```"
  },
  "10ae3682-ce22-4fe9-bd95-c9195c7c9007": {
    "id": "10ae3682-ce22-4fe9-bd95-c9195c7c9007",
