    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:42:50.175836",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T16:24:29.247123",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_162429.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_162429.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:14.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:38.600\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it. For example, when you try a new food, you're testing if you like it. Or, when you flip a light switch, you're testing if the lightbulb works.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:50.600\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:50.600 --> 01:00.500\nThe important thing is that they help us gather information and make decisions. They show us if something works, if something is true, or if we understand something.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:04.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of learning something new. It's a tool for exploring and understanding the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
