    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:17.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It's how we find out if something works, if it's true, or if someone understands something.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:39.100\nOr, you might check the batteries in your toy to test if they're dead.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:46.300\nIn school, a test helps your teacher see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:56.900\nSo, tests can be big or small, formal or informal. But they all have the same purpose: to give us information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.400\nWe use tests all the time, often without even realizing it! In short, a test is a way of checking something to learn more about it. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
