    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_165826.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:27.900\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or correct. Think of it like this: if you want to know if your cake is done baking, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:33.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:40.600\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, the test is whether you can balance and pedal without falling.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:45.400\nTests aren't just for baking or bikes, though. They're everywhere!\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:50.200\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:55.000\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:55.000 --> 01:01.400\nTests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:12.600\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to gather information and see if something is true.\n\n01:12.600 --> 01:23.100\nWhether it's a toothpick in a cake or a big exam at school, tests help us learn and improve.\n\n01:23.100 --> 01:28.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
