    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_170015.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.000\nWhat are they and why are they important?\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It helps us figure out if something is working correctly or if it's doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:38.200\nThink about it like this: If you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough. Or, if you buy a new toy, you play with it to test if it's fun.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:49.800\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are right, and doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:56.900\nSo, a test can be anything from a quick taste to a complicated experiment, but the main idea is always the same: to learn something by checking it.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.400\nRemember, testing helps us understand the world around us and make sure things are working as they should! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
