    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_170311.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered exactly what it means?\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:16.200\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer in a specific way.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like this: a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:33.000\nOr, a doctor might give you a vision test to see how well you can see.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:40.000\nIn both cases, they're using the test to gather information.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:47.000\nAnother example?\nImagine you're taking a quiz at school.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:58.200\nThat's a test to see how much you've learned about a certain subject!\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:07.700\nSo, basically, a test is just a tool we use to learn more about something, whether it's soup, eyesight, or even your knowledge.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:14.800\nSo, to recap: a test helps us find information by asking a question and looking for the answer in a structured way.\n\n01:14.800 --> 01:19.700\nIt's used everywhere, from cooking to school!\n\n01:19.700 --> 01:23.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
