    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:14.900\nYou've probably taken a few in school, but what exactly is a test in a general sense?\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:22.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:29.300\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, a product's quality, or even just to see if a light bulb works.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:35.500\nThink of it like this: A doctor gives you a blood test to find out if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:39.100\nThat's a test!\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:45.900\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:48.900\nThat's also a test!\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:51.900\nThe chef is testing the soup's flavor.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:55.900\nSo, tests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:01.300\nThey help us make decisions and understand things better.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:07.800\nThey can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:15.000\nIn essence, a test is a way of asking a question and getting an answer through observation or measurement.\n\n01:15.000 --> 01:18.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
