    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T17:21:28.462268",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_172128.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_172128.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is a way to see if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it as a little experiment. Basically, you give something a task, and then you check the result.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:32.000\nIf the result is what you expected, then the test passes! If not, the test fails.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:39.000\nFor example, imagine you\u2019re testing a lightbulb. You screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:44.600\nIf the lightbulb turns on, the test passes! If it stays dark, the test fails.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:53.000\nOr, think about a recipe. You follow the instructions, and then taste the food. If it tastes good, the recipe passed the test!\n\n00:53.000 --> 01:03.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something works as expected. It involves giving something a task and verifying the outcome.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:07.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
