    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_173520.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:16.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something. It's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a new toy to see if it\u2019s fun. Or, you might test a recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:36.000\nIn science, we test hypotheses, which are basically educated guesses, to see if our ideas about the world are correct.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:48.900\nFor example, let's say you think plants grow better in sunlight. You could test that by putting one plant in the sun and another in the shade and seeing which one grows taller.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:57.400\nThat's a test! So, remember, a test is just a way to check something to see if it works or if it's true.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:05.200\nIt's a tool we use to learn and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
