    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_173944.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.700 --> 00:03.000\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:03.400 --> 00:07.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly,\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:08.500\nor if something is true.\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:14.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you put it in a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:15.500\nThat's a test!\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:18.900\nIn school, tests help your teacher understand what you\u2019ve learned.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:24.700\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. Tasting the batter is a test to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:30.400\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it. Whether it\u2019s checking the temperature outside\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:33.400\nto decide what to wear, or seeing if your shoes fit\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:34.400\nbefore buying them.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:41.700\nSo, to recap, a test is just a method to find out if something is right, working, or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:43.400\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:46.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
