    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_174111.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:19.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see what you\u2019ve learned in class.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:38.200\nOr, maybe you\u2019re trying out a new recipe. Tasting it is a test to see if it\u2019s delicious!\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:49.000\nAnother example is when a doctor checks your reflexes. They tap your knee, and if your leg kicks, that's a test to see if your nerves are working properly.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:54.900\nSo, a test helps us understand and evaluate things. It can be a quiz, an experiment, or even just trying something out. It's all about learning and checking. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
