    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_174202.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:11.800\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:11.800 --> 020.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of your bath water to make sure it's not too hot or too cold.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:38.500\nIn many areas, tests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if someone understands a topic.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:47.900\nFor example, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:53.300\nSo, testing is just a simple way of checking something, whether it's your bath water, your health, or your knowledge.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:55.100\nIt helps us make sure everything is as it should be.\n```"
