    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_174806.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb. To test if it works, you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:31.100\nIf the light turns on, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:38.200\nSame idea with baking a cake. You follow the recipe, and the test is whether the cake tastes good.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:42.000\nDid it rise properly? Is it cooked all the way through?\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:49.100\nThose are all tests. So, a test is basically a way to confirm that something is functioning as expected.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:52.900\nIt could be anything from a simple lightbulb to a complex computer program.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:03.000\nWe run tests to make sure things are reliable and do what we want them to do. Hopefully that gives you a good basic understanding of what a test is.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:08.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
