    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:43:59.921464",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T17:51:24.301623",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_175124.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_175124.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.100\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:22.100\nIt's a process you use to see if something is true, or to measure something.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:26.200\nThink about it like this: a taste test!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:33.300\nYou taste something to see if you like it. That's a test!\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:47.700\nOr maybe you take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a subject. That's another kind of test! Even a doctor checking your temperature is performing a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:56.700\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all share the same basic goal: to give us information. They help us learn, understand, and make decisions.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.300\nRemember, a test is just a way to find something out. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "cc602785-9c27-409b-9462-b063fe7d39a6": {
    "id": "cc602785-9c27-409b-9462-b063fe7d39a6",
