    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_175213.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:18.600\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready. The test? You stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:30.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! It's done!\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:36.000\nAnother example: You want to know if your shoes fit. You put them on and walk around.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:40.100\nIf they feel comfortable, they pass the test! They fit!\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:48.400\nSo, a test helps us check something. It helps us make sure things are working, or ready, or just right.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:52.100\nIt's all about finding information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a770946b-0cf2-424f-91ef-aef4a326d0d8": {
    "id": "a770946b-0cf2-424f-91ef-aef4a326d0d8",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:44:01.358080",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T17:53:30.434899",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_175330.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_175330.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHello, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:23.900\nIt's a process that helps us learn more about a person, object, or even an idea. Think of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:32.300\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned in class. Or even a chef might taste a dish to test if it's seasoned correctly.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:42.800\nSo, tests can take many forms! They can be written questions, physical activities, or even just observations.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:52.800\nThe important thing is that they give us information and help us make better decisions. In short, a test is a tool for learning and understanding.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:56.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ca344654-210c-4aac-995d-c5ed0182a84a": {
    "id": "ca344654-210c-4aac-995d-c5ed0182a84a",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:44:02.089989",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T17:54:31.411062",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_175431.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_175431.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.500\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we simply mean a way to check something.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:38.800\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, if it meets certain standards, or even just to see what happens.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:48.100\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold, or a chef might taste their soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:53.300\nAnother example is checking if your bicycle tires have enough air.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:58.500\nYou can squeeze them \u2013 that\u2019s a test! If they feel firm, they pass the test.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:01.100\nIf they're squishy, they fail.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:05.700\nSo, in short, a test is just a way to check something and see if it meets our expectations.\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:07.600\nApilage AI.\n```"
  },
