    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:23.200\nWe use them all the time, in all sorts of situations. Think of it like this: a doctor uses tests to check your health, or a chef tastes food to see if it needs more seasoning.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:29.000\nThey're both performing tests! The goal of a test is to give us information.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:37.800\nMaybe you take a spelling test at school. That test helps your teacher understand what words you know and what words you need to practice.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:44.600\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake and you poke it with a fork. That's a test to see if it's done!\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:58.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of getting information. From checking if a cake is baked to figuring out what you know in school, tests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "93efe274-7ea4-4289-9ab9-605ca086c035": {
    "id": "93efe274-7ea4-4289-9ab9-605ca086c035",
