    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_182000.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's how we check if something is working, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:35.200\nAnother example is checking if a light bulb works. You flip the switch, and if it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:46.700\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your shoes are tied. The important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:54.700\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:58.200\nThat's it! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
