    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_182136.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.000\nwhat they are and why we use them.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:10.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like using a ruler to see how long something is.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:16.000\nIn everyday life, we use tests all the time.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:19.000\nFor example, a doctor might use a test to check your temperature.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.000\nA chef might taste food to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.000\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:29.000\nThey might ask you questions on a piece of paper\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:31.000\nor have you solve a math problem.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:32.000\nThese are all different kinds of tests.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:38.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to help us measure or understand something better.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:42.000\nIt's like a snapshot of what you know or how something is.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
