    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:20.300\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\nThink about it \u2013 a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:31.000\nOr a teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned in class.\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done, you can stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:39.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that\u2019s a test, and it tells you the cake is ready!\nAnother example?\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:45.700\nChecking the battery level on your phone.\nThat's a test to see how much power you have left.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:52.000\nSo, tests help us understand things better by giving us information.\nThey come in all shapes and sizes,\n\n00:52.000 --> 01:05.500\nfrom simple everyday checks to more complex scientific experiments.\nRemember, a test is just a way to get an answer.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:13.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "00c71ac8-05a9-41e7-8209-6c84ea158632": {
    "id": "00c71ac8-05a9-41e7-8209-6c84ea158632",
