    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:44:31.589781",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T18:31:56.138606",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_183156.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_183156.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:21.500\nIt's like asking a question and seeing if you get the right answer. Think about it like this.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:27.500\nImagine you're baking a cake. You test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:38.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, if you're checking if a light bulb works, you flip the switch.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:45.800\nIf it lights up, it passes the test; if not, well, it failed. Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:53.600\nDoctors use tests to check your health, teachers use tests to see what you've learned, and even apps on your phone have tests running in the background.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:01.400\nBasically, a test is a simple way to see if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:04.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a check!\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:08.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
