    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_183334.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let\u2019s talk about tests!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.900\nYou\u2019ve probably taken lots of them in school,\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:06.900\nbut what exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:10.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to see what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:12.200\nIt helps us measure something.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:16.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:19.500\nThat test is measuring your body temperature.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:24.400\nIn school, a test might measure how well you understand a particular subject, like math or history.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.600\nFor example, a quiz with multiple-choice questions is a type of test.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:30.300\nSo is a spelling bee!\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:37.000\nEven a simple experiment to see if a plant needs sunlight can be considered a test.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:48.700\nIt helps us understand something better by measuring it in some way.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:51.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
