    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nWell, simply put, a test is just a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps us understand something better.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: a chef tests the soup to see if it needs more salt. That's a test!\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:30.700\nOr, a doctor might give you a quick eye test to check your vision. They're both gathering information.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:36.600\nTests can be simple or complex.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:46.000\nYou might test a toy to see if it works. Or, scientists might run tests in a lab to discover new things.\n\n00:46.000 --> 01:00.000\nThe key is that a test helps us learn and make decisions. So, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information and checking something out.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:03.600\nIt helps us understand things better, from cooking soup to exploring the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
