    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_184825.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:30.700\nIt's a process designed to evaluate or assess something's qualities, performance, or reliability.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:43.500\nThink of it like this: if you're baking a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:54.000\nOr, if you're buying a used car, taking it for a test drive is a test to see if it runs smoothly.\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:04.500\nScientists use tests all the time to see if their ideas are correct.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:15.000\nThey might run an experiment, which is just a fancy word for a test! The important thing is that a test helps us learn and make better decisions.\n\n01:15.000 --> 01:23.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a method used to evaluate something, whether it's a cake, a car, or a scientific theory.\n\n01:23.200 --> 01:32.700\nIt helps us gather information and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
