    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_185418.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.800\nThe thing we're finding out about could be almost anything.\nMaybe you're testing a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:35.200\nOr maybe a doctor is testing your blood to see if you're healthy.\nFor example, a simple math test might ask you \"What's two plus two?\"\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:42.400\nThe answer, of course, is four.\nThat's the result of the test!\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:50.100\nOr, imagine you're testing a toy car to see how far it can roll.\nYou wind it up, let it go, and measure the distance.\n\n00:50.100 --> 01:01.200\nThat distance is the result of that test.\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information.\nYou ask a question, perform an action, and then see what the answer or result is.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:07.199\nIt's all about learning something new!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
