    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.400\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something, to see if it works, or if it's true.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer. In science, you might test a hypothesis.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:36.000\nFor example, \"Does sunlight help plants grow?\" You'd set up an experiment to find out.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:41.100\nIn school, a test helps your teacher see how well you understand what you've been learning.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:50.600\nIt's a way to measure your knowledge. A simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:55.700\nYou plug it in. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:05.200\nOr, if you want to test if a cookie is done baking, you poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, it's ready!\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:19.200\nSo, a test is simply a method to find out something, to confirm or deny something, or to evaluate something's performance.\n\n01:19.200 --> 01:28.700\nTests are all around us, helping us learn and understand the world. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
