    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:28.200\nThink of it as a way to check your understanding or the quality of something.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:35.000\nFor example, you might take a test at school to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:41.800\nOr, a company might test a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:44.400\nThey're both tests, just used for different things.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:51.900\nAnother example could be a taste test! If you're trying out different flavors of ice cream, you're essentially doing a test to see which one you like the best.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:54.500\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:07.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to evaluate knowledge, skills, or the quality of something. It helps us understand what we know or how well something performs.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:11.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
