    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_190027.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:05.100\nToday we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.600\nNow, a test is just a way of finding out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:14.100\nThink of it like asking a question,\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:20.700\nbut instead of just listening to an answer, you\u2019re actually checking if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:22.800\nSo, what are we testing?\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:23.900\nWell, it could be anything!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:28.600\nImagine you bake a cake. You might test it by poking it with a toothpick\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:30.500\nto see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:31.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:34.600\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, you're constantly testing your balance.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:39.500\nAnother example is a spelling test at school.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:42.000\nThat's a way to see if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.500\nBasically, any time you're checking something to see if it meets a certain standard, you're performing a test.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:54.200\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to check if something is true, correct, or working properly.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:59.300\nWe test things all the time in our daily lives, often without even realizing it!\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:01.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
