    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.400\nSo, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:26.000\nIt helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true. Think of it like this: if you want to know if a light bulb works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n00:26.000 --> 00:29.500\nThat\u2019s a test!\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:36.600\nOr, if you want to see if your cake is done baking, you poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:45.200\nTests aren't just for things we can see, though. You take tests in school to see how well you've learned a subject.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:52.900\nIt's all about checking knowledge or performance. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:03.000\nIt can be simple or complex, but the goal is always the same: to find out if something is working or true.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
