    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:17.200\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find something out.\nIt's a process we use to gather information.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:30.600\nThe toothpick test tells you if the cake is cooked inside.\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:42.400\nYou screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\nIf it lights up, the bulb passes the test!\nTests can be big, like a school exam, or small, like checking the temperature of your bathwater.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:50.100\nThe important thing is that a test helps you answer a question or check if something is working as it should.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:59.800\nSo, a test is simply a method for gathering information to answer a question.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
