    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_191421.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:22.700\nIt\u2019s a process of asking a question or performing an action to see what happens.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:29.700\nThink about it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:33.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:38.100\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, you might try to balance without holding on.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:42.300\nThat's a test too! You're testing your balance skills.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:49.900\nTests aren't just for baking or biking, though. Scientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:54.600\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:01.900\nBasically, anytime you're trying to learn something or figure something out, you're probably using a test of some kind.\n\n01:01.900 --> 01:04.500\nSo, a test is just a way to get information and learn.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:06.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
