    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_192029.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:17.300\nToday, we're tackling a fundamental concept: the test.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:26.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:32.200\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.500\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:44.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That\u2019s a test.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:49.600\nOr imagine checking if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:52.700\nIf it lights up, the test passes.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:59.100\nTests are super important in all sorts of areas. Scientists use them to prove theories, doctors use them to diagnose illnesses, and even you use them every day to make decisions.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.200\nThey give us information to make informed choices.\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:05.400\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and confirm something.\n01:05.400 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
