    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:15.900\nA test is basically a way to check something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like this: you test a cake by tasting it to see if it's good.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:34.000\nIn everyday life, tests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:43.000\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:50.200\nOr, you might test a new lightbulb to make sure it lights up.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:57.400\nTests can be simple, like pressing a button to see if it works, or more complex, like taking a quiz in school.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:09.700\nThe important thing is that a test gives us information. It tells us something about the thing we're testing.\n\n01:09.700 --> 01:14.800\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check something and get information about it.\n\n01:14.800 --> 01:22.800\nWhether it's a taste test or a science experiment, tests are all about learning!\n\n01:22.800 --> 01:26.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
