    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_193109.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests, but not the kind you take in school.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:17.000\nWe're talking about tests, as in, putting something to the test! It's all about figuring out if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:26.300\nBasically, a test is an experiment or a procedure you use to see if something is true, accurate, or effective.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:37.900\nThink about it like this: you bake a cake and you test it by tasting it to see if it's good. Or, you might test a new lightbulb to see if it actually lights up.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:48.400\nAnother example: A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Or, an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it can handle heavy loads.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:51.000\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:51.000 --> 01:00.100\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check if something works or is correct. It helps us learn and improve things.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:03.799\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
