    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_193205.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:11.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:20.000\nIt's a procedure we use to gather information.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:32.200\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:38.700\nOr, in school, you take a test to show what you've learned.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:45.200\nThese tests involve asking questions or performing tasks, and then evaluating the results.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:50.700\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:56.300\nYou plug it in. If it lights up, the test is passed! If it doesn't, the test failed.\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:01.800\nAnother test might be tasting something to see if it's sweet or sour.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:14.100\nSo, a test is a method for gathering information, often involving questions or tasks, to determine something specific.\n\n01:14.100 --> 01:20.700\nWe use tests every day, in big ways and small ways, to learn more about the world around us.\n\n01:20.700 --> 01:23.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
