    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_193404.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test is.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like an experiment, but often shorter and more focused.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:24.900\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it. Think about it: when you taste a new food, you're testing if you like it.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:34.600\nOr when you try a different route to school, you're testing if it's faster. In school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:42.100\nIt's a way to check your understanding. For example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:55.800\nOr a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt. Tests can be formal, like a written exam, or informal, like trying on a new pair of shoes to see if they fit.\n\n00:55.800 --> 01:06.500\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is just a method for gathering information and learning something new. Remember, it's all about finding out!\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:10.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
