    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:25.900\nIt helps us figure out if something works, if something is true, or even how well something is done.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:34.900\nThink about it like this: When you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:42.600\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, you're constantly testing your balance.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:50.300\nYou try different things and see what works. Tests aren't just for food and bikes, though.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:58.100\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct. Doctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:01.700\nSo, tests are all around us, helping us learn and understand the world better.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:04.700\nThey are a way to gather data.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.300\nRemember, a test is a way to check something and find out information.\n\n01:08.300 --> 01:11.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
