    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_193744.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:09.400\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. You're trying to see if something is true or false, working correctly, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:29.100\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:34.500\nThat's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:44.000\nOr, if you're checking if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:56.900\nSo, tests help us understand things better and make sure everything is working as it should. They are everywhere in our daily lives, even if you don't always realize it!\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
