    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_195020.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:24.800\nIt's a process we use to gather information or check if something is working correctly. Think of it like this: a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:35.000\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. In science, we use tests to see if our experiments work the way we expect.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:46.800\nFor example, you might test different types of soil to see which helps a plant grow the tallest. So, a test is just a structured way to ask a question and get an answer.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:57.500\nIt helps us learn, diagnose problems, and confirm our ideas. Remember, tests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
