    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.300\nNow, you might think of school tests, but a \"test\" is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:24.600\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:29.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:33.000\nYour test is to screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:36.800\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:41.500\nAnother example? You want to know if an apple is sweet.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:46.200\nYour test? Take a bite! If it tastes sweet, the test passes.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:57.300\nBasically, a test is a simple process to check if something is working correctly or has a certain quality. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:00.200\nSo next time you're \"testing\" something, you'll know exactly what you're doing!\n```"
