    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_200842.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something really important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:14.900\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to find out information or check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by poking it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:35.000\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned. Scientists use tests to see if their experiments worked.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:37.600\nAnd even game developers test their games to find bugs before they release them.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:48.400\nSee? Tests are everywhere! For example, a doctor might test your eyesight, or a car mechanic might test your brakes.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:58.900\nEach test helps them understand something better. So, to recap: a test is a way to gather information, check functionality, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:04.400\nPretty simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
