    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_201049.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.900\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:22.600\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:33.400\nSo, you poke it with a toothpick. The toothpick coming out clean is the \"test,\" and it tells you the cake IS ready.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:39.800\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:48.900\nYou screw it into a lamp. If it lights up, the \"test\" shows it's working!\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:59.900\nTests can be big and complicated, like medical tests, or super simple, like checking the weather forecast.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:09.900\nThe main idea is always the same: to get information. So, a test helps us learn something new or confirm what we already think.\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:14.900\nSo, remember, a test is a way to get information and learn about something.\n\n01:14.900 --> 01:19.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
