    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:68.4\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:21.400\nIt helps us understand if something is true, or working correctly, or even just what someone knows about a subject.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:29.100\nThink about it like this: a simple math quiz is a test to see how well you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:37.400\nOr, imagine a doctor checking your reflexes with a little hammer. That's a test to see if your nerves are working.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:47.900\nTests aren't just for school or the doctor's office, though. When you try a new recipe, you're essentially testing it out to see if you like the taste!\n\n00:47.900 --> 01:01.300\nSo, tests are all about gathering information and learning something new. Basically, a test is a way of checking something to see if it's right, working, or understood.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:08.400\nThat's it for today's quick introduction to tests! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
