    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_201538.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\nHey there, and welcome!\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:04.200\nToday we're going to explore\nsomething called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:07.200\nNow, in simple terms, a test is\njust a way of finding out something.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:09.600\nIt's like asking a question\nand then looking for the answer.\n\n00:09.600 --> 00:14.500\nThink about it like this: if you want to\nknow if a cake is ready, you might poke\nit with a toothpick.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:16.400\nThat poke is a test!\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:20.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean,\nthe cake's done.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:25.300\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure\nout if a light bulb is working.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:28.200\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:30.000\nIf it lights up, the test passed!\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:36.100\nA test can be anything from a simple\nobservation to a more complex experiment.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:42.000\nThe main idea is that it helps us learn\nsomething new or confirm something we\nalready suspect.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way\nto find out information.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:50.400\nIt helps us answer questions\nand understand the world around us.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:53.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
