    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_202005.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:25.100\nIt could be anything from a written exam at school to a quality control check in a factory. The main idea behind a test is to see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:33.600\nFor example, a math test checks if you understand math concepts. A taste test checks if food tastes good.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:44.400\nThink of it like this: your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Or a car manufacturer might test a car's safety features before it goes on sale.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:53.800\nTests help us make sure things are working as they should. So, remember, a test is all about checking and evaluating.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:03.400\nIt helps us understand if something is good, correct, or up to standard. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
