    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests, and what they're all about.\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:13.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something, or to find out how well something works.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:16.800\nThink of it like this: you might test a new lightbulb to see if it lights up.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:17.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:20.800\nOr, you might take a quiz at school.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:23.100\nThat's also a test, to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:26.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:30.600\nA doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel sick.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:34.400\nA chef might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:39.500\nReally, anything where you're checking something carefully can be considered a test.\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:42.800\nSo, in short, a test is just a way of finding something out.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:48.400\nIt helps us learn, improve things, and make sure everything's working the way it should.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:50.300\nThanks for watching!\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:53.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
