    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_202648.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.800\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, we're talking about testing something to see if it works as expected.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:33.200\nBasically, a test is a way to check if something is doing what it\u2019s supposed to do. Think of it like this: before you bake a whole batch of cookies, you might bake just one or two as a test to make sure the recipe is right and your oven is at the correct temperature. That's a test!\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:38.700\nAnother example: imagine you're building a birdhouse.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:45.900\nYou might test it by putting it outside and seeing if birds actually use it. If they do, great! If not, you know you need to make some changes.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:57.300\nSo, in short, a test is a way to verify if something is functioning correctly and meeting your needs.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:04.800\nIt helps you catch problems early and make improvements. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
