    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_202748.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:14.000\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:26.000\nThat's a test! The toothpick comes out clean? The cake is ready.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:30.100\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:34.400\nYou screw it in, flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:44.800\nOr maybe you're taking a spelling test in school. That test helps your teacher understand what words you know.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:51.900\nSo, tests help us understand things, check if something is working, or measure our knowledge.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:54.900\nThey're all about gathering information.\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:58.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
