    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_203014.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:16.500\nWhat are they and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well something works, or how much someone knows.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like checking if your cookies are done baking. You test them by poking them with a toothpick \u2013 if it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:35.200\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. In school, you take tests to show what you've learned in class.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:47.100\nScientists use tests to see if their new inventions actually work. For example, a car company might test a new car's engine to make sure it's reliable.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:55.400\nOr, a baker might test a new recipe to make sure it tastes good.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:01.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out information or see if something is working the way it should. They help us learn and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
