    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_203252.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:23.700\nIt's a process we use to gather information or check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:33.800\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:43.900\nOr, a taste test lets you decide which flavor of ice cream you like best.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:54.200\nIn science, tests can help us prove or disprove ideas. For example, a scientist might test if a new fertilizer helps plants grow faster.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:56.000\nThey'd compare plants with the fertilizer to plants without it.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.500\nSo, tests are all about finding answers and gathering information.\n```"
