    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:22.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:27.600\nThe toothpick comes out clean?\nTest passed, cake's ready.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:32.800\nToothpick comes out gooey?\nTest failed, needs more time.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:39.400\nTests are used everywhere!\nDoctors run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:52.300\nTeachers give tests to see how much you've learned.\nEven scientists use tests to prove if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:58.900\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something is working as expected, or if it needs some adjustments.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:01.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check something.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:04.800\nIt helps us make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:08.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
