    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_204903.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.600\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but a test in general, is really just a way to find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like checking if your phone charger works.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:29.200\nYou plug it in, that's the test! If your phone starts charging, the test passes.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:36.900\nIf not, well, the charger failed the test. Another example: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:44.000\nThey look at your throat, ask you questions, and based on that, decide if you're sick.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:51.100\nThat's a test, too! So, basically, a test is just a simple way to check something.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:57.300\nIt helps us understand if things are working as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
