    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_205701.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:13.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:20.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. It could be testing if a lightbulb works by screwing it in.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:26.600\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:34.800\nOr, imagine baking a cake. You might test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:37.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:43.400\nThat's a test! Tests help us make decisions and understand things better.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:49.100\nThey can be as simple as checking the weather before you go outside, or more complicated,\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:53.600\nlike a doctor running tests to figure out what's making you feel sick.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:01.200\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:03.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
