    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_210210.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:14.200\nToday we're diving into something fundamental: what is a test?\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:19.500\nThink of it like gathering information.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:24.700\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:29.300\nFor example, if you tap a piece of fruit to see if it's ripe, that's a test!\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:31.900\nYou're testing its ripeness.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.000\nOr, if you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like the taste.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:39.900\nAnother example could be a doctor checking your temperature.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:41.900\nThat's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:45.700\nTests help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:51.100\nThey can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your coffee is hot enough.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:59.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:03.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
