    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_210716.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. It's like asking a question to see if you know the answer, or trying something out to see if it works.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if your cookies are done baking, you do a test! You poke them with a toothpick.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:37.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies pass the test, and they're ready to eat. Or, imagine you have a new toy and you want to see if it needs batteries.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:42.800\nYou try to turn it on. If it turns on, the toy passes the battery test!\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:54.200\nSo, a test is simply a way to find out if something is true, correct, or working as it should. It helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:59.700\nPretty simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
