    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_211455.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:25.500\nIt could be checking if a light bulb works by flipping the switch. The switch is the \"test,\" and the light turning on is the \"answer.\" Or, imagine taking a quiz in school.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:32.500\nThe quiz questions are the \"test,\" and your answers show what you've learned.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:42.200\nHere\u2019s another example. When you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that\u2019s a test saying the cake is done.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:53.300\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is a way to find out if something is working, true, or ready. It\u2019s all about checking and verifying.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:56.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
