    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:23.300\nThat's a test!\nYou're checking if the light bulb does what it's supposed to do, which is light up.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:28.400\nTests aren't just for light bulbs, though.\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:33.500\nYou can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:38.600\nThat's another test!\nEssentially, a test is an action or procedure designed to reveal if something is working correctly or meeting certain requirements.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:50.000\nSo, whether it's a light bulb, a cake, or even a computer program, tests help us make sure things are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:58.300\nTo recap, a test is a simple way to check if something works!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
