    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:47:00.174421",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T21:50:31.946520",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_215031.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_215031.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey there, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.000\nToday, we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:11.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:14.000\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:18.500\nThink of it like this: a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:24.000\nOr a teacher might give you a quiz to test how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:28.000\nEven trying on a new pair of shoes is a test to see if they fit comfortably!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.000\nSo, a test can be anything from a formal exam to just trying something out.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.000\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make decisions.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:39.000\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:45.000\nBasically, a test is a procedure intended to establish the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:49.000\nIt can also just be a trial or experiment.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:52.000\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is!\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
