    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T21:52:04.258968",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_215204.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_215204.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nAlright, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:17.800\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:22.000\nWe use them all the time, whether we realize it or not.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:32.400\nSo, you screw it into a lamp. That's a test!\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:36.700\nThe test is: does the lightbulb light up?\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:41.500\nIf it does, the test passes. The bulb works.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:46.300\nIf it doesn't, the test fails. The bulb is broken.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:57.900\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs, though. A doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\nA teacher uses tests to see if you understand a lesson.\nAnd you use tests every day to make decisions.\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:01.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple question,\nand the answer helps you learn something.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:04.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
