    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_215249.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:14.900\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: you want to see if a light bulb works. The test is to screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:28.700\nIf the light comes on, it passes the test!\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:36.500\nOr imagine you're baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the center.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:44.300\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's another test!\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:51.400\nSo, a test is just a simple way to make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:55.200\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it. They help us know if something is good to go. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
