    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_215653.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:17.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, it's a way to see if something is working correctly, or to check the quality of something.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:23.500\nThink of it like this: You bake a cake, and you taste it. That's a test!\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:29.300\nYou're testing to see if it tastes good. Or imagine a doctor checking your temperature.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:40.800\nThat's another test to see if you have a fever. Tests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoelaces are tied.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:55.300\nThe main idea is to gather information to see if something meets a certain standard or requirement. So, a test helps us understand if something is good, bad, working, or broken.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:01.600\nThat's the basics of what a test is. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
