    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_215752.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:25.600\nIt helps us find out if something works, if something is true, or if something is good enough.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:36.800\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:48.000\nA taste test checks if you like a certain food. And when you're building something, like a bridge, engineers run tests to make sure it's strong and safe.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:57.800\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:07.600\nThey can be simple, like asking a friend if they like your new haircut, or really complicated, like testing a rocket before it goes to space.\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:17.400\nEither way, the goal is the same: to find out something specific.\n\n01:17.400 --> 01:24.200\nTo recap, a test is a way to check something. They help us learn and make things better.\n\n01:24.200 --> 01:29.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
