    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_215930.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:18.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to the answer, you\u2019re measuring something to get your answer.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:23.300\nSo, what kind of things can you test? Well, lots!\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:32.100\nYou might test how strong something is, like a bridge. Or you might test how well you understand a topic at school with a quiz.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:41.700\nEven doctors use tests to see if you're healthy. For example, a simple test could be dropping a ball to see how high it bounces.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:50.000\nThe higher it bounces, the more bouncy it is! Or maybe tasting different foods to see which one you like best.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:58.600\nThat\u2019s a test too! Basically, a test is a way of gathering information by observing or measuring something.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:06.000\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
