    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_222411.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nWhat are they, and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking. You can't see inside, right?\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.400\nSo, you do a test! You stick a toothpick in.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:34.900\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Another example: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:39.300\nThey check your temperature and ask about your symptoms. That's a test!\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:50.500\nIn school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand a subject. So, tests are really just tools to help us learn and figure things out.\n\n00:50.500 --> 01:03.900\nTo recap, tests help us gather information by giving us a way to check something. They can be as simple as sticking a toothpick in a cake, or a bit more involved like a doctor's visit.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:12.200\nHopefully, that gives you a basic understanding of what a test is. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
