    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:03.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:03.800 --> 00:06.000\nspecifically, what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:09.100\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:09.100 --> 00:12.400\nIt\u2019s a process or a procedure designed to see if something is true,\n00:12.400 --> 00:13.900\nor to measure something.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:18.200\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health,\n00:18.200 --> 00:21.200\nor a teacher gives you a quiz to see what you've learned.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:25.300\nTests can be formal, like a big exam, or informal, like trying a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:28.600\nThe key is that you're trying to gather information or confirm something.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:31.900\nAnother example? Checking if a light bulb works before you screw it in.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:32.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:38.000\nSo, remember, a test is any method used to determine or confirm something.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:40.800\nIt\u2019s all about finding things out.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:41.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
