    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_222749.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.600\nA test is basically a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you understand something.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:35.600\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:45.200\nBut tests aren't just for school. Doctors use tests to check your health, and engineers use tests to make sure bridges are safe.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:57.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words. A math test checks if you understand numbers and equations. And a simple test of a lightbulb is just turning it on to see if it lights up!\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:03.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to see if something works or if you understand something.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:08.000\nIt helps us learn and improve. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
