    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_222834.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:06.900 --> 00:16.200\nToday we're going to explore something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:28.700\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to gather information or evaluate something.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:36.300\nThink of it as a measuring stick for knowledge, skills, or even the quality of a product.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:43.900\nFor example, a school exam is a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:55.000\nA taste test helps determine which food people like best. And a medical test can tell you if you're healthy.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.700\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes, but they all share the same goal: to provide us with information and help us make informed decisions.\n```"
  },
