    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nNow, a test, in the simplest terms, is a way to check something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like asking a question to see if you understand the answer.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:30.900\nTests can be used to check all sorts of things.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.700\nMaybe your teacher gives you a math test to see how well you understand addition.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:42.500\nOr maybe you get a blood test at the doctor to check your health.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:48.300\nLet's say you're baking a cake.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:54.100\nYou might stick a toothpick in the middle to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:59.900\nThat's a test! It's testing if the cake is done.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:08.500\nAnother example is checking the batteries in your remote control to see if they still work.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:12.800\nThat's also a test!\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:18.800\nSo, tests are just ways to find out information and see if something is working as it should.\n\n01:18.800 --> 01:27.400\nThey help us learn, stay healthy, and make sure things are working properly.\n\n01:27.400 --> 01:36.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
