    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_225022.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:14.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like asking a question to get an answer.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:30.900\nA test can be used to check if something works, if something is true, or even just to see what someone knows.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:37.700\nFor example, a simple test could be flipping a light switch to see if the light bulb works.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:44.500\nThat's a test!\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to test your understanding of a lesson.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:48.600\nAnother example?\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.700\nA doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:59.200\nSee?\nTests are all around us, helping us learn and understand things.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:05.700\nSo, in short, a test is a process designed to provide information.\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:09.700\nIt's a way of checking, verifying, or evaluating something.\n\n01:09.700 --> 01:12.200\nHope that helps!\n\n01:12.200 --> 01:15.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
