    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_225200.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:26.700\nNow, you might think of school tests, but a test, in a more general sense, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:32.500\nIt's a procedure designed to see if something is true, or to check the quality of something.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:38.300\nThink about it like this: a taste test is a way to see if food tastes good.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:44.400\nYou\u2019re testing the flavor!\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:50.300\nOr imagine you're testing a new toy to see if it works.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:53.700\nYou're trying it out, observing what happens, and drawing a conclusion.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:57.900\nMaybe it lights up, maybe it rolls, maybe it does nothing!\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:01.200\nThat's still a test result.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.800\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:09.900\nThey can be simple or complex, but the basic idea is always the same:\n\n01:09.900 --> 01:13.800\nto explore something and learn more about it.\n\n01:13.800 --> 01:15.700\nThat's tests in a nutshell!\n\n01:15.700 --> 01:21.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
