    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_225258.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.700\nA test is simply a way to find\nout something about something else.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:11.000\nThink of it like asking a question\nand getting an answer.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:12.900\nTests are used everywhere!\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:17.400\nImagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:21.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean,\nthe cake passes the test!\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:25.100\nOr, think about a doctor checking\nyour temperature.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:27.000\nThat\u2019s a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:31.800\nAnother example? Your spelling quizzes at school!\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:35.500\nThose tests show how well you know\nyour spelling words.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:39.600\nSo, a test is just a procedure\nused to gather information.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:44.700\nIt can be a simple observation\nor a more complex process,\nbut it all comes down to finding out something new.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:51.300\nTo recap, tests help us understand\nand evaluate things around us.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:55.100\nThey give us information we can\nuse to make decisions.\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
