  "495b07d9-12e2-42b2-92af-490ad8c535fd": {
    "id": "495b07d9-12e2-42b2-92af-490ad8c535fd",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:47:51.699619",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T22:54:34.506081",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_225434.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_225434.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:19.100\nThink of a test as a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you understand something. It\u2019s like a detective, finding out if things are as they should be.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:26.100\nThere are all sorts of tests. For example, your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:39.200\nOr, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned. Even baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're checking if the ingredients combine correctly and taste good!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:44.400\nLet's say you're testing a lightbulb.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:49.600\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:58.600\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If not, something's wrong. Tests help us find problems and make things better.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:06.600\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something. It helps us confirm things are working right and learn new things.\n\n01:06.600 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
