    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_230520.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:18.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see what you know or what something can do.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You turn it on, and the test is whether it lights up!\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:30.400\nTests help us understand things better.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:40.200\nImagine you're baking a cake. You taste it to test if it's sweet enough. That's a test!\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:51.600\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down a few times is kind of like a test to see if you've got your balance.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:59.800\nSo, tests are all about learning and checking things. They can be formal, like school exams, or informal, like tasting your cooking.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.300\nThey all help us figure things out and improve. In short, a test is simply a way to evaluate something.\n```"
