    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_231326.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.000\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something, whether it's how well you know a subject, or if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:30.900\nThe important thing is that a test should be fair and accurate. So, if you're testing how fast someone can run, you'd want to make sure everyone runs the same distance.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:39.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling. Or, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:42.300\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:54.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a simple way to gather information by asking a question, or performing an experiment, and then evaluating the answer.\n\n00:54.600 --> 00:58.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
