    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_231856.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:06.700\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:10.600\nNow, you've probably heard that word before, maybe in school,\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:13.000\nbut what does it really mean?\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:17.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.400\nWe're trying to find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:29.200\nYou flip the switch; that's the test.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:32.700\nIf the light comes on, the test passes!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:39.200\nAnother example: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:43.600\nThey'll check your temperature, listen to your heart,\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:46.000\nand see if everything is running smoothly.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:47.500\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:53.700\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:59.800\nWhether it's a lightbulb, your health, or even a recipe, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:59.800 --> 01:03.000\nIn short, a test is simply a check.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:07.500\nIt helps us determine if something is working as it should, or if something is true.\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:10.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
