    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.600\nNo, not the kind you take in school, but tests that we use to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:21.100\nThink of it like this: a test is simply a way to see if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:24.900\nImagine you bake a cake. The test is taking a bite!\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:28.400\nDoes it taste good? Is it cooked all the way through? That's your test.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:36.300\nOr, if you're checking if a lightbulb works, you flip the switch. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:51.000\nTests are super important because they help us find problems and fix them. They can be quick and easy, or more complicated, but they all have the same goal: to make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:59.600\nSo next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a way to check something and make sure it's doing its job.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
