    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_233448.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.100\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you probably think of school, right?\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:25.300\nBut in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:29.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:33.900\nSo, you put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:40.400\nYou're testing if the light bulb's working. Or, maybe you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:52.300\nYou stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, that's a test showing the cake is ready. So, a test is simply a method to evaluate something and see if it meets a certain criteria.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:57.400\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:01.000\nSo remember, tests are everywhere, helping us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
