    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:48:34.983690",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T23:50:31.917329",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_235031.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_235031.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:23.800\nIt helps us understand if something is true, correct, or working as expected. Think about it like this: a spelling test tells you if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:31.200\nOr, a taste test helps you decide which cookie tastes better. Tests aren't just for school, though.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:41.000\nWhen you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:52.100\nTests help us make decisions and learn new things. So, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and check if something is right.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:55.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0b874135-ea4c-41b5-8178-214ce55d2e4b": {
    "id": "0b874135-ea4c-41b5-8178-214ce55d2e4b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:48:35.793136",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-05T23:51:18.672598",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260105_235118.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_235118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.900\nNow, you might think of tests as scary exams, but really, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:23.900\nIt's a process of asking a question and then figuring out the answer through observation or experimentation.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:33.900\nThink about it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:51.300\nOr a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar. In both cases, they're performing a test to get information.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:58.000\nSo, whether it's checking if your cookies are done in the oven, or scientists running experiments, tests are all about gathering data and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.700\nThey help us learn and improve! Remember, a test is just a tool for finding things out.\n```"
  },
