    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260105_235345.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.100\nHi everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.100 --> 00:06.700\nToday we're going to explore something really fundamental:\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:08.800\nwhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.800 --> 00:12.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:15.000\nThink of it like this: you're trying to understand something,\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:17.300\nand a test gives you clues.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:21.600\nIt's a set of questions or tasks designed to measure your knowledge, skill, or ability.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:25.300\nFor example, a spelling test measures your knowledge of spelling.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:28.500\nA driving test measures your ability to drive.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:31.500\nEven tasting a new food is a kind of test to see if you like it!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:37.400\nSo, tests help us understand what we know and what we can do.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:40.900\nThey can also help us identify areas where we might need to learn more.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:43.300\nBasically, they are a way to check up on things.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:45.800\nApilage AI.\n```"
  },
