    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_000419.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:10.600\nWhat are they? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:18.100\nIt's a process designed to give us information. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:22.800\nYou do a simple test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it!\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:27.300\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done. That's a test!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:31.700\nOr maybe you want to know if a lightbulb works. You screw it in.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:36.100\nIf it lights up, the test passes.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:40.800\nTests aren't just for baking or lightbulbs, though.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:45.500\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:49.900\nTeachers use tests to see how well you've learned.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:54.300\nBasically, whenever you want to check something, you can use a test.\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:04.500\nSo, to recap: a test is a method for gathering information, from checking if a cake is baked to seeing if a lightbulb works.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:07.700\nIt helps us understand things better.\n```"
  },
  "39f63a36-6398-4aa9-87e2-38a76a6458e7": {
    "id": "39f63a36-6398-4aa9-87e2-38a76a6458e7",
