    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_000508.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:16.500\nToday we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:27.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. It's how we find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:31.400\nThink about it like this: if you bake a cake, you might test it by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:38.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:45.000\nOr, maybe you're learning to ride a bike. The test is whether you can balance and pedal without falling.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:50.300\nIf you can, you've passed the test! Tests are all around us.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:54.200\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:56.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a check. It helps us understand something better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
