    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_000551.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:25.900\nIt's how we find out if something is working correctly or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:34.400\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it works.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:43.100\nThe test is simply screwing it into a lamp to see if it lights up.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:51.800\nAnother example is baking a cake. You follow a recipe, and the test is tasting the cake to see if it\u2019s delicious!\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:54.100\nIn science, we might test if a plant grows better with different amounts of sunlight.\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:56.300\nWe observe and measure the results.\n\n00:56.300 --> 00:57.700\nSo, a test is just a way of gathering information to confirm or deny something.\n\n00:57.700 --> 00:58.500\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
