    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_001001.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.700\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's definitely one kind.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:20.900\nBut in general, a test is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: imagine you bake a cake. Tasting it is a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:36.400\nOr, if you build a birdhouse, you might watch it to see if birds actually use it. That's a test too!\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:46.900\nTesting helps us find problems and fix them. If the cake isn't sweet enough, you add more sugar next time.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:53.700\nIf birds don't use the birdhouse, you might need to change the entrance.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:00.600\nSo, testing is all about checking things and making them better. It\u2019s a fundamental part of learning and creating. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
