    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of getting a verbal answer, you get data or a result.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:30.600\nBasically, you give something a try, and then you see what happens.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:36.600\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:45.000\nYou screw it in, flip the switch, and see if it lights up. That's a test!\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:54.000\nOr imagine baking a cake. You follow a recipe, put it in the oven, and then taste it to see if it's good. That's another test!\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:04.000\nTests help us understand if things are working the way we expect, or if we need to make some changes.\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:09.000\nSo, remember, a test is all about trying something out to learn something new.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:14.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
