    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but often with a specific purpose.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:22.000\nSo, what kind of things can we test?\nWell, pretty much anything!\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:30.000\nYou might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\nOr a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:38.000\nHere's a simple example: Imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might taste the batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:46.200\nThat's a test!\nOr, if your toy car isn't working, you might test the batteries to see if they're dead.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:57.400\nBasically, a test helps us understand something better by giving us information or evidence.\nIt's a simple but powerful tool for learning and problem-solving.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:00.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
