    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_003131.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:12.100\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests! A test, in the simplest terms, is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:19.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking. You perform a test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:27.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Tests aren't just for baking though. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:36.100\nTeachers use tests to see how well you understand a lesson. Even your car goes through tests to make sure it's running smoothly.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:44.900\nSo, a test is really just a method to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:53.000\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us. To recap, tests are everywhere and they help us check if things are working as they should.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:59.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
