    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.640\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.640 --> 00:06.380\nToday we're tackling something fundamental: the Test.\n\n00:06.380 --> 00:10.430\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:10.430 --> 00:13.470\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:13.470 --> 00:17.320\nIt's basically asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:17.320 --> 00:20.930\nThink about it like this: a chef tests the soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:20.930 --> 00:25.020\nOr, you might test a new pen to see if it writes smoothly.\n\n00:25.020 --> 00:26.950\nIn both cases, you're performing a test.\n\n00:26.950 --> 00:31.800\nAnother example?\nA doctor tests your reflexes to see if your nervous system is working properly.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:35.410\nThey tap your knee, and your leg kicks out.\n\n00:35.410 --> 00:36.330\nThat's a test!\n\n00:36.330 --> 00:40.740\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of finding out information by checking something.\n\n00:40.740 --> 00:46.610\nIt's about observing a result and making a judgement based on that result.\n\n00:46.610 --> 00:51.240\nIt's a crucial part of learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:51.240 --> 00:54.340\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
