    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a really important topic: tests.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:36.400\nThe main idea behind a test is to see if something works, or if something is present, or even how well something performs.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:46.200\nWe use tests all the time in our daily lives, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:54.900\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:01.200\nOr, when you turn on a light switch, you're testing to see if the bulb works. So, to recap, a test is just a simple way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard. It\u2019s a question with an expected answer. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
