    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_004227.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means in a general sense?\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:16.000\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:24.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:36.500\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might do a test by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:49.600\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a toy car needs new batteries, you might try turning it on.\nIf it doesn't move, that's a test showing the batteries are probably dead.\n\n00:49.600 --> 01:00.000\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\nThe important thing is they help us gather information and make decisions.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:03.500\nSo, a test is just a way to check something out and see what's what.\n01:03.500 --> 01:07.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
