    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_010205.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like this: you test if your bicycle brakes work before you ride it.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:32.700\nYou test if the stove is hot before you put a pan on it.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:38.800\nYou're checking to see if something is in the state that you expect.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:47.400\nAnother example? Imagine you baked cookies.\nTo test if they\u2019re done, you might poke one with a toothpick.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:56.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookie passes the test!\nIf it\u2019s still gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:56.000 --> 01:07.600\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to verify something.\nYou perform an action, and then you see if the result matches what you expected.\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:12.600\nSimple as that!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
