    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_010551.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:09.000\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:14.900\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:17.500\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:23.100\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:24.600\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:29.700\nOr, think about a doctor checking your temperature.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:31.400\nThat's another kind of test.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:32.600\nto see if you have a fever.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:37.700\nTests can be formal, like a school exam to see what you've learned.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:42.000\nOr, they can be informal, like tasting soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.600\nThe main idea is to get information.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:52.100\nWe perform a test, and we get some data back that helps us understand something better.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:57.600\nSo, tests help us learn, diagnose, and make decisions every day.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```\nKey improvements and explanations:\n\n* **Adherence to Timing:**  The code precisely follows the timing requirements for each section (animation time + wait time).  This was the most critical requirement.  I've double-checked the math to ensure it adds up to 60.2 seconds.\n* **Image Placeholders:** Added `ImageMobject` with placeholder filenames (\"cake.png\", \"doctor.png\").  The code will work, but you MUST replace these with actual image files in the same directory as your Python script.  I've suggested relevant images.\n* **Visual Design:** Implemented the requested visual design elements:\n    * GOLD, BLUE_B, GREEN_B, TEAL_A, ORANGE, PINK colors are used.\n    * `RoundedRectangle` backgrounds are behind key text elements.\n    * Colored `Dot` objects are used as bullet points.\n    * Font sizes are set according to the specifications.\n* **Slow Animations:**  `run_time` is consistently set to 1.5 (or slightly higher).\n* **Long Wait Times:**  `self.wait()` values are long (3+ seconds) in each section.\n* **Clear Structure:** The code is clearly structured with comments indicating each section and its duration.\n* **Ending Sequence:** Includes the ending sequence with the Apilage AI text and background.\n* **FadeOut Clearing:**  `self.play(*[FadeOut(mob) for mob in self.mobjects], run_time=0.5)` is used to clear the screen between sections.  This ensures that only the intended elements are visible in each section.\n* **VGroup for Organization:** Uses `VGroup` to group related objects (e.g., image and text, background and text). This makes it easier to manipulate and animate these elements together.\n* **Image Handling:**  Uses `ImageMobject` which is the correct way to include images in Manim.  Remember to provide actual image files.\n* **Subtitle File:** Generated a basic subtitle file that corresponds to the narration.  You can refine this further if needed.\n* **No Unnecessary Animations:**  Avoided adding animations that weren't explicitly requested, to keep the code clean and focused on the core requirements.\n\nTo use this code:\n\n1.  **Install Manim:**  If you haven't already, install Manim: `pip install manim`\n2.  **Save the Code:** Save the code as a Python file (e.g., `test_explanation.py`).\n3.  **Place Images:** Put the image files (\"cake.png\", \"doctor.png\") in the same directory as the Python file. *Important: You must provide actual image files!*\n4.  **Run Manim:**  Run the Manim script from the command line: `manim -pql test_explanation.py TestExplanation` (This renders the video at low quality for faster testing. Change `-pql` to `-pqh` for high quality.)\n5. **Add audio:** Add the prerecorded audio back in.\n\nThis revised response should now meet all the requirements!  Let me know if you have any other questions."
  },
  "8e5437e7-56c4-40b6-851f-6c4a460f8ae9": {
    "id": "8e5437e7-56c4-40b6-851f-6c4a460f8ae9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:49:34.434047",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T01:06:37.288215",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_010637.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_010637.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.400\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:09.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:12.700\nIt could be your knowledge, your skills, or even your opinion.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:15.700\nThink of it like this: a ruler is a test to measure length.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:19.800\nA scale is a test to measure weight.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:24.400\nIn school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand the lessons.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:29.300\nFor example, a math test checks if you know your addition and subtraction.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:32.800\nA spelling test shows if you can write words correctly.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:37.900\nOutside of school, tests are everywhere too!\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:41.300\nWhen you try a new recipe, you're testing if it tastes good.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:45.400\nWhen you try to ride a bike, you're testing your balance.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:50.200\nSo, a test is just a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:53.200\nIt helps us learn and improve!\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:58.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
