    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_011323.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:18.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to see if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:23.400\nThat's a test!\nYou're testing if the lightbulb is functional.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:31.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things.\nMaybe you're testing how well you understand a new topic by taking a quiz.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:42.400\nOr perhaps a doctor is testing your blood to check your health.\nThe goal is to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:54.700\nFor example, a baker might test the oven temperature to make sure it's hot enough to bake a cake.\nOr a teacher might give a spelling test to see how well students have learned their words.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:04.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get information.\nIt helps us understand if things are working as they should.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "dd81e3d9-0606-48c8-9b1f-133e08a08640": {
    "id": "dd81e3d9-0606-48c8-9b1f-133e08a08640",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:49:39.484175",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T01:14:05.922277",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_011405.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_011405.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:18.000\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out how much you know about something. Think of it like a measuring tool, but instead of measuring inches or pounds, it measures your understanding.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:26.800\nIt could be a quiz at school, a driving exam, or even just checking if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it! All of these are tests.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:35.000\nFor example, a multiple-choice quiz helps your teacher see what you\u2019ve learned in class. And when you bake a cake, the toothpick test tells you if the inside is cooked.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:48.800\nSo, a test is simply a method for checking knowledge, skills, or even the condition of something. It helps us understand where we're at and what we might need to learn more about.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:57.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
