    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_012408.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.000\nNow, you might think of school when you hear that word, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as it should.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb. To test if it's good, you screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.500\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:36.100\nSame idea applies to more complex things. A chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:43.700\nOr a doctor might check your reflexes to test your nervous system.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:50.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple check to see if something is working properly. It's a way to know for sure if things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:50.900 --> 00:55.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
