    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_014323.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:09.300\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:09.300 --> 00:14.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:20.500\nIt helps us understand if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:29.700\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe by cooking it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:36.800\nOr, a doctor might test your eyesight to see how well you can see.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:42.800\nIn the world of technology, tests are used to make sure software and hardware are working correctly.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:50.400\nFor example, we might test a button on a website to make sure it actually takes you to the right page when you click it.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:52.900\nOr test a lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:56.200\nSo, a test is just a simple way to check if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:56.200 --> 00:57.100\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:57.100 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
