    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This VTT file was automatically generated and may contain errors. Please review and correct as needed.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.120\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.120 --> 00:06.200\nToday, we're diving into what a test actually is.\n00:06.200 --> 00:10.410\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n00:10.410 --> 00:16.940\nIt\u2019s a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n00:16.940 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n00:22.200 --> 00:25.820\nA chef might taste a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n00:25.820 --> 00:29.070\nAnd in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n00:29.070 --> 00:34.030\nTests aren't just for school, though.\n00:34.030 --> 00:37.120\nCompanies use them to see if someone is right for a job.\n00:37.120 --> 00:41.720\nScientists use them to prove or disprove theories.\n00:41.720 --> 00:48.240\nBasically, anything where you need to gather information in a structured way can be considered a test.\n00:48.240 --> 00:54.750\nSo, remember, a test is a tool for gathering information.\n00:54.750 --> 00:59.040\nIt helps us understand something better by evaluating it in a specific way.\n00:59.040 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
