    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_014521.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:08.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:08.500 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like this: you might test the temperature of water to see if it's hot or cold.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:15.000\nOr, a doctor might test your eyesight to see how well you can see.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:17.500\nSo, tests help us gather information.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:20.500\nThey can be simple, like tasting a cookie to see if it's sweet, or more complex, like a school exam.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:24.500\nThe important thing is that a test gives us a result, something we can learn from.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:28.500\nFor example, you might test different lightbulbs to see which one shines the brightest.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:32.000\nOr, you could test different recipes to see which one tastes the best.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:36.000\nTests are everywhere, helping us understand the world around us.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:41.000\nIn short, a test is a method for gathering information and learning something new.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:42.000\nIt's all about finding out!\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
