    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_020019.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:14.500\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:20.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you put it in a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:33.200\nThat's a test! We use tests all the time to see if something is working as expected. In school, tests help us understand what you've learned.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:42.300\nA math test checks your understanding of numbers, while a spelling test sees if you know how to write words correctly.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:51.900\nOutside of school, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy. Mechanics use tests to find out what\u2019s wrong with your car.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:58.600\nSo, whether it's a light bulb, your spelling skills, or your health, tests help us learn and solve problems.\n\n00:58.600 --> 01:02.300\nEssentially, a test is a way to gather information and make sure things are working the way they should.\n```"
  },
  "0d06c49d-719c-4006-ad4a-a6998f805df1": {
    "id": "0d06c49d-719c-4006-ad4a-a6998f805df1",
    "topic": "Test",
