    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_020105.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like an experiment, but often with a right or wrong answer.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:32.400\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:38.000\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:41.600\nYou test if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:45.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:51.100\nOr, think about taking a spelling test in school.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:55.300\nThat test shows you, and your teacher, how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:02.500\nTests can be about anything! From checking if your batteries are working, to seeing how much weight a bridge can hold.\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:07.800\nThey help us understand the world around us, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:13.700\nSo remember, a test is just a simple way to get information and learn something new.\n\n01:13.700 --> 01:16.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
