    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_020352.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.900\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:22.500\nIt's like a little experiment. Basically, a test involves giving something a try and seeing what happens.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:29.700\nWe're looking for a specific result. For example, a taste test checks if food tastes good.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:35.400\nA medical test checks if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:41.800\nLet's say you're testing a new lightbulb. You put it in a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:53.700\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, the test fails. Easy peasy. So, remember, a test is simply a way to see if something works or is true, by trying it out and looking for a specific result.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:00.200\nThat\u2019s the basic idea of what a test is. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
