    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:03.500\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:05.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:06.800\nSimply put, it's a way to check something.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:10.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:13.200\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:15.800\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:19.000\nOr maybe you want to know if your friend knows the answer to a question.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:19.700\nYou ask them!\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:20.800\nThat's a test too.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:24.700\nTests aren't just for cakes and quizzes.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:27.600\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are right.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:31.900\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:38.600\nBasically, a test helps us learn something or make sure something is working the way it should.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:44.500\nSo, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:49.500\nIt could be a cake, a friend's knowledge, or even a scientific idea.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:50.500\nNow you know!\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:52.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
