    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_020757.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:04.900 --> 00:11.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:20.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a method or procedure used to determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something or someone.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:45.100\nEven tasting a new recipe is a type of test to see if you like it! Tests can be formal, like a standardized exam, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit before you buy them.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:52.600\nThe main idea is that you're gathering information to make a decision or understand something better.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:56.700\nSo, tests are all about finding things out!\n\n00:56.700 --> 00:59.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "37d51a86-2122-4d9c-a324-bdeed63745bf": {
    "id": "37d51a86-2122-4d9c-a324-bdeed63745bf",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:50:26.183007",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T02:08:41.678186",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_020841.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_020841.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in the world of computers, a test is simply a way of checking if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:35.800\nComputer tests are similar. We write small bits of code that test if our main code is doing what we expect.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:45.500\nFor example, imagine you're building a calculator. One test might check if 2 + 2 actually equals 4.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:54.400\nAnother test might check if dividing 10 by 2 gives you 5.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:12.800\nThese little tests help us catch mistakes early and make sure our programs are reliable. So, to recap, a test is a way to check if a piece of code is working correctly by giving it specific inputs and verifying the outputs match what we expect.\n\n01:12.800 --> 01:19.800\nThey're super important for building reliable software!\n\n01:19.800 --> 01:27.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
