    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_021326.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well something works or how good something is.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like checking if your cookies are done baking. You use a toothpick \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:34.400\nTests help us understand if something meets certain standards. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:45.900\nOr, a crash test for a car sees how safe it is in an accident.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:52.900\nAnother example: If you're building a birdhouse, you might test if the roof keeps the rain out.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:02.000\nYou pour water on it and see if the inside stays dry. That's a test too! So, remember, a test is just a way of finding out information. It helps us see if something is working as it should and meeting our expectations. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
