    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.800\nToday we're tackling something fundamental: what is a test?\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:16.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something. It's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.700\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling. \n\n00:23.700 --> 00:28.500\nA taste test checks your ability to distinguish flavors.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:35.000\nA stress test on a bridge checks its performance under pressure. See? They all gather information.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:45.400\nSo, a test isn\u2019t just about getting a grade in school. It's a tool used in all sorts of situations to learn and understand.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:53.700\nIt helps us see what we know, what we can do, and how things work. It's all about gathering information through a structured process.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:57.700\nThat's the basic idea behind a test.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
