    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_023252.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test is basically a way to check how well you know something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like a measuring stick for your knowledge.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:32.500\nIt helps you, and sometimes your teachers, understand what you've learned and where you might need a little more practice.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:42.700\nThere are all sorts of tests. You might have a quiz in class, which is a small test covering a specific topic.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:53.400\nOr maybe a bigger exam at the end of a unit, that checks everything you've learned.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:03.300\nEven just trying to remember something is a mini-test for yourself!\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:13.000\nFor example, imagine you're learning about animals. A test might ask you to name three types of mammals, or explain what an amphibian is.\n\n01:13.000 --> 01:22.900\nThe answers you give show how well you understand the animal kingdom.\n\n01:22.900 --> 01:33.000\nSo, remember, tests are just tools to help you learn and grow. They show you what you know and what you can work on.\n\n01:33.000 --> 01:39.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
