    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_023712.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:04.600\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:06.600\nnot the kind you dread taking,\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:09.000\nbut the kind that help us figure things out.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:12.300\nA test is really just a way to check if something works,\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:14.700\nor to see what something is like.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:17.800\nThink of it like this: if you're baking a cake,\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:20.700\nyou might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:22.200\nThat's a test to see if it's done.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:24.900\nOr, if you're buying a new toy,\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:27.600\nyou might try it out for a few minutes.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:29.200\nThat's a test to see if you like it.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:34.000\nTests can be simple, like tasting your food to see if it needs more salt,\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.500\nor more complicated, like doctors running blood work to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:41.300\nThe important thing is that a test gives you information.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:47.700\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to gather information about something, whether it's a cake, a toy, or even your own health.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:53.700\nThey help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:55.500\nThis video was created by\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:56.200\nApilage AI.\n```"
  },
