    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_024325.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:08.000\nToday we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:16.000\nThink of a test as a way to check if you know something, or if something works like it should.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:21.000\nIt's like a little investigation to see what's up.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:27.000\nThe main idea is to ask a question or try something out, and then see what happens.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:34.000\nIf you're baking a cake, you might test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:38.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:44.000\nAnother example is a spelling test at school.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:48.000\nIt checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:52.000\nSo, tests help us learn and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:59.000\nThey can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all have the same goal: to find out information.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:03.000\nRemember, tests are just tools to help us understand things better.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:05.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
