    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.200\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test,\" but what does it really mean?\n\n00:03.200 --> 00:07.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:11.100\nIt helps us understand if something works, if something is true, or if something is good.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:17.400\nThink about it like this: A doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:22.000\nA chef might taste a dish to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:27.300\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:31.000\nIn each of these examples, the test is giving us information.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:35.500\nThe doctor learns about your health, the chef learns about the flavor, and your teacher learns about your spelling skills.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:42.400\nSo, a test is just a tool for learning and understanding. It's how we check things!\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:44.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
