    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_025044.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.240 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.400\nNow, when you hear \"test,\" you might think of school.\nBut in the world of software, a test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and you want to make sure it rolls.\nThe \"test\" is pushing it to see if it moves!\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:36.800\nIn software, we write little bits of code that automatically do those checks for us.\nFor example, if you have a calculator app, a test might be to check if 2 plus 2 really equals 4.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:44.500\nOr, if you have a website, a test might check if the login button actually takes you to the right page.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:52.100\nSo, tests are just a way to make sure our software is working correctly and doing what we expect it to.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:57.600\nThey help us find problems early, before they cause bigger issues down the road.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:06.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
