    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:19.000\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:30.100\nNow, a test is basically a way to check something.\nIt could be anything from checking if you understand a lesson, to checking if a cake is ready to come out of the oven.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:35.900\nThe main idea is to see if something meets a certain standard or goal.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:41.900\nThink about it like this: you might take a math test to see if you've learned the addition facts.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:47.900\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:53.900\nAnother example?\nImagine you\u2019re baking cookies.\nYou poke them with a toothpick \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:59.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies are done.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:04.900\nSo, tests help us understand where we are and if we've reached our target.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:08.900\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the core purpose is always the same: to evaluate something.\n\n01:08.900 --> 01:12.500\nThat's the basics of what a test is!\n\n01:12.500 --> 01:15.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
