    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:51:06.003474",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T02:59:28.919340",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_025928.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_025928.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:30.600\nIt's a method or procedure used to determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\nThink of it like this: a taste test for a new cookie recipe is a test to see if people like it.\nOr a doctor giving you a check-up is performing tests to see how healthy you are.\nThey're gathering information.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:38.300\nSo, tests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb works by turning it on.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:51.900\nOr they can be more complex, like running experiments to see if a new medicine is effective.\nThe key thing is, they help us learn and make informed decisions.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:03.400\nTo recap, a test is a way to gather information and learn something about something else.\nIt helps us figure things out.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:09.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a9c470c5-9e56-4748-98ac-6f0fc84d0c23": {
    "id": "a9c470c5-9e56-4748-98ac-6f0fc84d0c23",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
