    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:51:06.732347",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T03:00:14.107242",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_030013.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_030013.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:15.900\nNow, don't worry, this isn't the kind you cram for!\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:25.400\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:30.700\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake.\nYou taste it \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:43.300\nYou're checking if it tastes good.\nOr, if you're buying a new toy, you might press all the buttons \u2013 testing if they work.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:55.700\nSo, a test is really just a way of asking a question and getting an answer.\nIt can be as simple as a taste test, or something a little more complicated.\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:00.300\nBut the basic idea is always the same: to check and see if something is as it should be.\nThat's it! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
