    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_031434.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.000\nWhat are they, and why are they important? Simply put, a test is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:26.200\nIt helps us understand if something works correctly, or if someone knows something. Think of it like this: A teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand the lesson.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:36.600\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste a little bit of the batter \u2013 that's a test to see if it tastes good before you bake the whole thing!\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:43.100\nTests aren\u2019t just for school or cooking. Engineers test bridges to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:49.600\nDoctors run tests to figure out what's making you sick. So, tests are all around us,\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:58.300\nhelping us learn and make sure things are working as they should. They help us identify problems and improve things.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:07.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. They're important for learning, safety, and making things better.\n\n01:07.200 --> 01:12.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
