    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_031626.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something scary, like in school, but in reality, a test is just a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:31.500\nYou plug it in and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:35.900\nThe test result is either the lightbulb lights up, or it doesn't.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:42.100\nSame thing with baking a cake. You taste it to see if it's good.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:46.600\nThat's a test too! Tests help us understand if something meets our expectations.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:52.800\nThey can be really simple, like checking if your shoes fit, or a little more complicated.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:06.500\nBut the basic idea is always the same: we're checking to see if something works as intended.\n\n01:06.500 --> 01:10.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n01:10.100 --> 01:16.800\nIt helps us know if our expectations are being met.\n\n01:16.800 --> 01:19.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
