    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_031829.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: the test.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:22.100\nThink of it like this: you test a lightbulb to see if it lights up. That's a test!\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:31.400\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it. Before you leave the house, you might test if your keys are in your pocket. You do that by reaching in and checking.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:35.900\nAnother example? A baker might taste a cake batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:50.200\nSo, to recap, a test is simply a way to find out if something is working as expected, or to confirm something is true. It's all about checking!\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:55.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
