    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_032003.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: it's how we gather information or check if something works the way it should.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:37.200\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:43.200\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:49.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done!\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:55.200\nTests aren\u2019t just in science or cooking, though. Taking a quiz in school?\n\n00:55.200 --> 01:01.100\nThat's a test to see how well you understand the material. Basically, a test helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working right. So, next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a way of finding things out! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
