    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.600\nYou might think of tests as something you take in school, but in general, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:21.500\nIt's a process designed to gather information.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:26.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:33.500\nYour test? Screwing it into a lamp and turning it on. If it lights up, the test is positive \u2013 the bulb works!\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:38.000\nIf it doesn't, the test is negative.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:48.600\nAnother example: a doctor might run blood tests to see if you have a vitamin deficiency. Or a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:60.100\nIn each case, they're performing a test to get an answer. So, remember, a test is just a way of gathering information to answer a question.\n\n00:60.100 --> 00:64.300\nIt\u2019s a simple process that helps us learn more about the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
