    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_033049.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.250\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.250 --> 00:04.040\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.740 --> 00:05.950\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.450 --> 00:11.020\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.020 --> 00:14.870\nIt's a process used to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:15.470 --> 00:20.110\nThink of it like this: a teacher gives you a quiz to test what you learned in class.\n\n00:20.710 --> 00:25.170\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to see how healthy you are.\n\n00:25.570 --> 00:28.940\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if the recipe works!\n\n00:29.540 --> 00:33.320\nTests can come in many forms: multiple choice, true or false, even practical demonstrations.\n\n00:33.820 --> 00:36.220\nThe important thing is they give us information.\n\n00:36.720 --> 00:40.590\nThey help us understand where we're at and what we might need to work on.\n\n00:41.190 --> 00:44.740\nSo, in short, a test is just a way of gathering information to measure something.\n\n00:45.240 --> 00:47.640\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n00:48.240 --> 00:49.820\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
