    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:12.200\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:19.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you poke them with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:25.200\nIn science, tests help us see if our ideas are correct.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:34.900\nFor example, if you think plants grow faster with more sunlight, you could test that by giving some plants lots of light and others less. Then you'd compare how they grow.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:39.000\nAnother example? Imagine you're trying out a new recipe.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:43.100\nThe taste test is crucial!\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:48.100\nDoes it need more salt? More sugar? That's testing in action!\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:51.000\nSo remember, a test is just a way to find out\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:53.900\nif something is true or works the way we think it does.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:01.500\nIt helps us learn and improve things all the time. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
