    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:27.400\nThink about it like this: a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt. Or, you might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:32.100\nSee? Tests can be used to evaluate all sorts of things!\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:40.700\nAnother example is a weather balloon. Scientists launch it to test the air temperature and pressure high above the ground.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:50.500\nThe balloon sends back data, giving them valuable information. So, to recap, a test helps us learn something.\n\n00:50.500 --> 01:00.300\nIt's a process of asking a question, performing an action, and then analyzing the results. It's all about gathering information!\n\n01:00.300 --> 01:03.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
