    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_034555.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:12.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:22.100\nWe use them all the time! Think of it like a question that needs an answer.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:27.400\nIt could be a school test to see what you've learned,\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:33.000\nor a simple test to see if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:38.600\nYou flip the switch, right? That's the test!\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:43.100\nIf the light comes on, the bulb passes the test.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:47.600\nIf it doesn't, well, you know it's time for a new one.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:54.300\nAnother example? Baking a cake! You test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:54.300 --> 00:58.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n```"
