    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_035915.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.500\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into something called a test.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:19.300\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking, so you stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:38.800\nBasically, a test helps us find out if something is true, false, working, or broken.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:46.500\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:55.000\nOr, maybe you take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a topic. Tests can be big or small, formal or informal.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:59.400\nThe important thing is they give us information.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:00.400\nSo, a test is simply a method used to get information, to check if something is correct or working as it should.\n01:00.400 --> 01:04.900\nThat's the basic idea!\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:05.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
