  "113ff631-7d7e-4bb2-b2d8-b09ba42a3a6c": {
    "id": "113ff631-7d7e-4bb2-b2d8-b09ba42a3a6c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:52:06.060468",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T04:05:33.911641",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_040533.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_040533.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.900\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like this: you have a lightbulb, and you want to know if it's good.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:28.900\nThe test is to screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:36.600\nIf it lights up, the test passes! It's working! If it doesn't, well, the test fails, and the lightbulb is probably broken.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:39.800\nAnother example? Maybe you baked cookies.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:43.000\nThe test? Trying one!\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:47.500\nIf it tastes good, the test passes. If it's burnt, it fails.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:49.000\nSimple, right?\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:58.900\nSo, a test is just a method to see if something meets a certain standard or works the way it should.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:01.100\nIt\u2019s all about checking and verifying.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:05.200\nRemember, tests help us make sure things are working properly!\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:06.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
