    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_040735.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nToday we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:25.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly or meeting a certain standard. Think of it like this: before you leave the house, you might test if your shoes are tied.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:34.700\nThe main idea is to see if something passes or fails based on a specific set of rules. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:42.500\nA taste test might see if you like a certain flavor.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:53.700\nAnother example could be testing a new lightbulb to see if it lights up. If it does, it passes the test! If it doesn't, well, it fails.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:04.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is doing what it's supposed to do. In summary, tests are everywhere, helping us make sure things are working as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
