    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_041134.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:14.100\nWhat are they and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:21.800\nIt's like a measuring stick for your knowledge! Imagine you're learning about animals.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:28.500\nA test might ask you to name different animals or describe what they eat.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:35.200\nOr, if you're learning math, a test could involve solving some simple addition problems.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:44.700\nSee? Tests can come in different forms too. Multiple choice, true or false, or even just writing down your answers.\n\n00:44.700 --> 00:52.600\nThe important thing is that they help you and your teachers understand what you've learned and what you might need to work on a little more.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:54.600\nSo, tests are really just a tool to help you learn better.\n```"
  },
