    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_041350.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the wonderful world of tests.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:15.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, right?\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:19.400\nYou might poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:26.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. Tests aren't just for baking, though.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:32.500\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Teachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:45.000\nEven video games have tests \u2013 like challenges to see if you can beat a level. The goal is always the same: to get information and see if something is working as it should.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:56.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something. From baking a cake to playing a game, tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:00.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
