    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_042025.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.800\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:23.900\nIt's a process designed to see if something is true, accurate, or working correctly. Think of it like this: your doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:33.500\nOr, a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it has enough sugar. In school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:44.900\nSo, tests can be big or small, formal or informal. But they all share the same goal: to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:53.500\nWhether it's checking your eyesight or taking a quiz, a test helps us understand more about the world around us and ourselves.\n\n00:53.500 --> 01:03.600\nTo recap, a test is a method of gathering information to determine the status of something.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:06.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
