    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nA test is simply a way to find out something specific. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but often with a consistent way to measure the result.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:26.900\nSo, how does this work? Well, a test usually has a set of steps or questions designed to measure a specific skill or knowledge.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:35.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know how to spell words. A taste test checks which food you prefer.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:41.500\nEven a simple temperature check is a test! It tests whether you have a fever.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:49.700\nThe important thing is that a test gives us some information, helps us learn, and lets us know where we stand.\n\n00:49.700 --> 00:60.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a process used to gather information or evaluate something. It helps us understand things better.\n\n00:60.000 --> 00:63.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
