    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like an experiment or a way to check if something is true. For example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:28.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. That's a test!\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:36.300\nOr, think about a spelling test at school. It helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:46.900\nSo, tests can come in many forms. They could be a quiz, a science experiment, or even just trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:56.500\nThe key thing is, a test helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:03.900\nTo recap: A test is a way to find something out. It uses questions or experiments to check if something is true or correct.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:07.500\nTests help us learn!\n\n01:07.500 --> 01:11.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
