    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_044855.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! \nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.000\nWhat are they? \nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:24.500\nIt\u2019s how we check if something is true, works correctly, or if someone understands something.\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\nOr a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:34.200\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\nThey're like little puzzles that show what you know.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:43.000\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nA math test checks if you understand how to solve problems.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:55.000\nThese tests aren't meant to trick you, but to show you and your teacher what you're good at and what you might need some extra help with.\n\n00:55.000 --> 01:05.400\nSo, remember, tests are just tools for learning and discovering.\nThey help us understand the world around us and ourselves a little bit better.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:08.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
