    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_045243.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.300\nWhat are they, and why do we need them?\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:20.300\nThink of it like this: you have an idea, and you want to know if it's correct.\nA test helps you find out!\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:31.000\nIt could be anything from a spelling test in school, where you check if you know your words, to testing a new cookie recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:41.700\nThe main idea is to try something out and see what happens.\nFor example, if you're learning to ride a bike, falling down is a kind of test!\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:53.100\nIt shows you what not to do next time.\nOr, if you're planting seeds, and some sprout and some don't, that's a test of which seeds were healthy.\n\n00:53.100 --> 01:02.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it works or if it's correct.\nThey help us learn and improve.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:06.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
