    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.100\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something, to see if it works or if it's true.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: you test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:31.300\nOr imagine testing a lightbulb. You screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:35.700\nIf it lights up, the lightbulb passes the test. It works!\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:42.900\nTests aren't just for physical things, though. You take a test in school to show what you've learned. The test checks your knowledge.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:54.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something, whether it's a cake, a lightbulb, or your knowledge. It helps us understand if something is working as it should or if something is true.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:03.799\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
