    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_050821.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.400 --> 00:02.900\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:05.700\nNow, you might think of school exams,\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:10.800\nbut a test in a general sense is really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:15.500\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and then you taste it.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:18.000\nThat taste is a test to see if it's sweet enough and tastes good.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:23.700\nOr, imagine you\u2019re building a tower of blocks. You gently push it.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:25.500\nThat's a test to see if it's stable.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:32.200\nTests can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch, or more complicated,\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.700\nlike seeing if a new medicine helps people feel better.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:45.300\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something is doing what we expect it to do.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:48.600\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way of checking things.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:51.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
