    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:24.100\nThink of it like this: You might test if a lightbulb works by flipping the switch. You're checking if it lights up.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:32.700\nOr maybe you test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:40.400\nTests are important because they help us know if things are working correctly or if something needs to be fixed.\n\n00:40.400 --> 00:50.400\nWhether it's testing a new recipe, checking your spelling, or making sure a toy is safe, tests help us learn and improve.\n\n00:50.400 --> 01:02.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it meets a certain standard. Tests are all around us, helping us every day.\n\n01:02.100 --> 01:05.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
