    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_052251.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:13.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well someone or something performs.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You turn it on \u2013 that's the test! If it lights up, it passes.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:26.600\nTests help us understand strengths and weaknesses.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:36.000\nFor example, a school test checks how well you've learned the material.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:46.200\nA strength test on a bridge checks if it can handle heavy weight.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:57.700\nSo, whether it\u2019s a pop quiz, a quality check on a product, or even trying out a new recipe, you're performing a test.\nIt's all about finding out if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.200\nIn short, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working properly.\n```"
