    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_052416.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:06.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests\n\n00:06.100 --> 00:08.100\nspecifically, what a test is\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:08.900\nin general terms.\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:11.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:14.700\nIt's a process we use to check something, or to see if something works\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:16.300\nthe way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:18.800\nThink of it like this: a taste test is a way to find out\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:20.500\nif food tastes good.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:23.100\nOr, a spelling test helps us see if we've learned how to spell\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:23.800\nwords correctly.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:27.400\nEven a doctor giving you a check-up is a type of test\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:28.500\nto see if you're healthy!\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:32.300\nSo, whether it\u2019s checking the flavor of soup, seeing how well you remember facts,\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:34.200\nor making sure your body is working right,\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:37.400\ntests are all about gathering information.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:39.600\nThey help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:41.400\nThat's the basic idea of a test!\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:44.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
