    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like an experiment, or a way of checking something. We use tests all the time without even realizing it.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:33.400\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like the taste.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:44.500\nOr, when you try to turn on a light switch and the light doesn't come on, you're testing if the lightbulb works.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:57.500\nYou're observing and drawing a conclusion. Tests can be simple, like that lightbulb example, or more complicated, like a school exam. But the basic idea is always the same: you're trying to answer a question by gathering information.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.100\nSo, a test is a process of gathering information to answer a question. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
