    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" before, right?\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:17.200\nBut what does it really mean? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:30.100\nIt could be a person, an object, or even an idea. We use tests to see how well something works, what it's made of, or if it's true or false.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:39.300\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:48.600\nA baker might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good. Or, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:51.900\nSo, tests help us learn more and make better decisions.\n\n00:51.900 --> 00:55.600\nThey can be simple or complex, but the goal is always the same: to get information.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:57.500\nRemember, a test is just a way to find things out.\n\n00:57.500 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
