    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! \n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.500\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:09.000\nNow, in everyday language, a test is really just a way to find something out, right?\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:15.000\nIt's a process you use to check if something is true or correct, or to see how well something works.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:19.000\nThink about it: a taste test lets you see if you like a new flavor.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.000\nA spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.000\nEven checking if your car starts in the morning is a kind of test to see if your battery is working!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:37.000\nSo, essentially, a test is an action or series of actions used to gather information and make a decision.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:45.000\nFrom simple taste tests to more complicated medical tests, they all help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:48.000\nThat's the basics of what a test is!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:52.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
