    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_054403.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:18.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about someone or something.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way. For example, a spelling test helps us see how well someone knows how to spell words.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:40.600\nOr, a taste test can help us figure out which cookie tastes the best!\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:53.000\nIn science, tests are often called experiments. Scientists might test if a plant grows better in sunlight or in shade.\n\n00:53.000 --> 01:03.500\nSo, tests help us gather information and make decisions. They can be as simple as asking a friend if they like pizza, or as complicated as a medical exam.\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:12.700\nThe important thing is that they give us valuable insights. To recap, a test is a structured way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:12.700 --> 01:15.900\nThey come in all shapes and sizes and help us understand the world around us better.\n\n01:15.900 --> 01:16.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
