    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.500\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:27.500\nSo, what kind of things can we test? Well, lots!\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:32.700\nWe can test if a light bulb works by turning it on. That's a test!\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:39.400\nOr, think about baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:46.100\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Similarly, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:54.700\nTests help us understand the world around us and make informed decisions.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:02.000\nBasically, a test is just a way of gathering information to see if something is true or false, works or doesn't work, or meets a certain requirement.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:09.300\nIt's a fundamental part of learning and problem-solving.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:16.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
