    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:19.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:23.300\nYou do a test! You stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:29.900\nIf it comes out clean, the test tells you the cake is ready.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:36.300\nTests are used everywhere. Doctors use tests to see if you\u2019re healthy.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:42.700\nTeachers use tests to see what you\u2019ve learned.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:49.100\nEven your phone runs tests to make sure all its parts are working correctly.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:55.500\nFor example, a doctor might test your blood to check your sugar levels.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:01.800\nOr, in school, you might take a quiz to see if you understand the material.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:13.000\nSo, a test is basically a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n01:13.000 --> 01:19.300\nWhether it's a cake, your health, or your knowledge, tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:19.300 --> 01:24.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
