    "subtitles": "[WebVTT]\n```\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you might test if a cake is done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:27.600\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\nIn general, a test helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:39.200\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check if your body is healthy.\nOr, a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and reliable.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:49.000\nSo, tests are all about checking things.\nThey help us understand if something is working as expected or if it needs improvement.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:57.400\nRemember, a test is just a way to learn more about something!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a6e653d7-fb87-4631-86a5-680cac2df393": {
    "id": "a6e653d7-fb87-4631-86a5-680cac2df393",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:53:35.547533",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T05:54:56.243159",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_055456.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_055456.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like a ruler, but instead of measuring length, we can measure knowledge, skills, or even abilities.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:35.000\nThe goal is to see how well you understand or can do something.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:44.100\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling rules.\nA driving test assesses your ability to safely operate a car.\nAnd a baking test might measure how well you can follow a recipe!\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:54.700\nBasically, tests help us understand what you know and where you might need some extra help.\nThey're a common way to learn and grow.\nSo next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a tool for measuring and understanding!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "43c3fac2-f60f-4fca-acd4-0a00fb7a2c84": {
    "id": "43c3fac2-f60f-4fca-acd4-0a00fb7a2c84",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:53:36.059140",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T05:55:38.136915",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_055537.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_055537.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what is a test?\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process designed to get information or see if something works.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like this: a spelling test in school checks how well you know your words.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:29.900\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:39.800\nAnother example? A doctor might run blood tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:53.800\nTests help us confirm things, identify problems, and learn more. So, a test is really just a systematic way of gathering information or evaluating something. It can be formal, like a quiz, or informal, like tasting that cake.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:00.300\nTesting helps us learn and improve. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "52f1b029-74af-4363-9f58-9301bc11d0bf": {
    "id": "52f1b029-74af-4363-9f58-9301bc11d0bf",
    "topic": "Test",
