    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_055843.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests! \n\n00:05.800 --> 00:13.500\nWhat are they, and why do we use them? \n\n00:13.500 --> 00:26.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to see what you know or can do. It helps measure your understanding. \n\n00:26.700 --> 00:29.900\nThink of it like this: \n\n00:29.900 --> 00:33.100\nif you're learning to bake a cake, a test could be\u2026 \n\n00:33.100 --> 00:36.000\nwell, baking the cake! \n\n00:36.000 --> 00:39.800\nThe finished cake shows if you understood the recipe and the steps involved.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:42.900\nAnother example? \n\n00:42.900 --> 00:44.500\nA spelling test! \n\n00:44.500 --> 00:48.900\nIt shows if you've learned how to spell specific words. \n\n00:48.900 --> 00:50.700\nThe higher your score, \n\n00:50.700 --> 00:53.500\nthe better you understand the spelling rules. \n\n00:53.500 --> 00:57.500\nSo, tests aren\u2019t scary. They\u2019re just tools to help you, and your teachers, see how far you've come in learning something new. They help identify what you know well and what you might need a little extra help with. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
