    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_061835.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:18.600\nNow, you\u2019ve probably taken lots of tests already, but what is a test, really?\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:28.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It\u2019s a procedure designed to evaluate something, whether that\u2019s your knowledge, a product's quality, or even someone's personality.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:40.100\nThink about it like this: a baking test could be tasting a cake to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:51.000\nOr, a spelling test checks how well you remember how to write words.\n\n00:51.000 --> 01:03.700\nIn science, you might test a new fertilizer on plants to see if it helps them grow.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:07.300\nSo, a test is just a structured way to get information.\n01:07.300 --> 01:11.800\nIt helps us understand things better, make decisions, and learn more.\n01:11.800 --> 01:15.300\nRemember, tests aren't always about grades; they're about learning and discovering.\n01:15.300 --> 01:18.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
