    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T06:42:19.245187",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_064219.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_064219.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.300\nIt helps us learn more about a person, an object, or even an idea. Think about it like this: a spelling test helps your teacher understand how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:31.400\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:35.300\nSee? Tests are everywhere! They give us information.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:44.500\nFor example, a doctor might use a blood test to check if you're healthy. A scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:56.700\nAnd you might test out different crayons to see which one makes the brightest color. So, to sum it up, a test is a process used to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:07.300\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the goal is always the same: to find out more.\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:12.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
