    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_064435.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.400\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:26.400\nIt could be checking if a lightbulb works, or if you know the answer to a question. Basically, you're trying to find out if something is true or false, right or wrong, working or not working.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:37.000\nThink of it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. Or, a battery test checks if a battery still has power.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:45.500\nSo, in both cases, we're testing something to see if it meets a certain standard or passes a certain requirement.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:53.900\nA test helps us understand the condition or quality of something. In short, a test is all about checking things!\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a0d8ea6b-89a0-4bcd-951c-eeec492a77f1": {
    "id": "a0d8ea6b-89a0-4bcd-951c-eeec492a77f1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:54:17.588182",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T06:45:25.399477",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_064525.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_064525.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.300\nNow, in everyday life, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:27.100\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer. In science and other fields, a test is a procedure designed to confirm or deny a hypothesis.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:38.700\nBasically, it's a structured experiment to see if your idea is right. For example, if you think plants grow better with more sunlight, your test could be growing two identical plants, one in sunlight and one in shade.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:46.300\nOr, if you believe a new medicine works, you'd test it on a group of people to see if they get better.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:56.000\nSo, a test is really just a method to gather evidence and see if your assumptions hold true. It's all about learning and exploring!\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
