    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_064845.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.600\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:28.700\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what answer you get. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:38.800\nFor example, if you flip a light switch and the light turns on, that's a test to see if the lightbulb is working.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:48.200\nOr, if you taste a new food, that's a test to see if you like it.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:57.600\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned. And in science, tests help us understand how things work.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:04.400\nMaybe you\u2019re testing if a plant grows faster with more sunlight. The test helps give us an answer. So, remember, a test is simply a way of checking something to get an answer. It\u2019s about asking a question and seeing what happens. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
