    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_065024.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of testing.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:15.700\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works like it should.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:24.300\nIt's like when you try a new recipe \u2013 you're testing to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:32.700\nIn general, a test is a procedure to determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:45.600\nIt could be anything! From checking if a lightbulb turns on, to seeing if your car engine is running smoothly.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:52.600\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:52.600 --> 01:04.300\nOr, if you're building with blocks, you might test if your tower can stand up without falling over.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:16.000\nTests help us learn and improve. They show us what we're doing right, and what we need to work on.\n\n01:16.000 --> 01:20.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as expected.\n01:20.000 --> 01:24.700\nIt helps us understand, learn, and make things better.\n\n01:24.700 --> 01:28.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
