    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests!\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.000\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, it's a way to check something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:22.700\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. Think about it: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:31.700\nThat's a test! Or, if you're buying a new phone, you might turn it on and tap around to make sure the screen works.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:39.700\nAnother test! Tests help us know if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:47.700\nThey can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on, or more complex, like a doctor running blood work.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:56.600\nEssentially, a test gives us information. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:04.200\nIt helps us understand if things are working as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
