  "5714da72-63de-4851-bb14-2de5b5559446": {
    "id": "5714da72-63de-4851-bb14-2de5b5559446",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:54:45.750738",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T07:20:43.391513",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_072043.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_072043.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests, and no, not the kind you worry about in school.\n\n00:09.400 --> 00:19.600\nIn the world of computers, a \"test\" is just a way of checking if something is working as it should.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:27.900\nThink of it like taste-testing a cake. You wouldn't serve it without making sure it tastes good first, right?\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:36.100\nWell, computer programs are the same. We write little mini-programs, called tests, to make sure the bigger program is doing what we expect.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:44.600\nFor example, if we're building a calculator, we might write a test to check if 2 + 2 really equals 4.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:51.000\nIf the test passes, great! If it fails, we know there's a problem we need to fix.\n\n00:51.000 --> 01:01.200\nSo, in short, tests are like quality control for software. They help us catch mistakes early and make sure everything runs smoothly.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0cc9028a-e49a-4e39-8d11-e5e57440f9b6": {
    "id": "0cc9028a-e49a-4e39-8d11-e5e57440f9b6",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:54:46.402235",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T07:21:34.359050",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_072134.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_072134.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:14.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:21.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:26.500\nThat's a test! In school, tests help us understand how much you've learned about a topic.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:32.300\nBut tests aren't just for school. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:42.400\nA chef tastes the soup to see if it needs more salt. Those are all tests, too!\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:48.600\nSo, a test is really just a process. You ask a question, or perform an action, and then see what the result is.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:52.200\nIt helps you learn and make decisions. That's the core of what a test is all about. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f89393dd-9f4f-4705-b9f5-9bf95aef711f": {
    "id": "f89393dd-9f4f-4705-b9f5-9bf95aef711f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:54:47.063983",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T07:22:26.630161",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_072226.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_072226.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of testing.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:16.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:24.200\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and then you taste it.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:32.300\nThat taste is your test \u2013 you're checking if the cake is sweet enough, cooked properly, and tastes good.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:38.900\nIn everyday life, we're constantly testing things.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:45.500\nWe test a light switch to see if the light turns on.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:52.100\nWe test the car brakes to make sure they stop the car.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:58.700\nSo, why is testing important? Well, it helps us find problems early on.\n\n00:58.700 --> 01:04.900\nFor example, testing a new app can reveal bugs before it's released to the public.\n\n01:04.900 --> 01:12.300\nTesting the cake batter before baking might tell you it needs more sugar.\n\n01:12.300 --> 01:21.500\nIn short, testing is all about checking, verifying, and making sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:21.500 --> 01:29.200\nIt\u2019s a crucial step in pretty much everything we do! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
