    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_072402.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:03.400\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:04.900\nNow, what is a test?\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:08.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:11.600\nIt helps us check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:14.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:16.800\nYou put it in a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:17.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:20.400\nIf it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:21.900\nIf it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:25.400\nAnother example could be a taste test.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:28.400\nYou try a new flavor of ice cream to see if you like it.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:31.900\nYour reaction, whether you like it or not, is the result of that test.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:39.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a process or action designed to determine something.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:44.200\nIt can be used to check if something works, if something is true, or even just to see if you like something.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:47.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
