    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_072633.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! \nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.400\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something. \nIt\u2019s a procedure designed to check the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:24.600\nThink about it like this: if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might use a toothpick test to see if it\u2019s done.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:37.200\nYou poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! \nOr, if you're buying a used car, you might take it for a test drive. \nThis helps you test how well the car runs before you decide to buy it.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:44.900\nTests aren't just for cakes and cars. \nThey\u2019re used in all sorts of situations, from science experiments to school exams.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:57.200\nBasically, a test helps us gather information and make informed decisions. \nSo, to recap: a test is a process used to evaluate something. \nIt helps us check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:07.300\nAnd it gives us information to make better choices.\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:14.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
