    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.210 --> 00:03.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:08.010\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013 not the kind you take in school,\n\n00:08.010 --> 00:12.900\nbut a basic concept used in all sorts of things, from science to cooking.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:15.450\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.450 --> 00:21.000\nYou're trying to figure out if something is true or false, good or bad, or just to learn more about it.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.690\nThink about baking a cake.\n\n00:24.690 --> 00:27.810\nYou might test the oven temperature to make sure it's hot enough.\n\n00:27.810 --> 00:33.750\nOr, when you're cooking pasta, you test a noodle to see if it's cooked al dente \u2013 just right!\n\n00:33.750 --> 00:38.280\nScientists test theories by performing experiments and looking at the results.\n\n00:38.280 --> 00:42.690\nEven playing a video game is a kind of test, seeing if you can beat the level.\n\n00:42.690 --> 00:51.030\nSo, a test is really just a way of gathering information and making a decision based on what you find.\n\n00:51.030 --> 00:54.690\nIt helps us understand the world around us.\n\n00:54.690 --> 00:57.570\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
