    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_074646.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.500\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:13.700\nIt's how we check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:18.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:24.200\nYou do a test! You poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:30.300\nTests aren't just for baking, though. A doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:35.800\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:41.800\nEven trying a new flavor of ice cream is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if you like it!\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:47.900\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:51.600\nRemember, tests help us understand the world better.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:57.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
