    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_075610.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:24.300\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:31.200\nFor example, a spelling test helps us find out how well we know how to spell different words.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:41.300\nOr, imagine baking a cake.\nTasting a small piece is a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:51.100\nSo, a test can be written, like an exam at school, or it can be something practical, like testing the strength of a bridge.\n\n00:51.100 --> 01:03.700\nThe main idea is that we're trying to learn something or confirm something with a set procedure.\nBasically, it\u2019s a way of checking things out!\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:07.300\nTo recap, a test is a process used to gather information or evaluate something.\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:11.100\nIt can be used in tons of different situations, from school to science.\n\n01:11.100 --> 01:14.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
