    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_080026.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:24.100\nThink of it like a question you ask to get an answer. It can be something formal, like a quiz in school, or something informal, like checking if the water is hot before you jump in the shower.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:34.200\nThe school quiz tests your knowledge, while the shower test checks the water temperature.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:42.500\nAnother example: Imagine you're baking a cake. You might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:56.700\nSo, a test is just a method to evaluate something.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:01.500\nWhether it's knowledge, temperature, or the doneness of a cake, tests help us learn and make decisions.\n```"
  },
  "57d9c0d6-c2b2-4499-9079-6e34335444da": {
    "id": "57d9c0d6-c2b2-4499-9079-6e34335444da",
