    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_080115.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in computers, a test is just a way of checking if something is true or false.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:22.600\nIt's like asking a question and getting a yes or no answer.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like this: Is the light switch on?\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:36.700\nYes or no. That's a test! Computers use tests all the time to decide what to do next.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:46.600\nFor example, a program might test if your password is correct before letting you log in. Or, a game might test if your score is high enough to unlock a new level.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:56.500\nIf the test is true, the computer does one thing. If it's false, it does something else.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:02.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply checking if something is true or false, helping computers make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
