    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_080249.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:16.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something scary, like in school. But really, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:27.400\nIt's a process where we check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:32.300\nThink of it like this: you test if your shoes fit before you go for a walk.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:38.600\nOr you test if the water is hot before you jump in the shower. See? It's just a simple check.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:45.600\nAnother example could be testing a lightbulb to see if it lights up.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:56.900\nIf it does, it passes the test! If it doesn't, well, then you know it's not working. So, in short, a test is a way to check something and see if it meets a certain requirement.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.400\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
