    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.200\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in the world of technology, a \"test\" is really just a way to check if something is working like it should.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:26.200\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car. A test would be pushing it to see if it rolls, or turning on the lights to see if they shine.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:37.700\nIt's a simple way to make sure everything is connected and doing its job. For example, if you're building a website, you might test to see if all the buttons work.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:51.600\nOr if you're writing a simple program, you might test to see if it adds two numbers correctly. So, to recap, a test is simply a check to make sure something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:51.600 --> 01:01.200\nIt's a fundamental part of building anything, making sure it works as intended. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
