    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:55:22.370041",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T08:08:07.193949",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_080806.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_080806.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:16.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information. Think of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:23.200\nWe use tests all the time! A quiz in school is a test to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:32.000\nA doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel sick. Even trying out a new recipe is a test to see if you like it!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:45.000\nSo, a test is basically a tool to learn something. It helps us understand things better, whether it's your knowledge, your health, or even just if a cake tastes good.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:51.400\nRemember, tests are all about gathering information. And that's the key thing to remember.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:55.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d5cf10ac-ae29-4221-9e79-73dc4ce2d79b": {
    "id": "d5cf10ac-ae29-4221-9e79-73dc4ce2d79b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:55:23.068744",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T08:09:06.914327",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_080906.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_080906.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.600\nToday we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:08.900\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.900 --> 00:14.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:18.900\nIt helps us figure out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:27.300\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:30.300\nIf the light turns on, the test is passed!\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:32.600\nIf it doesn't, the test is failed.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:35.600\nTests are used everywhere!\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:38.900\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:43.100\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:47.600\nEven bakers test their cake batter to make sure it\u2019s just right.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:51.500\nSo, a test is just a way of finding out information.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:55.100\nIt's a question or action that gives us an answer.\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:56.200\nThat's the basic idea!\n\n00:56.200 --> 00:56.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
