    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_081006.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:17.200\nIt's like asking a question and then seeing what the answer is. Think about it.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:24.000\nA recipe is a test! You follow the instructions and test whether you can make a delicious cake.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:30.700\nOr, when you try to open a door, you're testing if it's locked or unlocked.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:36.400\nThe result tells you something new.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:44.900\nAnother example? Imagine you're learning a new skill, like riding a bike.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:50.600\nEach time you try, you're testing your balance and coordination.\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:56.300\nYou might fall, but that's still a result!\n\n00:56.300 --> 01:04.800\nSo, tests are all about exploring and learning.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:13.900\nThey give us information, whether it's baking a cake, opening a door, or riding a bike.\n\n01:13.900 --> 01:23.100\nThey help us understand the world around us, one question at a time.\n\n01:23.100 --> 01:27.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
