    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_081238.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.000\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:10.500\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:10.500 --> 00:13.500\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:18.000\nThink about baking a cake. You might taste the batter to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:19.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.000\nOr maybe you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:26.000\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, it passes the test.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:31.500\nAnother example: a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:36.000\nOr a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:45.000\nSo, a test helps us gather information, confirm something, or make a decision.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:48.500\nIt\u2019s a simple process of asking a question and observing the result.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:52.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
