    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_082118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.800\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:12.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:17.300\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:23.100\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:25.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:27.700\nIt tells you if the cake is done.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:33.700\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:37.700\nThat's a test to see if a simple restart fixes the problem.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:41.800\nTests help us confirm something, identify a problem, or compare different things.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:49.600\nSo, a test is any procedure designed to evaluate something and give us information.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:53.600\nThey help us learn and make better decisions every day.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:57.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
