    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_082217.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.900\nHey there! Welcome! Today we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:01.900 --> 00:06.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:15.600\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch, and the light comes on \u2013 that\u2019s a successful test!\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.600\nTests aren't just for school. A doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:30.700\nA chef might taste food to test if it's seasoned right. See? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:33.300\nSo, whether it's a quiz in class, a medical check-up, or tasting your cooking,\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:36.000\ntests help us understand something better.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:38.300\nThey give us information.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:45.800\nTo recap: A test is a way to find out information. It can be used in lots of different situations to check if something is working, or to see how much you know.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:60.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
