    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.600\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is a way to check something. It's how we find out if something works, or if it's true.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:22.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works. Your test?\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:28.000\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:34.700\nAnother example: you want to know if your cake is done baking. You stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:49.200\nIf it comes out clean, the test is passed, and your cake is ready! Tests are used everywhere, from checking if your car is running smoothly, to making sure a bridge is safe to cross.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:60.300\nBasically, a test helps us confirm something is as it should be. So, remember, a test is simply a way to check and verify something.\n\n00:60.300 --> 00:63.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
