    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_083351.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:19.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:28.200\nIt could be to see if something works, or to measure its quality, or even just to gather information about it.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:35.100\nThink about it like this: you get a new phone and you test it out by making a call, right?\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:42.100\nThat's a test! Or maybe you\u2019re baking a cake and you taste the batter to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:49.100\nThat\u2019s testing too! We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:57.500\nTests help us make decisions. For instance, a doctor might run tests to see if you\u2019re sick.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:06.800\nA company might test a new product before they sell it. So, tests are a really important tool for learning, problem-solving, and making sure things are safe and reliable.\n\n01:06.800 --> 01:13.900\nSo remember, a test is simply a way to check something and get information.\n\n01:13.900 --> 01:16.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
