    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:70.8\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:07.500\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something super important: tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:25.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more organized way.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:34.400\nThink about it: a taste test tells you if you like a certain food.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:43.800\nA spelling test shows how well you know your words.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:53.200\nEven a doctor checking your temperature is performing a test to see if you have a fever!\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:54.900\nSo, tests help us learn and understand things.\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:07.400\nFor example, imagine you want to know if a plant needs more water. You could poke your finger in the soil \u2013 that\u2019s a test!\n\n01:07.400 --> 01:10.300\nIf it feels dry, the answer is yes, it needs water. See?\n\n01:10.300 --> 01:22.800\nEasy! Basically, tests are everywhere, helping us learn, improve, and discover new things.\n\n01:22.800 --> 01:27.300\nThey\u2019re just structured ways of asking questions and getting answers.\n\n01:27.300 --> 01:30.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
