    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_084557.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.600\nNow, you might think of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works as it should.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:22.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb is good. You screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:31.600\nThe lightbulb either lights up, meaning it passes the test, or it doesn't, meaning it fails.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:38.600\nAnother example: You bake a cake and taste it to see if it's sweet enough. That's a test too!\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:50.300\nYou're checking if the cake meets your sweetness requirement. So, a test is basically a way to confirm something is working correctly or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:58.400\nIt's a simple check to make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
