    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_084645.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:16.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:22.900\nYou know, like checking if you understand a topic, or checking if a food tastes good.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:29.000\nIt's a way to get information or see if something works as expected. Think about it.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:35.100\nA school test checks your knowledge. A taste test checks the flavor of a new recipe.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:41.200\nEven a doctor uses tests to check your health.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:48.600\nSo, a school test might ask you questions about history. A taste test might have you rate the sweetness of a cookie.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:54.900\nAnd a health test might involve checking your blood pressure.\n\n00:54.900 --> 00:57.500\nEssentially, tests help us understand things better by giving us measurable results.\n```"
