    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_084832.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information or evidence about something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:25.100\nIt helps us figure things out. Think of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:33.100\nA teacher uses a test to see what you've learned in class. Even baking a cake is a test!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:43.800\nYou're testing your recipe and your skills to see if you get a delicious result.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:54.400\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes. They can be written, like a quiz, or practical, like trying to ride a bike.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:01.100\nThe main idea is that they give us feedback, helping us learn and improve.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:08.900\nRemember, a test isn't just about getting a right or wrong answer. It's about understanding more!\n\n01:08.900 --> 01:16.700\nIn short, a test is a tool for learning and evaluation. It gives us information to help us understand something better.\n\n01:16.700 --> 01:18.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
