    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T08:50:32.956030",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_085032.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_085032.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey everyone, welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests!\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:15.000\nA test, at its core, is really just a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:34.600\nLike, if you're baking a cake and you poke it with a toothpick, that's a test! You're testing if the cake is done.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:40.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the test is positive, the cake is ready!\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:47.000\nOr imagine you're trying to figure out if your toy car needs new batteries. You turn it on.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:58.300\nIf it doesn't move, that's a test, and it tells you the batteries are probably dead. So, tests help us understand things by giving us information. They help us make decisions and solve problems every day!\n\n00:58.300 --> 00:59.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
