    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_085316.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:27.400\nThink of it like this: a baking test. You follow a recipe, that's your test, and the result, a cake, shows if you understood the instructions correctly.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:32.200\nOr imagine a color test. You're shown different colors and asked to name them.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:39.800\nThis tests your ability to see and identify colors. Tests aren't just in school or in labs, though.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:48.900\nYou test your shoelaces every time you tie them to make sure they're secure. You test a new video game by playing it to see if you like it.\n\n00:48.900 --> 01:01.400\nSo, basically, a test is just a procedure to gather information and learn something new. It helps us understand how things work or if something is working as it should.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:05.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
