    "id": "9ed63f68-7b47-4066-ad88-21abc58d7d3a",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:56:01.665227",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T08:58:32.605509",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_085832.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_085832.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of testing.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:12.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:22.600\nIt's a method we use to gather information and see how something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:27.100\nThink about it like this: a cooking test! You taste your soup.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:37.600\nThat's a test to see if it needs more salt. Or, a spelling test in school checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:48.600\nAnother example is testing a new toy to see if it's fun to play with! So, testing helps us learn, improve things, and make sure everything is working as it should.\n\n00:48.600 --> 00:51.100\nIt's all about gathering information!\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:52.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "60973f77-4142-41dc-9bac-eafcc3806262": {
    "id": "60973f77-4142-41dc-9bac-eafcc3806262",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:56:02.447454",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T08:59:20.356745",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_085920.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_085920.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:05.300\nToday we're going to explore something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:08.300\nNow, in everyday life, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:08.300 --> 00:10.900\nThink of it like an investigation.\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:13.700\nWe want to learn more about something, so we perform a test!\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:20.500\nA test is really just a set of steps we follow to get an answer.\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, tasting it is a test to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:26.800\nOr, if your phone isn't working, trying to turn it off and on is a test to see if that fixes the problem.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:29.200\nTests can be simple or complex.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:33.900\nBut the main idea is always the same: we do something, and then we see what happens.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:37.800\nThat \"what happens\" tells us something important!\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:41.500\nSo remember, a test is just a way to learn and figure things out.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:43.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "1f2f878f-e20d-45d0-8c81-d15d56dcde41": {
