    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_090213.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests!\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:14.500\nA test is basically a way to check how much you know about something. Think of it like a measuring tool for your brain.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:24.000\nSo, how does it work? Well, a test usually has questions or problems designed to see if you understand the key ideas.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:32.600\nFor example, a math test might ask you to solve an equation. A spelling test might ask you to spell words correctly.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:39.200\nA history test might ask you about important events. The answers you give show what you've learned.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:46.000\nTests help you and your teachers see what you're good at and where you might need a little extra help.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:52.800\nThey're not scary, just a helpful way to learn! In short, a test is a way to measure your knowledge.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:58.000\nIt uses questions to see what you've learned. And it helps you improve.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
