    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_090325.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.600\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out something. Think of it like a question you're asking to get an answer.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:20.600\nIt could be a quiz at school to see what you\u2019ve learned, or even tasting a new food to see if you like it.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:28.500\nThe main idea is to gather information. For example, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:37.700\nOr, you might test out a new toy to see if it works properly. So, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:47.700\nSee, you might try tasting two different kinds of cookies, a chocolate chip and an oatmeal raisin, to test which one you like more.\n\n00:47.700 --> 01:00.000\nThe test is your taste buds telling you which flavor is better! So, remember, a test is simply a way to learn something new by asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:06.400\nIt\u2019s all about gathering information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
