    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_091030.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNow, you've probably taken tests in school, but in general, a test is simply a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like this: you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in.\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:34.400\nOr, you might test if your car's brakes are working by gently applying them.\nIf the car slows down, the brakes pass the test.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:40.800\nTesting isn't just for objects.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:45.900\nA chef might test the soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:59.500\nA doctor might test your reflexes to check your nervous system.\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:05.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to see if something is working correctly, whether it's a lightbulb, your brakes, or even a bowl of soup.\nIt's all about checking things out!\n\n01:05.200 --> 01:11.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
