    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_091513.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:20.700\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works before you screw it in.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:31.800\nYou're testing it! Essentially, you're giving something a specific input, and then observing the output.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:43.500\nIf the output is what you expected, the test passes! For example, if you're testing a recipe, you follow the instructions and then taste the result.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:55.200\nIf it tastes good, the recipe passed the taste test! Tests are super important because they help us catch mistakes and make sure things are reliable.\n\n00:55.200 --> 01:03.900\nWhether it's a simple check or a complex experiment, testing is all about verifying that something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:07.500\nSo remember, testing is key to making sure everything works right.\n```"
