    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_091815.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.100\nNow, you've probably taken lots of tests in school, but in this video, we're talking about a broader idea.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:26.600\nA test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:39.400\nThink of it like this: if you're baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:52.200\nOr, if you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is burnt out, you can try turning it on. If it doesn't light up, that's a test that tells you the bulb is broken.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:01.100\nSo, tests can be big or small, simple or complex, but they all share the same goal: to give us information and help us make decisions.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:09.000\nBasically, it's a way to ask a question and get an answer that you can trust.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:14.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
