    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_092151.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nOkay, so what is a test?\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:16.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:20.600\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if the water is hot enough for a bath.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:34.200\nSo, you dip your toe in. That's a test!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.600\nYou're testing the water temperature.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:48.500\nOr, maybe you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:55.100\nYou poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:59.000\nIt's ready to eat.\n```"
