    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_092326.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:14.900\nToday we're going to talk about tests. Now, a test is basically a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like an experiment, but often a bit simpler. The main idea is that you do something, and then you observe the result to see what you've learned.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:32.600\nFor example, a spelling test lets you see how well you know your spelling.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:43.200\nA taste test lets you see which snack you like best. Another example is baking a cake. You follow the recipe \u2013 that\u2019s your \"test\" \u2013 and then you see if the cake tastes good.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:52.800\nIf it doesn't, you know you need to change something next time! So, remember, a test is all about trying something out and learning from the results.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:56.600\nIt helps us understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
