    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_092423.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.900\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:23.200\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that\u2019s a test to see how much you learned in class.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:29.300\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:36.300\nThat's a test too! Another example is checking if your bike's brakes work before riding downhill.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:43.300\nYou're testing them to make sure they're safe. Tests help us understand things and make sure everything is working correctly.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:54.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check on knowledge or function. It could be a quiz, a taste, or even a simple check.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:00.100\nThanks for watching! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
