    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_092857.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.000\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, right?\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:18.600\nSo you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:28.800\nBasically, a test is a process or procedure designed to evaluate something's quality, performance, or reliability.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:35.600\nWe use them all the time. For example, your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:50.000\nOr, a company might test a new product before it goes on sale to make sure it works properly.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:56.500\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:56.500 --> 00:59.500\nIt helps us make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:00.000\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is!\n```"
