    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_093118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.700\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:14.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but really, a test is simply a way of finding something out.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:26.000\nIt's a process to check if something is working, or if something is true.\nThink about it like this: a chef tastes their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.900\nOr, a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever.\nThey're both performing tests!\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:40.800\nAnother example is when you try a new lightbulb to test if it works.\nIf it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:48.900\nIf it doesn't, well, it failed the test.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:57.900\nIt helps us understand the world around us and make sure things are working correctly.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
