    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.500\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:09.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:16.600\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:20.300\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:24.800\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:30.900\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:34.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test to see if the cake is done!\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:40.600\nOr, think about checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:42.700\nYou flip the switch; if it lights up, the test passes.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:48.300\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if it needs some adjustments.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:52.600\nThey're a fundamental part of learning and problem-solving.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:56.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple check to see if something is working as expected.\n\n00:56.200 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
