    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.400\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you test them with a toothpick.\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:37.900\nTests help us understand if something is working correctly or if it meets certain standards.\nFor example, a math test checks if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:44.400\nOr, a spelling test shows if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:47.700\nAnother example could be testing if a new toy works right out of the box.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:51.000\nDoes it light up?\nDoes it make noise?\n\n00:51.000 --> 01:01.000\nThat's a test too!\nSo, tests come in many forms, but they all serve the same purpose: to give us information and help us make decisions.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:07.700\nEssentially, a test is just a way to check something and see if it's working as expected.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:17.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
