    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:04.400\nToday we're going to explore something really fundamental:\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:07.000\nthe concept of a test.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:09.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:12.500\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:16.500\nIt could be a written exam at school, where you're testing your knowledge on a subject.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:22.000\nOr, it could be something as simple as tasting a new food to test if you like it.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.000\nA doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you sick.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.000\nEven a scientist testing a new invention is performing a test to see if it works!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:38.000\nSo, tests help us learn, diagnose problems, and improve things.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:41.000\nThey are all about gathering information.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:44.000\nIn short, a test is just a way to get answers.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:55.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
