    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_094742.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:10.300\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:10.300 --> 00:13.700\nThink of it like checking if your shoes fit before you go for a run.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:17.600\nWe use tests every day, even without realizing it.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:21.900\nDid you check the weather forecast before deciding what to wear?\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:23.900\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:26.100\nYou're testing if it's going to rain.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:29.700\nHere's another example.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:31.700\nLet's say you bake a cake.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:34.300\nYou wouldn't just assume it's done, right?\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:37.700\nYou\u2019d probably poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:41.300\nIf it comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is baked through.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:48.800\nSo, remember, a test is all about checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:54.600\nIt helps us make better decisions based on facts, not just guesses.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:00.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
