    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_100013.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:15.900\nToday we're going to talk about tests. Now, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:21.800\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if an oven is hot.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:30.400\nHow do you find out? You might carefully put your hand near it.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:34.700\nThat's a test! You're testing to see if it's hot.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:43.400\nOr, let's say you're baking cookies. You test to see if they're done by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:45.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies pass the test.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:51.600\nSo, a test helps us answer a question. It can be a formal exam at school, or something as simple as checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:57.100\nTests help us learn and make decisions every day.\n\n00:57.100 --> 00:58.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
