    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_100116.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like a question you're trying to answer, or a problem you're trying to solve.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:33.200\nThe main idea behind any test is to gather information.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:39.900\nWe want to see if something is true, false, working, or not working.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:46.600\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:53.300\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:00.900\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n01:00.900 --> 01:08.500\nYou flip the switch! If it lights up, the test is passed, and the bulb works.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:14.900\nIf it stays dark, the test failed!\n\n01:14.900 --> 01:22.500\nAnother example is tasting food to see if it needs more salt.\n\n01:22.500 --> 01:24.900\nYou're testing the flavor!\n\n01:24.900 --> 01:35.800\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method of finding something out.\n\n01:35.800 --> 01:44.800\nIt helps us answer questions and solve problems by giving us information.\n\n01:44.800 --> 01:48.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
