    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_102000.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.500\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:26.800\nThink of it like a way to see if something is working as it should, or if you understand something. For example, when you take a spelling test at school, it's checking if you know how to spell different words.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:38.900\nOr, if you're baking a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar. Doctors use tests too, like checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:50.400\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all have the same basic goal: to give us information and help us understand something better.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:57.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get some information.\n\n00:57.300 --> 01:00.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
