    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if your lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp and see if it lights up.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:28.100\nThat's a test! Tests aren't just for lightbulbs, though.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:34.500\nDoctors use tests to check your health. Teachers use tests to see how well you're learning.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:48.300\nAnd even computer programmers use tests to make sure their programs are running smoothly. So, a test is really just a way to get information and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:58.000\nIt can be as simple as flipping a switch, or as complicated as a medical exam. The important thing is that it gives us an answer.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:03.800\nThat's the basics of tests! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
