    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_102253.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might think of school exams, but a test, in general, is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:22.200\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake. To test if it's done, you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:31.100\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, imagine you're building a tower of blocks. You gently push it to test its stability.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:37.300\nIf it stays standing, it passes! Essentially, a test is a simple process.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:47.300\nYou do something, then you observe the result to see if it meets your expectations.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:58.000\nSo, tests help us confirm things are working correctly and let us know if we need to make changes. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
