    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: the test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:17.500\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:24.700\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you stick a toothpick in to see if it comes out clean. That's a test!\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:30.900\nOr, maybe you're trying to turn on a light, and it doesn't work. You're testing if the lightbulb is good.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.700\nIf it doesn't light up, the test failed. So, tests help us understand if things are okay, or if they need fixing.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:53.700\nWhether it's a cake, a lightbulb, or something even more complex, the basic idea is the same: check and see if it works!\n\n00:53.700 --> 00:60.000\nAnd that's the lowdown on tests. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
