    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something called a test.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:21.400\nWe use tests all the time! For example, when you bake a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:31.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done. Or, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:37.700\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, the test is positive!\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:49.900\nTests help us make decisions and understand the world around us. They can be as simple as looking to see if it's raining, or more complex, like a doctor running blood work.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:57.600\nThe key thing is that a test gives us information. So remember, a test is a way to get information.\n\n00:57.600 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
