    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_102708.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:21.600\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:25.600\nThink of it like this: you want to know if an oven is hot.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:31.600\nYou might carefully hold your hand near it. That's a test! You're testing the oven's temperature.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:37.600\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a light bulb works. You plug it in.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:47.700\nIf it lights up, the test passed! If not, the bulb is probably broken. So, a test is just a procedure to check something.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:58.500\nTo see if it works, if it's true, or if it meets a certain standard. We use tests to learn, to improve things, and to make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```\nKey improvements and explanations:\n\n* **Timing Accuracy:** The `self.wait()` times are calculated precisely to match the narration segments.  Every segment adds up to the correct duration.\n* **Visuals:** Added image placeholders (oven.png, lightbulb.png).  You MUST replace these with actual image files in the same directory as your script.  I've also used more color and shapes as requested.\n* **Code Structure:** The code is organized into clear sections with comments indicating the timing.\n* **Rounded Rectangles:** Added `RoundedRectangle` backgrounds behind the text for better readability.\n* **Font Sizes and Colors:**  Adhered to the specified font sizes and color palette.\n* **Object Grouping**: To simplify animations, texts and backgrounds are grouped together, then animated.\n* **Clearance:** Each section ends with `self.play(*[FadeOut(mob) for mob in self.mobjects], run_time=0.5)` to clear the screen before the next section.\n* **WebVTT Subtitles:**  Generated a complete WebVTT file synchronized with the narration.\n* **Image Placeholders:** Added placeholder image file names.  **You must replace these with actual image files.**\n\nTo run this code:\n\n1.  **Install Manim:** `pip install manim`\n2.  **Install FFmpeg:**  Make sure FFmpeg is installed and accessible in your system's PATH.\n3.  **Save the code:** Save the Python code as a `.py` file (e.g., `test_explanation.py`).\n4.  **Place Image Files:** Put your `oven.png` and `lightbulb.png` images in the same directory as the Python file.  If you don't have these, find some free images and rename them.\n5.  **Run Manim:**  Use the command `manim -pql test_explanation.py TestExplanation` to render the video. The `-pql` option renders the video in low quality for faster processing; you can change it to `-pqh` for high quality.\n\nRemember to replace the image placeholders with your own images!  The subtitles can be used directly with your video editor."
  },
