    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_102925.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of what a \"test\" really is.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:25.300\nIt's a process or procedure designed to measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:33.400\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:39.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar!\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:44.600\nIn both cases, you're performing a test to get information.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:55.100\nTests aren't just for doctors or bakers, though. We use them all the time! When you try a new route to school, you're testing to see if it's faster.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:04.800\nWhen you try a new video game, you're testing to see if you like it.\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:09.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:09.700 --> 01:19.700\nIt helps us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
