    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.500\nNow, in the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer, you're actually checking something to see what the result is.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:32.300\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. For example, a doctor might run a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:42.200\nOr, a teacher might give you a test to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:50.000\nAnother example could be testing a cake to see if it is baked. You can test it by inserting a toothpick to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:50.000 --> 00:59.200\nIf it does, the cake is ready! So, to recap, a test is a process used to gather information or determine something.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:02.800\nIt helps us understand what's happening or if something is working the way it should.\n```"
