    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.900\nA test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time in everyday life, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:36.600\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if it tastes good. Or when you try a new route to school, you're testing to see if it's faster.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:45.500\nIn science and math, tests are more formal, but the idea is the same. We perform an action or experiment to see what happens.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:54.400\nImagine you're testing if a plant grows better in sunlight or shade. You put one plant in the sun and another in the shade, and then you observe which one grows taller.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:02.900\nThat's a test! So, remember, a test is just a way to learn something by trying something out.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:06.900\nIt's about asking a question and looking for the answer.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:07.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
