    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something, to check if something is working, or to see what you know.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:26.200\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:34.200\nA chef might taste a sauce to test if it has enough salt.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:45.500\nOr, you might take a math test at school to show what you've learned. Tests come in all shapes and sizes!\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:58.800\nSome are quick and easy, like testing if a light bulb works by flipping the switch. Others are longer and more involved, like studying for a big exam.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and see what\u2019s going on.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:05.100\nTests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:05.100 --> 01:08.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
