    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.600\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think about school, but in this case, we're talking about a way to check if something works correctly.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:30.000\nThink of it like this: If you bake a cake, you might take a bite to test if it tastes good. Or, if you build a tower of blocks, you might give it a little nudge to test if it's sturdy.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:42.000\nIn computers and electronics, tests are used to make sure everything is running as it should. For example, a lightbulb test would check if the bulb actually lights up.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:52.300\nA battery test would see if it has enough power. So, simply put, a test is a way of checking something to see if it's working properly.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:00.100\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
