  "e2c14593-0d60-4aef-b3d0-5c69678bd4da": {
    "id": "e2c14593-0d60-4aef-b3d0-5c69678bd4da",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:57:28.616219",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T10:41:57.645359",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_104157.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_104157.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests! In the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:16.600\nIt's a procedure we use to gather information.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes the soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:31.800\nOr, a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever. See? Everyday stuff!\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:55.500\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like checking if your phone is charged. The main idea is to observe or measure something, then compare it to a standard or expectation.\n\n00:55.500 --> 01:05.300\nSo, if the soup tastes bland, it fails the \"deliciousness test.\" And if your phone is dead, it fails the \"battery life test.\"\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:10.300\nEssentially, tests help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n01:10.300 --> 01:15.700\nThey\u2019re all about gathering information to see if something meets our needs or expectations.\n\n01:15.700 --> 01:17.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
