    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.400\nNow, a test, at its most basic, is just a way to find something out.\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:24.900\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you put it in a lamp and turn it on.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:32.200\nOr, if you want to know if your cookies taste good, you give one to a friend to try.\nThat's another test!\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:41.900\nTests can be simple, like tasting a cookie, or more complicated, like a science experiment.\nBut the idea is always the same: to get information and learn something new.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:56.800\nSo, a test is basically a method used to determine the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\nIt helps us confirm or deny our initial assumptions and gain a better understanding.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:08.800\nTo sum it up, tests help us answer questions and learn about the world around us.\n\n01:08.800 --> 01:12.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
