    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_104428.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_104428.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:25.100\nIt\u2019s a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:38.500\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a medical test to see if you're healthy. Or, if you're learning to bake, you might taste your cake batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:49.700\nIn school, your teacher gives you quizzes and exams; those are also tests! They help see what you've learned.\n\n00:49.700 --> 01:00.100\nSo, tests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking your knowledge to making sure equipment is working right.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:05.000\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:09.400\nIn short, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n01:09.400 --> 01:11.000\nThat's the basic idea!\n\n01:11.000 --> 01:16.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
