    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_104606.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE\nAll timestamps are approximate.\n\n00:00.116 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:21.700\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. Think of it like this: You might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:30.700\nIf it lights up, the test passes! Or, a doctor might test your eyesight by asking you to read letters on a chart.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:39.300\nTests can be anything from a simple yes or no question, to a more complicated problem with many possible answers.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:47.000\nThe important thing is that a test helps you learn something new, or confirm something you already thought was true.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:51.800\nSo, remember, a test is all about finding things out!\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:55.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
