    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_105248.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.700\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:14.800\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:24.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:37.900\nIt could be checking if you know your multiplication tables, or if a new medicine works, or even if a cake is baked all the way through.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:48.400\nThe main idea is to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or requirement.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:58.900\nThink of it like this: you take a spelling test to see if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:04.100\nOr, a chef might poke a cake with a toothpick.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:09.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the \"baked\" test!\n\n01:09.500 --> 01:19.600\nSo, tests help us understand things better and make informed decisions.\n\n01:19.600 --> 01:25.900\nFrom school quizzes to medical checkups, tests are all around us.\n\n01:25.900 --> 01:30.000\nThey help us learn and improve.\n\n01:30.000 --> 01:35.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
