    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_105331.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:20.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:31.000\nThink of it like a question you're asking, but instead of just getting an answer, you're getting data or evidence to help you understand something better.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:37.800\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you have enough iron.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:44.200\nA teacher might give you a math test to see how well you understand fractions.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:48.800\nAnd you might even test a new recipe to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:53.400\nTests can be formal, like those in school, or informal, like trying a new route to work to see if it's faster.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:56.900\nThe key is that you're trying to gather information to make a decision or learn something new.\n\n00:56.900 --> 00:58.600\nSo, a test helps you learn and understand the world around you.\n```"
  },
