    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_105841.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.230 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:24.200\nIt's a process that helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we know something, or even if we have a specific skill.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:34.300\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:44.800\nA driving test checks if you know how to operate a car safely, and even a doctor uses tests to figure out what's going on inside your body.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:53.700\nTests involve asking questions or performing actions to get results.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:02.600\nSo, whether it's a pop quiz in school, trying out a new recipe, or checking if your computer is connected to the internet, you're essentially running a test.\n\n01:02.600 --> 01:06.900\nIt's all about gathering information and seeing what the outcome is.\n\n01:06.900 --> 01:10.800\nRemember, a test is just a way to learn and improve.\n\n01:10.800 --> 01:14.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
