    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_110422.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out if something is working correctly, or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you can test it by screwing it in and turning on the switch.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:27.400\nThat's a test! Tests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:34.400\nA doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy. A teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:42.800\nOr a company might test a new product to make sure it's safe and reliable.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:47.700\nFor example, imagine you baked a cake. You could test it by taking a bite to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:54.700\nOr you could test how strong a bridge is by driving trucks over it. See? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:08.300\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to check something. It helps us understand if things are working as expected, and it's a super important part of learning and making sure things are safe.\n\n01:08.300 --> 01:11.900\nThanks for watching!\n\n01:11.900 --> 01:15.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
