    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_110727.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE: The timings here are estimates. Please sync them with the actual video.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:14.200\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:25.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but often in a more structured way. We use tests all the time to see how well we understand things, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:36.800\nThink about it like this: a spelling test shows how well you know your spelling words. Or, a taste test helps you decide which cookie is the tastiest.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:40.200\nSee? It's about gathering information.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:50.000\nAnother example is a simple lightbulb test. If the lightbulb lights up when you flip the switch, then the bulb and the circuit are probably working.\n\n00:50.000 --> 01:02.000\nWe use tests to learn, to diagnose problems, and to make decisions. So, a test is basically a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:09.200\nIt could be knowledge, a skill, or even a piece of equipment. It helps us understand things better!\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:12.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
