    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_110831.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:39.400\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. You poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, that's your answer \u2013 the cake is ready!\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:41.900\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike,\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:50.700\neach time you try, you're testing your balance. Did you stay upright? Great! That's a successful test.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:00.500\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:09.500\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the basic idea is always the same: ask a question, get an answer.\n\n01:09.500 --> 01:15.800\nAnd remember, every test, even if it doesn't go perfectly, teaches us something valuable.\n\n01:15.800 --> 01:17.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
