    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_111635.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it like a detective looking for clues. The main idea is to have a specific question or task, and then see what the answer or result is.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:30.100\nWe then compare that result to what we expected.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:37.300\nIf they match, great! The test passed. If they don't, something might be wrong.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:44.200\nFor example, imagine you're testing if a light bulb works. You screw it in, flip the switch, and\u2026it lights up!\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:52.900\nThat's a successful test. Or, maybe you're testing if you remember your friend's birthday. You try to recall the date and\u2026you get it right!\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:01.100\nAnother test passed. So, remember, a test is just a check to see if something is working as it should.\n\n01:01.100 --> 01:08.900\nIt helps us find problems and make sure things are reliable. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
