    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T11:20:43.224145",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_112043.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_112043.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:23.400\nIt's a process or procedure designed to evaluate something specific.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:28.000\nThink of it like this: a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:32.600\nThat's a test! Or, a chef might taste a sauce to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:42.500\nThat's also a test. Tests aren't just in science or cooking, though. You take tests in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:50.500\nYou might even test out a new video game before you buy it to see if you like it.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:54.500\nBasically, a test helps us learn, confirm, or compare something.\n```"
  },
