    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:29.600\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. For example, if you try to turn on a light switch and the light doesn't come on, you've just performed a test!\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:35.300\nYou're testing if the light bulb works.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:41.500\nAnother example: a taste test! You try a new food and decide if you like it or not.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:55.100\nThat's a test of your taste buds. So, a test is simply a method for finding out information about something. It helps us understand if something works, if something is true, or even just if we like something.\n\n00:55.100 --> 01:02.100\nTests are all about gathering information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
