    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:20.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information or measure something.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:33.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it\u2019s done by poking it with a fork.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:39.900\nIn science, tests are used to see if a hypothesis, or a guess, is right or wrong.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:49.200\nFor example, you could test if a plant grows faster with more sunlight.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:58.500\nYou'd give one plant lots of sun and another less, and then compare their growth. That's a test!\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:17.400\nTests can also be used to check your knowledge, like the quizzes you take in school. They help you and your teacher see what you\u2019ve learned.\n\n01:17.400 --> 01:21.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information or measure something.\n\n01:21.000 --> 01:29.400\nWhether it\u2019s checking if a cake is baked, seeing if a plant likes sunlight, or showing what you know in class, tests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:29.400 --> 01:33.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
