    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:16.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like a question you're asking, but instead of just talking, you're using a specific method to get an answer.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:34.000\nIt could be a written exam at school, a science experiment, or even just trying a new recipe to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:40.600\nThe main idea is to gather information to learn more.\n\n00:40.600 --> 00:51.200\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a software developer might run a test to make sure their program works correctly. See? Different situations, same basic principle.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:59.000\nSo, remember, a test is a way of learning by doing, or observing. It helps us understand things better by providing evidence. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
