    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:19.900\nIt helps us find out if something is working correctly, if it's true, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:29.200\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:37.800\nA baker might taste their cake to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:46.400\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to test what you've learned.\n\n00:46.400 --> 01:00.800\nSo, tests come in all shapes and sizes. They can be simple, like checking if a light bulb turns on, or more complex, like running a science experiment.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:07.300\nBut the main idea is always the same: to get information and see if something passes the test.\n\n01:07.300 --> 01:14.100\nTo recap: a test is a check to find out if something is working, true, or meets a standard.\n\n01:14.100 --> 01:17.500\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are right.\n\n01:17.500 --> 01:24.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
