    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_115712.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:22.300\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:26.000\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake,\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:34.000\nand you want to know if it's done. You might poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:39.300\nThe toothpick coming out clean tells you the cake is ready.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:44.600\nOr maybe you're wondering if your phone charger is working.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:55.600\nYou plug it in to see if your phone starts charging. That's another test! Tests help us check if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:58.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information\n\n00:58.200 --> 01:00.200\nand confirm something.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:03.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
