    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_115859.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.200\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.200 --> 00:14.600\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:21.000\nTests help us measure or evaluate things.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:27.300\nThink about a spelling test in school. It helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:35.600\nOr imagine baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:40.200\nAnother example is checking if a light bulb works before you screw it in.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:45.600\nThat's a test! You're seeing if it does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:55.900\nBasically, a test is any process that helps you determine if something is working correctly or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:01.300\nSo, remember, tests are all about finding things out.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:05.900\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:08.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
