  "0cd1e2df-2321-4828-9cb7-e99f3a1207a9": {
    "id": "0cd1e2df-2321-4828-9cb7-e99f3a1207a9",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:58:32.620183",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T12:00:34.694560",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_120034.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_120034.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.900\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.900 --> 00:12.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. In the world of computers, a test checks if something is true or false.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:28.500\nFor example, we could test if a number is bigger than ten.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:35.300\nIf it is, the test is true! If it's not, the test is false.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:37.900\nOr, we could test if two words are the same.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:41.700\nLike, is \"apple\" the same as \"apple\"? Yes!\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:45.500\nThat test is true. Is \"apple\" the same as \"orange\"?\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:47.600\nNo! That's a false test.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:53.600\nSo, remember, a test checks something and gives you a true or false result.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:57.400\nIt\u2019s a basic building block for making computers make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
