    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:23.100\nIt helps us gather information to see if something is true, or working, or even just to see what someone knows.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.500\nThink about it like this: a chef might test the soup to see if it needs more salt. That's a test!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:37.000\nOr, you might take a spelling test in school to see how many words you know.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.500\nAnother example is testing a toy car.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:48.000\nYou might push it down a ramp to see how far it goes. That's a test too!\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:57.600\nYou\u2019re finding out something about the car. So, a test is really just a process of trying something out and seeing what happens, giving us some information about it. Remember, tests help us learn and understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
