    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:07.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:12.100\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:14.900\nWe use tests every day, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:21.000\nThink about checking if a lightbulb works. You flip the switch \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.800\nThe result tells you if the bulb is good or needs replacing.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.600\nOr, imagine you're baking cookies and you taste one.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:33.800\nYou're testing if they taste good\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:35.900\nand if you need to add more sugar.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:41.400\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like trying a new recipe.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:45.500\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:48.400\nThey help us learn and make better decisions.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:53.800\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information and checking things out.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:59.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
