    "id": "2ef96454-f9de-4cd5-873d-896cda6b5785",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:58:49.257803",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T12:21:09.433601",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_122109.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_122109.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific. It's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:42.000\nOr, a doctor might give you a vision test to see how well you can see. Tests can be used for all sorts of things, from figuring out if something is working correctly, to checking your understanding of a new topic.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:50.400\nThey help us learn and make sure things are going as planned. So remember, a test is just a way to learn something new!\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:54.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
