    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_122323.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.300\nThink of a test like a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:21.600\nImagine you bake a cake. You test it by sticking a toothpick in \u2013 if it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:28.700\nThat's a test. Or, maybe you build a tower of blocks. You test it by seeing if it can stand up without falling.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:34.900\nTests aren't just for cakes and blocks, though. They're used in lots of different areas.\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:41.100\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:51.500\nOr a teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned. Basically, a test is just a way to get information. It helps us understand if something is working correctly or if it needs some improvement.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:59.900\nSo remember, tests are all about checking things and learning!\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:02.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "a24c16a1-69c2-42e4-b7ae-e01aebedbfe3": {
