    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_122514.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:18.300\nNot the kind that give you anxiety, but the kind that help us learn and understand things better.\nBasically, a test is a way to check if something works correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like this: you're trying a new recipe for cookies.\nThe test is tasting the cookies after they're baked to see if they're good.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:35.200\nOr, imagine you're building a tower with blocks.\nThe test is letting go to see if it stands up straight.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:42.800\nAnother example is when you use a flashlight.\nThe test is pressing the button to see if the light turns on.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:52.900\nIf it does, the flashlight passed the test!\nSo, tests are simply ways of checking to see if things work the way we expect them to.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:57.800\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to be doing.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
