    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_122656.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:19.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. We use tests to gather information, to see if something is working,\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:22.900\nor even to check our knowledge.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:31.400\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works by turning on the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:39.800\nAnother example? A doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:48.200\nOr, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:48.200 --> 01:06.400\nThe results of a test help us make decisions. If the lightbulb doesn't turn on, we know we need a new one. If your blood test isn't perfect, the doctor might suggest changes to your diet.\n\n01:06.400 --> 01:13.100\nSo, to recap: a test is a procedure designed to get information, whether it's about a lightbulb, your health, or your understanding of a subject.\n\n01:13.100 --> 01:18.000\nIt helps us learn and make informed choices.\n\n01:18.000 --> 01:24.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
