    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_123112.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, so what is a test?\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:06.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:11.000\nThink of it like an experiment, but it doesn't have to be complicated.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:15.500\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:19.800\nFor example, when you try a new food, you're testing if you like it!\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:24.100\nOr, if you push a door that you think is locked, you're testing to see if it opens.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:27.600\nIn science and school, tests are a bit more formal.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:32.100\nThey help us understand if something is true, or if we've learned something new.\n\n00:32.100 --> 00:37.400\nMaybe a math quiz to see if you understand addition, or a science experiment to see if a plant needs sunlight.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:40.500\nThe goal is always to learn and discover!\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:46.000\nSo, a test is just a way to find things out.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:50.700\nIt's a question asked in a specific way to get a clear answer.\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:52.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
