    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_123505.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really fundamental: tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:14.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:27.700\nWe want to learn more, so we ask questions or perform actions to get answers. Think about it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:34.400\nOr, if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you screw it into a lamp. Another test!\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:39.100\nTests aren't just for cakes and lightbulbs, though.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:43.800\nThey're used everywhere, from science experiments to checking if your homework is correct.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:48.500\nBasically, a test helps us confirm something or discover something new.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:53.000\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n00:53.000 --> 01:01.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn more by asking questions or taking action.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:09.900\nIt's a simple concept, but it's used in so many different ways. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
