    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:26.700\nThink of it like checking if your bike tires have enough air, or if your cookies are baked all the way through.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:42.900\nBasically, you perform an action or ask a question, and then you look at the result to see if it matches what you expect. For example, if you press the power button on your TV and it turns on, that's a successful test!\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:56.100\nOr, if you ask a friend their favorite color and they tell you, that's also a test \u2013 you tested their memory. Tests help us make sure things are reliable and working properly.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:06.200\nThey can be big or small, simple or complex, but they all have the same goal: to check for accuracy. So, remember, a test is just a way of checking if something works as expected. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
