    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_124258.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:24.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand something better.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:29.700\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you can use a toothpick.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:36.500\nSticking the toothpick in is the test. If it comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a good test result.\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:43.300\nOr, imagine you want to know if your plant needs water.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:48.700\nYou can poke your finger into the soil. If it feels dry, that's your test telling you it's time to water it.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:56.700\nTests are used all the time to check things, learn new things, or make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way of getting information.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:03.700\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:06.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
