    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_124825.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_124825.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nHey there, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:13.100\nNow, you might be thinking of school, but a test is really just a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:20.300\nIt's a process we use to get information.\n\n00:20.300 --> 00:27.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done. You test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:34.200\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:40.900\nOr, imagine you want to know if your bike tire has enough air. You test it by squeezing it.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:53.100\nIf it feels firm, it passes! So, a test is simply a way to check something and see if it meets a certain standard or tells us what we need to know.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:57.100\nIt can be as simple as looking, feeling, or even using special equipment.\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:01.000\nIn short, tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:04.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
