    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:08.600\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:10.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:14.000\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:19.400\nThis answer helps us understand or measure something.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:24.800\nThink about it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you can stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:27.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:30.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:36.100\nOr, maybe you want to see if a plant needs water.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:38.500\nYou can touch the soil.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:41.400\nDry soil?\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:41.600\nIt needs water.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:44.500\nThat's another test!\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:52.000\nTests can be simple, like those examples, or they can be more complicated.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:57.000\nBut the basic idea is always the same: to gather information.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.200\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:02.400\nby asking a question and observing the answer.\n```"
