    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_125700.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:21.900\nNow, in everyday life, we take tests all the time, whether we realize it or not. A test is simply a way to find out something, to check if something is true, or to see how well something works.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:36.000\nThink about it like this: When you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like the taste. Or, when you press the button on a remote control, you're testing if it will change the channel.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:44.400\nIn science and math, tests are a bit more formal. They help us prove ideas or understand the world around us.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:55.600\nFor example, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people feel better. Or a student might take a math test to show they understand the lessons.\n\n00:55.600 --> 01:02.000\nSo, tests are all about finding out information! They help us learn and improve.\n\n01:02.000 --> 01:12.400\nIn summary, a test is a way to gather information, to check something, or to prove an idea. It's a tool we use every day!\n\n01:12.400 --> 01:16.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
