    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_130617.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.110\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.110 --> 00:07.780\nAt its most basic, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.780 --> 00:11.000\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of words,\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:12.790\nyou're often using a process or a set of steps.\n\n00:12.790 --> 00:16.910\nSo, what kind of things do we test?\n\n00:16.910 --> 00:18.820\nWell, all sorts of things!\n\n00:18.820 --> 00:23.650\nYou might test if a new toy works by playing with it.\n\n00:23.650 --> 00:28.700\nOr a baker might test a cake recipe by baking it and seeing if it tastes good.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:32.670\nScientists test their ideas with experiments.\n\n00:32.670 --> 00:47.930\nFor example, you could test if a ball bounces higher on concrete or grass by dropping it from the same height on both surfaces and measuring how high it goes. That's a simple test!\n\n00:47.930 --> 00:54.340\nThe important thing is to have a plan, do it carefully, and see what happens.\n\n00:54.340 --> 01:01.620\nBasically, a test is a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:01.620 --> 01:04.720\nIt's all about asking questions and finding answers!\n\n01:04.720 --> 01:07.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
