    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_130839.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:24.600\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true, or to check how well something works.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:31.900\nThink of it like this: you might test a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:45.600\nOr, a doctor might run a test to see if you're healthy. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:54.700\nA simple test could be tasting a piece of fruit to see if it's ripe.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:03.800\nA more complex test might involve using special equipment to measure something precisely.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:15.300\nThe important thing is that a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n01:15.300 --> 01:24.400\nFor example, if your car isn't starting, a mechanic might run tests on the battery and the starter to figure out what's wrong.\n\n01:24.400 --> 01:36.900\nOr, if you're learning a new language, a quiz is a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n01:36.900 --> 01:49.400\nSo, a test is just a tool for learning and understanding. In summary, tests are all about finding things out, checking if things work, and helping us learn.\n\n01:49.400 --> 01:54.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
