    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:06.800\nEver wondered what a test actually is?\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's a process we use to gather information.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:18.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:28.000\nYou stick a toothpick in it. That's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:34.100\nOr imagine you're trying to figure out if a toy car needs new batteries. You turn it on.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:39.700\nIf it moves slowly, that's a test showing you need new batteries.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:51.300\nTests help us make decisions and understand things better. They can be simple, like checking the cake, or more complicated, like a school exam.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:56.000\nBut the basic idea is always the same: to get information.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find something out.\n```"
