    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:10.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:23.200\nA test is basically a way to check if something is working correctly, or to see how well you understand something.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:35.200\nThink of it like this: you might \"test\" if your bike's brakes work before riding down a hill, right?\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:44.500\nIn school, tests help your teacher see what you've learned.\nThey can be quizzes, exams, or even just little activities.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:51.100\nIf you're baking a cake, you might \"test\" the batter by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:54.600\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and see how things are going.\nIt helps us learn and improve.\nRemember, tests aren't scary, they're just tools!\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "452fbd66-29b6-4b31-922c-982463e08a28": {
    "id": "452fbd66-29b6-4b31-922c-982463e08a28",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:59:30.134765",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T13:14:42.800569",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_131442.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_131442.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNo need to panic, it's not that kind of test! In computing, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on after you flip the switch.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:36.900\nSo, what are we testing? Well, basically anything! We can test if a piece of code gives the right answer, if a website loads correctly, or even if an app does what it's supposed to do when you click a button.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:45.000\nFor example, imagine a calculator app. A test would be making sure that 2 plus 2 actually equals 4.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.100\nAnother test might be checking what happens if you divide by zero. Does it give an error message like it should?\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:59.900\nIn short, tests are like little detectives, making sure everything is working properly behind the scenes.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:07.900\nThey help us catch mistakes early and make sure things are reliable. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c9eb8f4c-42d9-4fa2-b80b-53e01a6ff0f1": {
    "id": "c9eb8f4c-42d9-4fa2-b80b-53e01a6ff0f1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T14:59:30.791386",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T13:15:29.198293",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_131529.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_131529.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something. It's a procedure we use to evaluate knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: you give a plant water, and then you test to see if it grows. That's a simple test!\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:33.900\nIn school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned. They might ask you questions on a piece of paper, or even have you demonstrate a skill.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:42.900\nFor example, a math test checks your ability to solve problems. A spelling test checks how well you know your words.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:52.200\nUltimately, tests help us understand where we are and what we might need to learn next. They're just one tool for learning and growing.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:55.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
