    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_131725.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.354 --> 00:05.154\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.154 --> 00:15.954\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.954 --> 00:26.054\nIt's like asking a question, but instead of just listening, you're looking for proof.\n\n00:26.054 --> 00:29.954\nThink of it like this: A chef tests a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:29.954 --> 00:43.554\nOr, a doctor tests your temperature to see if you have a fever.\nSee?\nThey're both using a test to get information.\n\n00:43.554 --> 00:52.554\nSo, examples of tests can be anything from a school quiz, to a scientist running an experiment, or even just checking if your car keys are in your pocket before you leave the house.\n\n00:52.554 --> 00:58.254\nYou're performing a little test!\nBasically, a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:58.254 --> 01:02.554\nIt's about gathering evidence to answer a question.\n\n01:02.554 --> 01:04.754\nAnd we use them all the time!\n\n01:04.754 --> 01:06.554\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
