    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_131944.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.700\nSimple tests. Think of a test as a way to check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:18.900\nIt's like a little experiment. We give something a try, and then we see what happens.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:29.900\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works. You screw it in, flip the switch, and poof, the light comes on! That means the bulb passed the test.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:33.700\nAnother example? Baking a cake!\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:44.900\nYou follow a recipe, put it in the oven, and if it comes out fluffy and delicious, your cake recipe test was a success.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:56.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to see if something does what it's supposed to do. We try it out, we observe, and then we know if it works.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:00.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
