    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_132042.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, it's a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:27.200\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way. Tests help us measure things, like how well you understand a topic, or how strong a material is.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:36.400\nFor example, a spelling test checks your spelling knowledge. A taste test lets you decide which food you like best.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:47.000\nEven a doctor uses tests, like a blood test, to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:52.500\nSo, tests are all about gathering information in a systematic way.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:55.900\nThey help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:57.800\nRemember, a test isn't just about right or wrong answers; it's about finding out something new.\n```"
  },
