    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:18.300\nToday we're diving into something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:25.000\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we simply mean a way to find out something.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.700\nIt's like a question you ask or a task you give to see what the answer or the result will be.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:38.400\nThink of it like this: a cooking test!\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:45.800\nYou taste the soup to see if it needs more salt. That's a test!\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:56.200\nOr, imagine you're testing a toy car to see how far it can travel when you push it.\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:03.200\nYou're observing and learning something about the car.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:10.600\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if the bathwater is too hot.\n\n01:10.600 --> 01:17.800\nThey help us learn, improve things, and make informed decisions.\n\n01:17.800 --> 01:23.900\nSo, a test is really just a way to gather information.\n\n01:23.900 --> 01:27.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
