    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_141728.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.220 --> 00:02.420\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.420 --> 00:05.320\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.730 --> 00:10.130\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of something you take in school,\n\n00:10.130 --> 00:11.730\nand that's definitely one kind of test.\n\n00:11.730 --> 00:14.330\nBut a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.330 --> 00:17.730\nIt's a process we use to see if something is working correctly,\n\n00:17.730 --> 00:20.830\nor to see what the result of something will be.\n\n00:21.050 --> 00:24.850\nThink about baking a cake.\n\n00:24.850 --> 00:28.150\nYou might taste the batter before you bake it \u2013 that's a little test to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:28.510 --> 00:33.810\nOr, imagine you're checking if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:33.810 --> 00:35.010\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:35.010 --> 00:37.910\nYou're testing if the lightbulb will turn on.\n\n00:38.350 --> 00:43.750\nSo, a test is simply a way to check something or learn something new.\n\n00:44.050 --> 00:48.750\nIt can be formal, like a quiz, or informal, like tasting cake batter.\n\n00:48.750 --> 00:50.850\nIt's all about finding answers.\n\n00:51.050 --> 00:52.850\nThat\u2019s the basic idea of a test!\n\n00:53.160 --> 00:55.260\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
