    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_141825.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the basics of tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.300\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.300 --> 00:21.900\nWe use them all the time, maybe without even realizing it. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:29.400\nYou poke it with a toothpick \u2013 that\u2019s a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:41.400\nOr, let's say you're trying to figure out which light switch turns on the living room lamp. You flip one switch, see if the light goes on \u2013 that's another test!\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:54.200\nBasically, a test helps you answer a question by giving you some kind of result. You ask a question, perform a test, and then look at the answer the test gives you.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:03.300\nThey are a quick and reliable way to find the answer to a specific question.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:06.800\nSo, tests are all about finding things out!\n\n01:06.800 --> 01:08.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "57935cdf-be2c-4ef7-a8a3-8605c0ac34d6": {
