    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_141918.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:14.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:25.800\nIt's like asking a question and then trying to find the answer.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:33.000\nThink about it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:36.900\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:40.800\nIn both cases, the test is giving us information.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:47.200\nLet's say you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:53.600\nYou can test it! Stick your finger in the soil.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:00.000\nIf it's dry, the test tells you it needs water.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:09.400\nIf it's damp, it probably doesn't.\n\n01:09.400 --> 01:17.900\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information.\n\n01:17.900 --> 01:22.700\nIt helps us learn, understand, and make decisions.\n\n01:22.700 --> 01:29.800\nRemember, it's all about asking a question and finding the answer.\n\n01:29.800 --> 01:31.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
