    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_142628.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:09.500\nToday we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:15.200\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way of finding out something.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:21.400\nIt's how we check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:28.100\nThink of it like this: a baker tests their oven to make sure it's hot enough to bake a cake.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:34.100\nOr, a doctor might test your vision to see how well you can see.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:35.900\nThese are all tests!\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:42.000\nLet\u2019s say you want to know if a toy car rolls faster on carpet or wood.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:46.900\nYou could run a test!\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:50.400\nYou\u2019d roll the car on both surfaces and see which one it goes faster on.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:51.800\nThat's testing in action!\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:56.400\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to learn something by checking it out.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:00.000\nIt's how we explore and understand the world around us.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:00.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
