    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T14:34:17.450124",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_143417.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_143417.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:3.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:07.500\nWe use them all the time!\nThink about it.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:10.500\nYou take a taste of soup \u2013 that's a test to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:10.500 --> 00:12.500\nOr you try on a shoe \u2013 that's a test to see if it fits.\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:16.500\nIn more formal situations, like school, a test helps us measure what you've learned.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:19.500\nMaybe it's a quiz on animals, or a spelling test.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:22.500\nThe goal is to see how much information you understand.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:28.500\nAnother example, if your computer isn\u2019t working you might run a diagnostic test to see if there are any broken parts.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:33.500\nSo, a test is just a method, big or small, to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:36.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "bf02216c-41c5-491b-931d-8e053a31d9e8": {
    "id": "bf02216c-41c5-491b-931d-8e053a31d9e8",
