    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_144335.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:24.500\nIt helps us see if something is true, or correct, or working properly.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:33.700\nThink about it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's done by poking it with a toothpick.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:43.400\nOr, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:51.400\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a lightbulb works to seeing how well you understand a new subject in school.\n\n00:51.400 --> 00:57.900\nThey give us information and help us make decisions.\nSo remember, a test is just a way to get answers.\nIt helps us learn and improve things.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c309c2f6-0911-4c02-8ec1-7f4e89622f35": {
    "id": "c309c2f6-0911-4c02-8ec1-7f4e89622f35",
