    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_145235.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to learn about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:18.600\nIt's like asking a question to see if you know the answer, or trying something out to see if it works.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:28.200\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:37.700\nOr, when you bake a cake, you taste it! That's a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:46.500\nEven when you try to turn on a light switch, you're testing to see if the light bulb is working.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:52.900\nSo, tests help us understand if something is correct, working properly, or meeting a certain standard.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:00.100\nThey're everywhere! Basically, if you're checking something, you're performing a test.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:03.700\nThat's the basics of what a test is all about.\n```"
  },
