    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:17.500\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:26.700\nBasically, a test helps us check if something is working correctly, or if it has certain qualities.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:35.800\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or a teacher might give you a quiz to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:48.300\nAnother example: You might test a new lightbulb to see if it turns on.\n\n00:48.300 --> 01:03.600\nDifferent tests use different methods, but they all have the same goal: to get information. So, to recap, a test is a procedure used to determine something about an object, person, or system.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:07.300\nIt helps us understand if something is working as expected or has the qualities we need.\n```"
