    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_151503.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.100 --> 00:19.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:24.400\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:31.400\nA math test checks your understanding of numbers, while a spelling test checks your knowledge of words.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:37.500\nAnother example? When you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:52.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! So, remember, a test is just a method to find out if something works, if something is true, or if something is ready.\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:00.100\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
