    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_151545.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're tackling a fundamental concept: the test.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:17.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt helps us check if something is true, works correctly, or meets certain standards.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:28.500\nThink of it like this: you test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\nOr, a doctor might test your vision to see how well you can see.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:38.500\nIn school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned.\nAnother example is testing a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:54.200\nWe perform different actions, like dropping it or pulling on parts, to see if anything breaks.\nSo, a test is just a process, big or small, to gather information and make a judgment.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:00.400\nIt's all about checking and confirming.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
