    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_152121.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. Think of it like an experiment, but often with a specific goal in mind.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:25.200\nWe use tests all the time! For example, when you check if your oven is hot enough to bake, you're performing a test.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:33.600\nOr when a doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:42.100\nAnother example is a taste test. You try a new food to see if you like it.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:53.700\nThe food is the subject, and your taste buds are performing the test. Tests help us make decisions and understand the world around us better.\n\n00:53.700 --> 01:02.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new. It could be anything from checking your oven to trying a new flavor of ice cream. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
