    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T15:24:52.003649",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_152451.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_152451.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.300\nNo need to panic, we're not grading anything! In the world of science and data, a \"test\" is simply a way to see if something is true or not.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:26.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a new plant food makes your flowers grow taller. You use the plant food on some flowers and leave others alone.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:30.900\nThat's a test! You're testing if the plant food has an effect.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:40.200\nAnother example could be testing if a new recipe tastes good. You bake the cake, let people try it, and see what they think.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:49.500\nYou're testing the recipe! So, a test is really just a way to gather information and make a decision based on that information.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:59.600\nIt helps us learn and understand the world around us. In short, a test is a structured way to find out if something works or is true.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:03.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
