    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_153756.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.300\nNow, a test, at its core, is simply a way to find out something. It's like an experiment, but usually shorter and more focused.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it as a question with a built-in answer key. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:37.400\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing if you like the flavor. Or, if you press a button on your phone and see if it works, you're running a simple test.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:46.800\nIn school, you take tests to see how well you understand a subject. Scientists use tests to prove or disprove theories.\n\n00:46.800 --> 00:54.100\nEven doctors use tests to figure out what's going on inside your body.\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:08.500\nSo, tests are everywhere! They help us learn, understand, and make informed decisions about the world around us.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:12.000\nTo summarize, a test is a method for discovering information, and it comes in many forms.\n\n01:12.000 --> 01:15.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "69634778-96bb-4e4f-87ea-476f83fce0d4": {
