    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_154121.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:23.000\nWe use tests all the time! For example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:29.000\nOr, think about baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:34.300\nThat's a test too! Another example is when you take a quiz in school.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:45.100\nThat's a test designed to see what you've learned. So, basically, a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:45.100 --> 00:55.900\nTests help us make decisions and understand the world around us. So, to recap, a test is a way to gather information and answer a question.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:05.900\nIt can be anything from a simple taste test to a complex scientific experiment. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "713f95f4-34de-4838-b31c-7d279f374e39": {
    "id": "713f95f4-34de-4838-b31c-7d279f374e39",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:01:02.047665",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T15:42:27.166236",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_154227.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_154227.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.000\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like this: it's a set of questions or problems designed to see if you understand a topic.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:32.500\nSo, how does it work? Well, you're presented with questions, and you answer them.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:39.300\nThese answers are then checked to see if they're correct. The more correct answers, the better you understand the topic!\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:49.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know how to spell words. A math test checks your understanding of numbers and equations.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:51.700\nEven just asking yourself questions after reading a book is a type of test!\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:56.500\nIn short, a test is a tool to measure knowledge.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:01.100\nIt helps you and your teachers understand what you've learned and what you might need to work on. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
