    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_154315.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:04.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:06.700\nThink of it like a question that needs an answer.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:10.500\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:10.500 --> 00:15.600\nFor example, when you try a new cookie recipe, you're testing it to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:20.200\nOr, when you press a button on a remote, you're testing if it will change the channel.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:26.000\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like seeing if your shoes fit.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.800\nThe important thing is that a test helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspect.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:37.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something out.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:42.400\nIt's a process of asking a question and finding the answer.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:45.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "58204062-66d1-4290-98d0-34dde9030fe1": {
    "id": "58204062-66d1-4290-98d0-34dde9030fe1",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:01:03.245576",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T15:44:01.923939",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_154401.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_154401.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.200 --> 00:03.800\nToday we're going to talk about tests,\n\n00:03.800 --> 00:05.500\nand no, not the kind you take in school.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:10.200\nIn computer programming, a test is simply a way to check if your code is working the way you expect it to.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:14.800\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and you taste it to make sure it's sweet enough.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:18.300\nA test in code is similar.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:23.500\nWe write small programs that automatically check if specific parts of our main program are behaving correctly.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:28.700\nFor example, let's say you have a function that's supposed to add two numbers together.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:33.100\nA test would check if that function actually adds them correctly!\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:36.900\nYou might give it 2 and 3, and the test will confirm that the answer is indeed 5.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:41.500\nIf it's not, that means there's a problem in your code that needs fixing.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:47.500\nSo, tests help us make sure our programs are reliable and do what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:51.500\nThey're a really important part of building good software.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:54.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
