    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_154558.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nAlright, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.400\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:25.300\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:34.300\nImagine you're baking a cake. You might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done. That's a test!\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:43.300\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again to see if that fixes it. Another test!\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:58.000\nBasically, a test helps us confirm something, or learn something new. It could be as simple as checking if the water's hot enough for a bath, or as complicated as scientists testing a new medicine.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.400\nThe point is, a test gives us information.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:05.500\nSo, remember, a test is a question, and the results are the answer.\n\n01:05.500 --> 01:07.000\nThis video was created by\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:08.000\nApilage AI.\n```"
