    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_154657.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:29.900\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is working, true, or accurate.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:41.400\nThink of it like this: if you're baking a cake, you might insert a toothpick to test if it's done.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:52.100\nOr, if you're trying out a new lightbulb, you turn it on to test if it works.\nIf it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:04.100\nTests can be formal, like quizzes, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\nThe key is that they help us learn and make decisions.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:07.700\nSo, a test is an action performed to ascertain if something is true, accurate, or effective.\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:11.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
