    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:01:08.879346",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T15:53:10.964278",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_155310.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_155310.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE: The subtitles are estimated based on the narration and may need adjustments for perfect sync.\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we mean a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: You have a flashlight. A test would be turning it on to see if the bulb lights up.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:30.300\nIf it does, the test passed! If it doesn't, the test failed, and you know something needs fixing.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:36.200\nAnother example is baking a cake. The test might be sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:42.200\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done. If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:52.800\nSo, a test is simply a way to verify that something is performing as expected. It's a quick check to make sure everything is working the way it should.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:58.500\nThat\u2019s testing in a nutshell! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
