    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_155712.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.000\nA test, simply put, is a way to check something.\nIt helps us find out if something is working correctly, is true or false, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:23.200\nThink about baking a cake.\nYou might taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:32.400\nOr, if you're building a bridge, engineers will run tests to make sure it can hold a lot of weight.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:44.400\nAnother example?\nA doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:59.000\nTests can be written, like a school exam, or practical, like checking if a lightbulb turns on.\nSo, to recap, a test is just a way to evaluate something and see if it's performing as expected.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.500\nIt's a fundamental tool for learning, building, and understanding the world around us.\n01:02.500 --> 01:06.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
