    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_155838.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.500\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:17.800\nWhat is a test, really?\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:28.500\nIt could be checking if you understand a lesson, or if a food is safe to eat, or even if a new medicine works.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:37.800\nThe main idea is to get information.\nWe perform a test, observe the results, and then we can make a decision based on what we find.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:43.600\nThink about it like this: Your doctor gives you a blood test.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:52.200\nThat test checks different things in your blood, like sugar levels or iron.\nThe results help your doctor understand your health.\n\n00:52.200 --> 00:58.000\nOr imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou might test it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:06.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that means the cake is ready!\nSo, a test is just a simple way to gather information and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:06.600 --> 01:14.800\nTests help us learn, stay safe, and make good choices.\n\n01:14.800 --> 01:17.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
