    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.500\nWhat are they? Well, simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.500 --> 00:17.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking. You use a toothpick! That's a test.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:25.500\nIn science and many other fields, tests are used to gather information and see if something is true.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:37.000\nFor example, you might test how strong a bridge is by putting weight on it. Or, a doctor might test your blood to see if you have a certain vitamin deficiency.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:43.700\nAnother example is a spelling test! It checks to see if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:53.000\nSo, tests help us understand things better and make sure things are working as they should. They are a way of checking and confirming.\n\n00:53.000 --> 01:03.200\nIn short, a test is a method of checking something to see if it's true or working properly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
