    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:15.100\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:22.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:31.500\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it. For example, when you try a new cookie recipe, you're testing it!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:40.900\nYou're seeing if it tastes good. Or, if you try to open a door, you're testing if it's unlocked.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:53.500\nTests aren't just for cooking or doors, though. In science, tests help us understand how things work. In school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:53.500 --> 01:03.600\nEssentially, a test is any procedure designed to evaluate something or someone. It can be as simple as trying something out or as complex as a carefully designed experiment.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:08.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn something by trying something out.\n\n01:08.600 --> 01:13.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "460cf7fe-aef2-401c-b6d9-e89ed446c7c0": {
    "id": "460cf7fe-aef2-401c-b6d9-e89ed446c7c0",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:01:27.456354",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T16:19:07.414318",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_161907.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_161907.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome!\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:10.200\nWhat are they?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:19.900\nIt helps us understand if something works, or if something is true.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:25.300\nYour test is screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\nDoes it light up?\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:30.400\nGreat, the test passed!\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:39.600\nYou test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, your test says the cake is ready.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:51.300\nTests are all around us, helping us learn and make sure things are working as they should.\nBasically, a test is just a way to ask a question and get an answer.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:54.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
