    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:22.700\nIt's a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:27.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:33.600\nYou might use a toothpick \u2013 that's your test! If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:40.500\nTests aren\u2019t just for baking, though. They\u2019re everywhere!\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:47.400\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:56.200\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned. Even trying a new food is a test to see if you like it!\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:02.000\nBasically, a test helps us answer a question. Whether it's \"Is the cake ready?\" or \"Am I healthy?\" tests provide us with answers and valuable information. So, remember, a test is just a tool to learn something new or confirm something we think we already know. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
