    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_162700.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of what a test is.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:17.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and getting an answer that shows what you know, or how something works.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:24.900\nThink about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:31.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake. You might taste it to test if it needs more sugar. That taste is a test!\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:42.700\nTests can be written, like exams, or they can be practical, like checking if a lightbulb works by plugging it in. The important thing is they give us information.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:52.800\nSo, in short, a test is a method of gathering information to determine something.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:04.700\nWhether it's knowledge, skill, or functionality, tests help us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "aa15c73f-a1cf-4065-9b8e-8b20500cbbc2": {
