    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_162852.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really fundamental: tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:15.600\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out if something works correctly, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:30.800\nOr, imagine you're building with LEGOs. You might test if a piece fits before snapping it on.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:38.000\nIn the real world, tests are everywhere. Doctors use tests to diagnose illnesses.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:45.000\nEngineers test bridges to make sure they're safe. Even your school exams are a type of test to see how much you've learned!\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:59.200\nSo, tests are all about checking something \u2013 confirming it's working as expected, or that it meets a certain requirement. They help us make sure things are safe, effective, and of good quality.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
