  "4a0f2cf5-8b43-4762-9ee1-07bffbeb830d": {
    "id": "4a0f2cf5-8b43-4762-9ee1-07bffbeb830d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:01:49.670311",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T16:46:16.998054",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_164616.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_164616.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.100\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working as it should.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: you buy a new lightbulb. To test if it works, you screw it into a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.500\nIf it lights up, the test passes! If not, the lightbulb is probably faulty.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:42.900\nSimilarly, a chef might test their soup by tasting it to see if it needs more salt. Or, a mechanic might test the brakes on a car to make sure they're safe.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:53.400\nSo, in short, a test is just a simple way to verify that something is doing what it's supposed to do. It's all about checking and making sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:53.400 --> 00:58.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4748afb7-69f9-4c5d-8902-43468eb18689": {
    "id": "4748afb7-69f9-4c5d-8902-43468eb18689",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
