    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_164837.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:16.300\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:20.400\nWe use them all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:24.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:30.800\nYou poke it with a toothpick, right? That's a test! The toothpick comes out clean?\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:34.300\nThe cake is ready.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:37.800\nOr imagine you're trying to figure out if your shoes fit.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:42.700\nYou try them on and walk around. That's another test!\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:46.200\nDo they feel comfortable?\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:47.000\nYes?\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:48.200\nGreat, they fit!\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:50.300\nSo, a test is basically a question we ask,\n00:50.300 --> 00:52.500\nfollowed by a way to get an answer.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:53.900\nIt helps us make decisions and learn new things.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:57.500\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all serve the same purpose:\n00:57.500 --> 01:00.500\nto give us information.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:03.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
