    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_165252.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:06.200\nYou've probably taken a bunch of them in school,\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:07.700\nbut what is a test, really?\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:12.500\nAt its core, a test is just a way to see if something is working correctly\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:14.200\nor if something is true.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:19.200\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:21.400\nWe use tests all the time in everyday life.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:26.700\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:26.700 --> 00:30.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test that tells you the cake is done!\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:35.500\nOr maybe you check the temperature outside before deciding what to wear.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:38.100\nThat's a test to see how warm or cold it is.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:42.200\nSo, tests help us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:44.200\nThey give us information.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:50.100\nWhether it's a school exam or just figuring out if your shoes match your outfit,\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:52.800\ntests are all about gathering evidence.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:55.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
