    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_170000.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:14.500\nA test is simply a way to find out something. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:19.900\nSo, what kind of things can you test? Well, almost anything!\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:27.900\nYou can test if a lightbulb works by turning it on.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:38.000\nYou can test if a cake is ready by sticking a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake's done!\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:47.900\nOr, you can take a math test at school to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:56.900\nBasically, a test helps you gather information to see if something is working, if something is true, or how well you know something.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:05.900\nIt's a tool for learning and understanding. To recap, a test is a structured way of asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:12.000\nIt helps you learn and understand the world around you. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
