    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_170052.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.999\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.699\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:22.299\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works. You flip the switch, and if the light comes on, the test passes!\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:28.299\nIf it doesn't, the test fails.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:34.399\nAnother example could be a food allergy test.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:42.799\nYou might eat a small amount of a food and see if you have a reaction. If you do, the test suggests you\u2019re allergic.\n\n00:42.800 --> 00:53.099\nIf not, you're probably okay. So, to recap: a test is a simple check to see if something meets a certain expectation.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:57.099\nIt's all about finding out if things are working as they should, or if a statement is true or false.\n\n00:57.100 --> 00:57.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
