    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.500\nToday, we're going to talk about tests. What are they, and why are they important?\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:22.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly or if you've learned something new.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:31.700\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:33.800\nDoes the light turn on?\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:36.100\nThat tells you if the bulb is good.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:44.900\nOr, imagine you've been learning about addition. A math quiz is a test to see how well you understand adding numbers together.\n\n00:44.900 --> 00:51.200\nTests aren't just about grades, though. They help us identify what we know and what we need to learn more about.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:52.700\nThey help us improve!\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:55.800\nSo, a test is basically a way to check something, whether it's a light bulb\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:57.800\nor your understanding of a new subject.\n\n00:57.800 --> 00:58.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
