    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_171834.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.999\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:19.799\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to. It's like a little experiment to see if an idea, a product, or even your understanding of something is correct.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:26.199\nImagine baking a cake. You wouldn't just serve it without trying a little piece first, right? That's a test!\n\n00:26.200 --> 00:31.399\nOr, let's say you're building a tower of blocks. You gently push it to see if it's stable. That's another kind of test.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:36.399\nTests help us learn and improve.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:42.699\nIf the cake tastes bad, we adjust the recipe. If the tower falls, we rebuild it stronger.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:52.099\nSo, a test is simply a way to confirm something and make it better. Ultimately, tests help us avoid problems and make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:54.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
