    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_173359.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_173359.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 but not the kind you take in school!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:19.100\nWe're talking about tests as a way to check if something is working the way it should. Think of it like this: you have a toy car, and you want to make sure it rolls.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:25.900\nThe test is simply pushing the car and seeing if it moves. If it does, the test passes! If it doesn't, something's wrong.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:30.100\nAnother example? You want to know if a light bulb works.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:35.500\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If the light turns on, the test passes.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:41.900\nIf it stays dark, the test fails. So, a test is just a simple way to see if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:50.300\nIt's checking for the right result. Simple, right? This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4197bea9-36f9-4cf7-9a4b-6fdc683b92ee": {
    "id": "4197bea9-36f9-4cf7-9a4b-6fdc683b92ee",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:02:27.995747",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T17:34:45.919498",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_173445.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_173445.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:21.300\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. Think of it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:30.100\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:37.300\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test! You're testing your recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:49.200\nSo, tests help us understand things better. They can tell us about our health, our knowledge, or even how well a recipe works.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:54.900\nBasically, a test is just a way to learn more and get some answers. That\u2019s the basics of tests! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
