    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_173549.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:21.500\nIt's like an experiment or a series of questions designed to give us information.\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:32.400\nThink about it: a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling. A taste test helps you decide which flavor of ice cream you like best.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:42.100\nEven when a doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:51.800\nSo, tests can be quizzes at school, experiments in a lab, or even just trying something out to see what happens.\n\n00:51.800 --> 00:57.800\nThe key is that they help us learn and understand things better. They give us answers.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:11.100\nTo recap, a test is a method for gathering information and finding things out. It can be formal or informal, but its purpose is always the same: to learn something new.\n\n01:11.100 --> 01:14.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
