    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_173704.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.300\nNo need to worry, this isn't the kind you need to study for! A test, in a general sense, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done, so you poke one with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:33.400\nThe toothpick comes out clean, so the test shows they're ready. Another example: a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:47.000\nOr, you might test a new lightbulb to see if it works. So, a test is simply a way to gather information and see if something meets a certain condition or expectation.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:54.700\nBasically, you perform an action or observation, and then you interpret the result. Easy peasy!\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:01.100\nRemember, a test is just a check. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
