    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_174921.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:19.800\nThink of it like an experiment, but usually a bit more focused.\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:27.400\nYour doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nA chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:44.800\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to test how well you understand a topic.\nSo, in each of these examples, we're performing an action \u2013 taking blood, tasting sauce, answering questions \u2013 to learn something.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:54.200\nThe results of that action, that's what tells us the answer.\nTests help us make decisions and learn more about the world around us.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:04.100\nTo sum it up, a test is a method for gathering information.\nIt helps us understand, measure, and evaluate things.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:07.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "38cad00b-e33d-46c0-8427-4b3fb5ba7563": {
    "id": "38cad00b-e33d-46c0-8427-4b3fb5ba7563",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:02:40.499678",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T17:50:10.952352",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_175010.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_175010.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but a test is really just a way to check something to see if it works, or if it's true.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:28.000\nThink of it like this: you might test the water in a pool to see if it's warm enough to swim in.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:37.800\nOr, a baker might test a cake with a toothpick to see if it's done. We're just checking to see if something meets a certain condition.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:43.800\nFor example, you could test if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:51.000\nIf it lights up, it passed the test! If it doesn't, well, it failed. So, a test is a simple way to confirm something.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:58.800\nWe check, we see, we know! In short, a test is a way to find out if something is working correctly or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:58.800 --> 01:02.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c7516946-ee18-4528-a7d3-247e43bb3bed": {
