    "id": "9db12891-b63c-4eed-ac7d-3dd9a2abef8b",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:02:47.092030",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T17:59:37.855475",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_175937.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_175937.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.800\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:04.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:08.200\nIt\u2019s a process, or a procedure, designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:15.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\nYou perform a test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it.\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:19.500\nTests aren't just for baking, though.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:22.500\nDoctors use tests to check your health, like taking your temperature.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.900\nTeachers use tests to see how much you've learned in class, like a quiz.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:28.800\nAnd even scientists use tests to prove if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:36.300\nSo, a test is just a tool.\nIt helps us gather information and make decisions based on that information.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:38.400\nRemember, it's all about finding something out!\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:40.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c8cceee3-1a29-4530-b59c-2d0584a9a83c": {
    "id": "c8cceee3-1a29-4530-b59c-2d0584a9a83c",
    "topic": "Test",
