    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_180041.mp4",
    "subtitles": "[WebVTT]\n```\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:21.000\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking, so you do a quick test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in them. If it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:26.900\nIn science and math, tests are similar. They help us see if an idea or a solution is right.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:36.800\nFor example, a math test checks if you understand how to solve problems. Or, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:47.900\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something is true or working correctly. It helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d465797e-3207-4974-b862-1ff91ba20068": {
    "id": "d465797e-3207-4974-b862-1ff91ba20068",
