    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_180439.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.400\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school exams.\nA test is really just a way of finding out something specific about something else.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:23.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\nThe \"something else\" could be anything!\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.800\nMaybe you're testing if a toy car goes faster with bigger wheels.\nOr maybe you're testing if a plant grows taller with more sunlight.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:41.400\nSo, how do you do a test?\nWell, you change one thing, what we call a variable, and see what happens.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:48.900\nFor example, you give one plant more water than another, and then you measure which one grows taller.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:54.100\nTests help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:02.500\nThey let us learn and discover new things.\nThey're a fundamental part of science, and they can be a lot of fun!\n\n01:02.500 --> 01:09.800\nRemember, a test is simply a way to find something out.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
