    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_180624.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:07.400\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:13.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:16.500\nIt's a process we use to gather information\nand see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:23.300\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:24.100\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:28.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:32.800\nOr maybe you want to see if you remember your friend's phone number.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:34.800\nYou try to recite it from memory.\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:35.700\nThat's another test!\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:37.200\nYou're testing your recall.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:43.300\nTests can be simple, like those examples, or more complex, like a school exam.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:47.500\nBut the basic idea is always the same: to learn something new or confirm something we already think we know.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:54.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and check if something is right.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
