    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_181506.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:11.200\nNow, what is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:21.000\nIt's like an experiment or a check-up. Think of it this way: when you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:34.200\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, if you're learning to ride a bike, each time you try and stay balanced, you're testing your skills.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:47.700\nTests aren't just for cakes and bikes, though. They're used in schools to see what you've learned, in science to prove new ideas, and even in everyday life to help us make decisions.\n\n00:47.700 --> 00:57.900\nSo, a test is just a process to see if something is true, works, or is ready. That's the basics of what a test is!\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
