    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_182057.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something. Think of it like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:21.400\nIn real life, we use tests all the time. Your doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:31.500\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done \u2013 if the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:37.800\nLet's say you want to know if your toy car needs new batteries. You could try turning it on.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:44.400\nIf it moves slowly or not at all, that's a test telling you the batteries are probably dead. See? A test!\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:54.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it's working correctly, or if something is true. Simple as that!\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:59.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
