    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:10.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:18.000\nIt's a process designed to measure your knowledge, ability, or understanding of a particular subject.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:25.800\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:29.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:36.600\nOr, if you want to know if you understand a new math concept, you might try solving a few practice problems.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:38.800\nThat's another test.\n\n00:38.800 --> 00:42.200\nTests come in many forms.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:46.600\nThey can be written, like quizzes or exams, or they can be practical, like a driving test.\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:54.400\nThe key thing is that they help us evaluate progress and identify areas where we might need to learn more.\n\n00:54.400 --> 01:01.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool for learning and improvement.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.400\nIt helps us see what we know and what we still need to work on.\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:08.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
