    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_182604.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:22.700\nIt's a process we use to check or evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, the quality of a product, or even how well something works.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:29.900\nThink about it like this: When you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:40.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test! Or, in school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:51.500\nTests can be quizzes, experiments, inspections, or even just observations. The important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:51.500 --> 01:01.000\nSo, to recap: a test is a method of finding something out, providing valuable information or confirmation.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:07.600\nIt helps us understand and improve things. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
