    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:15.600\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:25.400\nThink of it like a way to check your knowledge or the quality of a product.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:35.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:45.700\nOr, a taste test might help decide which cookie recipe tastes the best. In both cases, we're using the test to get information.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:59.300\nAnother example is testing a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids to play with. They might drop it, bend it, and see if anything breaks off.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:05.600\nTests are all about gathering information and learning something new.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:11.900\nSo, to recap, a test is a process designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or quality.\n\n01:11.900 --> 01:15.100\nIt helps us understand something better.\n\n01:15.100 --> 01:16.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
