    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_184155.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.900\nNow, a test, in the simplest terms, is just a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:22.000\nThink of it like checking if your cookies are baked by poking them with a toothpick. The toothpick is the test!\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:29.400\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:37.000\nBut tests aren't just for school. A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it's strong enough.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:52.400\nSo, tests are basically a way to get information and make sure things are working as they should. They can be simple, like tasting soup to see if it needs more salt, or more complex, like a big exam.\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:01.800\nThe main point is, they help us learn and improve. In short, a test is a way of assessing knowledge or performance.\n\n01:01.800 --> 01:05.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
