  "2b574901-a1ed-4ffd-aebe-051132b07c88": {
    "id": "2b574901-a1ed-4ffd-aebe-051132b07c88",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:03:24.328056",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T18:43:37.438950",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_184337.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_184337.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:05.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:10.700\nA test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:10.700 --> 00:17.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:20.500\nThat's a test! The toothpick comes out clean, the test passes, and you know the cake is ready.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:27.700\nOr maybe you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works. You screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:31.900\nIf it lights up, the test passes, the bulb is good.\n\n00:31.900 --> 00:36.000\nIf it stays dark, the test fails, and the bulb is probably broken.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:43.000\nSo, a test is just a procedure we use to check if something is working correctly or has a certain quality.\n\n00:43.000 --> 00:49.100\nBasically, we're asking a question and getting an answer through a specific action.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:52.300\nAnd that's the basic idea of what a test is!\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
