    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.400\nNow, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:22.200\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a cake is ready.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:29.600\nSo, you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:33.200\nThat's a test!\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:40.300\nThe toothpick comes out clean? The cake passes the test, it's done!\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:47.400\nThe toothpick has batter on it? The cake fails, and needs more time in the oven.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:54.100\nOr, imagine you're learning your ABCs. Your teacher might give you a quiz, right?\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:00.800\nThat quiz is a test to see if you know your letters.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:09.100\nTests can be used to check all sorts of things, from baking a cake to learning new skills.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:15.400\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method for figuring something out.\n\n01:15.400 --> 01:20.600\nIt's a question, and the answer tells you something important.\n\n01:20.600 --> 01:26.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
