    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_185224.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:20.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to find something out. It's a procedure we use to gather information, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:31.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. A teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:39.800\nOr, even simpler, you might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it into a lamp. You're performing a test!\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:52.300\nSo, a test involves a specific action, and then observing the result to reach a conclusion.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:04.100\nWe do tests all the time, often without even realizing it. They help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:09.100\nTo recap, a test is a process of gathering information or checking functionality.\n\n01:09.100 --> 01:12.700\nIt involves an action and an observation. Easy, right?\n\n01:12.700 --> 01:16.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
