    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.280 --> 00:03.710\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" before, right?\n\n00:03.710 --> 00:05.470\nBut what does it actually mean?\n\n00:05.770 --> 00:07.910\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:08.390 --> 00:09.850\nIt's like a question you ask to see what the answer is.\n\n00:10.480 --> 00:14.830\nThink of it like this: a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:15.160 --> 00:18.250\nOr, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:18.650 --> 00:22.990\nA scientist might run an experiment, which is a type of test, to see if their idea is correct.\n\n00:23.390 --> 00:26.090\nTests can be anything from a quick check to a long process.\n\n00:26.510 --> 00:29.650\nThe important thing is that they help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:29.970 --> 00:35.900\nSo, whether it's checking if your cookies are baked enough, or a big exam at the end of the year, a test is all about finding information.\n\n00:36.310 --> 00:38.440\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
