    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_190410.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.800\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something.\nIt's how we check if something is working, if something is true, or even just how well we know something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:27.500\nThink about it like this: your doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\nA teacher might give you a test to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:42.200\nAnd even you can do a test, like tasting a new food to see if you like it!\nSo, tests can be formal, like a big exam, or informal, like trying out a new video game.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:49.800\nThe important thing is that they help us get information.\nThey help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:57.500\nIn short, a test is a method to assess or evaluate something.\nThat's the basics of what a test is.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e29f970e-a6e5-48b5-a3cb-4a8f6032b514": {
    "id": "e29f970e-a6e5-48b5-a3cb-4a8f6032b514",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:03:39.566140",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T19:05:02.475466",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_190502.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_190502.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.700\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. We use tests all the time, whether we realize it or not.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:30.700\nThink of it like this: a test is like asking a question and seeing what the answer is. The main idea behind any test is to find out if something is working properly or if something is true.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:42.200\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:51.700\nAnother example is checking if your phone is charged. The battery icon is a test, showing you how much power you have left.\n\n00:51.700 --> 01:02.900\nTests help us make decisions and understand the world around us. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something and see what the result is.\n\n01:02.900 --> 01:06.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
