    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_190551.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:24.900\nIt\u2019s a process, usually with specific steps, designed to give us information.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:28.500\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:33.600\nYou screw it in, flip the switch, and bam, the light either shines or it doesn't.\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:38.700\nThat\u2019s a test! Another example?\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:42.200\nMaybe you're baking a cake.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:58.300\nYou taste the batter to see if it's sweet enough, that's testing the flavor, or a doctor might tap your knee with a little hammer to test your reflexes, so whether it's checking a lightbulb, tasting batter, or a doctor\u2019s checkup, a test is all about gathering information.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:04.600\nIt helps us understand something better.\n\n01:04.600 --> 01:06.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
