    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_190829.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What is a test?\n\n00:04.400 --> 00:12.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:21.600\nIt\u2019s a process designed to gather information. Think of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're sick.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:29.200\nOr, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:43.600\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. Some tests are simple, like checking if a light switch works. Other tests can be more complex, like taking a big exam in school.\n\n00:43.600 --> 01:00.100\nHere's another example: if you're building with LEGOs, you might test if two pieces fit together before you connect them. Or, if you're writing a story, you might read it aloud to test if it makes sense.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:03.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something, gather information, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n01:03.600 --> 01:07.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
