    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_191010.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:22.500\nIt\u2019s how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:30.600\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:38.700\nA chef might taste a dish to test if it tastes good.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:52.300\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to test what you've learned. So, tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:52.300 --> 01:03.700\nThey can be simple, like checking if a lightbulb turns on, or more complicated, like running a science experiment.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:09.000\nThe goal is always the same: to get information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:17.600\nIn short, a test is a way to evaluate something. It helps us understand how things work and make sure they're doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n01:17.600 --> 01:24.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d7e7480d-358a-4149-b035-847ce9b25a1b": {
