    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_191226.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.100\nToday we're going to talk about tests. A test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:29.600\nThat's a test! In more formal settings, tests help us measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:36.400\nLike, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling words. Or a taste test can help you decide which brand of soda you like best.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:41.200\nSo, tests help us answer questions. Does this work? How well do I know this? Which do I prefer?\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:47.800\nThey give us information we can use to make decisions or just understand things better.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:53.800\nBasically, a test is a way to get answers!\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
