    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_191839.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.600\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:14.000\nNow, a test is simply a way to check something, or find something out.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:29.500\nTests can be all sorts of things. You might take a quiz in school to test your knowledge.\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:36.400\nEven tasting a new recipe is a kind of test, to see if you like it!\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:41.700\nLet's say you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:46.900\nYou could test it by sticking your finger in the soil.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:51.600\nIf it feels dry, the plant probably needs watering. That's a test!\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:56.200\nAnother example: you try to turn on a light, but it doesn\u2019t work.\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:02.300\nYou test the bulb by replacing it with a new one.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:07.600\nIf the light turns on, you know the old bulb was the problem.\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:15.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information and learn something new.\n\n01:15.300 --> 01:19.700\nIt\u2019s a simple check to understand something better.\n\n01:19.700 --> 01:25.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
