    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_192543.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:12.000\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, a product, or even an idea.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:17.000\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.000\nThe toothpick is acting as a test! If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.000\nAnother example is a simple quiz in school. That's a test to see what you've learned.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:31.000\nCompanies also test their products before they sell them, making sure they're safe and work properly.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:37.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a process to learn something about something else.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.000\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:44.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
