    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_192736.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:25.600\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand better.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:32.500\nThink of it like this: You might test if a cake is done by poking it with a toothpick.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:37.900\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:43.300\nOr, maybe you're testing if you understand a new word.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:54.300\nYou could try using it in a sentence. If the sentence makes sense, you've passed that test!\n\n00:54.300 --> 01:00.700\nTests aren't scary. They're just tools to help us learn and see if something is working the way it should.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:07.100\nThey help us confirm our understanding and find areas where we might need to learn more.\n\n01:07.100 --> 01:13.400\nSo remember, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n01:13.400 --> 01:17.600\nIt gives us information.\n\n01:17.600 --> 01:21.700\nAnd that information helps us grow!\n\n01:21.700 --> 01:23.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "df3daaeb-76a9-40ef-82cb-d77956525129": {
    "id": "df3daaeb-76a9-40ef-82cb-d77956525129",
