    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_192933.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:12.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:21.200\nIt's a process designed to gather information. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to find out if you're sick.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:30.400\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt. In school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:41.000\nFor example, a simple quiz with multiple-choice questions is a test. So is checking the temperature of water to see if it's hot enough for tea.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:50.700\nBoth give you information to help you make a decision. So, to recap, a test is any procedure used to collect information.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:00.400\nIt could be a formal exam or just a quick observation. The goal is always the same: to learn something new!\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:03.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
