    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_193214.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:06.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests,\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:11.800\nwhich are basically just a way to check if something is working correctly or if you know something.\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:18.100\nThink of it like this: a test is like a question you ask to see if you get the right answer.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:23.600\nFor example, your teacher might give you a math test to see if you understand addition and subtraction.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:27.100\nOr, a doctor might run a test to check if you're healthy.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:29.700\nSee? Tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:35.300\nAnother example is baking a cake.\nYou might taste the batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:38.100\nIf it tastes good, you know you've got the right amount!\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:41.100\nSo, tests are all about checking and confirming.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:50.600\nIn short, a test is a method to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge, the functionality of a device, or even the taste of cake batter!\n\n00:50.600 --> 00:58.500\nThey help us learn and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
