    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_193719.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.100\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.100 --> 00:04.600\nToday we\u2019re going to explore the basics of a test.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:07.700\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school exams.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:13.100\nA test is really any process we use to gather information about something.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:16.900\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure something out, so you run a test to get some answers.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:22.800\nIt could be as simple as testing the temperature of water to see if it's hot enough for tea.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:26.500\nOr testing if a lightbulb works by screwing it in.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:28.200\nThese are all tests!\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:30.900\nWe observe what happens and then draw a conclusion.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:36.900\nSo, a test is all about asking a question and finding an answer through observation.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:39.700\nWe hope this helps you better understand the concept of a test.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:42.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
