    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_195251.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer that tells you more.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:38.400\nFor example, you might take a spelling test to see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:49.500\nOr, a scientist might test a new medicine to see if it helps people get better.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:56.500\nThe test gives them information, like scores on your spelling or if the medicine actually works.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:03.500\nTests aren't just in school or in labs, though! You test things all the time!\n\n01:03.500 --> 01:15.600\nLike, testing if the water is too hot before you get in the shower. Or testing if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n01:15.600 --> 01:26.700\nSo, to sum it up, a test is just a way to learn something new by asking a question and observing the answer.\n\n01:26.700 --> 01:33.000\nTests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:33.000 --> 01:34.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
