    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_200219.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something. It helps us find out if something is working as it should, or if something is true or false.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:26.000\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a fever. That's checking your temperature.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:33.300\nOr, when you're baking, you might test the cake with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:41.100\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. It checks if you've learned how to spell certain words correctly.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:53.100\nSo, remember, a test is simply a process for checking something. It helps us learn, diagnose, or make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:53.100 --> 00:56.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2897aa5b-35c7-4e76-aaef-324f1dec0741": {
    "id": "2897aa5b-35c7-4e76-aaef-324f1dec0741",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:04:25.381615",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T20:03:09.443593",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_200309.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_200309.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something really fundamental: tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:20.500\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to check if something works as expected. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb is good, so you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:32.400\nIn more formal settings, like in science or math, a test is a procedure designed to confirm or deny a specific hypothesis or idea.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:46.000\nFor example, if you think fertilizer makes plants grow faster, you could test that by growing two plants, giving one fertilizer and not the other, and then comparing their growth.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:58.300\nThe results of the test either support or refute your initial idea. So, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it's true or works correctly.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:08.500\nWhether it's a lightbulb or a plant, testing helps us understand the world around us. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4f92a6bc-baaa-49f5-a8dd-12dc8b3aaaec": {
    "id": "4f92a6bc-baaa-49f5-a8dd-12dc8b3aaaec",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:04:26.028307",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T20:04:07.906253",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_200407.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_200407.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something super important: the test.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:15.600\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we're usually talking about a way to check something. It could be anything, really!\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it as a question, or a challenge, that helps us understand more. So, what are we testing?\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:33.600\nWell, maybe you're testing if a cake is baked by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:44.100\nOr, imagine you're testing if a toy car needs new batteries. If it goes slow, that's a sign it's failing the test and needs fresh power.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:51.900\nTests help us learn. They tell us if things are working correctly, or if something needs to be fixed.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:01.400\nFrom checking if your homework is done to seeing if your eyes need glasses, tests are all around us, helping us every day!\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:11.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something to see if it works or if it's true. Easy peasy, right?\n\n01:11.000 --> 01:14.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
