    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_200451.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_200451.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.300\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:08.300 --> 00:12.900\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:12.900 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like gathering information. It could be anything!\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:25.100\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:29.700\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:34.300\nYou poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done. That's a test!\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:38.900\nOr maybe you try on a shirt to see if it fits.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:43.500\nAnother test! In school, tests help teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:50.400\nSo, whether it's checking a cake, trying on clothes, or answering questions in class, a test is simply a method to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:53.800\nIn short, it's a way of finding out something.\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
