    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:14.500\nSimply put, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.300\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that tells you more than you knew before.\n\n00:22.300 --> 00:24.900\nMaybe you're testing if a cake is done by poking it with a fork,\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:27.500\nor testing if your phone has Wi-Fi by trying to load a webpage.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:34.200\nSee? Tests are everywhere! Think of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:43.700\nYour test is screwing it into a lamp and flipping the switch. If the light comes on, the test is successful \u2013 the lightbulb works!\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:47.500\nIf it doesn't, well, you know the lightbulb is probably bad.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:53.600\nSo, tests help us learn, troubleshoot problems, and make decisions.\n\n00:53.600 --> 00:59.700\nThey're all about gathering information to see if something is true or false, working or not working.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:06.300\nThey are an essential part of everyday life. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
