    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_202804.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:19.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:26.600\nThe test? You stick your finger in the soil. If the soil feels dry, the test tells you the plant needs water!\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:31.500\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:37.400\nThe test to see if it's done? You poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:43.600\nThe test gave you information. So, a test is just a process to get an answer.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:53.800\nIt could be a science experiment, a classroom quiz, or even just checking the weather. Anything that helps you understand something better!\n\n00:53.800 --> 00:59.200\nThat's the basic idea of a test. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
