  "deda26bb-6df1-4a26-8b40-4fb2924aa596": {
    "id": "deda26bb-6df1-4a26-8b40-4fb2924aa596",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:04:54.396368",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T20:40:47.320595",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_204047.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_204047.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It's like asking a question, but instead of just talking, you're using a specific method to get an answer.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:27.200\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done. You could just guess, or you could test it by sticking a toothpick in the center.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:32.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That's a test!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:43.200\nOr, imagine you want to know if a lightbulb works. You don't just stare at it, you test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:45.800\nSee? Tests are everywhere.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:56.500\nThey help us learn things by giving us information. So, to recap, a test is a structured way to get information or find something out.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:03.600\nWe use tests all the time in our everyday lives. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
