    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_212230.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:11.800\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:11.800 --> 00:17.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:20.700\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets a certain standard.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like this: a spelling test shows if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:29.500\nA taste test tells you if food tastes good.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:31.700\nOr, a medical test can tell you if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:33.700\nSee?\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:35.400\nDifferent tests, different things they\u2019re checking.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:40.300\nSo, a test is really just a procedure designed to evaluate something.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:44.200\nIt could be your knowledge, the quality of a product, or even how well a website performs.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:49.300\nUltimately, tests provide information that helps us make decisions and improve things.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:56.400\nTo recap: tests are used to evaluate something, they help us learn about that thing, and they let us make informed decisions.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:00.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
