  "ae44a450-a06a-4b64-9666-236f724dadca": {
    "id": "ae44a450-a06a-4b64-9666-236f724dadca",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:05:29.322438",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T21:23:38.738968",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_212338.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_212338.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check if something works like it should.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it like a quality check. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:35.300\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:41.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:48.100\nOr, imagine you're trying out a new lightbulb. You screw it in to see if it lights up.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:54.500\nIf it does, the lightbulb passes the test.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:01.200\nSo, tests are a way to make sure things are working properly, whether it's a cake, a lightbulb, or even a computer program.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:05.900\nThey help us find problems and fix them.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:09.600\nIn short, a test verifies something is working as expected.\n\n01:09.600 --> 01:12.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f36f8007-8c10-4413-8371-896699910553": {
