    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_212659.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:15.700\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake and you take a bite. That bite is a test to see if the cake tastes good.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:30.600\nOr, you buy a new toy and press the button. That's a test to see if the toy turns on.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:37.900\nTests help us find problems early. If the cake tastes bad, you can change the recipe next time.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:44.000\nIf the toy doesn't work, you can exchange it. They give us valuable information.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:52.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a check, a simple way to see if something is doing what it's supposed to.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:55.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
