    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_213845.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:14.200\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:17.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:20.700\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:23.500\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:37.600\nThe toothpick comes out clean? Pass! The cake is ready. Tests can be formal, like the quizzes you take in school to see how well you understand a topic.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:45.000\nOr they can be informal, like testing if your new shoes are comfortable by wearing them around the house.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.400\nEven checking if the lightbulb works by flipping the switch is a test! You\u2019re testing if the bulb is good.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:56.600\nEssentially, a test helps you answer a question by giving you some kind of result.\n```"
