    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_213935.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests! In everyday life, we often use the word \"test\" to describe an exam at school.\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:19.700\nBut, in a broader sense, a test is really just a way of finding out something. It's a procedure designed to reveal information.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:24.400\nThink about it. A doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:33.700\nOr a chef might taste a sauce to see if it needs more salt. In both cases, they're performing a test to get specific information.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:40.100\nLet's say you want to know if your new plant needs water. You could stick your finger in the soil.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:45.700\nThat's a simple test! If the soil feels dry, it probably needs water.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:56.800\nIf it feels damp, it's likely fine. So, to recap, a test is any process we use to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:05.000\nIt can be a formal exam or a simple observation. The key is that it helps us understand something better.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:08.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
