    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_214130.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test, at its core, is simply a way to check something. Think of it like this: you're testing if a lightbulb works by turning it on.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:19.700\nDoes it light up? That's your test!\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:25.400\nTests are used everywhere. Your doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:33.700\nA chef might taste their food to test if it needs more salt. In school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:44.800\nFor example, a simple test could be asking \"What color is the sky?\" The correct answer, blue, shows you understand basic colors.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:55.900\nOr, a math test might ask \"What is 2 + 2?\" Answering with \"4\" proves you know your addition.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:04.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a method of checking something to see if it works, if it's correct, or if it meets a certain requirement.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:09.200\nThey help us understand and improve!\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:10.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
