  "1926f821-f56e-4cdd-add3-6df1b136b3d5": {
    "id": "1926f821-f56e-4cdd-add3-6df1b136b3d5",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:05:47.223986",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T21:46:34.877910",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_214634.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_214634.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:18.000\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:29.600\nThink about it like this. If you want to know if your cookies are done baking, you might use a toothpick as a test. You poke the cookie, and if the toothpick comes out clean, the cookies are ready.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:41.500\nOr, if you're buying a used car, you might take it for a test drive to see if it runs smoothly.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:49.200\nTests aren't just for baking or buying cars, though. Scientists use tests to prove their ideas, and doctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:56.900\nBasically, a test helps us learn something new or confirm what we already suspect.\n\n00:56.900 --> 01:00.500\nSo remember, a test is a tool for checking and confirming.\n\n01:00.500 --> 01:04.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
