    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_215548.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:05.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:09.200\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer,\n\n00:09.200 --> 00:12.100\nyou're looking for evidence.\n\n00:12.100 --> 00:14.800\nIt's a process where you give something a challenge,\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:17.100\nand then you observe how it responds.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:19.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:22.600\nA taste test checks how good something tastes.\n\n00:22.600 --> 00:26.300\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:28.700\nThe oven temperature is a test to see if the cake will bake properly.\n\n00:28.700 --> 00:33.200\nOr think about trying out a new app.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:36.700\nUsing the app is a test to see if it's easy to use and does what you expect.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:42.500\nSo, a test is really just a structured way to learn something by observing a response.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:47.200\nIt helps us understand and improve things all around us.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:49.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
