    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T22:04:26.780923",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_220426.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_220426.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.600\nOkay, let\u2019s talk about tests.\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:17.700\nYou\u2019ve probably taken a bunch of them in school, but what exactly is a test?\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:29.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out what someone knows or can do. It's like a measuring stick for knowledge or skill.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:37.800\nThink of it like this: if you want to know how tall you are, you use a ruler.\n\n00:37.800 --> 00:45.400\nIf you want to know how well you understand fractions, you take a math test.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:57.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling. A driving test checks your ability to drive safely. Even a taste test, like trying different kinds of ice cream, is a test to see which one you like best!\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:01.200\nSo, a test is just a tool we use to measure something.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.700\nIt helps us understand what we know, what we can do, and what we might need to learn more about.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:06.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
