    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_221118.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:15.900\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something specific.\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more organized way.\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might poke it with a toothpick.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:35.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\nOr, if you want to know if you understand a new math concept, you might try solving some problems.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:48.100\nIf you get them right, you've passed the test of understanding.\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking if a lightbulb works to seeing how much you've learned in school.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:57.700\nThey help us make decisions and understand the world around us better.\nSo remember, a test is just a structured way to get information.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
