    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_222313.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:13.400\nToday we're tackling a really important concept: Tests!\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:17.600\nNow, a test, at its simplest, is just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: you buy a new lightbulb, and you screw it in. That's a test!\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:26.600\nYou're checking if the lightbulb lights up.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:31.400\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs, though. They're used everywhere.\n\n00:31.400 --> 00:36.200\nA doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:41.000\nA baker tastes their cake batter to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.200\nEven you, when you try on a new pair of shoes, you\u2019re testing to see if they fit!\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:52.500\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to see if something is working correctly or meeting a certain requirement.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:55.600\nIt\u2019s all about checking and confirming.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:57.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
