    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_222406.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into what a test actually is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. Think of it as a question you're trying to answer, or a problem you're trying to solve.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:26.400\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. For example, when you bake a cake, you taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:35.100\nOr when you try a new route to school, you're testing if it's faster than your usual one.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:42.500\nTests aren't just for school! Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:50.700\nCompanies test new products to make sure people will like them.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:01.700\nSo, a test is really just a tool for learning and making decisions. It helps us understand something better.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:05.000\nSo remember, a test is a way to learn something new.\n\n01:05.000 --> 01:08.700\nIt could be as simple as tasting a cake or as complex as figuring out a medical diagnosis.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:12.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4e9ab657-9354-4174-88fb-3ebbe88b2aad": {
    "id": "4e9ab657-9354-4174-88fb-3ebbe88b2aad",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:06:22.010930",
