    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_222657.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:12.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:21.300\nIt\u2019s how we check if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like this: imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:29.300\nYou can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:33.300\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done! That\u2019s a test.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:39.100\nOr, say you build a tower of blocks. You can test its strength by gently pushing it.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:45.900\nDoes it wobble and fall, or does it stand strong? That's another test.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:52.700\nTests are super important because they help us learn and improve things. They tell us if we're on the right track.\n\n00:52.700 --> 00:55.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way of checking something\n\n00:55.500 --> 00:58.000\nto see if it works or is true.\n\n00:58.000 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
