    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.600\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:23.800\nBasically, a test is a way to check something, to see if it works, or if it's true.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:30.400\nThink of it like checking if your lightbulb works.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:37.000\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test!\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:43.600\nIn school, tests help teachers see what you've learned.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:53.100\nIf you get a good score, it shows you understand the material. But tests aren't just for school.\n\n00:53.100 --> 01:01.400\nDoctors use tests to check your health, like a blood test. And engineers test bridges to make sure they're safe.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:08.700\nSo, tests come in many forms and are used everywhere to confirm something is working as expected, or to gather information.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:14.800\nFrom simple lightbulb checks to complex medical analyses, tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:14.800 --> 01:17.600\nThat's the basics of what a test is!\n\n01:17.600 --> 01:23.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
