    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_223426.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_223426.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.000\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about something super important: tests!\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:16.300\nA test is simply a way to find out how much you know about a certain topic. Think of it like a measuring tool for your brain.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:25.700\nThey come in all shapes and sizes. Sometimes it's a multiple-choice quiz, like picking the right answer from a few options.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:34.900\nOther times, it might be writing an essay to explain your ideas. Or maybe even performing a task to show what you can do!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:44.200\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your words. A math test shows if you understand numbers and equations.\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:57.000\nAnd a driving test, well, that proves you can safely operate a car!\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:04.100\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool to help you and your teachers see what you've learned.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:11.200\nIt's a chance to show off your knowledge and identify areas where you might need a little more practice.\n\n01:11.200 --> 01:19.600\nDon't be afraid of them, embrace them as learning opportunities! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
