    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_224025.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something.\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:25.300\nEssentially, a test is a procedure to evaluate the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:36.100\nFor example, you might take a spelling test to see how well you know your spelling words.\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your overall health.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:45.800\nAnother example could be testing a new recipe.\nYou follow the instructions, and the result is the test of whether the recipe works!\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:54.900\nIf the cake rises and tastes good, the recipe passes the test.\nIf it's flat and burnt, well, it failed!\n\n00:54.900 --> 01:05.800\nSo, in short, a test is a method for gathering information and seeing if something meets a certain standard or works the way it's supposed to.\n\n01:05.800 --> 01:09.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
