    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:23.100\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:36.300\nTests can be used to check all sorts of things.\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\nA teacher gives you a test to see what you've learned.\nAnd you might even test out a new recipe to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:48.900\nThe core idea is always the same: you perform some action or ask some question, and then you look at the result.\nThat result tells you something about the thing you're testing.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:59.800\nSo, whether it's a pop quiz, a blood sample, or even just tasting a new cookie, that's a test!\nTo recap, a test helps us discover information by examining the outcome of an action or question.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
