    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.220 --> 00:03.330\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" thrown around,\n\n00:03.330 --> 00:05.150\nbut what does it really mean?\n\n00:05.150 --> 00:08.410\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out\nsomething about something!\n\n00:08.410 --> 00:11.130\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:11.130 --> 00:15.470\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:15.470 --> 00:21.190\nThink about it: When you try a new food, you're testing to see if you like it.\n\n00:21.190 --> 00:26.520\nOr when you press a button on a toy, you're testing to see if it works.\n\n00:26.520 --> 00:34.050\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if the water is warm enough before you jump in the pool.\n\n00:34.050 --> 00:41.290\nThe important thing is that a test helps us gather information and make decisions.\n\n00:41.290 --> 00:51.990\nSo, whether it's a science experiment or just seeing if your shoes fit, you're using a test to learn something new.\n\n00:51.990 --> 00:58.670\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
