    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_224711.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_224711.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:18.500\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:18.500 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. That's a test!\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:28.800\nYou screw it in and turn it on. If it lights up, the test passes. If it doesn't, it fails.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:35.600\nAnother example is a taste test. You try a new food to see if you like it. The test result is whether you enjoy the flavor or not.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:47.700\nSo, a test is just a way to check something, using a specific method, to see what the result is. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
