    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_225028.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_225028.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to explore something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:17.300\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school exams.\nA test is really just a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake.\nThe test is taking a bite to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:30.000\nOr, imagine you build a toy car.\nThe test is pushing it to see if it rolls.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:39.700\nIn computers, tests are the same idea.\nWe write small bits of code to check if our bigger programs are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:48.900\nFor example, if you write a program to add two numbers, a test would be to give it 2 and 3 and make sure it gives you 5.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:57.900\nSo, tests are simply ways to verify that things are working correctly, from cakes to cars to computer programs.\n\n00:57.900 --> 01:06.300\nThey help us catch mistakes early and make sure everything runs smoothly.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
