    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:25.100\nThink of it like a detective collecting clues.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:39.000\nWe use tests all the time, often without even realizing it! When you bake a cake, you test it with a toothpick to see if it's done. Or when you try on a new pair of shoes, you're testing to see if they fit.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:49.000\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like seeing if you can lift a heavy box.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:59.200\nThe point is always the same: to learn something new about ourselves, about objects, or about the world around us.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:05.700\nSo, to recap: a test is a method for collecting information, whether it's about a cake, shoes, or your knowledge.\n\n01:05.700 --> 01:09.200\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:14.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
