    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a structured way.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:36.000\nWe use tests every day, even if we don't realize it. For example, if you're baking a cake and you taste the batter, that's a test to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:46.000\nOr, if you try turning a key in a lock, you're testing if that key will open that lock.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:51.000\nIn school, you might take a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:54.000\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:54.000 --> 01:00.000\nEssentially, a test is just a method to check something and learn from the results.\n\n01:00.000 --> 01:07.000\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make decisions based on evidence.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:09.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
