    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:24.100\nWe use tests all the time, whether we realize it or not.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:30.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:34.400\nYou use a toothpick \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:36.800\nIf it comes out clean, the cookies are ready.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:40.800\nOr, maybe you're learning a new skill, like riding a bike.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:42.500\nFalling down?\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:43.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:48.100\nIt tells you what not to do next time.\n\n00:48.100 --> 00:52.800\nTests can be formal, like a school exam, or informal, like checking if your soup needs more salt.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:55.900\nThe important thing is that they give us information to help us learn and improve.\n\n00:55.900 --> 00:58.500\nIn short, a test is just a way to check something and get results.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:00.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "c925d600-fd9a-4af0-8fb4-154f3bb648e8": {
    "id": "c925d600-fd9a-4af0-8fb4-154f3bb648e8",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:06:48.780281",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-06T23:00:34.013273",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260106_230033.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_230033.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:19.800\nYou've probably taken a bunch of them, but what is a test, really?\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:28.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:33.700\nIt could be checking your knowledge, checking if a machine works, or even checking if food is safe to eat.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:39.700\nThe goal is to get information.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:43.600\nFor example, a math test helps your teacher see what you understand about numbers.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:49.600\nOr think about a smoke detector. That\u2019s testing the air for smoke!\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:57.700\nIf it finds smoke, it sounds an alarm. Another example is baking a cake. You might test it with a toothpick to see if it\u2019s done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.500\nSo, a test is just a way to find out something specific. It helps us understand things better and make sure everything is working as it should.\n```"
  },
