    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_230610.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.000\nThink of a test as a way to check something, to see if it works, or if it's true.\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:26.400\nIt\u2019s like a detective asking questions to solve a mystery.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:36.800\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:42.600\nFor example, you might test a cake to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:50.100\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:55.700\nSo, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:03.200\nIf it does, the test passes! If not, well, something's wrong.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:10.700\nAnother test might be reading a recipe and following the instructions.\n\n01:10.700 --> 01:14.900\nDoes the final dish look like the picture? That's a test!\n\n01:14.900 --> 01:19.600\nTests are everywhere, helping us learn and improve things.\n\n01:19.600 --> 01:25.000\nRemember, a test is just a way to check if something works or meets a standard.\n\n01:25.000 --> 01:34.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
