    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_232711.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nWhat is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:26.000\nThink of it like this: You might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:44.100\nOr, a doctor might run tests to see what's making you feel sick. Even baking a cake involves a test \u2013 you poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done!\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:53.600\nSo, whether it's checking your knowledge, diagnosing a problem, or making sure your cake is perfectly fluffy, a test helps us understand something better.\n\n00:53.600 --> 01:04.000\nBasically, it gives us information. To recap, a test is a process used to gather information and check on things. It can be used in all sorts of ways, from school to cooking, and even in medicine!\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:06.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
