    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_232759.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE duration:61.7\n1\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n2\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n3\n00:11.900 --> 00:23.800\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n4\n00:23.800 --> 00:33.500\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n5\n00:33.500 --> 00:43.200\nOr, a baker might taste their cake batter to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n6\n00:43.200 --> 00:50.300\nEven checking if a lightbulb turns on is a kind of test!\n\n7\n00:50.300 --> 00:58.100\nSo, tests help us learn, make decisions, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n8\n00:58.100 --> 01:01.700\nWhether it's a school exam, a science experiment, or just checking if your shoes fit, tests are everywhere!\n\n9\n01:01.700 --> 01:05.600\nEssentially, a test is a question with a way to find the answer.\n\n10\n01:05.600 --> 01:08.100\nAnd that's the basics of what a test is!\n\n11\n01:08.100 --> 01:11.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
