    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_233129.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:04.500\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:07.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:11.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:13.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:19.000\nFor example, you might take a spelling test in school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:23.000\nOr, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:25.000\nSee?\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:28.000\nDifferent kinds of tests, but the idea is the same:\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:30.000\nto learn something new.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:34.000\nAnother example, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:37.000\nIt's a quick and easy way to get information.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a method of gathering information.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.000\nIt helps us understand something better.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:47.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
