    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_233310.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.600\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:06.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:10.200\nThink of it like a question you're asking something, and you're looking for the answer.\n\n00:10.200 --> 00:12.600\nIt's a process we use to gather information.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:16.100\nFor example, a math test helps us see how well you understand numbers.\n\n00:16.100 --> 00:19.200\nOr, a taste test tells us which food tastes better.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:23.500\nEven checking if a lightbulb works is a type of test! You're testing if it lights up.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:28.000\nTests can be formal, like exams in school, or informal, like trying out a new recipe to see if you like it.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.800\nThe important thing is that you're trying to learn something by doing it.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:38.500\nSo, a test is just a way of asking a question and getting an answer to learn more.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:56.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
