    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_233353.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nWell, in simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:20.800\nIt's like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:20.800 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:32.200\nThe test? You poke it with a toothpick. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:37.900\nOr maybe you want to see if a friend knows their ABCs.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:43.300\nYou ask them to recite the alphabet. That's another test!\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:50.400\nTests can be anything from a simple question to a complicated experiment.\n\n00:50.400 --> 00:54.200\nThey help us learn, understand, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:54.200 --> 00:57.500\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information. It's a question asked and answered! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
