    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_234232.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find something out, to check if something works, or to see if something is true.\n\n00:19.900 --> 00:27.600\nThink of it like this: If you want to know if a lightbulb is working, you put it in a lamp and turn it on. That's a test! You're testing the lightbulb.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:31.100\nOr, if you follow a recipe for a cake, tasting it afterward is a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:40.700\nTests are everywhere! Scientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct. Doctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:49.100\nEssentially, a test is a simple way to get information.\n\n00:49.100 --> 01:01.000\nSo, remember, a test is any process designed to determine something about something else.\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:04.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
