    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:12.400\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:24.800\nIt's a method for gathering information or checking if something is working correctly. Think of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might use a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:31.600\nYou poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, you know it's ready. Or, if your doctor listens to your heart with a stethoscope, that's also a test.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:40.700\nThey're checking to see if everything sounds healthy. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:52.400\nThey can be simple, like checking if a light switch works, or more complex, like a science experiment.\n\n00:52.400 --> 01:04.200\nThe important thing is they help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:04.200 --> 01:07.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to get information\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:11.500\nand see if something is how it should be.\n\n01:11.500 --> 01:15.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
