    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_234645.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:13.100\nNow, a test is simply a way to see what you know about something.\n\n00:13.100 --> 00:19.600\nThink of it like checking your understanding. It's like a snapshot of your knowledge at a particular moment.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:30.100\nTests come in many forms. You might take a multiple-choice test where you pick the best answer from a list.\nOr, you could have a fill-in-the-blank test, where you complete a sentence.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:38.200\nSometimes, you'll even have a practical test, like showing someone how to ride a bike to prove you know how.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:46.300\nSo, let's say you've been learning about animals. A test might ask you to identify different animals from pictures, or maybe describe what they eat.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:57.200\nThe goal is to show that you've learned the material. In short, a test is just a tool to help you and your teachers understand what you've learned and what you might need to work on.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:01.700\nRemember, it's just a way to check your understanding!\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:09.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "eed1389f-efc1-4b9c-941c-eaf7ea8e7c7d": {
