    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_234741.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, right? You \"test\" it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.600\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:34.400\nOr, imagine you're trying to turn on a light. The \"test\" is flipping the switch.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:41.200\nIf the light comes on, the test passes! If it doesn't, something's wrong.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:50.500\nTests are super important because they help us find problems early and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to.\n\n00:50.500 --> 00:56.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is working.\n\n00:56.700 --> 00:58.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
