    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something super important: the concept of a test.\n\n00:08.600 --> 00:18.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information. Think of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:28.000\nWe use tests all the time, whether we realize it or not. For example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:37.400\nA teacher might give you a quiz to see what you've learned. Even trying a new recipe is a kind of test, seeing if you like the taste!\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:47.600\nThe key thing about a test is that it gives us data, or information, that we can then use to make decisions or understand something better.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:57.500\nSo, tests help us learn, diagnose, and even just try new things. That's the basics of what a test is.\n\n00:57.500 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "0cc5073e-e6d8-4bc3-aec5-2e2c81cebd37": {
