    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260106_235030.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:16.900\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:24.900\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:30.800\nThink of it like this: You want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:36.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:43.200\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake and you want to see if it's done.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:49.700\nYou stick a toothpick in it. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:49.700 --> 01:02.300\nTests aren't just for lightbulbs and cakes, though. They're used in all sorts of things, like checking if a website loads properly, or if a toy is safe for kids.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:09.200\nBasically, if you're trying to figure something out, chances are you'll use a test.\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:18.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is working or true.\n\n01:18.600 --> 01:25.400\nIt's a tool to help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:25.400 --> 01:29.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
