    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.280 --> 00:02.580\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.580 --> 00:03.710\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:03.710 --> 00:05.170\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.170 --> 00:08.850\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how well something works, or how much of something is present.\n\n00:08.850 --> 00:13.400\nThink about it like this: when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's done.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:16.470\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:16.470 --> 00:17.100\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:20.860\nOr, imagine you want to know how much water is in a glass.\n\n00:20.860 --> 00:23.270\nYou could use a measuring cup to test the water level.\n\n00:23.270 --> 00:29.870\nTests are used everywhere, from checking if your phone's battery is full, to doctors using medical tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:29.870 --> 00:33.890\nThey help us understand the world around us and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:33.890 --> 00:37.550\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:37.550 --> 00:39.990\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
