    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_000114.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:25.200\nIt's a process designed to evaluate your knowledge, skills, or abilities in a specific area.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:31.100\nThink of it like this: your doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:37.000\nOr, you might take a quiz in school to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:39.900\nSee? Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:49.200\nFor example, a multiple-choice test asks you to pick the best answer from a list.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:53.300\nA true or false test asks you to decide if a statement is correct.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:03.200\nAnd a practical test might involve doing something, like baking a cake or building a small model.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:13.300\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to measure something. It helps us understand what we know, what we can do, and where we might need some extra help.\n\n01:13.300 --> 01:16.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
