    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_001334.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:06.400\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:06.400 --> 00:10.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:14.400\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:14.400 --> 00:18.300\nFor example, if you're baking a cake and you poke it with a toothpick, that's a test.\n\n00:18.300 --> 00:20.700\nYou're testing if it's done.\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:24.600\nOr, when a doctor checks your temperature, that's a test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:30.200\nTests can be formal, like a school exam that helps your teacher know what you've learned.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:35.400\nOr, they can be informal, like tasting your soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:40.500\nBasically, a test is any process that helps us learn something new or confirm what we already suspect.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:44.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a tool for gathering information.\n\n00:44.400 --> 00:49.600\nIt helps us understand things better and make informed decisions.\n\n00:49.600 --> 00:52.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
