    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_001457.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:17.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:28.400\nIt could be about you, like a quiz to see what you know, or about something else, like testing the water to see if it's clean.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:35.300\nThe main idea is to gather information.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:44.100\nWe set up a situation, often with questions or tasks, and then we observe the results.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:51.500\nThese results give us data that we can use to draw conclusions.\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:58.900\nThink about a cookie recipe. You could \"test\" it by baking a small batch first.\n\n00:58.900 --> 01:06.300\nIf the cookies taste good, then you know the recipe works!\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:13.700\nOr imagine testing a toy to see how durable it is.\n\n01:13.700 --> 01:21.000\nYou might drop it a few times to see if it breaks.\n\n01:21.000 --> 01:29.300\nBasically, tests help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n01:29.300 --> 01:31.400\nThey\u2019re a crucial part of understanding the world around us.\n\n01:31.400 --> 01:41.100\nSo remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:41.100 --> 01:43.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
