    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_001741.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:15.400\nNow, a test is basically a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:24.600\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:35.900\nIn general, a test involves giving something an input, and then seeing if the output is what you expect.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:43.600\nSo, for example, if you pour water on a plant, a good test would be to check if it grows.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:49.100\nIf it does, the plant passed the test! If it doesn't, well, something might be wrong.\n\n00:49.100 --> 01:02.200\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it. Did you check if your shoes were tied before you went outside? That\u2019s a test!\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:06.000\nTests help us make sure things are working correctly and safely.\n\n01:06.000 --> 01:12.200\nSo, tests are just ways of checking if things work the way they should, by giving them something and seeing what happens.\n01:12.200 --> 01:15.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
