  "a1cb771b-baea-4f4e-ae88-405924cee2f7": {
    "id": "a1cb771b-baea-4f4e-ae88-405924cee2f7",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:08:01.086469",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T00:22:57.573153",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_002257.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_002257.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to see if something works correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:30.100\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:35.600\nIn science, tests are often experiments.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:43.200\nYou change one thing, like the amount of sunlight a plant gets, and then you watch what happens.\n\n00:43.200 --> 00:50.800\nThat's a test! Or imagine you're learning a new skill, like riding a bike.\n\n00:50.800 --> 01:01.600\nFalling down a few times is actually a test! It helps you figure out what you're doing wrong so you can improve.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:09.200\nSo, a test is basically a way of gathering information to learn something or to check if something is working as it should.\n\n01:09.200 --> 01:13.500\nWhether it\u2019s baking a cake, doing a science experiment, or even learning to ride a bike,\n\n01:13.500 --> 01:17.400\ntests help us understand the world around us.\n\n01:17.400 --> 01:19.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e709c48f-13f5-41db-8142-7909d01ede23": {
    "id": "e709c48f-13f5-41db-8142-7909d01ede23",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:08:02.250774",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T00:23:51.121412",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_002351.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_002351.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration:60.6\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're talking about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:11.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:22.500\nIt's how we check if something is true, or how well something works. Think of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you do a test!\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:30.000\nYou poke it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the test tells you the cake is ready.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:38.900\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, each time you try, you're essentially testing your balance and coordination.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:47.600\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like checking the weather before you go outside.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:57.100\nThey all help us gather information and make decisions. So, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new!\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:00.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "237dc8cf-8e31-4a9c-8152-9f669a824f73": {
