    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_002714.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```WebVTT\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat is a test?\nWell, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:23.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more structured way.\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a physical exam to test your health.\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:33.700\nEven your phone has built-in tests to make sure everything is working correctly!\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:38.900\nTests can come in many forms.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:50.900\nThey can be written, like a quiz in school.\nThey can be physical, like bending a piece of metal to see how strong it is.\nOr they can be digital, like running a computer program to see if it works as expected.\n\n00:50.900 --> 01:04.300\nSo, to recap, a test is a method for gathering information about something.\nIt helps us understand, diagnose, and improve all sorts of things in our world.\n\n01:04.300 --> 01:07.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
