    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_003727.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:24.500\nIt's like checking your understanding. Think of it like this: you learn about apples, and then a test might ask, \"What color are most apples?\"\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:35.600\nTests can come in many forms. Multiple choice, true or false, or even just answering questions out loud. The goal is always the same: to see what you've learned.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:47.400\nFor example, if you're learning about numbers, a test might ask you to add 2 + 2. If you get the right answer, it shows you understand basic addition!\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:57.700\nSo, a test is just a tool to measure your knowledge. It helps you and your teachers understand what you know and what you might need to learn more about.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
