    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_003836.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:07.000\nToday we're talking about tests, and no, not the kind you take in school!\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:13.000\nIn the world of science and technology, a test is simply a way to see if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, right?\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:21.000\nYou test it by sticking a toothpick in.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:24.000\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:25.000\nThat's a test.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:29.000\nOr maybe you build a toy car.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:33.000\nYou test it by letting it roll down a ramp to see if it goes straight.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:39.000\nTesting is super important because it helps us find problems and fix them before they become bigger issues.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:45.000\nWe test everything from apps on our phones to the brakes on our cars.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:48.000\nIt's all about making sure things are safe and reliable.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:54.000\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check if something works correctly.\n\n00:54.000 --> 00:58.000\nIt helps us improve things and make them better.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
