    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_004755.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:21.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:21.700 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like checking if your favorite toy still needs batteries, or seeing if you remember all the words to your favorite song.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:38.500\nThe main idea behind a test is to gather information and see if you've reached a certain level or standard.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:52.800\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly. A taste test checks how good food tastes.\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:03.200\nSo, if you're baking a cake, you might do a \"taste test\" to see if it needs more sugar.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:13.600\nOr, if you're learning a new language, a quiz is a test to see how many words you've learned.\n\n01:13.600 --> 01:19.200\nBasically, a test helps us measure and understand things better.\n\n01:19.200 --> 01:25.200\nTo sum it up, a test is a way to evaluate knowledge or performance.\n\n01:25.200 --> 01:29.200\nIt helps us learn and improve.\n\n01:29.200 --> 01:35.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
