    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_005528.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:18.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:27.300\nThink of it like this: you try a new recipe, that's a test to see if you like it!\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:37.300\nIn science and other fields, tests are more formal.\nThey help us understand if something is true or works as we expect.\n\n00:37.300 --> 00:53.000\nFor example, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\nOr, an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it's strong enough.\nTests usually involve a specific procedure, and we look at the results to draw a conclusion.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:56.200\nSo, you try the recipe, taste it, and then decide: did it pass the \"deliciousness test\"?\n\n00:56.200 --> 01:04.700\nSee?\nYou're a testing expert already!\nBasically, a test is a structured way to learn something new, or confirm something we already think we know.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
