    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_005658.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:16.900\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, but in a broader sense, a test is simply a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:23.700\nThink of it like this: you bake a cake, and then you taste it. That taste is a test!\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:31.800\nIt tells you if the cake is sweet enough, or if it needs more flavor. Or imagine you're trying to turn on a light.\n\n00:31.800 --> 00:48.400\nThe light switch is the test \u2013 does the light bulb turn on? In more formal settings, tests help us figure out if a product is safe, if a medicine is effective, or even if a computer program is working correctly.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:56.100\nSo, tests are all about checking and verifying. They're a crucial part of learning and building things.\n\n00:56.100 --> 01:03.200\nIn short, a test is just a way to see if something does what it's designed to do.\n\n01:03.200 --> 01:06.900\nSimple as that! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
