    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_005810.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling something fundamental: what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:15.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else. It's a method for gathering information.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a test to check your health. They might check your temperature to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:29.900\nThat temperature reading is the test's result.\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:37.900\nOr, imagine baking a cake. You might stick a toothpick in it to see if it's done.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:47.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready! That toothpick test tells you about the cake's doneness.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:59.000\nSo, tests are all around us, helping us understand the world. They help us figure out if something works, if something is safe, or simply what something is like.\n\n00:59.000 --> 01:02.600\nThey are a simple, yet powerful way to learn. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
