    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T01:03:38.738260",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_010338.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_010338.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:11.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like an experiment, but instead of chemicals, you're using questions or tasks. The main purpose of a test is to measure knowledge, skills, or abilities.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:35.900\nMaybe you're taking a math test to see how well you understand addition and subtraction. Or maybe you're taking a driving test to show you can safely operate a car.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:42.600\nTests can come in many forms. There are multiple choice tests, where you pick the best answer.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:51.900\nThere are written tests, where you write out your answers. And there are even practical tests, where you show what you can do.\n\n00:51.900 --> 01:06.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to measure something, whether it's knowledge, a skill, or an ability. It helps us understand what we know and where we might need to learn more.\n\n01:06.000 --> 01:09.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
