    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_011325.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.500\nA test is basically a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:18.100\nYou wouldn't just guess, right? You'd stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:26.800\nThat toothpick is your test! Tests help us understand if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:37.600\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. A software engineer might run a test to see if their program does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:37.600 --> 00:45.800\nSo, tests are important because they give us information. They help us make decisions and solve problems.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:54.600\nThey tell us if something is right or wrong. That's the power of a test! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
