  "3e62dcbd-370f-4b40-9381-9eab2398ab8d": {
    "id": "3e62dcbd-370f-4b40-9381-9eab2398ab8d",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:08:52.127300",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T01:14:58.879275",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_011458.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_011458.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:17.100\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like asking a question, but instead of just listening to an answer, you're actually observing something to get the answer.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:38.400\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done baking, you can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If the toothpick comes out clean, then the cake is probably ready!\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:41.200\nOr, if you want to know if a lightbulb works,\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:53.300\nyou test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on. Does it light up? That's your test. Basically, a test is any action or procedure designed to reveal information.\n\n00:53.300 --> 01:03.300\nIt helps us understand things better by giving us clear, observable results. So, remember, a test is just a way to get information through observation.\n\n01:03.300 --> 01:06.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ea960e2c-51a4-410a-9db6-2494749c3738": {
    "id": "ea960e2c-51a4-410a-9db6-2494749c3738",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
