    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_011554.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.100\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:27.700\nIt could be finding out if you know your ABCs, or if a cake is ready to come out of the oven.\n\n00:27.700 --> 00:36.000\nBasically, you're giving something a challenge and seeing how it responds.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:42.900\nThink about it like this: a spelling test checks your knowledge of spelling.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:49.800\nA taste test checks how something tastes.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:56.700\nHere's another example: Imagine you're checking if a lightbulb works.\n00:56.700 --> 01:03.600\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If the light comes on, the lightbulb passes the test!\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:08.500\nIf it doesn't, well, it fails.\n\n01:08.500 --> 01:16.300\nSo, a test is just a method for gathering information by observing a response to a specific situation.\n\n01:16.300 --> 01:21.600\nIt helps us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:21.600 --> 01:23.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "00427daf-92eb-446f-8fdb-c4861b2ede4f": {
    "id": "00427daf-92eb-446f-8fdb-c4861b2ede4f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:08:53.444709",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T01:16:32.060433",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_011631.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_011631.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey there! Ever heard the word \"test\" and wondered what it really means?\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.000\nWell, in simple terms, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like this: a chef might test a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:41.300\nOr, a doctor might test your eyesight to see if you need glasses. The test gives them information to make a decision.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:52.500\nSo, a test can be anything from a quiz at school, to checking if your car's brakes are working properly, to even trying out a new recipe to see if it tastes good. It's all about gathering information and seeing what the results tell you.\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:58.800\nBasically, a test is a way to learn more and make sure things are working as they should. It helps us understand things better! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
