    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_011716.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nHello everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:14.600\nToday, we're going to explore something super important: tests!\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:21.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out information.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:31.000\nIt could be about anything! Think of it like this: you might test a cake to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:36.900\nOr, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:45.200\nIn school, tests help your teacher understand what you've learned.\n\n00:45.200 --> 00:53.500\nSo, a pop quiz in class is a test. Tasting your food while cooking is a test. Even checking if your shoes fit is a type of test!\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:55.600\nIt's all about gathering information and seeing where things stand.\n\n00:55.600 --> 00:59.200\nTo recap, a test is a process designed to evaluate or measure something.\n```"
  },
