    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.100\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" thrown around,\n\n00:03.100 --> 00:06.300\nbut what does it really mean?\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:08.700\nSimply put, a test is a way\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:11.000\nto gather information about something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.800\nThink of it like an investigation.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:20.200\nWe ask questions or perform actions to see what happens and learn something new.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:23.900\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:28.000\nA taste test helps you decide which cookie is your favorite.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:32.600\nEven when you try a new game, you're essentially testing it out to see if you like it!\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:35.900\nTests help us learn, improve, and make decisions.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:42.000\nThey can be formal, like exams in school, or informal, like figuring out if your shoes still fit.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:45.800\nThe key is that they provide information.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:51.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to learn more by asking questions or trying things out.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:54.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
