    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_012427.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:08.000\nIn simple terms, a test is really just a way to find out something.\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:15.000\nThink of it like asking a question and seeing what answer you get.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:20.000\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:27.000\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.000\nThat's a test to see if the cake is done.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:37.000\nOr, imagine you\u2019re trying to guess what\u2019s inside a box.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:40.000\nShaking it and listening to the sound is a test to give you a clue.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:46.000\nTests can be formal, like the ones you take in school, or informal, like checking if your shoes are tied.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:52.000\nThe point is, a test helps you understand something better by giving you information.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:55.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:57.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
