    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T01:34:08.158600",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_013408.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_013408.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:10.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:10.900 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like this: you might test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough. In science and other fields, tests are used to gather information and see if something is true or works as expected.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:36.200\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health. Or, an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it's strong enough to hold cars.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:45.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something, whether it's a cake, your health, or a bridge.\n\n00:45.400 --> 00:52.900\nThey help us learn and make sure things are working properly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
