    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_013917.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:15.000\nAt its core, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:19.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works,\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:30.600\nso you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test! You\u2019re testing if the lightbulb turns on.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:41.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Maybe you're testing your knowledge with a quiz, or a scientist is testing a new medicine to see if it helps people.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:56.700\nEven a chef tasting their soup is performing a test to see if it needs more salt. Basically, a test is an action performed to get information about something. It helps us understand if something is working as expected, or if it needs improvement.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.300\nSo, remember, whenever you're trying to find something out by doing something, you're probably performing a test!\n```"
  },
