    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_014154.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:14.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:23.600\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. It helps us measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:33.200\nFor example, a spelling test helps us see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:36.100\nOr think about a taste test \u2013\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:40.700\nit helps us decide which food tastes best!\n\n00:40.700 --> 00:49.100\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works. You plug it in. That's the test!\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:56.800\nIf it lights up, it passes. If not, it fails. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something and see how it performs or what its characteristics are. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
