  "1288d838-3c7c-467d-95cf-c2cd5a6d749e": {
    "id": "1288d838-3c7c-467d-95cf-c2cd5a6d749e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:09:19.624141",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T01:49:30.916063",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_014930.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_014930.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:14.600\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:25.900\nThink of it like asking a question and then finding the answer. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it!\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:36.600\nFor example, when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:45.800\nYou poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, that's the answer: the cake is ready!\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:56.000\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Teachers use tests to see how much you've learned in class. Even scientists use tests to prove if their ideas are right or wrong.\n\n00:56.000 --> 00:59.600\nSo, in short, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n```"
  },
  "29d9b364-e509-4d22-957c-96aad4ffa352": {
    "id": "29d9b364-e509-4d22-957c-96aad4ffa352",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:09:20.413834",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T01:50:21.228165",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_015021.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_015021.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:11.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into the world of tests \u2013 not the kind you cram for, but the kind that helps us understand how things work.\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:20.100\nBasically, a test is just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:24.600\nYou put it in a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:29.400\nThe light either turns on, or it doesn't. Another example?\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:36.800\nImagine you're baking a cake. You follow the recipe, put it in the oven, and then\u2026 you check it!\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:44.200\nSticking a toothpick in is a test to see if it's done. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:44.200 --> 00:52.300\nSo, tests are all about checking if something is working correctly, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:63.500\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are doing what they're supposed to do. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
