    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_015849.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:17.200\nWhat are they, and why do we use them? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something, or how well you can do something.\n\n00:17.200 --> 00:26.300\nThink of it like this: if you're learning to ride a bike, a test might be seeing if you can ride all the way down the street without falling.\n\n00:26.300 --> 00:36.600\nOr, if you're learning your ABCs, a test could be naming all the letters in the alphabet.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:43.900\nTests aren't just for school, either.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:55.400\nA doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy, or a chef might taste a dish to test if it needs more salt. Ultimately, tests help us measure and understand things better.\n\n00:55.400 --> 00:59.000\nSo, tests help us see what we've learned, and what we still need to work on.\n```"
  },
