    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.700\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:16.200\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:23.000\nThink of it like this: you want to see if a lightbulb works, so you screw it in and flip the switch.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:32.700\nBasically, a test helps us find out if something is working the way it should.\nIt could be a math test in school to see if you understand fractions, or a quality control test on a new toy to make sure it's safe for kids.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:43.100\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\nOr a software developer might test their program to find and fix any bugs.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:45.600\nSee?\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:45.600 --> 00:55.900\nSo, to recap, a test is a method of checking something to see if it meets a certain standard or works as expected.\nIt helps us identify problems and make improvements.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
