    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_020833.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_020833.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:23.400\nIt's a procedure designed to measure or evaluate. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a physical exam \u2013 that's a test to check your health.\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:35.400\nOr, a teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see how well you understand the material. Even baking a cake is a kind of test; you're testing your recipe!\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:50.800\nSo, tests can be formal, like a standardized exam, or informal, like trying out a new recipe. They all have the same basic purpose: to gather information and learn something.\n\n00:50.800 --> 00:60.200\nThey help us understand where we are, and where we need to go. Remember, tests aren't scary, they're just tools.\n\n00:60.200 --> 00:63.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
