    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_021351.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.700\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:11.700 --> 00:21.900\nThink of it like this: you might test if your cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:21.900 --> 00:34.500\nIn science, tests are used to see if an idea, called a hypothesis, is correct.\nFor example, you might test if plants grow faster in sunlight.\nYou'd give some plants sunlight and keep others in the dark, then compare their growth.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:43.300\nTests aren't just for science or baking.\nWe use them every day!\nWhen you try a new restaurant, you're testing if you like the food.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:49.800\nSo, remember, a test is a way to find out if something is true, works, or if you simply like it.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:54.700\nIt helps us learn and make decisions.\n\n00:54.700 --> 00:57.100\nThis video was created by\n\n00:57.100 --> 01:00.600\nApilage AI.\n```"
