    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:22.500\nIt's like asking a question and seeing what the answer is.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:32.700\nThink of it like this: you might test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:32.700 --> 00:39.200\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:45.700\nOr, you could test the batteries in your remote control to see if they still have power.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:52.200\nTests aren't just for baking and electronics.\n\n00:52.200 --> 01:03.700\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Teachers use tests to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n01:03.700 --> 01:16.400\nBasically, whenever you want to check or evaluate something, you're probably using a test.\n\n01:16.400 --> 01:29.100\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to gather information or evaluate something. It can be as simple as poking a cake or as complex as a medical exam.\n\n01:29.100 --> 01:35.700\nThe goal is always to learn something new.\n\n01:35.700 --> 01:42.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
