  "78bce223-8cdc-4cce-8405-c0c0c22a7819": {
    "id": "78bce223-8cdc-4cce-8405-c0c0c22a7819",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:09:51.016536",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T02:21:22.980030",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_022122.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_022122.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, let\u2019s talk about tests!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.700\nAt its most basic, a test is simply a way to find something out.\n\n00:05.700 --> 00:08.700\nWe use them all the time, whether we realize it or not.\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:14.300\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if an oven is hot.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:19.000\nYou could stick your hand in it, but that's not a good idea!\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:22.500\nInstead, you might hold your hand near it to test if you feel heat.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:23.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.000\nOr, maybe you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.300\nYou screw it into a lamp and flip the switch.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:33.400\nIf it lights up, the test is successful!\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:34.700\nThe lightbulb works.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:36.300\nIf it doesn't, the test failed.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:41.100\nSo, a test is just a way of checking something.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:45.700\nIt helps us learn if something is true, false, working, or not working.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:52.900\nIt's a simple, but powerful tool for understanding the world around us.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:55.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e1840b35-85a5-43ad-bdd6-8d845e69e324": {
    "id": "e1840b35-85a5-43ad-bdd6-8d845e69e324",
    "topic": "Test",
