    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_022250.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:07.500\nWhat are they, and why are they important?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:13.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to see what you know or what you can do.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is ready, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:18.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:23.800\nIn school, tests help your teachers understand what you've learned.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:29.600\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you remember how to spell words.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:33.900\nA math test checks if you understand how to solve problems.\n\n00:33.900 --> 00:39.500\nTests aren't just for school, though. When you try to ride a bike for the first time, that's kind of a test too!\n\n00:39.500 --> 00:43.500\nYou're testing your balance and coordination.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:48.200\nSo, tests help us learn and understand things better.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:52.800\nThey show us what we're good at and what we need to work on.\n\n00:52.800 --> 00:56.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
