    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_022457.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nEver wondered what a test actually is?\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:18.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something. It could be your knowledge about a subject, your physical abilities, or even your personality.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:25.300\nThink of it like using a ruler to measure how tall you are. The ruler is the test, and your height is what we're measuring.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:35.100\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. A quiz in school is a test, a fitness challenge at the gym is a test, and even a survey you take online can be considered a test.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:44.800\nThey all give us information about something specific. For example, a math test tells us how well you understand math concepts. A running test shows us how fast you can run.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:54.500\nThe results help us understand where we are, and where we might need to improve.\n\n00:54.500 --> 01:03.800\nSo, in short, a test is a tool for measuring something. It helps us learn about ourselves and the world around us.\n\n01:03.800 --> 01:07.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
