    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_023358.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_023358.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to explore something really important: what is a test?\n\n00:08.400 --> 00:19.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\nIt's a process we use to gather information or see if something works the way we expect it to.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:26.800\nThink about it like this.\nIf you want to know if your cookies are done baking, you might use a toothpick.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:39.200\nSticking it in and seeing if it comes out clean is a test!\nOr, if you're learning a new language, a quiz is a test to see how well you understand the vocabulary.\n\n00:39.200 --> 00:47.300\nTests aren't just for school or baking, though!\nScientists use tests to see if new medicines are safe.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:59.600\nEngineers test bridges to make sure they can hold weight.\nBasically, anything where you're trying to confirm something or learn more, you're probably using some kind of test.\n\n00:59.600 --> 01:10.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information or check something.\nIt helps us learn and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n01:10.300 --> 01:13.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
