    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_023458.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like an experiment, where you try something out to see what happens. We use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:38.300\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. Or, if you're trying a new route to school, you're testing if it's faster than your old one.\n\n00:38.300 --> 00:53.900\nIn school, tests help your teachers see what you've learned. They aren't meant to be scary, but rather a way to show your understanding.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:00.200\nWhether it's a quiz, an exam, or even just trying something new, remember that a test is simply a tool for learning and understanding.\n\n01:00.200 --> 01:03.600\nSo, tests help us learn by experimenting.\n\n01:03.600 --> 01:06.200\nRemember that and you'll be fine.\n\n01:06.200 --> 01:07.700\nThis video was created by\n\n01:07.700 --> 01:08.700\nApilage AI.\n```"
  },
