    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.300\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're tackling something super important: tests.\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:16.300\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:27.900\nThink of it like checking your understanding of a topic. The main idea is to see if you\u2019ve learned the material.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:37.500\nIt\u2019s not about being perfect, but more about figuring out what you understand well and what you might need to review.\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:45.500\nFor example, if you're learning about animals, a test might ask you to name different types of animals or describe their habitats.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:53.500\nOr, if you're learning to bake, a test could involve following a recipe and seeing if your cake turns out right.\n\n00:53.500 --> 01:06.400\nThe result shows where you followed the recipe correctly, and where you may have made a mistake. So, to recap, a test is a tool to measure your knowledge on a specific subject.\n\n01:06.400 --> 01:11.700\nIt helps you and your teachers see what you've learned and what needs more work.\n\n01:11.700 --> 01:12.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
