    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_024458.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests \u2013 what they are and why we use them.\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:19.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:30.300\nThink of it like checking if something is working correctly, or seeing how much you've learned.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:38.400\nTests can be anything from a simple check, like making sure a light bulb turns on, to something more involved, like an exam at school.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:43.600\nThe important thing is that they give us data.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:52.100\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a chef might taste a soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:01.500\nSee? Tests are everywhere! So, in summary, a test is a process that gives us information about something. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
