    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_025336.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:13.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:17.500\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:26.600\nThink of it as a process. We use tests all the time. For example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:38.200\nA chef might taste their soup to see if it needs more salt. And you might take a quiz at school to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:52.600\nSo, tests help us learn, diagnose problems, and make decisions. They come in many different forms, but the main idea is always the same: to gather information.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:56.100\nIn short, a test is a structured way of gathering information to make an informed decision.\n```"
