    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:24.000\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:32.500\nThink of it like this: you touch a stove to see if it's hot \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:42.400\nOr maybe you check the weather forecast to see if you need an umbrella. That's another kind of test.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:54.600\nBasically, a test helps us gather information and make decisions. A doctor might run tests to see if you're sick. A chef might taste a soup to see if it needs more salt. And in school, your teacher gives you tests to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:54.600 --> 01:01.700\nSo, a test is just a process of gathering information.\n\n01:01.700 --> 01:04.700\nTests can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all help us learn something.\n\n01:04.700 --> 01:08.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
