    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_025635.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.700\nHey there! Ever heard someone say they took a test?\n\n00:04.000 --> 00:14.200\nWell, a test is simply a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:25.700\nThink of it like a game where you answer questions to show what you've learned. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:30.600\nSometimes it's a multiple-choice quiz, other times it might be solving a math problem, or even writing an essay.\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:34.500\nThe goal is always the same: to measure your understanding.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:39.700\nFor example, a spelling test checks how well you know your words.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:43.500\nA history test asks about important events from the past.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:47.600\nAnd a science test might ask you to explain how things work.\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:52.900\nSo, to sum it up, a test is just a tool to see what you know.\n\n00:52.900 --> 00:57.700\nIt helps you and your teachers understand where you're doing well and what you might need to work on.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:00.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
