    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_025716.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.600\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you put it in a lamp and turn it on.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:29.300\nThat's a test!\nEssentially, a test helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:41.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it to test if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:53.800\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:53.800 --> 01:01.200\nIt helps us make sure things are working the way we expect.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
