    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_025847.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: Tests.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:18.600\nThink of a test as a way to check if something works like it should. \nIt's like a doctor checking your heartbeat to see if you're healthy, but we can use tests for all sorts of things.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:30.500\nFor example, you might test a toy to make sure it's safe for kids. \nOr, a programmer might test some new computer code to see if it does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:42.000\nThe goal is always the same: to find out if something is working correctly. \nAnother simple test might be to see if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:42.000 --> 00:47.800\nIf it does, the test passes! If it doesn't, there's probably something wrong.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:58.300\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to check if something is working as expected. \nIt helps us find problems and make things better.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:01.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
