    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_030028.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.100\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to check something.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:25.100\nIt could be anything, really! We use tests to see if something works like it should, or if something is true.\n\n00:25.100 --> 00:33.300\nThink about it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:41.000\nA chef tastes their food to test if it's delicious.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.700\nEven you taking a quiz at school is a test to see how much you've learned.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:56.400\nSo, tests help us understand things better. They give us information we can use to make decisions.\n\n00:56.400 --> 01:04.100\nFor example, if your bike tire is flat, you might test it by putting air in it to see if it holds.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:14.800\nThat test tells you if you have a leak! Basically, tests are just a way to get answers and learn more.\n\n01:14.800 --> 01:23.500\nThey help us check things, understand things, and make sure things are working properly.\n\n01:23.500 --> 01:27.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
