    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_030434.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_030434.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so what is a test?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.000\nIn its simplest form, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.000 --> 00:11.000\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.000\nThink about it like this.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:17.000\nYou want to know if the water is hot enough for a bath.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:20.000\nYou don't just jump in! You test it with your hand.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:23.000\nOr, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.000\nYou test it with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.000\nThese are everyday examples, but tests are also used in science, medicine, and even in school.\n\n00:30.000 --> 00:35.000\nFrom simple experiments to quizzes, they all help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:40.000\nBasically, a test is a question and a way to find the answer.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:44.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
