    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_031308.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.600\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:22.400\nIt's a process of asking a question or performing an action to see what the result will be.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:34.600\nThink about it like this: You might test if the water in your shower is hot enough by turning the knob. You're performing a small action \u2013 turning the knob \u2013 to find out the answer \u2013 is it hot?\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:42.400\nOr, maybe you take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:52.800\nThe test is the set of questions, and the answer shows what you've learned. Tests are used everywhere!\n\n00:52.800 --> 01:02.400\nFrom science experiments to cooking recipes to trying a new video game, we're constantly testing things out to learn and understand the world around us.\n\n01:02.400 --> 01:05.900\nSo, a test is a process of asking a question or performing an action to see what the result will be.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:09.300\nIt helps us learn and understand.\n\n01:09.300 --> 01:12.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
