    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_032344.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.800\nNow, you might think of tests as something you take in school, and that's true, but in a broader sense, a test is really just a way to find out if something works or if something is true.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might test it by poking it with a toothpick. If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test!\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:35.700\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb is broken. You test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:42.200\nIf it lights up, it works! So, a test is simply a procedure designed to check the quality, performance, or reliability of something.\n\n00:42.200 --> 00:51.100\nWe use them all the time, even without realizing it. In short, tests help us learn and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:54.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
