    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_032606.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.700\nNow, a test is simply a way to find out something. It's how we check if something is working, or how well we understand something.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a light bulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and turn it on. That's a test!\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:28.200\nTests can be used for all sorts of things. Your doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:37.000\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to show your teacher what you've learned. See, a test doesn't have to be scary.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.900\nIt's just a way to get information. If the light bulb doesn't turn on, you know it's broken.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:52.300\nIf you get a good grade on your quiz, you know you understand the material. So, remember, a test is a way to find things out, whether it's about a lightbulb, your health, or what you've learned in class.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:58.100\nIt helps us understand the world around us.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:04.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
