    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_032846.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.800\nToday, we're going to talk about tests. Now, a test is basically a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:28.900\nIt could be anything, like checking if a lightbulb works or seeing how well you know your multiplication tables.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:37.900\nThink of it like this: you have a question, and the test is how you find the answer.\n\n00:37.900 --> 00:46.300\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, you might take a spelling test at school to see how many words you know how to spell.\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:54.700\nAnother example is testing a recipe. You follow the instructions, and then you taste it. The taste is the result of the test \u2013 did it turn out good?\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:00.100\nSo, to recap, a test is just a method used to get information or check if something is working as it should.\n\n01:00.100 --> 01:01.000\nIt helps us understand things better!\n\n01:01.000 --> 01:01.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
