    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_032927.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:09.000\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something specific about something else.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:12.000\nThink of it like a question you're asking, and the test gives you the answer.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:14.000\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:17.000\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:20.000\nYou might poke it with a toothpick to see if it's done.\n\n00:20.000 --> 00:21.000\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.000\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:28.000\nThat's a test to see if it fixes the problem.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.000\nAnother example: a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:36.000\nA teacher gives you a quiz to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:47.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a method or procedure used to determine a specific quality or ability.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:51.000\nIt's all about asking a question and finding the answer!\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:58.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e88a4be1-8517-4982-b0f4-375c00bf0fad": {
    "id": "e88a4be1-8517-4982-b0f4-375c00bf0fad",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:10:54.450014",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T03:30:19.317151",
