    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_033019.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:14.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's like asking a question and then figuring out the answer.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:22.500\nThink about it: a math test checks how well you understand numbers.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:33.300\nA taste test tells you which flavor is better. Even a simple weather forecast is a test of what the atmosphere will do.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:39.300\nFor example, if you\u2019re baking a cake, you might use a toothpick test.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:47.600\nYou stick it in, and if it comes out clean, the cake is done. That\u2019s a test!\n\n00:47.600 --> 00:55.900\nOr if you are learning to ride a bike, you might test your balance, by lifting your feet off the ground for a few seconds.\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:01.500\nSo, to sum it up, a test helps us learn, explore, and figure things out. It's all about gathering information. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
