    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.200\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:04.500\nToday we're going to talk about something really fundamental: a test.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:07.600\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:11.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out about something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:17.100\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see how well something performs, or to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:20.400\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:23.500\nA chef tastes a dish to test if it's seasoned well.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:29.600\nOr, maybe you take a quiz at school to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:29.600 --> 00:36.400\nSo, a test can be a question, an experiment, or even just an observation.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:42.100\nThe important thing is that it helps us learn something new or confirm something we already suspected.\n\n00:42.100 --> 00:48.500\nIn short, a test is a method for evaluating or measuring something.\n\n00:48.500 --> 00:54.400\nIt\u2019s a tool for gathering data and understanding the world around us.\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:57.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
