    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_035925.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.400\nNo, not that kind of test! We're talking about tests as a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:20.900\nThink of it like this: a test is just a way to see if something passes or fails a specific requirement.\n\n00:20.900 --> 00:28.500\nFor example, let's say you bake a cake. You can \"test\" it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:38.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test and is done! Or, imagine you're building with LEGOs.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:45.300\nYou might test if your tower is stable by gently pushing it. If it falls, it fails the test!\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:56.700\nSo, in short, a test is simply a way to check if something meets a certain standard or requirement. They help us make sure things are working as expected.\n\n00:56.700 --> 01:00.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
