    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_040656.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.600\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:25.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or even just the quality of something.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:35.300\nThink of it like this: a spelling test tells us how well we know our spelling words. Or, if you're baking a cake, tasting a small bit is a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:35.300 --> 00:43.600\nTests aren\u2019t just about school. A doctor might run blood tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:46.200\nA car company might test a new car model to make sure it's safe.\n\n00:46.200 --> 00:48.800\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:48.800 --> 00:51.400\nSo, remember, a test is a way to gather information.\n\n00:51.400 --> 01:02.300\nThey help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working correctly. Tests help us learn more about the world around us.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:07.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
