    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:02.800\nToday we're diving into something super important:\n\n00:02.800 --> 00:03.500\nTests!\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:04.500\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:06.600\nSimply put, it's a way to check something.\n\n00:06.600 --> 00:09.000\nWe use tests to see if something works, or if it's good enough,\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:10.600\nor if it meets certain rules.\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:13.700\nThink of it like this: a chef tastes the soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:17.000\nOr a doctor checks your temperature to test if you have a fever.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.000\nIn software, we write tests to make sure our code does what it\u2019s supposed to do.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.400\nFor example, a test might check if a calculator app adds numbers correctly.\n\n00:25.400 --> 00:28.300\nA good test gives us confidence that things are working as expected.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:31.200\nSo remember, a test is just a check.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:33.100\nIt helps us make sure things are right.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:34.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
