    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:11:47.251277",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T04:26:08.392293",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_042608.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_042608.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.300\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\nIt\u2019s a process designed to find out information, like if something works correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:24.400\nThink about it like this: When you bake a cake, you might stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a test! You're checking if the cake is done.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:32.800\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again.\nThat's a test to see if a simple restart fixes the problem.\n\n00:32.800 --> 00:38.900\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:51.200\nDoctors use tests to check your health, and teachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:51.200 --> 00:54.700\nSo remember, a test is just a way to find out information by checking something.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "3a4f11a1-34ed-4015-9290-88ff39c86ec0": {
    "id": "3a4f11a1-34ed-4015-9290-88ff39c86ec0",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:11:47.964117",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T04:27:09.930530",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_042709.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_042709.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nHey there! Ever wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:12.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information about something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:18.200\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:27.100\nWe use tests all the time! Your doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\nA teacher gives you a quiz to see what you've learned.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:39.300\nEven tasting a new food is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing if you like it!\nSo, a test can be anything from a multiple-choice exam to a scientific experiment.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:51.700\nThe key is that it helps us learn something new or confirm what we already know.\nTests help us make better decisions, understand the world around us, and even improve ourselves.\n\n00:51.700 --> 00:59.100\nTo recap: a test is a method for collecting information.\nIt can be formal or informal, and it helps us learn and understand.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:00.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "562f161c-ee24-48e2-a3b7-366c5804a44e": {
