    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_043132.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into the basics of what a test actually is.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:16.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. It helps us see how well something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:16.700 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:26.600\nThe test? You screw it in and flip the switch!\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:31.100\nDoes it light up? That's the result of the test.\n\n00:31.100 --> 00:35.200\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You taste it!\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:39.300\nThat's a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:39.300 --> 00:44.800\nIf it does, great! If not, you know you need to adjust the recipe.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:48.900\nSo, a test is just a simple way to check things and get information.\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:51.700\nIt's all about finding answers. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
