    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_043326.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:24.900\nIt's how we gather information to see if something is true, or to check how well something works.\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:35.400\nThink of it like this: A doctor might give you a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:43.400\nOr a teacher might give you a test to see what you've learned in class.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:51.500\nEven trying a new recipe is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing to see if it tastes good!\n\n00:51.500 --> 00:56.500\nSo, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:07.000\nThey can be simple, like checking if a light bulb works. Or they can be more complex, like a big exam at school.\n\n01:07.000 --> 01:15.100\nThe important thing is that they give us information. They give us results. And those results help us make decisions.\n\n01:15.100 --> 01:26.900\nIn short, a test is a method for gathering information and checking something. It's a fundamental part of learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n01:26.900 --> 01:30.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
