    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_044227.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:15.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.700 --> 00:20.100\nThink of it like this: you're trying to figure out if a cake is done.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:26.900\nYou poke it with a toothpick, right? That toothpick is a test! The test gives you information.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:32.400\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is ready. If it's gooey, it needs more time.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:39.800\nTests aren't just for baking. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Teachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:47.500\nScientists use tests to prove or disprove ideas.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:56.200\nThey all involve performing a procedure to gather evidence, and then drawing a conclusion from that evidence.\n\n00:56.200 --> 00:59.800\nSo, a test is really just a method for gathering information to help you make a decision or understand something better.\n```"
  },
  "7f587771-e184-41ab-9041-5d71db8268df": {
    "id": "7f587771-e184-41ab-9041-5d71db8268df",
