    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:16.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:24.300\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:24.300 --> 00:32.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if an apple is ripe.\nYou might give it a squeeze \u2013 that\u2019s a test!\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:38.400\nOr, maybe you want to know if you understand a new recipe.\nYou could try baking it \u2013 that's another kind of test.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:48.900\nIn computers, a test checks if something works the way it's supposed to.\nDoes this button do what it should?\nDoes this program calculate the right answer?\n\n00:48.900 --> 00:58.000\nTests help us catch mistakes early and make sure everything is working correctly.\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\nIt helps us confirm things are working as expected and helps us learn and improve.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
