  "65e5a13b-25ea-4b39-96d7-fad5c913192a": {
    "id": "65e5a13b-25ea-4b39-96d7-fad5c913192a",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:12:07.410489",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T04:45:53.731304",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_044553.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_044553.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in the tech world, a test is simply a way to check if something is working the way it should.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: you build a toy car, and to test it, you roll it down a ramp to see if it moves.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:30.100\nThat's a test! In computers, tests check if code does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:36.300\nFor example, if you have a program that adds two numbers, a test would check if 2 + 2 actually equals 4.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:45.300\nOr, if you have a button on a website, a test could check if it takes you to the right page when you click it.\n\n00:45.300 --> 00:53.300\nSo, tests are a crucial part of building anything, ensuring everything works reliably.\n\n00:53.300 --> 00:59.400\nThey help catch mistakes early and make sure things are working correctly.\n\n00:59.400 --> 01:02.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
