    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_045614.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.700\nYou might think of tests as something you take in school, but in this case, we\u2019re talking about how we check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:23.500\nBasically, a test is a way to see if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:23.500 --> 00:29.300\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:34.600\nYou screw it in and flip the switch. If it lights up, it passes the test!\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:42.300\nIf it doesn\u2019t, it fails. Another example could be baking a cake.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:49.100\nYou follow the recipe, put it in the oven, and when it comes out, you taste it.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:55.400\nIs it delicious? Then the cake passed the taste test!\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:03.400\nIf it\u2019s burnt or tastes bad, well, it failed. So, remember, a test is simply a way to check if something works correctly, by seeing if it meets certain expectations.\n\n01:03.400 --> 01:11.400\nHopefully, now you understand what a test is all about. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
