    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_050036.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:12.400\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:25.600\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if we know something well. Think about it like this: a spelling test at school tells your teacher if you've learned your spelling words.\n\n00:25.600 --> 00:32.500\nOr, when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough. That's a test too!\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:43.300\nEven checking if your bike tires have enough air is a kind of test. So, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are just right.\n\n00:43.300 --> 00:51.800\nThey can be big or small, formal or informal, but they all have the same goal: to give us information.\n\n00:51.800 --> 01:01.300\nTo recap, a test is just a way to gather information and see if something is as it should be. It's a helpful tool in everyday life!\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:04.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
