    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_050200.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is a way to check if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:21.800\nThink of it like this: you might test a lightbulb to see if it lights up. That's a simple test!\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:28.300\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:38.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test and it's ready! Tests can also be used to see if you understand something.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:51.000\nLike a quiz in school, that's a test to see how well you've learned the material. So, a test is really just a way to find out information and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n00:51.000 --> 01:03.000\nSo, to recap, a test is a process to check something, it can be physical, like a lightbulb, or knowledge-based, like a quiz!\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
