    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about what a test is.\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how well someone knows something, or how well something works.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:21.000\nThink of it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see how much you've learned in class.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:27.500\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might taste a little bit of the batter before baking it.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:33.700\nThat's a test to see if it tastes good! Tests can be used for all sorts of things.\n\n00:33.700 --> 00:41.000\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy. Scientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:48.300\nBasically, a test helps us understand something better by giving us some kind of result or measurement.\n\n00:48.300 --> 01:01.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to check knowledge, abilities, or how well something functions. It gives us information to help us learn and make decisions.\n\n01:01.600 --> 01:05.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
