    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:12.700 --> 00:27.600\nIt's a process of asking a question, or performing an action, and then observing the result. Think about it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done baking, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:27.600 --> 00:38.700\nThe question is, \"Is the cake done?\" The toothpick is the action, and whether it comes out clean or covered in batter is the result.\n\n00:38.700 --> 00:45.800\nAnother example: your doctor might order a blood test. They want to know what's going on inside your body.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:52.900\nThe blood draw is the action, and the lab results are the answer. So, tests help us learn things.\n\n00:52.900 --> 01:00.400\nThey give us information to make decisions. They are a fundamental part of learning and understanding the world around us.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:03.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
