    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_053123.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:20.100\nIt's a process designed to give you information about a specific question.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:31.300\nThink of it like this: baking a cake.\nYou might test the cake with a toothpick to see if it's cooked all the way through.\nThe toothpick is your test, and whether it comes out clean or not tells you if the cake is ready.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:38.900\nOr imagine checking the batteries in your remote.\nYou might try them in another device to see if they still have power.\nThat's another kind of test!\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:48.400\nSo, in a nutshell, a test helps you answer a question by giving you some kind of result.\nIt's all about gathering information.\n\n00:48.400 --> 00:54.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
