    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_054511.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:17.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:28.600\nThink of it like an experiment, but often shorter and more focused.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:39.100\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it! For example, when you're baking a cake, you might stick a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:39.100 --> 00:49.100\nIf it comes out clean, that's a test to see if the cake is done.\n\n00:49.100 --> 01:00.200\nOr, if your car won't start, you might try turning on the headlights. If they're dim, that's a test telling you the battery might be low. Tests help us make decisions based on evidence. They give us information we didn't have before, helping us understand something better. So, a test is just a process for gathering information, from baking to fixing cars. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
