  "452b5ce8-4364-4395-ad1c-39f298667849": {
    "id": "452b5ce8-4364-4395-ad1c-39f298667849",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:13:05.752203",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T05:56:44.625970",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_055644.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_055644.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:20.200\nNow, you've probably taken many tests in school, but what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know or how well you can do something.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:30.800\nIt helps measure your understanding or your skills. Think of it like this: If you want to know if a cake is done, you might stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:38.600\nOr, if you want to see if you can ride your bike without training wheels, you try it. That's another kind of test!\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:50.900\nTests can be written questions, like in school, or they can be something you perform, like singing a song or building a tower. The important thing is that a test gives us information.\n\n00:50.900 --> 00:59.500\nSo, a test is a method to measure knowledge or ability. And that\u2019s it!\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:04.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
