    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_055832.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_055832.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.500\nYou've probably taken lots of them in school,\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:10.000\nbut what is a test really?\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:15.500\nAt its most basic, a test is just a way to find out information.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:21.000\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate something, whether it's your knowledge,\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:25.500\na product's quality, or even the strength of a bridge.\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:29.500\nThink of it like this: a doctor gives you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:29.500 --> 00:31.500\nThat's a test!\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:36.000\nOr, imagine a chef tasting a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:37.500\nThat\u2019s a test too!\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:44.000\nSo, in essence, a test is a structured way of gathering evidence to make a judgment or decision about something.\n\n00:44.000 --> 00:51.000\nWhether it's a quiz in class or a stress test on a new building, tests help us understand and evaluate the world around us.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:57.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
