    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_060243.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.400 --> 00:04.100\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:04.100 --> 00:06.900\nNow, in really simple terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:10.600\nIt helps us gather information and see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:10.600 --> 00:14.500\nThink about it like this: you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:15.400\nThat's one example!\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:18.900\nOr imagine a chef tasting a soup to see if it needs more salt.\n\n00:18.900 --> 00:19.800\nThey're testing the flavor!\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:24.400\nEven a scientist running an experiment is performing a test to see if their idea works.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:28.600\nSo, tests can be used for lots of different things, from checking your knowledge to figuring out if something will work the way you expect it to.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:34.300\nBasically, a test is a process for gathering data and making a decision.\n\n00:34.300 --> 00:36.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
