    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.000\nEver wondered what a test actually is?\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:14.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:17.700\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:17.700 --> 00:21.400\nYou poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:25.200\nThe toothpick comes out clean? Cake's ready!\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:33.400\nThe toothpick has batter on it? Needs more time. That's how testing works. Another example: a doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:42.300\nThey might check your temperature or blood pressure. These tests give them information about your body.\n\n00:42.300 --> 00:47.900\nSo, a test is just a way to gather information and make a decision.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:50.400\nIt helps us understand things better and figure out what to do next. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
