    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_062638.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:04.300\nOkay, so you've probably heard the word \"test\" before,\n\n00:04.300 --> 00:05.600\nbut what does it really mean?\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:10.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:14.200\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge,\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:17.100\nability, or performance.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:20.500\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done,\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:23.000\nyou stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:23.800\nThat's a test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:26.600\nThe toothpick tells you if the inside is still gooey.\n\n00:26.800 --> 00:31.200\nAnother example is a spelling test in school.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:33.800\nIt helps your teacher see how well you've learned\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:35.100\nto spell different words.\n\n00:35.400 --> 00:39.400\nOr, think about testing a new toy to see if it's fun\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:42.400\nand works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:42.700 --> 00:44.700\nTests help us understand things better.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:49.000\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:50.600\nand learn something new.\n\n00:51.100 --> 00:58.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d5858115-ec9a-4513-bf96-2afd3207b81b": {
    "id": "d5858115-ec9a-4513-bf96-2afd3207b81b",
