    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_062756.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:18.000\nNow, a test, at its core, is simply a way to check something. It's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:26.100\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are delicious, right? You give one to a friend to taste. That's a test!\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:30.600\nOr maybe you're checking if a lightbulb works. You screw it in and flip the switch. Test passed if it lights up!\n\n00:30.600 --> 00:35.900\nTests can be formal, like a quiz in school, or informal, like seeing if your shoelaces are tied.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:52.100\nThe main goal is always the same: to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:01.800\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get an answer. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
