    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nOkay, so you've probably heard the word \"test\" before,\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:04.600\nbut what does it really mean?\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:08.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific\n\n00:08.400 --> 00:09.000\nabout something else.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:12.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer,\n\n00:12.200 --> 00:14.100\nbut in a more structured way.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:17.900\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:20.400\nto find out if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.400 --> 00:24.200\nOr a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\n\n00:24.200 --> 00:27.000\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test!\n\n00:27.000 --> 00:30.100\nYou're testing your recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:34.600\nEssentially, a test helps us measure or evaluate something.\n\n00:34.600 --> 00:38.500\nIt could be your knowledge, the quality of a product,\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:41.300\nor even the strength of a material.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:43.800\nWe design tests to get reliable information.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:49.100\nSo remember, a test is just a way of learning something by asking a specific question\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:52.100\nand observing the answer.\n\n00:52.100 --> 00:54.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
