    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_063612.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're diving into something super important: the test.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:13.700\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:25.300\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards. Think of it like this: a doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:36.000\nOr, a chef tastes their soup to test if it has enough salt. In school, tests help your teacher see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:45.800\nTests can be used for all sorts of things, from checking the battery in your flashlight, to making sure a bridge is safe to drive on.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:60.000\nThe main idea is to get information and make sure things are as they should be. So, to recap: a test is a check, used to understand if something is working correctly or meets standards.\n\n00:60.000 --> 00:67.600\nIt gives us information we can use to make decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
