    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:02.800 --> 00:07.100\nA test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something is working as expected.\n\n00:07.100 --> 00:09.600\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb turns on when you flip the switch.\n\n00:09.600 --> 00:14.100\nThe main idea behind testing is to make sure things are correct and reliable.\n\n00:14.100 --> 00:17.500\nWe want to know if something does what it's supposed to do, under different circumstances.\n\n00:17.500 --> 00:22.500\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake.\nYou taste it to test if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:25.800\nOr, think about a new app on your phone.\nYou use it to test if all the buttons work.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:30.500\nTests help us catch mistakes and make improvements.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:35.800\nSo, remember, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:41.400\nIt helps us find problems and make sure things are reliable.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:44.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
