    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_064354.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests, but not the kind you take in school.\n\n00:08.400 --> 00:17.600\nIn the world of technology, a test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:27.100\nThink of it like a quality check. Basically, we want to make sure that our software, hardware, or anything else we build is doing what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:40.800\nFor example, if you build a website, you might test to see if all the buttons work. Or, if you create a new app, you might test to see if it opens properly on different phones.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:50.100\nThese tests can be simple, like clicking a button, or more complicated, like simulating hundreds of users at once.\n\n00:50.100 --> 00:57.800\nThe important thing is that they help us find problems early, so we can fix them before they cause bigger issues.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:09.000\nSo, in short, a test is just a way to confirm that everything is running smoothly and as intended. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
