    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_064702.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.600\nNow, you might think of school exams, but in this case, we mean testing something to see if it works, or what it's made of.\n\n00:15.600 --> 00:23.900\nThink of it like this: a test is a way to gather information. It's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:34.400\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:42.400\nOr, you might test the batteries in your remote to see if they still have power.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:47.300\nAnother example is baking! When you\u2019re baking, you test if a cake is done by sticking a toothpick in it.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:49.300\nIf it comes out clean, the cake is ready.\n\n00:49.300 --> 00:50.800\nYou\u2019re testing the cake!\n\n00:50.800 --> 01:00.800\nSo, to recap, a test is a method used to find out something specific about an object, person, or process.\n\n01:00.800 --> 01:05.600\nIt helps us understand how things work and make sure they're working correctly. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
