    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_065906.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:19.800\nYou've probably taken a few in school, but what is a test, really?\n\n00:19.800 --> 00:33.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\nIt's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:38.400\nThink about it like this: A recipe is a test for your cooking skills.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:45.000\nYou follow the instructions, and the result \u2013 the dish you make \u2013 shows how well you understand the recipe.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:51.600\nOr, a quiz in class? That tests what you learned from the lesson.\n\n00:51.600 --> 00:59.100\nAnother example could be checking if a light bulb works.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:06.300\nIf it lights up, the test is successful! If not, well, the bulb probably needs replacing.\n\n01:06.300 --> 01:14.700\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:14.700 --> 01:18.300\nIn short, a test is a simple way to check something!\n\n01:18.300 --> 01:21.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
