    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_070124.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:18.100\nNot the kind you stress about in school, but the kind used to check if something works correctly.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:25.300\nBasically, a test is just a way to see if something does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:30.500\nThink about it like this: if you bake a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:30.500 --> 00:35.700\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done! That's a test.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:43.500\nOr, imagine you're buying a new toy. You might test it by pressing all the buttons to make sure they work.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:57.400\nSo, a test is simply a process to verify if something functions as expected. We use tests all the time, in all sorts of ways, to make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:57.400 --> 01:01.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
