    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_070428.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\n    WEBVTT\n    \n    00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\n    Okay, let's talk about tests!\n    \n    00:02.700 --> 00:06.200\n    You've probably taken a lot of them in school,\n    \n    00:06.200 --> 00:07.800\n    but what is a test, really?\n    \n    00:07.800 --> 00:12.300\n    At its core, a test is simply a way to find out something.\n    \n    00:12.300 --> 00:16.200\n    We use tests to check if something is working,\n    \n    00:16.200 --> 00:19.100\n    if something is true, or if someone knows something.\n    \n    00:19.100 --> 00:23.900\n    Think of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works,\n    \n    00:23.900 --> 00:27.800\n    you test it by screwing it into a lamp and turning it on.\n    \n    00:27.800 --> 00:29.700\n    Does it light up?\n    \n    00:29.700 --> 00:31.300\n    That's your test result!\n    \n    00:31.300 --> 00:34.600\n    Or, if you want to know if your friend knows what two plus two is,\n    \n    00:34.600 --> 00:35.800\n    you ask them.\n    \n    00:35.800 --> 00:37.300\n    Their answer is the test.\n    \n    00:37.300 --> 00:41.400\n    Tests can be simple or complex, but they all have the same goal:\n    \n    00:41.400 --> 00:43.600\n    to get information.\n    \n    00:43.600 --> 00:48.700\n    So, in short, a test is a way to gather data and learn something new.\n    \n    00:48.700 --> 00:58.800\n    This video was created by Apilage AI.\n    ```"
