    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_070842.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:15.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.500 --> 00:19.400\nIt\u2019s a process designed to give us information.\n\n00:19.400 --> 00:23.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:23.300 --> 00:34.100\nYou use a toothpick, right? That's a test! You stick it in, and if it comes out clean, the cake passes the test.\n\n00:34.100 --> 00:44.100\nAnother example: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you\u2019re healthy. Or, in school, you take tests to show what you\u2019ve learned.\n\n00:44.100 --> 00:50.200\nThey all have a goal: to measure something and give us results. So, remember, a test is just a method for gathering information about something. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
