    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_071103.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_071103.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:13.800\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:21.200\nThink of it like checking if a light bulb works. That's a test!\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:28.200\nThe main idea is to ask a question or try something out, and then see what happens.\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:33.200\nThe result tells you something. For example, a math test tells you how well you understand math.\n\n00:33.200 --> 00:39.600\nLet's say you're baking a cake. You taste the batter before you bake it.\n\n00:39.600 --> 00:46.000\nThat's a test to see if it needs more sugar! Or maybe you try a new video game before buying it.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:52.300\nThat\u2019s testing to see if you like it. So, remember, a test is a way to learn something by asking a question or trying something out.\n\n00:52.300 --> 00:56.100\nIt helps us understand things better. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "7ac3a75f-213e-47c1-a288-a197dc4a97af": {
    "id": "7ac3a75f-213e-47c1-a288-a197dc4a97af",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:14:08.571219",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T07:11:55.471919",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_071155.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_071155.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.100\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:13.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to see how much you know or can do.\n\n00:13.700 --> 00:18.200\nThink of it like checking if a cake is ready.\n\n00:18.200 --> 00:22.700\nYou poke it with a fork, right? That's a test!\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:33.300\nTests come in all shapes and sizes. Maybe it's a quiz in school, checking your knowledge of history. Or perhaps it's a physical fitness test, seeing how many push-ups you can do.\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:43.900\nEven a doctor checking your temperature is performing a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:43.900 --> 00:53.000\nSo, tests help us measure something, whether it's knowledge, skill, or even a condition. They give us information to help us understand where we are and what we might need to work on.\n\n00:53.000 --> 00:56.600\nIn short, a test is just a way of finding something out.\n```"
  },
