    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.000\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:16.500\nNow, a test is simply a way to see how well you know something or how well something works.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb lights up when you flip the switch.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:32.500\nThe main idea is to gather information. We use tests to understand things better.\n\n00:32.500 --> 00:39.800\nFor example, a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:50.300\nOr, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:59.200\nAnother example could be checking if a new toy works as it should when you take it out of its packaging. That's a test!\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:04.000\nSo, a test is just a way of finding out something, whether it's about you, an object, or anything else.\n\n01:04.000 --> 01:12.900\nTo recap, a test helps us learn and understand. It's a simple way to check if things are working or if we know something.\n\n01:12.900 --> 01:15.000\nHope this helps!\n\n01:15.000 --> 01:18.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
