    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T07:20:12.373386",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_072012.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_072012.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:10.100\nOkay, let's talk about tests! A test is simply a way to check if something is working correctly or to see how well something performs.\n\n00:10.100 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works, so you screw it into a lamp and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:23.000\nThe lightbulb either lights up, or it doesn't.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:28.500\nAnother example could be tasting food. You taste it to test if it's delicious.\n\n00:28.500 --> 00:35.500\nIf it tastes good, the test passes! If it doesn't, well, maybe you need a little more salt.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:42.500\nTests are everywhere! From checking if your car starts in the morning, to big science experiments.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:49.800\nThey help us understand the world around us and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:57.700\nSo, in short, a test is a way of checking something. You do something, and then you see what happens.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:03.000\nThat outcome tells you whether your test passed or failed.\n\n01:03.000 --> 01:06.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
