    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_072701.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.000\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:18.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:18.800 --> 00:27.900\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:37.000\nTests can be all sorts of things. A simple test could be checking if a light switch works.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:46.700\nYou flip the switch \u2013 that's the test \u2013 and see if the light turns on. If it does, the test passes!\n\n00:46.700 --> 00:55.400\nA more complex test might be a school exam, designed to see how much you've learned about a subject.\n\n00:55.400 --> 01:04.100\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health. Or a chef might taste a sauce to see if it needs more salt.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:18.900\nSo, in summary, a test is a process used to gather information and confirm something. It helps us check if something works, if something is true, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n01:18.900 --> 01:22.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
