    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:01.500 --> 00:03.600\nToday we're diving into something super important: tests!\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:05.600\nWhat exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:09.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly,\nor to see how well someone understands something.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:13.000\nThink of it like this: your doctor gives you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:13.000 --> 00:15.400\nThere are all sorts of tests.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:18.100\nIn school, you take tests to show what you've learned.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:22.000\nIf you're baking a cake, you might taste a little bit to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:25.800\nOr, if you're building something, you might give it a little shake to test its stability.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:32.900\nSo, to recap: a test helps us understand, verify, and improve things.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:38.500\nIt's a simple process of checking to see if something meets our expectations.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:39.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
