    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_073250.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.400 --> 00:3.900\nToday we're going to talk about something really fundamental: tests.\n\n00:03.900 --> 00:06.500\nSo, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.500 --> 00:09.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information.\n\n00:09.500 --> 00:12.000\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.400\nWe use tests all the time without even realizing it!\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:20.100\nThink about it.\n\n00:20.100 --> 00:23.800\nWhen you try a new recipe and taste it to see if it's good, that's a test!\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:25.800\nYou're testing the recipe.\n\n00:25.800 --> 00:31.200\nOr if you press the power button on your TV to see if it turns on, you\u2019re testing the TV.\n\n00:31.200 --> 00:34.500\nWe can use tests in school too.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:37.400\nLike if you have a spelling test, it shows how well you learned to spell.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:46.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to gather information and see if something works, is correct, or meets a certain standard.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:49.800\nIt helps us learn and improve!\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:52.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
