    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.300\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:05.300\nToday we're going to talk about tests \u2013\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:07.200\nwhat they are, and why they're important.\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:09.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:14.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are baked enough.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:16.900\nYou can take one out and try it \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:20.500\nIn the world around us, tests help us understand all kinds of things.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:24.600\nFor example, a doctor uses tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:24.600 --> 00:28.800\nOr a teacher uses tests to see how well you've learned a subject.\n\n00:28.800 --> 00:32.900\nTests can be as simple as tasting a cookie, or as complicated as a big exam.\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:37.400\nBut the main idea is always the same: to get information and learn something new.\n\n00:37.400 --> 00:39.700\nSo, tests help us learn and grow.\n\n00:39.700 --> 00:43.700\nThey show us what we know, and what we still need to work on.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:46.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
