    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_075753.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_075753.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about someone or something.\n\n00:09.300 --> 00:17.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand more.\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:26.600\nThere are all sorts of tests! A spelling test in school helps your teacher see how well you know your words.\n\n00:26.600 --> 00:36.600\nA taste test lets you decide which cookie is the tastiest. Even a doctor uses tests, like checking your temperature, to understand your health.\n\n00:36.600 --> 00:44.600\nLet's say you want to know if a plant needs water.\n\n00:44.600 --> 00:47.500\nYou can test it by sticking your finger in the soil.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:57.200\nIf it feels dry, the plant probably needs water! See? You just performed a test! So, a test is really just a process to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:57.200 --> 01:01.400\nIt's a simple way to answer a question you have.\n\n01:01.400 --> 01:04.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "d6ea7f57-27eb-4c74-a018-fb1f2476704e": {
    "id": "d6ea7f57-27eb-4c74-a018-fb1f2476704e",
