    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_075842.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:12.800\nWhat is a test, really? Well, simply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:23.200\nIt's how we find out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:30.700\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:36.300\nA chef might taste their food to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:36.300 --> 00:41.900\nA student takes a test to see what they've learned.\n\n00:41.900 --> 00:55.700\nSee? Different tests, different purposes, but the idea is the same. We're trying to learn something by checking it in a specific way.\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:05.100\nWhether it's a written exam, a scientific experiment, or even just trying a new recipe, a test gives us information.\n\n01:05.100 --> 01:09.500\nSo, remember, a test is a method for checking something to see if it works or is true.\n\n01:09.500 --> 01:19.500\nIt helps us learn and understand. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9e8d55a7-affa-4e3e-8d6f-cd87acbc3181": {
    "id": "9e8d55a7-affa-4e3e-8d6f-cd87acbc3181",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:14:48.348720",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T07:59:24.180968",
