    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_075924.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:16.900\nIn the simplest terms, a test is just a way to find out something.\nIt's a process we use to gather information or check if something is true or correct.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:41.200\nEven checking if a lightbulb works is a kind of test!\nSo, tests can be physical things, like a written exam, or something more informal, like observing how a plant grows.\n\n00:41.200 --> 00:49.400\nThe important thing is that they help us learn and understand things better.\nThey give us answers and help us make decisions.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:59.500\nIn short, a test is a way to get information and see if something is the way we think it is.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "72a9c2b2-bad6-4df8-a730-6d21d6505cd6": {
    "id": "72a9c2b2-bad6-4df8-a730-6d21d6505cd6",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:14:49.385456",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:00:22.002715",
