    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:14:50.367478",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:01:12.182089",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_080112.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_080112.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.800\nWhat is a test, really?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:26.100\nIt's a process we use to check if something is working, if something is true, or if someone knows something.\n\n00:26.100 --> 00:36.500\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a lightbulb works, you test it by screwing it in and turning it on.\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:36.500 --> 00:47.100\nOr, if you're learning your ABCs, a quiz is a test to see how well you remember them.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:57.700\nTests can be big and important, like a final exam in school, or small and simple, like checking the batteries in your flashlight.\n\n00:57.700 --> 01:07.600\nThe main idea is that a test gives us information.\nIt helps us learn, improve, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n01:07.600 --> 01:13.300\nSo, next time you hear the word \"test,\" remember it's just a way to find out something new.\n\n01:13.300 --> 01:18.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "97d79196-c5ef-47c8-88ee-8af7ae778dae": {
    "id": "97d79196-c5ef-47c8-88ee-8af7ae778dae",
