    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_080154.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_080154.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.800 --> 00:14.500\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to see how well you know something, or how well something works.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:22.000\nThink about it like this: your teacher gives you a quiz \u2013 that's a test to see how much you learned in class.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:27.400\nOr, imagine you\u2019re baking a cake. You might taste a little of the batter.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:40.100\nThat's a mini-test to see if it needs more sugar! Tests can be used to check your knowledge, like in school, or to check the quality of something, like food or even a new toy.\n\n00:40.100 --> 00:48.300\nThey help us understand what we know and what we might need to learn more about. So, a test is just a way to check and learn!\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:53.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ca3aaee4-83d2-4425-87c3-fe81d9dd643f": {
    "id": "ca3aaee4-83d2-4425-87c3-fe81d9dd643f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:14:52.593694",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:02:41.377809",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_080241.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_080241.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:15.300\nNow, when you hear the word \"test,\" you might think of school, but really, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:25.900\nIt's how we check if something is working, true, or present. Think of it like this: a doctor uses a test to see if you have a cold.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:37.200\nOr, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt. In computers, we use tests to make sure our programs are doing what they're supposed to do.\n\n00:37.200 --> 00:49.200\nFor example, you might test if a button on a website takes you to the right page when you click it. Or, you might test if a calculator app gives you the correct answer.\n\n00:49.200 --> 01:00.600\nSo, a test is simply a process to check something and see if it behaves as expected. It's a fundamental part of learning and building things.\n\n01:00.600 --> 01:04.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "47b5c436-cec9-4386-b6e5-f6dcdb38e2d2": {
    "id": "47b5c436-cec9-4386-b6e5-f6dcdb38e2d2",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:14:53.677948",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:03:31.318958",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_080331.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_080331.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nOkay, so what is a test?\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:15.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:22.400\nIt's like asking a question, but the answer comes from an action or an observation.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:29.000\nThink of it as a mini-experiment.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:35.800\nWe use tests all the time! Maybe you're baking a cake, and you poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:35.800 --> 00:41.600\nThat's a test to see if it's done.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:47.400\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a toy needs new batteries.\n\n00:47.400 --> 00:53.200\nYou try turning it on. If it doesn\u2019t work, that\u2019s the test telling you it needs new batteries.\n\n00:53.200 --> 01:06.600\nAnother example? A spelling quiz is a test to see how well you know your words. The \"action\" is you writing the word, and the \"observation\" is whether it's spelled correctly.\n\n01:06.600 --> 01:13.000\nSo, a test is a way to discover information through action and observation.\n\n01:13.000 --> 01:16.100\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:16.100 --> 01:22.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
