    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_080717.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:01.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:01.800 --> 00:04.400\nIn simple terms, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:04.700 --> 00:09.300\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done baking.\n\n00:09.300 --> 00:11.400\nYou perform a test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:11.400 --> 00:13.600\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:13.600 --> 00:15.200\nTests are everywhere.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:17.400\nDoctors use tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:21.300\nTeachers use tests to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:25.700\nAnd scientists use tests to prove if their ideas are right or wrong.\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:27.200\nAnother example?\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:32.400\nYou might test if a toy car rolls faster on a smooth floor or a carpet.\n\n00:32.400 --> 00:35.700\nYou'd roll it on both surfaces and see which goes further.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:36.700\nThat's a test!\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:43.700\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check something.\nIt helps us understand if something works,\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:48.200\nif something is true, or if something is ready.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:51.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
