    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_081051.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey there, and welcome! Today we're tackling something super important: tests!\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:16.200\nNow, a test isn't just something you take in school. It's really just a way to check if something works, or if you know something.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you taste the batter. That's a mini-test!\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:30.200\nYou're checking if it tastes good before you bake the whole thing. Or, imagine you're trying to fix a toy.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:37.700\nYou try different things, and each time you try something, you're testing to see if it fixes the problem.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:47.100\nSo, testing is all about trying something out and seeing what happens. It helps us learn and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:47.100 --> 00:56.800\nBasically, it's a quick way to check if something does what it's supposed to do. Remember, tests aren't scary, they're helpful!\n\n00:56.800 --> 01:00.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "5227a5a4-8276-425a-b71c-264e856eb1a5": {
