    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_081143.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:04.600\nHey there, welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.600 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Well, simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:22.500\nIt's like asking a question and then seeing what the answer is. Think about it: when you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it needs more sugar.\n\n00:22.500 --> 00:30.700\nOr, if your phone isn't working, you might try turning it off and on again to test if that fixes the problem.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:35.900\nIn science, tests are called experiments.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:41.100\nAnother example? A doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:41.100 --> 00:52.000\nSee, different kinds of tests help us learn different things! So, to recap: a test is a process used to gather information and determine if something is true, correct, or working properly.\n\n00:52.000 --> 01:02.200\nIt could be as simple as tasting a cake or as complex as running a scientific experiment. Tests help us understand the world around us!\n\n01:02.200 --> 01:05.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
