    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_081247.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:18.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something is working correctly or if something is true.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:28.600\nThink of it like this: you test a cake by tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:28.600 --> 00:36.100\nIn science, tests help us prove or disprove ideas.\n\n00:36.100 --> 00:43.400\nFor example, we might test if a new plant food makes flowers grow bigger.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:50.700\nWe'd give some plants the food and others none, and then compare the size of the flowers. That's a test!\n\n00:50.700 --> 00:58.000\nTests aren't just for science, though. You take tests at school to see how well you've learned something.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:05.600\nA doctor might run tests to figure out what's making you feel sick.\n\n01:05.600 --> 01:12.500\nSo, a test is basically a way of finding out if something is accurate, effective, or true.\n\n01:12.500 --> 01:19.300\nIt helps us learn and make better decisions.\n\n01:19.300 --> 01:26.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
