    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_081509.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:09.900\nAlright, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:09.900 --> 00:21.400\nIn pretty much everything we do, we need to check if something is working correctly, right?\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:33.800\nA test is just a way to do that, but in a more structured and, well, test-like way.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:43.800\nThink of it as a way to see if something passes or fails.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:52.100\nFor example, if you're baking a cake, you might test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:52.100 --> 01:00.400\nIf it comes out clean, the cake passes the test \u2013 it's done!\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:08.700\nOr, if you're trying to remember a phone number, you might test yourself by trying to recite it.\n\n01:08.700 --> 01:13.600\nIf you get it right, you passed!\n\n01:13.600 --> 01:22.300\nSo, basically, a test is just a process to check if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n01:22.300 --> 01:29.900\nIt helps us make sure things are working as they should.\n\n01:29.900 --> 01:34.700\nAnd remember, tests aren't scary, they're just helpful tools!\n\n01:34.700 --> 01:38.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
