    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_081637.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or correct.\n\n00:16.400 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like checking if your cookies are baked.\nYou wouldn't just guess, right?\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:26.500\nYou'd use a test, like poking them with a toothpick!\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:29.200\nThe toothpick comes out clean? That's a pass!\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:32.200\nThe cookies are done. Sticky? They need more time.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:35.200\nThat's a fail.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:38.400\nAnother example? A spelling test!\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:41.600\nIt checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:41.600 --> 00:44.800\nOr even testing if a light bulb works \u2013 you screw it in and see if it lights up.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:54.100\nSo, a test is just a method for checking something, confirming if it works, or seeing if something is true.\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:54.100 --> 00:59.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
