    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:15.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:24.800\nIt's a process or procedure designed to see what you know, what you can do, or even how something works.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:34.000\nThink about it like this: a spelling test shows if you know how to spell words.\nA taste test tells you which food you like better.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:41.500\nEven a simple experiment in science class, like seeing if a plant grows better in sunlight or shade, is a type of test!\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:49.000\nTests help us understand things better.\nThey give us information that we can use to learn and improve.\n\n00:49.000 --> 00:56.500\nRemember, a test isn't about being right or wrong all the time, it's about learning something new.\n\n00:56.500 --> 01:01.200\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information,\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.800\nwhether it's about your knowledge, your preferences,\n\n01:04.800 --> 01:07.800\nor how things work in the world around you.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:11.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4a6f0637-1b8d-4c6b-a220-a841c515f737": {
    "id": "4a6f0637-1b8d-4c6b-a220-a841c515f737",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:15:08.679041",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:18:20.921987",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_081820.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_081820.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to explore something really important: tests.\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.000\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:20.600\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more organized way.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:33.100\nThink about it. When you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's sweet enough. Or, if you\u2019re learning to ride a bike, falling down is kind of a test to see if you\u2019ve got your balance yet.\n\n00:33.100 --> 00:48.000\nTests can be formal, like a quiz at school, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit. The main idea is to gather information and see if something works, or if you understand something.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:58.000\nSo, tests help us learn, improve, and make sure things are working as they should. That's the basics of what a test is!\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:01.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2f103a74-e872-4cc5-9cc3-4ce69154eb82": {
    "id": "2f103a74-e872-4cc5-9cc3-4ce69154eb82",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:15:09.407283",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:19:05.974218",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_081905.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_081905.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.200\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something specific.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:21.100\nIt's like asking a question, and then carefully looking at the answer.\n\n00:21.100 --> 00:27.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done. You can use a toothpick!\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:34.000\nSticking it in the center is a test. If it comes out clean, the cake passes the test and it's ready.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:40.200\nIf it's sticky, it needs more time.\n\n00:40.200 --> 00:50.800\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike. Your ability to stay upright without falling is being tested every second!\n\n00:50.800 --> 01:00.400\nEach wobble is a little test, and you're constantly adjusting to pass.\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:08.400\nSo, a test is really just a way to check something, to see if it meets a certain standard, or to understand something better.\n\n01:08.400 --> 01:14.300\nWe use tests every day, often without even realizing it!\n\n01:14.300 --> 01:16.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
