  "7b6b3c6a-66c6-4c5f-907b-46de1fa43e3c": {
    "id": "7b6b3c6a-66c6-4c5f-907b-46de1fa43e3c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:15:11.485445",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:21:38.289957",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_082138.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_082138.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests! What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:17.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out. Think of it like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're getting proof, or evidence.\n\n00:17.900 --> 00:23.800\nTests are used everywhere! Your doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:32.000\nA chef might taste a sauce to see if it needs more salt. Or, you might take a quiz at school to show what you've learned.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.700\nSee? Different scenarios, same idea.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:49.000\nA test is just a process, or a method, used to evaluate something. It helps us confirm or deny ideas, assess progress, or identify problems.\n\n00:49.000 --> 01:02.600\nSo, remember: a test is a way to gather information and make decisions. They come in all shapes and sizes, but the goal is always the same: to learn something new!\n\n01:02.600 --> 01:06.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "14ba639a-6103-487a-9199-129db843bc46": {
    "id": "14ba639a-6103-487a-9199-129db843bc46",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:15:12.489566",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:22:22.570613",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_082222.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_082222.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so you're hearing the word \"test\" and maybe thinking about school, right?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:08.000\nBut in computers, a test is just a way of checking if something is working the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:12.000\nIt's like asking a simple question and making sure you get the right answer.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:16.000\nThink of it this way: if you have a program that's supposed to add two numbers,\n\n00:16.000 --> 00:21.000\na test would be giving it, say, 2 and 3, and making sure it gives you 5.\n\n00:21.000 --> 00:26.000\nAnother test could be giving it 0 and 0, and checking if it results in 0.\n\n00:26.000 --> 00:32.000\nThese tests help us find mistakes, or \"bugs,\" in our code before they cause problems.\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:39.000\nSo, a test is simply a way to verify that a small part of your program is behaving as expected.\n\n00:39.000 --> 00:45.000\nIt's a crucial part of making sure your software is reliable.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:48.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
