    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_083106.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:08.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:08.200 --> 00:14.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:24.100\nThink of it like an experiment, but often shorter and more focused.\n\n00:24.100 --> 00:35.100\nWe use tests all the time to see if something works, if something is true, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:35.100 --> 00:46.600\nFor example, your doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\nOr, a chef might taste their soup to see if it needs more salt.\nEven a kid trying a new toy to see if it's fun is performing a test!\n\n00:46.600 --> 00:54.800\nThe goal is always the same: to gather information and learn something new.\nSo, remember, a test is just a simple way to learn something by observing or measuring.\n\n00:54.800 --> 00:58.300\nIt helps us make decisions and understand the world around us.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
