    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_083352.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:17.600\nYou've probably taken them in school, but what is a test, really?\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:26.400\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:35.700\nIt could be your knowledge, your skills, or even your personality.\n\n00:35.700 --> 00:43.600\nThink of it like this: a doctor uses a thermometer to test your temperature.\n\n00:43.600 --> 00:54.800\nIt tells them if you have a fever or not. Or, imagine testing a cake with a toothpick \u2013 if it comes out clean, the cake is done!\n\n00:54.800 --> 01:01.500\nTests aren't just for school. Companies test new products to make sure they work right.\n\n01:01.500 --> 01:08.200\nScientists test their ideas to see if they're true.\n\n01:08.200 --> 01:15.300\nSo, a test is just a tool to help us learn and understand things better.\n\n01:15.300 --> 01:22.300\nIt helps us see if something is working, or if we need to make some changes.\n\n01:22.300 --> 01:25.700\nSo, remember, a test is a measurement.\n\n01:25.700 --> 01:28.600\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:28.600 --> 01:32.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
