    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:06.000\nA test, in its simplest form, is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:06.000 --> 00:10.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are done baking.\n\n00:10.400 --> 00:12.500\nYou use a toothpick \u2013 that's a test!\n\n00:12.500 --> 00:17.000\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something is working correctly, or if it meets certain standards.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:21.400\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:26.400\nAnother example? Imagine you're buying a used car.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:30.200\nYou'd probably want a mechanic to give it a test, right?\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:34.700\nTo check the engine, brakes, and everything else.\n\n00:34.700 --> 00:36.800\nThat test would tell you if the car is in good shape.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:42.400\nSo, tests are all about checking things, giving us information, and helping us make decisions.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:46.000\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but the idea is always the same: to evaluate something.\n\n00:46.000 --> 00:49.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
