    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:07.600\nAt its most basic, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.600 --> 00:15.000\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:19.000\nThink of it like asking a question, but sometimes the question is asked with tools or experiments.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:25.000\nThe main idea is to see how something behaves under certain conditions.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:29.000\nFor instance, a simple test could be dropping a ball to see if it bounces.\n\n00:29.000 --> 00:32.000\nThat's a test of its bounciness!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:35.000\nOr, imagine baking a cake and tasting it.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:37.000\nThat's a test to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:41.500\nHere's another example. A doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:47.000\nOr a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand the material.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:55.000\nSo, remember, a test is simply a way to gather information and learn something new about the world around us.\n\n00:55.000 --> 00:58.500\nTests help us understand how things work.\n\n00:58.500 --> 01:02.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
