    "id": "e444e740-f804-44fd-a49c-ae3b876c7b6c",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:15:36.319936",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:56:10.928526",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_085610.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_085610.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.700\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.700 --> 00:07.700\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:07.700 --> 00:13.200\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see how well someone or something performs.\n\n00:13.200 --> 00:18.000\nThink of it like this: you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you've learned your vocabulary.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:22.400\nOr a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:27.400\nTests can be formal, like exams, or informal, like checking if your shoes fit.\n\n00:27.400 --> 00:34.500\nThe key thing is that they give us data, a measurable result that helps us understand something better.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:41.300\nSo, a test is really just a tool for learning and assessment.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:48.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "2c2bab0c-d731-4693-b99e-0054486e5893": {
    "id": "2c2bab0c-d731-4693-b99e-0054486e5893",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:15:36.886538",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T08:57:05.013425",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_085704.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_085704.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.200\nNow, you might be thinking of school tests, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check if something works as expected.\n\n00:15.200 --> 00:22.900\nThink of it like this: you build a Lego tower, and you test it by gently pushing it to see if it's stable.\n\n00:22.900 --> 00:30.200\nThat's a test! Or, if you write a recipe, you test it by cooking it to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:30.200 --> 00:47.300\nTests help us find mistakes and make sure things are working correctly before we rely on them. Whether it's a toy, a recipe, or even a complicated machine, testing is a crucial step to making sure everything is safe and reliable.\n\n00:47.300 --> 00:57.600\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to check if something does what it\u2019s supposed to do. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "e5454f2b-04f2-4ba6-a89a-8a57384c917e": {
    "id": "e5454f2b-04f2-4ba6-a89a-8a57384c917e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
