    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_085923.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.100\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re talking about tests.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:16.300\nNow, that word might sound scary, but in this case, a test is simply a way to check something.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works. You turn it on, and that's the test!\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:36.000\nThe whole point is to see if something is working correctly, or to find out more information about it.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:45.500\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:54.700\nOr, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:54.700 --> 01:03.900\nSo, a test can be anything from a simple on/off check, to a more complicated investigation.\n\n01:03.900 --> 01:13.100\nThe important thing is that it gives us information.\n\n01:13.100 --> 01:17.000\nWe use tests all the time, without even realizing it!\n\n01:17.000 --> 01:22.300\nThey help us understand things better and make informed decisions.\n\n01:22.300 --> 01:29.000\nTo recap, a test is just a way to check something, to see if it works or to learn more about it.\n\n01:29.000 --> 01:32.300\nIt's a fundamental part of how we learn and improve.\n\n01:32.300 --> 01:35.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
