    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_090912.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:19.200\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:31.300\nIt could be a topic you've studied, a skill you've practiced, or even just a general understanding of the world.\n\n00:31.300 --> 00:40.900\nThink of it like this: if you bake a cake, you might taste it to test if it's good.\nOr if you're learning to ride a bike, you'll test your balance to see if you can stay upright.\n\n00:40.900 --> 00:49.800\nSimilarly, in school or in life, we use tests to measure progress and identify areas where we might need more practice.\n\n00:49.800 --> 00:58.200\nSo, tests help us learn and improve!\nIn short, tests are just tools that help us see how much we've learned.\nThey provide valuable feedback that can guide us on our learning journey.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
