    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_092024.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.400\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:03.400 --> 00:07.800\nYou've probably taken a test at school, but in general, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:07.800 --> 00:15.400\nIt's a process that helps us learn more about a person, object, or even an idea.\n\n00:15.400 --> 00:19.700\nThink of it like this: a doctor might give you a test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:19.700 --> 00:23.800\nOr, a chef might taste a sauce to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:24.900\nSee?\n\n00:24.900 --> 00:27.800\nIt's about gathering information.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:34.000\nFor example, a simple test could be checking if a light bulb works.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:39.800\nYou screw it in, flip the switch, and if it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:39.800 --> 00:45.000\nOr, you could give a plant water and see if it grows; that\u2019s a test of whether the plant is getting what it needs.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:52.400\nSo, to recap, a test is a procedure designed to gather information and answer a question.\n\n00:52.400 --> 00:57.000\nIt helps us learn and make better decisions.\n\n00:57.000 --> 01:00.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
