    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.200 --> 00:22.800\nThink of it like an experiment or a structured question.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:29.400\nWe use tests all the time, even without realizing it!\n\n00:29.400 --> 00:36.000\nImagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:36.000 --> 00:42.600\nYou taste the batter \u2013 that's a test to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:49.200\nOr, think about checking if a lightbulb works before you screw it in.\n\n00:49.200 --> 00:55.900\nThat's a test too!\n\n00:55.900 --> 01:10.700\nTests aren't just for school or doctors' offices. They help us understand things, make decisions, and solve problems every single day.\n\n01:10.700 --> 01:17.300\nThey can be simple like checking the weather, or more complex like a scientific study.\n\n01:17.300 --> 01:25.600\nEssentially, if you're trying to confirm something or learn something new, you're probably using some kind of test.\n\n01:25.600 --> 01:32.400\nSo, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and answer a question.\n\n01:32.400 --> 01:37.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
