    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.000\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:06.200\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:7.500\nIt could be about you, an object, or even an idea.\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:10.800\nThink of it like asking a question and then looking for the answer in a structured way.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:12.400\nTests help us measure things.\n\n00:12.400 --> 00:15.800\nFor example, a math test measures how well you understand math.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:19.000\nA stress test on a bridge measures how much weight it can hold.\n\n00:19.000 --> 00:22.700\nImagine you want to know if a cookie is delicious.\n\n00:22.700 --> 00:25.300\nYou test it by taking a bite!\n\n00:25.300 --> 00:29.100\nYou gather data \u2013 the taste, the texture \u2013 and then you make a judgment:\n\n00:29.100 --> 00:30.900\ndelicious or not delicious.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:37.100\nSo, tests are all about gathering information, measuring something, and then drawing a conclusion.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:41.700\nThey help us learn, improve, and make better decisions.\n\n00:41.700 --> 00:43.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
