    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:12.600\nAt its most basic, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:12.600 --> 00:21.300\nThink of it as a question, or a series of questions, designed to give you information.\n\n00:21.300 --> 00:29.200\nIt could be a written exam in school, where you\u2019re being tested on what you've learned.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:37.100\nOr, it could be something much simpler, like testing the temperature of bathwater to see if it's too hot or too cold.\n\n00:37.100 --> 00:41.500\nYou're gathering data to make a decision.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:45.900\nFor example, a doctor might order a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:54.100\nA chef might taste a sauce to see if it needs more salt. See? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:54.100 --> 01:02.300\nSo, in short, a test is a process to gather information and learn something.\n\n01:02.300 --> 01:05.900\nIt helps us understand things better.\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:06.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
