    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_093516.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're talking about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.200\nNow, a test is really just a way to check something. Think of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:14.200 --> 00:18.100\nYou use a toothpick, right? That's a test!\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:29.300\nIn school, tests help teachers see how well you understand the material. They can be quizzes, exams, or even just a quick question.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:39.400\nA test isn't about tricking you, it's about showing what you've learned. For example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words.\n\n00:39.400 --> 00:43.800\nA math test checks if you can solve problems.\n\n00:43.800 --> 00:48.200\nSimple, right?\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:59.300\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to check understanding. It can be about anything, from baking a cake to learning new things in school. It helps us all see where we're at.\n\n00:59.300 --> 01:05.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
