  "e28ad742-55df-4fa2-a3af-d210e6b24817": {
    "id": "e28ad742-55df-4fa2-a3af-d210e6b24817",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:16:18.501924",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T09:43:28.828938",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_094328.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_094328.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, a test, in its simplest form, is just a way to see if something works as it should.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like checking if your shoes fit. You try them on \u2013 that\u2019s the test \u2013 and see if they're comfortable.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:35.000\nIn science and technology, tests are super important. They help us make sure things like new medicines or computer programs actually do what they\u2019re supposed to do, and that they're safe to use.\n\n00:35.000 --> 00:46.100\nFor example, before a new phone comes out, engineers test it to make sure the battery lasts long enough and that the screen doesn't break easily.\n\n00:46.100 --> 00:53.900\nOr, a chef might test a new recipe by making it and having people try it to see if they like the taste.\n\n00:53.900 --> 01:04.500\nSo, a test is simply a way to check if something works, whether it's trying on shoes, checking a phone, or tasting a new dish.\n\n01:04.500 --> 01:10.800\nThey help us learn and improve things! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9e63d181-9fbf-4949-9ed2-f314c534c1c7": {
    "id": "9e63d181-9fbf-4949-9ed2-f314c534c1c7",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:16:19.092551",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T09:44:24.158592",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_094424.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_094424.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:19.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to measure something.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:30.800\nThink of it like using a ruler to see how long your pencil is, but instead of length, we can measure things like knowledge, skills, or even how well something works.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:40.300\nThe main idea is to get a number or a result that tells us about whatever we're testing.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:47.900\nFor example, a spelling test measures how well you know how to spell words. A software test checks if a computer program does what it's supposed to do.\n\n00:47.900 --> 00:57.600\nSo, tests help us understand things better. They give us information to make decisions. They let us see where we're doing well and where we might need to improve. Basically, a test is just a structured way of learning something about something else. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
