    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_094924.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.143 --> 00:05.403\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.403 --> 00:11.023\nNo need to feel stressed, we're just going to cover the basics.\n\n00:11.023 --> 00:19.023\nA test, in its simplest form, is a way to check or evaluate something.\n\n00:19.023 --> 00:27.023\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:27.023 --> 00:35.223\nMore formally, a test helps us understand if something works as it should, or if it meets certain requirements.\n\n00:35.223 --> 00:44.823\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\nOr a strength test can measure how much weight you can lift.\n\n00:44.823 --> 00:47.423\nSee?\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:47.423 --> 00:50.023\nSo, to recap:\n\n00:50.023 --> 00:57.023\na test is simply a method for checking something.\nIt helps us understand its quality or ability.\n\n00:57.023 --> 01:04.303\nAnd, just like that toothpick in the cake, it gives us valuable information.\n\n01:04.303 --> 01:04.903\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
