    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_095104.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:11.200\nWhat is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.200 --> 00:23.100\nIt helps us learn if something is true, or how well something works. Think about it like this: You might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:33.600\nOr, a baker might test a new cookie recipe to see if it tastes good. Even a doctor uses tests to figure out what's going on with your body!\n\n00:33.600 --> 00:40.800\nTests aren't just for school or baking. Scientists use tests to see if their ideas are correct.\n\n00:40.800 --> 00:48.600\nEngineers test bridges to make sure they're safe. All sorts of people use tests to learn and improve things.\n\n00:48.600 --> 01:01.200\nSo, remember: a test is a way of gathering information and checking how things work. They help us learn, improve, and make sure things are safe and reliable.\n\n01:01.200 --> 01:04.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
