    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_095249.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.300\nHi everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:11.900\nWhat exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:11.900 --> 00:18.100\nThink of it like asking a question and then getting an answer.\n\n00:18.100 --> 00:32.200\nWe use tests all the time! For example, when you bake a cake, you might use a toothpick to test if it's done. You poke the cake, and if the toothpick comes out clean, that's your answer: the cake is ready!\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:40.500\nOr, if you're learning a new language, a quiz is a test to see how well you understand the words and grammar.\n\n00:40.500 --> 00:50.700\nThe quiz asks you questions, and your answers show what you've learned. So, a test is really just a method for gathering information.\n\n00:50.700 --> 01:00.400\nIt helps us check if something works, or if we understand something. Remember, tests are a tool for learning and discovery!\n\n01:00.400 --> 01:04.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
