    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_095834.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:10.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests! You've probably taken a bunch in school, but in general, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:10.500 --> 00:18.700\nIt's a method we use to see if something works, if something is true, or if something meets a certain standard.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:28.400\nThink about it like this: a chef tastes the soup to test if it needs more salt. Or, a doctor might run a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:32.600\nThese are both tests! They help us gather information.\n\n00:32.600 --> 00:36.800\nAnother example? Imagine you're building a birdhouse.\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:48.700\nYou might test it by putting it outside to see if it can withstand the wind and rain. So, to recap, a test is simply a procedure to evaluate something.\n\n00:48.700 --> 00:59.500\nIt can be a physical exam, a questionnaire, or even just observing how something behaves. Tests help us understand and improve things.\n\n00:59.500 --> 01:03.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
