    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_100859.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about something fundamental: a test.\n\n00:06.900 --> 00:15.300\nNow, what exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:24.400\nThink of it like asking a question, but in a more structured way.\nThe main idea behind a test is to gather information.\n\n00:24.400 --> 00:32.900\nIt could be to see if something works, to check its quality, or even to understand how well you understand a topic!\n\n00:32.900 --> 00:42.900\nFor example, a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to test your knowledge of a subject.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:45.500\nSee? Tests are everywhere!\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:56.600\nThey help us make decisions and learn more.\nSo, to recap, a test is a structured way to gather information and find out something specific.\n\n00:56.600 --> 01:05.800\nThey come in all shapes and sizes, but they all share that core purpose.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "9fd8856b-c048-4d05-be23-3549c51355f4": {
    "id": "9fd8856b-c048-4d05-be23-3549c51355f4",
