    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_101009.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.800\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're tackling a really fundamental concept: the test.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:21.200\nIt's a method to gather information.\n\n00:21.200 --> 00:26.400\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:26.400 --> 00:30.100\nYou screw it in and flip the switch \u2013 that's your test!\n\n00:30.100 --> 00:33.800\nThe goal of a test is to answer a question.\n\n00:33.800 --> 00:42.400\nDoes the bulb light up? Is the cake done baking? Can you ride a bike? These are all questions we can answer with a test.\n\n00:42.400 --> 00:47.500\nFor example, a spelling test checks if you know how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:47.500 --> 00:57.000\nA taste test helps you decide which flavor of ice cream you like best. See? Tests are everywhere! So, remember, a test is just a way to learn something by asking a question and finding the answer.\n\n00:57.000 --> 00:59.300\nIt's a simple but powerful tool. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
