    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_101503.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:16.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:27.100\nIt's a process, or a set of questions, designed to measure your knowledge, skill, or even your opinion about something.\n\n00:27.100 --> 00:38.900\nThink about it like this: you take a spelling test to see how well you know your spelling words. Or a doctor might run a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:50.300\nEven trying out a new recipe is a kind of test to see if you like it! So, tests help us learn, improve, and make informed decisions.\n\n00:50.300 --> 00:59.100\nThey can be formal, like school exams, or informal, like trying that new recipe. The key is that they're all about gathering information.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:00.600\nIn short, a test is a tool that helps us learn something new or confirm what we already know.\n```"
