    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_102531.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:22.000\nIt helps us understand if something is working correctly, or to see how much someone knows about a topic.\n\n00:22.000 --> 00:26.900\nThink of it like this: a simple battery test.\n\n00:26.900 --> 00:36.400\nWe use a tester to see if the battery still has enough power. That's a test!\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:43.400\nOr, imagine your teacher giving you a quiz. That quiz is a test to see how well you understand what you've been learning in class.\n\n00:43.400 --> 00:59.100\nTests aren't just for batteries or school, though. Doctors use tests to check your health. Scientists use tests to see if their experiments work. Basically, a test is a way to gather information and make a decision based on that information.\n\n00:59.100 --> 01:02.800\nSo, tests are all around us, helping us learn, diagnose, and understand the world better.\n```"
  },
