  "d694962d-4056-4e9f-88b2-c202ca39478f": {
    "id": "d694962d-4056-4e9f-88b2-c202ca39478f",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:16:58.154950",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T10:34:48.483680",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_103448.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_103448.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.700 --> 00:21.600\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true, or how well something works.\n\n00:21.600 --> 00:23.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:29.300\nYou test it by plugging it in! Does it light up? Great! That's a successful test.\n\n00:29.300 --> 00:35.900\nOr maybe you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:48.000\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in the middle. If it comes out clean, your cake is ready! Tests are everywhere, from simple everyday things to complex scientific experiments.\n\n00:48.000 --> 00:57.300\nThey help us understand the world around us and make sure things are working properly. So, a test is just a method to gather information and learn something new. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
