    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_104050.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, let's talk about tests!\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:17.600\nIn the simplest terms, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:17.600 --> 00:23.200\nWe use tests every day, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:23.200 --> 00:29.200\nBasically, a test involves doing something and then observing the result.\n\n00:29.200 --> 00:35.200\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:41.000\nThe recipe is your test plan. You follow the instructions, and the result is the cake!\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:46.500\nHere's another example. Let's say you want to know if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:52.000\nThe test is easy: you screw it into a lamp. If it lights up, the test passes!\n\n00:52.000 --> 01:02.800\nIf it doesn't, the test fails. So, to recap, a test is just a structured way to check if something works as expected.\n\n01:02.800 --> 01:09.000\nIt involves a specific action and observing the outcome.\n\n01:09.000 --> 01:14.000\nIt helps us confirm things and make sure everything is working correctly.\n\n01:14.000 --> 01:16.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
