    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_104814.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean school exams. A test is really just a way to check if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:24.000\nIt's a simple way to get information. Think about it: You might test if a lightbulb works by screwing it in.\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:30.700\nYou're checking if it lights up. Or, a chef might taste a soup to test if it has enough salt.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:35.500\nThey're checking the flavor. Tests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:45.900\nSometimes they're formal, like a quiz. Other times, they're informal, like wiggling a loose tooth to see if it's ready to come out.\n\n00:45.900 --> 00:57.800\nThe key is that you're trying to learn something or see if something's working correctly. So, remember, a test is just a way to check something and get information.\n\n00:57.800 --> 01:01.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
