    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:14.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:14.900 --> 00:23.900\nIt could be finding out what you know, like a school test, or finding out if something works correctly.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:35.600\nThink of it like a question that needs an answer, but instead of just asking, we use a specific process to get that answer.\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:51.300\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy. Or, a software developer might run a test on their code to make sure it doesn't have any errors.\n\n00:51.300 --> 00:59.300\nThe results of a test help us make decisions, fix problems, or just understand things better. So, to recap, a test is a procedure used to gather information and answer a specific question. It helps us learn, improve, and make informed choices. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
