    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_110202.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:14.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:14.600 --> 00:23.100\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see how something performs, or what something is like.\n\n00:23.100 --> 00:31.500\nThink about it this way: a taste test tells you how something tastes.\n\n00:31.500 --> 00:38.900\nA spelling test shows you how well you can spell.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:46.300\nA math test shows how well you know math!\n\n00:46.300 --> 00:58.000\nAnother example: Imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works. You screw it into a lamp, and that's your test! If the light comes on, the bulb passes the test. If it doesn't, well, it failed.\n\n00:58.000 --> 01:08.000\nSo, a test is just a way of checking something, evaluating it, or finding out more about it.\n\n01:08.000 --> 01:16.500\nIt can be as simple as tasting food, or as complicated as a big exam.\n\n01:16.500 --> 01:20.600\nThe important thing is, it helps us learn!\n\n01:20.600 --> 01:24.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
