    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:17:25.755780",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T11:11:52.973560",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_111152.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_111152.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, when you hear the word \u201ctest,\u201d you might think of school, but tests are really just a way to check if something works the way it's supposed to.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:25.700\nBasically, a test is a procedure designed to evaluate something.\nIt could be a product, an idea, or even a skill!\n\n00:25.700 --> 00:36.200\nFor example, a taste test checks if a new flavor of ice cream is yummy.\nOr, a software test makes sure a new app doesn't crash.\n\n00:36.200 --> 00:49.100\nEven your doctor uses tests, like checking your temperature to see if you have a fever.\nSo, remember, a test is a way to see if something is doing what it's meant to do.\n\n00:49.100 --> 00:57.200\nThey help us improve things and make sure everything is working correctly.\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "f5886ad7-2f33-4fc5-af83-927218abe448": {
    "id": "f5886ad7-2f33-4fc5-af83-927218abe448",
