    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_111242.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.200\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.200 --> 00:16.500\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific. \nIt's like asking a question, but in a more formal and structured way.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:23.900\nThink about it: a quiz in school is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:23.900 --> 00:38.000\nA taste test checks if you like a food. Even a doctor checking your temperature is a type of test to see if you have a fever.\n\n00:38.000 --> 00:45.500\nSo, a test involves doing something, observing the result, and then using that result to learn something.\n\n00:45.500 --> 00:53.500\nIt could be as simple as checking if a light bulb works before you screw it in. You're \"testing\" it! Essentially, tests help us make informed decisions and understand the world around us.\n\n00:53.500 --> 00:55.100\nThey're everywhere!\n\n00:55.100 --> 00:57.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "220284ee-e5ae-446e-9a93-ae59df13a566": {
