    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_111423.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:02.200\nOkay, so what is a test?\n\n00:02.200 --> 00:05.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:05.300 --> 00:07.300\nThink of it like an experiment,\n\n00:07.300 --> 00:08.000\nbut maybe a little less formal.\n\n00:08.000 --> 00:09.700\nWe use tests all the time!\n\n00:09.700 --> 00:13.800\nImagine you're baking a cake. You taste the batter \u2013 that's a test to see if it tastes good\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:15.100\nbefore it goes in the oven.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:19.200\nOr, if your phone isn't turning on, you might try plugging it into a different charger.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:22.100\nThat's testing to see if the charger is the problem.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:28.300\nTests can be used to check anything, from a recipe to an idea to a piece of equipment.\n\n00:28.300 --> 00:30.700\nThe main idea is to try something out\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:32.200\nand see what happens.\n\n00:32.200 --> 00:34.200\nDoes the cake taste good?\n\n00:34.200 --> 00:35.600\nDoes the phone charge?\n\n00:35.600 --> 00:40.000\nSo, a test is just a way to learn something by trying something out.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:45.000\nIt helps us understand if something works, or if it needs some tweaking.\n\n00:45.000 --> 00:47.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
