    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.900 --> 00:05.000\nToday we're diving into something called a \"test.\"\n\n00:05.000 --> 00:07.900\nNow, in everyday language, a test is simply a way to check or find something out.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:09.800\nThink of it like a quick investigation.\n\n00:09.800 --> 00:14.300\nBasically, a test helps us understand if something is working properly, or if a statement is true or false.\n\n00:14.300 --> 00:18.600\nIt could be anything from a taste test to see if a new recipe is delicious, to a medical test to check your health.\n\n00:18.600 --> 00:24.800\nFor example, when you take a spelling test at school, it's testing your knowledge of how to spell words correctly.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:28.400\nOr, if you try a new brand of juice, you're doing a taste test to see if you like it.\n\n00:28.400 --> 00:36.400\nSo, a test is just a process designed to gather information and see if something meets a certain standard or expectation.\n\n00:36.400 --> 00:38.200\nPretty simple, right?\n\n00:38.200 --> 00:40.600\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
