    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_112159.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.000\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.000 --> 00:05.900\nIn simple terms, a test is just a way to find something out.\n\n00:05.900 --> 00:09.000\nThink of it like an experiment, or even just asking a question.\n\n00:09.000 --> 00:14.000\nWe use tests all the time, often without even realizing it!\n\n00:14.000 --> 00:18.000\nFor example, when you\u2019re baking a cake, you might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:18.000 --> 00:21.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that\u2019s a test!\n\n00:21.500 --> 00:23.000\nIt tells you the cake is done.\n\n00:23.000 --> 00:27.500\nOr, if you try to open a door, and it's locked, that's a test that tells you you need a key.\n\n00:27.500 --> 00:33.500\nBasically, a test helps us confirm if something is true, or if something is working like it should.\n\n00:33.500 --> 00:35.500\nIt gives us information.\n\n00:35.500 --> 00:41.500\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:41.500 --> 00:44.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
