    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.200 --> 00:03.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:03.500 --> 00:08.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something,\n\n00:08.100 --> 00:10.500\nor how well you can do something.\n\n00:10.800 --> 00:13.900\nThink of it like checking if a lightbulb works.\n\n00:13.900 --> 00:16.700\nYou're testing the lightbulb to see if it lights up!\n\n00:17.100 --> 00:19.600\nTests come in all shapes and sizes.\n\n00:19.600 --> 00:23.500\nYou might have a written test at school, with questions you need to answer.\n\n00:23.800 --> 00:26.900\nOr, it could be a practical test, like seeing if you can ride a bike without falling.\n\n00:27.200 --> 00:30.500\nFor example, a spelling test shows how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:30.700 --> 00:33.700\nA taste test checks if you can tell the difference between different flavors.\n\n00:34.000 --> 00:36.700\nAnd a reading test shows how well you understand what you're reading.\n\n00:37.000 --> 00:42.400\nSo, in a nutshell, a test is just a way to measure knowledge or ability.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:46.600\nIt helps us see what we've learned and what we still need to work on.\n\n00:47.000 --> 00:49.700\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
