    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_112656.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nEver wondered what a test really is?\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:13.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to gather information about something.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:23.400\nThink of it like checking if a cake is done baking. You might stick a toothpick in it. That toothpick is your test!\n\n00:23.400 --> 00:34.400\nIn general, tests help us understand what someone knows, or how well something works. For example, a spelling test checks how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:34.400 --> 00:45.700\nOr, a stress test on a bridge checks if it's strong enough to hold traffic.\n\n00:45.700 --> 00:53.700\nSo, whether it's a quiz in school, or checking the strength of a new material, tests are all about collecting information and making informed decisions. Testing is a key part of learning and building a better world. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
