  "917ec972-d2b5-46c9-bed7-c8fad8e8bf4e": {
    "id": "917ec972-d2b5-46c9-bed7-c8fad8e8bf4e",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:17:39.996887",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T11:28:22.281522",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_112822.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_112822.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we\u2019re diving into something super important: what is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:19.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something specific about something else. Think of it like asking a question and getting an answer, but in a more organized way.\n\n00:19.300 --> 00:26.500\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done, you can stick a toothpick in it. That's a test!\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:33.300\nOr, if you want to know if you understand a lesson, you might take a quiz. That\u2019s a test too!\n\n00:33.300 --> 00:41.300\nTests can be used to check all sorts of things, from the quality of food to how well you know your ABCs.\n\n00:41.300 --> 00:54.200\nThe key is that a test gives you information you didn\u2019t have before. So, to recap, a test is a process or procedure designed to gather information or evaluate something.\n\n00:54.200 --> 01:01.200\nIt helps us learn and make better decisions. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
