    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:01.900\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:01.900 --> 00:05.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something.\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:6.800\nIt helps us understand if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:06.800 --> 00:12.800\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cookies are baked enough.\nYou can test them by poking them with a toothpick.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:15.900\nIf it comes out clean, they're ready!\n\n00:15.900 --> 00:20.600\nAnother example is checking if your plant needs water.\nYou can test the soil by sticking your finger in it.\n\n00:20.600 --> 00:23.700\nIf it feels dry, it's time to water.\n\n00:23.700 --> 00:29.800\nTests are everywhere, from checking your spelling with a spell checker, to seeing if your new toy car can make it down a ramp.\n\n00:29.800 --> 00:36.900\nSo, a test is just a simple way to get information and see if something passes a certain requirement.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:44.300\nWhether it's cookies, plants, or toy cars, tests help us learn and improve things.\n\n00:44.300 --> 00:47.200\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
