    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_114611.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.200\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.200 --> 00:13.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:13.300 --> 00:17.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your cake is done.\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:19.100\nYou poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:19.100 --> 00:21.400\nThat's a test!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:32.300\nThe toothpick comes out clean? Pass! It's done. In science, tests are really important for proving ideas.\n\n00:32.300 --> 00:41.800\nFor example, you might test if a new plant food helps tomatoes grow bigger. You'd give some plants the food, and others nothing, then compare the results.\n\n00:41.800 --> 00:47.200\nTests aren't just for baking or science though.\n\n00:47.200 --> 00:59.900\nA spelling test checks your knowledge of words. A medical test checks your health. They all help us understand something better. So, a test is basically a way to gather information and see if something is true, correct, or working the way it should.\n\n00:59.900 --> 01:03.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
