    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_115525.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\nToday we\u2019re going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:15.800\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean something you take in school.\nA test is really just a way of finding out information about something.\n\n00:15.800 --> 00:24.800\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\nThe test itself is the question, and the result you get is the answer.\n\n00:24.800 --> 00:32.000\nFor example, if you want to know if a cake is done, you can stick a toothpick in it.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:32.000 --> 00:41.000\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is probably ready.\nAnother example is checking if a lightbulb works.\nYou screw it in and flip the switch.\n\n00:41.000 --> 00:46.900\nIf it lights up, the test is successful!\nSo, remember, a test is simply a procedure to determine something.\n\n00:46.900 --> 00:58.100\nIt could be checking a cake, a lightbulb, or even your knowledge.\nTests help us learn and understand the world around us.\n\n00:58.100 --> 01:05.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
