    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_115824.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.300\nHello everyone, and welcome! Today, we're going to explore what a test is.\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:16.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:16.600 --> 00:26.500\nThink of it as asking a question and then finding the answer through a process.\n\n00:26.500 --> 00:36.900\nIt could be a written exam at school, checking if you understand a subject. Or maybe you're testing a new recipe to see if it tastes good.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:48.200\nEven checking if a light bulb works before you install it \u2013 that's a test! For example, a doctor might give you a blood test to check your health.\n\n00:48.200 --> 00:59.700\nA teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you learned a lesson. We use tests all the time to learn, improve, and make sure things are working properly.\n\n00:59.700 --> 01:04.600\nSo, to recap, a test is a process designed to gather information."
  },
