    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T12:00:27.761269",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_120026.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_120026.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:03.600\nOkay, so you've heard the word \"test\" thrown around, but what does it really mean?\n\n00:03.600 --> 00:11.600\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a procedure designed to evaluate knowledge, ability, or performance.\n\n00:11.600 --> 00:16.500\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done, so you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:17.300\nThat's a test!\n\n00:17.300 --> 00:22.800\nAnother example is a spelling test at school. It helps your teacher see how well you know your spelling words.\n\n00:22.800 --> 00:29.700\nOr, imagine you're trying out a new recipe. Tasting it is a test to see if you need to add more salt or sugar.\n\n00:29.700 --> 00:43.100\nSo, a test is a simple way to check something out, whether it's knowing your ABCs, baking a cake, or anything in between. It helps us understand and measure things.\n\n00:43.100 --> 00:58.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
