    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_120256.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.900\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:13.400\nToday, we're going to explore something super important: a test.\n\n00:13.400 --> 00:19.200\nNow, when we say \"test,\" we simply mean a way to check something.\n\n00:19.200 --> 00:25.000\nThink of it like this: a test helps us find out if something is working correctly, or if something is true.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:30.800\nFor example, imagine you're baking a cake.\n\n00:30.800 --> 00:36.700\nYou might poke it with a toothpick. That's a test! If the toothpick comes out clean, the cake is done.\n\n00:36.700 --> 00:42.600\nOr, think about checking if your bike tires have enough air. You press on them.\n\n00:42.600 --> 00:48.300\nThat's a test to see if they're firm enough.\n\n00:48.300 --> 00:54.100\nSo, a test is just a simple way to gather information and make sure things are as they should be. It's all about checking and confirming! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
