    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_121221.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What exactly is a test?\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.100\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something. It's a process of asking a question or performing an action to see what happens.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:22.400\nThink of it like this: a taste test! You try a new flavor of ice cream to see if you like it. That's a test.\n\n00:22.400 --> 00:27.800\nOr, imagine you're trying to figure out if a lightbulb works. You screw it into a lamp.\n\n00:27.800 --> 00:33.400\nIf it lights up, the test is successful! The bulb works.\n\n00:33.400 --> 00:36.900\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:42.900\nDoctors use tests to check your health. Teachers use tests to see what you've learned.\n\n00:42.900 --> 00:55.800\nEven baking a cake is a kind of test \u2013 you're testing your recipe and your skills. So, remember, a test is just a way to learn something new by trying something out.\n\n00:55.800 --> 00:59.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
