    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_121353.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.200\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:05.200 --> 00:15.100\nWhat exactly is a test?\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:22.200\nIt's like asking a question and getting an answer that helps you understand something better.\n\n00:22.200 --> 00:29.900\nThink about it like this: A doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\nThat's a test!\n\n00:29.900 --> 00:36.800\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to see how well you understand a lesson.\nThat's another kind of test!\n\n00:36.800 --> 00:43.700\nTests aren't always about getting a grade.\nSometimes, they're just about gathering information.\n\n00:43.700 --> 00:55.700\nFor example, you might test a new recipe by changing one ingredient and seeing if it tastes better.\nOr you could test if a toy car rolls faster on carpet or wood.\n\n00:55.700 --> 01:05.900\nSo, a test is really just a process of asking a question, trying something out, and then looking at the results to learn something new.\nIt's all about discovery!\n\n01:05.900 --> 01:11.500\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
