    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_121711.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:04.500\nToday we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:04.500 --> 00:07.500\nNow, what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.500 --> 00:11.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out information about something.\n\n00:11.000 --> 00:14.500\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer.\n\n00:14.500 --> 00:16.500\nWe use tests all the time.\n\n00:16.500 --> 00:20.500\nYour doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:20.500 --> 00:24.500\nA chef might taste their food to test if it needs more salt.\n\n00:24.500 --> 00:28.000\nOr, you might take a quiz at school to test what you've learned.\n\n00:28.000 --> 00:33.000\nSo, let's say you're baking a cake. You might poke it with a toothpick.\n\n00:33.000 --> 00:37.500\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is done!\n\n00:37.500 --> 00:42.500\nOr, imagine you're buying a new lightbulb. You might check the box to see how bright it is.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:44.500\nThat's another kind of test!\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:52.000\nTests are a fundamental part of learning and understanding the world around us. They help us confirm things, solve problems, and make better decisions.\n\n00:52.000 --> 00:55.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
