    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_124330.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:17.400\nToday we're going to talk about tests. Now, when we say \"test,\" we don't just mean something you take in school.\n\n00:17.400 --> 00:25.900\nA test is really just a way of finding out if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:25.900 --> 00:30.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if your lightbulb works, right?\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:34.900\nSo you screw it in and flip the switch. That's a test!\n\n00:34.900 --> 00:41.400\nYou're testing if the lightbulb will light up. Or, maybe you're baking a cake and you want to know if it's done.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:54.400\nYou stick a toothpick in it. If it comes out clean, that's a test telling you the cake is ready. So, to recap, a test is simply a procedure to check if something meets a certain condition or standard.\n\n00:54.400 --> 00:55.700\nIt helps us confirm things and make decisions.\n\n00:55.700 --> 00:57.300\nTests are everywhere!\n\n00:57.300 --> 00:59.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
