    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_124641.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:13.800\nNow, what exactly is a test? Simply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:13.800 --> 00:22.100\nThink of it like asking a question and getting an answer. We use tests all the time, even without realizing it.\n\n00:22.100 --> 00:35.200\nFor example, when you try a new recipe, you're testing it to see if you like the taste. Or, if you press a button on a remote, you're testing if it will change the channel.\n\n00:35.200 --> 00:50.900\nTests help us understand if things are working correctly, or if we need to make some changes. They can be big and formal, like a school exam, or small and informal, like checking if your shoelaces are tied.\n\n00:50.900 --> 01:01.300\nThe important thing is that they give us information. So, remember, a test is just a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:04.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "4471f44e-f5c3-488c-899c-886f7b18e41a": {
    "id": "4471f44e-f5c3-488c-899c-886f7b18e41a",
    "topic": "Test",
