    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_124733.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:19.500\nNow, a test is basically a way to find out something. Think of it like a question you're trying to answer, but instead of just guessing, you're gathering information to help you find the right answer.\n\n00:19.500 --> 00:24.700\nThere are all kinds of tests! Imagine you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:24.700 --> 00:31.000\nYou can test it by sticking a toothpick in. If it comes out clean, the cake is ready!\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:40.000\nOr, if you want to know if you understand a lesson, you might take a quiz at school. That quiz is a test of your knowledge.\n\n00:40.000 --> 00:44.800\nAnother example? A doctor might run tests to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:44.800 --> 00:53.400\nThey might check your temperature or blood pressure. All of these are tests, helping us learn and understand different things.\n\n00:53.400 --> 01:05.400\nSo, to recap, a test is a way to gather information and answer a question. They come in many forms, from checking a cake to taking a quiz. They all help us learn!\n\n01:05.400 --> 01:10.800\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
