  "e74e4ade-c84f-4295-9e14-fe456e5c7843": {
    "id": "e74e4ade-c84f-4295-9e14-fe456e5c7843",
    "topic": "Test",
    "level": "basic",
    "status": "completed",
    "queue_position": 1,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T15:18:47.519119",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-07T12:49:15.357034",
    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_124915.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_124915.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.800\nOkay, let\u2019s talk about tests.\n\n00:05.800 --> 00:08.700\nWhat are they, and why do we use them?\n\n00:08.700 --> 00:12.800\nSimply put, a test is a way to check something.\n\n00:12.800 --> 00:16.900\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done baking.\n\n00:16.900 --> 00:21.400\nYou poke it with a toothpick. The toothpick is your test!\n\n00:21.400 --> 00:30.900\nIn many different fields, we use tests to find out information. A scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works.\n\n00:30.900 --> 00:40.300\nA teacher gives you a test to see how well you understand a subject.\n\n00:40.300 --> 00:49.500\nOr maybe you test the batteries in your flashlight to see if they still have power.\n\n00:49.500 --> 00:53.900\nSo, tests help us understand things better.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:56.800\nThey give us information we can use to make decisions or learn more.\n\n00:56.800 --> 00:58.200\nThey can be as simple as poking a cake or as complex as a scientific experiment.\n```"
  },
  "6630495e-7cdf-46a0-9031-6a2c0888f258": {
    "id": "6630495e-7cdf-46a0-9031-6a2c0888f258",
