    "video_url": "/uploads/MathExplanationScene_20260107_125128.mp4",
    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_125128.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:02.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests.\n\n00:02.600 --> 00:05.100\nYou've probably taken a lot of them in school,\n\n00:05.100 --> 00:06.300\nbut what exactly is a test?\n\n00:06.300 --> 00:11.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out how much you know about something,\n\n00:11.300 --> 00:15.300\nor how well you can do something.\n\n00:15.300 --> 00:17.800\nIt's like a measuring stick for your knowledge or skills.\n\n00:17.800 --> 00:25.200\nThink of it like this: If you're learning to bake a cake, a test might be tasting it to see if it's sweet enough.\n\n00:25.200 --> 00:30.300\nOr, if you're learning to ride a bike, a test is whether you can balance and pedal without falling.\n\n00:30.300 --> 00:34.500\nTests can be written questions, like a multiple-choice quiz.\n\n00:34.500 --> 00:37.700\nThey can also be practical, like performing a task.\n\n00:37.700 --> 00:43.500\nThe important thing is that they give us information.\n\n00:43.500 --> 00:47.800\nThey help us see what we've learned and what we still need to work on.\n\n00:47.800 --> 00:52.600\nSo, a test is really just a helpful tool for learning.\n\n00:52.600 --> 00:56.100\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
