    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_125440.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.100 --> 00:02.300\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.300 --> 00:06.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:13.500\nIt's a process we use to gather information and see if something is true or working correctly.\n\n00:13.500 --> 00:20.200\nThink of it like this: if you want to know if a cake is done, you might do a test \u2013 you stick a toothpick in it.\n\n00:20.200 --> 00:23.600\nIf the toothpick comes out clean, the cake passes the test!\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:28.100\nOr, imagine you're learning to ride a bike.\n\n00:28.100 --> 00:31.600\nYou might test your balance.\n\n00:31.600 --> 00:34.800\nYou wobble a bit, maybe fall, but that's part of the test!\n\n00:34.800 --> 00:36.900\nEach time, you learn something.\n\n00:36.900 --> 00:42.500\nTests aren't just in baking or biking, though.\n\n00:42.500 --> 00:46.500\nScientists use tests to see if their ideas are right.\n\n00:46.500 --> 00:51.000\nDoctors use tests to figure out what's wrong when you're sick.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:53.900\nWe use tests all the time to learn and improve.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:58.300\nSo, a test is just a way to check something out.\n\n00:58.300 --> 01:00.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
