    "error": null,
    "progress": "Completed!",
    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_125924.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nNOTE This is a sample subtitle file.  Finetune timings to match the audio!\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're diving into something super important: tests.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:15.100\nA test, at its core, is simply a way to check if something is working correctly, or if you know something.\n\n00:15.100 --> 00:24.000\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you poke it with a toothpick. If it comes out clean, that's a test!\n\n00:24.000 --> 00:28.900\nIt tells you the cake is done. Tests aren't just for baking though.\n\n00:28.900 --> 00:35.900\nImagine you're learning your ABCs. Your teacher might give you a little quiz to see if you remember them.\n\n00:35.900 --> 00:39.900\nThat's a test too! It helps show what you've learned.\n\n00:39.900 --> 00:51.600\nSo, whether it\u2019s checking if your cake is cooked or seeing how well you understand a new topic, tests help us understand where we are and what we might need to work on.\n\n00:51.600 --> 01:04.100\nThey're a valuable tool for learning and making sure things are working as they should. In short, tests are checkpoints that help us measure progress and identify areas for improvement.\n\n01:04.100 --> 01:11.300\nRemember, they're just tools to help us learn and grow! This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
  "ce75a4d0-e070-4703-80ff-53ba9ac5cc62": {
