    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_130732.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.600\nOkay, let's talk about tests. What is a test, anyway?\n\n00:05.600 --> 00:15.000\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something.\n\n00:15.000 --> 00:18.400\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a cake is done.\n\n00:18.400 --> 00:21.800\nYou poke it with a toothpick. That's a test!\n\n00:21.800 --> 00:30.400\nTests aren't just for baking, though. Doctors use tests to see if you're healthy, like checking your temperature.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:38.900\nTeachers use tests to see what you've learned in class. And even scientists use tests to see if their ideas are right.\n\n00:38.900 --> 00:50.200\nSo, a test can be anything from a quick check to a long exam, but the basic idea is always the same: it\u2019s a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n00:50.200 --> 00:53.900\nIn short, tests help us understand the world around us better.\n\n00:53.900 --> 00:56.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
