    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:07.400\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:07.400 --> 00:16.300\nSimply put, a test is a way to find something out.\n\n00:16.300 --> 00:27.300\nIt's like asking a question, but instead of just getting an answer, you're gathering evidence to help you understand something better.\n\n00:27.300 --> 00:38.600\nThink about it like this: a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:38.600 --> 00:49.900\nOr, you might take a spelling test at school to see how well you know your words.\n\n00:49.900 --> 00:52.500\nTests aren't just for people either!\n\n00:52.500 --> 00:59.200\nA scientist might test a new medicine to see if it works, or an engineer might test a bridge to make sure it's strong enough.\n\n00:59.200 --> 01:00.700\nBasically, anything you want to learn more about, you can probably design a test for it.\n\n01:00.700 --> 01:05.300\nSo, to recap: a test is a way to gather information and learn something new.\n\n01:05.300 --> 01:07.800\nIt's a structured way of asking a question and getting useful answers.\n\n01:07.800 --> 01:10.300\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
