    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE duration: 67.2\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.000\nHey everyone, and welcome!\n\n00:02.000 --> 00:05.500\nToday, we're going to talk about something super important: tests.\n\n00:05.500 --> 00:12.000\nNow, when I say \"test,\" I don't just mean school exams. A test is basically a way to see if something works, or if something is true.\n\n00:12.000 --> 00:17.000\nThink of it like this: you want to know if a lightbulb works. The test? Plugging it in!\n\n00:17.000 --> 00:20.700\nIf it lights up, the test is passed!\n\n00:20.700 --> 00:25.000\nOr, maybe you're baking a cake. You can test if it's done by sticking a toothpick in the middle.\n\n00:25.000 --> 00:28.200\nIf it comes out clean, the cake's ready!\n\n00:28.200 --> 00:31.000\nSo, a test is just a way to check something.\n\n00:31.000 --> 00:38.500\nIt helps us learn, fix problems, and make sure things are working the way they should.\n\n00:38.500 --> 00:44.500\nTests are everywhere, from checking your eyesight to figuring out why your computer is slow.\n\n00:44.500 --> 00:51.000\nRemember, a test is simply a way to find out if something is true, or if something works.\n\n00:51.000 --> 00:54.000\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
