    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_131728.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:05.400\nHey everyone, and welcome! Today we're going to talk about tests.\n\n00:05.400 --> 00:14.800\nNow, you might think of school exams, but a test, in a broader sense, is really just a way to check something.\n\n00:14.800 --> 00:27.900\nIt\u2019s how we find out if something is working as it should, or if something is true. Think about it like this: you might test a cake by sticking a toothpick in it to see if it comes out clean.\n\n00:27.900 --> 00:38.100\nThat tells you if the cake is done! Or, if your car won't start, a mechanic might run a diagnostic test to figure out what's wrong.\n\n00:38.100 --> 00:46.400\nThe test gives them information. So, a test is simply a way to gather information and confirm something.\n\n00:46.400 --> 00:55.300\nFrom simple everyday checks to more complex scientific experiments, tests help us understand the world around us.\n\n00:55.300 --> 01:01.300\nThey help us make sure things are working correctly. That's the basics of what a test is!\n\n01:01.300 --> 01:04.900\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
  },
