    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:02.500\nOkay, so what exactly is a test?\n\n00:02.500 --> 00:07.900\nSimply put, a test is a way to find out something about something else.\n\n00:07.900 --> 00:10.000\nThink of it like a detective gathering clues!\n\n00:10.000 --> 00:16.800\nWe use tests all the time, even if we don't realize it.\n\n00:16.800 --> 00:23.600\nFor example, a doctor might give you a blood test to see if you're healthy.\n\n00:23.600 --> 00:30.400\nOr, a teacher might give you a quiz to check if you understand the lesson.\n\n00:30.400 --> 00:41.400\nAnother example is checking the battery on your phone. That's a test to see how much power is left.\n\n00:41.400 --> 00:49.400\nBasically, a test helps us learn something we didn't know before by giving us information.\n\n00:49.400 --> 00:53.000\nWe design and perform the test, and then analyze the results.\n\n00:53.000 --> 01:00.500\nSo, to recap: A test is a tool for gathering information. It helps us understand the world around us, from our health to our knowledge. This video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
