    "video_filename": "MathExplanationScene_20260107_132523.mp4",
    "subtitles": "```webvtt\nWEBVTT\n\n00:00.000 --> 00:06.700\nHey everyone, welcome! Today we're going to talk about something super important: Tests.\n\n00:06.700 --> 00:18.700\nSimply put, a test is a way to check if something works like it's supposed to.\n\n00:18.700 --> 00:25.500\nThink of it like this: you're baking a cake, and you taste it to see if it's sweet enough. That's a test!\n\n00:25.500 --> 00:31.700\nIn school, tests help teachers see if you understand what you've been learning.\n\n00:31.700 --> 00:38.400\nOr, imagine you're building a toy car. You'd push it to see if it rolls, right? That's testing the car's wheels.\n\n00:38.400 --> 00:45.800\nSo, tests can be big or small, formal or informal. The main idea is to see if something is doing what it should.\n\n00:45.800 --> 00:53.200\nThey help us find problems and make things better. To recap: a test is a check, it helps us learn, and it helps us improve things. Easy peasy!\n\n00:53.200 --> 00:58.400\nThis video was created by Apilage AI.\n```"
